msgid "API reference"
msgstr "API 参考"

msgid ""
"Import each function from its module, as in ``from kivi.woe import woe_table``. "
":doc:`api/conventions` describes the rules that every function follows for its arguments, results"
" and errors, :doc:`api/compatibility` what a release may change and how it announces the change, "
"and :doc:`api/glossary` defines the terms of the guides. Each of the other pages documents one "
"module, in the order of the user guide."
msgstr ""
"请从各自所在的模块导入函数，例如 ``from kivi.woe import woe_table`` 。 :doc:`api/conventions` "
"说明所有函数在参数、结果和错误方面共同遵守的规则， :doc:`api/compatibility` 说明一个版本可以改变什么以及如何预告这些改变， :doc:`api/glossary` "
"给出各篇指南所用术语的定义。其余每一页对应一个模块，按用户指南的顺序排列。"

msgid "Binning"
msgstr "分箱"

msgid ""
"Fit bin edges on a reference sample and group every sample with the same edges. "
":func:`~kivi.binning.bin_edges` fits quantile or uniform edges from the values alone; "
":func:`~kivi.binning.chimerge_edges`, :func:`~kivi.binning.tree_edges` and "
":func:`~kivi.binning.monotonic_edges` also use a binary target. :func:`~kivi.binning.cut` groups "
"a sample and gives each special code a group of its own."
msgstr ""
"在基准样本上拟合分箱边界，并用同一组边界对每个样本分组。 :func:`~kivi.binning.bin_edges` 只根据取值拟合等频或等距边界； "
":func:`~kivi.binning.chimerge_edges` 、 :func:`~kivi.binning.tree_edges` 和 "
":func:`~kivi.binning.monotonic_edges` 还会用到二元目标变量。 :func:`~kivi.binning.cut` 对样本分组，并让每个特殊值单独成组。"

msgid ""
"For categorical variables, :func:`~kivi.binning.category_groups` pools rare categories and "
":func:`~kivi.binning.chimerge_groups` merges categories with similar event rates; "
":func:`~kivi.binning.group_categories` applies the resulting dict to a sample."
msgstr ""
"对类别变量， :func:`~kivi.binning.category_groups` 归并稀有类别， :func:`~kivi.binning.chimerge_groups` "
"合并事件率相近的类别； :func:`~kivi.binning.group_categories` 把得到的 dict 应用到样本上。"

msgid "See :doc:`/user_guide/binning` for examples and how to choose the edges."
msgstr "示例以及如何选择边界，见 :doc:`/user_guide/binning` 。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`bin_edges <kivi.binning.bin_edges>`\\ \\(values\\[\\, bins\\, method\\, special\\, "
"...\\]\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`bin_edges <kivi.binning.bin_edges>`\\ \\(values\\[\\, bins\\, method\\, special\\, "
"...\\]\\)"

msgid "Fit numeric bin edges on a reference sample."
msgstr "在基准样本上拟合数值变量的分箱边界。"

msgid ":py:obj:`cut <kivi.binning.cut>`\\ \\(values\\, edges\\, \\*\\[\\, special\\]\\)"
msgstr ":py:obj:`cut <kivi.binning.cut>`\\ \\(values\\, edges\\, \\*\\[\\, special\\]\\)"

msgid "Assign values to bins, with a separate group for each special value."
msgstr "将取值分配到各箱，每个特殊值单独成组。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`chimerge_edges <kivi.binning.chimerge_edges>`\\ \\(values\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, "
"...\\]\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`chimerge_edges <kivi.binning.chimerge_edges>`\\ \\(values\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, "
"...\\]\\)"

msgid "Fit edges by merging adjacent quantile bins with ChiMerge."
msgstr "用 ChiMerge（卡方分箱）合并相邻的等频箱，拟合分箱边界。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`tree_edges <kivi.binning.tree_edges>`\\ \\(values\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, max\\_bins\\, "
"...\\]\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`tree_edges <kivi.binning.tree_edges>`\\ \\(values\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, max\\_bins\\, "
"...\\]\\)"

msgid "Fit edges with the splits of a decision tree on one variable."
msgstr "用单变量决策树的切分点拟合分箱边界。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`monotonic_edges <kivi.binning.monotonic_edges>`\\ \\(values\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, "
"...\\]\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`monotonic_edges <kivi.binning.monotonic_edges>`\\ \\(values\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, "
"...\\]\\)"

msgid "Fit edges by merging adjacent quantile bins until the WOE is monotonic."
msgstr "合并相邻的等频箱，直到 WOE 单调，以此拟合分箱边界。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`category_groups <kivi.binning.category_groups>`\\ \\(values\\, \\*\\[\\, min\\_share\\, "
"...\\]\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`category_groups <kivi.binning.category_groups>`\\ \\(values\\, \\*\\[\\, min\\_share\\, "
"...\\]\\)"

msgid "Fit a grouping that pools the rare categories of a reference sample."
msgstr "在基准样本上拟合类别分组，把稀有类别归为一组。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`chimerge_groups <kivi.binning.chimerge_groups>`\\ \\(values\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, "
"...\\]\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`chimerge_groups <kivi.binning.chimerge_groups>`\\ \\(values\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, "
"...\\]\\)"

msgid "Fit a grouping that merges categories with similar event rates by ChiMerge."
msgstr "用 ChiMerge（卡方分箱）合并事件率相近的类别，拟合类别分组。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`group_categories <kivi.binning.group_categories>`\\ \\(values\\, groups\\, \\*\\[\\, "
"unseen\\]\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`group_categories <kivi.binning.group_categories>`\\ \\(values\\, groups\\, \\*\\[\\, "
"unseen\\]\\)"

msgid "Assign category labels to the groups of a fitted grouping."
msgstr "按已拟合的分组映射，把类别标签分配到各组。"

msgid ""
"The edges are fitted once and then applied with ``pandas.cut`` to the reference and to every "
"sample compared with it."
msgstr "边界只拟合一次，然后用 ``pandas.cut`` 应用到基准样本以及每个与之比较的样本上。"

msgid "Parameters"
msgstr "参数"

msgid "**values**"
msgstr "**values**"

msgid "array_like"
msgstr "array_like"

msgid ""
"One-dimensional numeric reference values, such as a list, a NumPy array or a pandas Series. "
"Missing values are omitted."
msgstr "一维数值型基准取值，可以是列表、NumPy 数组或 pandas Series。拟合时忽略缺失值。"

msgid "**bins**"
msgstr "**bins**"

msgid "int, default 5"
msgstr "int，默认 5"

msgid "Requested number of bins. Tied quantiles can reduce this number."
msgstr "期望箱数。分位点重合时实际箱数可能减少。"

msgid "**method**"
msgstr "**method**"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "{\"quantile\", \"uniform\"}, default \"quantile\""
msgstr "{\"quantile\", \"uniform\"}，默认 \"quantile\""

msgid "Use sample quantiles or equally spaced edges."
msgstr "使用样本分位数或等距边界。"

msgid "**special**"
msgstr "**special**"

msgid "array_like, optional"
msgstr "array_like，可选"

msgid ""
"Special values, such as codes for \"not applicable\", that are omitted when the edges are fitted."
" Pass the same values to `cut` so that each one forms its own group."
msgstr "特殊值，例如表示“不适用”的编码，拟合边界时会被排除。请把同样的值传给 `cut` ，使每个特殊值单独成组。"

msgid "**weights**"
msgstr "**weights**"

msgid ""
"Non-negative weight of each value, for example the inverse of its sampling rate. Values with zero"
" weight are left out. With weights, quantile edges are weighted quantiles by the inverted CDF, so"
" every interior edge is an observed value."
msgstr "每个取值的非负权重，例如其抽样比例的倒数。权重为零的取值会被排除。使用权重时，等频边界取逆累积分布（inverted CDF）意义下的加权分位数，因此每个内部边界都是实际观测到的取值。"

msgid "Returns"
msgstr "返回值"

msgid "numpy.ndarray"
msgstr "numpy.ndarray"

msgid "Increasing edges with infinite endpoints, suitable for pandas.cut."
msgstr "严格递增的边界数组，两端为负无穷和正无穷，可直接传给 pandas.cut。"

msgid "Raises"
msgstr "异常"

msgid "ValueError"
msgstr "ValueError"

msgid ""
"If `bins` is not a positive integer, `method` is not recognized, `values` is not one-dimensional "
"or not numeric, `special` is not one-dimensional or contains a missing value or a boolean, or the"
" reference has no observations or contains an infinite value apart from special values. Also if "
"`weights` is not numeric, does not give each value one finite, non-negative weight with a "
"positive total, or has an index other than that of `values`."
msgstr ""
"如果 `bins` 不是正整数、 `method` 无法识别、 `values` 不是一维或不是数值、 `special` "
"不是一维或含有缺失值或布尔值，或者除特殊值外基准样本没有观测值或含有无穷值。此外，如果 `weights` 不是数值、没有为每个取值给出一个有限非负的权重、权重总和不为正，或其索引与 "
"`values` 不同。"

msgid "Warns"
msgstr "警告"

msgid "UserWarning"
msgstr "UserWarning"

msgid ""
"If tied edges leave fewer bins than requested, for example when a single value accounts for a "
"large share of the reference."
msgstr "如果边界重合导致实际箱数少于期望箱数，例如某个取值在基准样本中占比很大。"

msgid ":obj:`cut`"
msgstr ":obj:`cut`"

msgid ":obj:`pandas.cut`"
msgstr ":obj:`pandas.cut`"

msgid "Assign values to the bins defined by the edges."
msgstr "按边界把取值分配到各箱。"

msgid ":obj:`numpy.quantile`"
msgstr ":obj:`numpy.quantile`"

msgid "Compute the quantile edges."
msgstr "计算分位数边界。"

msgid ":obj:`kivi.woe.woe_table`"
msgstr ":obj:`kivi.woe.woe_table`"

msgid "Weight of evidence of the resulting groups."
msgstr "计算所得分组的证据权重。"

msgid ":obj:`kivi.stability.psi_table`"
msgstr ":obj:`kivi.stability.psi_table`"

msgid "Stability of the resulting groups."
msgstr "计算所得分组的稳定性。"

msgid "Notes"
msgstr "说明"

msgid ""
"Quantile edges are the sample quantiles at equally spaced probabilities, computed with the "
"default linear interpolation of ``numpy.quantile``. Uniform edges divide the range from the "
"smallest to the largest value into equal widths."
msgstr "分位数边界是在等间距概率处取的样本分位数，使用 ``numpy.quantile`` 默认的线性插值计算。等距边界把从最小值到最大值的区间等分。"

msgid ""
"Repeated edges are merged, and the outer edges are replaced with infinities, so every finite "
"value falls into exactly one interval. The intervals of ``pandas.cut`` are closed on the right."
msgstr "重复的边界会被合并，最外侧的两个边界替换为无穷，因此每个有限值都恰好落入一个区间。 ``pandas.cut`` 的区间为左开右闭。"

msgid "Examples"
msgstr "示例"

msgid "A special value is left out of the fit:"
msgstr "特殊值不参与拟合："

msgid "Without `special` the result is the same as ``pandas.cut(values, edges)`` for every finite value."
msgstr "不传 `special` 时，每个有限值的结果都与 ``pandas.cut(values, edges)`` 相同。"

msgid ""
"One-dimensional numeric values to assign. Missing values stay missing. Infinite values must be "
"special codes."
msgstr "待分箱的一维数值。缺失值保持缺失。无穷值必须是特殊值编码。"

msgid "**edges**"
msgstr "**edges**"

msgid "Increasing bin edges, usually from `bin_edges`."
msgstr "递增的分箱边界，通常来自 `bin_edges` 。"

msgid ""
"Special values that each form their own group instead of falling into an interval. Use the values"
" passed to `bin_edges`."
msgstr "每个特殊值单独成组，不落入任何区间。请使用传给 `bin_edges` 的同一组值。"

msgid "pandas.Series or pandas.Categorical"
msgstr "pandas.Series 或 pandas.Categorical"

msgid ""
"Categorical groups whose categories are the special values, in the order given, followed by the "
"intervals. A Series input gives a Series with the same index and name."
msgstr "分类型的分组结果，类别依次为按给定顺序排列的特殊值和各区间。输入为 Series 时返回 Series，索引和名称保持不变。"

msgid ""
"If `values` is not one-dimensional, is not numeric apart from special values or has an infinite "
"value that is not a special value, `edges` does not increase, or `special` is not one-dimensional"
" or contains a missing value or a boolean."
msgstr "如果 `values` 不是一维、除特殊值外不是数值或含有不属于特殊值的无穷值、 `edges` 不是递增的，或者 `special` 不是一维或含有缺失值或布尔值。"

msgid ":obj:`bin_edges`"
msgstr ":obj:`bin_edges`"

msgid "Fit the edges on a reference sample."
msgstr "在基准样本上拟合边界。"

msgid "Assign values to intervals only."
msgstr "只把取值分配到区间。"

msgid ""
"A special value is matched by equality, so ``-1`` and ``-1.0`` are the same code. Values that are"
" not numbers, such as strings read from a file, are also matched after conversion with "
"``pandas.to_numeric``, so the string ``\"-1\"`` falls into the group of the code ``-1``. Finite "
"values outside the edges become missing, as with ``pandas.cut``; the infinite outer edges of "
"`bin_edges` avoid this. An infinite value raises an error unless it is a special value, because "
"``pandas.cut`` would leave ``-inf`` in no interval, so that it would count as a missing value, "
"and put ``inf`` in the last interval."
msgstr ""
"特殊值按相等关系匹配，因此 ``-1`` 和 ``-1.0`` 视为同一个编码。不是数字的值（例如从文件读入的字符串）还会在经 ``pandas.to_numeric`` "
"转换后再匹配一次，因此字符串 ``\"-1\"`` 会落入编码 ``-1`` 的分组。与 ``pandas.cut`` 一样，超出边界的有限值会变为缺失； `bin_edges` "
"两端的无穷边界可以避免这种情况。无穷值除非是特殊值，否则会引发错误，因为 ``pandas.cut`` 会让 ``-inf`` 不落入任何区间、从而被算作缺失值，而把 ``inf`` "
"放进最后一个区间。"

msgid ""
"The values are first cut into ``initial_bins`` quantile bins, or into one bin per distinct value "
"if there are no more distinct values than that. The adjacent pair with the smallest chi-square "
"statistic, the pair whose event rates are most alike, is then merged, and merging is repeated "
"while more than ``max_bins`` bins remain or while some adjacent pair is not significantly "
"different at level ``alpha``."
msgstr ""
"先将数值切成 ``initial_bins`` 个等频箱；若不同取值的个数不超过该数，则每个取值单独成一箱。随后合并卡方统计量最小、即事件率最接近的一对相邻箱。只要箱数仍多于 "
"``max_bins``，或仍有相邻两箱在显著性水平 ``alpha`` 下差异不显著，就继续合并。"

msgid ""
"One-dimensional numeric values, such as a list, a NumPy array or a pandas Series. Missing values "
"and their labels are omitted."
msgstr "一维数值，可以是列表、NumPy 数组或 pandas Series。缺失值及其标签会被忽略。"

msgid "**target**"
msgstr "**target**"

msgid ""
"Binary labels, with 1 indicating the event. If `values` and `target` are both pandas Series, they"
" must have identical indices; otherwise they are matched by position."
msgstr "二分类标签，1 表示事件。如果 `values` 和 `target` 都是 pandas Series，二者的索引必须完全相同；否则按位置对应。"

msgid "**max_bins**"
msgstr "**max_bins**"

msgid "Maximum number of bins."
msgstr "最大箱数。"

msgid "**alpha**"
msgstr "**alpha**"

msgid "float or None, default 0.05"
msgstr "float 或 None，默认 0.05"

msgid ""
"Significance level of the chi-square test with one degree of freedom. Adjacent bins are merged "
"until every pair differs at this level. Pass None to merge down to ``max_bins`` only."
msgstr "自由度为 1 的卡方检验的显著性水平。相邻箱会一直合并，直到每一对在该水平下都差异显著。传入 None 时只合并到 ``max_bins`` 个箱。"

msgid "**initial_bins**"
msgstr "**initial_bins**"

msgid "int, default 20"
msgstr "int，默认 20"

msgid "Number of quantile bins to start from. Tied quantiles can reduce it."
msgstr "起始的等频箱数。分位点重合时实际箱数可能减少。"

msgid ""
"Special values, such as codes for \"not applicable\", that are omitted with their labels when the"
" edges are fitted. Pass the same values to `cut` so that each one forms its own group."
msgstr "特殊值，例如表示“不适用”的编码；拟合边界时，这些值连同其标签一起被排除。请把同样的值传给 `cut` ，使每个特殊值单独成组。"

msgid ""
"Non-negative weight of each observation, for example the inverse of its sampling rate, matched "
"like `target`. Observations with zero weight are left out, and the counts in each bin are sums of"
" weights. The initial quantile bins then use weighted quantiles by the inverted CDF, so unit "
"weights can give other edges than no weights when there are more distinct values than "
"`initial_bins`. The chi-square test treats the weighted counts as counts, so scale the weights to"
" sum to the sample size when the p-values matter."
msgstr ""
"每个观测的非负权重，例如其抽样比例的倒数，对应方式与 `target` "
"相同。权重为零的观测会被排除，每箱的计数为权重之和。此时初始的等频细分箱也使用逆累积分布意义下的加权分位数，因此当不同取值的个数多于 `initial_bins` 时，权重全为 1 "
"与不传权重得到的边界可能不同。卡方检验把加权计数当作计数处理，因此在需要参考 p 值时，请把权重缩放到总和等于样本量。"

msgid ""
"If `max_bins` or `initial_bins` is not a positive integer, `alpha` is neither None nor between 0 "
"and 1, `values` and `target` are not one-dimensional or their indices or lengths do not match, "
"`special` is not one-dimensional or contains a missing value or a boolean, `values` is not "
"numeric or has no finite observations apart from missing and special values, or `target` has "
"labels other than 0 and 1 or lacks one of them in the rows that are fitted. Also if `weights` is "
"not numeric, does not give each value one finite, non-negative weight with a positive total, or "
"has an index other than that of `values`."
msgstr ""
"`max_bins` 或 `initial_bins` 不是正整数，`alpha` 既不是 None 也不在 0 与 1 之间，`values` 与 `target` "
"不是一维、索引或长度不一致，`special` 不是一维或含有缺失值或布尔值，`values` 不是数值或除缺失值和特殊值外没有有限观测值，或者 `target` 含有 0 和 1 "
"以外的标签、在参与拟合的行中缺少其中一类，都会引发此异常。此外，如果 `weights` 不是数值、没有为每个取值给出一个有限非负的权重、权重总和不为正，或其索引与 `values` 不同。"

msgid ":obj:`tree_edges`"
msgstr ":obj:`tree_edges`"

msgid "Split the values recursively instead of merging."
msgstr "递归切分数值，而不是合并。"

msgid ":obj:`monotonic_edges`"
msgstr ":obj:`monotonic_edges`"

msgid "Merge until the WOE is monotonic."
msgstr "合并到 WOE 单调为止。"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"For an adjacent pair of bins with observed counts :math:`O_{ij}` (bin :math:`i`, class :math:`j`)"
" and expected counts :math:`E_{ij} = R_i C_j / N` under equal event rates,"
msgstr ""
"对相邻的两个箱，记观测计数为 :math:`O_{ij}` （箱 :math:`i`，类别 :math:`j`），事件率相同假设下的期望计数为 :math:`E_{ij} = R_i C_j /"
" N`，则"

msgid "\\chi^2 = \\sum_{i=1}^{2} \\sum_{j=0}^{1} \\frac{(O_{ij} - E_{ij})^2}{E_{ij}}"
msgstr "\\chi^2 = \\sum_{i=1}^{2} \\sum_{j=0}^{1} \\frac{(O_{ij} - E_{ij})^2}{E_{ij}}"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"where cells with :math:`E_{ij} = 0` contribute nothing. A pair stays separate when the p-value of"
" :math:`\\chi^2` is below ``alpha``."
msgstr "其中 :math:`E_{ij} = 0` 的单元格不计入。当 :math:`\\chi^2` 的 p 值小于 ``alpha`` 时，这两个箱保持分开。"

msgid ""
"The tree grows best first: of all current bins, the one whose best split most reduces the total "
"impurity is split next, until there are ``max_bins`` bins or no split reduces the impurity while "
"leaving at least ``min_bin_share`` of the observations on each side."
msgstr ""
"决策树按最优优先的顺序生长：在当前所有箱中，最优切分能让总不纯度下降最多的箱先被切分，直到箱数达到 ``max_bins``，或者在两侧都保留至少 ``min_bin_share`` "
"观测的前提下，已没有能降低不纯度的切分。"

msgid "Maximum number of bins, the leaves of the tree."
msgstr "最大箱数，即决策树的叶节点数。"

msgid "**min_bin_share**"
msgstr "**min_bin_share**"

msgid "float, default 0.05"
msgstr "float，默认 0.05"

msgid ""
"Minimum share of the fitted values in every bin, from 0 to 0.5, or of their total weight when "
"`weights` is given. Missing and special values do not count towards it."
msgstr "每个箱至少包含的拟合取值占比，取值范围为 0 到 0.5；传入 `weights` 时按权重总和计算。缺失值和特殊值不计入。"

msgid "**criterion**"
msgstr "**criterion**"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "{\"entropy\", \"gini\"}, default \"entropy\""
msgstr "{\"entropy\", \"gini\"}，默认 \"entropy\""

msgid "Impurity measure: entropy for information gain, or the Gini index."
msgstr "不纯度指标：熵（即信息增益）或基尼指数。"

msgid ""
"Non-negative weight of each observation, for example the inverse of its sampling rate, matched "
"like `target`. Observations with zero weight are left out, and the counts in each bin are sums of"
" weights."
msgstr "每个观测的非负权重，例如其抽样比例的倒数，对应方式与 `target` 相同。权重为零的观测会被排除，每箱的计数为权重之和。"

msgid ""
"Increasing edges with infinite endpoints, suitable for pandas.cut. Every interior edge is an "
"observed value, the largest one in the bin to its left."
msgstr "严格递增的边界数组，两端为负无穷和正无穷，可直接传给 pandas.cut。每个内部边界都是一个观测值，即其左侧箱中的最大值。"

msgid ""
"If `max_bins` is not a positive integer, `min_bin_share` is not between 0 and 0.5, `criterion` is"
" not recognized, `values` and `target` are not one-dimensional or their indices or lengths do not"
" match, `special` is not one-dimensional or contains a missing value or a boolean, `values` is "
"not numeric or has no finite observations apart from missing and special values, or `target` has "
"labels other than 0 and 1 or lacks one of them in the rows that are fitted. Also if `weights` is "
"not numeric, does not give each value one finite, non-negative weight with a positive total, or "
"has an index other than that of `values`."
msgstr ""
"`max_bins` 不是正整数，`min_bin_share` 不在 0 与 0.5 之间，`criterion` 无法识别，`values` 与 `target` "
"不是一维、索引或长度不一致，`special` 不是一维或含有缺失值或布尔值，`values` 不是数值或除缺失值和特殊值外没有有限观测值，或者 `target` 含有 0 和 1 "
"以外的标签、在参与拟合的行中缺少其中一类，都会引发此异常。此外，如果 `weights` 不是数值、没有为每个取值给出一个有限非负的权重、权重总和不为正，或其索引与 `values` 不同。"

msgid ":obj:`chimerge_edges`"
msgstr ":obj:`chimerge_edges`"

msgid "Merge fine bins instead of splitting."
msgstr "合并细分箱，而不是切分。"

msgid ""
"For a bin with :math:`n` observations (their total weight, with `weights`) and event rate "
":math:`p`, the impurity is :math:`H(p) = -p \\ln p - (1 - p) \\ln(1 - p)` (entropy) or "
":math:`G(p) = 2p(1 - p)` (Gini). A split into :math:`n_L` and :math:`n_R` observations reduces "
"the total impurity by :math:`n H(p) - n_L H(p_L) - n_R H(p_R)`, and the largest reduction over "
"all bins and cut points is chosen."
msgstr ""
"对含 :math:`n` 个观测（传入 `weights` 时为其权重总和）、事件率为 :math:`p` 的箱，不纯度为 :math:`H(p) = -p \\ln p - (1 - p) "
"\\ln(1 - p)` （熵）或 :math:`G(p) = 2p(1 - p)` （基尼指数）。把它切成 :math:`n_L` 和 :math:`n_R` 个观测的两部分，总不纯度下降 "
":math:`n H(p) - n_L H(p_L) - n_R H(p_R)`；在所有箱和切分点中选择下降最多的一个。"

msgid ""
"The values are first cut into ``initial_bins`` quantile bins, or into one bin per distinct value "
"if there are no more distinct values than that. While two adjacent bins break the trend, the "
"first such pair is merged and the WOE is recomputed (pool adjacent violators), so the WOE of the "
"final bins is strictly increasing or strictly decreasing. While more than ``max_bins`` bins "
"remain, the adjacent pair with the smallest chi-square statistic is merged as in "
":func:`chimerge_edges`, and the trend is checked again."
msgstr ""
"先将数值切成 ``initial_bins`` 个等频箱；若不同取值的个数不超过该数，则每个取值单独成一箱。只要有相邻两箱违背趋势，就合并第一对这样的箱并重新计算 "
"WOE（合并相邻违序者，pool adjacent violators），因此最终各箱的 WOE 严格递增或严格递减。若箱数仍多于 ``max_bins``，则像 "
":func:`chimerge_edges` 一样合并卡方统计量最小的相邻两箱，再重新检查趋势。"

msgid "int or None, default 5"
msgstr "int 或 None，默认 5"

msgid "Maximum number of bins. Pass None to stop as soon as the WOE is monotonic."
msgstr "最大箱数。传入 None 时，WOE 一旦单调即停止合并。"

msgid "**direction**"
msgstr "**direction**"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "{\"auto\", \"increasing\", \"decreasing\"}, default \"auto\""
msgstr "{\"auto\", \"increasing\", \"decreasing\"}，默认 \"auto\""

msgid ""
"Trend of the WOE as the values grow. ``\"auto\"`` fits both directions and keeps the one with the"
" larger information value, preferring ``\"increasing\"`` on a tie."
msgstr "随数值增大时 WOE 的趋势。``\"auto\"`` 会两个方向都拟合，保留信息值较大的一个；两者相等时取 ``\"increasing\"``。"

msgid "**smoothing**"
msgstr "**smoothing**"

msgid "float, default 0.5"
msgstr "float，默认 0.5"

msgid ""
"Positive replacement for a zero count when calculating the WOE, as in :func:`kivi.woe.woe_table`."
" Use the same value there to see the same trend."
msgstr "计算 WOE 时用这个正数替代零计数，含义与 :func:`kivi.woe.woe_table` 相同。在那里使用同一取值，才能看到同样的趋势。"

msgid ""
"Special values, such as codes for \"not applicable\", that are omitted with their labels when the"
" edges are fitted. Pass the same values to `cut` so that each one forms its own group. The trend "
"applies to the intervals only; a special group can have any WOE."
msgstr "特殊值，例如表示“不适用”的编码；拟合边界时，这些值连同其标签一起被排除。请把同样的值传给 `cut` ，使每个特殊值单独成组。单调趋势只约束各区间，特殊值组的 WOE 不受限制。"

msgid ""
"Non-negative weight of each observation, for example the inverse of its sampling rate, matched "
"like `target`. Observations with zero weight are left out, and the counts in each bin are sums of"
" weights. The initial quantile bins then use weighted quantiles by the inverted CDF, so unit "
"weights can give other edges than no weights when there are more distinct values than "
"`initial_bins`. `smoothing` is then in units of weight."
msgstr ""
"每个观测的非负权重，例如其抽样比例的倒数，对应方式与 `target` "
"相同。权重为零的观测会被排除，每箱的计数为权重之和。此时初始的等频细分箱也使用逆累积分布意义下的加权分位数，因此当不同取值的个数多于 `initial_bins` 时，权重全为 1 "
"与不传权重得到的边界可能不同。此时 `smoothing` 以权重为单位。"

msgid ""
"If `max_bins` is neither None nor a positive integer, `initial_bins` is not a positive integer, "
"`direction` is not recognized, `smoothing` is not finite and positive, `values` and `target` are "
"not one-dimensional or their indices or lengths do not match, `special` is not one-dimensional or"
" contains a missing value or a boolean, `values` is not numeric or has no finite observations "
"apart from missing and special values, or `target` has labels other than 0 and 1 or lacks one of "
"them in the rows that are fitted. Also if `weights` is not numeric, does not give each value one "
"finite, non-negative weight with a positive total, or has an index other than that of `values`."
msgstr ""
"`max_bins` 既不是 None 也不是正整数，`initial_bins` 不是正整数，`direction` 无法识别，`smoothing` 不是有限正数，`values` 与 "
"`target` 不是一维、索引或长度不一致，`special` 不是一维或含有缺失值或布尔值，`values` 不是数值或除缺失值和特殊值外没有有限观测值，或者 `target` 含有 0 和"
" 1 以外的标签、在参与拟合的行中缺少其中一类，都会引发此异常。此外，如果 `weights` 不是数值、没有为每个取值给出一个有限非负的权重、权重总和不为正，或其索引与 `values` "
"不同。"

msgid "Merge fine bins by a chi-square test."
msgstr "按卡方检验合并细分箱。"

msgid "Split the values recursively."
msgstr "递归切分数值。"

msgid ""
"A category is rare when it makes up less than ``min_share`` of the fitted values or has fewer "
"than ``min_count`` of them. The rare categories form one group labelled ``rare_label``, and every"
" other category is a group of its own. Apply the grouping with `group_categories` to the "
"reference and to every sample compared with it."
msgstr ""
"某个类别在拟合取值中的占比低于 ``min_share`` ，或个数少于 ``min_count`` 时，即为稀有类别。稀有类别合为一组，标签为 ``rare_label`` "
"；其他类别各自单独成组。请用 `group_categories` 把分组映射应用到基准样本和与之比较的每个样本上。"

msgid ""
"One-dimensional category labels of the reference sample, such as a list, a NumPy array or a "
"pandas Series of strings. Missing values are omitted."
msgstr "基准样本的一维类别标签，可以是字符串组成的列表、NumPy 数组或 pandas Series。拟合时忽略缺失值。"

msgid "**min_share**"
msgstr "**min_share**"

msgid ""
"Share of the fitted values, from 0 to 1, below which a category is rare. With `weights`, the "
"share of their total weight."
msgstr "类别在拟合取值中的占比低于该值（取值范围为 0 到 1）即为稀有类别。传入 `weights` 时按权重总和中的占比计算。"

msgid "**min_count**"
msgstr "**min_count**"

msgid "float, default 0"
msgstr "float，默认 0"

msgid ""
"Number of fitted values, or their total weight with `weights`, below which a category is rare. "
"The default leaves the decision to `min_share`."
msgstr "类别的拟合取值个数（传入 `weights` 时为其权重总和）低于该值即为稀有类别。默认值把判断交给 `min_share` 。"

msgid "**rare_label**"
msgstr "**rare_label**"

msgid "str, int or float, default \"other\""
msgstr "str、int 或 float，默认 \"other\""

msgid ""
"Label of the group of rare categories. It must differ from the categories that are not rare and "
"from the special codes."
msgstr "稀有类别所在组的标签。它不能与非稀有类别或特殊值相同。"

msgid ""
"Special codes, such as ``\"unknown\"``, that are omitted when the grouping is fitted. Each one is"
" a group of its own, however rare."
msgstr "特殊值，例如 ``\"unknown\"`` ，拟合分组映射时会被排除。无论多么稀有，每个特殊值都单独成组。"

msgid ""
"Non-negative weight of each value, for example the inverse of its sampling rate. Values with zero"
" weight are left out, and the counts of the categories are sums of weights."
msgstr "每个取值的非负权重，例如其抽样比例的倒数。权重为零的取值会被排除，各类别的计数为权重之和。"

msgid "dict"
msgstr "dict"

msgid ""
"The group of each category: first the special codes in the order given, then the categories that "
"are not rare, each mapped to itself, then the rare categories, mapped to `rare_label`. Categories"
" follow the order in which they first appear, or the order of the categories of a categorical "
"input."
msgstr "每个类别所属的组：先是按给定顺序排列的特殊值，再是各自映射到自身的非稀有类别，最后是映射到 `rare_label` 的稀有类别。类别按首次出现的次序排列；输入为分类型时按其类别顺序排列。"

msgid ""
"If `values` is not one-dimensional or has no values apart from missing, special and zero-weight "
"values, `min_share` is not between 0 and 1, `min_count` is not a finite, non-negative number, "
"`rare_label` is neither a string nor a number or is the label of a category that is not rare or "
"of a special code, or `special` is not one-dimensional or contains a missing value or a boolean. "
"Also if `weights` is not numeric, does not give each value one finite, non-negative weight with a"
" positive total, or has an index other than that of `values`."
msgstr ""
"如果 `values` 不是一维或除缺失值、特殊值和零权重取值外没有其他取值， `min_share` 不在 0 与 1 之间， `min_count` 不是有限非负数， "
"`rare_label` 既不是字符串也不是数值，或者是某个非稀有类别或特殊值的标签，或者 `special` 不是一维或含有缺失值或布尔值。此外，如果 `weights` "
"不是数值、没有为每个取值给出一个有限非负的权重、权重总和不为正，或其索引与 `values` 不同。"

msgid ":obj:`chimerge_groups`"
msgstr ":obj:`chimerge_groups`"

msgid "Merge categories with similar event rates."
msgstr "合并事件率相近的类别。"

msgid ":obj:`group_categories`"
msgstr ":obj:`group_categories`"

msgid "Assign values to the fitted groups."
msgstr "把取值分配到拟合的各组。"

msgid ""
"Rare categories are pooled whatever their event rates, so a rare category with a high event rate "
"can share a group with one with a low rate. `chimerge_groups` uses the target to avoid this. The "
"group of rare categories can itself hold less than `min_share` of the values."
msgstr ""
"稀有类别不论事件率高低都会合为一组，因此事件率高的稀有类别可能与事件率低的类别同组。 `chimerge_groups` 利用目标变量避免这一点。稀有类别组本身的占比也可能低于 "
"`min_share` 。"

msgid ""
"The categories are sorted by their WOE, with zero counts smoothed as in "
":func:`kivi.woe.woe_table`, and neighbours in that order are merged. First, while some group "
"holds less than ``min_group_share`` of the fitted values, the smallest one is merged with the "
"neighbour whose chi-square statistic with it is smaller. Then, as in `chimerge_edges`, the "
"adjacent pair with the smallest chi-square statistic is merged while more than ``max_groups`` "
"groups remain or while some adjacent pair is not significantly different at level ``alpha``. The "
"groups are sorted by WOE again after every merge, so the WOE of the final groups increases from "
"the first to the last."
msgstr ""
"先按 WOE 对类别排序（零计数按 :func:`kivi.woe.woe_table` 的方式平滑），再合并该顺序下相邻的类别。首先，只要有组的占比低于拟合取值的 "
"``min_group_share`` ，就把其中最小的组与卡方统计量较小的那个相邻组合并。然后像 `chimerge_edges` 一样，只要组数仍多于 ``max_groups`` "
"，或仍有相邻两组在显著性水平 ``alpha`` 下差异不显著，就合并卡方统计量最小的一对相邻组。每次合并后都重新按 WOE 排序，因此最终各组的 WOE 从第一组到最后一组递增。"

msgid ""
"One-dimensional category labels, such as a list, a NumPy array or a pandas Series of strings. "
"Missing values and their labels are omitted."
msgstr "一维类别标签，可以是字符串组成的列表、NumPy 数组或 pandas Series。缺失值及其标签会被忽略。"

msgid "**max_groups**"
msgstr "**max_groups**"

msgid "Maximum number of groups, not counting the special codes."
msgstr "最大组数，不计特殊值。"

msgid ""
"Significance level of the chi-square test with one degree of freedom. Adjacent groups are merged "
"until every pair differs at this level. Pass None to merge down to ``max_groups`` only."
msgstr "自由度为 1 的卡方检验的显著性水平。相邻组会一直合并，直到每一对在该水平下都差异显著。传入 None 时只合并到 ``max_groups`` 个组。"

msgid "**min_group_share**"
msgstr "**min_group_share**"

msgid ""
"Minimum share of the fitted values in every group, from 0 to 0.5, or of their total weight when "
"`weights` is given. Missing and special values do not count towards it."
msgstr "每个组至少包含的拟合取值占比，取值范围为 0 到 0.5；传入 `weights` 时按权重总和计算。缺失值和特殊值不计入。"

msgid ""
"Positive replacement for a zero count when calculating the WOE that orders the groups, as in "
":func:`kivi.woe.woe_table`. Use the same value there to see the same order."
msgstr "计算用于排序各组的 WOE 时，用这个正数替代零计数，含义与 :func:`kivi.woe.woe_table` 相同。在那里使用同一取值，才能看到同样的顺序。"

msgid ""
"Special codes, such as ``\"unknown\"``, that are omitted with their labels when the grouping is "
"fitted. Each one is a group of its own."
msgstr "特殊值，例如 ``\"unknown\"`` ；拟合分组映射时，这些值连同其标签一起被排除。每个特殊值单独成组。"

msgid ""
"Non-negative weight of each observation, for example the inverse of its sampling rate, matched "
"like `target`. Observations with zero weight are left out, and the counts of each group are sums "
"of weights. The chi-square test treats the weighted counts as counts, so scale the weights to sum"
" to the sample size when the p-values matter. `smoothing` is then in units of weight."
msgstr ""
"每个观测的非负权重，例如其抽样比例的倒数，对应方式与 `target` 相同。权重为零的观测会被排除，每组的计数为权重之和。卡方检验把加权计数当作计数处理，因此在需要参考 p "
"值时，请把权重缩放到总和等于样本量。此时 `smoothing` 以权重为单位。"

msgid ""
"The group of each category: first the special codes in the order given, each mapped to itself, "
"then the categories of each group, in increasing order of the group's WOE. A group of one "
"category keeps its label; a merged group is labelled with the labels of its categories, in "
"increasing order of their own WOE, joined by ``\", \"``. A group of more than five categories "
"shows the first four, followed by ``\", ... (+n)\"`` with the number ``n`` of the others."
msgstr ""
"每个类别所属的组：先是按给定顺序排列、各自映射到自身的特殊值，再按组的 WOE "
"从小到大依次列出各组的类别。只含一个类别的组沿用该类别的标签；合并后的组以其各类别的标签为标签，这些标签按类别自身的 WOE 从小到大排列，并用 ``\", \"`` "
"连接。超过五个类别的组只列出前四个，后接 ``\", ... (+n)\"`` ，其中 ``n`` 为其余类别的个数。"

msgid ""
"If `max_groups` is not a positive integer, `alpha` is neither None nor between 0 and 1, "
"`min_group_share` is not between 0 and 0.5, `smoothing` is not finite and positive, `values` and "
"`target` are not one-dimensional or their indices or lengths do not match, `special` is not one-"
"dimensional or contains a missing value or a boolean, `values` has no values apart from missing, "
"special and zero-weight values, `target` has labels other than 0 and 1 or lacks one of them in "
"the rows that are fitted, or the label of a merged group would be the label of another group. "
"Also if `weights` is not numeric, does not give each value one finite, non-negative weight with a"
" positive total, or has an index other than that of `values`."
msgstr ""
"如果 `max_groups` 不是正整数， `alpha` 既不是 None 也不在 0 与 1 之间， `min_group_share` 不在 0 与 0.5 之间， "
"`smoothing` 不是有限正数， `values` 与 `target` 不是一维、索引或长度不一致， `special` 不是一维或含有缺失值或布尔值， `values` "
"除缺失值、特殊值和零权重取值外没有其他取值， `target` 含有 0 和 1 以外的标签、在参与拟合的行中缺少其中一类，或者合并后某组的标签会与另一组的标签相同。此外，如果 "
"`weights` 不是数值、没有为每个取值给出一个有限非负的权重、权重总和不为正，或其索引与 `values` 不同。"

msgid ":obj:`category_groups`"
msgstr ":obj:`category_groups`"

msgid "Pool rare categories without a target."
msgstr "不使用目标变量，归并稀有类别。"

msgid "Merge the bins of a numeric variable in the same way."
msgstr "用同样的方法合并数值变量的箱。"

msgid ""
"The chi-square statistic of two adjacent groups is the one described in `chimerge_edges`. Sorting"
" by WOE puts categories with similar event rates next to each other, so that each merge joins the"
" categories most alike. A category that is not merged is a group of its own, so with "
"``min_group_share=0`` and ``alpha=None`` a variable with at most ``max_groups`` categories keeps "
"all of them."
msgstr ""
"相邻两组的卡方统计量与 `chimerge_edges` 中说明的相同。按 WOE 排序会让事件率相近的类别彼此相邻，因此每次合并的都是最相似的类别。未被合并的类别单独成组，因此在 "
"``min_group_share=0`` 且 ``alpha=None`` 时，类别数不超过 ``max_groups`` 的变量会保留全部类别。"

msgid ""
"Ties go to the category that appears first, or that comes first among the categories of a "
"categorical input: categories with the same smoothed WOE keep that order, and of two pairs, or of"
" two small groups, whose statistics or totals agree to a relative 1e-10, the first one is merged."
" Each merge takes time in proportion to the number of groups, so the fit takes time in proportion"
" to the square of the number of categories, a few seconds for 20,000 of them."
msgstr ""
"并列时取先出现的类别；输入为分类型时取类别顺序在前的类别：平滑后 WOE 相同的类别保持这一顺序；两对相邻组或两个小组的统计量或总量在相对 1e-10 "
"以内相等时，合并前面的那一个。每次合并所需的时间与组数成正比，因此拟合所需的时间与类别数的平方成正比，2 万个类别需要几秒钟。"

msgid ""
"Each value is replaced with its group in `groups`, the dict returned by `category_groups` or "
"`chimerge_groups`, or one written or edited by hand. Missing values stay missing, so "
":func:`kivi.woe.woe_table` counts them as a group of their own."
msgstr ""
"每个取值都被替换为它在 `groups` 中所属的组； `groups` 是 `category_groups` 或 `chimerge_groups` 返回的 "
"dict，也可以手工编写或修改。缺失值保持缺失，因此 :func:`kivi.woe.woe_table` 把它们单独计为一组。"

msgid "One-dimensional category labels to assign."
msgstr "待分配的一维类别标签。"

msgid "**groups**"
msgstr "**groups**"

msgid "mapping"
msgstr "mapping"

msgid ""
"Group of each category, as a dict from category to group. Neither a category nor a group can be "
"missing."
msgstr "每个类别所属的组，即从类别到组的 dict。类别和组都不能是缺失值。"

msgid "**unseen**"
msgstr "**unseen**"

msgid "default \"raise\""
msgstr "默认 \"raise\""

msgid ""
"Group of the values whose category is not in `groups`, such as a new category: one of the groups "
"in `groups`, for example the group of rare categories. By default such values raise an error, so "
"that they never become missing values."
msgstr "类别不在 `groups` 中的取值（例如新类别）所归入的组，必须是 `groups` 中的某个组，例如稀有类别组。默认情况下这样的取值会引发错误，因此它们绝不会变成缺失值。"

msgid ""
"Categorical groups whose categories are the groups in the order in which they first appear in "
"`groups`. A Series input gives a Series with the same index and name."
msgstr "分类型的分组结果，类别为各组，按其在 `groups` 中首次出现的次序排列。输入为 Series 时返回 Series，索引和名称保持不变。"

msgid ""
"If `values` is not one-dimensional, `groups` is not a mapping or has a missing or non-scalar "
"category or group, `unseen` is neither ``\"raise\"`` nor one of the groups, or `unseen` is "
"``\"raise\"`` and some values are categories that `groups` does not map."
msgstr ""
"如果 `values` 不是一维， `groups` 不是映射或含有缺失或非标量的类别或组， `unseen` 既不是 ``\"raise\"`` 也不是其中某个组，或者 `unseen` 为 "
"``\"raise\"`` 而部分取值的类别不在 `groups` 中。"

msgid "Pool rare categories."
msgstr "归并稀有类别。"

msgid "Assign numeric values to bins."
msgstr "把数值分配到各箱。"

msgid ":obj:`kivi.woe.woe_transform`"
msgstr ":obj:`kivi.woe.woe_transform`"

msgid "Replace each group with its WOE."
msgstr "将每个分组替换为其 WOE。"

msgid ""
"Categories are matched by equality, as in :func:`kivi.woe.woe_transform`, so ``1`` and ``1.0`` "
"are the same category but ``\"1\"`` is another. The string ``\"raise\"`` always raises, so it "
"cannot name the group of unseen categories."
msgstr ""
"类别按相等关系匹配，与 :func:`kivi.woe.woe_transform` 相同，因此 ``1`` 和 ``1.0`` 是同一个类别，而 ``\"1\"`` 是另一个类别。字符串 "
"``\"raise\"`` 总是表示引发错误，因此不能用作未见类别所归入的组名。"

msgid "A category that the grouping does not know raises an error unless `unseen` names a group for it:"
msgstr "分组映射中没有的类别会引发错误，除非 `unseen` 为它指定了一个组："

msgid "Calibration"
msgstr "校准"

msgid ""
"Check and correct predicted probabilities. :func:`~kivi.calibration.prior_correction` and "
":func:`~kivi.calibration.corrected_intercept` correct them for the sampling of the development "
"data, :func:`~kivi.calibration.master_scale`, :func:`~kivi.calibration.fit_grade_pd` and "
":func:`~kivi.calibration.assign_grades` build a master scale and assign its grades, "
":func:`~kivi.calibration.calibration_table` and the tests count and test the grades, and "
":func:`~kivi.calibration.platt_fit` and :func:`~kivi.calibration.isotonic_fit` recalibrate a "
"score."
msgstr ""
"检查并校正预测概率。 :func:`~kivi.calibration.prior_correction` 和 "
":func:`~kivi.calibration.corrected_intercept` 按开发数据的抽样方式校正概率， "
":func:`~kivi.calibration.master_scale` 、 :func:`~kivi.calibration.fit_grade_pd` 和 "
":func:`~kivi.calibration.assign_grades` 构建主标尺并分配等级， :func:`~kivi.calibration.calibration_table` "
"和各项检验统计并检验各等级， :func:`~kivi.calibration.platt_fit` 和 :func:`~kivi.calibration.isotonic_fit` "
"重新校准评分。"

msgid "See :doc:`/user_guide/calibration` for examples on the bundled data."
msgstr "基于内置数据的示例见 :doc:`/user_guide/calibration` 。"

msgid ":py:obj:`prior_correction <kivi.calibration.prior_correction>`\\ \\(probability\\, \\*\\, ...\\)"
msgstr ":py:obj:`prior_correction <kivi.calibration.prior_correction>`\\ \\(probability\\, \\*\\, ...\\)"

msgid "Correct event probabilities for a development sample with another event rate."
msgstr "当开发样本的事件率与总体不同时，校正事件概率。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`corrected_intercept <kivi.calibration.corrected_intercept>`\\ \\(intercept\\, \\*\\, "
"...\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`corrected_intercept <kivi.calibration.corrected_intercept>`\\ \\(intercept\\, \\*\\, "
"...\\)"

msgid "Correct a logistic intercept for a development sample with another event rate."
msgstr "当开发样本的事件率与总体不同时，校正逻辑回归的截距。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`calibration_table <kivi.calibration.calibration_table>`\\ \\(groups\\, target\\, "
"probability\\, \\*\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`calibration_table <kivi.calibration.calibration_table>`\\ \\(groups\\, target\\, "
"probability\\, \\*\\)"

msgid "Compare the predicted and observed event rates of each group."
msgstr "比较每组的预测事件率与实际观测事件率。"

msgid ":py:obj:`binomial_test <kivi.calibration.binomial_test>`\\ \\(event\\, total\\, probability\\)"
msgstr ":py:obj:`binomial_test <kivi.calibration.binomial_test>`\\ \\(event\\, total\\, probability\\)"

msgid "Test whether each grade has more events than its probability predicts."
msgstr "检验每个等级的事件数是否多于其概率所预测的数量。"

msgid ":py:obj:`jeffreys_test <kivi.calibration.jeffreys_test>`\\ \\(event\\, total\\, probability\\)"
msgstr ":py:obj:`jeffreys_test <kivi.calibration.jeffreys_test>`\\ \\(event\\, total\\, probability\\)"

msgid "Test each grade's probability against its event rate with the Jeffreys prior."
msgstr "基于 Jeffreys 先验，检验每个等级的概率是否与其事件率相符。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`hosmer_lemeshow <kivi.calibration.hosmer_lemeshow>`\\ \\(event\\, total\\, "
"probability\\, \\*\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`hosmer_lemeshow <kivi.calibration.hosmer_lemeshow>`\\ \\(event\\, total\\, "
"probability\\, \\*\\)"

msgid "Test the calibration of all groups at once with the Hosmer-Lemeshow statistic."
msgstr "用 Hosmer-Lemeshow 统计量一次检验所有分组的校准情况。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`herfindahl_index <kivi.calibration.herfindahl_index>`\\ \\(counts\\, \\*\\[\\, "
"normalize\\]\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`herfindahl_index <kivi.calibration.herfindahl_index>`\\ \\(counts\\, \\*\\[\\, "
"normalize\\]\\)"

msgid "Measure how concentrated a portfolio is across grades."
msgstr "衡量资产组合在各等级间的集中程度。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`master_scale <kivi.calibration.master_scale>`\\ \\(probability\\, \\*\\[\\, boundary\\, "
"labels\\]\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`master_scale <kivi.calibration.master_scale>`\\ \\(probability\\, \\*\\[\\, boundary\\, "
"labels\\]\\)"

msgid "Build a master scale from the PD of each grade."
msgstr "根据每个等级的 PD 构建主标尺。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`fit_grade_pd <kivi.calibration.fit_grade_pd>`\\ \\(event\\, total\\, \\*\\[\\, "
"smoothing\\]\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`fit_grade_pd <kivi.calibration.fit_grade_pd>`\\ \\(event\\, total\\, \\*\\[\\, "
"smoothing\\]\\)"

msgid "Fit the PD of each grade to observed default rates, log-linear in the grade."
msgstr "按观测违约率拟合每个等级的 PD，其对数与等级呈线性关系。"

msgid ":py:obj:`assign_grades <kivi.calibration.assign_grades>`\\ \\(probability\\, scale\\)"
msgstr ":py:obj:`assign_grades <kivi.calibration.assign_grades>`\\ \\(probability\\, scale\\)"

msgid "Give each predicted PD the grade of a master scale."
msgstr "为每个预测 PD 指定主标尺上的等级。"

msgid ":py:obj:`platt_fit <kivi.calibration.platt_fit>`\\ \\(score\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, weights\\]\\)"
msgstr ":py:obj:`platt_fit <kivi.calibration.platt_fit>`\\ \\(score\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, weights\\]\\)"

msgid "Fit Platt scaling, a logistic curve from a score to event probabilities."
msgstr "拟合 Platt 缩放，即从评分到事件概率的逻辑曲线。"

msgid ":py:obj:`platt_predict <kivi.calibration.platt_predict>`\\ \\(score\\, slope\\, intercept\\)"
msgstr ":py:obj:`platt_predict <kivi.calibration.platt_predict>`\\ \\(score\\, slope\\, intercept\\)"

msgid "Turn scores into event probabilities with a fitted Platt scaling."
msgstr "用拟合好的 Platt 缩放把评分转换为事件概率。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`isotonic_fit <kivi.calibration.isotonic_fit>`\\ \\(score\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, "
"weights\\, ...\\]\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`isotonic_fit <kivi.calibration.isotonic_fit>`\\ \\(score\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, "
"weights\\, ...\\]\\)"

msgid "Fit an isotonic calibration, a step function from a score to event probabilities."
msgstr "拟合保序校准，即从评分到事件概率的阶梯函数。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`isotonic_predict <kivi.calibration.isotonic_predict>`\\ \\(score\\, edges\\, "
"probability\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`isotonic_predict <kivi.calibration.isotonic_predict>`\\ \\(score\\, edges\\, "
"probability\\)"

msgid "Give each score the probability of its band from an isotonic calibration."
msgstr "按保序校准，给每个评分赋予其所在分段的概率。"

msgid ""
"A model developed on a sample that over- or undersamples events predicts probabilities for that "
"sample. The correction rescales the odds so the probabilities refer to the population."
msgstr "如果开发样本对事件做了过采样或欠采样，模型预测的是该样本上的概率。本函数按比例调整几率，使概率对应总体。"

msgid "**probability**"
msgstr "**probability**"

msgid "Event probabilities from the model, between 0 and 1. Missing values stay missing."
msgstr "模型给出的事件概率，取值在 0 与 1 之间。缺失值保持缺失。"

msgid "**sample_rate**"
msgstr "**sample_rate**"

msgid "float"
msgstr "float"

msgid "Event rate of the development sample, strictly between 0 and 1."
msgstr "开发样本的事件率，严格介于 0 与 1 之间。"

msgid "**population_rate**"
msgstr "**population_rate**"

msgid "Event rate of the population, strictly between 0 and 1."
msgstr "总体的事件率，严格介于 0 与 1 之间。"

msgid "float, pandas.Series or numpy.ndarray"
msgstr "float、pandas.Series 或 numpy.ndarray"

msgid ""
"Corrected probabilities with the shape of `probability`. A Series input gives a Series with the "
"same index and name, and a scalar gives a float."
msgstr "校正后的概率，形状与 `probability` 相同。输入为 Series 时返回 Series，索引和名称保持不变；输入为标量时返回 float。"

msgid "If `probability` has values outside [0, 1], or a rate is not strictly between 0 and 1."
msgstr "如果 `probability` 含有 [0, 1] 以外的值，或者某个事件率不严格介于 0 与 1 之间。"

msgid ":obj:`corrected_intercept`"
msgstr ":obj:`corrected_intercept`"

msgid "Apply the same correction to a logistic intercept."
msgstr "对逻辑回归截距做同样的校正。"

msgid ":obj:`calibration_table`"
msgstr ":obj:`calibration_table`"

msgid "Compare predicted and observed event rates."
msgstr "比较预测事件率与观测事件率。"

msgid ""
"With sample event rate :math:`\\bar y` and population event rate :math:`\\tau`, the odds of every"
" probability are multiplied by"
msgstr "设样本事件率为 :math:`\\bar y` ，总体事件率为 :math:`\\tau` ，则每个概率的几率都乘以"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\\omega = \\frac{\\tau / (1 - \\tau)}{\\bar y / (1 - \\bar y)}, \\qquad\n"
"\\tilde p = \\frac{\\omega p}{\\omega p + 1 - p}."
msgstr ""
"\\omega = \\frac{\\tau / (1 - \\tau)}{\\bar y / (1 - \\bar y)}, \\qquad\n"
"\\tilde p = \\frac{\\omega p}{\\omega p + 1 - p}."

msgid ""
"This is the prior correction of King and Zeng [R4b74edbba56e-1]_. It changes the level of the "
"probabilities but not their order. For a logistic regression it equals adding :math:`\\ln "
"\\omega` to the intercept."
msgstr ""
"这是 King 和 Zeng [R4b74edbba56e-1]_ 提出的先验校正（prior correction）。它改变概率的水平，但不改变其排序。对逻辑回归而言，这等价于在截距上加上 "
":math:`\\ln \\omega` 。"

msgid "References"
msgstr "参考文献"

msgid ""
"G. King and L. Zeng, \"Logistic Regression in Rare Events Data\", Political Analysis, vol. 9, no."
" 2, pp. 137-163, 2001."
msgstr ""
"G. King and L. Zeng, \"Logistic Regression in Rare Events Data\", Political Analysis, vol. 9, no."
" 2, pp. 137-163, 2001."

msgid "[R4b74edbba56e-1]_"
msgstr "[R4b74edbba56e-1]_"

msgid ""
"The corrected model gives the probabilities of `prior_correction`: only the intercept changes, so"
" the coefficients and the order of applicants stay as they are."
msgstr "校正后的模型给出与 `prior_correction` 相同的概率：只有截距改变，系数和申请人的排序都保持不变。"

msgid "**intercept**"
msgstr "**intercept**"

msgid "Intercept of a logistic regression of the event."
msgstr "以事件为因变量的逻辑回归的截距。"

msgid "The intercept for the population, ``intercept + ln(omega)``."
msgstr "适用于总体的截距，即 ``intercept + ln(omega)`` 。"

msgid "If `intercept` is not a finite number, or a rate is not strictly between 0 and 1."
msgstr "如果 `intercept` 不是有限数值，或者某个事件率不严格介于 0 与 1 之间。"

msgid ":obj:`prior_correction`"
msgstr ":obj:`prior_correction`"

msgid "Apply the correction to probabilities."
msgstr "对概率做同样的校正。"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"King and Zeng [Rc67660983562-1]_ subtract :math:`\\ln\\left[\\frac{1 - \\tau}{\\tau} \\cdot "
"\\frac{\\bar y}{1 - \\bar y}\\right] = -\\ln \\omega` from the intercept; see `prior_correction`."
msgstr ""
"King 和 Zeng [Rc67660983562-1]_ 从截距中减去 :math:`\\ln\\left[\\frac{1 - \\tau}{\\tau} \\cdot "
"\\frac{\\bar y}{1 - \\bar y}\\right] = -\\ln \\omega` ；参见 `prior_correction` 。"

msgid "[Rc67660983562-1]_"
msgstr "[Rc67660983562-1]_"

msgid ""
"The groups are typically the grades of a master scale, formed by cutting the probabilities at "
"fixed edges, or score bands. Each row has the inputs of the calibration tests."
msgstr "分组通常是主标尺的等级（按固定边界切分概率得到），或者分数段。每一行都包含校准检验所需的输入。"

msgid "Grade or group labels. Missing values form a group."
msgstr "等级或分组标签。缺失值独立成组。"

msgid "Binary labels, with 1 indicating the event. A group, or the whole sample, may have no events."
msgstr "二分类标签，1 表示事件。某个分组乃至整个样本都可以没有事件。"

msgid ""
"Predicted event probabilities between 0 and 1. Series inputs must have identical indices; "
"otherwise the inputs are matched by position."
msgstr "预测的事件概率，取值在 0 与 1 之间。作为 Series 传入的输入，索引必须完全相同；否则按位置对应。"

msgid ""
"Non-negative weight of each observation, such as the inverse of its sampling rate, matched like "
"`target`. ``total`` and ``event`` are then sums of weights, the rate and the mean probability are"
" weighted, and groups whose weights sum to zero are left out."
msgstr "每个观测的非负权重，例如其抽样比例的倒数，对应方式与 `target` 相同。此时 ``total`` 和 ``event`` 为权重之和，事件率和平均概率都按权重计算，权重之和为零的组会被排除。"

msgid "pandas.DataFrame"
msgstr "pandas.DataFrame"

msgid ""
"One row per group with the number of observations ``total``, the number of events ``event``, the "
"observed ``event_rate`` and the mean predicted probability ``mean_probability``."
msgstr "每组一行，包括观测数 ``total`` 、事件数 ``event`` 、观测事件率 ``event_rate`` 以及平均预测概率 ``mean_probability`` 。"

msgid ""
"If the inputs are not one-dimensional, are empty, or their indices or lengths do not match, "
"`target` has labels other than 0 and 1, or `probability` has missing values or values outside [0,"
" 1]. Also if `weights` is not numeric, does not give each observation one finite, non-negative "
"weight with a positive total, or has an index other than that of `groups`."
msgstr ""
"如果输入不是一维、为空，或者索引或长度不一致， `target` 含有 0 和 1 以外的标签，或者 `probability` 含有缺失值或 [0, 1] 以外的值。此外，如果 "
"`weights` 不是数值、没有为每个观测给出一个有限非负且总和为正的权重，或者索引与 `groups` 不同。"

msgid ":obj:`binomial_test`"
msgstr ":obj:`binomial_test`"

msgid "Test whether a grade has more events than predicted."
msgstr "检验某个等级的事件数是否多于预测。"

msgid ":obj:`jeffreys_test`"
msgstr ":obj:`jeffreys_test`"

msgid "The Bayesian counterpart of the binomial test."
msgstr "二项检验的贝叶斯版本。"

msgid ":obj:`hosmer_lemeshow`"
msgstr ":obj:`hosmer_lemeshow`"

msgid "Test the calibration of all groups at once."
msgstr "一次检验所有分组的校准情况。"

msgid ":obj:`herfindahl_index`"
msgstr ":obj:`herfindahl_index`"

msgid "Measure how concentrated the grades are."
msgstr "衡量各等级的集中程度。"

msgid ""
"Groups are counted as in `kivi.woe.woe_table`. Rows follow the order of the categories when "
"`groups` is categorical, such as the result of ``pandas.cut``, with missing values last. "
"Otherwise they follow the order in which the groups first appear. Categories that are never "
"observed are omitted."
msgstr ""
"分组的计数方式与 `kivi.woe.woe_table` 相同。当 `groups` 为分类型（例如 ``pandas.cut`` "
"的结果）时，各行按类别顺序排列，缺失值排在最后。否则按分组首次出现的次序排列。从未出现的类别不会列出。"

msgid ""
"The binomial, Jeffreys and Hosmer-Lemeshow tests need whole numbers of observations and events, "
"so run them on an unweighted table."
msgstr "二项检验、Jeffreys 检验和 Hosmer-Lemeshow 检验需要整数的观测数和事件数，因此请在不加权的表上进行这些检验。"

msgid ""
"The one-sided exact binomial test assumes independent events. A small p-value means that the "
"probability underestimates the event rate of the grade."
msgstr "单侧精确二项检验假定各事件相互独立。p 值较小，说明该概率低估了这个等级的事件率。"

msgid "**event**"
msgstr "**event**"

msgid "Number of events in each grade."
msgstr "每个等级的事件数。"

msgid "**total**"
msgstr "**total**"

msgid "Number of observations in each grade, a positive whole number."
msgstr "每个等级的观测数，为正整数。"

msgid ""
"Predicted event probability of each grade, between 0 and 1, such as the ``mean_probability`` "
"column of `calibration_table`. The three inputs are broadcast together; Series inputs must have "
"identical indices."
msgstr ""
"每个等级的预测事件概率，取值在 0 与 1 之间，例如 `calibration_table` 的 ``mean_probability`` 列。三个输入会一起广播；作为 Series "
"传入的输入，索引必须完全相同。"

msgid ""
"One-sided p-values: a Series with the index of the Series inputs, a float for scalar inputs and "
"an array otherwise."
msgstr "单侧 p 值：有 Series 输入时返回 Series，索引与 Series 输入相同；输入为标量时返回 float；其他情况返回数组。"

msgid ""
"If the inputs cannot be broadcast or their Series indices differ, `total` is not a positive whole"
" number, `event` is not a whole number between 0 and `total`, or `probability` is outside [0, 1]."
msgstr "如果输入无法广播或 Series 的索引不一致、 `total` 不是正整数、 `event` 不是介于 0 与 `total` 之间的整数，或者 `probability` 超出 [0, 1]。"

msgid "The Bayesian counterpart of this test."
msgstr "本检验的贝叶斯版本。"

msgid "The counts and predicted probabilities of each grade."
msgstr "每个等级的计数和预测概率。"

msgid ""
"Under the null hypothesis the number of events :math:`D` among :math:`N` observations follows a "
"binomial distribution with probability :math:`p`. The p-value is"
msgstr "在原假设下， :math:`N` 个观测中的事件数 :math:`D` 服从概率为 :math:`p` 的二项分布。p 值为"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"P(D \\ge d) = \\sum_{k=d}^{N} \\binom{N}{k} p^k (1 - p)^{N - k}\n"
"= I_p(d, N - d + 1),"
msgstr ""
"P(D \\ge d) = \\sum_{k=d}^{N} \\binom{N}{k} p^k (1 - p)^{N - k}\n"
"= I_p(d, N - d + 1),"

msgid ""
"with the regularized incomplete beta function :math:`I`, and 1 when :math:`d = 0`. Correlated "
"defaults, as in an economic downturn, make the test reject more often than its nominal level "
"[Rb734fd528b30-1]_."
msgstr ""
"其中 :math:`I` 为正则化不完全贝塔函数；当 :math:`d = 0` 时 p 值为 1。违约之间存在相关性时（例如经济下行期），该检验的拒绝频率会高于名义水平 "
"[Rb734fd528b30-1]_ 。"

msgid ""
"Basel Committee on Banking Supervision, \"Studies on the Validation of Internal Rating Systems\","
" Working Paper No. 14, 2005."
msgstr ""
"Basel Committee on Banking Supervision, \"Studies on the Validation of Internal Rating Systems\","
" Working Paper No. 14, 2005."

msgid "[Rb734fd528b30-1]_"
msgstr "[Rb734fd528b30-1]_"

msgid ""
"The p-value is the posterior probability that the true event rate is at most the predicted "
"probability. A small p-value means that the probability underestimates the event rate of the "
"grade."
msgstr "p 值是真实事件率不超过预测概率的后验概率。p 值较小，说明该概率低估了这个等级的事件率。"

msgid "The frequentist counterpart of this test."
msgstr "本检验的频率学派版本。"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"With the Jeffreys prior Beta(1/2, 1/2), the posterior of the event rate after :math:`d` events "
"among :math:`N` observations is :math:`\\mathrm{Beta}(d + 1/2, N - d + 1/2)`, and the p-value is "
"its distribution function at the predicted probability :math:`p`:"
msgstr ""
"取 Jeffreys 先验 Beta(1/2, 1/2)，在 :math:`N` 个观测中出现 :math:`d` 个事件后，事件率的后验分布为 :math:`\\mathrm{Beta}(d "
"+ 1/2, N - d + 1/2)` ，p 值就是该分布在预测概率 :math:`p` 处的分布函数值："

msgid "I_p\\left(d + \\tfrac12, N - d + \\tfrac12\\right)."
msgstr "I_p\\left(d + \\tfrac12, N - d + \\tfrac12\\right)."

msgid ""
"This is the test that the European Central Bank asks for in the validation of PD models "
"[R73613bff641b-1]_. Unlike the binomial test, a grade without events still has a p-value below 1."
msgstr "这是欧洲央行在 PD 模型验证中要求使用的检验 [R73613bff641b-1]_ 。与二项检验不同，没有事件的等级其 p 值仍小于 1。"

msgid ""
"European Central Bank, \"Instructions for reporting the validation results of internal models: "
"IRB Pillar I models for credit risk\", 2019."
msgstr ""
"European Central Bank, \"Instructions for reporting the validation results of internal models: "
"IRB Pillar I models for credit risk\", 2019."

msgid "[R73613bff641b-1]_"
msgstr "[R73613bff641b-1]_"

msgid ""
"The statistic adds up the squared differences between observed and predicted events of each "
"group. A small p-value means that the probabilities do not match the observed event rates."
msgstr "该统计量把各组观测事件数与预测事件数之差的平方累加起来。p 值较小，说明概率与观测到的事件率不符。"

msgid "Number of events in each group."
msgstr "每组的事件数。"

msgid "Number of observations in each group, a positive whole number."
msgstr "每组的观测数，为正整数。"

msgid ""
"Mean predicted event probability of each group, strictly between 0 and 1, such as the "
"``mean_probability`` column of `calibration_table`. Series inputs must have identical indices."
msgstr ""
"每组的平均预测事件概率，严格介于 0 与 1 之间，例如 `calibration_table` 的 ``mean_probability`` 列。作为 Series "
"传入的输入，索引必须完全相同。"

msgid "**ddof**"
msgstr "**ddof**"

msgid "int, default 2"
msgstr "int，默认 2"

msgid "The chi-square distribution has as many degrees of freedom as there are groups, minus `ddof`."
msgstr "卡方分布的自由度等于分组数减去 `ddof` 。"

msgid "**statistic**"
msgstr "**statistic**"

msgid "The Hosmer-Lemeshow statistic."
msgstr "Hosmer-Lemeshow 统计量。"

msgid "**pvalue**"
msgstr "**pvalue**"

msgid "Its upper tail probability under the chi-square distribution."
msgstr "该统计量在卡方分布下的上尾概率。"

msgid ""
"If the inputs are not one-dimensional, have different lengths or Series indices, `total` is not a"
" positive whole number, `event` is not a whole number between 0 and `total`, `probability` is not"
" strictly between 0 and 1, or `ddof` is negative or leaves no degree of freedom."
msgstr ""
"如果输入不是一维、长度或 Series 索引不一致、 `total` 不是正整数、 `event` 不是介于 0 与 `total` 之间的整数、 `probability` 不严格介于 0 与"
" 1 之间，或者 `ddof` 为负数或使自由度不足 1。"

msgid "The counts and predicted probabilities of each group."
msgstr "每组的计数和预测概率。"

msgid "Test each grade on its own."
msgstr "逐个检验每个等级。"

msgid ""
"For :math:`g` groups with :math:`d_k` events among :math:`n_k` observations and mean predicted "
"probability :math:`\\bar p_k`,"
msgstr "对 :math:`g` 个分组，设第 :math:`k` 组有 :math:`n_k` 个观测、 :math:`d_k` 个事件，平均预测概率为 :math:`\\bar p_k` ，则"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "H = \\sum_{k=1}^{g} \\frac{(d_k - n_k \\bar p_k)^2}{n_k \\bar p_k (1 - \\bar p_k)},"
msgstr "H = \\sum_{k=1}^{g} \\frac{(d_k - n_k \\bar p_k)^2}{n_k \\bar p_k (1 - \\bar p_k)},"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"compared with a chi-square distribution with :math:`g - \\mathrm{ddof}` degrees of freedom. "
"Hosmer and Lemeshow [Rde8a0df3097b-1]_ form about ten groups of similar size from the sorted "
"probabilities of the sample the model was fitted on, which gives :math:`g - 2`. For probabilities"
" that were not fitted on the tested sample, such as a validation sample, use ``ddof=0`` "
"[Rde8a0df3097b-2]_."
msgstr ""
"并与自由度为 :math:`g - \\mathrm{ddof}` 的卡方分布比较。Hosmer 和 Lemeshow [Rde8a0df3097b-1]_ "
"将拟合模型所用样本的概率排序后分成约十个大小相近的组，此时自由度为 :math:`g - 2` 。如果概率不是在被检验的样本上拟合的（例如验证样本），请使用 ``ddof=0`` "
"[Rde8a0df3097b-2]_ 。"

msgid ""
"D. W. Hosmer and S. Lemeshow, \"Goodness of fit tests for the multiple logistic regression "
"model\", Communications in Statistics - Theory and Methods, vol. 9, no. 10, pp. 1043-1069, 1980."
msgstr ""
"D. W. Hosmer and S. Lemeshow, \"Goodness of fit tests for the multiple logistic regression "
"model\", Communications in Statistics - Theory and Methods, vol. 9, no. 10, pp. 1043-1069, 1980."

msgid ""
"D. W. Hosmer, S. Lemeshow and R. X. Sturdivant, \"Applied Logistic Regression\", 3rd ed., Wiley, "
"2013."
msgstr ""
"D. W. Hosmer, S. Lemeshow and R. X. Sturdivant, \"Applied Logistic Regression\", 3rd ed., Wiley, "
"2013."

msgid "[Rde8a0df3097b-1]_, [Rde8a0df3097b-2]_"
msgstr "[Rde8a0df3097b-1]_, [Rde8a0df3097b-2]_"

msgid ""
"The Herfindahl-Hirschman index is the sum of the squared shares of the grades. It is 1 when every"
" observation is in one grade and :math:`1/k` when :math:`k` grades are equally full."
msgstr "赫芬达尔-赫希曼指数（HHI）是各等级占比的平方和。所有观测都在同一等级时为 1； :math:`k` 个等级人数相同时为 :math:`1/k` 。"

msgid "**counts**"
msgstr "**counts**"

msgid ""
"Number of observations, or exposure, in each grade, such as the ``total`` column of "
"`calibration_table`."
msgstr "每个等级的观测数或敞口，例如 `calibration_table` 的 ``total`` 列。"

msgid "**normalize**"
msgstr "**normalize**"

msgid "bool, default False"
msgstr "bool，默认 False"

msgid "Rescale the index to run from 0 for equally full grades to 1 for a single full grade."
msgstr "重新缩放指数，使各等级人数相同时为 0，全部集中在一个等级时为 1。"

msgid "The index."
msgstr "指数值。"

msgid ""
"If `counts` is not one-dimensional, has negative or non-finite values or sums to zero, or "
"`normalize` is not a boolean or is set with fewer than two grades."
msgstr "如果 `counts` 不是一维、含有负值或非有限值、总和为零，或者 `normalize` 不是布尔值，或在少于两个等级时设置了 `normalize` 。"

msgid "The number of observations in each grade."
msgstr "每个等级的观测数。"

msgid "For grade shares :math:`s_i = c_i / \\sum_j c_j` of :math:`k` grades,"
msgstr "对 :math:`k` 个等级，设各等级占比为 :math:`s_i = c_i / \\sum_j c_j` ，则"

msgid ""
"\\mathrm{HHI} = \\sum_{i=1}^{k} s_i^2, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathrm{HHI}^* = \\frac{\\mathrm{HHI} - 1/k}{1 - 1/k}."
msgstr ""
"\\mathrm{HHI} = \\sum_{i=1}^{k} s_i^2, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathrm{HHI}^* = \\frac{\\mathrm{HHI} - 1/k}{1 - 1/k}."

msgid ""
"A rating scale whose observations crowd into a few grades differentiates risk poorly. Empty "
"grades count towards :math:`k`."
msgstr "如果观测集中在少数几个等级，评级标尺对风险的区分能力就较差。空等级也计入 :math:`k` 。"

msgid ""
"A master scale divides the PD range from 0 to 1 into grades, each with one PD. The bounds between"
" adjacent grades lie between their PDs, so that `assign_grades` can give every predicted PD its "
"grade."
msgstr "主标尺把从 0 到 1 的 PD 范围划分为若干等级，每个等级有一个 PD。相邻等级之间的界限位于两者的 PD 之间，因此 `assign_grades` 能为每个预测 PD 指定其等级。"

msgid ""
"PD of each grade, strictly increasing from the grade with the lowest risk and strictly between 0 "
"and 1. ``numpy.geomspace(first, last, grades)`` gives a geometric grid, and `fit_grade_pd` fits "
"the PDs to observed default rates."
msgstr ""
"每个等级的 PD，从风险最低的等级起严格递增，且严格介于 0 和 1 之间。 ``numpy.geomspace(first, last, grades)`` 给出几何网格， "
"`fit_grade_pd` 则按观测违约率拟合这些 PD。"

msgid "**boundary**"
msgstr "**boundary**"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "{\"geometric\", \"arithmetic\"}, default \"geometric\""
msgstr "{\"geometric\", \"arithmetic\"}，默认 \"geometric\""

msgid ""
"Bound between two adjacent grades: the geometric mean of their PDs, the midpoint on a logarithmic"
" scale, or their arithmetic mean."
msgstr "相邻两个等级之间的界限：取两者 PD 的几何平均数，即对数尺度上的中点，或取其算术平均数。"

msgid "**labels**"
msgstr "**labels**"

msgid ""
"Unique label of each grade, such as ``list(\"ABCDEFG\")``. By default the index of `probability` "
"if it is a Series, such as the result of `fit_grade_pd` for a table of grades; otherwise the "
"grades are numbered from 1."
msgstr ""
"每个等级唯一的标签，例如 ``list(\"ABCDEFG\")`` 。默认情况下，如果 `probability` 是 Series（例如 `fit_grade_pd` "
"对等级表的结果），则取其索引；否则从 1 开始为等级编号。"

msgid ""
"One row per grade, indexed by its label in an index named ``grade``, with the columns ``lower``, "
"``probability`` and ``upper``. The first grade starts at 0, the last one ends at 1, and each "
"grade ends where the next one starts."
msgstr ""
"每个等级一行，以其标签为索引（索引名为 ``grade`` ），包含 ``lower`` 、 ``probability`` 和 ``upper`` 三列。第一个等级从 0 开始，最后一个等级在"
" 1 结束，每个等级在下一个等级开始处结束。"

msgid ""
"If `probability` is empty, not one-dimensional or not real and numeric, has a missing value, is "
"not strictly increasing or is not strictly between 0 and 1, `boundary` is not recognized, or "
"`labels` (or the index of a Series `probability` without `labels`) does not give one unique, non-"
"missing label per grade."
msgstr ""
"如果 `probability` 为空、不是一维、不是实数数值、含有缺失值、不严格递增或不严格介于 0 和 1 之间， `boundary` 无法识别，或 `labels` （未给出 "
"`labels` 时为 Series `probability` 的索引）没有为每个等级给出一个唯一且非缺失的标签。"

msgid ":obj:`fit_grade_pd`"
msgstr ":obj:`fit_grade_pd`"

msgid "Fit the PD of each grade to observed default rates."
msgstr "按观测违约率拟合每个等级的 PD。"

msgid ":obj:`assign_grades`"
msgstr ":obj:`assign_grades`"

msgid "Give each predicted PD the grade of the scale."
msgstr "为每个预测 PD 指定标尺上的等级。"

msgid "Compare the grades with their observed default rates."
msgstr "比较各等级与其观测违约率。"

msgid ""
"For the PDs :math:`p_1 < \\dots < p_K` of the grades, the bound between grades :math:`k` and "
":math:`k + 1` is"
msgstr "设各等级的 PD 为 :math:`p_1 < \\dots < p_K` ，等级 :math:`k` 与 :math:`k + 1` 之间的界限为"

msgid ""
"b_k = \\sqrt{p_k \\, p_{k+1}} \\quad \\text{(geometric)}, \\qquad\n"
"b_k = \\frac{p_k + p_{k+1}}{2} \\quad \\text{(arithmetic)},"
msgstr ""
"b_k = \\sqrt{p_k \\, p_{k+1}} \\quad \\text{(geometric)}, \\qquad\n"
"b_k = \\frac{p_k + p_{k+1}}{2} \\quad \\text{(arithmetic)},"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"and grade :math:`k` holds the PDs in :math:`(b_{k-1}, b_k]`, with :math:`b_0 = 0` and :math:`b_K "
"= 1`. PDs of a master scale usually grow by a constant factor from grade to grade, so they are "
"evenly spaced on a logarithmic scale. The geometric bound is the midpoint on that scale: a PD "
"goes to the grade whose PD is nearer by ratio. The arithmetic mean, which the 0.2 versions of "
"kivi used, always lies above the geometric one, so each grade reaches further towards the grade "
"above it than towards the grade below. With PDs that double from grade to grade, a grade with PD "
":math:`p` then holds the PDs up to :math:`1.5 p` instead of :math:`\\sqrt 2 p \\approx 1.41 p`, "
"and its observed default rate tends to exceed its PD."
msgstr ""
"等级 :math:`k` 包含 :math:`(b_{k-1}, b_k]` 中的 PD，其中 :math:`b_0 = 0` ， :math:`b_K = 1` 。主标尺的 PD "
"通常逐级按固定倍数增长，因此在对数尺度上等距分布。几何界限正是该尺度上的中点：PD 归入按比值更接近的那个等级。kivi 0.2 "
"版本使用的算术平均数总是高于几何平均数，因此每个等级向上一个等级延伸得比向下一个等级更远。若 PD 逐级翻倍，PD 为 :math:`p` 的等级将包含直到 :math:`1.5 p` 的 "
"PD，而不是 :math:`\\sqrt 2 p \\approx 1.41 p` ，其观测违约率往往高于其 PD。"

msgid "The arithmetic mean of adjacent PDs gives higher bounds:"
msgstr "相邻 PD 的算术平均数给出更高的界限："

msgid "A Series gives its index as the labels:"
msgstr "Series 以其索引作为标签："

msgid ""
"The logarithm of the default rate is fitted as a straight line in the grade number, so the fitted"
" PDs grow by a constant factor from grade to grade. Pass the result to `master_scale` for the "
"bounds of the grades."
msgstr "把违约率的对数拟合为等级编号的直线，因此拟合的 PD 逐级按固定倍数增长。把结果传给 `master_scale` 即可得到各等级的界限。"

msgid ""
"Number of defaults in each grade, ordered from the grade with the lowest risk to the grade with "
"the highest. Weighted counts, such as those of a weighted `calibration_table`, must be on the "
"scale of observation counts, because `smoothing` is a number of defaults: on a smaller scale, "
"such as with weights that sum to 1, the smoothed rate of a grade without defaults is too high."
msgstr ""
"每个等级的违约数，从风险最低的等级排到风险最高的等级。加权计数（例如加权 `calibration_table` 中的计数）必须与观测数处于同一量级，因为 `smoothing` "
"是一个违约数：量级更小时（例如权重之和为 1），没有违约的等级经平滑后的违约率会过高。"

msgid ""
"Number of observations in each grade. A grade without observations is left out of the fit but "
"still gets a fitted PD, so pass a 0 for every grade of the scale that the data do not cover. "
"Series inputs must have identical indices."
msgstr "每个等级的观测数。没有观测的等级不参与拟合，但仍会得到拟合的 PD，因此对数据未覆盖的每个标尺等级都传入 0。Series 输入必须具有相同的索引。"

msgid ""
"Number of defaults that replaces a count of zero, whose logarithm is undefined, as "
"`kivi.woe.woe_table` replaces an empty cell."
msgstr "替换零计数（其对数无定义）的违约数，与 `kivi.woe.woe_table` 替换空单元格的方式相同。"

msgid "pandas.Series or numpy.ndarray"
msgstr "pandas.Series 或 numpy.ndarray"

msgid ""
"Fitted PD of each grade, strictly increasing and below 1: a Series with the index of the Series "
"inputs, an array otherwise."
msgstr "每个等级拟合的 PD，严格递增且小于 1：有 Series 输入时返回 Series，索引与 Series 输入相同；否则返回数组。"

msgid ""
"If the inputs are not one-dimensional, have different lengths or Series indices, are not finite "
"and non-negative, or `event` exceeds `total`; if fewer than two grades have observations, or "
"`smoothing` is not finite and positive or not smaller than the total of a grade without defaults."
" Also if the fitted PDs do not rise with the grade or reach 1."
msgstr ""
"如果输入不是一维、长度或 Series 索引不同、不是有限的非负数，或 `event` 超过 `total` ；如果有观测的等级少于两个，或 `smoothing` "
"不是有限的正数，或不小于某个没有违约的等级的总数。此外，如果拟合的 PD 不随等级上升或达到 1，也会抛出。"

msgid ":obj:`master_scale`"
msgstr ":obj:`master_scale`"

msgid "Build the scale from the fitted PDs."
msgstr "用拟合的 PD 构建标尺。"

msgid "Count the observations and defaults of each grade."
msgstr "统计每个等级的观测数和违约数。"

msgid ""
"With :math:`d_k` defaults among :math:`n_k` observations in grade :math:`k = 1, \\dots, K`, the "
"intercept :math:`a` and the slope :math:`b` minimize the weighted sum of squares"
msgstr ""
"设等级 :math:`k = 1, \\dots, K` 的 :math:`n_k` 个观测中有 :math:`d_k` 次违约，截距 :math:`a` 和斜率 :math:`b` "
"使如下加权平方和最小"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "\\sum_{k : n_k > 0} n_k \\left(\\ln \\frac{d_k}{n_k} - a - b k\\right)^2,"
msgstr "\\sum_{k : n_k > 0} n_k \\left(\\ln \\frac{d_k}{n_k} - a - b k\\right)^2,"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"where :math:`d_k` is replaced by `smoothing` when it is 0. The fitted PD of grade :math:`k` is "
":math:`e^{a + b k}`, and consecutive PDs have the constant ratio :math:`e^b`. The weights give "
"each observation the same influence, so integer counts weigh like repeated observations; the 0.2 "
"versions of kivi fitted the line by ordinary least squares, giving each grade the same influence "
"instead."
msgstr ""
"其中 :math:`d_k` 为 0 时用 `smoothing` 代替。等级 :math:`k` 的拟合 PD 为 :math:`e^{a + b k}` ，相邻 PD 之比恒为 "
":math:`e^b` 。这种权重让每个观测具有相同的影响，因此整数计数的权重与重复的观测相同；kivi 0.2 版本用普通最小二乘拟合这条直线，让每个等级具有相同的影响。"

msgid ""
"The fit extrapolates beyond the observed grades, so grades at the edges of the scale can get PDs "
"no observation supports. A default rate of zero says only that the grade is safe, not how safe: "
"the smoothed rate :math:`0.5 / n_k` stands in for it."
msgstr "拟合会外推到观测到的等级之外，因此标尺两端的等级可能得到没有任何观测支持的 PD。违约率为零只说明该等级安全，而不说明有多安全：用平滑后的违约率 :math:`0.5 / n_k` 代替它。"

msgid ""
"The grades are an ordered categorical of the labels of the scale, so `calibration_table` counts "
"them directly, in the order of the scale, for the tests of each grade."
msgstr "等级是标尺标签的有序分类变量，因此 `calibration_table` 可以直接按标尺的顺序统计各等级，供逐个等级的检验使用。"

msgid "One-dimensional predicted PDs between 0 and 1. Missing values stay missing."
msgstr "一维的预测 PD，介于 0 和 1 之间。缺失值保持缺失。"

msgid "**scale**"
msgstr "**scale**"

msgid ""
"Master scale, as returned by `master_scale`: one row per grade, indexed by unique labels, with "
"the columns ``lower`` and ``upper``. The first grade must start at 0, each grade where the one "
"before it ends, and the last one must end at 1."
msgstr ""
"主标尺，即 `master_scale` 的返回值：每个等级一行，以唯一的标签为索引，包含 ``lower`` 和 ``upper`` 两列。第一个等级必须从 0 "
"开始，每个等级从上一个等级结束处开始，最后一个等级必须在 1 结束。"

msgid ""
"Grade of each PD, an ordered categorical whose categories are the labels of the scale from the "
"lowest risk to the highest. A Series input gives a Series with the same index and name."
msgstr "每个 PD 的等级，为有序分类变量，其类别是标尺的标签，从风险最低到最高排列。输入为 Series 时返回 Series，索引和名称保持不变。"

msgid ""
"If `probability` is not one-dimensional, is not real and numeric, or has values outside [0, 1], "
"or `scale` is not a DataFrame with unique, non-missing labels and ``lower`` and ``upper`` columns"
" that cover [0, 1] with increasing, adjacent grades."
msgstr ""
"如果 `probability` 不是一维、不是实数数值或有取值超出 [0, 1]，或者 `scale` 不是这样的 DataFrame：具有唯一且非缺失的标签，其 ``lower`` 和 "
"``upper`` 列用递增且首尾相接的等级覆盖 [0, 1]。"

msgid "Build the scale."
msgstr "构建标尺。"

msgid "Compare the observed and predicted default rates of each grade."
msgstr "比较每个等级的观测违约率与预测违约率。"

msgid "Assign values to intervals given by their edges."
msgstr "按边界把取值分配到各区间。"

msgid ""
"Grade :math:`k` holds the PDs above its ``lower`` bound up to and including its ``upper`` bound, "
"as the intervals of ``pandas.cut`` are closed on the right, and a PD of 0 belongs to the first "
"grade, as with ``include_lowest=True``. The result equals ``pandas.cut(probability, edges, "
"labels=scale.index, include_lowest=True)`` for the edges ``[0, *scale[\"upper\"]]``; the "
"``upper`` column, not the PDs, decides the grade. The 0.2 versions of kivi gave a PD on a bound "
"the grade above it instead."
msgstr ""
"等级 :math:`k` 包含高于其 ``lower`` 界限、直到并包括其 ``upper`` 界限的 PD，因为 ``pandas.cut`` 的区间是左开右闭的；PD 为 0 "
"时属于第一个等级，与 ``include_lowest=True`` 相同。结果等于以 ``[0, *scale[\"upper\"]]`` 为边界的 "
"``pandas.cut(probability, edges, labels=scale.index, include_lowest=True)`` ；决定等级的是 ``upper`` "
"列，而不是各等级的 PD。kivi 0.2 版本则把恰好落在界限上的 PD 归入上面的等级。"

msgid ""
"The slope and intercept are fitted once, on a development or calibration sample, and "
"`platt_predict` applies them to the scores of any sample."
msgstr "斜率和截距只需在开发样本或校准样本上拟合一次，再由 `platt_predict` 应用到任何样本的评分上。"

msgid "**score**"
msgstr "**score**"

msgid ""
"Finite numeric scores, such as the log odds of a model, a PD or scorecard points. The direction "
"does not matter: a score that falls as the risk rises gets a negative slope."
msgstr "有限的数值评分，例如模型的对数几率、PD 或评分卡分值。方向无关紧要：风险越高评分越低时，斜率为负。"

msgid ""
"Binary labels, with 1 indicating the event. Both classes must be present. If `score` and `target`"
" are both pandas Series, they must have identical indices; otherwise they are matched by "
"position."
msgstr "二分类标签，1 表示事件。两个类别都必须出现。如果 `score` 和 `target` 都是 pandas Series，二者的索引必须完全相同；否则按位置对应。"

msgid ""
"Non-negative frequency weight of each observation, matched like `target`: a weight of 2 counts an"
" observation twice."
msgstr "每个观测的非负频数权重，对应方式与 `target` 相同：权重为 2 的观测计为两次。"

msgid "**slope**"
msgstr "**slope**"

msgid "Coefficient of the score in the log odds of the event."
msgstr "评分在事件对数几率中的系数。"

msgid "Log odds of the event at a score of 0."
msgstr "评分为 0 时事件的对数几率。"

msgid "kivi.selection.SeparationError"
msgstr "kivi.selection.SeparationError"

msgid ""
"If the score separates the classes, so that the slope that maximizes the likelihood is infinite. "
"It is a ValueError."
msgstr "如果评分把两类完全分开，以致使似然最大的斜率为无穷大。该异常属于 ValueError。"

msgid ""
"If the inputs are empty or not one-dimensional, their indices or lengths do not match, `target` "
"has a label other than 0 and 1 or lacks one of them, `score` is not real and numeric, has a "
"missing or infinite value or does not vary, or `weights` is invalid or leaves a class without "
"weight."
msgstr ""
"如果输入为空或不是一维的，索引或长度不一致，`target` 含有 0 和 1 以外的标签或缺少其中之一，`score` 不是实数数值、含有缺失值或无穷值或者没有变化，或者 `weights` "
"无效或使某一类没有权重。"

msgid "RuntimeWarning"
msgstr "RuntimeWarning"

msgid "If the fit does not converge."
msgstr "如果拟合未能收敛。"

msgid ":obj:`platt_predict`"
msgstr ":obj:`platt_predict`"

msgid "Apply the slope and intercept to scores."
msgstr "把斜率和截距应用到评分上。"

msgid ":obj:`isotonic_fit`"
msgstr ":obj:`isotonic_fit`"

msgid "A calibration that only assumes that the rate rises."
msgstr "只假定事件率随评分上升的校准。"

msgid ":obj:`kivi.selection.logistic_regression`"
msgstr ":obj:`kivi.selection.logistic_regression`"

msgid "The same kind of fit with standard errors."
msgstr "同类拟合，并给出标准误。"

msgid "The event probability at score :math:`s` is modelled as"
msgstr "评分为 :math:`s` 时的事件概率建模为"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "p(s) = \\frac{1}{1 + \\exp(-(a s + b))},"
msgstr "p(s) = \\frac{1}{1 + \\exp(-(a s + b))},"

msgid ""
"and the slope :math:`a` and the intercept :math:`b` maximize the log-likelihood, fitted by "
"iteratively reweighted least squares as in `kivi.selection.logistic_regression`. At the maximum, "
"the mean fitted probability equals the event rate of the sample, weighted with `weights`."
msgstr ""
"其中斜率 :math:`a` 和截距 :math:`b` 使对数似然最大，与 `kivi.selection.logistic_regression` "
"一样用迭代重加权最小二乘法拟合。在最大值处，拟合概率的均值等于样本的事件率（按 `weights` 加权）。"

msgid ""
"When the score is the log odds of a model, this is the logistic recalibration of Cox "
"[Rd112ce059dd4-2]_: a slope of 1 and an intercept of 0 mean that the model is calibrated on the "
"sample, and a slope below 1 that its probabilities are too extreme, as after overfitting."
msgstr ""
"当评分是某个模型的对数几率时，这就是 Cox 的逻辑再校准 [Rd112ce059dd4-2]_ ：斜率为 1、截距为 0 说明模型在该样本上是校准的；斜率小于 1 "
"则说明其概率过于极端，例如过拟合之后。"

msgid ""
"Platt [Rd112ce059dd4-1]_, and scikit-learn's ``CalibratedClassifierCV`` after him, replace the "
"labels 1 and 0 with :math:`(n_1 + 1) / (n_1 + 2)` and :math:`1 / (n_0 + 2)` for :math:`n_1` "
"events and :math:`n_0` non-events. This matters only in small samples, where it also keeps the "
"slope finite when the score separates the classes. Here the labels are used as they are, so a "
"separating score raises an error instead; `isotonic_fit` handles such a score."
msgstr ""
"Platt [Rd112ce059dd4-1]_ 以及沿用其做法的 scikit-learn ``CalibratedClassifierCV`` ，在有 :math:`n_1` 个事件和 "
":math:`n_0` 个非事件时，把标签 1 和 0 替换为 :math:`(n_1 + 1) / (n_1 + 2)` 和 :math:`1 / (n_0 + 2)` "
"。这只在小样本中有影响，在评分把两类完全分开时还能让斜率保持有限。这里直接使用原始标签，因此完全分开两类的评分会引发错误；这种评分可以改用 `isotonic_fit` 处理。"

msgid ""
"J. C. Platt, \"Probabilistic outputs for support vector machines and comparisons to regularized "
"likelihood methods\", in Advances in Large Margin Classifiers, MIT Press, pp. 61-74, 1999."
msgstr ""
"J. C. Platt, \"Probabilistic outputs for support vector machines and comparisons to regularized "
"likelihood methods\", in Advances in Large Margin Classifiers, MIT Press, pp. 61-74, 1999."

msgid ""
"D. R. Cox, \"Two further applications of a model for binary regression\", Biometrika, 45(3-4), "
"pp. 562-565, 1958."
msgstr ""
"D. R. Cox, \"Two further applications of a model for binary regression\", Biometrika, 45(3-4), "
"pp. 562-565, 1958."

msgid "[Rd112ce059dd4-1]_, [Rd112ce059dd4-2]_"
msgstr "[Rd112ce059dd4-1]_, [Rd112ce059dd4-2]_"

msgid ""
"The probabilities follow the logistic curve with the slope and intercept from `platt_fit`, so the"
" same calibration applies to the development sample, a validation sample and new applicants."
msgstr "概率沿着由 `platt_fit` 得到的斜率和截距所确定的逻辑曲线，因此开发样本、验证样本和新申请人都使用同一个校准。"

msgid "Numeric scores on the scale of the fit. Missing values give missing probabilities."
msgstr "与拟合时尺度相同的数值评分。缺失值对应的概率也为缺失。"

msgid "Coefficient of the score, as returned by `platt_fit`."
msgstr "评分的系数，即 `platt_fit` 的返回值。"

msgid "Intercept, as returned by `platt_fit`."
msgstr "截距，即 `platt_fit` 的返回值。"

msgid ""
"Event probabilities with the shape of `score`. A Series input gives a Series with the same index "
"and name, and a scalar gives a float."
msgstr "事件概率，形状与 `score` 相同。输入为 Series 时返回 Series，索引和名称保持不变；输入为标量时返回 float。"

msgid "If `score` is not real and numeric, or `slope` or `intercept` is not a finite number."
msgstr "如果 `score` 不是实数数值，或者 `slope` 或 `intercept` 不是有限数。"

msgid ":obj:`platt_fit`"
msgstr ":obj:`platt_fit`"

msgid "Fit the slope and intercept."
msgstr "拟合斜率和截距。"

msgid ":obj:`isotonic_predict`"
msgstr ":obj:`isotonic_predict`"

msgid "Apply an isotonic calibration."
msgstr "应用保序校准。"

msgid ""
"The probability is :math:`1 / (1 + \\exp(-(a s + b)))` for slope :math:`a`, intercept :math:`b` "
"and score :math:`s`, computed without overflow for extreme scores."
msgstr "对斜率 :math:`a` 、截距 :math:`b` 和评分 :math:`s` ，概率为 :math:`1 / (1 + \\exp(-(a s + b)))` ，对极端评分也不会溢出。"

msgid ""
"The score range is split into bands whose event rates rise with the score, so the calibration "
"assumes only that a higher score means a higher risk. Fit the bands once and apply them to the "
"scores of any sample with `isotonic_predict`."
msgstr "把评分范围划分为若干分段，各段的事件率随评分上升，因此这种校准只假定评分越高风险越高。分段只需拟合一次，再用 `isotonic_predict` 应用到任何样本的评分上。"

msgid "Finite numeric scores, such as a PD or the log odds of a model."
msgstr "有限的数值评分，例如 PD 或模型的对数几率。"

msgid ""
"Non-negative frequency weight of each observation, matched like `target`: a weight of 2 counts an"
" observation twice. Scores whose weights sum to zero are ignored."
msgstr "每个观测的非负频数权重，对应方式与 `target` 相同：权重为 2 的观测计为两次。权重之和为零的评分会被忽略。"

msgid "**increasing**"
msgstr "**increasing**"

msgid "bool, default True"
msgstr "bool，默认 True"

msgid ""
"Whether the probability rises with the score, as for a PD. Pass False for scorecard points, which"
" are higher for a lower risk."
msgstr "概率是否随评分上升，PD 就是如此。评分卡分值越高表示风险越低，因此对其传入 False。"

msgid ""
"Increasing band edges from ``-inf`` to ``inf``, like those of `kivi.binning.bin_edges`. The bands"
" are closed on the right, as in ``pandas.cut``, and each interior edge is the highest score of "
"the band below it."
msgstr ""
"从 ``-inf`` 到 ``inf`` 递增的分段边界，与 `kivi.binning.bin_edges` 的结果形式相同。各分段与 ``pandas.cut`` "
"一样为右闭区间，每个内部边界是其下方分段中的最高评分。"

msgid ""
"Event rate of each band, one fewer than `edges`. The rates are strictly increasing, or strictly "
"decreasing with ``increasing=False``."
msgstr "每个分段的事件率，个数比 `edges` 少一个。事件率严格递增；若 ``increasing=False`` ，则严格递减。"

msgid ""
"If the inputs are empty or not one-dimensional, their indices or lengths do not match, `target` "
"has a label other than 0 and 1 or lacks one of them, `score` is not real and numeric or has a "
"missing or infinite value, `weights` is invalid or leaves a class without weight, or `increasing`"
" is not a boolean."
msgstr ""
"如果输入为空或不是一维的，索引或长度不一致，`target` 含有 0 和 1 以外的标签或缺少其中之一，`score` 不是实数数值或含有缺失值、无穷值，`weights` "
"无效或使某一类没有权重，或者 `increasing` 不是布尔值。"

msgid "Apply the bands to scores."
msgstr "把分段应用到评分上。"

msgid "A calibration by a logistic curve."
msgstr "用逻辑曲线进行的校准。"

msgid "Compare the bands with the outcomes of another sample."
msgstr "将分段与另一个样本的实际结果进行比较。"

msgid ""
"Among all probabilities :math:`p_i` that rise with the score, isotonic regression minimizes "
":math:`\\sum_i w_i (y_i - p_i)^2`, and the same solution maximizes the binomial likelihood "
"[R79aaa79b7808-1]_. The pool-adjacent-violators algorithm finds it: each distinct score starts as"
" a band with its event rate, and adjacent bands are merged while the lower one has a rate at "
"least as high as the one above it. The probability of a band is then its pooled event rate. Tied "
"scores always share a band, and since bands with equal rates are merged too, no two adjacent "
"bands have the same probability."
msgstr ""
"在所有随评分上升的概率 :math:`p_i` 中，保序回归使 :math:`\\sum_i w_i (y_i - p_i)^2` 最小，同一个解也使二项似然最大 "
"[R79aaa79b7808-1]_ 。相邻违序合并算法（pool-adjacent-"
"violators）可以求出这个解：每个不同的评分起初各成一段，取其事件率；只要较低一段的事件率不低于其上方一段，就把这两段合并。每段的概率就是合并后的事件率。相同的评分总在同一段中；由于事件率相等的相邻分段也会合并，任意两个相邻分段的概率都不相同。"

msgid ""
"The outer edges are infinite, so a score below or above the fitted range gets the probability of "
"the lowest or highest band. A score between the observed scores of two bands falls into the upper"
" one, whose interval it belongs to; with ``increasing=False``, that is the band with the lower "
"risk. scikit-learn's ``IsotonicRegression`` interpolates linearly between the bands instead; both"
" give the same probability at every score of the fitted sample [R79aaa79b7808-2]_."
msgstr ""
"两端边界为无穷，因此低于或高于拟合范围的评分分别取最低或最高分段的概率。落在两个分段的观测评分之间的评分属于上方的分段，因为它在该段的区间内；若 ``increasing=False`` "
"，这就是风险较低的分段。scikit-learn 的 ``IsotonicRegression`` 则在分段之间线性插值；在拟合样本的每个评分上，两者给出的概率相同 "
"[R79aaa79b7808-2]_ 。"

msgid ""
"A band without events has probability 0 and a band with only events has probability 1; a score "
"that separates the classes gives just these two bands. Floor the probabilities where 0 is not "
"allowed, for example before `kivi.scorecard.pd_to_score`. The bands can also serve as the grades "
"of `calibration_table`, by cutting the scores at `edges`."
msgstr ""
"没有事件的分段概率为 0，只有事件的分段概率为 1；把两类完全分开的评分只会得到这两个分段。在不允许概率为 0 的场合（例如调用 `kivi.scorecard.pd_to_score` "
"之前），请为概率设定下限。按 `edges` 切分评分后，这些分段也可以作为 `calibration_table` 的等级。"

msgid ""
"M. Ayer, H. D. Brunk, G. M. Ewing, W. T. Reid and E. Silverman, \"An empirical distribution "
"function for sampling with incomplete information\", The Annals of Mathematical Statistics, "
"26(4), pp. 641-647, 1955."
msgstr ""
"M. Ayer, H. D. Brunk, G. M. Ewing, W. T. Reid and E. Silverman, \"An empirical distribution "
"function for sampling with incomplete information\", The Annals of Mathematical Statistics, "
"26(4), pp. 641-647, 1955."

msgid ""
"B. Zadrozny and C. Elkan, \"Transforming classifier scores into accurate multiclass probability "
"estimates\", Proceedings of the 8th ACM SIGKDD Conference, pp. 694-699, 2002."
msgstr ""
"B. Zadrozny and C. Elkan, \"Transforming classifier scores into accurate multiclass probability "
"estimates\", Proceedings of the 8th ACM SIGKDD Conference, pp. 694-699, 2002."

msgid "[R79aaa79b7808-1]_, [R79aaa79b7808-2]_"
msgstr "[R79aaa79b7808-1]_, [R79aaa79b7808-2]_"

msgid ""
"The bands come from `isotonic_fit` on a development or calibration sample, so the same step "
"function applies to every later sample."
msgstr "分段由 `isotonic_fit` 在开发样本或校准样本上得到，因此之后的每个样本都使用同一个阶梯函数。"

msgid "Increasing band edges from ``-inf`` to ``inf``, as returned by `isotonic_fit`."
msgstr "从 ``-inf`` 到 ``inf`` 递增的分段边界，即 `isotonic_fit` 的返回值。"

msgid "Probability of each band, between 0 and 1, one fewer than `edges`."
msgstr "每个分段的概率，介于 0 和 1 之间，个数比 `edges` 少一个。"

msgid ""
"If `score` is not real and numeric, `edges` is not increasing from ``-inf`` to ``inf``, or "
"`probability` does not give one value between 0 and 1 for each band."
msgstr "如果 `score` 不是实数数值， `edges` 不是从 ``-inf`` 到 ``inf`` 递增，或者 `probability` 没有为每个分段给出一个介于 0 和 1 之间的值。"

msgid "Fit the bands and their probabilities."
msgstr "拟合分段及其概率。"

msgid "Apply a Platt scaling."
msgstr "应用 Platt 缩放。"

msgid ""
"The bands are closed on the right, as in ``pandas.cut``: a score equal to an interior edge gets "
"the probability of the band below the edge. Since the outer edges are infinite, every score that "
"is not missing falls into a band."
msgstr "与 ``pandas.cut`` 一样，各分段为右闭区间：等于某个内部边界的评分取该边界下方分段的概率。由于两端边界为无穷，每个非缺失的评分都会落入某个分段。"

msgid "Compatibility"
msgstr "兼容性"

msgid ""
"This page states what a release of kivi may change and what it keeps: the versions it supports, "
"the public names, the layout of the tables it returns, its exception types and the files of "
":class:`~kivi.spec.BinningSpec`. The rules that every function follows, such as the order of the "
"arguments, are on :doc:`conventions`, and they are part of the API too."
msgstr ""
"本页说明 kivi 的一个版本可以改变什么、保留什么：支持的版本、公共名称、返回表格的结构、异常类型，以及 :class:`~kivi.spec.BinningSpec` "
"的文件。每个函数都遵循的规则（例如参数的顺序）见 :doc:`conventions` ，它们同样属于 API。"

msgid "Releases and deprecations"
msgstr "版本与弃用"

msgid "From version 1.0, kivi follows semantic versioning:"
msgstr "从 1.0 版起，kivi 遵循语义化版本："

msgid "A major release, such as 2.0, may remove or change any part of the public API."
msgstr "主版本（例如 2.0）可以移除或修改公共 API 的任何部分。"

msgid ""
"A minor release, such as 1.3, adds functions, arguments, table columns or format versions, and "
"may deprecate a part of the API."
msgstr "次版本（例如 1.3）会新增函数、参数、表格列或格式版本，并可能弃用 API 的某一部分。"

msgid "A patch release, such as 1.3.1, only fixes errors."
msgstr "补丁版本（例如 1.3.1）只修复错误。"

msgid ""
"A deprecated function, argument or behavior keeps working, with a ``FutureWarning`` that says "
"what to use instead, for the rest of the major version. It changes in the next major release, so "
"a deprecation of 1.4 takes effect in 2.0. The release notes list each deprecation under Changed."
msgstr ""
"已弃用的函数、参数或行为在该主版本的其余版本中继续可用，并发出说明替代用法的 ``FutureWarning`` 。它在下一个主版本中才改变，因此 1.4 中的弃用在 2.0 "
"中生效。版本说明在“变更”下列出每项弃用。"

msgid ""
"A fix of a wrong result can come in any release, minor or patch, even when code relies on the "
"wrong result. The release notes list such fixes under Fixed."
msgstr "对错误结果的修复可以出现在任何版本中，无论次版本还是补丁版本，即使已有代码依赖该错误结果。版本说明在“修复”下列出这类修复。"

msgid ""
"Before 1.0 a shorter rule applied: what 0.9 deprecated changed in 1.0, as "
":doc:`/release/migration` lists. To find the calls that a release will change, run the code or "
"its tests with ``FutureWarning`` turned into an error, as ``python -W error::FutureWarning`` or "
"``pytest -W error::FutureWarning`` do."
msgstr ""
"1.0 之前曾适用更短的规则：0.9 中弃用的内容已在 1.0 中改变，见 :doc:`/release/migration` 。要找出某个版本将会改变的调用，可以把 "
"``FutureWarning`` 变为错误来运行代码或其测试，例如 ``python -W error::FutureWarning`` 或 ``pytest -W "
"error::FutureWarning`` 。"

msgid "Supported versions"
msgstr "支持的版本"

msgid ""
"kivi supports Python 3.10 or newer, NumPy 1.24 or newer and pandas 2.0 or newer, and its tests "
"run on these oldest versions and on the newest releases. From 1.0, a minimum version rises only "
"in a minor release, and the notes of the release before it announce the change. A patch release "
"never raises a minimum."
msgstr ""
"kivi 支持 Python 3.10 或更高版本、NumPy 1.24 或更高版本，以及 pandas 2.0 或更高版本，其测试同时在这些最低版本和最新版本上运行。从 1.0 "
"起，最低版本只会在次版本中提高，并由前一个版本的版本说明预先公布。补丁版本从不提高最低版本。"

msgid "What is public"
msgstr "哪些属于公共 API"

msgid ""
"The names that a public module lists in its ``__all__``: :mod:`kivi.binning`, :mod:`kivi.woe`, "
":mod:`kivi.stability`, :mod:`kivi.univariate`, :mod:`kivi.selection`, :mod:`kivi.scorecard`, "
":mod:`kivi.metrics`, :mod:`kivi.calibration`, :mod:`kivi.strategy`, :mod:`kivi.reject_inference`,"
" :mod:`kivi.spec`, :mod:`kivi.monitoring`, :mod:`kivi.vintage`, :mod:`kivi.lifetime` and "
":mod:`kivi.datasets`. Each has a page in this reference that documents every such name. "
"``kivi.__version__`` is public too."
msgstr ""
"公共模块在其 ``__all__`` 中列出的名称，这些模块是 :mod:`kivi.binning` 、 :mod:`kivi.woe` 、 :mod:`kivi.stability` 、 "
":mod:`kivi.univariate` 、 :mod:`kivi.selection` 、 :mod:`kivi.scorecard` 、 :mod:`kivi.metrics` 、 "
":mod:`kivi.calibration` 、 :mod:`kivi.strategy` 、 :mod:`kivi.reject_inference` 、 :mod:`kivi.spec` "
"、 :mod:`kivi.monitoring` 、 :mod:`kivi.vintage` 、 :mod:`kivi.lifetime` 和 :mod:`kivi.datasets` "
"。本参考中每个模块都有一页，记录所有这些名称。 ``kivi.__version__`` 也是公共的。"

msgid ""
"The documented members of :class:`~kivi.spec.BinningSpec`: its fields, ``FORMAT_VERSION``, "
"``format_version`` and ``columns``, its methods, and its equality, hashing, pickling and "
"``dataclasses.replace``. :exc:`~kivi.selection.SeparationError`, which "
":func:`~kivi.calibration.platt_fit` raises as well, stays in :mod:`kivi.selection`."
msgstr ""
":class:`~kivi.spec.BinningSpec` 有文档的成员：它的字段、 ``FORMAT_VERSION`` 、 ``format_version`` 和 "
"``columns`` ，它的方法，以及它的相等比较、哈希、pickle 序列化和 ``dataclasses.replace`` 。 "
":exc:`~kivi.selection.SeparationError` 也会由 :func:`~kivi.calibration.platt_fit` 引发，但它仍位于 "
":mod:`kivi.selection` 。"

msgid ""
"The names of the arguments. A keyword is part of a call, so renaming an argument needs a "
"deprecation, even one that is usually passed by position."
msgstr "参数的名称。关键字是调用的一部分，因此重命名参数需要经过弃用，即使该参数通常按位置传入。"

msgid ""
"Everything else is private: the modules and names that start with an underscore, and the modules "
"that a public module imports, such as ``kivi.binning.np``. They can change in any release."
msgstr "其余一切都是私有的：以下划线开头的模块和名称，以及公共模块导入的模块，例如 ``kivi.binning.np`` 。它们可能在任何版本中改变。"

msgid ""
"Results that are pairs of parameters, such as the ``(factor, offset)`` of "
":func:`~kivi.scorecard.score_scaling`, the ``(slope, intercept)`` of "
":func:`~kivi.calibration.platt_fit`, the ``(edges, probability)`` of "
":func:`~kivi.calibration.isotonic_fit` and the ``(statistic, p_value)`` of "
":func:`~kivi.calibration.hosmer_lemeshow`, are tuples. A minor release may turn them into named "
"tuples, which unpack in the same way."
msgstr ""
"成对参数的结果是元组，例如 :func:`~kivi.scorecard.score_scaling` 的 ``(factor, offset)`` 、 "
":func:`~kivi.calibration.platt_fit` 的 ``(slope, intercept)`` 、 "
":func:`~kivi.calibration.isotonic_fit` 的 ``(edges, probability)`` ，以及 "
":func:`~kivi.calibration.hosmer_lemeshow` 的 ``(statistic, p_value)`` 。次版本可能把它们改为具名元组，其解包方式不变。"

