msgid "Errors and warnings"
msgstr "错误与警告"

msgid ""
"The exception types are public. Invalid input raises ``ValueError``, and a model that cannot be "
"fitted raises :exc:`~kivi.selection.SeparationError`, a subclass of ``ValueError``. A call that "
"Python itself rejects, such as one with a missing or an unknown argument, raises ``TypeError``."
msgstr ""
"异常类型是公共的。无效输入引发 ``ValueError`` ，无法拟合的模型引发 ``ValueError`` 的子类 "
":exc:`~kivi.selection.SeparationError` 。Python 本身会拒绝的调用（例如缺少参数或含有未知参数）引发 ``TypeError`` 。"

msgid ""
"The warning categories are public: a ``UserWarning`` means that a result differs from the "
"request, a ``RuntimeWarning`` that a fit did not converge, and a ``FutureWarning`` that a part of"
" the API is deprecated."
msgstr ""
"警告类别是公共的： ``UserWarning`` 表示结果与请求不同， ``RuntimeWarning`` 表示拟合未收敛， ``FutureWarning`` 表示 API "
"的某一部分已被弃用。"

msgid ""
"The wording of a message is not public and may change in any release. The rule that a message "
"names the argument and the value received stays."
msgstr "消息的措辞不是公共的，可能在任何版本中改变。消息指出参数名称和所收到的值，这一规则保持不变。"

msgid "Saved specifications"
msgstr "已保存的分箱方案"

msgid ""
":meth:`BinningSpec.to_json <kivi.spec.BinningSpec.to_json>` writes a file that later releases "
"read; :doc:`/user_guide/spec` describes its format."
msgstr ""
":meth:`BinningSpec.to_json <kivi.spec.BinningSpec.to_json>` 写出的文件可以被以后的版本读取； "
":doc:`/user_guide/spec` 说明其格式。"

msgid ""
"``format`` is always ``\"kivi.BinningSpec\"``, and ``format_version`` is an integer: 1 for a "
"specification without category groupings, 2 for one that groups a column."
msgstr "``format`` 总是 ``\"kivi.BinningSpec\"`` ， ``format_version`` 是整数：没有类别分组的分箱方案为 1，对某列分组的分箱方案为 2。"

msgid "Every 1.x release reads every format version written by kivi 0.6.0 or later."
msgstr "每个 1.x 版本都能读取 kivi 0.6.0 及以后版本写出的每种格式版本。"

msgid ""
"A specification is written in the lowest format version that can hold it, so a file that uses no "
"newer feature stays readable by older releases. A new format version only adds content, and "
"within a major version the meaning of an existing key never changes."
msgstr "分箱方案以能够容纳它的最低格式版本写出，因此不使用较新功能的文件仍可被较早的版本读取。新的格式版本只会增加内容，在同一个主版本内，已有键的含义从不改变。"

msgid ""
"A file with a newer format version raises ``ValueError`` and names the version, instead of being "
"read in part. Unknown keys raise as well, so a new key always comes with a new format version."
msgstr "格式版本较新的文件会引发指出该版本的 ``ValueError`` ，而不是只读取其中一部分。未知的键同样会引发错误，因此新键总是伴随新的格式版本出现。"

msgid ""
"``kivi_version`` records the release that fitted the specification and never changes how a file "
"is read. Equality and hashing include it, as they include every field, so a specification saved "
"by an earlier release differs from the same fit today; :ref:`spec-saving` shows how to compare "
"their content."
msgstr ""
"``kivi_version`` 记录拟合该分箱方案的版本，从不影响文件的读取方式。相等比较和哈希像包含每个字段一样包含它，因此由较早版本保存的分箱方案与今天的同一拟合结果不相等； :ref"
":`spec-saving` 说明如何比较二者的内容。"

msgid ""
"Encoding reads only the ``bin`` and ``woe`` of each table row. The other columns describe the fit"
" and are loaded as written."
msgstr "编码只读取表格每行的 ``bin`` 和 ``woe`` 。其他列描述拟合结果，按写入时的内容加载。"

msgid ""
"The tests of kivi keep files written by 0.6.0, in format version 1, and by 0.8.0, in format "
"version 2, and check that each loads and encodes a fixed sample exactly as the release that wrote"
" it did, and that it matches a fresh fit apart from ``kivi_version`` and the rounding of the last"
" digits."
msgstr ""
"kivi 的测试保存了由 0.6.0 写出的格式版本 1 文件和由 0.8.0 写出的格式版本 2 文件，并检查每个文件都能加载、对一个固定样本的编码与写出它的版本完全相同，并且除 "
"``kivi_version`` 和末位数字的舍入外与重新拟合的结果一致。"

msgid "Conventions"
msgstr "约定"

msgid ""
"Every public function of kivi follows the rules on this page. The module pages and the guides "
"take them for granted, and the docstrings mention only where a function departs from them or adds"
" to them."
msgstr "kivi 的每个公共函数都遵守本页的规则。模块页面和各篇指南默认这些规则成立，docstring 只说明某个函数与之不同或在其之外补充的地方。"

msgid "Imports"
msgstr "导入"

msgid ""
"kivi has no top-level imports. Import each function from its module, as in ``from kivi.woe import"
" woe_table``; each module has its own page in this reference."
msgstr "kivi 没有顶层导入。请从各自所在的模块导入函数，例如 ``from kivi.woe import woe_table`` ；每个模块在本参考中都有自己的页面。"

msgid ""
"Only the names that a module lists in ``__all__`` are public. :doc:`compatibility` says which of "
"them a release may change, and how it announces the change."
msgstr "只有模块在 ``__all__`` 中列出的名称是公共的。 :doc:`compatibility` 说明版本可以改变其中哪些名称，以及如何预先公布这种改变。"

msgid "Arguments"
msgstr "参数"

msgid ""
"The data come first and the target follows them, as in ``woe_table(groups, target)``, "
"``roc_auc(score, target)``, ``stepwise(X, target)`` and ``fit_spec(frame, target)``. A function "
"with several data arguments takes all of them before the target, as ``swap_set(current, new, "
"target)`` does, and a predicted probability comes after the target, as in "
"``calibration_table(groups, target, probability)``. scikit-learn's metrics take the target first,"
" so check the order when porting code from them."
msgstr ""
"数据在前，目标变量在数据之后，例如 ``woe_table(groups, target)`` 、 ``roc_auc(score, target)`` 、 ``stepwise(X, "
"target)`` 和 ``fit_spec(frame, target)`` 。有多个数据参数的函数先接收全部数据参数，再接收目标变量，例如 ``swap_set(current, new, "
"target)`` ；预测概率放在目标变量之后，例如 ``calibration_table(groups, target, probability)`` 。scikit-learn "
"的指标函数把目标变量放在前面，从那里移植代码时请检查参数顺序。"

msgid ""
"Data that describe other observations, such as the rejected applicants, follow the data and the "
"target of the main sample, as in ``parceling(score, target, reject_score)`` and in "
"``reweighting(score, reject_score)``, which has no target."
msgstr ""
"描述其他观测的数据（例如被拒绝的申请人）位于主样本的数据和目标变量之后，例如 ``parceling(score, target, reject_score)`` ，以及没有目标变量的 "
"``reweighting(score, reject_score)`` 。"

msgid ""
"``X`` is a numeric model matrix, as in :func:`~kivi.selection.stepwise`, "
":func:`~kivi.selection.logistic_regression`, :func:`~kivi.selection.vif` and "
":func:`~kivi.selection.correlation_filter`. ``frame`` holds raw columns, as in "
":func:`~kivi.spec.fit_spec`, :func:`~kivi.univariate.profile_table` and :meth:`BinningSpec.cut "
"<kivi.spec.BinningSpec.cut>`, and ``woe`` is the matrix of WOE values that "
":func:`~kivi.scorecard.woe_to_points` turns into points."
msgstr ""
"``X`` 是数值型模型矩阵，例如 :func:`~kivi.selection.stepwise` 、 :func:`~kivi.selection.logistic_regression` "
"、 :func:`~kivi.selection.vif` 和 :func:`~kivi.selection.correlation_filter` 中的 ``X`` 。 ``frame`` "
"包含原始列，例如 :func:`~kivi.spec.fit_spec` 、 :func:`~kivi.univariate.profile_table` 和 "
":meth:`BinningSpec.cut <kivi.spec.BinningSpec.cut>` 中的 ``frame`` ； ``woe`` 是 "
":func:`~kivi.scorecard.woe_to_points` 转换为分数的 WOE 值矩阵。"

msgid ""
"A predicted probability of an event, such as a PD, is always called ``probability``, as in "
"``brier_score(probability, target)``, ``calibration_table(groups, target, probability)`` and "
"``expected_loss(probability, lgd, ead)``. What a ``score`` is depends on the module; see :ref"
":`conventions-scores`. A second probability is named after its meaning, as "
"``origination_probability`` in :func:`~kivi.lifetime.significant_increase`."
msgstr ""
"事件的预测概率（例如 PD）一律称为 ``probability`` ，例如 ``brier_score(probability, target)`` 、 "
"``calibration_table(groups, target, probability)`` 和 ``expected_loss(probability, lgd, ead)`` 。 "
"``score`` 的含义因模块而异，见 :ref:`conventions-scores` 。第二个概率参数按其含义命名，例如 "
":func:`~kivi.lifetime.significant_increase` 中的 ``origination_probability`` 。"

msgid ""
"An option with the same meaning has the same name in every module, such as ``bins``, ``special``,"
" ``smoothing``, ``unseen`` and ``weights``. ``level`` is the confidence level of an interval, a "
"number strictly between 0 and 1 that defaults to 0.95, as in "
":func:`~kivi.metrics.roc_auc_interval`."
msgstr ""
"含义相同的选项在各个模块中同名，例如 ``bins`` 、 ``special`` 、 ``smoothing`` 、 ``unseen`` 和 ``weights`` 。 ``level`` "
"是区间的置信水平，为严格介于 0 和 1 之间的数，默认 0.95，例如 :func:`~kivi.metrics.roc_auc_interval` 。"

msgid ""
"``bins`` defaults to 5 for the bins of a variable, as in :func:`~kivi.binning.bin_edges`, "
":func:`~kivi.spec.fit_spec` and :func:`~kivi.univariate.profile_table`, and to 10 for the bands "
"of a score, as in :func:`~kivi.metrics.gains_table`, :func:`~kivi.monitoring.monitoring_table`, "
":func:`~kivi.reject_inference.parceling` and :func:`~kivi.reject_inference.reweighting`. The "
"``cutoffs`` of :func:`~kivi.strategy.cutoff_table` default to 10 bands as well."
msgstr ""
"对变量分箱时 ``bins`` 默认为 5，例如 :func:`~kivi.binning.bin_edges` 、 :func:`~kivi.spec.fit_spec` 和 "
":func:`~kivi.univariate.profile_table` ；对评分划分区段时默认为 10，例如 :func:`~kivi.metrics.gains_table` 、 "
":func:`~kivi.monitoring.monitoring_table` 、 :func:`~kivi.reject_inference.parceling` 和 "
":func:`~kivi.reject_inference.reweighting` 。 :func:`~kivi.strategy.cutoff_table` 的 ``cutoffs`` "
"同样默认为 10 个区段。"

msgid ""
"``special`` is a list of codes for a function of one variable, and a dict by column for "
":func:`~kivi.spec.fit_spec` and :func:`~kivi.univariate.profile_table`, which reject a list."
msgstr ""
"对单个变量的函数， ``special`` 是特殊值的列表；对 :func:`~kivi.spec.fit_spec` 和 "
":func:`~kivi.univariate.profile_table` ，它是按列给出的 dict，这两个函数拒绝列表。"

msgid ""
"Some options have similar names but different meanings. The ``min_share`` of "
":func:`~kivi.binning.category_groups` is the share below which a category counts as rare, while "
"the ``min_bin_share`` of :func:`~kivi.binning.tree_edges` and the ``min_group_share`` of "
":func:`~kivi.binning.chimerge_groups` set the smallest bin or group of the result. Only "
":func:`~kivi.binning.monotonic_edges` accepts ``max_bins=None``, which merges bins only until the"
" WOE is monotonic. ``unseen`` says what to do with a group that a table lacks and defaults to "
"``\"raise\"``, while ``unseen_points`` is a number of points or None."
msgstr ""
"有些选项名称相近但含义不同。 :func:`~kivi.binning.category_groups` 的 ``min_share`` 是低于它即视为稀有类别的占比，而 "
":func:`~kivi.binning.tree_edges` 的 ``min_bin_share`` 和 :func:`~kivi.binning.chimerge_groups` 的 "
"``min_group_share`` 设定结果中最小的分箱或分组。只有 :func:`~kivi.binning.monotonic_edges` 接受 ``max_bins=None`` "
"，此时只合并分箱直到 WOE 单调。 ``unseen`` 说明如何处理表中没有的分组，默认为 ``\"raise\"`` ；而 ``unseen_points`` 是一个分数值或 None。"

msgid ""
"A reference that could be read in two ways has one argument for each. The functions of "
":mod:`kivi.monitoring` take either ``reference_period``, a label of the period argument, or a "
"reference sample in ``reference_score`` or ``reference_groups``, and raise unless exactly one is "
"given."
msgstr ""
"可能有两种理解的参考对象会分成两个参数。 :mod:`kivi.monitoring` 的函数要么接收 ``reference_period`` （期间参数中的一个标签），要么接收 "
"``reference_score`` 或 ``reference_groups`` 中的基准样本；两者必须恰好给出一个，否则引发错误。"

msgid ""
"The data, and the fitted results that a function applies, such as the edges of "
":func:`~kivi.binning.cut` or the table of :func:`~kivi.woe.woe_transform`, are positional "
"arguments. Every option after them is keyword-only. The number of bins of "
":func:`~kivi.binning.bin_edges` is the one option that can also be passed by position:"
msgstr ""
"数据以及函数要应用的拟合结果（例如 :func:`~kivi.binning.cut` 的边界或 :func:`~kivi.woe.woe_transform` "
"的表）是位置参数。其后的所有选项都仅限关键字。 :func:`~kivi.binning.bin_edges` 的箱数是唯一也可以按位置传入的选项："

msgid "Inputs and results"
msgstr "输入与结果"

msgid ""
"A one-dimensional input is array_like: a list, a NumPy array or a pandas Series. A function that "
"works on several columns at once, such as :func:`~kivi.selection.stepwise` or "
":func:`~kivi.spec.fit_spec`, takes a DataFrame."
msgstr ""
"一维输入是类数组（array_like）：列表、NumPy 数组或 pandas Series。同时处理多列的函数，例如 :func:`~kivi.selection.stepwise` 或 "
":func:`~kivi.spec.fit_spec` ，接收 DataFrame。"

msgid ""
"The binning functions read their ``values`` with ``pandas.to_numeric``, so strings of numbers and"
" booleans count as numbers there. Special codes must not be booleans, because ``True == 1``, and "
":func:`~kivi.spec.fit_spec` groups a boolean column as categorical instead of binning it."
msgstr ""
"分箱函数用 ``pandas.to_numeric`` 读取 ``values`` ，因此数字字符串和布尔值在那里都算作数值。特殊值不能是布尔值，因为 ``True == 1`` ；而 "
":func:`~kivi.spec.fit_spec` 把布尔列当作类别列分组，而不是对其分箱。"

msgid ""
"A result with one value per input value is shaped like the input. A Series gives a Series with "
"the same index and name, other array_like input gives a NumPy array, and a single number gives a "
"float. :func:`~kivi.binning.cut` and :func:`~kivi.calibration.assign_grades` return groups, so "
"for input other than a Series they return a ``pandas.Categorical``:"
msgstr ""
"每个输入值对应一个结果值时，结果的形状与输入相同。传入 Series 得到索引和名称都相同的 Series，传入其他类数组得到 NumPy 数组，传入单个数得到 float。 "
":func:`~kivi.binning.cut` 和 :func:`~kivi.calibration.assign_grades` 返回的是分组，因此输入不是 Series 时，它们返回 "
"``pandas.Categorical`` ："

msgid ""
"A Series result takes the name of the first data argument, as the results of "
":func:`~kivi.scorecard.pd_to_score`, :func:`~kivi.binning.cut` and "
":func:`~kivi.woe.woe_transform` do, so the scores of a Series named ``pd`` are named ``pd`` too. "
"A result that is a new quantity is named after it: :func:`~kivi.woe.woe` names its result "
"``woe``, :func:`~kivi.strategy.expected_loss` ``expected_loss``, "
":func:`~kivi.lifetime.significant_increase` ``significant_increase``, "
":func:`~kivi.lifetime.assign_stages` ``stage`` and :func:`~kivi.reject_inference.reweighting` "
"``weight``."
msgstr ""
"Series 结果采用第一个数据参数的名称， :func:`~kivi.scorecard.pd_to_score` 、 :func:`~kivi.binning.cut` 和 "
":func:`~kivi.woe.woe_transform` 的结果都是如此，因此由名为 ``pd`` 的 Series 算出的评分也名为 ``pd`` 。表示新量的结果以该量命名： "
":func:`~kivi.woe.woe` 把结果命名为 ``woe`` ， :func:`~kivi.strategy.expected_loss` 命名为 ``expected_loss``"
" ， :func:`~kivi.lifetime.significant_increase` 命名为 ``significant_increase`` ， "
":func:`~kivi.lifetime.assign_stages` 命名为 ``stage`` ， :func:`~kivi.reject_inference.reweighting` "
"命名为 ``weight`` 。"

msgid ""
"Some inputs must be one-dimensional even for one exposure. "
":func:`~kivi.lifetime.significant_increase` and :func:`~kivi.lifetime.assign_stages` raise for a "
"single number, and :func:`~kivi.lifetime.expected_credit_loss` takes one row per account, so pass"
" the single curve of :func:`~kivi.lifetime.convert_pd` as ``curve[None, :]``."
msgstr ""
"有些输入即使只有一个敞口也必须是一维的。 :func:`~kivi.lifetime.significant_increase` 和 "
":func:`~kivi.lifetime.assign_stages` 对单个数值会引发错误，而 :func:`~kivi.lifetime.expected_credit_loss` "
"要求每个账户一行，因此请把 :func:`~kivi.lifetime.convert_pd` 返回的单条曲线以 ``curve[None, :]`` 传入。"

msgid ""
"Series that describe the same observations, such as the data, the target, the probabilities and "
"the weights, must have identical indices; they are not aligned. Any other combination of these "
"inputs is matched by position. Inputs that describe other observations, such as the two samples "
"of :func:`~kivi.stability.psi_table` or the rejected applicants of "
":func:`~kivi.reject_inference.parceling`, can have any index. Counts per group, as in "
":func:`~kivi.woe.woe`, :func:`~kivi.woe.iv` and :func:`~kivi.stability.psi`, describe the same "
"groups, so two Series of counts must have identical indices too."
msgstr ""
"描述同一批观测的 Series，例如数据、目标变量、概率和权重，必须具有完全相同的索引；它们不会被对齐。这些输入的其他任何组合都按位置对应。描述其他观测的输入，例如 "
":func:`~kivi.stability.psi_table` 的两个样本或 :func:`~kivi.reject_inference.parceling` "
"的拒绝申请人，可以使用任意索引。每组的计数，例如 :func:`~kivi.woe.woe` 、 :func:`~kivi.woe.iv` 和 "
":func:`~kivi.stability.psi` 的输入，描述的是同一批分组，因此两个计数 Series 也必须具有完全相同的索引。"

msgid ""
"Tables are DataFrames. A table of the groups passed in, such as that of "
":func:`~kivi.woe.woe_table`, is indexed by the group labels, in an index named ``bin``. Other "
"tables name the index after their rows, such as ``variable``, ``grade``, ``cutoff``, "
"``threshold``, ``statistic``, ``period``, ``cohort``, ``state``, ``stage`` or ``before``, and "
"name their columns when these are labels too, such as ``horizon``, ``after`` or "
"``month_on_book``. :doc:`compatibility` lists the index and the columns of every table. A total "
"is the sum of a column, such as ``woe_table(groups, target)[\"iv\"].sum()``."
msgstr ""
"表格是 DataFrame。由传入的分组构成的表格（例如 :func:`~kivi.woe.woe_table` 的结果）以分组标签为索引，索引名为 ``bin`` "
"。其他表格按其行的含义命名索引，例如 ``variable`` 、 ``grade`` 、 ``cutoff`` 、 ``threshold`` 、 ``statistic`` 、 "
"``period`` 、 ``cohort`` 、 ``state`` 、 ``stage`` 或 ``before`` ；当列也是标签时还会为列命名，例如 ``horizon`` 、 "
"``after`` 或 ``month_on_book`` 。 :doc:`compatibility` 列出了每个表格的索引和列。合计是某一列的和，例如 ``woe_table(groups,"
" target)[\"iv\"].sum()`` 。"

msgid ""
"Named statistics come back as a Series or a DataFrame, as from :func:`~kivi.metrics.delong_test` "
"and :func:`~kivi.metrics.roc_auc_interval`. Parameters that another function applies come back as"
" a tuple, such as the edges and the probabilities that :func:`~kivi.calibration.isotonic_fit` "
"returns for :func:`~kivi.calibration.isotonic_predict`, and so does the statistic and p-value "
"pair of :func:`~kivi.calibration.hosmer_lemeshow`."
msgstr ""
"具名的统计量以 Series 或 DataFrame 返回，例如 :func:`~kivi.metrics.delong_test` 和 "
":func:`~kivi.metrics.roc_auc_interval` 。供另一个函数使用的参数以元组返回，例如 "
":func:`~kivi.calibration.isotonic_fit` 为 :func:`~kivi.calibration.isotonic_predict` 返回的边界和概率； "
":func:`~kivi.calibration.hosmer_lemeshow` 的统计量与 p 值也以元组返回。"

msgid ""
"Functions do not modify their inputs. Random draws come from a local generator seeded by ``rng``,"
" so they never change NumPy's global state, and the same seed gives the same result."
msgstr "函数不会修改输入。随机抽样来自以 ``rng`` 为种子的局部生成器，因此不会改变 NumPy 的全局状态，相同的种子给出相同的结果。"

msgid ""
"``rng`` takes what ``numpy.random.default_rng`` takes, such as None, an integer, a "
"``SeedSequence`` or a ``Generator``. A ``Generator`` is used and advanced rather than copied, so "
"two calls with the same ``Generator`` give different draws, while two calls with the same integer"
" agree."
msgstr ""
"``rng`` 接受 ``numpy.random.default_rng`` 所接受的值，例如 None、整数、 ``SeedSequence`` 或 ``Generator`` 。 "
"``Generator`` 会被直接使用并推进，而不是被复制，因此用同一个 ``Generator`` 的两次调用抽样结果不同，而用同一个整数的两次调用结果一致。"

msgid "Targets, scores and probabilities"
msgstr "目标变量、评分与概率"

msgid ""
"A target is 1 for an event, such as a default, and 0 for a non-event. Any other label, and a "
"missing label, raises an error. :func:`~kivi.strategy.swap_set` and "
":func:`~kivi.monitoring.monitoring_table` are the exceptions: they read a missing label as an "
"outcome that is not known, such as that of a declined applicant or of a loan whose outcome window"
" has not ended."
msgstr ""
"目标变量中 1 表示事件（例如违约），0 表示非事件。其他任何标签以及缺失标签都会引发错误。 :func:`~kivi.strategy.swap_set` 和 "
":func:`~kivi.monitoring.monitoring_table` 是例外：它们把缺失标签视为结果未知，例如被拒申请人的结果，或表现期尚未结束的贷款的结果。"

msgid ""
"The ``bad`` argument of :func:`~kivi.vintage.vintage_table` is the status of a loan in a month, "
"such as being 90 days past due, rather than the target of an observation. It takes booleans or 0 "
"and 1, without missing values."
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.vintage.vintage_table` 的 ``bad`` 参数是贷款在某个月的状态（例如逾期 90 天），而不是某个观测的目标变量。它接受布尔值或 0 和 "
"1，不能有缺失值。"

msgid ""
"In :mod:`kivi.metrics`, :mod:`kivi.monitoring` and :mod:`kivi.strategy`, a score rises with the "
"event probability. Pass a PD as it is, and negate scorecard points, which fall as the risk rises."
" A cut-off of :mod:`kivi.strategy` approves the scores at or below it."
msgstr ""
"在 :mod:`kivi.metrics` 、 :mod:`kivi.monitoring` 和 :mod:`kivi.strategy` 中，评分随事件概率升高而增大。PD "
"可直接传入；评分卡分值随风险升高而降低，须先取负。 :mod:`kivi.strategy` 的截断点通过不高于它的评分。"

msgid ""
"In :mod:`kivi.scorecard`, a ``score`` is scorecard points, which fall as the risk rises: "
":func:`~kivi.scorecard.score_to_pd` gives a lower PD for a higher score."
msgstr ""
"在 :mod:`kivi.scorecard` 中， ``score`` 是评分卡分值，随风险升高而降低： :func:`~kivi.scorecard.score_to_pd` "
"对更高的评分给出更低的 PD。"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.calibration.platt_fit` accepts a score in either direction and fits a negative slope"
" to one that falls as the risk rises. :func:`~kivi.calibration.isotonic_fit` assumes a rising "
"score unless ``increasing=False``."
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.calibration.platt_fit` 接受任一方向的评分，对随风险升高而降低的评分会拟合出负的斜率。 "
":func:`~kivi.calibration.isotonic_fit` 默认评分随风险升高而增大，除非设置 ``increasing=False`` 。"

msgid ""
"True and False count as 1 and 0 in targets, scores and probabilities. Weights, LGDs, exposures "
"and losses reject them, and so do most numeric options, such as ``bins``, ``max_bins``, "
"``factor`` and the cut-offs. Four inputs reject them because a boolean there is more likely a "
"mistake: the ``reference_score`` of :func:`~kivi.monitoring.monitoring_table`, which would "
"usually be a row mask, the ``matrix`` of :func:`~kivi.lifetime.transition_pd`, the ``stage`` of "
":func:`~kivi.lifetime.stage_table` and the ``days_past_due`` of "
":func:`~kivi.lifetime.assign_stages`:"
msgstr ""
"在目标变量、评分和概率中，True 和 False 分别计为 1 和 0。权重、LGD、敞口和损失拒绝布尔值，大多数数值选项也是如此，例如 ``bins`` 、 ``max_bins`` 、 "
"``factor`` 和各截断点。另有四个输入拒绝布尔值，因为布尔值出现在那里更可能是错误： :func:`~kivi.monitoring.monitoring_table` 的 "
"``reference_score`` （布尔值通常是行掩码）、 :func:`~kivi.lifetime.transition_pd` 的 ``matrix`` 、 "
":func:`~kivi.lifetime.stage_table` 的 ``stage`` ，以及 :func:`~kivi.lifetime.assign_stages` 的 "
"``days_past_due`` ："

msgid "Groups and missing values"
msgstr "分组与缺失值"

msgid ""
"The functions that count groups, such as :func:`~kivi.woe.woe_table`, "
":func:`~kivi.stability.psi_table` and :func:`~kivi.calibration.calibration_table`, take the "
"labels as they are: the intervals of ``pandas.cut`` or :func:`kivi.binning.cut`, strings, numbers"
" or categories."
msgstr ""
"对分组计数的函数，例如 :func:`~kivi.woe.woe_table` 、 :func:`~kivi.stability.psi_table` 和 "
":func:`~kivi.calibration.calibration_table` ，按原样接收标签： ``pandas.cut`` 或 :func:`kivi.binning.cut` "
"的区间、字符串、数字或类别。"

msgid "Missing values form a group of their own."
msgstr "缺失值单独成组。"

msgid ""
"Only observed groups appear. Unused categories are left out, and so are the groups whose weights "
"sum to zero. Tables with a fixed set of rows are the exception and keep their empty rows: "
":func:`~kivi.lifetime.stage_table` always has stages 1, 2 and 3, :func:`~kivi.strategy.swap_set` "
"always has its four rows, and the period tables of :mod:`kivi.monitoring` keep a row for every "
"category of a categorical period, so that the rows of all reports line up."
msgstr ""
"只出现观测到的分组。未使用的类别不会出现，权重之和为零的分组也不会出现。行集合固定的表格是例外，会保留空行： :func:`~kivi.lifetime.stage_table` 总有阶段 "
"1、2 和 3， :func:`~kivi.strategy.swap_set` 总有四行， :mod:`kivi.monitoring` "
"的逐期表格为类别型期间的每个类别都保留一行，使各份报告的行能够对齐。"

msgid ""
"Categorical groups, including the intervals of ``pandas.cut``, follow the order of their "
"categories, with the missing group last. Other labels follow the order in which they first "
"appear."
msgstr "分类型分组（包括 ``pandas.cut`` 的区间）按类别顺序排列，缺失组排在最后。其他标签按首次出现的次序排列。"

msgid ""
"Two samples, as in :func:`~kivi.stability.psi_table`, follow the order of the categories only "
"when both have the same categorical dtype. Otherwise, as for an ordered and an unordered "
"categorical, their groups follow the order in which they first appear, in the reference sample "
"and then in the current one."
msgstr ""
"两个样本（例如 :func:`~kivi.stability.psi_table` 中的样本）只有在具有相同的分类型 dtype "
"时才按类别顺序排列。否则（例如一个是有序分类型、另一个是无序分类型时），分组按首次出现的次序排列，先看基准样本，再看当前样本。"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.binning.cut` returns the ordered categorical of ``pandas.cut`` when there are no "
"special codes, and an unordered one with ``special``, because the special codes come first and "
"have no order with the intervals."
msgstr ""
"没有特殊值时， :func:`~kivi.binning.cut` 返回 ``pandas.cut`` 的有序分类型；给出 ``special`` "
"时返回无序分类型，因为特殊值排在最前，与各区间之间没有顺序。"

msgid ""
"Categories are matched to a fitted table or grouping by equality, and a category that it does not"
" know raises an error unless ``unseen`` says how to treat it. :func:`~kivi.woe.woe_transform`, "
":func:`~kivi.binning.group_categories` and :func:`~kivi.stability.csi_table` share this rule, the"
" last through ``unseen_points``. :func:`~kivi.scorecard.reason_codes` matches points rather than "
"categories, and its ``unseen_points`` exempts the points that ``woe_transform`` gave unseen "
"groups."
msgstr ""
"类别按相等关系与拟合好的表格或分组匹配；表格或分组不认识的类别会引发错误，除非 ``unseen`` 指定了处理方式。 :func:`~kivi.woe.woe_transform` 、 "
":func:`~kivi.binning.group_categories` 和 :func:`~kivi.stability.csi_table` 遵循同一规则，最后一个通过 "
"``unseen_points`` 指定。 :func:`~kivi.scorecard.reason_codes` 匹配的是分值而不是类别，它的 ``unseen_points`` 豁免 "
"``woe_transform`` 赋给未见分组的分值。"

msgid ""
"The functions that fit edges or groupings, such as :func:`~kivi.binning.bin_edges`, "
":func:`~kivi.binning.chimerge_edges` and :func:`~kivi.binning.category_groups`, leave missing "
"values out of the fit, and :func:`~kivi.binning.cut` and :func:`~kivi.binning.group_categories` "
"keep them missing, so that they form a group of their own when counted."
msgstr ""
"拟合边界或分组的函数，例如 :func:`~kivi.binning.bin_edges` 、 :func:`~kivi.binning.chimerge_edges` 和 "
":func:`~kivi.binning.category_groups` ，在拟合时不使用缺失值；而 :func:`~kivi.binning.cut` 和 "
":func:`~kivi.binning.group_categories` 保持其缺失，因此计数时它们自成一组。"

msgid ""
"The functions that count, rank or fit, such as :func:`~kivi.metrics.roc_auc`, "
":func:`~kivi.calibration.calibration_table`, :func:`~kivi.strategy.cutoff_table` and "
":func:`~kivi.calibration.platt_fit`, raise an error for a missing score or probability instead, "
"so decide how missing values are scored before passing them in. The functions that convert each "
"value on its own, such as :func:`~kivi.scorecard.pd_to_score`, "
":func:`~kivi.calibration.platt_predict` and :func:`~kivi.strategy.expected_loss`, return NaN for "
"a missing value, and :func:`~kivi.calibration.assign_grades` returns a missing grade. The staging"
" functions of :mod:`kivi.lifetime` work value by value but raise for a missing value, because a "
"missing PD or number of days past due must not decide a stage, and the functions of "
":mod:`kivi.monitoring` raise for a missing period."
msgstr ""
"进行计数、排序或拟合的函数，例如 :func:`~kivi.metrics.roc_auc` 、 :func:`~kivi.calibration.calibration_table` 、 "
":func:`~kivi.strategy.cutoff_table` 和 :func:`~kivi.calibration.platt_fit` "
"，遇到缺失的评分或概率则会引发错误，因此请在传入之前决定如何为缺失值打分。逐个转换取值的函数，例如 :func:`~kivi.scorecard.pd_to_score` 、 "
":func:`~kivi.calibration.platt_predict` 和 :func:`~kivi.strategy.expected_loss` ，对缺失值返回 NaN， "
":func:`~kivi.calibration.assign_grades` 则返回缺失的等级。 :mod:`kivi.lifetime` "
"的阶段划分函数虽然逐个处理取值，但遇到缺失值会引发错误，因为缺失的 PD 或逾期天数不应决定阶段； :mod:`kivi.monitoring` 的函数遇到缺失的期间也会引发错误。"

msgid "Sample weights"
msgstr "样本权重"

msgid ""
"Most functions that count observations or fit a model take ``weights``: one finite, non-negative "
"number per observation, matched to the data like the target. :func:`~kivi.stability.psi_table` "
"and :func:`~kivi.stability.csi_table` take one set for each sample, ``reference_weights`` and "
"``current_weights``."
msgstr ""
"大多数对观测计数或拟合模型的函数都接受 ``weights`` ：每个观测一个有限的非负数，与数据的对应方式和目标变量相同。 :func:`~kivi.stability.psi_table` "
"和 :func:`~kivi.stability.csi_table` 为每个样本各接收一组权重，即 ``reference_weights`` 和 ``current_weights`` 。"

msgid ""
"``weights`` belongs to the main data, and the weights of another sample are named after it, as "
"the ``reference_weights`` of :func:`~kivi.monitoring.monitoring_table` and "
":func:`~kivi.monitoring.stability_table`. :func:`~kivi.selection.vif`, "
":func:`~kivi.selection.correlation_filter`, :func:`~kivi.reject_inference.parceling` and "
":func:`~kivi.reject_inference.reweighting` take no weights and give every row the same weight."
msgstr ""
"``weights`` 属于主数据，另一个样本的权重以该样本命名，例如 :func:`~kivi.monitoring.monitoring_table` 和 "
":func:`~kivi.monitoring.stability_table` 的 ``reference_weights`` 。 :func:`~kivi.selection.vif` 、 "
":func:`~kivi.selection.correlation_filter` 、 :func:`~kivi.reject_inference.parceling` 和 "
":func:`~kivi.reject_inference.reweighting` 不接受权重，对每行一视同仁。"

msgid ""
"Counts become sums of weights, and observations with zero weight are left out. Integer weights "
"therefore give the same counts as repeating each row that many times."
msgstr "计数变为权重之和，权重为零的观测会被排除。因此整数权重与把每一行重复相应次数得到的计数相同。"

msgid ""
"Weighted quantiles use the inverted CDF, so every interior quantile edge is an observed value, "
"while unweighted quantiles interpolate between observations. Weighted edges therefore agree with "
"repeated rows only where no interpolation is needed, and weights of 1 do not give the same edges "
"as no weights."
msgstr ""
"加权分位数采用逆累积分布（inverted CDF），因此每个内部分位数边界都是实际观测到的取值，而不加权的分位数会在观测之间插值。因此加权边界只在不需要插值时与重复行的结果一致，权重全为 1 "
"也不等同于不加权。"

msgid "``smoothing`` replaces an empty cell in units of weight and is not rescaled with the weights."
msgstr "``smoothing`` 以权重为单位替换空单元格，不会随权重缩放。"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.selection.logistic_regression`, :func:`~kivi.selection.stepwise`, "
":func:`~kivi.metrics.roc_auc_interval` and :func:`~kivi.metrics.delong_test` read the weights as "
"frequency weights, so their standard errors count the total weight as the number of observations."
" Weights that correct for sampling, such as inverse sampling rates, make these standard errors "
"too small."
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.selection.logistic_regression` 、 :func:`~kivi.selection.stepwise` 、 "
":func:`~kivi.metrics.roc_auc_interval` 和 :func:`~kivi.metrics.delong_test` "
"把权重视为频数权重，因此它们的标准误把权重总和当作观测数。用于纠正抽样的权重（例如抽样比例的倒数）会使这些标准误偏小。"

msgid "Periods and thresholds"
msgstr "期间与阈值"

msgid ""
"Periods are ordered as their categories when they are categorical and sorted otherwise. Period 1 "
"of a term structure or an expected credit loss is the first period after its starting point, such"
" as the reporting date, and :func:`~kivi.lifetime.expected_credit_loss` discounts a default in "
"period :math:`t` over :math:`t` periods."
msgstr ""
"类别型期间按类别顺序排列，其他期间按升序排列。期限结构或预期信用损失的第 1 期是起点之后的第一期，起点例如报告日； "
":func:`~kivi.lifetime.expected_credit_loss` 把第 :math:`t` 期的违约折现 :math:`t` 期。"

msgid ""
"A threshold is compared as the rule it implements is worded. A cut-off approves the scores at or "
"below it. :func:`~kivi.lifetime.significant_increase` flags a PD increase only when it exceeds "
"its thresholds, and :func:`~kivi.lifetime.assign_stages` moves a loan to stage 2 when it is more "
"than ``stage_2_days`` past due and to stage 3 when it is at least ``stage_3_days`` past due, as "
"IFRS 9 words its 30-day and 90-day presumptions."
msgstr ""
"阈值按其所实现规则的措辞进行比较。截断点通过不高于它的评分。 :func:`~kivi.lifetime.significant_increase` 仅在 PD 的增幅超过阈值时才标记； "
":func:`~kivi.lifetime.assign_stages` 在逾期超过 ``stage_2_days`` 天时把贷款划入第 2 阶段，在逾期达到 ``stage_3_days`` "
"天及以上时划入第 3 阶段，与 IFRS 9 对 30 天和 90 天推定的表述一致。"

msgid ""
"Invalid input raises ``ValueError``, and so does a model that cannot be fitted, such as one with "
"separated classes, which raises :exc:`kivi.selection.SeparationError`. The message names the "
"argument and, where a single value is at fault, shows the value that was received:"
msgstr ""
"无效输入会引发 ``ValueError`` ，无法拟合的模型也是如此，例如类别完全分离时会引发 :exc:`kivi.selection.SeparationError` "
"。错误信息会写明参数名；如果问题出在某个取值上，还会给出收到的值："

msgid ""
"A ``UserWarning`` means that the result differs from the request, for example fewer bins than "
"requested because of tied values, and says what to change. :func:`kivi.univariate.profile_table` "
"records such ties in a column instead, so that profiling many columns raises no warnings."
msgstr ""
"``UserWarning`` 表示结果与请求不同，例如因取值重复而得到的箱数少于请求的箱数，并说明应如何修改。 :func:`kivi.univariate.profile_table` "
"则把这类重合记录在一列中，因此分析很多列时不会产生警告。"

msgid "A ``RuntimeWarning`` means that a fit stopped before it converged."
msgstr "``RuntimeWarning`` 表示拟合在收敛之前停止。"

msgid ""
"A ``FutureWarning`` announces a change of the public API. :doc:`compatibility` says when the "
"change takes effect."
msgstr "``FutureWarning`` 预先通知公共 API 的变更。 :doc:`compatibility` 说明变更何时生效。"

msgid ""
"The wording of the messages may change in any release, so a test that matches a message may need "
"an update; the types of the errors and warnings stay."
msgstr "消息的措辞可能在任何版本中改变，因此匹配消息的测试可能需要更新；错误和警告的类型保持不变。"

msgid "Example data"
msgstr "示例数据"

msgid ""
"Example data for the guides: the bank marketing data of :func:`~kivi.datasets.load_bank`, and the"
" synthetic loan panel and loan applications of :func:`~kivi.datasets.make_loan_panel` and "
":func:`~kivi.datasets.make_applications`."
msgstr ""
"各篇指南使用的示例数据： :func:`~kivi.datasets.load_bank` 提供的银行营销数据，以及 :func:`~kivi.datasets.make_loan_panel`"
" 和 :func:`~kivi.datasets.make_applications` 生成的合成贷款面板和合成贷款申请。"

msgid "See :doc:`/user_guide/datasets` for their columns and how the synthetic data are simulated."
msgstr "各列含义以及合成数据的模拟方式见 :doc:`/user_guide/datasets` 。"

msgid ":py:obj:`load_bank <kivi.datasets.load_bank>`\\ \\(\\)"
msgstr ":py:obj:`load_bank <kivi.datasets.load_bank>`\\ \\(\\)"

msgid "Load 4,521 observations from UCI Bank Marketing."
msgstr "读取 UCI Bank Marketing 的 4,521 条营销记录。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`make_loan_panel <kivi.datasets.make_loan_panel>`\\ \\(\\*\\[\\, n\\_loans\\, "
"n\\_months\\, rng\\]\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`make_loan_panel <kivi.datasets.make_loan_panel>`\\ \\(\\*\\[\\, n\\_loans\\, "
"n\\_months\\, rng\\]\\)"

msgid "Generate a synthetic monthly panel of instalment loans."
msgstr "生成分期贷款的合成月度面板数据。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`make_applications <kivi.datasets.make_applications>`\\ \\(\\*\\[\\, n\\_applicants\\, "
"rng\\]\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`make_applications <kivi.datasets.make_applications>`\\ \\(\\*\\[\\, n\\_applicants\\, "
"rng\\]\\)"

msgid "Generate synthetic loan applications with an approval decision."
msgstr "生成带审批决策的合成贷款申请数据。"

msgid "The ``y`` response of the original data is returned as the binary ``target`` column."
msgstr "原始数据中的响应列 ``y`` 以二分类的 ``target`` 列返回。"

msgid "Sixteen features and the integer target. A value of 1 indicates a term deposit subscription."
msgstr "返回 16 个特征和整数标签 target。1 表示客户认购了定期存款。"

msgid "Relate a feature to ``target``."
msgstr "将某个特征与 ``target`` 关联起来。"

msgid ":obj:`make_loan_panel`"
msgstr ":obj:`make_loan_panel`"

msgid "Synthetic monthly history of a loan portfolio."
msgstr "贷款资产组合的合成月度历史。"

msgid ""
"Bank Marketing by S. Moro, P. Rita and P. Cortez (2014) is distributed under CC BY 4.0. The "
"bundled CSV was converted from the legacy workbook."
msgstr "Bank Marketing 由 S. Moro、P. Rita 和 P. Cortez 于 2014 年发布，按 CC BY 4.0 授权。随包 CSV 由旧版工作簿转换而来。"

msgid ""
"S. Moro, P. Rita and P. Cortez, \"Bank Marketing\", UCI Machine Learning Repository, 2014. "
"https://doi.org/10.24432/C5K306"
msgstr ""
"S. Moro, P. Rita and P. Cortez, \"Bank Marketing\", UCI Machine Learning Repository, 2014. "
"https://doi.org/10.24432/C5K306"

msgid "[Rd093f8221f97-1]_"
msgstr "[Rd093f8221f97-1]_"

msgid ""
"The loans are originated over `n_months` months and observed at the end of every month on book "
"until the month after the last origination month. Delinquency rolls forward when a borrower "
"misses instalments and cures when the arrears are paid, and a loan that reaches 90 days past due "
"stays there. The data is simulated, not drawn from a real portfolio."
msgstr ""
"贷款在 `n_months` 个月内陆续发放，并在每个账龄月的月末观测一次，直到最后一个放款月的下一个月。借款人漏缴期款时逾期向前滚动，还清欠款后回到正常；逾期达到 90 "
"天的贷款会一直停留在该状态。数据是模拟生成的，并非取自真实的资产组合。"

msgid "**n_loans**"
msgstr "**n_loans**"

msgid "int, default 5000"
msgstr "int，默认 5000"

msgid "Number of loans, each assigned to an origination month at random."
msgstr "贷款笔数，每笔贷款随机分配到一个放款月。"

msgid "**n_months**"
msgstr "**n_months**"

msgid "int, default 24"
msgstr "int，默认 24"

msgid ""
"Number of origination months, starting with January 2024. The oldest cohort is observed for "
"`n_months` months on book and the youngest for one."
msgstr "放款月份数，从 2024 年 1 月开始。最早的批次观测 `n_months` 个账龄月，最晚的批次只观测一个。"

msgid "**rng**"
msgstr "**rng**"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "{None, int, numpy.random.Generator}, optional"
msgstr "{None, int, numpy.random.Generator}，可选"

msgid ""
"Seed or generator passed to `numpy.random.default_rng`. The global NumPy random state is not "
"used, so the same seed always returns the same panel."
msgstr "传给 `numpy.random.default_rng` 的种子或生成器。不使用 NumPy 的全局随机状态，因此同一个种子总是返回同样的面板数据。"

msgid ""
"One row per loan and month on book, sorted by loan and then by month on book, with the columns "
"described in the Notes."
msgstr "每笔贷款的每个账龄月一行，先按贷款、再按账龄排序。各列含义见“说明”。"

msgid ""
"If `n_loans` or `n_months` is not a positive integer, or `rng` is not a seed or generator that "
"`numpy.random.default_rng` accepts."
msgstr "如果 `n_loans` 或 `n_months` 不是正整数，或 `rng` 不是 `numpy.random.default_rng` 接受的种子或生成器。"

msgid ":obj:`kivi.vintage.vintage_table`"
msgstr ":obj:`kivi.vintage.vintage_table`"

msgid "Cumulative bad rates by cohort and month on book."
msgstr "按批次和账龄统计的累计坏账率。"

msgid ":obj:`kivi.vintage.transition_matrix`"
msgstr ":obj:`kivi.vintage.transition_matrix`"

msgid "Movements between delinquency buckets."
msgstr "贷款在逾期档位之间的迁移。"

msgid ":obj:`load_bank`"
msgstr ":obj:`load_bank`"

msgid "Real data with a binary target."
msgstr "带二分类目标的真实数据。"

msgid "The columns are:"
msgstr "各列为："

msgid "``loan_id``: integer identifier, increasing with the origination month;"
msgstr "``loan_id`` ：整数标识，随放款月份递增；"

msgid "``cohort``: the origination month, a monthly ``pandas.Period``;"
msgstr "``cohort`` ：放款月份，为月度 ``pandas.Period`` ；"

msgid "``month``: the month of the observation, ``cohort + month_on_book``;"
msgstr "``month`` ：观测所在月份，即 ``cohort + month_on_book`` ；"

msgid "``month_on_book``: months since origination, from 1;"
msgstr "``month_on_book`` ：放款后经过的月数（账龄），从 1 开始；"

msgid "``term``: contractual number of monthly instalments, 12, 24 or 36;"
msgstr "``term`` ：合同约定的月供期数，为 12、24 或 36；"

msgid "``amount``: amount lent;"
msgstr "``amount`` ：放款金额；"

msgid "``balance``: outstanding principal at the end of the month;"
msgstr "``balance`` ：月末的剩余本金；"

msgid ""
"``status``: days past due at the end of the month, an ordered categorical with the categories "
"``current``, ``1-29``, ``30-59``, ``60-89`` and ``90+``."
msgstr "``status`` ：月末的逾期天数，为有序分类变量，类别依次为 ``current`` 、 ``1-29`` 、 ``30-59`` 、 ``60-89`` 和 ``90+`` 。"

#, python-format
msgid ""
"Each loan is repaid in equal monthly instalments at 1% interest a month. Its status counts the "
"months since its oldest unpaid instalment fell due: one is ``1-29``, two ``30-59``, three "
"``60-89`` and four or more ``90+``. Within the term this is the number of instalments past due, "
"and a loan that is still behind after its term keeps rolling."
msgstr ""
"每笔贷款按月等额本息还款，月利率为 1%。其状态记录自最早一期未还期款到期以来的月数：一个月为 ``1-29`` ，两个月为 ``30-59`` ，三个月为 ``60-89`` ，四个月及以上为"
" ``90+`` 。在期限内，这就是逾期未还的期数；期限结束后仍有欠款的贷款会继续滚动。"

msgid ""
"Every month, a current loan misses its instalment with a probability that rises over the first "
"six months on book and then declines, scaled by a risk factor of the loan and one of its cohort, "
"so cohorts differ in quality. A delinquent loan pays all its arrears and becomes current, pays "
"one instalment and keeps its status, or pays nothing and rolls to the next bucket; the chance of "
"curing falls and that of rolling rises with the days past due. A ``90+`` loan makes no further "
"payments, so its balance stays the same. A loan leaves the panel after its last instalment is "
"paid; loans are not charged off."
msgstr ""
"每个月，正常贷款漏缴当期期款的概率在放款后前六个月逐渐上升，之后下降，并乘以该贷款和所在批次各自的风险系数，因此不同批次的质量不同。逾期贷款要么还清全部欠款、回到正常，要么只还一期、保持原状态，要么完全不还、滚动到下一个逾期档位；逾期天数越长，回到正常的概率越低，滚动的概率越高。"
" ``90+`` 的贷款不再还款，因此余额保持不变。贷款还清最后一期后离开面板；贷款不会被核销。"

msgid ""
"Every applicant has a few numeric and categorical features, the PD of an incumbent scorecard and "
"a true default flag. The incumbent PD and two policy rules decide who is approved, so the data "
"show the selection that reject inference corrects for. The data is simulated, not drawn from a "
"real portfolio."
msgstr ""
"每个申请人都有若干数值型和类别型特征、现行评分卡给出的 PD 以及真实的违约标记。现行评分卡的 PD "
"和两条政策规则决定谁获批，因此数据带有拒绝推断所要纠正的样本选择。数据是模拟的，并非取自真实的资产组合。"

msgid "**n_applicants**"
msgstr "**n_applicants**"

msgid "int, default 10000"
msgstr "int，默认 10000"

msgid "Number of applications."
msgstr "申请笔数。"

msgid ""
"Seed or generator passed to `numpy.random.default_rng`. The global NumPy random state is not "
"used, so the same seed always returns the same applications."
msgstr "传给 `numpy.random.default_rng` 的种子或生成器。不使用 NumPy 的全局随机状态，因此同一个种子总是返回同样的申请数据。"

msgid "One row per application with the columns described in the Notes."
msgstr "每笔申请一行，各列含义见“说明”。"

msgid ""
"If `n_applicants` is not a positive integer, or `rng` is not a seed or generator that "
"`numpy.random.default_rng` accepts."
msgstr "如果 `n_applicants` 不是正整数，或 `rng` 不是 `numpy.random.default_rng` 接受的种子或生成器。"

msgid ":obj:`kivi.reject_inference.fuzzy_augmentation`"
msgstr ":obj:`kivi.reject_inference.fuzzy_augmentation`"

msgid "Infer the outcomes of rejected applicants."
msgstr "推断拒绝申请人的结果。"

msgid "``age``: age in years, from 18 to 75;"
msgstr "``age`` ：年龄（岁），从 18 到 75；"

msgid "``income``: monthly income, rounded to tens;"
msgstr "``income`` ：月收入，取整到十位；"

msgid "``debt_to_income``: monthly debt payments over income, rounded to hundredths;"
msgstr "``debt_to_income`` ：每月还债额与收入之比，保留两位小数；"

msgid "``inquiries``: number of credit inquiries in the last six months;"
msgstr "``inquiries`` ：近六个月的征信查询次数；"

msgid "``housing``: a categorical with the categories ``own``, ``mortgage`` and ``rent``;"
msgstr "``housing`` ：分类变量，类别为 ``own`` 、 ``mortgage`` 和 ``rent`` ；"

msgid ""
"``employment``: a categorical with the categories ``permanent``, ``temporary`` and "
"``self_employed``;"
msgstr "``employment`` ：分类变量，类别为 ``permanent`` 、 ``temporary`` 和 ``self_employed`` ；"

msgid "``incumbent_pd``: the PD of the scorecard that decided the application, rounded to four decimals;"
msgstr "``incumbent_pd`` ：决定该申请的评分卡给出的 PD，保留四位小数；"

msgid ""
"``policy_decline``: True if a policy rule declined the application, whatever its PD: a debt-to-"
"income ratio above 0.6 or an age below 21;"
msgstr "``policy_decline`` ：若某条政策规则拒绝了该申请（无论其 PD 如何）则为 True，规则为负债收入比高于 0.6 或年龄低于 21 岁；"

msgid "``approved``: True if ``incumbent_pd`` is below 0.15 and no policy rule declined the application;"
msgstr "``approved`` ：若 ``incumbent_pd`` 低于 0.15 且没有政策规则拒绝该申请，则为 True；"

msgid "``target``: 1 if the applicant defaults, else 0."
msgstr "``target`` ：申请人违约为 1，否则为 0。"

msgid ""
"The default probability rises with the debt-to-income ratio and the number of inquiries, falls "
"with age and income, and is higher for renters and for temporary and self-employed applicants. A "
"hidden risk factor that no column holds also raises it, and the number of inquiries rises with "
"that factor."
msgstr "违约概率随负债收入比和征信查询次数上升，随年龄和收入下降，租房者以及临时雇佣和自雇的申请人违约概率更高。一个不在任何列中的隐藏风险因子也会提高违约概率，征信查询次数也随该因子增加。"

msgid ""
"The incumbent scorecard weighs the features differently, ignores ``housing`` and, like an "
"underwriter with a credit bureau report, sees part of the hidden risk factor. Rejected applicants"
" are therefore riskier than approved applicants with the same features, so a model fitted on the "
"approved applicants alone underestimates their default rate."
msgstr ""
"现行评分卡对各特征的权重不同，不使用 ``housing`` "
"，并且像手握征信报告的审批人员一样，能看到隐藏风险因子的一部分。因此，在特征相同时，拒绝申请人比获批申请人风险更高，只用获批申请人拟合的模型会低估他们的违约率。"

msgid ""
"In practice, the outcome is known only for approved applicants. Here ``target`` is also given for"
" rejected applicants, but only to evaluate reject inference: a model must not be fitted on it, or"
" reject inference would be pointless."
msgstr "实际中只有获批申请人的结果是已知的。这里也给出了拒绝申请人的 ``target`` ，但只用于评估拒绝推断：不能用它拟合模型，否则拒绝推断就失去了意义。"

msgid ""
"The rejected applicants default three times as often as the approved ones, an outcome that only "
"synthetic data can show:"
msgstr "拒绝申请人的违约频率是获批申请人的三倍，这只有合成数据才能展示："

msgid "Glossary"
msgstr "术语表"

msgid ""
"The terms of credit risk modeling as the guides and the docstrings use them. Each entry links to "
"the guide that explains the term with an example."
msgstr "本页按各篇指南和 docstring 中的用法列出信用风险建模的术语。每个条目都链接到用示例解释该术语的指南。"

msgid "Absorbing state"
msgstr "吸收状态"

msgid ""
"A state of a transition matrix that a loan never leaves once it has entered it, such as default. "
"The powers of the matrix then accumulate the probability of having reached it; see "
":doc:`/user_guide/lifetime`."
msgstr "转移矩阵中贷款一旦进入就不会离开的状态，例如违约。矩阵的各次幂会累积到达该状态的概率；见 :doc:`/user_guide/lifetime` 。"

msgid "Accepts and rejects"
msgstr "通过样本与拒绝样本"

msgid ""
"The applicants that a previous policy approved and declined. The outcome is known only for the "
"accepts, so a model developed on them alone may misjudge the rejects; see "
":doc:`/user_guide/reject_inference`."
msgstr "以往策略批准和拒绝的申请人。只有通过样本的结果是已知的，因此只在它们上面开发的模型可能误判拒绝样本；见 :doc:`/user_guide/reject_inference` 。"

msgid "Area under the ROC curve (AUC)"
msgstr "ROC 曲线下面积（AUC）"

msgid ""
"The probability that a randomly chosen event scores higher than a randomly chosen non-event, with"
" ties counted as one half. A score unrelated to the target has an AUC of about 0.5; see "
":doc:`/user_guide/metrics`."
msgstr "随机抽取的一个事件比随机抽取的一个非事件评分更高的概率，评分相同时计为二分之一。与目标变量无关的评分 AUC 约为 0.5；见 :doc:`/user_guide/metrics` 。"

msgid ""
"Dividing the values of a numeric variable into intervals, the bins, whose edges are fitted on a "
"reference sample and then applied to every other sample. Scorecard development calls it classing:"
" fine classing forms many small bins, and coarse classing merges them into a few that are large "
"enough to be stable. A categorical variable is binned by grouping its categories instead; see "
":doc:`/user_guide/binning`."
msgstr ""
"把数值变量的取值划分为若干区间（即箱）：边界在基准样本上拟合，然后应用于其他每个样本。评分卡开发中也称为 classing：细分箱（fine "
"classing）先形成许多小箱，粗分箱（coarse classing）再把它们合并为少数几个足够大、足够稳定的箱。类别变量则通过对类别分组来分箱；见 "
":doc:`/user_guide/binning` 。"

msgid "Binning specification"
msgstr "分箱方案"

msgid ""
"The edges, category groupings, special codes and WOE tables of every column of a model, fitted "
"together and saved as versioned JSON, so that production data are grouped and encoded exactly as "
"the development sample; see :doc:`/user_guide/spec`."
msgstr "模型每一列的边界、类别分组、特殊值和 WOE 表，一起拟合并保存为带版本号的 JSON，使生产数据的分组和编码与开发样本完全一致；见 :doc:`/user_guide/spec` 。"

msgid "Category grouping"
msgstr "类别分组"

msgid ""
"A mapping from each category of a categorical variable to a group, fitted on a reference sample "
"by pooling rare categories or by merging categories with similar event rates, and applied "
"unchanged to every other sample; see :ref:`category-groups`."
msgstr "把类别变量的每个类别映射到一个分组：在基准样本上拟合，方法是合并稀有类别或合并事件率相近的类别，然后原样应用于其他每个样本；见 :ref:`category-groups` 。"

msgid "Characteristic stability index (CSI)"
msgstr "特征稳定性指标（CSI）"

msgid ""
"The change of a variable's average scorecard points from a reference sample to a current one: the"
" change of each group's share times the group's points, summed over the groups. Over all the "
"variables of a scorecard, the CSI values add up to the change of the average score; see :ref"
":`characteristic-stability`."
msgstr ""
"变量的平均评分卡分值从基准样本到当前样本的变化：每组占比的变化乘以该组的分值，再对所有组求和。对评分卡的全部变量，CSI 之和等于平均分的变化；见 :ref:`characteristic-"
"stability` 。"

msgid "Cohort"
msgstr "放款批次"

msgid ""
"The loans originated in the same period, usually a month, followed together as they age in a "
"vintage table; see :doc:`/user_guide/vintage`."
msgstr "同一时期（通常是同一个月）发放的贷款，在 Vintage 表中随账龄一起跟踪；见 :doc:`/user_guide/vintage` 。"

msgid "Conditional PD"
msgstr "条件 PD"

msgid ""
"The probability of a default in a period given that there was none before it, also called the "
"hazard rate; see :doc:`/user_guide/lifetime`."
msgstr "在之前未违约的条件下，某一期发生违约的概率，也称风险率；见 :doc:`/user_guide/lifetime` 。"

msgid "Coverage ratio"
msgstr "覆盖率"

msgid "The loss allowance of a group of loans divided by their exposure; see :doc:`/user_guide/lifetime`."
msgstr "一组贷款的损失准备除以其敞口；见 :doc:`/user_guide/lifetime` 。"

msgid "Credit-impaired"
msgstr "已发生信用减值"

msgid ""
"IFRS 9 calls a loan credit-impaired once events with a detrimental effect on its expected cash "
"flows have occurred, such as significant financial difficulty of the borrower or a breach of "
"contract like a default or a past-due event. Lenders usually align it with their definition of "
"default, and such loans are in stage 3; see :doc:`/user_guide/lifetime`."
msgstr ""
"IFRS 9 "
"规定，一旦发生了对贷款预计现金流量产生不利影响的事件，例如借款人发生重大财务困难，或发生违约、逾期等违反合同的情况，该贷款即为已发生信用减值。贷款人通常使其与自身的违约定义保持一致，此类贷款处于第"
" 3 阶段；见 :doc:`/user_guide/lifetime` 。"

msgid "Cumulative PD"
msgstr "累计 PD"

msgid ""
"The probability of a default in any of the periods from the first up to a given one, which never "
"falls as the horizon grows; see :doc:`/user_guide/lifetime`."
msgstr "从第一期到某一期之间任意一期发生违约的概率，它不会随期限延长而下降；见 :doc:`/user_guide/lifetime` 。"

msgid "Cut-off"
msgstr "截断点"

msgid ""
"The score that separates approval from decline. kivi approves the scores at or below the cut-off,"
" because its scores rise with the risk; see :doc:`/user_guide/strategy`."
msgstr "区分通过与拒绝的评分。kivi 的评分随风险升高而增大，因此通过不高于截断点的评分；见 :doc:`/user_guide/strategy` 。"

msgid "Days past due (DPD)"
msgstr "逾期天数（DPD）"

msgid ""
"The number of days for which a contractual payment has been overdue. IFRS 9 rebuttably presumes a"
" significant increase in credit risk when a payment is more than 30 days past due, and default no"
" later than when it is 90 days past due; see :doc:`/user_guide/lifetime`."
msgstr ""
"合同约定的还款已逾期的天数。IFRS 9 作出可反驳的推定：还款逾期超过 30 天时信用风险已显著增加，违约不晚于逾期达到 90 天之时发生；见 "
":doc:`/user_guide/lifetime` 。"

msgid "DeLong test"
msgstr "DeLong 检验"

msgid ""
"A test of whether two scores have the same AUC on the same sample. It uses the variances and the "
"covariance of the two AUCs that DeLong, DeLong and Clarke-Pearson (1988) derived from the "
"placement values; see :doc:`/user_guide/metrics`."
msgstr ""
"检验同一样本上两个评分的 AUC 是否相同。它使用 DeLong、DeLong 和 Clarke-Pearson（1988）由位置值推导出的两个 AUC 的方差和协方差；见 "
":doc:`/user_guide/metrics` 。"

msgid "Deprecation"
msgstr "弃用"

msgid ""
"A part of the public API that still works but warns with a ``FutureWarning``, because a later "
"release removes or changes it. The warning says what to use instead; see :doc:`compatibility`."
msgstr "公共 API 中仍然可用、但会发出 ``FutureWarning`` 的部分，因为以后的版本会移除或修改它。警告会说明替代用法；参见 :doc:`compatibility` 。"

msgid "Effective interest rate"
msgstr "实际利率"

msgid ""
"The rate that discounts the estimated future cash flows of a loan over its expected life to its "
"gross carrying amount at initial recognition. IFRS 9 discounts expected credit losses at this "
"rate; see :doc:`/user_guide/lifetime`."
msgstr "在初始确认时，把贷款在预计存续期内的估计未来现金流量折现为其账面余额的利率。IFRS 9 按这一利率折现预期信用损失；见 :doc:`/user_guide/lifetime` 。"

msgid "Event and non-event"
msgstr "事件与非事件"

msgid ""
"The two outcomes of a binary target: an event has target 1, such as a default or another bad "
"outcome, and a non-event has target 0. The guides read the subscription of the bundled bank data "
"as the event; see :doc:`/user_guide/woe_iv`."
msgstr "二元目标变量的两种结果：事件的目标值为 1，例如违约或其他不良结果；非事件的目标值为 0。各篇指南把内置银行数据中的认购视为事件；见 :doc:`/user_guide/woe_iv` 。"

msgid "Event rate"
msgstr "事件率"

msgid ""
"The share of events among the observations of a group, called the bad rate when the event is a "
"default. It is computed from the raw counts, without smoothing; see :doc:`/user_guide/woe_iv`."
msgstr "某组观测中事件所占的比例，事件为违约时称为坏账率。它按原始计数计算，不做平滑；见 :doc:`/user_guide/woe_iv` 。"

msgid "Ever bad"
msgstr "曾经为坏（ever bad）"

msgid ""
"A loan is ever bad by a month on book if it was bad at any month on book up to then, even if it "
"has cured since. The cumulative bad rates of a vintage table count the loans that are ever bad; "
"see :doc:`/user_guide/vintage`."
msgstr ""
"如果一笔贷款在某个账龄及之前的任一账龄为坏，即使之后已经恢复正常，它在该账龄也算曾经为坏。Vintage 表的累计坏账率统计的就是曾经为坏的贷款；见 "
":doc:`/user_guide/vintage` 。"

msgid "Expected credit loss (ECL)"
msgstr "预期信用损失（ECL）"

msgid ""
"Under IFRS 9, the present value of the credit losses of an exposure, weighted with the "
"probabilities of default. The 12-month ECL counts the losses from defaults in the next 12 months,"
" and the lifetime ECL those over the remaining life of the exposure; see "
":doc:`/user_guide/lifetime`."
msgstr ""
"在 IFRS 9 下，以违约概率为权重的敞口信用损失现值。12 个月 ECL 计入未来 12 个月内违约造成的损失，整个存续期 ECL 计入敞口剩余存续期内的损失；见 "
":doc:`/user_guide/lifetime` 。"

msgid "Expected loss (EL)"
msgstr "预期损失（EL）"

msgid ""
"The loss that an exposure is expected to cause: its probability of default times its loss given "
"default times its exposure at default; see :doc:`/user_guide/strategy`."
msgstr "一笔敞口预期造成的损失：违约概率乘以违约损失率再乘以违约风险敞口；见 :doc:`/user_guide/strategy` 。"

msgid "Exposure at default (EAD)"
msgstr "违约风险敞口（EAD）"

msgid ""
"The amount owed when a borrower defaults, such as the outstanding balance of a loan; see "
":doc:`/user_guide/strategy`."
msgstr "借款人违约时所欠的金额，例如贷款的未偿余额；见 :doc:`/user_guide/strategy` 。"

msgid "Format version"
msgstr "格式版本"

msgid ""
"The version of the JSON format of a binning specification, stored in each file. A release reads "
"every format version up to its own and rejects a newer one; see :doc:`compatibility`."
msgstr "分箱方案 JSON 格式的版本，保存在每个文件中。一个版本能读取不高于其自身的每种格式版本，并拒绝更新的格式版本；参见 :doc:`compatibility` 。"

msgid "Gains table"
msgstr "增益表"

msgid ""
"A table of score bands from the riskiest to the safest, with the event rate and lift of each band"
" and the cumulative shares of events and non-events; see :doc:`/user_guide/metrics`."
msgstr "按评分段从风险最高到最低排列的表，列出每段的事件率和提升度，以及事件和非事件的累计占比；见 :doc:`/user_guide/metrics` 。"

msgid "Gini coefficient"
msgstr "Gini 系数"

msgid ""
"Twice the AUC minus 1: 0 for a score unrelated to the target and 1 for a score that ranks every "
"event above every non-event. Scorecard development reports it more often than the AUC itself; see"
" :doc:`/user_guide/metrics`."
msgstr ""
"AUC 的两倍减 1：与目标变量无关的评分为 0，把每个事件都排在每个非事件之前的评分为 1。评分卡开发中报告 Gini 系数比报告 AUC 本身更常见；见 "
":doc:`/user_guide/metrics` 。"

msgid "Grade"
msgstr "等级"

msgid ""
"One class of a rating system or master scale, with a PD of its own and bounds that decide which "
"predicted PDs fall into it; see :doc:`/user_guide/calibration`."
msgstr "评级体系或主标尺中的一个类别，有自己的 PD，并由上下界决定哪些预测 PD 落入其中；见 :doc:`/user_guide/calibration` 。"

msgid "Information value (IV)"
msgstr "信息值（IV）"

msgid ""
"The sum of the differences between the event share and the non-event share of each group, each "
"times the group's WOE. It measures how strongly a grouped variable separates events from non-"
"events on its own; see :doc:`/user_guide/woe_iv`."
msgstr "每组事件占比与非事件占比之差乘以该组 WOE，再对所有组求和。它衡量一个分组后的变量单独区分事件与非事件的能力；见 :doc:`/user_guide/woe_iv` 。"

msgid "Kolmogorov-Smirnov statistic (KS)"
msgstr "Kolmogorov-Smirnov 统计量（KS）"

msgid ""
"The largest absolute gap between the distribution functions of the scores of events and of non-"
"events; see :doc:`/user_guide/metrics`."
msgstr "事件评分与非事件评分的分布函数之间的最大绝对差距；见 :doc:`/user_guide/metrics` 。"

msgid "Lift"
msgstr "提升度（lift）"

msgid ""
"The event rate of a group divided by the event rate of the whole sample. A lift above 1 marks a "
"group that is riskier than average; see :doc:`/user_guide/metrics`."
msgstr "某组的事件率除以整个样本的事件率。提升度大于 1 表示该组风险高于平均水平；见 :doc:`/user_guide/metrics` 。"

msgid "Loss allowance"
msgstr "损失准备"

msgid ""
"The provision that IFRS 9 requires for the expected credit losses of a loan: the 12-month ECL in "
"stage 1 and the lifetime ECL in stages 2 and 3; see :doc:`/user_guide/lifetime`."
msgstr "IFRS 9 要求为贷款的预期信用损失计提的准备：第 1 阶段为 12 个月 ECL，第 2 和第 3 阶段为整个存续期 ECL；见 :doc:`/user_guide/lifetime` 。"

msgid "Loss given default (LGD)"
msgstr "违约损失率（LGD）"

msgid ""
"The share of the exposure that is lost when a borrower defaults, after recoveries and collateral;"
" see :doc:`/user_guide/strategy`."
msgstr "借款人违约时，扣除回收和抵押品之后损失的敞口比例；见 :doc:`/user_guide/strategy` 。"

msgid "Marginal PD"
msgstr "边际 PD"

msgid ""
"The probability, seen from the starting point, of a default in one given period. The marginal PDs"
" of the periods up to a horizon add up to the cumulative PD; see :doc:`/user_guide/lifetime`."
msgstr "从起点看，在某一给定期间发生违约的概率。截至某一期限的各期边际 PD 之和即为累计 PD；见 :doc:`/user_guide/lifetime` 。"

msgid "Master scale"
msgstr "主标尺"

msgid ""
"A fixed set of grades that divides the PD range from 0 to 1, so that ratings from different "
"models share one meaning; see :doc:`/user_guide/calibration`."
msgstr "把 0 到 1 的 PD 区间划分为一组固定等级，使不同模型给出的评级具有同一含义；见 :doc:`/user_guide/calibration` 。"

msgid "Monitoring report"
msgstr "监控报告"

msgid ""
"A table with one row per period that tracks a model in use: its population, the known outcomes, "
"its discrimination and the stability of its score against a reference sample; see "
":doc:`/user_guide/monitoring`."
msgstr "每期一行、跟踪在用模型的表格：样本量、已知结果、区分能力，以及评分相对于基准样本的稳定性；见 :doc:`/user_guide/monitoring` 。"

msgid "Month on book"
msgstr "账龄（month on book）"

msgid ""
"The number of months since a loan was originated. A vintage table compares cohorts at the same "
"month on book; see :doc:`/user_guide/vintage`."
msgstr "贷款发放以来的月数。Vintage 表在相同账龄上比较各放款批次；见 :doc:`/user_guide/vintage` 。"

msgid "Outcome window"
msgstr "表现期"

msgid ""
"The time after which the outcome of an observation is known, such as twelve months after a loan "
"was granted. Until it has passed, the target is missing and the outcome counts as unknown; see "
":doc:`/user_guide/monitoring`."
msgstr "观测结果得以知晓所需的时间，例如贷款发放后十二个月。在此之前，目标变量缺失，结果视为未知；见 :doc:`/user_guide/monitoring` 。"

msgid "PD term structure"
msgstr "PD 期限结构"

msgid ""
"The PD of each period after a starting point, such as the origination of a loan or the reporting "
"date, given as cumulative, marginal or conditional PDs; see :doc:`/user_guide/lifetime`."
msgstr "起点（例如贷款发放日或报告日）之后每一期的 PD，以累计、边际或条件 PD 的形式给出；见 :doc:`/user_guide/lifetime` 。"

msgid "Placement value"
msgstr "位置值"

msgid ""
"For an event, the share of non-events that score below it, and for a non-event, the share of "
"events that score above it, with ties counted as one half. The average over either class is the "
"AUC, and their variances give its DeLong standard error; see :doc:`/user_guide/metrics`."
msgstr ""
"对于一个事件，是评分低于它的非事件所占的比例；对于一个非事件，是评分高于它的事件所占的比例；评分相同时按一半计。任一类别的位置值的平均数就是 AUC，它们的方差给出 AUC 的 DeLong "
"标准误；见 :doc:`/user_guide/metrics` 。"

msgid "Points to double the odds (PDO)"
msgstr "好坏比翻倍所需分数（PDO）"

msgid ""
"The number of scorecard points by which the score rises when the good:bad odds double. Together "
"with a base score and the odds at that score, it sets the scale of a scorecard; see "
":doc:`/user_guide/scorecard`."
msgstr "好坏比翻倍时评分增加的分数。它与基准分及基准分对应的好坏比一起确定评分卡的刻度；见 :doc:`/user_guide/scorecard` 。"

msgid "Population stability index (PSI)"
msgstr "群体稳定性指标（PSI）"

msgid ""
"A measure of how much the distribution of a variable or a score has shifted between a reference "
"sample and a current one, summed over the groups from the change of each group's share; see "
":doc:`/user_guide/psi`."
msgstr "衡量变量或评分的分布在基准样本与当前样本之间偏移了多少，由每组占比的变化计算并对所有组求和；见 :doc:`/user_guide/psi` 。"

msgid "Precision"
msgstr "精确率"

msgid ""
"The share of events among the observations that a score flags at a threshold, that is, the event "
"rate of the flagged observations; see :doc:`/user_guide/metrics`."
msgstr "评分在某一阈值下标记的观测中事件所占的比例，即被标记观测的事件率；见 :doc:`/user_guide/metrics` 。"

msgid "Probability of default (PD)"
msgstr "违约概率（PD）"

msgid ""
"The probability that a borrower defaults within a given horizon, usually twelve months. kivi "
"calls a predicted PD, or any other predicted event probability, ``probability``; see "
":doc:`/user_guide/calibration`."
msgstr ""
"借款人在给定期限内（通常为十二个月）违约的概率。kivi 把预测的 PD 以及其他任何预测的事件概率都称为 ``probability`` ；见 "
":doc:`/user_guide/calibration` 。"

msgid "Reason codes"
msgstr "原因码"

msgid ""
"The variables that lowered an applicant's score most, compared with the best group of each "
"variable, as given to a declined applicant; see :doc:`/user_guide/scorecard`."
msgstr "与每个变量的最优分组相比，使申请人评分降低最多的变量，通常告知被拒绝的申请人；见 :doc:`/user_guide/scorecard` 。"

msgid "Reference sample"
msgstr "基准样本"

msgid ""
"The sample that later samples are compared with, usually the development sample or a period right"
" after it. Bin edges, score bands and groups are fitted on it; see :doc:`/user_guide/monitoring`."
msgstr "后续样本与之比较的样本，通常是开发样本或紧随其后的一期。分箱边界、评分段和分组都在它上面拟合；见 :doc:`/user_guide/monitoring` 。"

msgid "Reject inference"
msgstr "拒绝推断"

msgid ""
"Methods that supply outcomes for rejected applicants, as rows with weights or as weights for the "
"accepts, so that a model can be refitted on all applicants; see "
":doc:`/user_guide/reject_inference`."
msgstr "为被拒绝的申请人补充结果的方法，结果以带权重的行或通过样本的权重给出，从而可以在全部申请人上重新拟合模型；见 :doc:`/user_guide/reject_inference` 。"

msgid "Reporting date"
msgstr "报告日"

msgid ""
"The date at which a loss allowance is measured. Period 1 of an expected credit loss is the first "
"period after it; see :doc:`/user_guide/lifetime`."
msgstr "计量损失准备的日期。预期信用损失的第 1 期是报告日之后的第一期；见 :doc:`/user_guide/lifetime` 。"

msgid "ROC curve"
msgstr "ROC 曲线"

msgid ""
"The true positive rate, the share of events flagged, against the false positive rate, the share "
"of non-events flagged, as the threshold moves through the scores from the riskiest down. The area"
" under it is the AUC, and its largest vertical distance from the diagonal is the KS; see "
":doc:`/user_guide/metrics`."
msgstr ""
"阈值从风险最高的评分开始依次下移时，真正例率（被标记的事件所占比例）对假正例率（被标记的非事件所占比例）的曲线。曲线下的面积就是 AUC，曲线与对角线之间的最大纵向距离就是 KS；见 "
":doc:`/user_guide/metrics` 。"

msgid "Roll rate"
msgstr "滚动率"

msgid ""
"The share of the loans in a delinquency bucket at one month end that are in the next worse bucket"
" at the next month end; see :doc:`/user_guide/vintage`."
msgstr "某个月末处于某一逾期档位的贷款中，到下一个月末进入更差一档的比例；见 :doc:`/user_guide/vintage` 。"

msgid "Significant increase in credit risk (SICR)"
msgstr "信用风险显著增加（SICR）"

msgid ""
"The IFRS 9 criterion that moves a loan from stage 1 to stage 2: its risk of default has risen "
"significantly since initial recognition. Each lender sets the test in its own policy, for example"
" as relative and absolute increases of the PD; see :doc:`/user_guide/lifetime`."
msgstr ""
"IFRS 9 中把贷款从第 1 阶段移至第 2 阶段的标准：自初始确认以来，其违约风险已显著上升。每个贷款人在自己的政策中设定这一判断，例如 PD 的相对增幅和绝对增幅；见 "
":doc:`/user_guide/lifetime` 。"

msgid "Smoothing"
msgstr "平滑"

msgid ""
"The value that replaces an empty count before shares are computed, 0.5 by default, so that the "
"WOE, the IV and the PSI of a group stay finite. Counts are reported as observed, and only the "
"shares are smoothed; see :doc:`/user_guide/woe_iv`."
msgstr "计算占比之前用来替换空计数的值，默认为 0.5，使每组的 WOE、IV 和 PSI 保持有限。计数按观测值报告，只有占比经过平滑；见 :doc:`/user_guide/woe_iv` 。"

msgid "Special codes"
msgstr "特殊编码"

msgid ""
"Values that stand for a state rather than a measurement, such as -1 for \"never contacted\", 999 "
"for \"no record\" or the label \"unknown\" of a categorical variable. Passed in ``special``, they"
" are left out of the fit of the edges or of the grouping and each gets a group of its own; see "
":ref:`special-values`."
msgstr ""
"表示某种状态而不是测量值的取值，例如表示“从未联系”的 -1、表示“无记录”的 999，或类别变量的标签“unknown”。传入 ``special`` "
"后，它们不参与边界或分组的拟合，并且各自单独成组；见 :ref:`special-values` 。"

msgid "Stage"
msgstr "阶段"

msgid ""
"One of the three IFRS 9 buckets of a loan: stage 1 for loans without a significant increase in "
"credit risk, with a 12-month ECL; stage 2 for loans with one, with a lifetime ECL; and stage 3 "
"for credit-impaired loans, also with a lifetime ECL; see :doc:`/user_guide/lifetime`."
msgstr ""
"IFRS 9 对贷款划分的三个阶段之一：第 1 阶段为信用风险未显著增加的贷款，计提 12 个月 ECL；第 2 阶段为信用风险已显著增加的贷款，计提整个存续期 ECL；第 3 "
"阶段为已发生信用减值的贷款，同样计提整个存续期 ECL；见 :doc:`/user_guide/lifetime` 。"

msgid "Standard error and confidence interval"
msgstr "标准误与置信区间"

#, python-format
msgid ""
"The standard error measures how much an estimate, such as an AUC, would vary from sample to "
"sample. A confidence interval at a level such as 95% is a range around the estimate that would "
"cover the true value in that share of samples; see :doc:`/user_guide/metrics`."
msgstr ""
"标准误衡量 AUC 等估计值在不同样本之间会有多大波动。置信水平为 95% 等的置信区间是估计值周围的一个范围，在相应比例的样本中它会覆盖真实值；见 "
":doc:`/user_guide/metrics` 。"

msgid "Swap set"
msgstr "交换集"

msgid ""
"The four groups of applicants that two scores, each with its cut-off, approve or decline. The "
"swap-outs are approved only by the current score and the swap-ins only by the new one; see "
":doc:`/user_guide/strategy`."
msgstr "两个评分各按自己的截断点通过或拒绝申请人，由此形成的四组申请人。换出是只有现行评分通过的申请人，换入是只有新评分通过的申请人；见 :doc:`/user_guide/strategy` 。"

msgid "Total"
msgstr "合计"

msgid ""
"The number of observations in a row of a table, missing values included, or their sum of weights."
" The ``count`` of :func:`~kivi.univariate.profile_table` is the number of values that are not "
"missing instead, as in ``pandas.DataFrame.describe``; see :doc:`/user_guide/univariate`."
msgstr ""
"表格中一行的观测数（包括缺失值），或这些观测的权重之和。而 :func:`~kivi.univariate.profile_table` 的 ``count`` 是非缺失值的个数，与 "
"``pandas.DataFrame.describe`` 相同；参见 :doc:`/user_guide/univariate` 。"

msgid "Transition matrix"
msgstr "转移矩阵"

msgid ""
"A table that counts the loans or obligors that moved from each state to each other state between "
"two dates, such as delinquency buckets or rating grades; see :doc:`/user_guide/vintage`."
msgstr "统计贷款或债务人在两个日期之间从每种状态转移到其他每种状态的数量的表，状态可以是逾期档位或评级等级；见 :doc:`/user_guide/vintage` 。"

msgid "Unseen category"
msgstr "未见类别"

msgid ""
"A category of a later sample that did not occur in the reference sample, so that its grouping or "
"WOE table has no row for it. kivi raises an error for such a category unless an ``unseen`` policy"
" says how to treat it; see :doc:`/user_guide/woe_iv`."
msgstr ""
"后续样本中出现、但基准样本中没有的类别，因此其分组或 WOE 表中没有对应的行。kivi 对此类类别引发错误，除非 ``unseen`` 策略指定了处理方式；见 "
":doc:`/user_guide/woe_iv` 。"

msgid "Vintage table"
msgstr "Vintage 表"

msgid "The cumulative ever-bad rate of each cohort by month on book; see :doc:`/user_guide/vintage`."
msgstr "每个放款批次按账龄统计的累计曾经为坏比例；见 :doc:`/user_guide/vintage` 。"

msgid "Weight of evidence (WOE)"
msgstr "证据权重（WOE）"

msgid ""
"The logarithm of a group's share of all events over its share of all non-events. A positive WOE "
"marks a group that is relatively more common among events; see :doc:`/user_guide/woe_iv`."
msgstr "某组在全部事件中的占比与在全部非事件中的占比之比的对数。WOE 为正表示该组在事件中相对更常见；见 :doc:`/user_guide/woe_iv` 。"

msgid "Lifetime PD and expected credit loss"
msgstr "存续期 PD 与预期信用损失"

msgid ""
"Turn PD term structures into the expected credit loss and the stages of IFRS 9. "
":func:`~kivi.lifetime.convert_pd` converts a term structure between cumulative, marginal and "
"conditional PDs, :func:`~kivi.lifetime.transition_pd` projects one from a transition matrix, "
":func:`~kivi.lifetime.expected_credit_loss` gives the 12-month and the lifetime expected credit "
"loss of each account, and :func:`~kivi.lifetime.significant_increase`, "
":func:`~kivi.lifetime.assign_stages` and :func:`~kivi.lifetime.stage_table` allocate the stages "
"and sum the loss allowance of each stage."
msgstr ""
"把 PD 期限结构转化为 IFRS 9 的预期信用损失和阶段。 :func:`~kivi.lifetime.convert_pd` 在累计、边际和条件 PD 之间转换期限结构， "
":func:`~kivi.lifetime.transition_pd` 由转移矩阵推算期限结构， :func:`~kivi.lifetime.expected_credit_loss` "
"给出每个账户的 12 个月预期信用损失和整个存续期预期信用损失， :func:`~kivi.lifetime.significant_increase` 、 "
":func:`~kivi.lifetime.assign_stages` 和 :func:`~kivi.lifetime.stage_table` 划分阶段并汇总每个阶段的损失准备。"

msgid "See :doc:`/user_guide/lifetime` for examples on the bundled data."
msgstr "基于随包数据的示例见 :doc:`/user_guide/lifetime` 。"

msgid ":py:obj:`convert_pd <kivi.lifetime.convert_pd>`\\ \\(probability\\, \\*\\, kind\\, to\\)"
msgstr ":py:obj:`convert_pd <kivi.lifetime.convert_pd>`\\ \\(probability\\, \\*\\, kind\\, to\\)"

msgid "Convert a PD term structure between cumulative, marginal and conditional PDs."
msgstr "在累计、边际和条件 PD 之间转换 PD 期限结构。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`transition_pd <kivi.lifetime.transition_pd>`\\ \\(matrix\\, \\*\\, horizons\\[\\, "
"...\\]\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`transition_pd <kivi.lifetime.transition_pd>`\\ \\(matrix\\, \\*\\, horizons\\[\\, "
"...\\]\\)"

msgid "Project the cumulative PD of each state from a transition matrix."
msgstr "由转移矩阵推算每个状态的累计 PD。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`expected_credit_loss <kivi.lifetime.expected_credit_loss>`\\ \\(probability\\, lgd\\, "
"ead\\, ...\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`expected_credit_loss <kivi.lifetime.expected_credit_loss>`\\ \\(probability\\, lgd\\, "
"ead\\, ...\\)"

msgid "Compute the 12-month or lifetime expected credit loss of each account."
msgstr "计算每个账户的 12 个月或整个存续期预期信用损失。"

msgid ":py:obj:`significant_increase <kivi.lifetime.significant_increase>`\\ \\(probability\\, ...\\)"
msgstr ":py:obj:`significant_increase <kivi.lifetime.significant_increase>`\\ \\(probability\\, ...\\)"

msgid "Flag a significant increase in credit risk since initial recognition."
msgstr "标记自初始确认以来信用风险是否显著增加。"

msgid ":py:obj:`assign_stages <kivi.lifetime.assign_stages>`\\ \\(significant\\_increase\\[\\, ...\\]\\)"
msgstr ":py:obj:`assign_stages <kivi.lifetime.assign_stages>`\\ \\(significant\\_increase\\[\\, ...\\]\\)"

msgid "Allocate exposures to the three stages of IFRS 9."
msgstr "把敞口划分到 IFRS 9 的三个阶段。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`stage_table <kivi.lifetime.stage_table>`\\ \\(stage\\, exposure\\, allowance\\, "
"\\*\\[\\, ...\\]\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`stage_table <kivi.lifetime.stage_table>`\\ \\(stage\\, exposure\\, allowance\\, "
"\\*\\[\\, ...\\]\\)"

msgid "Summarize the exposure and the expected credit loss of each stage."
msgstr "汇总每个阶段的敞口和预期信用损失。"

msgid ""
"A term structure gives the probability of default in each period after a starting point, such as "
"the origination of a loan. The cumulative PD of period :math:`k` is the probability of a default "
"in periods 1 to :math:`k`, the marginal PD the probability of a default in period :math:`k`, and "
"the conditional PD, or hazard rate, the probability of a default in period :math:`k` given that "
"there was none before."
msgstr ""
"期限结构给出从某个起点（例如贷款发放）开始每一期的违约概率。第 :math:`k` 期的累计 PD 是在第 1 期到第 :math:`k` 期之间违约的概率，边际 PD 是在第 "
":math:`k` 期违约的概率，条件 PD（又称风险率，hazard rate）是此前未违约的前提下在第 :math:`k` 期违约的概率。"

msgid "array_like or pandas.DataFrame"
msgstr "array_like 或 pandas.DataFrame"

msgid ""
"PDs from 0 to 1, as one curve, one-dimensional, or one curve per row, two-dimensional, such as "
"the cumulative bad rates of `kivi.vintage.vintage_table` with one row per cohort and one column "
"per month on book. The periods are the positions along the curve: the first is period 1. Missing "
"values mark the periods that are not observed, such as the months on book that a cohort has not "
"reached. Booleans count as 0 and 1."
msgstr ""
"取值在 0 到 1 之间的 PD：一条曲线（一维），或每行一条曲线（二维），例如 `kivi.vintage.vintage_table` "
"给出的累计坏账率，每个批次一行、每个账龄一列。各期就是曲线上的位置：第一个位置是第 1 期。缺失值表示没有观测到的期，例如批次尚未达到的账龄。布尔值按 0 和 1 计。"

msgid "**kind**"
msgstr "**kind**"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "{\"cumulative\", \"marginal\", \"conditional\"}"
msgstr "{\"cumulative\", \"marginal\", \"conditional\"}"

msgid "Kind of the PDs in `probability`."
msgstr "`probability` 中 PD 的种类。"

msgid "**to**"
msgstr "**to**"

msgid "Kind of the PDs to return."
msgstr "要返回的 PD 种类。"

msgid "pandas.DataFrame, pandas.Series or numpy.ndarray"
msgstr "pandas.DataFrame、pandas.Series 或 numpy.ndarray"

msgid ""
"PDs of kind `to` in the shape of `probability`, with its index, columns and name. Missing values "
"stay missing, and so do the PDs that depend on them, as described in the Notes."
msgstr "种类为 `to` 的 PD，形状与 `probability` 相同，并保留其索引、列和名称。缺失值保持缺失，依赖于它们的 PD 也为缺失，详见“说明”。"

msgid ""
"If `kind` or `to` is not one of the three kinds, `probability` is not real and numeric, is not "
"one- or two-dimensional, has no period or has a value outside [0, 1]. Also if cumulative PDs "
"decrease along a curve or the marginal PDs of a curve add up to more than 1."
msgstr ""
"如果 `kind` 或 `to` 不是这三种之一， `probability` 不是实数数值、不是一维或二维、没有任何一期，或有取值超出 [0, 1]。此外，如果累计 PD "
"沿曲线下降，或一条曲线的边际 PD 之和超过 1。"

msgid ":obj:`transition_pd`"
msgstr ":obj:`transition_pd`"

msgid "Cumulative PDs from a transition matrix."
msgstr "由转移矩阵得到的累计 PD。"

msgid ":obj:`expected_credit_loss`"
msgstr ":obj:`expected_credit_loss`"

msgid "Expected credit loss from marginal PDs."
msgstr "由边际 PD 计算的预期信用损失。"

msgid ""
"With the cumulative PDs :math:`C_k`, the marginal PDs :math:`m_k` and the conditional PDs "
":math:`h_k` of periods :math:`k = 1, 2, \\ldots`, and :math:`C_0 = 0`,"
msgstr ""
"设第 :math:`k = 1, 2, \\ldots` 期的累计 PD 为 :math:`C_k` 、边际 PD 为 :math:`m_k` 、条件 PD 为 :math:`h_k` ，并令 "
":math:`C_0 = 0` ，则"

msgid ""
"m_k = C_k - C_{k-1}, \\qquad\n"
"h_k = \\frac{C_k - C_{k-1}}{1 - C_{k-1}}, \\qquad\n"
"C_k = \\sum_{j \\le k} m_j = 1 - \\prod_{j \\le k} (1 - h_j)."
msgstr ""
"m_k = C_k - C_{k-1}, \\qquad\n"
"h_k = \\frac{C_k - C_{k-1}}{1 - C_{k-1}}, \\qquad\n"
"C_k = \\sum_{j \\le k} m_j = 1 - \\prod_{j \\le k} (1 - h_j)."

msgid ""
"The conversions are inverses of each other, up to rounding. The labels of the periods are not "
"used: the columns of a vintage table that start at month on book 1 give monthly PDs, and columns "
"of quarterly snapshots give the PDs of the quarters between them."
msgstr "在舍入误差范围内，这些转换互为逆运算。各期的标签不参与计算：从账龄 1 开始的 vintage 表各列给出月度 PD，按季度快照的各列给出相邻快照之间各季度的 PD。"

msgid ""
"Missing values are not filled. The marginal and the conditional PD of a period need the "
"cumulative PDs at its end and at the end of the period before, and the cumulative PD of a period "
"needs the marginal or conditional PDs of every period up to it. The months on book that a cohort "
"has not reached therefore stay missing in every kind, also after a round trip. Missing values at "
"the start of a curve, which `kivi.vintage.vintage_table` gives when the panel starts after "
"origination, leave the marginal and conditional PDs known from the second observed period on, but"
" converting those back cannot restore the cumulative PDs, because the cumulative PD before the "
"panel starts is not known."
msgstr ""
"缺失值不会被填补。某一期的边际 PD 和条件 PD 需要该期期末和上一期期末的累计 PD，某一期的累计 PD 则需要截至该期每一期的边际或条件 PD。因此，批次尚未达到的账龄在每一种 PD "
"中都保持缺失，往返转换之后也是如此。曲线开头的缺失值（面板晚于放款开始时， `kivi.vintage.vintage_table` 会给出这样的缺失值）不影响从第二个观测期起的边际和条件 "
"PD，但由它们无法再转换回累计 PD，因为面板开始之前的累计 PD 未知。"

msgid ""
"Once the cumulative PD of a curve reaches 1, no exposure is left to default, and the conditional "
"PDs of the later periods, 0 / 0, are 0, so that the conversions stay inverses."
msgstr "一条曲线的累计 PD 达到 1 之后，已没有敞口可以违约，此后各期的条件 PD 为 0 / 0，取为 0，以保证这些转换仍互为逆运算。"

msgid ""
"The cumulative bad rates of `kivi.vintage.vintage_table` count every loan of a cohort, also the "
"loans that were repaid early and can no longer default. Its marginal PDs therefore already allow "
"for early repayment, and its conditional PDs are conditional on no default, not on the loan still"
" being on book."
msgstr ""
"`kivi.vintage.vintage_table` 的累计坏账率计入批次中的每一笔贷款，也包括提前还清、不会再违约的贷款。因此它的边际 PD 已经考虑了提前还款，它的条件 PD "
"是以未违约为条件，而不是以贷款仍在账上为条件。"

msgid ""
"A vintage table has one curve per cohort, and the months on book that a cohort has not reached "
"stay missing:"
msgstr "Vintage 表每个批次一条曲线，批次尚未达到的账龄保持缺失："

msgid ""
"Row :math:`i` of a transition matrix holds the probabilities of moving from state :math:`i`, such"
" as a rating grade or a delinquency bucket, to each state over one period. If the movements "
"follow a time-homogeneous Markov chain, the :math:`h`-th power of the matrix holds the "
"probabilities over :math:`h` periods, and its default column the cumulative PD of each starting "
"state."
msgstr ""
"转移矩阵的第 :math:`i` 行给出一期内从状态 :math:`i` （例如某个评级或逾期档位）迁移到各个状态的概率。如果迁移服从时齐马尔可夫链，矩阵的 :math:`h` 次幂给出 "
":math:`h` 期内的迁移概率，其违约列就是每个起始状态的累计 PD。"

msgid "**matrix**"
msgstr "**matrix**"

msgid ""
"Square matrix of the probabilities of moving between the states over one period, such as a year "
"or a month, for example the result of `kivi.vintage.transition_matrix` with ``normalize=True``. "
"Each row holds probabilities from 0 to 1 that add up to 1, except that the row of the default "
"state is not used. The states of a DataFrame are its index, which must equal its columns; the "
"states of an array are the positions 0, 1, and so on."
msgstr ""
"一期（例如一年或一个月）内各状态之间迁移概率的方阵，例如 `kivi.vintage.transition_matrix` 在 ``normalize=True`` 时的结果。每一行是取值在 0"
" 到 1 之间、和为 1 的概率，但违约状态所在的行不会被使用。DataFrame 的状态是其索引，必须与列相同；数组的状态是位置 0、1，依此类推。"

msgid "**horizons**"
msgstr "**horizons**"

msgid "int or array_like"
msgstr "int 或 array_like"

msgid ""
"Numbers of periods after which to report the cumulative PD: a positive integer :math:`n` for "
"every horizon from 1 to :math:`n`, or increasing positive integers, such as ``[12, 24, 36]``."
msgstr "报告累计 PD 的期数：正整数 :math:`n` 表示从 1 到 :math:`n` 的每一个期限，也可以是递增的正整数序列，例如 ``[12, 24, 36]`` 。"

msgid "**default_state**"
msgstr "**default_state**"

msgid "optional"
msgstr "可选"

msgid ""
"Label of the default state. By default the last state, the worst one when the states are ordered "
"from the best to the worst, as for `kivi.vintage.transition_matrix`."
msgstr "违约状态的标签。默认取最后一个状态；状态按从最好到最差排列时（如 `kivi.vintage.transition_matrix` ），它就是最差的状态。"

msgid ""
"Cumulative PD with one row per starting state, indexed by ``state`` or, for states with several "
"levels, by the levels of the index of `matrix`, and one column per horizon, labelled ``horizon``."
" The row of the default state is 1."
msgstr "累计 PD，每个起始状态一行（索引名为 ``state`` ；状态有多个层级时，索引为 `matrix` 索引的各层级），每个期限一列（列名为 ``horizon`` ）。违约状态所在的行为 1。"

msgid ""
"If `matrix` is not a square, two-dimensional matrix of real numbers, a DataFrame's index and "
"columns differ or have duplicates, `default_state` is not one of the states, or a row of another "
"state has a missing value or a value outside [0, 1] or does not add up to 1. Also if `horizons` "
"is not a positive integer or a sequence of increasing positive integers."
msgstr ""
"如果 `matrix` 不是由实数构成的二维方阵，DataFrame 的索引与列不同或有重复， `default_state` 不是其中的状态，或者其他状态所在的行含有缺失值、有取值超出 [0,"
" 1] 或之和不为 1。此外，如果 `horizons` 不是正整数，也不是递增的正整数序列。"

msgid "Transition matrix of observed movements."
msgstr "由观测到的迁移得到的转移矩阵。"

msgid ":obj:`convert_pd`"
msgstr ":obj:`convert_pd`"

msgid "Marginal and conditional PDs from the cumulative PDs."
msgstr "由累计 PD 得到的边际 PD 和条件 PD。"

msgid ""
"The default state is made absorbing: its row is replaced by one that stays in default with "
"probability 1. Exposures that cure from default in the data therefore still count as defaulted, "
"as in the ever-bad rates of `kivi.vintage.vintage_table`. With this matrix :math:`P` and the "
"default state :math:`d`, the cumulative PD of state :math:`i` at horizon :math:`h` is"
msgstr ""
"违约状态被设为吸收态：它所在的行被替换为以概率 1 停留在违约状态的行。因此，数据中从违约状态回到正常的敞口仍算作违约，与 `kivi.vintage.vintage_table` "
"的“曾经为坏”比例一致。对于这个矩阵 :math:`P` 和违约状态 :math:`d` ，状态 :math:`i` 在期限 :math:`h` 的累计 PD 为"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "\\mathrm{PD}_i(h) = (P^h)_{id}."
msgstr "\\mathrm{PD}_i(h) = (P^h)_{id}."

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"It never decreases with the horizon and never exceeds 1. Because :math:`P^{a+b} = P^a P^b`, the "
"PD at :math:`a + b` periods is the PD at :math:`b` periods of the states reached after :math:`a` "
"periods, weighted by the probabilities of reaching them."
msgstr ""
"它不随期限下降，也不会超过 1。由于 :math:`P^{a+b} = P^a P^b` ， :math:`a + b` 期的 PD 等于 :math:`a` 期后所到达各状态的 "
":math:`b` 期 PD，以到达这些状态的概率加权。"

msgid ""
"The projection assumes that the probabilities of moving between states are the same in every "
"period and do not depend on how long an exposure has been in its state or on book. A matrix "
"estimated over one year gives annual PDs, and a monthly one monthly PDs. Rows must add up to 1 "
"within 1e-9; divide a published matrix that was rounded by its row sums first."
msgstr ""
"这一推算假设各状态之间的迁移概率每一期都相同，且与敞口在当前状态或在账上停留的时间无关。用一年数据估计的矩阵给出年度 PD，月度矩阵给出月度 PD。每行之和与 1 的差不得超过 "
"1e-9；经过舍入的公开矩阵，请先把每行除以该行之和。"

msgid ""
"After two periods, state A has defaulted with probability 0.90 × 0.02 + 0.08 × 0.20 + 0.02 = "
"0.054."
msgstr "两期之后，状态 A 违约的概率为 0.90 × 0.02 + 0.08 × 0.20 + 0.02 = 0.054。"

msgid ""
"The expected credit loss of IFRS 9 adds up, over the periods after the reporting date, the "
"probability of a default in each period times the loss given default and the exposure at default "
"in that period, discounted to the reporting date at the effective interest rate. Pass the number "
"of periods in 12 months as `horizon` for the 12-month expected credit loss of stage 1, and leave "
"it out for the lifetime expected credit loss of stages 2 and 3."
msgstr ""
"IFRS 9 的预期信用损失对报告日之后的各期求和：每一期的违约概率乘以该期的违约损失率和违约风险敞口，再按实际利率折现到报告日。把 12 个月对应的期数作为 `horizon` "
"传入，得到第一阶段的 12 个月预期信用损失；不传则得到第二、三阶段的整个存续期预期信用损失。"

msgid ""
"Marginal PDs with one row per account and one column per period after the reporting date: column "
":math:`t` holds the probability, seen at the reporting date, that the account defaults in period "
":math:`t`. Each row adds up to at most 1. `convert_pd` gives the marginal PDs of a cumulative or "
"conditional term structure. Booleans count as 0 and 1."
msgstr ""
"边际 PD，每个账户一行，报告日之后每一期一列：第 :math:`t` 列是在报告日看来该账户在第 :math:`t` 期违约的概率。每行之和至多为 1。 `convert_pd` "
"可由累计或条件期限结构得到边际 PD。布尔值按 0 和 1 计。"

msgid "**lgd**"
msgstr "**lgd**"

msgid "float, array_like or pandas.DataFrame"
msgstr "float、array_like 或 pandas.DataFrame"

msgid ""
"Loss given default as a share of the exposure at default, from 0 to 1: one value for all accounts"
" and periods, a one-dimensional array_like with one value per account, or a two-dimensional "
"schedule with one value per account and period. A two-dimensional array may also have one row for"
" all accounts or one column for all periods."
msgstr ""
"违约损失率，即占违约风险敞口的比例，取值在 0 到 1 之间：可以是适用于所有账户和各期的一个值，每个账户一个值的一维 "
"array_like，或每个账户每期一个值的二维计划表。二维数组也可以只有一行（适用于所有账户）或只有一列（适用于各期）。"

msgid "**ead**"
msgstr "**ead**"

msgid ""
"Exposure at default, finite and non-negative, in the same forms as `lgd`: one value, one value "
"per account, such as the balance at the reporting date, or a schedule, such as the balance "
"expected in each period. Give the periods after the maturity of an account an exposure of 0. "
"Series and DataFrames with one row per account must have identical indices, and DataFrames with "
"one column per period identical columns. A single row or column is broadcast, so with one account"
" or one period only the labels of `probability` are used."
msgstr ""
"违约风险敞口，须为有限非负值，形式与 `lgd` 相同：一个值，每个账户一个值（例如报告日的余额），或计划表（例如每期预计的余额）。账户到期之后的各期，敞口请设为 0。每个账户一行的 "
"Series 和 DataFrame 必须具有相同的索引，每期一列的 DataFrame 必须具有相同的列。只有一行或一列的输入会被广播，因此只有一个账户或一期时，只使用 "
"`probability` 的标签。"

msgid "**rate**"
msgstr "**rate**"

msgid "float or array_like"
msgstr "float 或 array_like"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Effective interest rate per period at which the losses are discounted, greater than -1, as one "
"value or one value per account. For monthly periods and an annual rate :math:`r`, pass :math:`(1 "
"+ r)^{1/12} - 1`. Pass 0 to leave the losses undiscounted."
msgstr ""
"用于折现损失的每期实际利率，须大于 -1，可以是一个值，也可以每个账户一个值。按月分期、年利率为 :math:`r` 时，传入 :math:`(1 + r)^{1/12} - 1` 。传入 0 "
"表示不折现。"

msgid "**horizon**"
msgstr "**horizon**"

msgid "int, optional"
msgstr "int，可选"

msgid ""
"Number of periods to add up, starting from period 1: 12 for monthly periods, or 1 for annual "
"ones, gives the 12-month expected credit loss. By default all the periods of `probability`, which"
" give the lifetime expected credit loss."
msgstr "从第 1 期起求和的期数：按月分期时为 12，按年分期时为 1，得到 12 个月预期信用损失。默认取 `probability` 的全部期数，得到整个存续期预期信用损失。"

msgid ""
"Expected credit loss of each account, in the units of `ead`. If `probability` is a DataFrame, or "
"another input with one row per account of several is a pandas object, a Series named "
"``expected_credit_loss`` with its index; otherwise an array."
msgstr ""
"每个账户的预期信用损失，单位与 `ead` 相同。如果 `probability` 是 DataFrame，或在有多个账户时另一个每个账户一行的输入是 pandas 对象，返回名为 "
"``expected_credit_loss`` 、具有其索引的 Series；否则返回数组。"

msgid ""
"If `probability` is not two-dimensional with at least one account and one period, an input is not"
" real and numeric or does not have one of the shapes described, or pandas inputs have different "
"indices or columns. Also if `probability` or `lgd` has a value outside [0, 1], a row of "
"`probability` adds up to more than 1, `ead` has a negative or infinite value, `rate` is infinite,"
" not greater than -1 or makes a discount factor overflow, or `horizon` is not a positive integer "
"up to the number of periods."
msgstr ""
"如果 `probability` 不是至少有一个账户和一期的二维输入，某个输入不是实数数值或不具有上述任何一种形状，或 pandas 输入的索引或列不同。此外，如果 `probability` "
"或 `lgd` 有取值超出 [0, 1]， `probability` 某一行之和超过 1， `ead` 含有负值或无穷值， `rate` 为无穷值、不大于 -1 或使折现因子溢出，或者 "
"`horizon` 不是不超过期数的正整数。"

msgid "Marginal PDs from cumulative or conditional ones."
msgstr "由累计或条件 PD 得到的边际 PD。"

msgid ":obj:`assign_stages`"
msgstr ":obj:`assign_stages`"

msgid "Stage of each account, which decides the horizon."
msgstr "每个账户的阶段，它决定了求和的期限。"

msgid ":obj:`stage_table`"
msgstr ":obj:`stage_table`"

msgid "Exposure and expected credit loss by stage."
msgstr "按阶段汇总的敞口和预期信用损失。"

msgid ":obj:`kivi.strategy.expected_loss`"
msgstr ":obj:`kivi.strategy.expected_loss`"

msgid "Expected loss over a single horizon."
msgstr "单一期限内的预期损失。"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"For an account with the marginal PD :math:`m_t`, the loss given default :math:`\\mathrm{LGD}_t` "
"and the exposure at default :math:`\\mathrm{EAD}_t` of period :math:`t`, and the effective "
"interest rate :math:`r` per period,"
msgstr ""
"对于第 :math:`t` 期边际 PD 为 :math:`m_t` 、违约损失率为 :math:`\\mathrm{LGD}_t` 、违约风险敞口为 "
":math:`\\mathrm{EAD}_t` ，每期实际利率为 :math:`r` 的账户，"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\\mathrm{ECL} = \\sum_{t=1}^{H} m_t \\, \\mathrm{LGD}_t \\,\n"
"               \\mathrm{EAD}_t \\, (1 + r)^{-t},"
msgstr ""
"\\mathrm{ECL} = \\sum_{t=1}^{H} m_t \\, \\mathrm{LGD}_t \\,\n"
"               \\mathrm{EAD}_t \\, (1 + r)^{-t},"

msgid "where :math:`H` is `horizon` or the number of periods. The conventions are:"
msgstr "其中 :math:`H` 为 `horizon` 或期数。约定如下："

msgid ""
"Period 1 starts at the reporting date and ends one period later; period :math:`t` ends :math:`t` "
"periods after the reporting date."
msgstr "第 1 期从报告日开始，一期后结束；第 :math:`t` 期在报告日之后 :math:`t` 期结束。"

msgid ""
"A default in period :math:`t` is taken to occur at the end of the period, so its loss is "
"discounted over :math:`t` periods."
msgstr "第 :math:`t` 期的违约视为发生在该期期末，因此其损失折现 :math:`t` 期。"

msgid ""
"The marginal PDs are not conditional on survival: they are seen from the reporting date and add "
"up to the cumulative PD. For an account that has not defaulted by the reporting date, convert the"
" conditional PDs of its term structure from its age at the reporting date on, with "
"``kind=\"conditional\"`` and ``to=\"marginal\"``."
msgstr ""
"边际 PD 不以存续为条件：它们是在报告日看来的概率，之和等于累计 PD。对于截至报告日未违约的账户，请把其期限结构中从报告日时的账龄开始的条件 PD 用 "
"``kind=\"conditional\"`` 和 ``to=\"marginal\"`` 转换。"

msgid ""
"The columns must cover the remaining life of the longest account. An account that matures within "
"the horizon has an exposure of 0 after maturity, so its 12-month and lifetime expected credit "
"losses are equal."
msgstr "各列必须覆盖期限最长的账户的剩余存续期。在求和期限内到期的账户，到期后的敞口为 0，因此其 12 个月预期信用损失与整个存续期预期信用损失相等。"

msgid ""
"An exposure already in default at the reporting date has defaulted at that date, not at the end "
"of a period. Give it a marginal PD of 1 in period 1 and a rate of 0, so that its expected credit "
"loss is its LGD times its EAD: the LGD of a defaulted exposure usually discounts the recoveries "
"already."
msgstr ""
"报告日已经违约的敞口在报告日就已违约，而不是在某一期期末。请为其设置第 1 期边际 PD 为 1、利率为 0，使其预期信用损失等于 LGD 乘以 EAD：已违约敞口的 LGD "
"通常已经对回收款做了折现。"

msgid ""
"A missing PD, LGD or EAD in a period that is added up, or a missing rate, gives the account a "
"missing expected credit loss, as in `kivi.strategy.expected_loss`. Missing values in the periods "
"after `horizon` are not used."
msgstr ""
"若求和的某一期 PD、LGD 或 EAD 缺失，或者利率缺失，该账户的预期信用损失为缺失，与 `kivi.strategy.expected_loss` 一致。 `horizon` "
"之后各期的缺失值不会被使用。"

msgid ""
"The first account loses 0.02 × 0.5 × 1000 / 1.05 = 9.52 in period 1, 0.03 × 0.5 × 700 / 1.05² = "
"9.52 in period 2 and 0.03 × 0.5 × 400 / 1.05³ = 5.18 in period 3."
msgstr ""
"第一个账户在第 1 期损失 0.02 × 0.5 × 1000 / 1.05 = 9.52，在第 2 期损失 0.03 × 0.5 × 700 / 1.05² = 9.52，在第 3 期损失 "
"0.03 × 0.5 × 400 / 1.05³ = 5.18。"

msgid ""
"IFRS 9 moves an exposure to stage 2 when its credit risk has increased significantly since "
"initial recognition. A common quantitative test compares the PD at the reporting date with the PD"
" expected at origination, as a ratio, a difference or both. The thresholds are the policy of the "
"reporting entity, not values set by the standard, so they have no defaults."
msgstr ""
"当敞口的信用风险自初始确认以来显著增加时，IFRS 9 将其划入第二阶段。常见的定量测试比较报告日的 PD 与发放时预期的 "
"PD，可以看比率、差值或两者兼看。阈值是报告主体的政策，而不是准则规定的数值，因此没有默认值。"

msgid "PD of each exposure at the reporting date, from 0 to 1."
msgstr "每笔敞口在报告日的 PD，取值在 0 到 1 之间。"

msgid "**origination_probability**"
msgstr "**origination_probability**"

msgid ""
"PD of each exposure expected at initial recognition for the same period, from 0 to 1. If both "
"inputs are Series, they must have identical indices; otherwise they are matched by position."
msgstr "每笔敞口在初始确认时对同一期间预期的 PD，取值在 0 到 1 之间。如果两个输入都是 Series，二者的索引必须完全相同；否则按位置对应。"

msgid "**relative**"
msgstr "**relative**"

msgid "float or None"
msgstr "float 或 None"

msgid ""
"The increase is significant if `probability` is more than `relative` times "
"`origination_probability`, so 2 flags the PDs that more than doubled. It must be greater than 1. "
"None leaves out this test."
msgstr ""
"如果 `probability` 超过 `origination_probability` 的 `relative` 倍，即为显著增加，因此 2 会标记 PD 增加到两倍以上的敞口。必须大于 "
"1。传入 None 表示不做这项测试。"

msgid "**absolute**"
msgstr "**absolute**"

msgid ""
"The increase is significant if `probability` exceeds `origination_probability` by more than "
"`absolute`, in units of PD, so 0.01 flags the PDs that rose by more than one percentage point. It"
" must be between 0 and 1. None leaves out this test."
msgstr ""
"如果 `probability` 比 `origination_probability` 高出 `absolute` 以上（以 PD 为单位），即为显著增加，因此 0.01 会标记 PD "
"上升超过一个百分点的敞口。必须介于 0 和 1 之间。传入 None 表示不做这项测试。"

msgid ""
"Booleans that are True for a significant increase. If an input is a Series, a Series named "
"``significant_increase`` with its index; otherwise an array."
msgstr "布尔值，信用风险显著增加时为 True。如果某个输入是 Series，返回名为 ``significant_increase`` 、具有其索引的 Series；否则返回数组。"

msgid ""
"If the inputs are empty, not one-dimensional, of different lengths, Series with different "
"indices, not real and numeric, or have a missing value or a value outside [0, 1]. Also if "
"`relative` is not None or a number greater than 1, `absolute` is not None or a number between 0 "
"and 1, or both are None."
msgstr ""
"如果输入为空、不是一维、长度不同、是索引不同的 Series、不是实数数值，或含有缺失值或 [0, 1] 以外的值。此外，如果 `relative` 既不是 None 也不是大于 1 的数， "
"`absolute` 既不是 None 也不是介于 0 和 1 之间的数，或者两者都是 None。"

msgid "Stages from the flags and the days past due."
msgstr "由这些标记和逾期天数确定阶段。"

msgid "Cumulative PDs over the remaining life from a term structure."
msgstr "由期限结构得到剩余存续期内的累计 PD。"

msgid ""
"With the PD :math:`p` at the reporting date and the PD :math:`p_0` expected at origination, the "
"tests are"
msgstr "设报告日的 PD 为 :math:`p` ，发放时预期的 PD 为 :math:`p_0` ，测试为"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"p > \\mathrm{relative} \\cdot p_0 \\qquad \\text{and} \\qquad\n"
"p - p_0 > \\mathrm{absolute}."
msgstr ""
"p > \\mathrm{relative} \\cdot p_0 \\qquad \\text{且} \\qquad\n"
"p - p_0 > \\mathrm{absolute}."

msgid ""
"Both comparisons are strict, and a PD that meets a threshold up to the rounding of floating-point"
" numbers, within a few units in the last place of the PD, meets it exactly: in floating point, "
"``0.04 - 0.03`` exceeds ``0.01`` and ``1.5 * 0.30`` is below ``0.45``, but neither pair is "
"flagged."
msgstr ""
"两项比较都是严格的；PD 在浮点数舍入误差范围内（与 PD 的末位相差几个单位以内）等于阈值时，视为恰好等于阈值：在浮点运算中 ``0.04 - 0.03`` 大于 ``0.01`` ， "
"``1.5 * 0.30`` 小于 ``0.45`` ，但这两对都不会被标记。"

msgid ""
"With both thresholds, an increase is significant only if it passes both tests, so that the "
"absolute threshold keeps small changes of low PDs from counting. For a rule under which either "
"test suffices, combine two calls with ``|``, each with one threshold. Qualitative criteria, such "
"as a watch list or forbearance, combine with the flags in the same way."
msgstr ""
"同时给出两个阈值时，只有两项测试都通过才算显著增加，这样绝对阈值可以避免低 PD 的微小变化被计入。若规则只要求通过任一项测试，请分别用一个阈值调用两次，再用 ``|`` "
"合并。定性标准（例如关注名单或债务重组）也以同样的方式与这些标记合并。"

msgid ""
"IFRS 9 assesses the change in the risk of a default over the expected life of the exposure, and "
"allows the risk over the next 12 months where it gives a reasonable approximation. Compare PDs of"
" the same horizon: for a lifetime PD, the PD over the same remaining life that was expected at "
"origination."
msgstr ""
"IFRS 9 评估的是敞口在预计存续期内违约风险的变化；若未来 12 个月的违约风险能给出合理的近似，也允许使用它。请比较相同期限的 PD：对于存续期 PD，应与发放时对同一剩余存续期预期的 "
"PD 比较。"

msgid ""
"The first PD quadrupled but rose by only 0.3 percentage points, and the last one rose by 4 points"
" without doubling."
msgstr "第一个 PD 增加到四倍，但只上升了 0.3 个百分点；最后一个上升了 4 个百分点，但没有翻倍。"

msgid ""
"Stage 1 holds the exposures whose credit risk has not increased significantly since initial "
"recognition, stage 2 those whose credit risk has, and stage 3 the credit-impaired exposures. The "
"days past due act as backstops: an exposure more than `stage_2_days` past due is at least in "
"stage 2, and one at least `stage_3_days` past due, or flagged as defaulted, is in stage 3."
msgstr ""
"第一阶段包括自初始确认以来信用风险没有显著增加的敞口，第二阶段包括信用风险已显著增加的敞口，第三阶段包括已发生信用减值的敞口。逾期天数作为兜底标准：逾期超过 `stage_2_days` "
"天的敞口至少处于第二阶段，逾期至少 `stage_3_days` 天或被标记为违约的敞口处于第三阶段。"

msgid "**significant_increase**"
msgstr "**significant_increase**"

msgid ""
"Whether the credit risk of each exposure has increased significantly since initial recognition, "
"as booleans or 0 and 1, such as the result of the function `significant_increase`, possibly "
"combined with qualitative criteria."
msgstr "每笔敞口的信用风险自初始确认以来是否显著增加，取布尔值或 0 和 1，例如函数 `significant_increase` 的结果，也可以与定性标准合并。"

msgid "**days_past_due**"
msgstr "**days_past_due**"

msgid ""
"Days past due of each exposure at the reporting date, finite and non-negative. Without it, the "
"backstops do not apply."
msgstr "每笔敞口在报告日的逾期天数，须为有限非负值。不传入时不适用兜底标准。"

msgid "**defaulted**"
msgstr "**defaulted**"

msgid ""
"Whether each exposure is credit-impaired, usually because it is in default under the entity's "
"definition of default, as booleans or 0 and 1. These exposures are in stage 3."
msgstr "每笔敞口是否已发生信用减值（通常是因为按主体的违约定义处于违约状态），取布尔值或 0 和 1。这些敞口处于第三阶段。"

msgid "**stage_2_days**"
msgstr "**stage_2_days**"

msgid "float, default 30"
msgstr "float，默认 30"

msgid ""
"Exposures more than this many days past due are at least in stage 2. The default follows the "
"rebuttable presumption of IFRS 9, paragraph 5.5.11, that credit risk has increased significantly "
"when contractual payments are more than 30 days past due."
msgstr "逾期超过该天数的敞口至少处于第二阶段。默认值依据 IFRS 9 第 5.5.11 段的可推翻假设：合同付款逾期超过 30 天时，信用风险已显著增加。"

msgid "**stage_3_days**"
msgstr "**stage_3_days**"

msgid "float, default 90"
msgstr "float，默认 90"

msgid ""
"Exposures this many days past due or more are in stage 3. The default follows the rebuttable "
"presumption of IFRS 9, paragraph B5.5.37, that default occurs no later than when a financial "
"asset is 90 days past due. It must be greater than `stage_2_days`."
msgstr "逾期达到或超过该天数的敞口处于第三阶段。默认值依据 IFRS 9 第 B5.5.37 段的可推翻假设：违约的发生不晚于金融资产逾期 90 天之时。必须大于 `stage_2_days` 。"

msgid ""
"Stage of each exposure, 1, 2 or 3, as integers. If an input is a Series, a Series named ``stage``"
" with its index; otherwise an array."
msgstr "每笔敞口的阶段，取整数 1、2 或 3。如果某个输入是 Series，返回名为 ``stage`` 、具有其索引的 Series；否则返回数组。"

msgid ""
"If the inputs are empty, not one-dimensional, of different lengths or Series with different "
"indices, `significant_increase` or `defaulted` has a value other than 0 and 1, or `days_past_due`"
" is not real and numeric or has a missing, negative or infinite value. Also if `stage_2_days` or "
"`stage_3_days` is not a finite, non-negative number, or `stage_3_days` is not greater than "
"`stage_2_days`."
msgstr ""
"如果输入为空、不是一维、长度不同或是索引不同的 Series， `significant_increase` 或 `defaulted` 含有 0 和 1 以外的值，或者 "
"`days_past_due` 不是实数数值或含有缺失值、负值或无穷值。此外，如果 `stage_2_days` 或 `stage_3_days` 不是有限的非负数，或 "
"`stage_3_days` 不大于 `stage_2_days` 。"

msgid ":obj:`significant_increase`"
msgstr ":obj:`significant_increase`"

msgid "Quantitative test of a significant increase."
msgstr "信用风险显著增加的定量测试。"

msgid "12-month and lifetime expected credit losses."
msgstr "12 个月和整个存续期的预期信用损失。"

msgid ""
"The stage of an exposure is 3 if it is defaulted or at least `stage_3_days` past due, otherwise 2"
" if `significant_increase` is true or it is more than `stage_2_days` past due, and otherwise 1. "
"With the defaults, an exposure exactly 30 days past due therefore stays in stage 1, and one "
"exactly 90 days past due is in stage 3, as the wording of the two presumptions says."
msgstr ""
"敞口已违约或逾期至少 `stage_3_days` 天时处于第三阶段；否则，若 `significant_increase` 为真或逾期超过 `stage_2_days` "
"天，处于第二阶段；其余处于第一阶段。因此按默认值，恰好逾期 30 天的敞口仍处于第一阶段，而恰好逾期 90 天的敞口处于第三阶段，与两项假设的表述一致。"

msgid ""
"IFRS 9 defines credit-impaired exposures by events that hurt their expected cash flows, such as a"
" default or the significant financial difficulty of the borrower. In practice, entities usually "
"align them with their definition of default. The thresholds, the definition of default and the "
"treatment of cures are the policy of the reporting entity. Probation periods, during which an "
"exposure that no longer meets a criterion stays in its stage, need the history of each exposure "
"and are not applied."
msgstr ""
"IFRS 9 "
"按对预计现金流量产生不利影响的事件来界定已发生信用减值的敞口，例如违约或借款人发生重大财务困难。实务中，主体通常使其与自身的违约定义保持一致。阈值、违约定义以及回到正常的处理都是报告主体的政策。观察期（敞口不再满足某项标准后仍留在原阶段的期间）需要每笔敞口的历史，此处不予处理。"

msgid ""
"Each row adds up the exposures and the loss allowances of one stage and gives their ratio, the "
"coverage ratio that banks report by stage."
msgstr "每行汇总一个阶段的敞口和损失准备，并给出二者之比，即银行按阶段披露的覆盖率。"

msgid "**stage**"
msgstr "**stage**"

msgid "Stage of each exposure, 1, 2 or 3, such as the result of `assign_stages`."
msgstr "每笔敞口的阶段，取 1、2 或 3，例如 `assign_stages` 的结果。"

msgid "**exposure**"
msgstr "**exposure**"

msgid ""
"Exposure of each account at the reporting date, such as its gross carrying amount, finite and "
"non-negative."
msgstr "每个账户在报告日的敞口，例如其账面余额，须为有限非负值。"

msgid "**allowance**"
msgstr "**allowance**"

msgid ""
"Loss allowance of each account, finite and non-negative: its 12-month expected credit loss in "
"stage 1 and its lifetime expected credit loss in stages 2 and 3. Series inputs must have "
"identical indices; otherwise the inputs are matched by position."
msgstr "每个账户的损失准备，须为有限非负值：第一阶段为其 12 个月预期信用损失，第二、三阶段为其整个存续期预期信用损失。作为 Series 传入的输入，索引必须完全相同；否则按位置对应。"

msgid ""
"Non-negative weight of each exposure, such as the inverse of its sampling rate, matched like "
"`exposure`. Counts, exposures and allowances become sums of weights, so integer weights give the "
"same table as repeating rows."
msgstr "每笔敞口的非负权重，例如其抽样比例的倒数，对应方式与 `exposure` 相同。计数、敞口和损失准备都变为加权和，因此整数权重与重复相应行得到的表相同。"

msgid ""
"One row for each of the stages 1, 2 and 3, indexed by ``stage``, also for a stage without "
"exposures, with the columns described in the Notes."
msgstr "阶段 1、2、3 各占一行（索引名为 ``stage`` ），没有敞口的阶段也保留，各列含义见“说明”。"

msgid ""
"If the inputs are empty, not one-dimensional, of different lengths or Series with different "
"indices, or not real and numeric. Also if `stage` has a value other than 1, 2 and 3, `exposure` "
"or `allowance` has a missing, negative or infinite value, or `weights` is not numeric or does not"
" give each exposure one finite, non-negative weight with a positive total."
msgstr ""
"如果输入为空、不是一维、长度不同或是索引不同的 Series，或不是实数数值。此外，如果 `stage` 含有 1、2、3 以外的值， `exposure` 或 `allowance` "
"含有缺失值、负值或无穷值，或者 `weights` 不是数值，或没有为每笔敞口给出一个有限非负、总和为正的权重。"

msgid "Stage of each exposure."
msgstr "每笔敞口的阶段。"

msgid ":obj:`kivi.strategy.expected_loss_table`"
msgstr ":obj:`kivi.strategy.expected_loss_table`"

msgid "Exposure and expected loss by grade."
msgstr "按等级汇总的敞口和预期损失。"

msgid ""
"For the exposures :math:`i` of a stage, with weights :math:`w_i`, 1 without `weights`, the "
"columns are:"
msgstr "对于一个阶段中的敞口 :math:`i` ，权重为 :math:`w_i` （不传 `weights` 时为 1），各列为："

msgid "``total``: the number of exposures, :math:`\\sum_i w_i`;"
msgstr "``total``：敞口数， :math:`\\sum_i w_i`；"

msgid "``exposure``: :math:`\\sum_i w_i E_i`, with the exposures :math:`E_i`;"
msgstr "``exposure`` ： :math:`\\sum_i w_i E_i` ，其中 :math:`E_i` 为敞口；"

msgid ""
"``exposure_share``: the stage's share of the exposure of all stages, NaN for every stage when the"
" total exposure is 0;"
msgstr "``exposure_share`` ：该阶段占全部阶段敞口的比例；总敞口为 0 时，每个阶段均为 NaN；"

msgid "``expected_credit_loss``: :math:`\\sum_i w_i L_i`, with the loss allowances :math:`L_i`;"
msgstr "``expected_credit_loss`` ： :math:`\\sum_i w_i L_i` ，其中 :math:`L_i` 为损失准备；"

msgid "``coverage``: ``expected_credit_loss`` divided by ``exposure``, NaN for a stage without exposure."
msgstr "``coverage`` ： ``expected_credit_loss`` 除以 ``exposure`` ，没有敞口的阶段为 NaN。"

msgid ""
"The portfolio's exposure and loss allowance are the sums of the ``exposure`` and "
"``expected_credit_loss`` columns, and its coverage ratio is the second sum divided by the first."
msgstr "资产组合的敞口和损失准备分别是 ``exposure`` 列和 ``expected_credit_loss`` 列之和，其覆盖率是后者之和除以前者之和。"

msgid "Model performance"
msgstr "模型表现"

msgid ""
"Measure how well a score that rises with the event probability separates events from non-events. "
":func:`~kivi.metrics.roc_auc`, :func:`~kivi.metrics.gini` and :func:`~kivi.metrics.ks` summarize "
"the ranking, :func:`~kivi.metrics.roc_table` lists the ROC curve, "
":func:`~kivi.metrics.roc_auc_interval` and :func:`~kivi.metrics.delong_test` add DeLong's "
"standard errors, :func:`~kivi.metrics.gains_table` breaks the ranking down by score band, and "
":func:`~kivi.metrics.brier_score` compares probabilities with outcomes."
msgstr ""
"衡量随事件概率升高而增大的评分区分事件与非事件的能力。 :func:`~kivi.metrics.roc_auc` 、 :func:`~kivi.metrics.gini` 和 "
":func:`~kivi.metrics.ks` 概括排序能力， :func:`~kivi.metrics.roc_table` 列出 ROC 曲线， "
":func:`~kivi.metrics.roc_auc_interval` 和 :func:`~kivi.metrics.delong_test` 给出 DeLong 标准误， "
":func:`~kivi.metrics.gains_table` 按评分段分解排序能力， :func:`~kivi.metrics.brier_score` 把概率与实际结果比较。"

msgid "See :doc:`/user_guide/metrics` for the definitions, examples and how to read a gains table."
msgstr "定义、示例以及如何解读增益表，见 :doc:`/user_guide/metrics` 。"

msgid ":py:obj:`roc_auc <kivi.metrics.roc_auc>`\\ \\(score\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, weights\\]\\)"
msgstr ":py:obj:`roc_auc <kivi.metrics.roc_auc>`\\ \\(score\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, weights\\]\\)"

msgid "Compute the area under the ROC curve of a score."
msgstr "计算评分的 ROC 曲线下面积。"

msgid ":py:obj:`gini <kivi.metrics.gini>`\\ \\(score\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, weights\\]\\)"
msgstr ":py:obj:`gini <kivi.metrics.gini>`\\ \\(score\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, weights\\]\\)"

msgid "Compute the Gini coefficient of a score."
msgstr "计算评分的 Gini 系数。"

msgid ":py:obj:`ks <kivi.metrics.ks>`\\ \\(score\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, weights\\]\\)"
msgstr ":py:obj:`ks <kivi.metrics.ks>`\\ \\(score\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, weights\\]\\)"

msgid "Compute the Kolmogorov-Smirnov statistic of a score."
msgstr "计算评分的 Kolmogorov-Smirnov 统计量。"

msgid ":py:obj:`roc_table <kivi.metrics.roc_table>`\\ \\(score\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, weights\\]\\)"
msgstr ":py:obj:`roc_table <kivi.metrics.roc_table>`\\ \\(score\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, weights\\]\\)"

msgid "Tabulate the ROC curve of a score, with one row per distinct score."
msgstr "列出评分的 ROC 曲线，每个不同的评分一行。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`roc_auc_interval <kivi.metrics.roc_auc_interval>`\\ \\(score\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, "
"level\\, ...\\]\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`roc_auc_interval <kivi.metrics.roc_auc_interval>`\\ \\(score\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, "
"level\\, ...\\]\\)"

msgid "Estimate the standard error and a confidence interval of the AUC."
msgstr "估计 AUC 的标准误和置信区间。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`delong_test <kivi.metrics.delong_test>`\\ \\(current\\, new\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, "
"...\\]\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`delong_test <kivi.metrics.delong_test>`\\ \\(current\\, new\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, "
"...\\]\\)"

msgid "Test whether two scores of the same observations have the same AUC."
msgstr "检验同一批观测的两个评分的 AUC 是否相同。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`gains_table <kivi.metrics.gains_table>`\\ \\(score\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, bins\\, "
"weights\\]\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`gains_table <kivi.metrics.gains_table>`\\ \\(score\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, bins\\, "
"weights\\]\\)"

msgid "Summarize events by score band, from the highest scores to the lowest."
msgstr "按评分段汇总事件，从最高评分到最低评分排列。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`brier_score <kivi.metrics.brier_score>`\\ \\(probability\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, "
"weights\\]\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`brier_score <kivi.metrics.brier_score>`\\ \\(probability\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, "
"weights\\]\\)"

msgid "Compute the Brier score of predicted event probabilities."
msgstr "计算预测事件概率的 Brier 分数。"

msgid ""
"The AUC is the probability that a randomly chosen event has a higher score than a randomly chosen"
" non-event, with ties counted as one half."
msgstr "AUC 是随机抽取的一个事件比随机抽取的一个非事件评分更高的概率，评分相同时计为二分之一。"

msgid ""
"The score comes first and the target second, as in `kivi.woe.woe_table`; scikit-learn's metrics "
"take the target first."
msgstr "评分在前、目标在后，与 `kivi.woe.woe_table` 相同；scikit-learn 的指标函数则把目标放在前面。"

msgid ""
"Finite numeric scores that are higher for a higher event probability. Negate scorecard points, "
"which are higher for a lower risk."
msgstr "有限的数值评分，事件概率越高，评分越高。评分卡分数越高表示风险越低，因此须取负后再传入。"

msgid ""
"Non-negative weight of each observation, such as the inverse of its sampling rate, matched like "
"`target`. Every count becomes a sum of weights, so integer weights give the same result as "
"repeating rows."
msgstr "每个观测的非负权重，例如其抽样比例的倒数，对应方式与 `target` 相同。每个计数都变为权重之和，因此整数权重与重复相应行的结果相同。"

msgid ""
"The AUC, from 0 to 1. A score unrelated to the target gives about 0.5, and a value below 0.5 "
"suggests that the score runs the other way."
msgstr "AUC，取值 0 到 1。与目标无关的评分约为 0.5，低于 0.5 则说明评分方向可能相反。"

msgid ""
"If the inputs are empty or not one-dimensional, their indices or lengths do not match, `target` "
"has a label other than 0 and 1 or lacks one of them, or `score` is not real and numeric or has a "
"missing or infinite value. Also if `weights` is not numeric, does not give each observation one "
"finite, non-negative weight, has an index other than that of `score`, or leaves a class without "
"weight."
msgstr ""
"如果输入为空或不是一维的，索引或长度不一致，`target` 含有 0 和 1 以外的标签或缺少其中之一，或 `score` 不是实数数值或含有缺失值、无穷值。此外，如果 `weights` "
"不是数值、没有为每个观测给出一个有限非负的权重、索引与 `score` 不同，或使某一类没有权重。"

msgid ":obj:`gini`"
msgstr ":obj:`gini`"

msgid "The same ranking measure on a scale from -1 to 1."
msgstr "同一排序度量，取值范围为 -1 到 1。"

msgid ":obj:`ks`"
msgstr ":obj:`ks`"

msgid "Largest gap between the score distributions of the two classes."
msgstr "两个类别评分分布之间的最大差距。"

msgid ":obj:`gains_table`"
msgstr ":obj:`gains_table`"

msgid "Event rates and captured events by score band."
msgstr "各评分段的事件率和捕获的事件。"

msgid ""
"With :math:`n_1` events and :math:`n_0` non-events, let :math:`R_1` be the sum of the ranks of "
"the events among all scores, where tied scores share their average rank. The Mann-Whitney "
"statistic gives"
msgstr "设有 :math:`n_1` 个事件和 :math:`n_0` 个非事件，:math:`R_1` 为事件在全部评分中的秩之和，相同评分取平均秩。由 Mann-Whitney 统计量得"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "\\mathrm{AUC} = \\frac{R_1 - n_1 (n_1 + 1) / 2}{n_1 n_0}."
msgstr "\\mathrm{AUC} = \\frac{R_1 - n_1 (n_1 + 1) / 2}{n_1 n_0}."

msgid ""
"With weights, each pair of an event :math:`i` and a non-event :math:`j` counts with weight "
":math:`w_i w_j`, and :math:`n_1` and :math:`n_0` are the total weights of the two classes."
msgstr "使用权重时，每一对事件 :math:`i` 与非事件 :math:`j` 以权重 :math:`w_i w_j` 计入， :math:`n_1` 和 :math:`n_0` 则是两类的权重总和。"

msgid ""
"J. A. Hanley and B. J. McNeil, \"The meaning and use of the area under a receiver operating "
"characteristic (ROC) curve\", Radiology, 143(1), pp. 29-36, 1982."
msgstr ""
"J. A. Hanley and B. J. McNeil, \"The meaning and use of the area under a receiver operating "
"characteristic (ROC) curve\", Radiology, 143(1), pp. 29-36, 1982."

msgid "[R8309ac12020d-1]_"
msgstr "[R8309ac12020d-1]_"

msgid "Scorecard points are higher for a lower risk, so negate them:"
msgstr "评分卡分数越高表示风险越低，因此要取负："

msgid ""
"The Gini coefficient rescales the AUC to run from -1 to 1, so that a score unrelated to the "
"target gives about 0."
msgstr "Gini 系数把 AUC 换算到 -1 到 1 的范围，使与目标无关的评分约为 0。"

msgid "The Gini coefficient, from -1 to 1. A negative value suggests that the score runs the other way."
msgstr "Gini 系数，取值 -1 到 1。负值说明评分方向可能相反。"

msgid ":obj:`roc_auc`"
msgstr ":obj:`roc_auc`"

msgid "The area under the ROC curve."
msgstr "ROC 曲线下面积。"

msgid "The Gini coefficient, also called the accuracy ratio, is"
msgstr "Gini 系数也称为准确性比率（accuracy ratio），其定义为"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "\\mathrm{Gini} = 2\\,\\mathrm{AUC} - 1."
msgstr "\\mathrm{Gini} = 2\\,\\mathrm{AUC} - 1."

msgid ""
"The KS statistic is the largest gap between the cumulative distribution of the scores of events "
"and that of non-events."
msgstr "KS 统计量是事件评分的累计分布与非事件评分的累计分布之间的最大差距。"

msgid "Finite numeric scores, such as predicted event probabilities."
msgstr "有限的数值评分，例如预测的事件概率。"

msgid "The largest gap, from 0 to 1."
msgstr "最大差距，取值 0 到 1。"

msgid "The gap at the edge of each score band."
msgstr "每个评分段边界处的差距。"

msgid "The probability that an event scores higher than a non-event."
msgstr "事件评分高于非事件评分的概率。"

msgid ""
"Let :math:`F_1` and :math:`F_0` be the empirical distribution functions of the scores of events "
"and of non-events. Then"
msgstr "设 :math:`F_1` 和 :math:`F_0` 分别为事件评分和非事件评分的经验分布函数，则"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "\\mathrm{KS} = \\max_t \\, \\lvert F_1(t) - F_0(t) \\rvert,"
msgstr "\\mathrm{KS} = \\max_t \\, \\lvert F_1(t) - F_0(t) \\rvert,"

msgid ""
"where :math:`t` runs over the observed scores. With weights, the distribution functions are "
"weighted. As in the two-sample Kolmogorov-Smirnov test, the gap is taken in absolute value, so "
"negated scores give the same KS; use the sign of `gini` to check the direction."
msgstr ""
"其中 :math:`t` 取遍观测到的评分。使用权重时，分布函数按权重计算。与双样本 Kolmogorov-Smirnov 检验一样，差距取绝对值，因此评分取负后 KS 不变；请用 `gini`"
" 的符号检查方向。"

msgid ""
"The largest gap can come from a region where the score runs the wrong way, for example when "
"events gather among the lowest scores as well as the highest. The KS then measures how far apart "
"the two distributions are rather than how well the score ranks events above non-events. The "
"cumulative shares in `gains_table` show where the gap occurs."
msgstr ""
"最大差距可能来自评分方向相反的区域，例如事件既集中在最高评分处，也集中在最低评分处。此时 KS 衡量的是两个分布相距多远，而不是评分把事件排在非事件之前的能力。`gains_table` "
"中的累计占比可以显示差距出现的位置。"

msgid "L. C. Thomas, D. B. Edelman and J. N. Crook, \"Credit Scoring and Its Applications\", SIAM, 2002."
msgstr "L. C. Thomas, D. B. Edelman and J. N. Crook, \"Credit Scoring and Its Applications\", SIAM, 2002."

msgid "[Rbfc1ea3c8bbd-1]_"
msgstr "[Rbfc1ea3c8bbd-1]_"

msgid ""
"Each row flags the observations that score at or above its threshold and counts the events and "
"non-events among them. Plotting ``true_positive_rate`` against ``false_positive_rate`` gives the "
"ROC curve, from the highest threshold to the lowest."
msgstr ""
"每一行标记评分不低于该行阈值的观测，并统计其中的事件数和非事件数。以 ``false_positive_rate`` 为横轴、 ``true_positive_rate`` "
"为纵轴作图，就得到从最高阈值到最低阈值的 ROC 曲线。"

msgid ""
"Non-negative weight of each observation, such as the inverse of its sampling rate, matched like "
"`target`. The counts become sums of weights, and a score whose observations all have zero weight "
"has no row, so integer weights give the same table as repeating rows."
msgstr "每个观测的非负权重，例如其抽样比例的倒数，对应方式与 `target` 相同。计数变为权重之和，所有观测权重都为零的评分不占一行，因此整数权重与重复相应行得到相同的表。"

msgid ""
"One row per threshold, in an index named ``threshold``: first infinity, which flags no "
"observation, then every distinct score from the highest to the lowest, which flags them all. The "
"columns are described in the Notes."
msgstr "每个阈值一行，索引名为 ``threshold`` ：第一行为无穷大，不标记任何观测；其后是从高到低的每个不同评分，最后一行标记全部观测。各列见“说明”。"

msgid "The area under the curve."
msgstr "曲线下面积。"

msgid "The largest gap between the two rates."
msgstr "两个比率之间的最大差距。"

msgid "The same cumulative shares by score band."
msgstr "按评分段计算的同样的累计占比。"

msgid ""
"``cum_non_event`` and ``cum_event``: non-events and events that score at or above the threshold, "
"or the sums of their weights;"
msgstr "``cum_non_event`` 和 ``cum_event`` ：评分不低于阈值的非事件数和事件数，或者它们的权重之和；"

msgid ""
"``false_positive_rate`` and ``true_positive_rate``: these counts as shares of all non-events and "
"of all events;"
msgstr "``false_positive_rate`` 和 ``true_positive_rate`` ：上述计数分别占全部非事件和全部事件的比例；"

msgid ""
"``precision``: ``cum_event`` divided by the sum of both counts, the event rate among the flagged "
"observations, which is NaN in the first row."
msgstr "``precision`` ： ``cum_event`` 除以两项计数之和，即被标记观测中的事件率，第一行为 NaN。"

msgid ""
"Tied scores share a row, so the curve crosses a tie diagonally. The trapezoids under the curve "
"therefore add up to `roc_auc`, which counts a tied pair as one half,"
msgstr "评分相同的观测共用一行，因此曲线沿对角方向越过并列的评分。于是曲线下各梯形的面积之和等于 `roc_auc` ，后者把评分相同的一对计为二分之一："

msgid ""
"\\mathrm{AUC} = \\sum_{k \\ge 1} (\\mathrm{FPR}_k - \\mathrm{FPR}_{k-1})\n"
"\\, \\frac{\\mathrm{TPR}_k + \\mathrm{TPR}_{k-1}}{2},"
msgstr ""
"\\mathrm{AUC} = \\sum_{k \\ge 1} (\\mathrm{FPR}_k - \\mathrm{FPR}_{k-1})\n"
"\\, \\frac{\\mathrm{TPR}_k + \\mathrm{TPR}_{k-1}}{2},"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"and the largest gap between the two rates, :math:`\\max_k \\lvert \\mathrm{TPR}_k - "
"\\mathrm{FPR}_k \\rvert`, is `ks`. The rows are those of ``sklearn.metrics.roc_curve`` with "
"``drop_intermediate=False``."
msgstr ""
"而两个比率之间的最大差距 :math:`\\max_k \\lvert \\mathrm{TPR}_k - \\mathrm{FPR}_k \\rvert` 等于 `ks` 。各行与 "
"``sklearn.metrics.roc_curve`` 在 ``drop_intermediate=False`` 时返回的点相同。"

msgid ""
"The standard error is that of DeLong, DeLong and Clarke-Pearson [R7ccb11fdd3fb-1]_, which makes "
"no assumption about the distribution of the scores. The interval of the Gini coefficient follows "
"from that of the AUC."
msgstr "标准误采用 DeLong、DeLong 和 Clarke-Pearson 的方法 [R7ccb11fdd3fb-1]_ ，不对评分的分布作任何假设。Gini 系数的区间由 AUC 的区间换算得到。"

msgid ""
"Binary labels, with 1 indicating the event. Without `weights` there must be at least two events "
"and two non-events. If `score` and `target` are both pandas Series, they must have identical "
"indices; otherwise they are matched by position."
msgstr ""
"二分类标签，1 表示事件。不使用 `weights` 时，至少要有两个事件和两个非事件。如果 `score` 和 `target` 都是 pandas "
"Series，二者的索引必须完全相同；否则按位置对应。"

msgid "**level**"
msgstr "**level**"

msgid "float, default 0.95"
msgstr "float，默认 0.95"

msgid "Confidence level of the interval, between 0 and 1."
msgstr "区间的置信水平，介于 0 和 1 之间。"

msgid ""
"Non-negative frequency weight of each observation, matched like `target`. An observation of "
"weight :math:`w` counts as :math:`w` observations, so integer weights give the same result as "
"repeating rows, standard error included. The weights of each class must add up to more than 1."
msgstr ""
"每个观测的非负频数权重，对应方式与 `target` 相同。权重为 :math:`w` 的观测计为 :math:`w` "
"个观测，因此整数权重与重复相应行的结果相同，标准误也是如此。每一类的权重之和必须大于 1。"

msgid ""
"Two rows, ``auc`` and ``gini``, in an index named ``statistic``, and the columns ``estimate``, "
"``se`` for the standard error, and ``lower`` and ``upper`` for the bounds of the interval."
msgstr ""
"两行 ``auc`` 和 ``gini`` ，位于名为 ``statistic`` 的索引中；列为 ``estimate`` 、表示标准误的 ``se`` ，以及表示区间上下限的 "
"``lower`` 和 ``upper`` 。"

msgid ""
"If the inputs are empty or not one-dimensional, their indices or lengths do not match, `target` "
"has a label other than 0 and 1 or, without `weights`, fewer than two of either, or `score` is not"
" real and numeric or has a missing or infinite value. Also if `level` is not a number between 0 "
"and 1, or if `weights` is not numeric, does not give each observation one finite, non-negative "
"weight, has an index other than that of `score`, or gives a class a total weight of 1 or less."
msgstr ""
"如果输入为空或不是一维的，索引或长度不一致，`target` 含有 0 和 1 以外的标签，或在不使用 `weights` 时其中某一类少于两个，或 `score` "
"不是实数数值或含有缺失值、无穷值。此外，如果 `level` 不是介于 0 和 1 之间的数，或者 `weights` 不是数值、没有为每个观测给出一个有限非负的权重、索引与 `score` "
"不同，或使某一类的权重之和不超过 1。"

msgid "The AUC alone."
msgstr "只计算 AUC。"

msgid ":obj:`delong_test`"
msgstr ":obj:`delong_test`"

msgid "Compare the AUCs of two scores on the same observations."
msgstr "在同一批观测上比较两个评分的 AUC。"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Let :math:`n_1` be the number of events and :math:`n_0` that of non-events. The placement value "
":math:`V_{10,i}` of event :math:`i` is the share of non-events that score below it, and the "
"placement value :math:`V_{01,j}` of non-event :math:`j` is the share of events that score above "
"it, with ties counted as one half. Both average to the AUC :math:`\\hat\\theta`, and its variance"
" is estimated by"
msgstr ""
"设 :math:`n_1` 为事件数， :math:`n_0` 为非事件数。事件 :math:`i` 的位置值 :math:`V_{10,i}` 是评分低于它的非事件所占的比例，非事件 "
":math:`j` 的位置值 :math:`V_{01,j}` 是评分高于它的事件所占的比例，评分相同时计为二分之一。两组位置值的均值都等于 AUC :math:`\\hat\\theta` "
"，其方差的估计为"

msgid ""
"\\widehat{\\mathrm{Var}}(\\hat\\theta) = \\frac{S_{10}}{n_1} + \\frac{S_{01}}{n_0},\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"S_{10} = \\frac{1}{n_1 - 1} \\sum_{i=1}^{n_1} (V_{10,i} - \\hat\\theta)^2,"
msgstr ""
"\\widehat{\\mathrm{Var}}(\\hat\\theta) = \\frac{S_{10}}{n_1} + \\frac{S_{01}}{n_0},\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"S_{10} = \\frac{1}{n_1 - 1} \\sum_{i=1}^{n_1} (V_{10,i} - \\hat\\theta)^2,"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"with :math:`S_{01}` defined in the same way over the non-events. The placement values come from "
"midranks, as in the algorithm of Sun and Xu [R7ccb11fdd3fb-2]_: the rank of an event among all "
"scores minus its rank among the events is the number of non-events below it, a tie counting as "
"one half. The computation thus takes :math:`O(N \\log N)` time for :math:`N` observations instead"
" of comparing every pair."
msgstr ""
"其中 :math:`S_{01}` 在非事件上按同样的方式定义。与 Sun 和 Xu 的算法 [R7ccb11fdd3fb-2]_ "
"一样，位置值由中秩求得：一个事件在全部评分中的秩减去它在事件中的秩，就是评分低于它的非事件个数，评分相同时计为二分之一。因此，对 :math:`N` 个观测，计算耗时为 :math:`O(N "
"\\log N)` ，无须比较每一对观测。"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The interval is :math:`\\hat\\theta \\pm z \\, \\mathrm{SE}`, cut off at 0 and 1, where :math:`z`"
" is the quantile of the standard normal distribution at :math:`(1 + \\mathrm{level}) / 2`. For "
"the Gini coefficient, :math:`2\\,\\mathrm{AUC} - 1`, the estimate and the bounds are rescaled in "
"the same way and the standard error doubles."
msgstr ""
"区间为 :math:`\\hat\\theta \\pm z \\, \\mathrm{SE}` ，并截断到 0 与 1 之间，其中 :math:`z` 是标准正态分布在 :math:`(1 +"
" \\mathrm{level}) / 2` 处的分位数。Gini 系数为 :math:`2\\,\\mathrm{AUC} - 1` ，其估计值和区间上下限按同样的方式换算，标准误加倍。"

msgid ""
"The normal approximation is poor when the AUC is close to 0 or 1 or a class has few observations."
" The standard error is 0 whenever the placement values are constant within each class, as they "
"are for a score that separates the classes perfectly, one that reverses them and a constant "
"score, so the interval collapses to the estimate."
msgstr ""
"当 AUC 接近 0 或 1，或某一类的观测很少时，正态近似的效果较差。只要每一类内部的位置值都相同，标准误就为 "
"0，例如把两类完全分开的评分、把两类完全颠倒的评分以及常数评分，此时区间缩为估计值本身。"

msgid ""
"With weights, :math:`n_1` and :math:`n_0` are the total weights of the two classes, and each "
"squared deviation counts with the weight of its observation. Weights that stand for a population "
"larger than the sample, such as inverse sampling rates, therefore give too small a standard "
"error."
msgstr "使用权重时， :math:`n_1` 和 :math:`n_0` 是两类的权重总和，每个离差平方按其观测的权重计入。因此，代表比样本更大的总体的权重（例如抽样比例的倒数）会使标准误偏小。"

msgid ""
"E. R. DeLong, D. M. DeLong and D. L. Clarke-Pearson, \"Comparing the areas under two or more "
"correlated receiver operating characteristic curves: a nonparametric approach\", Biometrics, "
"44(3), pp. 837-845, 1988."
msgstr ""
"E. R. DeLong, D. M. DeLong and D. L. Clarke-Pearson, \"Comparing the areas under two or more "
"correlated receiver operating characteristic curves: a nonparametric approach\", Biometrics, "
"44(3), pp. 837-845, 1988."

msgid ""
"X. Sun and W. Xu, \"Fast implementation of DeLong's algorithm for comparing the areas under "
"correlated receiver operating characteristic curves\", IEEE Signal Processing Letters, 21(11), "
"pp. 1389-1393, 2014."
msgstr ""
"X. Sun and W. Xu, \"Fast implementation of DeLong's algorithm for comparing the areas under "
"correlated receiver operating characteristic curves\", IEEE Signal Processing Letters, 21(11), "
"pp. 1389-1393, 2014."

msgid "[R7ccb11fdd3fb-1]_, [R7ccb11fdd3fb-2]_"
msgstr "[R7ccb11fdd3fb-1]_, [R7ccb11fdd3fb-2]_"

msgid "Six observations leave a wide interval, whose upper bound is cut off at 1:"
msgstr "六个观测给出的区间很宽，其上限被截断为 1："

msgid ""
"DeLong's test [R8b376e8c83e6-1]_ compares two scores of the same sample, such as a new model and "
"the model it would replace. Both scores rank the same pairs of events and non-events, so their "
"AUCs are correlated, and the standard error of the difference takes that into account."
msgstr ""
"DeLong 检验 [R8b376e8c83e6-1]_ 比较同一样本上的两个评分，例如新模型与它要替换的模型。两个评分对同样的事件与非事件对进行排序，因此它们的 AUC "
"是相关的，差值的标准误考虑了这种相关性。"

msgid ""
"The scores come first and the target last, as in `kivi.strategy.swap_set`; scikit-learn's metrics"
" take the target first."
msgstr "评分在前、目标在后，与 `kivi.strategy.swap_set` 相同；scikit-learn 的指标函数则把目标放在前面。"

msgid "**current**"
msgstr "**current**"

msgid ""
"Finite numeric scores of one model, such as the model in use, that are higher for a higher event "
"probability."
msgstr "其中一个模型（例如现行模型）的有限数值评分，事件概率越高，评分越高。"

msgid "**new**"
msgstr "**new**"

msgid "Finite numeric scores of the other model for the same observations, in the same direction."
msgstr "另一个模型对同一批观测的有限数值评分，方向相同。"

msgid ""
"Binary labels, with 1 indicating the event. Without `weights` there must be at least two events "
"and two non-events. Any two of `current`, `new` and `target` that are pandas Series must have "
"identical indices; otherwise they are matched by position."
msgstr ""
"二分类标签，1 表示事件。不使用 `weights` 时，至少要有两个事件和两个非事件。 `current` 、 `new` 和 `target` 中任意两个 pandas Series "
"的索引必须完全相同；否则按位置对应。"

msgid "Confidence level of the interval of the difference, between 0 and 1."
msgstr "差值区间的置信水平，介于 0 和 1 之间。"

msgid ""
"Non-negative frequency weight of each observation, matched like `target`. An observation of "
"weight :math:`w` counts as :math:`w` observations, so integer weights give the same result as "
"repeating rows. The weights of each class must add up to more than 1."
msgstr "每个观测的非负频数权重，对应方式与 `target` 相同。权重为 :math:`w` 的观测计为 :math:`w` 个观测，因此整数权重与重复相应行的结果相同。每一类的权重之和必须大于 1。"

msgid "pandas.Series"
msgstr "pandas.Series"

msgid ""
"``current_auc`` and ``new_auc``, the AUCs of the two scores; ``difference``, which is ``new_auc``"
" minus ``current_auc``; ``se``, its standard error; ``lower`` and ``upper``, the bounds of its "
"interval at `level`, cut off at -1 and 1; ``z``, the difference divided by its standard error; "
"and ``p_value``, the two-sided p-value of ``z``."
msgstr ""
"``current_auc`` 和 ``new_auc`` ：两个评分的 AUC； ``difference`` ： ``new_auc`` 减去 ``current_auc`` ； "
"``se`` ：差值的标准误； ``lower`` 和 ``upper`` ：差值在 `level` 下的区间上下限，截断到 -1 与 1 之间； ``z`` ：差值除以其标准误； "
"``p_value`` ： ``z`` 的双侧 p 值。"

msgid ""
"If the inputs are empty or not one-dimensional, their indices or lengths do not match, `target` "
"has a label other than 0 and 1 or, without `weights`, fewer than two of either, or `current` or "
"`new` is not real and numeric or has a missing or infinite value. Also if `level` is not a number"
" between 0 and 1, or if `weights` is not numeric, does not give each observation one finite, non-"
"negative weight, has an index other than that of a Series among the scores, or gives a class a "
"total weight of 1 or less."
msgstr ""
"如果输入为空或不是一维的，索引或长度不一致，`target` 含有 0 和 1 以外的标签，或在不使用 `weights` 时其中某一类少于两个，或 `current` 或 `new` "
"不是实数数值或含有缺失值、无穷值。此外，如果 `level` 不是介于 0 和 1 之间的数，或者 `weights` 不是数值、没有为每个观测给出一个有限非负的权重、索引与评分中某个 "
"Series 的索引不同，或使某一类的权重之和不超过 1。"

msgid ":obj:`roc_auc_interval`"
msgstr ":obj:`roc_auc_interval`"

msgid "The standard error and interval of one AUC."
msgstr "单个 AUC 的标准误和区间。"

msgid ":obj:`kivi.strategy.swap_set`"
msgstr ":obj:`kivi.strategy.swap_set`"

msgid "The applicants that two scores decide differently at their cut-offs."
msgstr "两个评分在各自的截断点上决策不同的申请人。"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"With the placement values of `roc_auc_interval` computed for each score, let :math:`D_{10,i}` be "
"the placement value of event :math:`i` under the new score minus that under the current one, and "
":math:`D_{01,j}` the same difference for non-event :math:`j`. They average to the difference of "
"the AUCs, and its variance is estimated by"
msgstr ""
"对每个评分分别计算 `roc_auc_interval` 中的位置值，设 :math:`D_{10,i}` 为事件 :math:`i` 在新评分下的位置值减去其在现行评分下的位置值， "
":math:`D_{01,j}` 为非事件 :math:`j` 的同一差值。它们的均值都等于两个 AUC 之差，其方差的估计为"

msgid ""
"\\widehat{\\mathrm{Var}}(\\hat\\theta_{\\mathrm{new}} -\n"
"\\hat\\theta_{\\mathrm{current}}) = \\frac{S^D_{10}}{n_1} +\n"
"\\frac{S^D_{01}}{n_0},"
msgstr ""
"\\widehat{\\mathrm{Var}}(\\hat\\theta_{\\mathrm{new}} -\n"
"\\hat\\theta_{\\mathrm{current}}) = \\frac{S^D_{10}}{n_1} +\n"
"\\frac{S^D_{01}}{n_0},"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"where :math:`S^D_{10}` and :math:`S^D_{01}` are the sample variances of :math:`D_{10,i}` over the"
" :math:`n_1` events and of :math:`D_{01,j}` over the :math:`n_0` non-events. This equals the "
"variance of the contrast in DeLong et al., which adds the two variances and subtracts twice the "
"covariance. Under the hypothesis of equal AUCs, :math:`z` is approximately standard normal."
msgstr ""
"其中 :math:`S^D_{10}` 和 :math:`S^D_{01}` 分别是 :math:`D_{10,i}` 在 :math:`n_1` 个事件上的样本方差和 "
":math:`D_{01,j}` 在 :math:`n_0` 个非事件上的样本方差。它等于 DeLong 等人的对比方差，即两个方差之和减去两倍的协方差。在两个 AUC 相等的假设下， "
":math:`z` 近似服从标准正态分布。"

msgid ""
"For a one-sided test that the new score ranks better, halve ``p_value`` when ``z`` is positive. "
"When the two scores order every pair of an event and a non-event in the same way, the difference "
"and its standard error are both 0, and ``z`` and ``p_value`` are NaN; with fractional weights, a "
"difference and a standard error that are both within rounding error of 0 count as 0. A difference"
" with a standard error of 0, such as that between a constant score and one that separates the "
"classes, gives an infinite ``z`` and a ``p_value`` of 0."
msgstr ""
"如需单侧检验新评分的排序是否更好，在 ``z`` 为正时把 ``p_value`` 减半。当两个评分对每一对事件与非事件的排序都相同时，差值及其标准误都为 0， ``z`` 和 "
"``p_value`` 为 NaN；使用非整数权重时，若差值和标准误都与 0 只差舍入误差，二者都按 0 处理。标准误为 0 而差值不为 0 时（例如常数评分与把两类完全分开的评分之间）， "
"``z`` 为无穷大， ``p_value`` 为 0。"

msgid "Weights count as in `roc_auc_interval`, so inverse sampling rates give too small a standard error."
msgstr "权重的计法与 `roc_auc_interval` 相同，因此抽样比例的倒数会使标准误偏小。"

msgid "[R8b376e8c83e6-1]_"
msgstr "[R8b376e8c83e6-1]_"

msgid "The new score separates the six observations perfectly:"
msgstr "新评分把六个观测完全分开："

msgid ""
"Each row shows how many events a band holds and what share of all events is captured by reviewing"
" that band and every band above it."
msgstr "每行给出该评分段的事件数，以及审查该段及其以上各段时捕获的事件占全部事件的比例。"

msgid "int or array_like, default 10"
msgstr "int 或 array_like，默认 10"

msgid ""
"Number of quantile bands, or increasing band edges. An integer is the same as passing "
"``kivi.binning.bin_edges(score, bins=bins)``, so tied scores can leave fewer bands than "
"requested. Pass the edges fitted on a development sample to compare later samples on the same "
"bands. With `weights`, an integer gives weighted quantile edges, as ``bin_edges(score, bins=bins,"
" weights=weights)`` does."
msgstr ""
"分位数评分段的数量，或递增的分段边界。整数等同于传入 ``kivi.binning.bin_edges(score, "
"bins=bins)``，因此相同评分可能使评分段少于请求的数量。传入在开发样本上拟合的边界，即可在同一组评分段上比较后续样本。使用 `weights` 时，整数会得到加权分位数边界，与 "
"``bin_edges(score, bins=bins, weights=weights)`` 相同。"

msgid ""
"Non-negative weight of each observation, such as the inverse of its sampling rate, matched like "
"`target`. The counts become sums of weights. On the same edges, integer weights give the same "
"table as repeating rows; an integer `bins` can give other edges, because weighted quantiles use "
"the inverted CDF."
msgstr ""
"每个观测的非负权重，例如其抽样比例的倒数，对应方式与 `target` 相同。计数变为权重之和。在相同边界上，整数权重与重复相应行得到的表相同；而整数 `bins` "
"可能得到不同的边界，因为加权分位数采用逆累积分布（inverted CDF）。"

msgid ""
"One row per score band, from the highest band to the lowest, indexed by the interval of the band."
" The columns are described in the Notes."
msgstr "每个评分段一行，从最高段到最低段排列，以评分段的区间为索引。各列含义见“说明”。"

msgid ""
"If the inputs are empty or not one-dimensional, their indices or lengths do not match, `target` "
"has a label other than 0 and 1 or lacks one of them, `score` is not real and numeric or has a "
"missing or infinite value, `bins` is neither a positive integer nor increasing edges, or a score "
"lies outside the edges. Also if `weights` is not numeric, does not give each observation one "
"finite, non-negative weight, has an index other than that of `score`, or leaves a class without "
"weight."
msgstr ""
"如果输入为空或不是一维的，索引或长度不一致，`target` 含有 0 和 1 以外的标签或缺少其中之一，`score` 不是实数数值或含有缺失值、无穷值，`bins` "
"既不是正整数也不是递增的边界，或有评分落在边界之外。此外，如果 `weights` 不是数值、没有为每个观测给出一个有限非负的权重、索引与 `score` 不同，或使某一类没有权重。"

msgid ""
"If `bins` is an integer and tied scores leave fewer bands than requested, as in "
"`kivi.binning.bin_edges`."
msgstr "如果 `bins` 是整数，且相同评分使评分段少于请求的数量，与 `kivi.binning.bin_edges` 相同。"

msgid "The largest gap over all scores rather than band edges."
msgstr "在全部评分上而非仅在分段边界上取的最大差距。"

msgid "Ranking quality over all pairs of events and non-events."
msgstr "在全部事件与非事件配对上衡量的排序质量。"

msgid ":obj:`kivi.binning.bin_edges`"
msgstr ":obj:`kivi.binning.bin_edges`"

msgid "Fit band edges on a development sample."
msgstr "在开发样本上拟合分段边界。"

msgid ""
"Bands are intervals closed on the right, as in ``pandas.cut``, so tied scores always share a "
"band. Every band is reported, including bands without observations, so samples cut on the same "
"edges give tables with the same rows. An empty band has a NaN ``event_rate`` and ``lift``, and "
"``cum_lift`` is NaN until the first band with observations."
msgstr ""
"评分段是右闭区间，与 ``pandas.cut`` 相同，因此相同评分总在同一段。结果列出每个评分段，包括没有观测的评分段，因此用相同边界切分的样本得到的表行相同。空评分段的 "
"``event_rate`` 和 ``lift`` 为 NaN，在第一个有观测的评分段之前 ``cum_lift`` 也为 NaN。"

msgid ""
"``non_event``, ``event`` and ``total``: non-events, events and all observations in the band, or "
"the sums of their weights;"
msgstr "``non_event``、``event`` 和 ``total``：该段的非事件数、事件数和总观测数，或者它们的权重之和；"

msgid "``event_rate``: ``event`` divided by ``total``;"
msgstr "``event_rate``：``event`` 除以 ``total``；"

msgid "``lift``: ``event_rate`` divided by the event rate of the sample;"
msgstr "``lift``：``event_rate`` 除以整个样本的事件率；"

msgid ""
"``cum_non_event_share``, ``cum_event_share`` and ``cum_total_share``: shares of all non-events, "
"events and observations in the band and the bands above it;"
msgstr "``cum_non_event_share``、``cum_event_share`` 和 ``cum_total_share``：该段及其以上各段占全部非事件、事件和观测的比例；"

msgid "``ks``: the absolute difference between ``cum_event_share`` and ``cum_non_event_share``;"
msgstr "``ks``：``cum_event_share`` 与 ``cum_non_event_share`` 之差的绝对值；"

msgid "``cum_lift``: ``cum_event_share`` divided by ``cum_total_share``."
msgstr "``cum_lift``：``cum_event_share`` 除以 ``cum_total_share``。"

msgid ""
"The largest ``ks`` is at most the value of `ks`, and the two are equal when each distinct score "
"forms its own band."
msgstr "``ks`` 列的最大值不超过 `ks` 的结果；当每个不同的评分各自成段时，二者相等。"

msgid ""
"The Brier score is the mean squared difference between the predicted probability and the observed"
" outcome, so a lower value is better."
msgstr "Brier 分数是预测概率与观测结果之差的平方的均值，因此越低越好。"

msgid ""
"The probabilities come first and the target second, as in `kivi.woe.woe_table`; scikit-learn's "
"metrics take the target first."
msgstr "概率在前、目标在后，与 `kivi.woe.woe_table` 相同；scikit-learn 的指标函数则把目标放在前面。"

msgid "Predicted event probabilities from 0 to 1."
msgstr "预测的事件概率，取值 0 到 1。"

msgid ""
"Binary labels, with 1 indicating the event. If `probability` and `target` are both pandas Series,"
" they must have identical indices; otherwise they are matched by position."
msgstr "二分类标签，1 表示事件。如果 `probability` 和 `target` 都是 pandas Series，二者的索引必须完全相同；否则按位置对应。"

msgid ""
"Non-negative weight of each observation, matched like `target`. The score is then the weighted "
"mean of the squared differences."
msgstr "每个观测的非负权重，对应方式与 `target` 相同。此时 Brier 分数为平方差的加权平均。"

msgid "The Brier score, from 0 for perfect forecasts to 1."
msgstr "Brier 分数，取值从 0（完美预测）到 1。"

msgid ""
"If the inputs are empty or not one-dimensional, their indices or lengths do not match, `target` "
"has a label other than 0 and 1, or `probability` is not real and numeric or has a missing value "
"or a value outside 0 to 1. Also if `weights` is not numeric, does not give each observation one "
"finite, non-negative weight with a positive total, or has an index other than that of "
"`probability`."
msgstr ""
"如果输入为空或不是一维的，索引或长度不一致，`target` 含有 0 和 1 以外的标签，或 `probability` 不是实数数值、含有缺失值或含有 0 到 1 以外的值。此外，如果 "
"`weights` 不是数值、没有为每个观测给出一个有限非负且总和为正的权重，或者索引与 `probability` 不同。"

msgid "Ranking quality, which ignores the probability scale."
msgstr "排序质量，与概率的尺度无关。"

msgid "For outcomes :math:`y_i` and probabilities :math:`p_i`,"
msgstr "对结果 :math:`y_i` 和概率 :math:`p_i`，"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "\\mathrm{BS} = \\frac{1}{n} \\sum_{i=1}^{n} (p_i - y_i)^2,"
msgstr "\\mathrm{BS} = \\frac{1}{n} \\sum_{i=1}^{n} (p_i - y_i)^2,"

msgid "or :math:`\\sum_i w_i (p_i - y_i)^2 / \\sum_i w_i` with weights."
msgstr "使用权重时则为 :math:`\\sum_i w_i (p_i - y_i)^2 / \\sum_i w_i` 。"

msgid ""
"Unlike the ranking measures, the Brier score depends on the probability values themselves, so it "
"rewards calibration, and it is defined even when the sample has only one class. Predicting the "
"event rate :math:`\\bar y` for everyone scores :math:`\\bar y (1 - \\bar y)`, a useful baseline."
msgstr ""
"与排序度量不同，Brier 分数取决于概率值本身，因此会奖励校准良好的预测，并且在样本只有一个类别时也有定义。对所有人都预测事件率 :math:`\\bar y` 的得分为 "
":math:`\\bar y (1 - \\bar y)`，可作为有用的基准。"

msgid ""
"G. W. Brier, \"Verification of forecasts expressed in terms of probability\", Monthly Weather "
"Review, 78(1), pp. 1-3, 1950."
msgstr ""
"G. W. Brier, \"Verification of forecasts expressed in terms of probability\", Monthly Weather "
"Review, 78(1), pp. 1-3, 1950."

msgid "[R88e41552d980-1]_"
msgstr "[R88e41552d980-1]_"

msgid "Model monitoring"
msgstr "模型监控"

msgid ""
"Track a score and its variables period by period. :func:`~kivi.monitoring.monitoring_table` gives"
" the population, the events, the discrimination and the PSI of a score in every period, and "
":func:`~kivi.monitoring.stability_table` the PSI of every grouped variable."
msgstr ""
"按期跟踪评分及其变量。 :func:`~kivi.monitoring.monitoring_table` 给出评分在每一期的样本量、事件、区分能力和 PSI， "
":func:`~kivi.monitoring.stability_table` 给出每个已分组变量的 PSI。"

msgid "See :doc:`/user_guide/monitoring` for examples on synthetic applications."
msgstr "基于合成申请数据的示例见 :doc:`/user_guide/monitoring` 。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`monitoring_table <kivi.monitoring.monitoring_table>`\\ \\(score\\, period\\[\\, "
"target\\, ...\\]\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`monitoring_table <kivi.monitoring.monitoring_table>`\\ \\(score\\, period\\[\\, "
"target\\, ...\\]\\)"

msgid "Monitor the population, event rate, discrimination and stability of a score."
msgstr "监控评分的样本量、事件率、区分能力和稳定性。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`stability_table <kivi.monitoring.stability_table>`\\ \\(groups\\, period\\, \\*\\[\\, "
"...\\]\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`stability_table <kivi.monitoring.stability_table>`\\ \\(groups\\, period\\, \\*\\[\\, "
"...\\]\\)"

msgid "Monitor the population stability of grouped variables over time."
msgstr "按期监控已分组变量的群体稳定性。"

msgid ""
"Each row summarizes one period, such as a month or a quarter: how many observations it has, how "
"many events among those with a known outcome, how well the score separates the two classes and "
"how far the distribution of the score has moved from a reference sample."
msgstr "每行汇总一期，例如一个月或一个季度：该期有多少观测、结果已知的观测中有多少事件、评分区分两类结果的能力如何，以及评分分布相对基准样本偏移了多少。"

msgid ""
"Finite numeric scores that are higher for a higher event probability, such as a PD. Negate "
"scorecard points, which are higher for a lower risk."
msgstr "有限的数值评分，事件概率越高，评分越高，例如 PD。评分卡分数越高表示风险越低，因此须取负后再传入。"

msgid "**period**"
msgstr "**period**"

msgid ""
"Period of each observation, such as the month of application, without missing values. Periods are"
" sorted, and categorical periods follow the order of their categories. If `score` and `period` "
"are both pandas Series, they must have identical indices; otherwise they are matched by position."
msgstr ""
"每个观测所属的期，例如申请月份，不能有缺失值。各期按升序排列，分类型的期按类别顺序排列。如果 `score` 和 `period` 都是 pandas "
"Series，二者的索引必须完全相同；否则按位置对应。"

msgid ""
"Binary labels, with 1 indicating the event, and missing values for outcomes that are not known "
"yet, such as those of loans that have not reached the end of the outcome window, matched like "
"`period`. Without `target`, every outcome is unknown and the table only has the columns ``total``"
" and ``psi``."
msgstr ""
"二元标签，1 表示事件；结果尚未得知时为缺失值，例如尚未走完表现期的贷款，对应方式与 `period` 相同。不给出 `target` 时，所有结果都视为未知，表中只有 ``total`` 和 "
"``psi`` 两列。"

msgid "**reference_period**"
msgstr "**reference_period**"

msgid "object, optional"
msgstr "object，可选"

msgid ""
"The label of the period that every period is compared with, such as the first month after the "
"development sample. For datetime periods and pandas periods, a string that names exactly one "
"period, such as ``\"2024-01\"`` for months, selects it. Give either `reference_period` or "
"`reference_score`."
msgstr ""
"每一期都与之比较的那一期的标签，例如开发样本之后的第一个月。对于日期时间型的期和 pandas 的 Period，恰好指向其中一期的字符串（例如月份 ``\"2024-01\"`` "
"）会选中该期。 `reference_period` 和 `reference_score` 二者给出其一。"

msgid "**reference_score**"
msgstr "**reference_score**"

msgid ""
"The scores of a reference sample that every period is compared with, such as the development "
"sample, with any index. Pass the scores of the reference rows, such as ``score[mask]``, rather "
"than a boolean mask, which is rejected."
msgstr "每一期都与之比较的基准样本的评分，例如开发样本，索引不限。应传入基准行的评分，例如 ``score[mask]`` ，而不是布尔掩码；布尔掩码会被拒绝。"

msgid ""
"Number of quantile bands of the reference scores, or increasing band edges. An integer is the "
"same as passing ``kivi.binning.bin_edges(reference, bins=bins)`` for the reference scores, with "
"their weights as ``weights``, so tied scores can leave fewer bands than requested. Every period "
"is compared on the same bands."
msgstr ""
"基准评分的分位数评分段个数，或递增的评分段边界。整数等同于对基准评分传入 ``kivi.binning.bin_edges(reference, bins=bins)`` ，并以其权重作为 "
"``weights`` ，因此并列的评分可能使评分段少于请求的数量。每一期都在同一组评分段上比较。"

msgid ""
"Positive replacement for a zero count when calculating the PSI, as in `kivi.stability.psi_table`,"
" in units of weight with `weights`."
msgstr "计算 PSI 时用这个正数替代零计数，含义与 `kivi.stability.psi_table` 相同；给出 `weights` 时以权重为单位。"

msgid ""
"Non-negative weight of each observation, such as the inverse of its sampling rate, matched like "
"`period`. Counts become sums of weights, and the discrimination and the PSI are weighted. On the "
"same band edges, integer weights give the same table as repeating rows."
msgstr "每个观测的非负权重，例如其抽样比例的倒数，对应方式与 `period` 相同。计数变为权重之和，区分能力和 PSI 也按权重计算。在相同的评分段边界上，整数权重与重复相应行得到的表相同。"

msgid "**reference_weights**"
msgstr "**reference_weights**"

msgid ""
"Non-negative weight of each score of `reference_score`, matched like it. A reference period takes"
" its weights from `weights`."
msgstr "`reference_score` 中每个评分的非负权重，对应方式与它相同。基准期的权重取自 `weights` 。"

msgid "One row per period, indexed by ``period``, with the columns described in the Notes."
msgstr "每期一行，索引名为 ``period`` ，各列含义见“说明”。"

msgid ""
"If `score` or `period` is empty, an input is not one-dimensional, the inputs have different "
"lengths or are Series with different indices, `score` is not real and numeric or has a missing or"
" infinite value, `target` has a value other than 0, 1 and missing, or `period` has a missing "
"value. Also if neither or both of `reference_period` and `reference_score` are given, "
"`reference_period` is not one period with observations, `reference_score` is empty, boolean or "
"not finite and numeric, `reference_weights` is given with `reference_period`, `bins` is neither a"
" positive integer nor increasing edges, a score lies outside the edges, `smoothing` is not finite"
" and positive, or a weight array is not numeric, does not give each observation one finite, non-"
"negative weight with a positive total, or has an index other than that of its sample."
msgstr ""
"如果 `score` 或 `period` 为空，某个输入不是一维的，输入长度不同或是索引不同的 Series， `score` 不是实数型数值或含有缺失值或无穷值， `target` 含有 "
"0、1 和缺失值以外的值，或 `period` 含有缺失值。此外，如果 `reference_period` 和 `reference_score` 都没有给出或同时给出， "
"`reference_period` 不是有观测的某一期， `reference_score` 为空、为布尔型或不是有限数值，给出 `reference_period` 的同时给出了 "
"`reference_weights` ， `bins` 既不是正整数也不是递增边界，某个评分落在边界之外， `smoothing` "
"不是有限正数，或者某个权重数组不是数值型、没有为每个观测给出一个有限非负且总和为正的权重，或其索引与对应样本的索引不同。"

msgid ""
"If `bins` is an integer and tied reference scores leave fewer bands than requested, as in "
"`kivi.binning.bin_edges`."
msgstr "如果 `bins` 是整数，且并列的基准评分使评分段少于请求的数量，与 `kivi.binning.bin_edges` 相同。"

msgid ":obj:`stability_table`"
msgstr ":obj:`stability_table`"

msgid "The PSI of each variable of the score in each period."
msgstr "评分各变量在每一期的 PSI。"

msgid ":obj:`kivi.metrics.roc_auc`"
msgstr ":obj:`kivi.metrics.roc_auc`"

msgid "The AUC of one sample."
msgstr "单个样本的 AUC。"

msgid "The PSI of one sample and its contributions."
msgstr "单个样本的 PSI 及各组贡献。"

msgid ""
"``total``: observations in the period, or the sum of their weights, including those whose outcome"
" is not known yet;"
msgstr "``total`` ：该期的观测数或其权重之和，包括结果尚未得知的观测；"

msgid "``known``: observations with a known outcome;"
msgstr "``known`` ：结果已知的观测数；"

msgid "``event``: events among them;"
msgstr "``event`` ：其中的事件数；"

msgid "``event_rate``: ``event`` divided by ``known``, NaN without known outcomes;"
msgstr "``event_rate`` ： ``event`` 除以 ``known`` ，没有已知结果时为 NaN；"

msgid ""
"``auc``, ``gini`` and ``ks``: `kivi.metrics.roc_auc`, `kivi.metrics.gini` and `kivi.metrics.ks` "
"of the known outcomes of the period, NaN unless both classes are present;"
msgstr ""
"``auc`` 、 ``gini`` 和 ``ks`` ：该期已知结果的 `kivi.metrics.roc_auc` 、 `kivi.metrics.gini` 和 "
"`kivi.metrics.ks` ，两类结果不全时为 NaN；"

msgid ""
"``psi``: the population stability index of the period's scores against the reference scores, on "
"the bands described under `bins`."
msgstr "``psi`` ：该期评分相对基准评分的群体稳定性指标，基于 `bins` 所描述的评分段。"

msgid ""
"Without a target the columns are ``total`` and ``psi``. Each row equals what the metric functions"
" and ``psi_table(pandas.cut(reference, edges), pandas.cut(period_score, edges))`` give for the "
"period alone, with the weights of the two samples as ``reference_weights`` and "
"``current_weights``. For a band :math:`i` with shares :math:`q_i` of the reference scores and "
":math:`p_i` of the period's scores, after smoothing,"
msgstr ""
"没有目标变量时，表中只有 ``total`` 和 ``psi`` 两列。每一行都等于仅对该期计算时指标函数和 ``psi_table(pandas.cut(reference, edges), "
"pandas.cut(period_score, edges))`` 的结果，两个样本的权重分别作为 ``reference_weights`` 和 ``current_weights`` "
"传入。记 :math:`q_i` 和 :math:`p_i` 为评分段 :math:`i` 在基准评分和该期评分中平滑后的占比，则"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "\\mathrm{PSI} = \\sum_i (p_i - q_i) \\ln \\frac{p_i}{q_i},"
msgstr "\\mathrm{PSI} = \\sum_i (p_i - q_i) \\ln \\frac{p_i}{q_i},"

msgid "where bands empty in both samples are left out. The reference period has a PSI of 0."
msgstr "其中两个样本中都为空的评分段不计入。基准期的 PSI 为 0。"

msgid ""
"A category of a categorical `period` without observations, or whose weights sum to zero, keeps "
"its row with zero counts and NaN in the other columns, so that monitoring tables of different "
"samples line up. Here the rule differs from `kivi.vintage.vintage_table` and "
"`kivi.calibration.calibration_table`, which leave such categories out. Other periods exist only "
"through their observations, and those whose weights sum to zero are left out, as repeated rows "
"would leave them out."
msgstr ""
"分类型 `period` 中没有观测或权重之和为零的类别仍保留一行，计数为零，其他列为 NaN，以便不同样本的监控表能够对齐。这一规则与 `kivi.vintage.vintage_table`"
" 和 `kivi.calibration.calibration_table` 不同，后两者会略去这样的类别。其他类型的期只由其观测产生，权重之和为零的期会被排除，与重复相应行时一样。"

msgid ""
"The discrimination of the most recent periods usually rests on few known outcomes, and the PSI of"
" a small period mostly reflects sampling noise, so read both together with ``known`` and "
"``total``."
msgstr "最近几期的区分能力通常只基于很少的已知结果，而小样本期的 PSI 主要反映抽样噪声，因此应结合 ``known`` 和 ``total`` 一起解读。"

msgid ""
"The March outcomes of two observations are not known yet, so its discrimination rests on the "
"other two."
msgstr "3 月有两个观测的结果尚未得知，因此其区分能力只基于另外两个。"

msgid ""
"Each entry is the PSI of one variable in one period against a reference sample, as "
"`kivi.stability.psi_table` computes it for the period alone. With the groups of a scorecard's "
"variables this is the variable part of a stability report, and the variables that move explain a "
"shift of the score that `monitoring_table` shows."
msgstr ""
"每个值是某个变量在某一期相对基准样本的 PSI，与 `kivi.stability.psi_table` "
"仅对该期计算的结果相同。对评分卡各变量的分组而言，这就是稳定性报告中的变量部分，发生变化的变量可以解释 `monitoring_table` 所显示的评分偏移。"

msgid ""
"One column per variable, holding labels or values binned using the same edges in every period, "
"such as the result of ``kivi.spec.BinningSpec.cut``. Missing values form a group, and groups "
"observed in only one sample are included."
msgstr "每个变量一列，存放标签或在每一期都使用相同边界分箱后的值，例如 ``kivi.spec.BinningSpec.cut`` 的结果。缺失值单独成组，只在一个样本中出现的组也会包含在内。"

msgid ""
"Period of each row of `groups`, without missing values. Periods are sorted, and categorical "
"periods follow the order of their categories. A Series must have the index of `groups`."
msgstr "`groups` 每一行所属的期，不能有缺失值。各期按升序排列，分类型的期按类别顺序排列。Series 的索引必须与 `groups` 相同。"

msgid ""
"The label of the period that every period is compared with, as in `monitoring_table`. Give either"
" `reference_period` or `reference_groups`."
msgstr "每一期都与之比较的那一期的标签，与 `monitoring_table` 相同。 `reference_period` 和 `reference_groups` 二者给出其一。"

msgid "**reference_groups**"
msgstr "**reference_groups**"

msgid "pandas.DataFrame, optional"
msgstr "pandas.DataFrame，可选"

msgid ""
"The groups of a reference sample that every period is compared with, such as the development "
"sample, with every column of `groups` and any index. Its other columns are ignored."
msgstr "每一期都与之比较的基准样本（例如开发样本）的分组，须包含 `groups` 的每一列，索引不限。其他列会被忽略。"

msgid "Positive replacement for a zero count when calculating shares, in units of weight with `weights`."
msgstr "计算占比时用这个正数替代零计数；给出 `weights` 时以权重为单位。"

msgid ""
"Non-negative weight of each row of `groups`, matched like `period`. Counts become sums of "
"weights, so integer weights give the same table as repeating rows."
msgstr "`groups` 每一行的非负权重，对应方式与 `period` 相同。计数变为权重之和，因此整数权重与重复相应行得到的表相同。"

msgid ""
"Non-negative weight of each row of `reference_groups`. A reference period takes its weights from "
"`weights`."
msgstr "`reference_groups` 每一行的非负权重。基准期的权重取自 `weights` 。"

msgid ""
"One row per period, indexed by ``period``, and one column per variable, with the columns of "
"`groups` and the column index named ``variable``. Each entry is the PSI of the variable in the "
"period."
msgstr "每期一行，索引名为 ``period`` ；每个变量一列，列与 `groups` 的列相同，列索引名为 ``variable`` 。每个值是该变量在该期的 PSI。"

msgid ""
"If `groups` is not a DataFrame, has no rows, no columns, repeated column names or more than one "
"level of column names, `period` is not one-dimensional, does not have one value per row or has a "
"missing value, or a Series argument has an index other than that of `groups`. Also if neither or "
"both of `reference_period` and `reference_groups` are given, `reference_period` is not one period"
" with observations, `reference_groups` is not a DataFrame with rows, unique column names and "
"every column of `groups`, `reference_weights` is given with `reference_period`, `smoothing` is "
"not finite and positive, or a weight array is not numeric, does not give each row one finite, "
"non-negative weight with a positive total, or has an index other than that of its sample."
msgstr ""
"如果 `groups` 不是 DataFrame，没有行、没有列、列名重复或列名不止一层， `period` 不是一维的、不是每行一个值或含有缺失值，或某个 Series 参数的索引与 "
"`groups` 的索引不同。此外，如果 `reference_period` 和 `reference_groups` 都没有给出或同时给出， `reference_period` "
"不是有观测的某一期， `reference_groups` 不是有行、列名唯一且包含 `groups` 每一列的 DataFrame，给出 `reference_period` 的同时给出了 "
"`reference_weights` ， `smoothing` 不是有限正数，或者某个权重数组不是数值型、没有为每一行给出一个有限非负且总和为正的权重，或其索引与对应样本的索引不同。"

msgid ":obj:`monitoring_table`"
msgstr ":obj:`monitoring_table`"

msgid "The population, discrimination and PSI of the score."
msgstr "评分的样本量、区分能力和 PSI。"

msgid ":obj:`kivi.stability.csi_table`"
msgstr ":obj:`kivi.stability.csi_table`"

msgid "The change of a variable's average points."
msgstr "变量平均分值的变化。"

msgid ""
"For a group :math:`i` of a variable, with shares :math:`q_i` of the reference sample and "
":math:`p_i` of the period, after smoothing,"
msgstr "对变量的第 :math:`i` 组，记 :math:`q_i` 和 :math:`p_i` 为其在基准样本和该期中平滑后的占比，则"

msgid ""
"over the groups observed in the reference sample or in the period. The reference period has a PSI"
" of 0."
msgstr "求和范围为在基准样本或该期中出现的组。基准期的 PSI 为 0。"

msgid ""
"A category of a categorical `period` without observations, or whose weights sum to zero, keeps "
"its row with NaN entries, as in `monitoring_table`. Other periods exist only through their rows, "
"and those whose weights sum to zero are left out, as repeated rows would leave them out."
msgstr ""
"分类型 `period` 中没有观测或权重之和为零的类别仍保留一行，其值为 NaN，与 `monitoring_table` "
"相同。其他类型的期只由其行产生，权重之和为零的期会被排除，与重复相应行时一样。"

msgid "One value of the February region is missing, a group that January does not have."
msgstr "2 月有一个 region 值缺失，这是 1 月没有的一组。"

msgid "Charts"
msgstr "图表"

msgid ""
"Draw the result tables of the other modules with matplotlib, one function per table, such as "
":func:`~kivi.plotting.woe_chart` for a WOE table, :func:`~kivi.plotting.roc_chart` for a ROC "
"table and :func:`~kivi.plotting.monitoring_chart` for a monitoring report. Each function draws on"
" the Axes passed as ``ax``, or on a new figure, and returns the Axes it drew on. matplotlib is an"
" optional dependency: install it with ``pip install \"kivi[plot]\"``."
msgstr ""
"用 matplotlib 绘制其他模块的结果表，每种表对应一个函数，例如 WOE 表用 :func:`~kivi.plotting.woe_chart` ，ROC 表用 "
":func:`~kivi.plotting.roc_chart` ，监控报告用 :func:`~kivi.plotting.monitoring_chart` 。每个函数在 ``ax`` 传入的"
" Axes 上作图，未传入时新建一个图形，并返回所用的 Axes。matplotlib 是可选依赖，用 ``pip install \"kivi[plot]\"`` 安装。"

msgid "See :doc:`/user_guide/plotting` for examples on the bundled data."
msgstr "基于内置数据的示例见 :doc:`/user_guide/plotting` 。"

msgid ":py:obj:`woe_chart <kivi.plotting.woe_chart>`\\ \\(table\\, \\*\\[\\, line\\, ax\\]\\)"
msgstr ":py:obj:`woe_chart <kivi.plotting.woe_chart>`\\ \\(table\\, \\*\\[\\, line\\, ax\\]\\)"

msgid "Draw the population share of each group with its event rate or WOE."
msgstr "绘制每个分组的样本占比，以及其事件率或 WOE。"

msgid ":py:obj:`correlation_chart <kivi.plotting.correlation_chart>`\\ \\(matrix\\, \\*\\[\\, ax\\]\\)"
msgstr ":py:obj:`correlation_chart <kivi.plotting.correlation_chart>`\\ \\(matrix\\, \\*\\[\\, ax\\]\\)"

msgid "Draw a correlation matrix as a heatmap with the value in each cell."
msgstr "把相关系数矩阵绘制成热力图，并在每个单元格中标出数值。"

msgid ":py:obj:`roc_chart <kivi.plotting.roc_chart>`\\ \\(table\\, \\*\\[\\, ks\\, label\\, ax\\]\\)"
msgstr ":py:obj:`roc_chart <kivi.plotting.roc_chart>`\\ \\(table\\, \\*\\[\\, ks\\, label\\, ax\\]\\)"

msgid "Draw the ROC curve, with the largest gap between the two rates marked."
msgstr "绘制 ROC 曲线，并标出两个比率之间的最大差距。"

msgid ":py:obj:`gains_chart <kivi.plotting.gains_chart>`\\ \\(table\\, \\*\\[\\, ks\\, label\\, ax\\]\\)"
msgstr ":py:obj:`gains_chart <kivi.plotting.gains_chart>`\\ \\(table\\, \\*\\[\\, ks\\, label\\, ax\\]\\)"

msgid "Draw the cumulative shares of events and non-events by score band."
msgstr "按评分段绘制事件与非事件的累计占比。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`calibration_chart <kivi.plotting.calibration_chart>`\\ \\(table\\, \\*\\[\\, label\\, "
"ax\\]\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`calibration_chart <kivi.plotting.calibration_chart>`\\ \\(table\\, \\*\\[\\, label\\, "
"ax\\]\\)"

msgid "Draw the observed event rate of each group against its mean predicted PD."
msgstr "绘制每个分组的观测事件率与其平均预测 PD 的对比。"

msgid ":py:obj:`cutoff_chart <kivi.plotting.cutoff_chart>`\\ \\(table\\, \\*\\[\\, label\\, ax\\]\\)"
msgstr ":py:obj:`cutoff_chart <kivi.plotting.cutoff_chart>`\\ \\(table\\, \\*\\[\\, label\\, ax\\]\\)"

msgid "Draw the event rate of the approved book against the approval rate."
msgstr "绘制通过客群的事件率随通过率的变化。"

msgid ":py:obj:`psi_chart <kivi.plotting.psi_chart>`\\ \\(table\\, \\*\\[\\, ax\\]\\)"
msgstr ":py:obj:`psi_chart <kivi.plotting.psi_chart>`\\ \\(table\\, \\*\\[\\, ax\\]\\)"

msgid "Draw the reference and the current share of each group side by side."
msgstr "并排绘制每个分组的基准占比和当前占比。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`monitoring_chart <kivi.plotting.monitoring_chart>`\\ \\(table\\, \\*\\[\\, column\\, "
"kind\\, ...\\]\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`monitoring_chart <kivi.plotting.monitoring_chart>`\\ \\(table\\, \\*\\[\\, column\\, "
"kind\\, ...\\]\\)"

msgid "Draw one column of a monitoring report period by period."
msgstr "逐期绘制监控报告中的一列。"

msgid ":py:obj:`vintage_chart <kivi.plotting.vintage_chart>`\\ \\(table\\, \\*\\[\\, ax\\]\\)"
msgstr ":py:obj:`vintage_chart <kivi.plotting.vintage_chart>`\\ \\(table\\, \\*\\[\\, ax\\]\\)"

msgid "Draw one curve per cohort of its cumulative bad rate by month on book."
msgstr "为每个批次绘制一条按账龄变化的累计坏账率曲线。"

msgid ""
"The bars show ``total_share``, the share of the sample in each group, on the left y-axis, and a "
"line shows ``event_rate`` or ``woe`` on a second y-axis on the right. This is the one chart of "
"the module with two y-axes, and so the one that returns two Axes. The groups keep the order of "
"the table, and the legend gives the IV of the whole table."
msgstr ""
"柱形在左侧 y 轴上表示 ``total_share`` ，即每个分组在样本中的占比；折线在右侧的第二个 y 轴上表示 ``event_rate`` 或 ``woe`` "
"。这是本模块中唯一带有两个 y 轴的图表，因此也是唯一返回两个 Axes 的图表。各分组保持表中的顺序，图例给出整张表的 IV。"

msgid "**table**"
msgstr "**table**"

msgid ""
"A table from `kivi.woe.woe_table`, or one of the tables of a `kivi.spec.BinningSpec`. It needs "
"the columns ``total_share``, ``iv`` and the column named by `line`."
msgstr ""
"由 `kivi.woe.woe_table` 得到的表，或 `kivi.spec.BinningSpec` 中的某张表。需要包含 ``total_share`` 、 ``iv`` 列以及 "
"`line` 指定的列。"

msgid "**line**"
msgstr "**line**"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "{'event_rate', 'woe'}, default 'event_rate'"
msgstr "{'event_rate', 'woe'}，默认 'event_rate'"

msgid "Column drawn as the line."
msgstr "绘制为折线的列。"

msgid "**ax**"
msgstr "**ax**"

msgid "matplotlib.axes.Axes, optional"
msgstr "matplotlib.axes.Axes，可选"

msgid "Axes of the bars. A new figure is created when it is not given."
msgstr "绘制柱形的 Axes。未给出时新建一个图形。"

msgid "**bars**"
msgstr "**bars**"

msgid "matplotlib.axes.Axes"
msgstr "matplotlib.axes.Axes"

msgid "Axes of the bars, `ax` when it is given."
msgstr "绘制柱形的 Axes；给出 `ax` 时即为 `ax` 。"

msgid "Axes of the line, a twin of `bars` that shares its x-axis."
msgstr "绘制折线的 Axes，是与 `bars` 共用 x 轴的孪生坐标轴。"

msgid "ImportError"
msgstr "ImportError"

msgid "If matplotlib is not installed."
msgstr "如果未安装 matplotlib。"

msgid ""
"If `table` is not a DataFrame, lacks a column it needs or has no rows, a column it needs is not "
"numeric, `line` is neither ``'event_rate'`` nor ``'woe'``, or `ax` is not a matplotlib Axes."
msgstr ""
"如果 `table` 不是 DataFrame、缺少所需的列或没有任何行，所需的列不是数值， `line` 既不是 ``'event_rate'`` 也不是 ``'woe'`` ，或者 `ax`"
" 不是 matplotlib 的 Axes。"

msgid "The table that this chart draws."
msgstr "此图表所绘制的表。"

msgid ":obj:`psi_chart`"
msgstr ":obj:`psi_chart`"

msgid "Compare the shares of two samples in the same groups."
msgstr "比较两个样本在相同分组中的占比。"

msgid ""
"The tick labels are the group labels of the index, with ``NaN`` for the group of missing values. "
"Sort the table first, for example with ``table.sort_index()`` or ``table.sort_values(\"woe\")``, "
"to draw the groups in another order."
msgstr ""
"刻度标签是索引中的分组标签，缺失值分组标为 ``NaN`` 。要按其他顺序绘制各分组，请先对表排序，例如使用 ``table.sort_index()`` 或 "
"``table.sort_values(\"woe\")`` 。"

msgid ""
"Each y-axis is labeled in the color of what it shows, and the dotted line of zero WOE belongs to "
"the right axis. Both axes leave room at the top for the legend, so that it covers no bar and no "
"point."
msgstr "每个 y 轴的标签使用其所示内容的颜色，WOE 为零的点线属于右侧坐标轴。两个坐标轴都在顶部为图例留出空间，使图例不遮挡任何柱形和点。"

msgid ""
"Positive correlations are blue and negative ones amber, darker as they approach 1 or -1, so that "
"pairs of variables that carry the same information stand out before a model is fitted."
msgstr "正相关显示为蓝色，负相关显示为琥珀色，越接近 1 或 -1 颜色越深，这样在拟合模型之前就能看出哪些变量对携带相同的信息。"

msgid ""
"Square matrix of correlations with the same labels, in the same order, in its index and columns, "
"such as ``X.corr()`` or ``X.corr(method=\"spearman\")`` of the WOE-encoded candidates ``X``."
msgstr "相关系数方阵，其索引和列具有相同的标签且顺序相同，例如 WOE 编码后的候选变量 ``X`` 的 ``X.corr()`` 或 ``X.corr(method=\"spearman\")`` 。"

msgid "Axes to draw on. A new figure, sized to the number of variables, is created when it is not given."
msgstr "用于作图的 Axes。未给出时新建一个图形，其尺寸随变量个数而定。"

msgid "The Axes drawn on, `ax` when it is given."
msgstr "所绘制的 Axes；给出 `ax` 时即为 `ax` 。"

msgid ""
"If `matrix` is not a DataFrame, has no rows, does not have the same labels in its index and "
"columns, has a column that is not numeric or a value outside [-1, 1], such as a covariance, or "
"`ax` is not a matplotlib Axes."
msgstr ""
"如果 `matrix` 不是 DataFrame、没有任何行、索引与列的标签不同、有非数值的列或有超出 [-1, 1] 的值（例如协方差），或者 `ax` 不是 matplotlib 的 "
"Axes。"

msgid ":obj:`kivi.selection.correlation_filter`"
msgstr ":obj:`kivi.selection.correlation_filter`"

msgid "Drop one variable of each highly correlated pair."
msgstr "对每一对高度相关的变量，剔除其中一个。"

msgid ":obj:`kivi.selection.vif`"
msgstr ":obj:`kivi.selection.vif`"

msgid "Variance inflation factor of each variable."
msgstr "每个变量的方差膨胀因子。"

msgid ""
"The colors run from -1 to 1 whatever the values, and a missing value, such as the correlation of "
"a constant column, leaves its cell empty. The heatmap is ``ax.images[0]``, so "
"``ax.figure.colorbar(ax.images[0], ax=ax)`` adds a color bar."
msgstr ""
"无论取值如何，颜色都从 -1 覆盖到 1；缺失值（例如常数列的相关系数）所在的单元格留空。热力图即 ``ax.images[0]`` ，因此 "
"``ax.figure.colorbar(ax.images[0], ax=ax)`` 可以加上颜色条。"

msgid ""
"The curve plots ``true_positive_rate`` against ``false_positive_rate`` from the strictest "
"threshold to the loosest, next to the diagonal of a score that ranks at random. With `ks`, a "
"vertical segment marks the KS statistic: the largest distance between the curve and the diagonal."
msgstr ""
"曲线从最严格的阈值到最宽松的阈值，绘制 ``true_positive_rate`` 相对于 ``false_positive_rate`` 的变化，旁边是随机排序评分对应的对角线。设置 "
"`ks` 时，一条竖直线段标出 KS 统计量，即曲线与对角线之间的最大距离。"

msgid ""
"A table from `kivi.metrics.roc_table`. It needs the columns ``false_positive_rate`` and "
"``true_positive_rate``."
msgstr "由 `kivi.metrics.roc_table` 得到的表。需要包含 ``false_positive_rate`` 和 ``true_positive_rate`` 列。"

msgid "**ks**"
msgstr "**ks**"

msgid "Whether to mark the KS statistic."
msgstr "是否标出 KS 统计量。"

msgid "**label**"
msgstr "**label**"

msgid "str, optional"
msgstr "str，可选"

msgid "Legend entry of the curve. A legend is drawn only when a curve has a label."
msgstr "曲线在图例中的名称。只有当某条曲线带有标签时才绘制图例。"

msgid "Axes to draw on. A new figure is created when it is not given."
msgstr "用于作图的 Axes。未给出时新建一个图形。"

msgid ""
"If `table` is not a DataFrame, lacks a column it needs or has no rows, a column it needs is not "
"numeric, `ks` is not True or False, or `ax` is not a matplotlib Axes."
msgstr "如果 `table` 不是 DataFrame、缺少所需的列或没有任何行，所需的列不是数值， `ks` 不是 True 或 False，或者 `ax` 不是 matplotlib 的 Axes。"

msgid ":obj:`kivi.metrics.roc_table`"
msgstr ":obj:`kivi.metrics.roc_table`"

msgid "Area under the curve."
msgstr "曲线下面积。"

msgid ":obj:`gains_chart`"
msgstr ":obj:`gains_chart`"

msgid "The same separation against the share of the sample."
msgstr "以样本占比为横轴展示同样的区分能力。"

msgid ""
"The curve takes the next color of the Axes' color cycle, so that ROC curves of several scores "
"drawn on the same `ax` are told apart by color and by `label`. The KS segment and its value share"
" the color of their curve."
msgstr "曲线使用 Axes 颜色循环中的下一种颜色，因此在同一个 `ax` 上绘制多个评分的 ROC 曲线时，可以通过颜色和 `label` 区分它们。KS 线段及其数值与所属曲线颜色相同。"

msgid ""
"Reviewing the bands from the highest scores down, the curves show the share of all events and of "
"all non-events captured against the share of the sample reviewed, ``cum_total_share``. With `ks`,"
" a vertical segment marks the band with the largest ``ks``, the gap between the two curves."
msgstr ""
"从评分最高的评分段开始逐段向下审视，两条曲线分别表示已覆盖的事件和非事件占全部事件和全部非事件的比例，横轴是已审视的样本占比 ``cum_total_share`` 。设置 `ks` "
"时，一条竖直线段标出 ``ks`` （两条曲线之间的差距）最大的评分段。"

msgid ""
"A table from `kivi.metrics.gains_table`, with the highest band first. It needs the columns "
"``cum_total_share``, ``cum_event_share``, ``cum_non_event_share`` and ``ks``."
msgstr ""
"由 `kivi.metrics.gains_table` 得到的表，评分最高的评分段在前。需要包含 ``cum_total_share`` 、 ``cum_event_share`` 、 "
"``cum_non_event_share`` 和 ``ks`` 列。"

msgid "Whether to mark the largest ``ks``."
msgstr "是否标出最大的 ``ks`` 。"

msgid "Name of the score, added to the legend entries of both curves, as in ``cum_event_share (label)``."
msgstr "评分的名称，附加在两条曲线的图例名称之后，例如 ``cum_event_share (label)`` 。"

msgid ":obj:`kivi.metrics.gains_table`"
msgstr ":obj:`kivi.metrics.gains_table`"

msgid ":obj:`roc_chart`"
msgstr ":obj:`roc_chart`"

msgid "The same separation over all thresholds."
msgstr "在所有阈值上展示同样的区分能力。"

msgid ""
"Both curves start at the origin, before the first band is reviewed, and each band adds one point."
" The diagonal is the ``cum_event_share`` of a score that ranks at random."
msgstr "两条曲线都从原点出发（此时尚未审视任何评分段），每个评分段增加一个点。对角线是随机排序评分的 ``cum_event_share`` 。"

msgid ""
"The ``cum_event_share`` curve is solid and the ``cum_non_event_share`` curve dashed, both in the "
"next color of the Axes' color cycle, so that the gains of several scores drawn on the same `ax` "
"are told apart by color and by `label`. The KS segment and its value share that color. The legend"
" goes where it covers the fewest points; with several scores it has two entries for each, and "
"``ax.legend(loc=...)`` moves it."
msgstr ""
"``cum_event_share`` 曲线为实线， ``cum_non_event_share`` 曲线为虚线，两者都使用 Axes 颜色循环中的下一种颜色，因此在同一个 `ax` "
"上绘制多个评分的增益曲线时，可以通过颜色和 `label` 区分它们。KS 线段及其数值也使用该颜色。图例放在遮挡点最少的位置；有多个评分时，每个评分在图例中占两项，可以用 "
"``ax.legend(loc=...)`` 移动图例。"

msgid ""
"Each group of the table, such as a grade or a PD band, is one point with ``mean_probability`` on "
"the x-axis and ``event_rate`` on the y-axis. Points on the diagonal are calibrated, points above "
"it have more events than predicted and points below it fewer."
msgstr ""
"表中的每个分组（例如一个等级或一个 PD 区间）是一个点，x 轴为 ``mean_probability`` ，y 轴为 ``event_rate`` "
"。位于对角线上的点是校准良好的，位于对角线上方的点事件多于预测，位于下方的点事件少于预测。"

msgid ""
"A table from `kivi.calibration.calibration_table`. It needs the columns ``mean_probability`` and "
"``event_rate``."
msgstr "由 `kivi.calibration.calibration_table` 得到的表。需要包含 ``mean_probability`` 和 ``event_rate`` 列。"

msgid "Legend entry of the points. A legend is drawn only when a line has a label."
msgstr "这些点在图例中的名称。只有当某条线带有标签时才绘制图例。"

msgid ""
"If `table` is not a DataFrame, lacks a column it needs or has no rows, a column it needs is not "
"numeric, or `ax` is not a matplotlib Axes."
msgstr "如果 `table` 不是 DataFrame、缺少所需的列或没有任何行，所需的列不是数值，或者 `ax` 不是 matplotlib 的 Axes。"

msgid ":obj:`kivi.calibration.calibration_table`"
msgstr ":obj:`kivi.calibration.calibration_table`"

msgid ":obj:`kivi.calibration.binomial_test`"
msgstr ":obj:`kivi.calibration.binomial_test`"

msgid "Test the default rate of each grade."
msgstr "检验每个等级的违约率。"

msgid ""
"Both axes run from 0 to just above the largest rate drawn on `ax`, so that the diagonal stays at "
"45 degrees. The points are joined in the order of the table and take the next color of the Axes' "
"color cycle, so that the PDs of several models, or the same PDs before and after a correction, "
"can be compared on one `ax`."
msgstr ""
"两个坐标轴都从 0 延伸到略高于 `ax` 上所绘的最大比率，使对角线保持 45 度。各点按表中的顺序连接，并使用 Axes 颜色循环中的下一种颜色，因此可以在同一个 `ax` 上比较多个模型的"
" PD，或同一组 PD 校正前后的结果。"

msgid ""
"Each cut-off of the table is one point, with ``approval_rate`` on the x-axis and "
"``approved_event_rate``, the bad rate of the approved book, on the y-axis. A higher cut-off "
"approves more applicants and lets more events through, so the curve shows the price in risk of "
"each extra point of approval rate."
msgstr ""
"表中的每个截断点是一个点，x 轴为 ``approval_rate`` ，y 轴为通过客群的坏账率 ``approved_event_rate`` "
"。截断点越高，通过的申请人越多，放进来的事件也越多，因此这条曲线展示了通过率每提高一个百分点所付出的风险代价。"

msgid ""
"A table from `kivi.strategy.cutoff_table`. It needs the columns ``approval_rate`` and "
"``approved_event_rate``."
msgstr "由 `kivi.strategy.cutoff_table` 得到的表。需要包含 ``approval_rate`` 和 ``approved_event_rate`` 列。"

msgid ":obj:`kivi.strategy.cutoff_table`"
msgstr ":obj:`kivi.strategy.cutoff_table`"

msgid "Compare the decisions of two scores."
msgstr "比较两个评分的审批决策。"

msgid ""
"A cut-off below every score approves nothing and has a missing ``approved_event_rate``, so it is "
"left out of the curve. The curve takes the next color of the Axes' color cycle, so that the "
"curves of a current and a new score can be compared on one `ax`. The y-axis runs from 0 to just "
"above the largest rate drawn on `ax`."
msgstr ""
"低于所有评分的截断点不通过任何申请人，其 ``approved_event_rate`` 缺失，因此不出现在曲线上。曲线使用 Axes 颜色循环中的下一种颜色，因此可以在同一个 `ax` "
"上比较现行评分与新评分的曲线。y 轴从 0 延伸到略高于 `ax` 上所绘的最大比率。"

msgid ""
"Each group of the table gets a pair of bars, ``reference_share`` and ``current_share``, and the "
"legend gives the PSI of the whole table, so that the groups whose shares moved most can be read "
"off directly."
msgstr "表中的每个分组对应一对柱形，即 ``reference_share`` 和 ``current_share`` ，图例给出整张表的 PSI，因此可以直接看出哪些分组的占比变化最大。"

msgid ""
"A table from `kivi.stability.psi_table`. It needs the columns ``reference_share``, "
"``current_share`` and ``psi``."
msgstr "由 `kivi.stability.psi_table` 得到的表。需要包含 ``reference_share`` 、 ``current_share`` 和 ``psi`` 列。"

msgid ":obj:`monitoring_chart`"
msgstr ":obj:`monitoring_chart`"

msgid "The PSI of a score in each period."
msgstr "评分在每一期的 PSI。"

msgid ""
"The shares are those of the table, so with smoothing a group that is empty in one sample shows "
"the small share that smoothing gave it. The tick labels are the group labels of the index, with "
"``NaN`` for the group of missing values."
msgstr "图中的占比就是表中的占比，因此在平滑之下，某个样本中为空的分组会显示平滑赋予它的微小占比。刻度标签是索引中的分组标签，缺失值分组标为 ``NaN`` 。"

msgid "The y-axis leaves room at the top for the legend, so that it covers no bar."
msgstr "y 轴在顶部为图例留出空间，使图例不遮挡任何柱形。"

msgid ""
"The periods of the table run along the x-axis in its order, and `column` is drawn as a line or as"
" bars, as `kind` says. Dashed lines can mark the `levels` that the column is compared with, such "
"as the PSI thresholds or the Gini of the development sample."
msgstr "表中的各期按表的顺序沿 x 轴排列， `column` 按 `kind` 的指定绘制为折线或柱形。可以用虚线标出与该列比较的 `levels` ，例如 PSI 阈值或开发样本的 Gini。"

msgid ""
"A table from `kivi.monitoring.monitoring_table`, or another table with one row per period, such "
"as one from `kivi.monitoring.stability_table`. It needs the column named by `column`."
msgstr ""
"由 `kivi.monitoring.monitoring_table` 得到的表，或其他每期一行的表，例如 `kivi.monitoring.stability_table` 的结果。需要包含"
" `column` 指定的列。"

msgid "**column**"
msgstr "**column**"

msgid "str, default 'psi'"
msgstr "str，默认 'psi'"

msgid "Column to draw."
msgstr "要绘制的列。"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "{'line', 'bar'}, default 'line'"
msgstr "{'line', 'bar'}，默认 'line'"

msgid ""
"Draw the column as a line, which suits rates and measures such as ``event_rate`` and ``gini`` and"
" several columns on one `ax`, or as bars, which suit counts such as ``total`` and a single "
"``psi``."
msgstr ""
"把该列绘制为折线，适合 ``event_rate`` 和 ``gini`` 等比率和指标，也适合在同一个 `ax` 上绘制多列；或者绘制为柱形，适合 ``total`` 等计数和单独的 "
"``psi`` 。"

msgid ""
"Legend entry of the line or the bars. A legend is drawn only when something on the Axes has a "
"label."
msgstr "折线或柱形在图例中的名称。只有当 Axes 上有带标签的元素时才绘制图例。"

msgid "**levels**"
msgstr "**levels**"

msgid "float or sequence of float, default ()"
msgstr "float 或 float 序列，默认 ()"

msgid ""
"Values of `column` to mark with dashed horizontal lines, such as the PSI thresholds ``[0.1, "
"0.25]`` or the Gini of the development sample. Each line is labeled with its value at its right "
"end."
msgstr "用水平虚线标出的 `column` 取值，例如 PSI 阈值 ``[0.1, 0.25]`` 或开发样本的 Gini。每条虚线的右端标有其数值。"

msgid ""
"If `table` is not a DataFrame, has no rows or has no numeric column named `column`, `kind` is "
"neither ``'line'`` nor ``'bar'``, a level is not a finite number, or `ax` is not a matplotlib "
"Axes."
msgstr ""
"如果 `table` 不是 DataFrame、没有任何行或没有名为 `column` 的数值列， `kind` 既不是 ``'line'`` 也不是 ``'bar'`` "
"，某个水平值不是有限数，或者 `ax` 不是 matplotlib 的 Axes。"

msgid ":obj:`kivi.monitoring.monitoring_table`"
msgstr ":obj:`kivi.monitoring.monitoring_table`"

msgid "The shares behind the PSI of one period."
msgstr "某一期 PSI 背后的各分组占比。"

msgid ""
"The y-axis is labeled with `column`, or with ``psi`` when the columns of `table` are named "
"``variable``, as those of `kivi.monitoring.stability_table` are, whose columns are the PSIs of "
"the variables. The x-axis is labeled with the name of the index."
msgstr ""
"y 轴以 `column` 为标签；当 `table` 的列名为 ``variable`` 时（ `kivi.monitoring.stability_table` "
"的列就是如此，其各列是各变量的 PSI），则以 ``psi`` 为标签。x 轴以索引的名称为标签。"

msgid ""
"A missing value, such as the ``gini`` of a period whose outcomes are not known yet, leaves a gap "
"in the line and no bar. To draw several columns, call the function once for each: on the panels "
"of one figure for columns on different scales, or on one `ax` with a `label` each, as for the "
"variables of a stability table. The line or the bars take the next color of the Axes' color "
"cycle, and the legend sits to the right of the Axes, so that it covers no line."
msgstr ""
"缺失值（例如结果尚未可知的某一期的 ``gini`` "
"）会在折线上留下缺口，也不画柱形。要绘制多列，请对每一列各调用一次此函数：量纲不同的列画在同一图形的不同子图上，或者像稳定性表的各变量那样，各自带一个 `label` 画在同一个 `ax` "
"上。折线或柱形使用 Axes 颜色循环中的下一种颜色，图例位于 Axes 的右侧，不遮挡任何折线。"

msgid ""
"Each row of the table is a cohort and each column a month on book. Later cohorts are drawn in "
"darker blue, so that a cohort whose curve rises faster than those before it stands out."
msgstr "表中的每一行是一个批次，每一列是一个账龄月。越晚的批次蓝色越深，因此曲线比之前各批次上升得更快的批次会很醒目。"

msgid ""
"A table from `kivi.vintage.vintage_table`, with one row per cohort and one numeric column per "
"month on book, or another table of the same shape, such as cumulative PDs from "
"`kivi.lifetime.convert_pd`."
msgstr ""
"由 `kivi.vintage.vintage_table` 得到的表，每个批次一行、每个账龄月一个数值列；也可以是形状相同的其他表，例如 `kivi.lifetime.convert_pd` "
"给出的累计 PD。"

msgid ""
"If `table` is not a DataFrame or has no rows, its columns are not numbers, it holds a value that "
"is not numeric, or `ax` is not a matplotlib Axes."
msgstr "如果 `table` 不是 DataFrame 或没有任何行、列名不是数字、含有非数值的值，或者 `ax` 不是 matplotlib 的 Axes。"

msgid ":obj:`kivi.lifetime.convert_pd`"
msgstr ":obj:`kivi.lifetime.convert_pd`"

msgid "Turn the curves into marginal or conditional PDs."
msgstr "把这些曲线转换为边际 PD 或条件 PD。"

msgid ""
"The missing months of a cohort, those it has not reached or that come before its first observed "
"month on book, are left out of its curve. The x-axis is labeled with the name of the columns."
msgstr "批次缺失的月份（尚未到达的账龄月，或首个观测账龄月之前的月份）不画入其曲线。x 轴以列的名称为标签。"

msgid ""
"The legend sits to the right of the Axes, so that it covers no curve, and is titled with the name"
" of the index. It names every cohort when there are at most eight, and otherwise eight cohorts "
"evenly spread from the first to the last, since the shades of the others lie between theirs. In a"
" figure of several panels, use a layout engine, such as ``layout=\"constrained\"``, to make room "
"for it."
msgstr ""
"图例位于 Axes "
"的右侧，不遮挡任何曲线，并以索引的名称为标题。批次不超过八个时，图例列出每个批次；否则列出从第一个到最后一个均匀分布的八个批次，其余批次的颜色深浅介于它们之间。在包含多个子图的图形中，请使用布局引擎（例如"
" ``layout=\"constrained\"`` ）为图例留出空间。"

msgid ""
"Supply outcomes for rejected applicants, so that a model developed on the approved applicants can"
" be refitted on all of them. :func:`~kivi.reject_inference.fuzzy_augmentation` and "
":func:`~kivi.reject_inference.parceling` return inferred rows with weights, and "
":func:`~kivi.reject_inference.reweighting` returns weights for the approved applicants."
msgstr ""
"为被拒绝的申请人补充结果，从而可以把在获批申请人上开发的模型在全部申请人上重新拟合。 :func:`~kivi.reject_inference.fuzzy_augmentation` 和 "
":func:`~kivi.reject_inference.parceling` 返回带权重的推断行， :func:`~kivi.reject_inference.reweighting` "
"返回获批申请人的权重。"

msgid "See :doc:`/user_guide/reject_inference` for a comparison of the methods on synthetic applications."
msgstr "各方法在合成申请数据上的比较见 :doc:`/user_guide/reject_inference` 。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`fuzzy_augmentation <kivi.reject_inference.fuzzy_augmentation>`\\ \\(probability\\, "
"\\*\\[\\, factor\\]\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`fuzzy_augmentation <kivi.reject_inference.fuzzy_augmentation>`\\ \\(probability\\, "
"\\*\\[\\, factor\\]\\)"

msgid "Split each rejected applicant into a bad and a good row with fractional weights."
msgstr "把每个拒绝申请人拆成带小数权重的一行坏样本和一行好样本。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`parceling <kivi.reject_inference.parceling>`\\ \\(score\\, target\\, reject\\_score\\, "
"\\*\\[\\, ...\\]\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`parceling <kivi.reject_inference.parceling>`\\ \\(score\\, target\\, reject\\_score\\, "
"\\*\\[\\, ...\\]\\)"

msgid "Label rejected applicants bad or good at the bad rate of their score band."
msgstr "按所在评分段的坏账率把拒绝申请人标记为坏或好。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`reweighting <kivi.reject_inference.reweighting>`\\ \\(score\\, reject\\_score\\, "
"\\*\\[\\, bins\\]\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`reweighting <kivi.reject_inference.reweighting>`\\ \\(score\\, reject\\_score\\, "
"\\*\\[\\, bins\\]\\)"

msgid "Weight accepted applicants to stand in for the rejected applicants of their score band."
msgstr "给获批申请人加权，使其代表同一评分段的拒绝申请人。"

msgid ""
"The PD of a reject under the model fitted on the accepted applicants alone gives the weight of "
"its bad row, and the rest of its weight of 1 goes to its good row. Concatenate the rows with the "
"accepted applicants at weight 1 and refit the model with weights."
msgstr "拒绝申请人在仅用获批申请人拟合的模型下的 PD 作为其坏样本行的权重，总权重 1 的其余部分归其好样本行。把这些行与权重为 1 的获批申请人拼接起来，再带权重重新拟合模型。"

msgid "PD of each rejected applicant under the accepts-only model, between 0 and 1."
msgstr "每个拒绝申请人在仅用通过样本拟合的模型下的 PD，介于 0 和 1 之间。"

msgid "**factor**"
msgstr "**factor**"

msgid "float, default 1"
msgstr "float，默认 1"

msgid ""
"Positive multiplier of the PDs. A factor above 1 assumes that the rejects are riskier than "
"accepted applicants with the same PD, as when the approval used information that the model does "
"not have."
msgstr "PD 的正乘数。大于 1 的倍数假定拒绝样本比 PD 相同的获批申请人风险更高，例如审批时用到了模型所没有的信息。"

msgid ""
"Two rows per rejected applicant, the bad row first, with the columns ``target``, 1 and then 0, "
"and ``weight``, the PD times `factor` clipped to [0, 1] and its complement. The index repeats the"
" index of `probability`, or its positions when it is not a Series. When `probability` is a Series"
" with the unique index of the rejects, ``rejects.loc[result.index]`` gives the features of every "
"row."
msgstr ""
"每个拒绝申请人两行，坏样本行在前，列为 ``target`` （先 1 后 0）和 ``weight`` （PD 乘以 `factor` 后截断到 [0, 1] 的值及其补数）。索引重复 "
"`probability` 的索引，不是 Series 时重复其位置。当 `probability` 是索引与拒绝样本相同且不重复的 Series 时， "
"``rejects.loc[result.index]`` 给出每一行的特征。"

msgid ""
"If `probability` is empty, not one-dimensional or not numeric, or has a value that is missing or "
"outside [0, 1]; or if `factor` is not a positive finite number."
msgstr "如果 `probability` 为空、不是一维或不是数值，或有缺失值或位于 [0, 1] 之外的值；或者 `factor` 不是有限正数。"

msgid ":obj:`parceling`"
msgstr ":obj:`parceling`"

msgid "Infer the outcomes from the bad rate of a score band."
msgstr "根据评分段的坏账率推断结果。"

msgid ":obj:`reweighting`"
msgstr ":obj:`reweighting`"

msgid "Weight the accepted applicants instead."
msgstr "改为给获批申请人加权。"

msgid "Refit the model with ``weights``."
msgstr "用 ``weights`` 重新拟合模型。"

msgid "A reject with PD :math:`p` and the factor :math:`k` gets the rows"
msgstr "PD 为 :math:`p` 、倍数为 :math:`k` 的拒绝申请人得到以下两行"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"(y = 1,\\ w = \\min(k p, 1)) \\quad \\text{and} \\quad\n"
"(y = 0,\\ w = 1 - \\min(k p, 1))."
msgstr ""
"(y = 1,\\ w = \\min(k p, 1)) \\quad \\text{和} \\quad\n"
"(y = 0,\\ w = 1 - \\min(k p, 1))."

msgid ""
"Clipping keeps both weights in [0, 1]: when :math:`k p \\ge 1`, the reject counts as bad with its"
" whole weight and its good row has weight 0, which kivi's ``weights`` arguments ignore. Each "
"reject keeps a total weight of 1, so the weighted bad rate of its rows is the mean of "
":math:`\\min(k p_i, 1)`."
msgstr ""
"截断使两个权重都在 [0, 1] 之内：当 :math:`k p \\ge 1` 时，拒绝申请人以全部权重计为坏样本，其好样本行的权重为 0，kivi 的 ``weights`` "
"参数会忽略这样的行。每个拒绝申请人的总权重保持为 1，因此这些行的加权坏账率是 :math:`\\min(k p_i, 1)` 的均值。"

msgid ""
"With ``factor=1``, refitting the same logistic regression on the same encoding returns the "
"coefficients of the accepts-only model exactly: at those coefficients, the weight of each "
"reject's bad row equals its fitted PD, so the inferred rows leave the score equations unchanged. "
"The refit only narrows the standard errors, although the inferred rows add no information: with "
"these weights, the standard errors of `kivi.selection.logistic_regression` are too small. The "
"model changes only with a factor other than 1, with another encoding, such as WOE refitted on the"
" augmented sample, or with other variables."
msgstr ""
"当 ``factor=1`` 时，在同一编码上重新拟合同一个逻辑回归，得到的恰好是仅用通过样本拟合的模型的系数：在这组系数下，每个拒绝申请人坏样本行的权重等于其拟合 "
"PD，因此推断出的行不改变得分方程。重新拟合只会缩小标准误，尽管推断出的行并没有增加任何信息：在这样的权重下， `kivi.selection.logistic_regression` "
"的标准误偏小。只有倍数不为 1、换用其他编码（例如在扩充后的样本上重新拟合 WOE）或换用其他变量时，模型才会改变。"

msgid ""
"N. Siddiqi, \"Credit Risk Scorecards: Developing and Implementing Intelligent Credit Scoring\", "
"Wiley, 2006."
msgstr ""
"N. Siddiqi, \"Credit Risk Scorecards: Developing and Implementing Intelligent Credit Scoring\", "
"Wiley, 2006."

msgid "[R163332bd4527-1]_"
msgstr "[R163332bd4527-1]_"

msgid ""
"The scores of the accepted and the rejected applicants are divided into bands. In each band, the "
"bad rate of the rejects is `factor` times the observed bad rate of the accepted applicants, at "
"most 1, and that share of the band's rejects, chosen at random, is labelled bad."
msgstr "把获批申请人和拒绝申请人的评分划分为若干评分段。在每个评分段内，拒绝样本的坏账率为获批申请人观测坏账率的 `factor` 倍（最多为 1），并随机选取该比例的拒绝样本标记为坏。"

msgid ""
"Finite numeric scores of the accepted applicants, such as their PD under the accepts-only model. "
"The direction does not matter."
msgstr "获批申请人的有限数值评分，例如其在仅用通过样本拟合的模型下的 PD。方向无关紧要。"

msgid ""
"Observed outcomes of the accepted applicants, 1 for bad and 0 for good, with both present. If "
"`score` and `target` are both pandas Series, they must have identical indices; otherwise they are"
" matched by position."
msgstr "获批申请人观测到的结果，1 表示坏、0 表示好，两者都必须出现。如果 `score` 和 `target` 都是 pandas Series，二者的索引必须完全相同；否则按位置对应。"

msgid "**reject_score**"
msgstr "**reject_score**"

msgid "Finite numeric scores of the rejected applicants, on the scale of `score`."
msgstr "拒绝申请人的有限数值评分，与 `score` 的尺度相同。"

msgid ""
"Number of quantile bands, fitted with `kivi.binning.bin_edges` on the scores of accepted and "
"rejected applicants together, so tied scores can leave fewer bands; or increasing band edges, "
"closed on the right, that hold every score."
msgstr "分位数评分段的个数，由 `kivi.binning.bin_edges` 在获批和拒绝申请人的评分合并后拟合，因此评分并列时评分段可能更少；或者递增的右闭评分段边界，须包含所有评分。"

msgid ""
"Positive multiplier of the accepted applicants' bad rate in each band. A factor above 1 assumes "
"that the rejects are riskier than accepted applicants with the same score."
msgstr "各评分段内获批申请人坏账率的正乘数。大于 1 的倍数假定拒绝样本比评分相同的获批申请人风险更高。"

msgid "**expected**"
msgstr "**expected**"

msgid ""
"Return two rows per reject, weighted with the band's inferred bad rate and its complement as in "
"`fuzzy_augmentation`, instead of a random label."
msgstr "每个拒绝申请人返回两行，像 `fuzzy_augmentation` 那样以该评分段推断的坏账率及其补数为权重，而不是随机标签。"

msgid ""
"Seed or generator passed to `numpy.random.default_rng` to draw the labels. The global NumPy "
"random state is not used, so the same seed gives the same labels. Not used with "
"``expected=True``."
msgstr ""
"传给 `numpy.random.default_rng` 、用于抽取标签的种子或生成器。不使用 NumPy 的全局随机状态，因此同一个种子总是给出同样的标签。 "
"``expected=True`` 时不使用。"

msgid ""
"The columns ``target`` and ``weight``, indexed like `reject_score`, or by position when it is not"
" a Series. One row per rejected applicant with its label and the weight 1, or, with "
"``expected=True``, two rows per rejected applicant as returned by `fuzzy_augmentation`."
msgstr ""
"包含 ``target`` 和 ``weight`` 两列，索引与 `reject_score` 相同（不是 Series 时为位置）。每个拒绝申请人一行，带其标签和权重 1；或者在 "
"``expected=True`` 时，每个拒绝申请人两行，与 `fuzzy_augmentation` 的返回值相同。"

msgid ""
"If `score` and `target` are invalid as for `kivi.metrics.gains_table`; if `reject_score` is "
"empty, not one-dimensional or not numeric, or has a missing or infinite value; if `bins` is "
"neither a positive integer nor at least two increasing edges, or a score lies outside the edges; "
"if a band holds rejected applicants but no accepted one, so that its bad rate is unknown; or if "
"`factor` is not a positive finite number, `expected` is not a boolean, or `rng` is not a seed or "
"generator that `numpy.random.default_rng` accepts."
msgstr ""
"如果 `score` 和 `target` 不符合 `kivi.metrics.gains_table` 的要求；如果 `reject_score` "
"为空、不是一维或不是数值，或含有缺失值或无穷值；如果 `bins` "
"既不是正整数，也不是至少两个递增的边界，或者有评分落在边界之外；如果某个评分段有拒绝申请人却没有获批申请人，因而其坏账率未知；或者 `factor` 不是有限正数， `expected` "
"不是布尔值，或 `rng` 不是 `numpy.random.default_rng` 接受的种子或生成器。"

msgid "If tied scores leave fewer quantile bands than `bins`."
msgstr "如果评分并列使分位数评分段少于 `bins` 。"

msgid ":obj:`fuzzy_augmentation`"
msgstr ":obj:`fuzzy_augmentation`"

msgid "Infer the outcomes from each reject's own PD."
msgstr "根据每个拒绝申请人自己的 PD 推断结果。"

msgid "Weight the accepted applicants of each band instead."
msgstr "改为给各评分段的获批申请人加权。"

msgid "Bad rates by score band."
msgstr "各评分段的坏账率。"

msgid ""
"In a band with :math:`a` accepted applicants of whom :math:`b` are bad, and :math:`n` rejects, "
"the inferred bad rate is :math:`r = \\min(k b / a, 1)` for the factor :math:`k`. The number of "
"bad rejects is :math:`r n` rounded down or up at random, up with a probability equal to its "
"fractional part, so it is :math:`r n` on average and never further from it than 1. With "
"``expected=True``, each reject instead gets a bad row with the weight :math:`r` and a good row "
"with :math:`1 - r`, which removes the noise of the draw."
msgstr ""
"若一个评分段有 :math:`a` 个获批申请人（其中 :math:`b` 个为坏）和 :math:`n` 个拒绝申请人，则倍数为 :math:`k` 时推断的坏账率为 :math:`r = "
"\\min(k b / a, 1)` 。坏的拒绝申请人个数为 :math:`r n` 随机向下或向上取整，向上取整的概率等于其小数部分，因此平均为 :math:`r n` ，且与之相差从不超过 "
"1。 ``expected=True`` 时，每个拒绝申请人改为得到权重为 :math:`r` 的坏样本行和权重为 :math:`1 - r` 的好样本行，从而消除抽样噪声。"

msgid ""
"Parceling uses the score only: within a band, it treats every reject alike, whatever its "
"features. A reject's inferred bad rate depends on the accepted applicants of its band, which are "
"few in the bands where the approval rate is low."
msgstr "打包法只使用评分：在一个评分段内，它对每个拒绝申请人一视同仁，不论其特征如何。拒绝申请人推断的坏账率取决于其所在评分段的获批申请人，而在通过率低的评分段里，获批申请人很少。"

msgid "[Rc29e884af050-1]_"
msgstr "[Rc29e884af050-1]_"

msgid ""
"The accepted applicants have the bad rate 1/4 in the low band and 3/4 in the high band. Three of "
"the four rejects of the high band are therefore labelled bad, and the one reject of the low band "
"is bad with the probability 1/4:"
msgstr "获批申请人在低评分段的坏账率为 1/4，在高评分段为 3/4。因此高评分段的四个拒绝申请人中有三个被标记为坏，低评分段唯一的拒绝申请人以 1/4 的概率为坏："

msgid ""
"With ``expected=True``, every reject instead gets the bad rate of its band as the weight of its "
"bad row:"
msgstr "``expected=True`` 时，每个拒绝申请人改为以所在评分段的坏账率作为其坏样本行的权重："

msgid ""
"In each band of the score, every accepted applicant gets the weight (accepted + rejected) / "
"accepted, the inverse of the band's approval rate. The weighted accepted applicants then add up "
"to all the applicants of their band, so a model refitted with these weights gives each band its "
"share of the applicant population."
msgstr ""
"在每个评分段内，每个获批申请人得到权重（获批 + 拒绝）/ "
"获批，即该评分段通过率的倒数。加权后的获批申请人合计等于该评分段的全部申请人，因此用这些权重重新拟合的模型让每个评分段占有其在申请人总体中的份额。"

msgid ""
"Weight of each accepted applicant, at least 1. A Series named ``weight`` with the index of "
"`score` when `score` is a Series, otherwise an array."
msgstr "每个获批申请人的权重，至少为 1。 `score` 是 Series 时返回名为 ``weight`` 、索引与 `score` 相同的 Series，否则返回数组。"

msgid ""
"If `score` or `reject_score` is empty, not one-dimensional or not numeric, or has a missing or "
"infinite value; if `bins` is neither a positive integer nor at least two increasing edges, or a "
"score lies outside the edges; or if a band holds rejected applicants but no accepted one."
msgstr ""
"如果 `score` 或 `reject_score` 为空、不是一维或不是数值，或含有缺失值或无穷值；如果 `bins` "
"既不是正整数，也不是至少两个递增的边界，或者有评分落在边界之外；或者某个评分段有拒绝申请人却没有获批申请人。"

msgid "Infer outcomes for the rejects instead."
msgstr "改为推断拒绝样本的结果。"

msgid "Label the rejects of each band at its bad rate."
msgstr "按各评分段的坏账率标记其中的拒绝样本。"

msgid ""
"With :math:`a` accepted and :math:`n` rejected applicants in a band, each accepted applicant of "
"the band gets the weight"
msgstr "若一个评分段有 :math:`a` 个获批申请人和 :math:`n` 个拒绝申请人，该评分段的每个获批申请人得到权重"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "w = \\frac{a + n}{a}."
msgstr "w = \\frac{a + n}{a}."

msgid ""
"Reweighting assumes that, within a band, the rejects default like the accepted applicants. It "
"changes how much each band weighs in the fit, but adds no outcomes, so the rejects are predicted "
"to be as risky as accepted applicants with the same score. It cannot represent applicants that no"
" accepted applicant resembles: a band of rejects without accepted applicants raises an error. "
"Bands of a score that decided the approval with a hard cut-off have no accepted applicants beyond"
" the cut-off, so use a score on which accepted and rejected applicants overlap, such as the PD of"
" the accepts-only model."
msgstr ""
"重新加权假定在一个评分段内，拒绝样本与获批申请人的违约情况相同。它改变各评分段在拟合中的分量，但不增加任何结果，因此拒绝样本被预测为与评分相同的获批申请人风险相当。它无法代表与任何获批申请人都不相似的申请人：只有拒绝样本而没有获批申请人的评分段会引发错误。若某个评分以硬截断决定审批，按它划分的评分段在截断点以外没有获批申请人，因此应使用获批与拒绝申请人有重叠的评分，例如仅用通过样本拟合的模型的"
" PD。"

msgid ""
"The weights add up to more than the number of accepted applicants, so the standard errors of a "
"fit with them are too small, as if the outcomes of all applicants had been observed."
msgstr "这些权重之和大于获批申请人的个数，因此用它们拟合得到的标准误偏小，就好像所有申请人的结果都被观测到了一样。"

msgid "[R0bbcb3cec2a1-1]_"
msgstr "[R0bbcb3cec2a1-1]_"

msgid "The low band has 4 accepted applicants and 1 reject, the high band 2 and 4:"
msgstr "低评分段有 4 个获批申请人和 1 个拒绝申请人，高评分段分别为 2 个和 4 个："

msgid "Scorecard"
msgstr "评分卡"

msgid ""
"Turn a logistic regression on WOE values into points. :func:`~kivi.scorecard.score_scaling`, "
":func:`~kivi.scorecard.pd_to_score` and :func:`~kivi.scorecard.score_to_pd` set and apply the "
"scale, :func:`~kivi.scorecard.points_table` and :func:`~kivi.scorecard.woe_to_points` give the "
"points, and :func:`~kivi.scorecard.reason_codes` lists the variables that lowered a score most."
msgstr ""
"把基于 WOE 的逻辑回归转换为分值。 :func:`~kivi.scorecard.score_scaling` 、 :func:`~kivi.scorecard.pd_to_score` 和"
" :func:`~kivi.scorecard.score_to_pd` 设定并应用刻度， :func:`~kivi.scorecard.points_table` 和 "
":func:`~kivi.scorecard.woe_to_points` 给出分值， :func:`~kivi.scorecard.reason_codes` 列出使评分降低最多的变量。"

msgid "See :doc:`/user_guide/scorecard` for a scorecard built on the bundled data."
msgstr "基于内置数据构建的评分卡见 :doc:`/user_guide/scorecard` 。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`score_scaling <kivi.scorecard.score_scaling>`\\ \\(\\*\\, pdo\\, base\\_score\\, "
"base\\_odds\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`score_scaling <kivi.scorecard.score_scaling>`\\ \\(\\*\\, pdo\\, base\\_score\\, "
"base\\_odds\\)"

msgid "Return the factor and offset that turn log odds into a score."
msgstr "返回把对数几率转换为分数的因子（factor）和偏移量（offset）。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`pd_to_score <kivi.scorecard.pd_to_score>`\\ \\(probability\\, \\*\\, pdo\\, "
"base\\_score\\, ...\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`pd_to_score <kivi.scorecard.pd_to_score>`\\ \\(probability\\, \\*\\, pdo\\, "
"base\\_score\\, ...\\)"

msgid "Convert event probabilities to scorecard scores."
msgstr "把事件概率转换为评分卡分数。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`score_to_pd <kivi.scorecard.score_to_pd>`\\ \\(score\\, \\*\\, pdo\\, base\\_score\\, "
"base\\_odds\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`score_to_pd <kivi.scorecard.score_to_pd>`\\ \\(score\\, \\*\\, pdo\\, base\\_score\\, "
"base\\_odds\\)"

msgid "Convert scorecard scores to event probabilities."
msgstr "把评分卡分数转换为事件概率。"

msgid ":py:obj:`points_table <kivi.scorecard.points_table>`\\ \\(tables\\, coefficients\\, ...\\)"
msgstr ":py:obj:`points_table <kivi.scorecard.points_table>`\\ \\(tables\\, coefficients\\, ...\\)"

msgid "Turn a logistic regression on WOE values into points for each group."
msgstr "把基于 WOE 的逻辑回归转换为每个分组的分值。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`woe_to_points <kivi.scorecard.woe_to_points>`\\ \\(woe\\, coefficients\\, intercept\\, "
"...\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`woe_to_points <kivi.scorecard.woe_to_points>`\\ \\(woe\\, coefficients\\, intercept\\, "
"...\\)"

msgid "Give each applicant the points of each variable from its WOE values."
msgstr "根据 WOE 值给出每个申请人在各变量上的分值。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`reason_codes <kivi.scorecard.reason_codes>`\\ \\(points\\, table\\, \\*\\[\\, top\\, "
"atol\\, ...\\]\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`reason_codes <kivi.scorecard.reason_codes>`\\ \\(points\\, table\\, \\*\\[\\, top\\, "
"atol\\, ...\\]\\)"

msgid "Name the variables that cost each applicant the most points."
msgstr "列出让每个申请人失分最多的变量。"

msgid ""
"A scorecard score is linear in the log of the good:bad odds. It equals `base_score` at odds of "
"`base_odds` and rises by `pdo` points each time the odds double."
msgstr "评分卡分数与好坏比（good:bad odds）的对数呈线性关系。几率为 `base_odds` 时分数等于 `base_score` ，几率每翻一倍，分数增加 `pdo` 分。"

msgid "**pdo**"
msgstr "**pdo**"

msgid "Points to double the odds. Must be positive."
msgstr "几率翻倍所需增加的分数（PDO），必须为正数。"

msgid "**base_score**"
msgstr "**base_score**"

msgid "Score at the base odds."
msgstr "基准几率对应的分数。"

msgid "**base_odds**"
msgstr "**base_odds**"

msgid "Good:bad odds at the base score, such as 50 for 50 non-events per event. Must be positive."
msgstr "基准分数对应的好坏比，例如 50 表示每个事件对应 50 个非事件。必须为正数。"

msgid "Points per unit of log odds, ``pdo / ln 2``."
msgstr "对数几率每增加一个单位对应的分数，即 ``pdo / ln 2`` 。"

msgid "**offset**"
msgstr "**offset**"

msgid "Score at even odds, ``base_score - factor * ln(base_odds)``."
msgstr "几率为 1:1 时的分数，即 ``base_score - factor * ln(base_odds)`` 。"

msgid "If an argument is not a finite number, or `pdo` or `base_odds` is not positive."
msgstr "如果某个参数不是有限数值，或者 `pdo` 或 `base_odds` 不是正数。"

msgid ":obj:`pd_to_score`"
msgstr ":obj:`pd_to_score`"

msgid "Convert event probabilities to scores."
msgstr "把事件概率转换为分数。"

msgid ":obj:`score_to_pd`"
msgstr ":obj:`score_to_pd`"

msgid "Convert scores to event probabilities."
msgstr "把分数转换为事件概率。"

msgid "With odds :math:`o = (1 - p) / p` for an event probability :math:`p`,"
msgstr "对事件概率 :math:`p` ，记几率 :math:`o = (1 - p) / p` ，则"

msgid ""
"\\mathrm{score} = \\mathrm{offset} + \\mathrm{factor} \\cdot \\ln o,\n"
"\n"
"\\mathrm{factor} = \\frac{\\mathrm{pdo}}{\\ln 2}, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathrm{offset} = \\mathrm{base\\_score} - \\mathrm{factor} \\cdot \\ln \\mathrm{base\\_odds}."
msgstr ""
"\\mathrm{score} = \\mathrm{offset} + \\mathrm{factor} \\cdot \\ln o,\n"
"\n"
"\\mathrm{factor} = \\frac{\\mathrm{pdo}}{\\ln 2}, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathrm{offset} = \\mathrm{base\\_score} - \\mathrm{factor} \\cdot \\ln \\mathrm{base\\_odds}."

msgid ""
"A lower probability of the event, such as a default, gives a higher score. The scaling is set by "
"`pdo`, `base_score` and `base_odds`, as in `score_scaling`."
msgstr "事件（例如违约）的概率越低，分数越高。刻度由 `pdo` 、 `base_score` 和 `base_odds` 决定，与 `score_scaling` 相同。"

msgid "Event probabilities strictly between 0 and 1. Missing values give missing scores."
msgstr "严格介于 0 与 1 之间的事件概率。缺失值对应的分数也为缺失。"

msgid "Good:bad odds at the base score. Must be positive."
msgstr "基准分数对应的好坏比，必须为正数。"

msgid ""
"Scores with the shape of `probability`. A Series input gives a Series with the same index and "
"name, and a scalar gives a float."
msgstr "分数，形状与 `probability` 相同。输入为 Series 时返回 Series，索引和名称保持不变；输入为标量时返回 float。"

msgid ""
"If `probability` is not real and numeric or has values outside the open interval (0, 1), or the "
"scaling arguments are invalid."
msgstr "如果 `probability` 不是实数数值或含有开区间 (0, 1) 以外的值，或者刻度参数无效。"

msgid "The inverse conversion."
msgstr "反向转换。"

msgid ":obj:`score_scaling`"
msgstr ":obj:`score_scaling`"

msgid "The factor and offset of the scaling."
msgstr "刻度的因子和偏移量。"

msgid ""
"The score is ``offset + factor * ln((1 - probability) / probability)``. A probability of exactly "
"0 or 1 has no finite score and raises an error; see `score_to_pd` for the scores whose "
"probability rounds to 1."
msgstr ""
"分数为 ``offset + factor * ln((1 - probability) / probability)`` 。概率恰好为 0 或 1 "
"时没有有限的分数，会引发错误；哪些分数对应的概率会舍入为 1，参见 `score_to_pd` 。"

msgid ""
"This is the inverse of `pd_to_score` for the same scaling, so it gives the probability of the "
"event implied by each score."
msgstr "在相同刻度下，这是 `pd_to_score` 的逆运算，给出每个分数所隐含的事件概率。"

msgid "Scores. Missing values give missing probabilities."
msgstr "分数。缺失值对应的概率也为缺失。"

msgid "If `score` is not real and numeric, or the scaling arguments are invalid."
msgstr "如果 `score` 不是实数数值，或者刻度参数无效。"

msgid ""
"The probability is ``1 / (1 + exp((score - offset) / factor))``, computed without overflow for "
"extreme scores. In double precision it rounds to exactly 1 for scores more than about ``36.7 * "
"factor`` below the offset, -572 for the scale in the example, and `pd_to_score` rejects such "
"probabilities. Scores that low do not occur on a practical scale."
msgstr ""
"概率为 ``1 / (1 + exp((score - offset) / factor))`` ，计算方式保证极端分数也不会溢出。在双精度下，比偏移量低约 ``36.7 * factor`` "
"以上的分数（示例刻度下为 -572）对应的概率会舍入为 1，而 `pd_to_score` 不接受这样的概率。在实际使用的刻度上不会出现这么低的分数。"

msgid ""
"The points of an applicant's groups, one per variable, add up to the score that `pd_to_score` "
"gives for the model's probability. The intercept is spread evenly across the variables."
msgstr "申请人在各变量上所属分组的分值（每个变量一个）之和，等于 `pd_to_score` 对模型概率给出的分数。截距平均分摊到各个变量。"

msgid "**tables**"
msgstr "**tables**"

msgid ""
"For each variable, its `kivi.woe.woe_table` result or a Series of WOE values indexed by group. "
"Tables of variables without a coefficient are ignored."
msgstr "每个变量对应其 `kivi.woe.woe_table` 结果，或以分组为索引的 WOE 值 Series。没有系数的变量的表会被忽略。"

msgid "**coefficients**"
msgstr "**coefficients**"

msgid "mapping or pandas.Series"
msgstr "mapping 或 pandas.Series"

msgid ""
"Logistic regression coefficient of each variable's WOE, for a model of the event probability. The"
" rows follow this order."
msgstr "事件概率模型中各变量 WOE 的逻辑回归系数。结果各行按此顺序排列。"

msgid "Intercept of the same model."
msgstr "同一模型的截距。"

msgid ""
"One row per variable and group, indexed by ``variable``, with the group label ``bin`` and the "
"group's ``woe`` and ``points``. Select a variable's rows with ``table.loc[[variable]]``."
msgstr ""
"每个变量的每个分组一行，以 ``variable`` 为索引，列出分组标签 ``bin`` 以及该组的 ``woe`` 和 ``points`` 。用 "
"``table.loc[[variable]]`` 选出某个变量的各行。"

msgid ""
"If `tables` is not a mapping or lacks a variable of `coefficients`, a table has no ``woe`` "
"column, repeats a group or has non-finite WOE values, the coefficients are empty, repeated or not"
" finite numbers or include the intercept, or the scaling arguments are invalid."
msgstr ""
"如果 `tables` 不是映射或缺少 `coefficients` 中的某个变量、某张表没有 ``woe`` 列、有重复分组或含有非有限的 WOE "
"值、系数为空、重复、不是有限数值或包含截距，或者刻度参数无效。"

msgid ":obj:`woe_to_points`"
msgstr ":obj:`woe_to_points`"

msgid "The points of each applicant."
msgstr "每个申请人的分值。"

msgid ":obj:`reason_codes`"
msgstr ":obj:`reason_codes`"

msgid "The variables that cost an applicant the most points."
msgstr "让申请人失分最多的变量。"

msgid "Fit the WOE of each group."
msgstr "拟合每个分组的 WOE。"

msgid ""
"With kivi's WOE, :math:`\\ln(p_i / q_i)` for event and non-event shares :math:`p_i` and "
":math:`q_i`, the model is :math:`\\ln \\frac{\\mathrm{PD}}{1 - \\mathrm{PD}} = \\beta_0 + \\sum_j"
" \\beta_j \\mathrm{WOE}_j`. A higher WOE means more risk and, for a positive coefficient, fewer "
"points. Group :math:`i` of variable :math:`j`, one of :math:`m` variables, receives"
msgstr ""
"kivi 的 WOE 为 :math:`\\ln(p_i / q_i)` ，其中 :math:`p_i` 和 :math:`q_i` 分别为事件占比和非事件占比，模型为 :math:`\\ln "
"\\frac{\\mathrm{PD}}{1 - \\mathrm{PD}} = \\beta_0 + \\sum_j \\beta_j \\mathrm{WOE}_j` 。WOE "
"越高表示风险越高；系数为正时，分值越低。共有 :math:`m` 个变量时，变量 :math:`j` 的第 :math:`i` 组得到"

msgid ""
"\\mathrm{points}_{ij} = \\frac{\\mathrm{offset} - \\mathrm{factor} \\cdot \\beta_0}{m}\n"
"- \\mathrm{factor} \\cdot \\beta_j \\, \\mathrm{WOE}_{ij},"
msgstr ""
"\\mathrm{points}_{ij} = \\frac{\\mathrm{offset} - \\mathrm{factor} \\cdot \\beta_0}{m}\n"
"- \\mathrm{factor} \\cdot \\beta_j \\, \\mathrm{WOE}_{ij},"

msgid ""
"with the factor and offset of `score_scaling`. Each variable carries the same share of the "
"intercept and offset, so the points of a variable's groups differ only by their WOE term."
msgstr "其中因子和偏移量来自 `score_scaling` 。每个变量分摊相同份额的截距和偏移量，因此同一变量各分组的分值只在 WOE 项上有差别。"

msgid ""
"The group labels stay in a column rather than an index level, so labels that compare equal across"
" variables, such as ``True`` and ``1``, keep their own values."
msgstr "分组标签放在列中而不是索引层级中，因此不同变量中比较结果相等的标签（例如 ``True`` 和 ``1`` ）仍保留各自的取值。"

msgid "[Rc133f1fff48a-1]_"
msgstr "[Rc133f1fff48a-1]_"

msgid ""
"The points are those of `points_table` for the same model and scaling. Their row sums are the "
"scores, equal to `pd_to_score` of the model's probabilities."
msgstr "对相同的模型和刻度，这些分值与 `points_table` 一致。每行之和即为分数，等于 `pd_to_score` 对模型概率给出的结果。"

msgid "**woe**"
msgstr "**woe**"

msgid "pandas.DataFrame or mapping"
msgstr "pandas.DataFrame 或 mapping"

msgid ""
"WOE values with one column per variable, such as the result of `kivi.woe.woe_transform` for each "
"variable. Columns without a coefficient are ignored. The Series of a mapping must have identical "
"indices; other values are matched by position."
msgstr "WOE 值，每个变量一列，例如对每个变量调用 `kivi.woe.woe_transform` 的结果。没有系数的列会被忽略。映射中的 Series 必须具有相同的索引；其他值按位置匹配。"

msgid ""
"Logistic regression coefficient of each variable's WOE, for a model of the event probability. The"
" columns follow this order."
msgstr "事件概率模型中各变量 WOE 的逻辑回归系数。结果各列按此顺序排列。"

msgid "Points with the index of `woe` and one column per variable."
msgstr "分值，索引与 `woe` 相同，每个变量一列。"

msgid ""
"If `woe` is not a DataFrame or mapping, lacks or repeats a variable of `coefficients`, has non-"
"finite values or is a mapping of Series with different indices, the coefficients are empty, "
"repeated, not finite or include the intercept, or the scaling arguments are invalid."
msgstr ""
"如果 `woe` 不是 DataFrame 或映射、缺少或重复 `coefficients` 中的某个变量、含有非有限值或是由索引不同的 Series "
"组成的映射、系数为空、重复、不是有限值或包含截距，或者刻度参数无效。"

msgid ":obj:`points_table`"
msgstr ":obj:`points_table`"

msgid "The points of every group."
msgstr "每个分组的分值。"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The points of variable :math:`j` are :math:`(\\mathrm{offset} - \\mathrm{factor} \\cdot \\beta_0)"
" / m - \\mathrm{factor} \\cdot \\beta_j \\, \\mathrm{WOE}_j` for :math:`m` variables, as in "
"`points_table`. They are computed in the same way, so rounding both gives the same points."
msgstr ""
"共有 :math:`m` 个变量时，变量 :math:`j` 的分值为 :math:`(\\mathrm{offset} - \\mathrm{factor} \\cdot \\beta_0) "
"/ m - \\mathrm{factor} \\cdot \\beta_j \\, \\mathrm{WOE}_j` ，与 `points_table` "
"相同。两者的计算方式完全一致，因此取整后得到相同的分值。"

msgid ""
"A variable costs an applicant the difference between the points of the variable's best group and "
"the points of the applicant's group. Variables are listed from the largest cost; those that cost "
"nothing are not listed."
msgstr "某个变量让申请人损失的分数，是该变量最佳分组的分值与申请人所在分组的分值之差。变量按损失从大到小列出；没有造成损失的变量不列出。"

msgid "**points**"
msgstr "**points**"

msgid "Points of each applicant, as returned by `woe_to_points`."
msgstr "每个申请人的分值，即 `woe_to_points` 的返回结果。"

msgid "The `points_table` result for the same model and scaling."
msgstr "相同模型和刻度下 `points_table` 的结果。"

msgid "**top**"
msgstr "**top**"

msgid "int, default 3"
msgstr "int，默认 3"

msgid "Number of reasons per applicant."
msgstr "每个申请人列出的原因个数。"

msgid "**atol**"
msgstr "**atol**"

msgid "float, default 1e-4"
msgstr "float，默认 1e-4"

msgid ""
"Largest difference, in points, between an applicant's points and the points of a group for the "
"applicant to be in that group. It absorbs rounding, for example of WOE values stored with six "
"decimals."
msgstr "申请人分值与某个分组分值之间允许的最大差值（以分计），差值不超过它时即认为申请人属于该分组。它可以吸收舍入误差，例如以六位小数存储的 WOE 值带来的误差。"

msgid "**unseen_points**"
msgstr "**unseen_points**"

msgid "float, mapping or pandas.Series, optional"
msgstr "float、mapping 或 pandas.Series，可选"

msgid ""
"Points of applicants in groups that `kivi.woe.woe_transform` encoded with ``unseen``, one value "
"for every variable or values by variable. Points that match no group but lie within `atol` of "
"their variable's `unseen_points` cost nothing, so the variable is not a reason for those "
"applicants. They are the `woe_to_points` result for the WOE passed as ``unseen``; see the "
"Examples. By default every point must match a group."
msgstr ""
"`kivi.woe.woe_transform` 用 ``unseen`` 编码的分组中申请人的分值，可以是所有变量共用的一个值，也可以按变量给出。与任何分组都不匹配、但与其变量的 "
"`unseen_points` 相差不超过 `atol` 的分值视为没有造成损失，因此该变量不会成为这些申请人的原因。这些分值就是对 ``unseen`` 所给 WOE 调用 "
"`woe_to_points` 的结果；参见示例。默认情况下，每个分值都必须匹配某个分组。"

msgid ""
"Variable names in columns ``reason_1`` to ``reason_<top>``, with the index of `points`. An "
"applicant with fewer costly variables has None in the remaining columns."
msgstr "变量名位于 ``reason_1`` 到 ``reason_<top>`` 各列，索引与 `points` 相同。造成损失的变量较少的申请人，其余各列为 None。"

msgid ""
"If `points` is not a DataFrame, repeats a column or has non-finite values, `table` is not a "
"`points_table` result, lacks a variable of `points` or has non-finite points for one, some points"
" are farther than `atol` from every group of their variable and from its `unseen_points`, `top` "
"is not a positive integer, `atol` is not a finite positive number, or `unseen_points` is not a "
"finite number or a mapping or Series of finite numbers."
msgstr ""
"如果 `points` 不是 DataFrame、有重复的列或含有非有限值、 `table` 不是 `points_table` 的结果、缺少 `points` "
"中的某个变量或该变量的分值不是有限数、某些分值与其变量的所有分组以及其 `unseen_points` 相差都超过 `atol` 、 `top` 不是正整数、 `atol` 不是有限正数，或者 "
"`unseen_points` 既不是有限数，也不是由有限数组成的映射或 Series。"

msgid ""
"Each applicant's points are matched to the nearest group of the variable in `table`, and the "
"costs are differences between the points of `table`'s groups. Costs that differ by less than "
"about `atol` count as equal, so such variables keep the order of the columns of `points`, and a "
"cost below about `atol` is no cost."
msgstr ""
"每个申请人的分值会匹配到 `table` 中该变量最接近的分组，损失分数是 `table` 中各分组分值之差。相差不到约 `atol` 的损失视为相等，因此这些变量保持 `points` "
"中的列顺序；低于约 `atol` 的损失视为没有损失。"

msgid ""
"Points that match no group, such as those from a different intercept or scaling, or WOE values "
"rounded more coarsely than `atol` allows, raise an error rather than giving reasons against the "
"wrong groups. So do, by default, the points of applicants in a group that had no development "
"observations, such as a new category, whose WOE came from ``unseen`` in `kivi.woe.woe_transform`."
" That WOE is a value chosen for the group, not evidence about the applicant, so with "
"`unseen_points` such points give no reason instead of the distance to the best group. Only points"
" near `unseen_points` are exempt; any other mismatch still raises. Points that lie within `atol` "
"of a group are matched to that group, even when their WOE came from ``unseen``."
msgstr ""
"与任何分组都不匹配的分值（例如来自不同截距或刻度的分值，或 WOE 的舍入比 `atol` "
"允许的更粗）会引发错误，而不是给出针对错误分组的原因。默认情况下，开发样本中没有观测的分组（例如新类别）里的申请人也是如此：其 WOE 来自 `kivi.woe.woe_transform` "
"中的 ``unseen`` 。这个 WOE 是为该分组选定的取值，并不是关于申请人的证据，因此给出 `unseen_points` "
"时，这些分值不产生原因，而不是按它与最佳分组的差距给出原因。只有接近 `unseen_points` 的分值才会豁免；其他任何不匹配仍会引发错误。与某个分组相差不超过 `atol` "
"的分值会匹配到该分组，即使其 WOE 来自 ``unseen`` 。"

msgid ""
"An applicant with a housing status that the development sample did not have was encoded with "
"``woe_transform(..., unseen=0.0)``. The points of a WOE of 0 are the `woe_to_points` result for a"
" row of zeros, the same base points for every variable. With these points as `unseen_points`, "
"housing is not one of the applicant's reasons:"
msgstr ""
"某个申请人的住房状况在开发样本中从未出现，因此用 ``woe_transform(..., unseen=0.0)`` 编码。WOE 为 0 时的分值，就是对一行全零调用 "
"`woe_to_points` 的结果，每个变量都是相同的基础分值。把这些分值作为 `unseen_points` 传入后，housing 不在该申请人的原因之中："

msgid "Variable selection"
msgstr "变量筛选"

msgid ""
"Select the variables of a scorecard and fit its logistic regression on WOE-encoded columns. "
":func:`~kivi.selection.correlation_filter` and :func:`~kivi.selection.vif` check the candidates "
"for collinearity, and :func:`~kivi.selection.logistic_regression` and "
":func:`~kivi.selection.stepwise` fit and select the model."
msgstr ""
"为评分卡筛选变量，并在 WOE 编码的列上拟合逻辑回归。 :func:`~kivi.selection.correlation_filter` 和 "
":func:`~kivi.selection.vif` 检查候选变量的共线性， :func:`~kivi.selection.logistic_regression` 和 "
":func:`~kivi.selection.stepwise` 拟合并筛选模型。"

msgid "See :doc:`/user_guide/selection` for a selection on the bundled data."
msgstr "基于内置数据的变量筛选见 :doc:`/user_guide/selection` 。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`correlation_filter <kivi.selection.correlation_filter>`\\ \\(X\\, \\*\\[\\, threshold\\,"
" priority\\]\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`correlation_filter <kivi.selection.correlation_filter>`\\ \\(X\\, \\*\\[\\, threshold\\,"
" priority\\]\\)"

msgid "Drop one variable of each strongly correlated pair."
msgstr "对每一对强相关的变量，剔除其中一个。"

msgid ":py:obj:`vif <kivi.selection.vif>`\\ \\(X\\)"
msgstr ":py:obj:`vif <kivi.selection.vif>`\\ \\(X\\)"

msgid "Compute the variance inflation factor of each variable."
msgstr "计算每个变量的方差膨胀因子。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`logistic_regression <kivi.selection.logistic_regression>`\\ \\(X\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, "
"weights\\]\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`logistic_regression <kivi.selection.logistic_regression>`\\ \\(X\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, "
"weights\\]\\)"

msgid "Fit a logistic regression and test each coefficient."
msgstr "拟合逻辑回归并检验每个系数。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`stepwise <kivi.selection.stepwise>`\\ \\(X\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, p\\_enter\\, "
"p\\_remove\\, ...\\]\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`stepwise <kivi.selection.stepwise>`\\ \\(X\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, p\\_enter\\, "
"p\\_remove\\, ...\\]\\)"

msgid "Select variables for a logistic regression by their p-values."
msgstr "按 p 值为逻辑回归筛选变量。"

msgid ":py:obj:`SeparationError <kivi.selection.SeparationError>`"
msgstr ":py:obj:`SeparationError <kivi.selection.SeparationError>`"

msgid "The classes are separated, so the logistic regression has no estimates."
msgstr "两类被完全分开，因此逻辑回归没有估计值。"

msgid ""
"Variables are visited from the highest `priority` to the lowest. A variable is kept unless its "
"absolute Pearson correlation with a variable that is already kept exceeds `threshold`."
msgstr "按 `priority` 从高到低依次考察各变量。若某变量与已保留的某个变量的 Pearson 相关系数绝对值超过 `threshold` ，则将其剔除，否则保留。"

msgid "**X**"
msgstr "**X**"

msgid "pandas.DataFrame or array_like"
msgstr "pandas.DataFrame 或 array_like"

msgid ""
"Two-dimensional numeric values with one column per variable, such as WOE values from "
"`kivi.woe.woe_transform`."
msgstr "二维数值，每个变量一列，例如 `kivi.woe.woe_transform` 输出的 WOE 值。"

msgid "**threshold**"
msgstr "**threshold**"

msgid "float, default 0.7"
msgstr "float，默认 0.7"

msgid "Largest absolute correlation allowed between two kept variables, between 0 and 1."
msgstr "两个保留变量之间允许的最大相关系数绝对值，取值在 0 到 1 之间。"

msgid "**priority**"
msgstr "**priority**"

msgid ""
"One number per column, such as its information value; of two correlated variables, the one with "
"the higher priority is kept. A pandas Series is matched to the columns by label, other inputs by "
"position. Ties, and every column when `priority` is omitted, follow the column order, so earlier "
"columns are kept."
msgstr ""
"每列一个数值，例如该变量的信息值；两个相关变量中保留优先级较高的一个。pandas Series 按标签与列对应，其他输入按位置对应。优先级相同时，以及省略 `priority` "
"时，按列的顺序处理，因此靠前的列被保留。"

msgid "pandas.Index"
msgstr "pandas.Index"

msgid "Labels of the kept columns, in the order of `X`. Column positions when `X` is not a DataFrame."
msgstr "保留列的标签，按 `X` 中的顺序排列。当 `X` 不是 DataFrame 时为列的位置。"

msgid ""
"If `X` is not two-dimensional, has fewer than 2 rows or no columns, repeats a column label, or "
"has a column that is not numeric, contains missing or infinite values or is constant; if "
"`threshold` is not between 0 and 1; or if `priority` does not give one number for every column."
msgstr ""
"如果 `X` 不是二维、少于 2 行或没有列、列标签重复，或者某列不是数值、含有缺失值或无穷值、或为常数；如果 `threshold` 不在 0 到 1 之间；或者 `priority` "
"没有为每一列给出一个数值。"

msgid ":obj:`vif`"
msgstr ":obj:`vif`"

msgid "Measure how well the other variables explain each variable."
msgstr "衡量每个变量能被其他变量解释的程度。"

msgid ":obj:`stepwise`"
msgstr ":obj:`stepwise`"

msgid "Select variables by their significance in a logistic regression."
msgstr "按逻辑回归中的显著性筛选变量。"

msgid ""
"A variable is dropped only because of a variable that is kept. When ``a`` is correlated with "
"``b`` and ``b`` with ``c``, but ``a`` not with ``c``, and the priorities decrease from ``a`` to "
"``c``, then ``b`` is dropped and ``c`` is kept."
msgstr ""
"变量只会因为与某个保留变量相关而被剔除。若 ``a`` 与 ``b`` 相关、 ``b`` 与 ``c`` 相关，但 ``a`` 与 ``c`` 不相关，且优先级从 ``a`` 到 ``c`` "
"递减，则 ``b`` 被剔除而 ``c`` 被保留。"

msgid ""
"The VIF of a variable measures how well the other variables explain it in a linear regression. It"
" is 1 for a variable that is uncorrelated with the others and grows without bound as the variable"
" approaches a linear combination of them."
msgstr "变量的 VIF 衡量在线性回归中其他变量对它的解释程度。与其他变量不相关的变量 VIF 为 1；变量越接近其他变量的线性组合，VIF 越大，且没有上限。"

msgid ""
"VIF of each column, indexed by the column labels of `X` (positions when `X` is not a DataFrame) "
"in an index named ``variable``, and named ``vif``. It is infinite for a column that is a linear "
"combination of the others."
msgstr ""
"每列的 VIF，以 `X` 的列标签为索引（当 `X` 不是 DataFrame 时为列的位置），索引名为 ``variable`` ，Series 名称为 ``vif`` "
"。某列是其他列的线性组合时，其 VIF 为无穷大。"

msgid ""
"If `X` is not two-dimensional, has fewer than 2 rows or no columns, repeats a column label, or "
"has a column that is not numeric, contains missing or infinite values or is constant."
msgstr "如果 `X` 不是二维、少于 2 行或没有列、列标签重复，或者某列不是数值、含有缺失值或无穷值、或为常数。"

msgid ":obj:`correlation_filter`"
msgstr ":obj:`correlation_filter`"

msgid ":obj:`logistic_regression`"
msgstr ":obj:`logistic_regression`"

msgid "Fit the scorecard model."
msgstr "拟合评分卡模型。"

msgid ""
"For column :math:`j`, let :math:`R_j^2` be the coefficient of determination of the least-squares "
"regression of column :math:`j` on an intercept and the other columns. Then"
msgstr "对第 :math:`j` 列，记 :math:`R_j^2` 为第 :math:`j` 列对截距项和其他各列做最小二乘回归的决定系数，则"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "\\mathrm{VIF}_j = \\frac{1}{1 - R_j^2}."
msgstr "\\mathrm{VIF}_j = \\frac{1}{1 - R_j^2}."

msgid ""
"The square root of the VIF is the factor by which collinearity inflates the standard error of the"
" variable's coefficient. With two columns of correlation :math:`r`, both have a VIF of :math:`1 /"
" (1 - r^2)`."
msgstr "VIF 的平方根是共线性使该变量系数的标准误放大的倍数。两列的相关系数为 :math:`r` 时，二者的 VIF 都是 :math:`1 / (1 - r^2)` 。"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"A column counts as a linear combination of the others, with an infinite VIF, when it is one up to"
" rounding: when the singular value decomposition of the standardized columns gives it a component"
" in their null space, or when its VIF reaches :math:`1 / \\epsilon \\approx 4.5 \\cdot 10^{15}`, "
"so that :math:`1 - R_j^2` is at most the machine epsilon :math:`\\epsilon`, the spacing of "
"double-precision numbers at 1. Two rows, for example, make any two columns collinear."
msgstr ""
"某列在舍入误差范围内是其他列的线性组合时，就视为线性组合，其 VIF 为无穷大：标准化各列的奇异值分解使该列在零空间中有分量，或者其 VIF 达到 :math:`1 / \\epsilon "
"\\approx 4.5 \\cdot 10^{15}` ，使 :math:`1 - R_j^2` 不超过机器精度 :math:`\\epsilon` ，即双精度数在 1 "
"附近的间距。例如，只有两行时任意两列都共线。"

msgid "Two columns with a correlation of 0.9 both have a VIF of :math:`1 / (1 - 0.9^2) = 5.263`:"
msgstr "相关系数为 0.9 的两列，VIF 都是 :math:`1 / (1 - 0.9^2) = 5.263` ："

msgid "Adding their sum makes every column a linear combination of the others:"
msgstr "加入二者之和后，每一列都是其他列的线性组合："

msgid ""
"The model has an intercept and one coefficient per column of `X`. The coefficients are maximum "
"likelihood estimates, and each is tested against zero with a Wald test."
msgstr "模型包含截距项，并为 `X` 的每一列估计一个系数。系数为最大似然估计，并用 Wald 检验逐一检验其是否为零。"

msgid ""
"Binary labels, with 1 indicating the event. If `X` is a DataFrame and `target` a Series, they "
"must have identical indices; otherwise they are matched by position."
msgstr "二分类标签，1 表示事件。如果 `X` 是 DataFrame 且 `target` 是 Series，二者的索引必须完全相同；否则按位置对应。"

msgid ""
"Non-negative frequency weight of each row, matched like `target`: a row with weight 2 counts as "
"two identical observations, so integer weights give the same estimates, standard errors and log-"
"likelihood as repeating rows. Rows with zero weight are left out of the fit. See the Notes on "
"weights that do not count observations."
msgstr ""
"每一行的非负频数权重，对应方式与 `target` 相同：权重为 2 "
"的行计为两个相同的观测，因此整数权重与重复行得到相同的估计值、标准误和对数似然。权重为零的行不参与拟合。关于不表示观测个数的权重见“说明”。"

msgid ""
"One row for the intercept, labelled ``intercept``, and one for each column of `X`, with the "
"coefficient, its standard error, the Wald z statistic and its two-sided p-value, in an index "
"named ``variable``. ``attrs[\"log_likelihood\"]`` holds the maximized log-likelihood and "
"``attrs[\"converged\"]`` whether the fit converged."
msgstr ""
"截距项一行（标签为 ``intercept`` ）， `X` 的每一列各一行，包含系数、标准误、Wald z 统计量及其双侧 p 值，索引名为 ``variable`` 。 "
"``attrs[\"log_likelihood\"]`` 保存最大化后的对数似然， ``attrs[\"converged\"]`` 表示拟合是否收敛。"

msgid "SeparationError"
msgstr "SeparationError"

msgid "If the columns separate the classes, so that the estimates do not exist."
msgstr "如果各列把两类完全分开，以致估计值不存在。"

msgid ""
"If `X` is not two-dimensional, has fewer than 2 rows or no columns, repeats a column label, has a"
" column labelled ``intercept``, or has a column that is not numeric, contains missing or infinite"
" values, is constant or is a linear combination of the intercept and the columns before it, or so"
" close to one that its coefficient cannot be estimated; if `target` is not one-dimensional, its "
"index or length does not match `X`, or it does not contain both 0 and 1 or has missing or other "
"labels; or if `weights` is not numeric, does not give each row one finite, non-negative weight, "
"or leaves a class without weight. With `weights`, only the checks for constant columns and linear"
" combinations are limited to the rows with positive weight."
msgstr ""
"如果 `X` 不是二维、少于 2 行或没有列、列标签重复、有标签为 ``intercept`` "
"的列，或者某列不是数值、含有缺失值或无穷值、为常数、是截距项与前面各列的线性组合或与之过于接近以致无法估计其系数；如果 `target` 不是一维、索引或长度与 `X` 不一致，或者没有同时包含"
" 0 和 1 或含有缺失值及其他标签；或者 `weights` 不是数值、没有给每一行一个有限的非负权重，或者使某一类别没有权重。给定 `weights` "
"时，只有常数列和线性组合的检查仅针对权重为正的行。"

msgid "If the fit does not converge for a reason other than separation."
msgstr "如果拟合因分离以外的原因未能收敛。"

msgid "Select the columns of the model by their p-values."
msgstr "按 p 值筛选模型的列。"

msgid "Check the columns for collinearity."
msgstr "检查各列的共线性。"

msgid "Encode groups with their WOE."
msgstr "用 WOE 对分组编码。"

msgid "The model is"
msgstr "模型为"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "\\ln \\frac{P(y = 1)}{P(y = 0)} = \\beta_0 + \\sum_j \\beta_j x_j."
msgstr "\\ln \\frac{P(y = 1)}{P(y = 0)} = \\beta_0 + \\sum_j \\beta_j x_j."

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The estimates are found by Newton-Raphson, also known as iteratively reweighted least squares, on"
" centred and scaled columns, so that an offset or the unit of a column does not affect their "
"accuracy. The standard errors are the square roots of the diagonal of the inverse Fisher "
"information, :math:`z = \\hat\\beta / \\mathrm{se}`, and the p-value is :math:`P(|Z| > |z|)` for "
"a standard normal :math:`Z`."
msgstr ""
"估计值在中心化并标准化后的列上用牛顿-拉弗森法（也称迭代重加权最小二乘法）求得，因此列的偏移量或单位不会影响其精度。标准误是 Fisher 信息矩阵之逆的对角线元素的平方根， :math:`z "
"= \\hat\\beta / \\mathrm{se}` ，p 值为 :math:`P(|Z| > |z|)` ，其中 :math:`Z` 服从标准正态分布。"

msgid "With WOE-encoded variables, the coefficients are expected to be positive: see `stepwise`."
msgstr "对 WOE 编码的变量，系数应为正，参见 `stepwise` 。"

msgid ""
"With `weights` :math:`w_i`, the estimates maximize the weighted log-likelihood :math:`\\sum_i w_i"
" [y_i \\ln p_i + (1 - y_i) \\ln(1 - p_i)]`, and the standard errors come from the weighted Fisher"
" information :math:`\\sum_i w_i p_i (1 - p_i) x_i x_i^\\top`. These are frequency weights, as in "
"statsmodels' ``GLM(freq_weights=...)``: the total weight counts as the number of independent "
"observations, so multiplying every weight by :math:`c` divides the variances by :math:`c`. "
"Integer weights that count repeated rows therefore give the standard errors of the repeated rows."
" Weights that do not count observations do not: those of "
"`kivi.reject_inference.fuzzy_augmentation`, which split each rejected applicant into a bad and a "
"good row, and those of `kivi.reject_inference.reweighting`, which let each accepted applicant "
"stand for several, make the standard errors too small and the p-values too low. The inferred rows"
" and the extra weight count as observations, although they add no observed outcomes."
msgstr ""
"给定权重 `weights` :math:`w_i` 时，估计值最大化加权对数似然 :math:`\\sum_i w_i [y_i \\ln p_i + (1 - y_i) \\ln(1 - "
"p_i)]` ，标准误来自加权的 Fisher 信息 :math:`\\sum_i w_i p_i (1 - p_i) x_i x_i^\\top` 。这是频数权重，与 statsmodels "
"的 ``GLM(freq_weights=...)`` 相同：总权重被当作独立观测的个数，因此把每个权重乘以 :math:`c` 会使方差除以 :math:`c` "
"。表示重复行数的整数权重因而给出重复行的标准误。不表示观测个数的权重则不然： `kivi.reject_inference.fuzzy_augmentation` "
"把每个拒绝申请人拆成一行坏样本和一行好样本时的权重，以及 `kivi.reject_inference.reweighting` 让每个获批申请人代表多个申请人时的权重，都会使标准误偏小、p "
"值偏低。推断出的行和额外的权重被计为观测，尽管它们没有增加任何观测到的结果。"

msgid "[R238aee73b2df-1]_"
msgstr "[R238aee73b2df-1]_"

msgid ""
"With a single binary variable, the coefficient is the log odds ratio: the odds of the event are "
"1:3 at ``x = 0`` and 3:1 at ``x = 1``, so the coefficient is :math:`\\ln 9` and the intercept "
":math:`\\ln(1/3)`."
msgstr ""
"只有一个二值变量时，系数就是对数优势比：事件的优势在 ``x = 0`` 时为 1:3，在 ``x = 1`` 时为 3:1，因此系数为 :math:`\\ln 9` ，截距为 "
":math:`\\ln(1/3)` 。"

msgid ""
"Integer weights count repeated rows, so the four distinct rows with their counts give the same "
"fit:"
msgstr "整数权重表示重复的行数，因此四个不同的行加上各自的次数会得到相同的拟合结果："

msgid ""
"Forward selection starts from the intercept and adds, one at a time, the variable with the "
"smallest p-value while that p-value is below `p_enter`. Backward elimination starts from all "
"variables and removes, one at a time, the variable with the largest p-value while that p-value is"
" above `p_remove`. Selection in both directions adds variables like forward selection, but after "
"each addition removes the variables that no longer meet `p_remove`."
msgstr ""
"向前选择从只含截距的模型开始，每次加入 p 值最小的变量，直到最小的 p 值不再低于 `p_enter` 。向后剔除从包含全部变量的模型开始，每次移除 p 值最大的变量，直到最大的 p "
"值不再高于 `p_remove` 。双向逐步选择像向前选择一样加入变量，但每加入一个变量后，都会移除不再满足 `p_remove` 的变量。"

msgid ""
"Two-dimensional numeric values with one column per candidate variable, such as WOE values from "
"`kivi.woe.woe_transform`."
msgstr "二维数值，每个候选变量一列，例如 `kivi.woe.woe_transform` 输出的 WOE 值。"

msgid "**p_enter**"
msgstr "**p_enter**"

msgid ""
"A variable enters only if its p-value in the extended model is below this level, which is greater"
" than 0 and at most 1."
msgstr "只有当变量在扩展后模型中的 p 值低于该水平时才会入选；该水平大于 0 且不超过 1。"

msgid "**p_remove**"
msgstr "**p_remove**"

msgid "float, default 0.10"
msgstr "float，默认 0.10"

msgid ""
"A variable is removed if its p-value is above this level, which is greater than 0 and at most 1 "
"and, in both directions, not below `p_enter`."
msgstr "变量的 p 值高于该水平时被移除；该水平大于 0 且不超过 1，双向选择时不得低于 `p_enter` 。"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "{\"both\", \"forward\", \"backward\"}, default \"both\""
msgstr "{\"both\", \"forward\", \"backward\"}，默认 \"both\""

msgid "Whether variables are added and removed, only added, or only removed."
msgstr "既加入也移除变量、只加入变量，还是只移除变量。"

msgid "**positive**"
msgstr "**positive**"

msgid ""
"Keep every coefficient of the selected model positive. A variable enters only if all coefficients"
" of the extended model are positive, and a variable whose coefficient is not positive is removed "
"before any other, starting with the smallest z statistic."
msgstr "使所选模型的每个系数都为正。只有扩展后模型的所有系数都为正时变量才会入选；系数不为正的变量优先于其他变量被移除，z 统计量最小的最先移除。"

msgid ""
"Non-negative frequency weight of each row, as in `logistic_regression`. Integer weights select "
"the same variables as repeating rows. The p-values depend on the scale of the weights as they do "
"on the sample size. The weights of reject inference make them too low, so that more variables "
"enter than the observed outcomes support; select the variables on the accepted applicants "
"instead."
msgstr ""
"每一行的非负频数权重，与 `logistic_regression` 相同。整数权重与重复行选出相同的变量。p 值取决于权重的尺度，正如取决于样本量。拒绝推断的权重会使 p "
"值偏低，从而选入超出观测结果所能支持的变量；应改为在获批申请人上选择变量。"

msgid "Labels of the selected columns, in the order of `X`. Column positions when `X` is not a DataFrame."
msgstr "入选列的标签，按 `X` 中的顺序排列。当 `X` 不是 DataFrame 时为列的位置。"

msgid "If `direction` is ``\"backward\"`` and the model with every column separates the classes."
msgstr "如果 `direction` 为 ``\"backward\"`` ，且包含全部列的模型把两类完全分开。"

msgid ""
"If `X`, `target` or `weights` is invalid as described for `logistic_regression`, in every "
"direction; if `p_enter` or `p_remove` is not greater than 0 and at most 1, or `p_enter` exceeds "
"`p_remove` when `direction` is ``\"both\"``; or if `direction` is not one of the three options or"
" `positive` is not a boolean."
msgstr ""
"如果 `X` 、 `target` 或 `weights` 不符合 `logistic_regression` 中所述的要求（任何方向都会检查）；如果 `p_enter` 或 "
"`p_remove` 不是大于 0 且不超过 1 的数，或 `direction` 为 ``\"both\"`` 时 `p_enter` 超过 `p_remove` ；或者 "
"`direction` 不是三个选项之一，或 `positive` 不是布尔值。"

msgid "If the model of the selected variables does not converge for a reason other than separation."
msgstr "如果所选变量的模型因分离以外的原因未能收敛。"

msgid "Fit the selected model and read its coefficients."
msgstr "拟合所选模型并查看其系数。"

msgid "Drop strongly correlated variables first."
msgstr "先剔除强相关的变量。"

msgid ""
"The p-values are those of the Wald tests reported by `logistic_regression`. Each candidate is "
"tested in the model made of the selected variables and the candidate, so every step refits one "
"model per candidate. A candidate does not enter if that model would separate the classes, does "
"not converge or is numerically singular. In both directions, a variable cannot enter if that "
"would recreate a set of variables that was selected before, which guarantees that the selection "
"stops."
msgstr ""
"p 值即 `logistic_regression` 报告的 Wald 检验 p "
"值。每个候选变量都在由已选变量和该候选变量组成的模型中检验，因此每一步都要为每个候选变量重新拟合一个模型。如果这个模型会使两类完全分开、无法收敛或在数值上奇异，候选变量就不会入选。双向选择时，如果加入某个变量会重现之前选过的变量组合，该变量不能入选，这保证了筛选过程一定会终止。"

msgid ""
"kivi defines the WOE of a group as the log of its share of events over its share of non-events, "
"so a higher WOE means a higher event rate. In a logistic regression of `target` on a single WOE-"
"encoded variable, the coefficient is therefore positive; it is exactly 1 when no cell needed "
"smoothing. A negative coefficient in a model with several variables means that the variable's "
"effect is reversed by the others, usually because of collinearity, and makes the scorecard points"
" of its bins contradict their event rates. ``positive=True`` rules out such models."
msgstr ""
"kivi 将分组的 WOE 定义为其事件占比与非事件占比之比的对数，因此 WOE 越高，事件率越高。所以在 `target` 对单个 WOE "
"编码变量的逻辑回归中，系数为正；没有单元格需要平滑时，系数恰好为 1。在多变量模型中，负系数表示该变量的作用被其他变量反转（通常源于共线性），会使其各箱的评分卡分数与事件率相矛盾。 "
"``positive=True`` 会排除这样的模型。"

msgid "[R44bd75d8258f-1]_, [R44bd75d8258f-2]_"
msgstr "[R44bd75d8258f-1]_, [R44bd75d8258f-2]_"

msgid ""
"A combination of the variables predicts the target without error, for every observation (complete"
" separation) or for every observation off a boundary (quasi-complete separation). The likelihood "
"then keeps growing as the coefficients grow, so the maximum likelihood estimates do not exist."
msgstr "变量的某个组合能无误地预测目标变量：对所有观测都成立（完全分离），或对边界以外的所有观测成立（准完全分离）。此时似然随系数增大而不断增大，因此最大似然估计不存在。"

msgid "Raises this error."
msgstr "会抛出此错误。"

msgid "Leaves out candidates that separate the classes."
msgstr "不选入会把两类完全分开的候选变量。"

msgid "Binning specifications"
msgstr "分箱方案"

msgid ""
"Bin and encode every column of a data frame in one step. :func:`~kivi.spec.fit_spec` fits the "
"binning and the WOE of each column, and the resulting :class:`~kivi.spec.BinningSpec` groups and "
"encodes any other sample in the same way and saves itself as versioned JSON."
msgstr ""
"一步完成数据框所有列的分箱和编码。 :func:`~kivi.spec.fit_spec` 拟合每一列的分箱和 WOE，得到的 :class:`~kivi.spec.BinningSpec` "
"以同样的方式对其他任何样本分组和编码，并能保存为带版本号的 JSON。"

msgid "See :doc:`/user_guide/spec` for examples and the file format."
msgstr "示例和文件格式见 :doc:`/user_guide/spec` 。"

msgid ":py:obj:`fit_spec <kivi.spec.fit_spec>`\\ \\(frame\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, columns\\, ...\\]\\)"
msgstr ":py:obj:`fit_spec <kivi.spec.fit_spec>`\\ \\(frame\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, columns\\, ...\\]\\)"

msgid "Fit the binning and WOE of every column of a development sample."
msgstr "在开发样本上拟合每一列的分箱和 WOE。"

msgid ":py:obj:`BinningSpec <kivi.spec.BinningSpec>`\\ \\(kinds\\, edges\\, special\\, tables\\, ...\\)"
msgstr ":py:obj:`BinningSpec <kivi.spec.BinningSpec>`\\ \\(kinds\\, edges\\, special\\, tables\\, ...\\)"

msgid "Binning and WOE encoding of every column, fitted on a development sample."
msgstr "在开发样本上拟合的、每一列的分箱和 WOE 编码。"

msgid ""
"Numeric columns are binned with the method chosen for them and grouped with `kivi.binning.cut`. "
"Categorical columns that `method` names are grouped with `kivi.binning.category_groups` or "
"`kivi.binning.chimerge_groups` and `kivi.binning.group_categories`; the other categorical columns"
" keep their labels as groups. The WOE of each group is then measured with `kivi.woe.woe_table`. "
"Nothing is re-binned automatically: the method, the number of bins and the options of each column"
" decide how coarse its bins are."
msgstr ""
"数值列按为其选定的方法分箱，并用 `kivi.binning.cut` 分组。 `method` 中指定的类别列用 `kivi.binning.category_groups` 或 "
"`kivi.binning.chimerge_groups` 以及 `kivi.binning.group_categories` 分组；其他类别列以自身标签作为分组。然后用 "
"`kivi.woe.woe_table` 计算每个分组的 WOE。不会自动重新分箱：每一列分箱的粗细由其方法、箱数和选项决定。"

msgid "**frame**"
msgstr "**frame**"

msgid ""
"Development sample with one column per variable. Columns with a numeric dtype other than bool and"
" complex are binned, and complex columns are rejected. Columns of any other dtype, such as "
"object, string, category or bool, are categorical: each label is a group unless `method` groups "
"the column. Convert integer codes to the category dtype to keep them as labels."
msgstr ""
"开发样本，每个变量一列。数值 dtype（bool 和复数除外）的列会被分箱，复数列会引发错误。其他 dtype 的列（例如 object、string、category 或 "
"bool）是类别列：除非 `method` 对该列分组，否则每个标签是一个分组。若要把整数编码当作标签，请先将其转换为 category dtype。"

msgid ""
"Binary labels, with 1 indicating the event, one per row of `frame`. A Series must have the same "
"index as `frame`; other inputs are matched by position."
msgstr "二分类标签，1 表示事件， `frame` 的每一行一个。Series 必须与 `frame` 的索引相同；其他输入按位置对应。"

msgid "**columns**"
msgstr "**columns**"

msgid "sequence of str, optional"
msgstr "str 序列，可选"

msgid "Columns to fit, in the order of the specification. By default every column of `frame`."
msgstr "要拟合的列，其顺序即分箱方案中的顺序。默认为 `frame` 的所有列。"

msgid "str or dict, default \"quantile\""
msgstr "str 或 dict，默认 \"quantile\""

msgid ""
"Binning method of the numeric columns: ``\"quantile\"`` or ``\"uniform\"`` for "
"`kivi.binning.bin_edges`, or ``\"chimerge\"``, ``\"tree\"`` or ``\"monotonic\"`` for "
"`kivi.binning.chimerge_edges`, `kivi.binning.tree_edges` or `kivi.binning.monotonic_edges`. A "
"dict maps columns to methods, and the numeric columns it leaves out use ``\"quantile\"``. A "
"method applies only to the columns without edges in `bins`, so a dict must not name a column "
"whose edges `bins` gives. A dict can also group categorical columns, with ``\"rare\"`` for "
"`kivi.binning.category_groups` or ``\"chimerge\"`` for `kivi.binning.chimerge_groups`; the "
"categorical columns it leaves out keep their labels."
msgstr ""
"数值列的分箱方法： ``\"quantile\"`` 或 ``\"uniform\"`` 对应 `kivi.binning.bin_edges` ， ``\"chimerge\"`` 、 "
"``\"tree\"`` 或 ``\"monotonic\"`` 分别对应 `kivi.binning.chimerge_edges` 、 `kivi.binning.tree_edges` 和"
" `kivi.binning.monotonic_edges` 。dict 把列映射到方法，dict 中未列出的数值列使用 ``\"quantile\"`` 。方法只作用于 `bins` "
"中没有给出边界的列，因此 dict 不能列出边界由 `bins` 给出的列。dict 也可以对类别列分组： ``\"rare\"`` 对应 "
"`kivi.binning.category_groups` ， ``\"chimerge\"`` 对应 `kivi.binning.chimerge_groups` ；dict "
"中未列出的类别列保留其标签。"

msgid "int or dict, default 5"
msgstr "int 或 dict，默认 5"

msgid ""
"Number of bins, passed as ``bins`` to `kivi.binning.bin_edges`, as ``max_bins`` to the supervised"
" methods and as ``max_groups`` to `kivi.binning.chimerge_groups`. A dict maps columns to a number"
" of bins or to edges, which must increase from ``-inf`` to ``inf`` and are used as given. With "
"``\"monotonic\"``, None merges bins only until the WOE is monotonic. The numeric and "
"``\"chimerge\"`` columns that a dict leaves out get 5 bins. Columns grouped with ``\"rare\"`` "
"take no number of bins."
msgstr ""
"箱数，作为 ``bins`` 传给 `kivi.binning.bin_edges` ，作为 ``max_bins`` 传给有监督方法，作为 ``max_groups`` 传给 "
"`kivi.binning.chimerge_groups` 。dict 把列映射到箱数或边界；边界必须从 ``-inf`` 递增到 ``inf`` ，并按原样使用。对 "
"``\"monotonic\"`` ，None 表示只合并到 WOE 单调为止。dict 中未列出的数值列和 ``\"chimerge\"`` 列分为 5 箱。用 ``\"rare\"`` "
"分组的列不接受箱数。"

msgid "dict, optional"
msgstr "dict，可选"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Special codes of numeric and grouped categorical columns, such as ``{\"pdays\": [-1], \"job\": "
"[\"unknown\"]}``. The codes of a numeric column must be numbers, possibly infinite; those of a "
"categorical column are labels. They are left out of the fit, and each code forms its own group."
msgstr ""
"数值列和已分组类别列的特殊值编码，例如 ``{\"pdays\": [-1], \"job\": [\"unknown\"]}`` "
"。数值列的编码必须是数值，可以是无穷；类别列的编码是标签。拟合时排除这些编码，每个编码单独成组。"

msgid "**options**"
msgstr "**options**"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Further keyword arguments for the binning or grouping function of each column, such as "
"``{\"balance\": {\"alpha\": None}}`` with ``\"chimerge\"`` or ``{\"job\": {\"min_share\": "
"0.02}}`` with ``\"rare\"``. The special codes, the weights, the number of bins and, for "
"``\"monotonic\"`` and the grouping with ``\"chimerge\"``, the smoothing are passed by `fit_spec` "
"and cannot be given here."
msgstr ""
"传给每一列分箱或分组函数的其他关键字参数，例如配合 ``\"chimerge\"`` 使用的 ``{\"balance\": {\"alpha\": None}}`` ，或配合 "
"``\"rare\"`` 使用的 ``{\"job\": {\"min_share\": 0.02}}`` 。特殊值、权重、箱数，以及 ``\"monotonic\"`` 和用 "
"``\"chimerge\"`` 分组时的平滑参数，由 `fit_spec` 传入，不能在这里指定。"

msgid "float, \"raise\" or dict, default \"raise\""
msgstr "float、\"raise\" 或 dict，默认 \"raise\""

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"WOE for values whose group is not in a column's table when a sample is encoded: a new category, a"
" special code or an interval without development observations, or missing values when development"
" had none. By default such values raise an error. A dict maps columns to a WOE or ``\"raise\"``, "
"and the columns it leaves out raise. For a grouped column, ``{\"group\": label}`` gives such "
"values the WOE of that group instead, and `BinningSpec.cut` assigns new categories to it; the "
"group must be in the fitted table. A dict is always read by column, so give ``{\"group\": "
"label}`` for each grouped column, as in ``{\"job\": {\"group\": \"other\"}}``."
msgstr ""
"编码样本时，分组不在该列 WOE 表中的取值所用的 WOE：新类别、开发样本中没有观测值的特殊值或区间，或开发样本没有缺失值时的缺失值。默认情况下，这类取值会引发错误。dict 把列映射到 "
"WOE 或 ``\"raise\"`` ，dict 中未列出的列会引发错误。对已分组的列， ``{\"group\": label}`` 让这类取值改用该组的 WOE，并且 "
"`BinningSpec.cut` 会把新类别分配到该组；该组必须在拟合得到的 WOE 表中。dict 总是按列读取，因此请为每个已分组的列分别给出 ``{\"group\": label}``"
" ，例如 ``{\"job\": {\"group\": \"other\"}}`` 。"

msgid ""
"Positive replacement for a zero count when calculating the WOE, as in `kivi.woe.woe_table`. "
"``\"monotonic\"`` binning uses the same value, so its trend holds in the tables."
msgstr "计算 WOE 时用这个正数替代零计数，含义与 `kivi.woe.woe_table` 相同。 ``\"monotonic\"`` 分箱使用同一取值，因此其单调趋势在 WOE 表中同样成立。"

msgid ""
"Non-negative weight of each row, matched like `target`, for the binning functions and "
"`kivi.woe.woe_table`. Counts are then sums of weights, and `smoothing` is in units of weight."
msgstr "每一行的非负权重，对应方式与 `target` 相同，会传给分箱函数和 `kivi.woe.woe_table` 。此时计数为权重之和， `smoothing` 也以权重为单位。"

msgid "BinningSpec"
msgstr "BinningSpec"

msgid "The kind, edges, special codes, grouping, WOE table and unseen policy of every column."
msgstr "每一列的类型、边界、特殊值、分组映射、WOE 表和未见分组策略。"

msgid ""
"If `frame` is not a DataFrame or has no columns to fit, `columns` repeats a column or names one "
"that `frame` lacks, a column name is not a string, a column has a complex dtype, the columns "
"include the target, or `target` does not give each row a label 0 or 1 or lacks one of the two "
"classes. If a dict names a column that is not fitted, `method` gives a categorical column a "
"method other than ``\"chimerge\"`` or ``\"rare\"``, `bins`, `special` or `options` names a "
"categorical column that `method` does not group, or a value is invalid, such as a special code of"
" a numeric column that is not a number. Also if `smoothing` or `weights` are invalid, a numeric "
"column has infinite values that are not special codes, or the binning or grouping of a column "
"fails; the message then names the column."
msgstr ""
"如果 `frame` 不是 DataFrame 或没有可拟合的列， `columns` 重复某一列或指定了 `frame` 中没有的列，列名不是字符串，某一列的 dtype "
"为复数，拟合的列包含目标变量，或 `target` 的标签不是每行一个 0 或 1，或者缺少两类中的一类。如果某个 dict 指定了未拟合的列， `method` 为类别列指定了 "
"``\"chimerge\"`` 或 ``\"rare\"`` 以外的方法， `bins` 、 `special` 或 `options` 指定了 `method` "
"未分组的类别列，或某个取值无效，例如数值列的特殊值编码不是数值。此外，如果 `smoothing` 或 `weights` "
"无效，某个数值列含有不属于特殊值的无穷值，或某一列分箱或分组失败；此时错误信息会指明该列。"

msgid ""
"If tied quantiles leave a column with fewer bins than requested, as in `kivi.binning.bin_edges`, "
"if a numeric column has no values to fit apart from missing, special and zero-weight values, so "
"that its edges are ``[-inf, inf]``, if a grouped column has no such values, so that its groups "
"are its special codes, or if a column of dtype object holds only numbers, which makes each "
"distinct number a group. The message names the column."
msgstr ""
"如果重合的分位数使某一列的箱数少于期望值（与 `kivi.binning.bin_edges` 相同），某个数值列除缺失值、特殊值和零权重的取值外没有可拟合的值，从而其边界为 ``[-inf, "
"inf]`` ，某个已分组的列没有这样的值，从而其分组只有特殊值，或者某个 object dtype 的列只含数值，使每个不同的数值各成一组。警告信息会指明该列。"

msgid ":obj:`BinningSpec`"
msgstr ":obj:`BinningSpec`"

msgid "Group, encode and save the fitted columns."
msgstr "对拟合好的列分组、编码并保存。"

msgid "Fit the edges of one column."
msgstr "拟合单列的边界。"

msgid ":obj:`kivi.binning.chimerge_groups`"
msgstr ":obj:`kivi.binning.chimerge_groups`"

msgid "Group the categories of one column."
msgstr "对单列的类别分组。"

msgid "The WOE table of one column."
msgstr "单列的 WOE 表。"

msgid ""
"Each column is fitted on its own with the public functions, so a column of the specification has "
"the same edges and table as the steps of :doc:`/user_guide/binning` and :doc:`/user_guide/woe_iv`"
" applied to it alone."
msgstr ""
"每一列都用公开函数单独拟合，因此分箱方案中某一列的边界和 WOE 表，与单独对该列执行 :doc:`/user_guide/binning` 和 "
":doc:`/user_guide/woe_iv` 中的步骤所得的结果相同。"

msgid ""
"For each column, a specification records whether it is numeric or categorical, the edges and "
"special codes of a numeric column, the grouping of a grouped categorical column, the WOE table of"
" its groups and the policy for groups that are not in the table. `cut` groups any sample with the"
" same edges and groupings, `woe_transform` encodes it with the same WOE, and `to_json` and "
"`from_json` save and load the specification without changing its groups or its encoding. Fit a "
"specification with `fit_spec` rather than calling the constructor."
msgstr ""
"对每一列，分箱方案记录：它是数值列还是类别列、数值列的边界和特殊值、已分组类别列的分组映射、其各分组的 WOE 表，以及不在表中的分组的处理策略。 `cut` "
"用同样的边界和分组映射对任意样本分组， `woe_transform` 用同样的 WOE 编码， `to_json` 和 `from_json` 保存并加载分箱方案，且不会改变分组和编码。请用 "
"`fit_spec` 拟合分箱方案，而不是直接调用构造函数。"

msgid ""
"A specification is immutable. Its mappings are read-only, and ``edges``, ``groups`` and "
"``tables`` return a new copy of an array, a dict or a table on each access, so changing the copy "
"leaves the specification as it was. To change a field, such as the unseen policy, use "
"`dataclasses.replace`, which validates the result again."
msgstr ""
"分箱方案不可变。其映射是只读的， ``edges`` 、 ``groups`` 和 ``tables`` 每次访问都返回数组、dict "
"或表的新副本，因此修改副本不会影响分箱方案。若要修改某个字段（例如未见分组策略），请使用 `dataclasses.replace` ，它会重新校验结果。"

msgid "**kinds**"
msgstr "**kinds**"

msgid "``\"numeric\"`` or ``\"categorical\"`` for each column, in the order of the specification."
msgstr "每一列为 ``\"numeric\"`` 或 ``\"categorical\"`` ，顺序即分箱方案中的顺序。"

msgid "Edges of each numeric column, increasing from ``-inf`` to ``inf``."
msgstr "每个数值列的边界，从 ``-inf`` 递增到 ``inf`` 。"

msgid ""
"Special codes of each numeric column, possibly none. The codes are numbers, and each forms its "
"own group, as in `kivi.binning.cut`."
msgstr "每个数值列的特殊值，可以为空。这些编码是数值，与 `kivi.binning.cut` 相同，每个编码单独成组。"

msgid ""
"The `kivi.woe.woe_table` result of each column. The groups of a numeric column are its special "
"codes and the intervals of its edges, labelled as `kivi.binning.cut` labels them or by the exact "
"edges, and those of a grouped column the groups of its grouping. Missing values form a group "
"labelled NaN. The tables keep the labels of `kivi.binning.cut`."
msgstr ""
"每一列的 `kivi.woe.woe_table` 结果。数值列的分组是其特殊值和由边界构成的区间，区间可以使用 `kivi.binning.cut` "
"给出的标签，也可以用精确的边界表示；已分组列的分组是其分组映射中的各组。缺失值单独成组，标签为 NaN。保存的表使用 `kivi.binning.cut` 的标签。"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"``\"raise\"`` or a finite WOE for each column, used for values whose group is not in the column's"
" table. A grouped column can instead name one of its groups as ``{\"group\": label}``: such "
"values then get that group's WOE, and `cut` assigns the categories that its grouping does not map"
" to that group."
msgstr ""
"每列的 ``\"raise\"`` 或有限的 WOE，用于分组不在该列 WOE 表中的取值。已分组的列也可以用 ``{\"group\": label}`` 指定其中一个组：这类取值改用该组的 "
"WOE，并且 `cut` 会把分组映射中没有的类别分配到该组。"

msgid "Smoothing with which the tables were computed."
msgstr "计算 WOE 表时所用的平滑参数。"

msgid "**kivi_version**"
msgstr "**kivi_version**"

msgid "Version of kivi that fitted the specification. By default, or if None, the installed version."
msgstr "拟合该分箱方案的 kivi 版本。默认或为 None 时取已安装的版本。"

msgid "mapping, optional"
msgstr "mapping，可选"

msgid ""
"Grouping of each grouped categorical column: a dict from category to group, as returned by "
"`kivi.binning.category_groups` or `kivi.binning.chimerge_groups`. Categorical columns without an "
"entry keep their labels as groups. By default no column is grouped."
msgstr ""
"每个已分组类别列的分组映射：从类别到组的 dict，与 `kivi.binning.category_groups` 或 `kivi.binning.chimerge_groups` "
"的返回值相同。没有对应项的类别列以自身标签作为分组。默认不对任何列分组。"

msgid "Attributes"
msgstr "属性"

msgid "**FORMAT_VERSION**"
msgstr "**FORMAT_VERSION**"

msgid "int"
msgstr "int"

msgid ""
"Newest version of the JSON format, which `from_json` reads and `to_json` writes for a "
"specification with grouped columns."
msgstr "JSON 格式的最新版本， `from_json` 能读取该版本，含已分组列的分箱方案由 `to_json` 按该版本写出。"

msgid ""
"If `kinds` is empty or has a name that is not a string or a kind other than the two above, if "
"`edges` and `special` do not have one entry per numeric column, `groups` has an entry for a "
"column that is not categorical, or `tables` and `unseen` do not have one entry per column, or if "
"an entry is invalid: edges that do not increase from ``-inf`` to ``inf``, a missing or "
"unsupported special code, a grouping with a missing or unsupported category or group, a table "
"without a finite ``woe`` column or with a repeated group, a group of a numeric column that is "
"neither one of its special codes nor an interval of its edges, a group of a grouped column that "
"its grouping lacks, or an unseen policy that is neither ``\"raise\"`` nor a finite number nor, "
"for a grouped column, a group of its table. Also if `smoothing` is not finite and positive or "
"`kivi_version` is not a string."
msgstr ""
"如果 `kinds` 为空、含有非字符串的列名或上述两种以外的类型；如果 `edges` 和 `special` 不是每个数值列恰好一项， `groups` 含有非类别列的项，或 "
"`tables` 和 `unseen` 不是每列恰好一项；或某一项无效：边界没有从 ``-inf`` 递增到 ``inf`` "
"、特殊值缺失或类型不受支持、分组映射含有缺失或类型不受支持的类别或组、WOE 表没有有限的 ``woe`` "
"列或有重复分组、数值列的某个分组既不是其特殊值也不是其边界构成的区间、已分组列的某个分组不在其分组映射中，或未见分组策略既不是 ``\"raise\"`` 也不是有限数值，对已分组的列也不是其 "
"WOE 表中的组。此外，如果 `smoothing` 不是有限正数，或 `kivi_version` 不是字符串。"

msgid ":obj:`fit_spec`"
msgstr ":obj:`fit_spec`"

msgid "Fit a specification on a development sample."
msgstr "在开发样本上拟合分箱方案。"

msgid ":obj:`kivi.binning.cut`"
msgstr ":obj:`kivi.binning.cut`"

msgid "Group one numeric column."
msgstr "对单个数值列分组。"

msgid "Encode one column with its WOE table."
msgstr "用单列的 WOE 表对该列编码。"

msgid ""
"Labels of categorical columns must be strings, integers, floats, booleans or intervals, which the"
" JSON format keeps apart. Within a column, labels that compare equal, such as ``True`` and ``1``,"
" form one group, because `kivi.woe.woe_table` and `kivi.woe.woe_transform` match labels by "
"equality. The same holds for the categories and groups of a grouping, which keeps the categories "
"of each group together, in the order in which the groups first appear."
msgstr ""
"类别列的标签必须是字符串、整数、浮点数、布尔值或区间，JSON 格式会区分这些类型。在同一列中，相等的标签（例如 ``True`` 和 ``1`` ）属于同一分组，因为 "
"`kivi.woe.woe_table` 和 `kivi.woe.woe_transform` "
"按相等关系匹配标签。分组映射中的类别和组同样如此；分组映射会把同一组的类别放在一起，并按各组首次出现的次序排列。"

msgid ""
"Two specifications are equal when `to_json` gives the same text for both, which includes "
"`kivi_version`. The text is computed once and kept, so comparing and hashing a specification "
"again is cheap."
msgstr "当 `to_json` 为两个分箱方案给出相同的文本时，二者相等；文本中包含 `kivi_version` 。文本只计算一次并保留下来，因此再次比较或计算哈希的开销很小。"

msgid "Version of the JSON format that `to_json` writes."
msgstr "`to_json` 写出的 JSON 格式的版本。"

msgid ""
"Version 2 adds the groupings of categorical columns to version 1. A specification without grouped"
" columns is written as version 1, which earlier versions of kivi read as well. `FORMAT_VERSION` "
"is the newest version."
msgstr "版本 2 在版本 1 的基础上增加了类别列的分组映射。没有已分组列的分箱方案按版本 1 写出，早期版本的 kivi 也能读取。 `FORMAT_VERSION` 是最新的版本。"

msgid ":obj:`to_json`"
msgstr ":obj:`to_json`"

msgid "Write the specification."
msgstr "写出分箱方案。"

msgid "Names of the columns in the specification."
msgstr "分箱方案中各列的名称。"

msgid ""
"The columns are in the order in which they were fitted, which is the order of the columns of "
"`cut` and `woe_transform`."
msgstr "各列按拟合时的顺序排列，也就是 `cut` 和 `woe_transform` 结果中列的顺序。"

msgid ":obj:`select`"
msgstr ":obj:`select`"

msgid "A specification of some of the columns."
msgstr "只含部分列的分箱方案。"

msgid "Group every column of a sample as in development."
msgstr "按开发时的方式对样本的每一列分组。"

msgid ""
"Numeric columns are assigned to their bins with `kivi.binning.cut`, using the fitted edges and "
"special codes; an infinite value that is not a special code is in no bin and stays missing. "
"Grouped categorical columns are assigned to their groups as by `kivi.binning.group_categories`. A"
" category that the grouping does not map joins the group that the column's unseen policy names, "
"if any, and otherwise keeps its own label, so that `kivi.stability.psi_table` shows it as a new "
"group. Other categorical columns are returned unchanged, because their labels are their groups."
msgstr ""
"数值列用 `kivi.binning.cut` 按拟合的边界和特殊值分箱；不属于特殊值的无穷值不落入任何分箱，保持缺失。已分组的类别列按 "
"`kivi.binning.group_categories` 的方式分配到各组。分组映射中没有的类别归入该列未见分组策略指定的组；若没有指定，则保留自身标签，这样 "
"`kivi.stability.psi_table` 会把它显示为一个新组。其他类别列原样返回，因为其标签就是分组。"

msgid "Sample that has every column of the specification. Other columns are ignored."
msgstr "包含分箱方案中所有列的样本。其他列会被忽略。"

msgid ""
"The groups of each column of the specification, in its order, with the index of `frame`. Numeric "
"columns are categorical, with the special codes followed by every interval of the edges. Grouped "
"columns are categorical, with the groups in the order of the grouping followed by the categories "
"that it does not map and that no unseen group receives."
msgstr ""
"分箱方案中每一列的分组，按分箱方案的顺序排列，索引与 `frame` "
"相同。数值列为分类型，类别依次为特殊值和由边界构成的全部区间。已分组列为分类型，类别依次为按分组映射顺序排列的各组，以及分组映射中没有、也没有归入未见分组的类别。"

msgid ""
"If `frame` is not a DataFrame, lacks a column of the specification or has it twice, a column "
"fitted as numeric has values but not a real numeric dtype, such as a string or complex dtype, "
"which could hide its special codes; convert such a column with ``pandas.to_numeric``. Also if a "
"grouped column without an unseen group has a category that its grouping does not map but that is "
"the label of one of its groups, so that its group would be ambiguous. The message names the "
"column."
msgstr ""
"如果 `frame` 不是 DataFrame、缺少分箱方案中的某一列或该列出现两次，或者按数值列拟合的某一列有取值但不是实数 dtype（例如字符串或复数 "
"dtype），这可能使其特殊值无法匹配；请用 ``pandas.to_numeric`` "
"转换这样的列。此外，如果没有指定未见分组的已分组列含有分组映射中没有、却与其某个组的标签相同的类别，其分组就会含糊不清，也会引发错误。错误信息会指明该列。"

msgid ":obj:`woe_transform`"
msgstr ":obj:`woe_transform`"

msgid "Encode the groups with the fitted WOE."
msgstr "用拟合的 WOE 对分组编码。"

msgid ":obj:`kivi.binning.group_categories`"
msgstr ":obj:`kivi.binning.group_categories`"

msgid "Group one categorical column."
msgstr "对单个类别列分组。"

msgid "Encode every column of a sample with the WOE fitted in development."
msgstr "用开发时拟合的 WOE 对样本的每一列编码。"

msgid ""
"The columns are grouped as by `cut`, and each group is replaced with its WOE by "
"`kivi.woe.woe_transform`. A group that is not in a column's table, such as a new category, gets "
"the column's unseen policy, which by default raises an error. So does a category that the "
"grouping of a grouped column does not map, even when it equals the label of a group, for which "
"`cut` raises an error. An unseen group gives such values the WOE of that group."
msgstr ""
"各列先按 `cut` 的方式分组，再由 `kivi.woe.woe_transform` 把每个分组替换为其 WOE。不在该列 WOE "
"表中的分组（例如新类别）按该列的未见分组策略处理，默认会引发错误。已分组列中分组映射没有的类别也按此处理，即使它与某个组的标签相同（此时 `cut` "
"会引发错误）。指定了未见分组时，这类取值使用该组的 WOE。"

msgid "Float WOE values of each column of the specification, in its order, with the index of `frame`."
msgstr "分箱方案中每一列的浮点 WOE 值，按分箱方案的顺序排列，索引与 `frame` 相同。"

msgid ""
"If `frame` is not a DataFrame, lacks a column of the specification or has it twice, a column "
"fitted as numeric has values but not a real numeric dtype, or a column with the unseen policy "
"``\"raise\"`` has values whose group is not in its table, infinite values that are not special "
"codes or, for a grouped column, categories that its grouping does not map. The message names the "
"column."
msgstr ""
"如果 `frame` 不是 DataFrame、缺少分箱方案中的某一列或该列出现两次，按数值列拟合的某一列有取值但不是实数 dtype，或者未见分组策略为 ``\"raise\"`` "
"的列含有分组不在其 WOE 表中的取值、不属于特殊值的无穷值，或（对已分组的列而言）不在其分组映射中的类别。错误信息会指明该列。"

msgid "Group the columns without encoding them."
msgstr "只对各列分组，不编码。"

msgid "Encode one column."
msgstr "对单列编码。"

msgid ":obj:`kivi.scorecard.woe_to_points`"
msgstr ":obj:`kivi.scorecard.woe_to_points`"

msgid "Turn the WOE values into points."
msgstr "把 WOE 值转换为分值。"

msgid ""
"An infinite value that is not a special code of its column, such as the result of a division by "
"zero, is in no group: `cut` leaves it missing, and `woe_transform` treats it as unseen rather "
"than giving it the WOE of missing values or of the last interval."
msgstr "不属于该列特殊值的无穷值（例如除以零的结果）不属于任何分组： `cut` 把它留为缺失值，而 `woe_transform` 把它视为未见分组，而不是赋予缺失组或最后一个区间的 WOE。"

msgid "With an unseen WOE for ``housing``, the new label gets 0:"
msgstr "为 ``housing`` 指定未见分组的 WOE 后，新标签得到 0："

msgid "Return the specification of some of the columns."
msgstr "返回只含部分列的分箱方案。"

msgid ""
"Use it to keep only the variables of the final model before saving the specification for "
"production. The selected columns keep their edges, special codes, groupings, tables and unseen "
"policies."
msgstr "在为生产环境保存分箱方案之前，可用它只保留最终模型的变量。选中的列保留各自的边界、特殊值、分组映射、WOE 表和未见分组策略。"

msgid "sequence of str"
msgstr "str 序列"

msgid "Columns to keep, in the order of the new specification."
msgstr "要保留的列，其顺序即新分箱方案中的顺序。"

msgid "A specification of `columns` only."
msgstr "只含 `columns` 的分箱方案。"

msgid ""
"If `columns` is a string, is empty, repeats a column or names a column that is not in the "
"specification."
msgstr "如果 `columns` 是字符串、为空、重复某一列，或指定了分箱方案中没有的列。"

msgid ":obj:`columns`"
msgstr ":obj:`columns`"

msgid "The columns of the specification."
msgstr "分箱方案中的列。"

msgid "Save the specification."
msgstr "保存分箱方案。"

msgid "Return the specification as a dict of JSON types."
msgstr "以由 JSON 类型构成的 dict 返回分箱方案。"

msgid ""
"The result holds only dicts, lists, strings, numbers, booleans and None, so ``json.dumps`` can "
"write it without further conversion. Its keys are always in the same order. `to_json` writes this"
" dict."
msgstr "结果只包含 dict、list、字符串、数值、布尔值和 None，因此 ``json.dumps`` 无需额外转换即可写出。其键的顺序始终相同。 `to_json` 写出的就是这个 dict。"

msgid ""
"The keys ``format``, ``format_version``, ``kivi_version``, ``smoothing`` and ``variables``, a "
"list with one dict per column. See the user guide for the format."
msgstr ""
"包含键 ``format`` 、 ``format_version`` 、 ``kivi_version`` 、 ``smoothing`` 和 ``variables`` ；后者是每列一个 "
"dict 的列表。格式说明见用户指南。"

msgid ":obj:`from_dict`"
msgstr ":obj:`from_dict`"

msgid "Rebuild the specification."
msgstr "重建分箱方案。"

msgid "Write the dict as JSON."
msgstr "把该 dict 写成 JSON。"

msgid "Rebuild a specification from the result of `to_dict`."
msgstr "由 `to_dict` 的结果重建分箱方案。"

msgid ""
"The dict is checked before the specification is built, so that a damaged or hand-edited file "
"fails with a message that names the problem instead of encoding wrong values."
msgstr "构建分箱方案之前会先检查该 dict，因此损坏或被手工改动的文件会报错并指明问题，而不会编码出错误的值。"

msgid "**data**"
msgstr "**data**"

msgid "A dict in the format of `to_dict`, for example from ``json.load``."
msgstr "符合 `to_dict` 格式的 dict，例如来自 ``json.load`` 。"

msgid "The specification, equal to the one that wrote `data`."
msgstr "分箱方案，与写出 `data` 的那个相等。"

msgid ""
"If `data` is not a kivi binning specification, has a ``format_version`` newer than this version "
"of kivi reads, lacks a key or has an unknown one, or holds an invalid value. The message names "
"the column."
msgstr "如果 `data` 不是 kivi 分箱方案、其 ``format_version`` 比当前 kivi 能读取的版本更新、缺少某个键或含有未知的键，或含有无效的值。错误信息会指明相应的列。"

msgid ":obj:`to_dict`"
msgstr ":obj:`to_dict`"

msgid "The dict format."
msgstr "dict 格式。"

msgid ":obj:`from_json`"
msgstr ":obj:`from_json`"

msgid "Read the specification from JSON text."
msgstr "从 JSON 文本读取分箱方案。"

msgid "Return the specification as JSON text."
msgstr "以 JSON 文本返回分箱方案。"

msgid ""
"The text is the dict of `to_dict` written by ``json.dumps``. The same specification always gives "
"the same text, so saved specifications can be compared and kept under version control. Non-ASCII "
"labels are written as they are, so save the text as UTF-8."
msgstr ""
"该文本就是由 ``json.dumps`` 写出的 `to_dict` 的 dict。同一个分箱方案总是得到相同的文本，因此保存的分箱方案可以相互比较，并纳入版本控制。非 ASCII "
"标签按原样写出，因此请以 UTF-8 保存文本。"

msgid "**indent**"
msgstr "**indent**"

msgid "Indentation of nested values, as in ``json.dumps``. By default the text is a single line."
msgstr "嵌套值的缩进，含义与 ``json.dumps`` 相同。默认文本只有一行。"

msgid "str"
msgstr "str"

msgid "JSON text that `from_json` reads back into an equal specification."
msgstr "JSON 文本， `from_json` 可将其读回为相等的分箱方案。"

msgid "Read the specification back."
msgstr "读回分箱方案。"

msgid "The same content as a dict."
msgstr "以 dict 表示的相同内容。"

msgid "Write the text to a file with ``Path(\"spec.json\").write_text(text, encoding=\"utf-8\")``."
msgstr "用 ``Path(\"spec.json\").write_text(text, encoding=\"utf-8\")`` 把文本写入文件。"

msgid "Read a specification from the JSON text of `to_json`."
msgstr "从 `to_json` 写出的 JSON 文本读取分箱方案。"

msgid ""
"The loaded specification groups and encodes every sample exactly as the one that was saved. A "
"file written by a newer version of the format is rejected rather than read in part."
msgstr "加载的分箱方案对每个样本的分组和编码，与保存时的分箱方案完全相同。由更新版本格式写出的文件会被拒绝，而不会只读取其中一部分。"

msgid "**text**"
msgstr "**text**"

msgid "str or bytes"
msgstr "str 或 bytes"

msgid "JSON text, for example from ``Path(...).read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")``."
msgstr "JSON 文本，例如来自 ``Path(...).read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")`` 。"

msgid "The specification, equal to the one that wrote `text`."
msgstr "分箱方案，与写出 `text` 的那个相等。"

msgid ""
"If `text` is neither a str nor bytes, is not valid JSON, contains ``NaN`` or ``Infinity``, or "
"does not describe a valid specification; see `from_dict`."
msgstr "如果 `text` 既不是 str 也不是 bytes、不是有效的 JSON、含有 ``NaN`` 或 ``Infinity`` ，或没有描述一个有效的分箱方案；参见 `from_dict` 。"

msgid "Rebuild the specification from a dict."
msgstr "由 dict 重建分箱方案。"

msgid "Population stability index"
msgstr "群体稳定性指标"

msgid ""
"Measure how far a distribution has shifted between two samples. :func:`~kivi.stability.psi_table`"
" and :func:`~kivi.stability.psi` give the population stability index, and "
":func:`~kivi.stability.csi_table` gives the change of a scorecard's average points that the shift"
" causes."
msgstr ""
"衡量分布在两个样本之间偏移了多少。 :func:`~kivi.stability.psi_table` 和 :func:`~kivi.stability.psi` 给出群体稳定性指标， "
":func:`~kivi.stability.csi_table` 给出这种偏移使评分卡平均分值发生的变化。"

msgid "See :doc:`/user_guide/psi` for examples and the usual thresholds."
msgstr "示例和常用阈值见 :doc:`/user_guide/psi` 。"

msgid ":py:obj:`psi_table <kivi.stability.psi_table>`\\ \\(reference\\, current\\, \\*\\[\\, ...\\]\\)"
msgstr ":py:obj:`psi_table <kivi.stability.psi_table>`\\ \\(reference\\, current\\, \\*\\[\\, ...\\]\\)"

msgid "Compare two samples using their population stability index."
msgstr "通过群体稳定性指标（PSI）比较两个样本的分布。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`psi <kivi.stability.psi>`\\ \\(reference\\_counts\\, current\\_counts\\, \\*\\[\\, "
"...\\]\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`psi <kivi.stability.psi>`\\ \\(reference\\_counts\\, current\\_counts\\, \\*\\[\\, "
"...\\]\\)"

msgid "Compute the population stability index from counts per group."
msgstr "根据每组的计数计算群体稳定性指标（PSI）。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`csi_table <kivi.stability.csi_table>`\\ \\(reference\\, current\\, points\\, \\*\\[\\, "
"...\\]\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`csi_table <kivi.stability.csi_table>`\\ \\(reference\\, current\\, points\\, \\*\\[\\, "
"...\\]\\)"

msgid "Measure how much a variable's shift moves the average score."
msgstr "衡量变量分布的变化使平均分数移动了多少。"

msgid ""
"Each group's share of the current sample is compared with its share of the reference sample. Sum "
"the ``psi`` column for the index."
msgstr "比较每组在当前样本中的占比与在基准样本中的占比。将 ``psi`` 列求和即得到该指数。"

msgid "**reference, current**"
msgstr "**reference, current**"

msgid ""
"Labels or values binned using the same edges. Missing values and categories observed in only one "
"sample are included."
msgstr "类别标签或按相同边界分箱的数值。保留缺失值以及仅出现在一侧的类别。"

msgid "Positive replacement for a zero count when calculating shares."
msgstr "计算占比时，用这个正数替代零计数。"

msgid "**reference_weights, current_weights**"
msgstr "**reference_weights, current_weights**"

msgid ""
"Non-negative weight of each observation in the reference and the current sample, matched like the"
" samples. The counts are then sums of weights, and groups whose weights sum to zero in both "
"samples are left out. `smoothing` is then in units of weight."
msgstr "基准样本和当前样本中每个观测的非负权重，对应方式与样本相同。此时计数为权重之和，在两个样本中权重之和都为零的组会被排除，且 `smoothing` 以权重为单位。"

msgid ""
"Counts, normalized shares and the PSI contribution of each group. Sum the psi column for the "
"population stability index."
msgstr "各组的原始计数、归一化占比和 PSI 贡献。对 psi 列求和即得到总体 PSI。"

msgid ""
"If either sample is empty or not one-dimensional, or `smoothing` is not finite and positive. Also"
" if a weight array is not numeric, does not give each observation of its sample one finite, non-"
"negative weight with a positive total, or has an index other than that of its sample."
msgstr "如果任一样本为空或不是一维，或者 `smoothing` 不是有限正数。此外，如果某个权重数组不是数值、没有为对应样本的每个观测给出一个有限非负的权重、权重总和不为正，或其索引与对应样本不同。"

msgid ":obj:`psi`"
msgstr ":obj:`psi`"

msgid "The same index from counts per group."
msgstr "根据每组计数计算同一指标。"

msgid ":obj:`csi_table`"
msgstr ":obj:`csi_table`"

msgid "Weight the change of each group's share with its points."
msgstr "以分组分值为权重衡量每组占比的变化。"

msgid "Fit edges on the reference sample."
msgstr "在基准样本上拟合分箱边界。"

msgid "Relate the groups to a binary target."
msgstr "将分组与二分类目标关联起来。"

msgid ""
"For group :math:`i`, let :math:`q_i` be its share of the reference sample and :math:`p_i` its "
"share of the current sample. Then"
msgstr "对第 :math:`i` 组，令 :math:`q_i` 为其在基准样本中的占比，:math:`p_i` 为其在当前样本中的占比，则"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\\mathrm{PSI}_i = (p_i - q_i) \\ln \\frac{p_i}{q_i}, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathrm{PSI} = \\sum_i \\mathrm{PSI}_i."
msgstr ""
"\\mathrm{PSI}_i = (p_i - q_i) \\ln \\frac{p_i}{q_i}, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathrm{PSI} = \\sum_i \\mathrm{PSI}_i."

msgid ""
"Each zero count is replaced with `smoothing` before the shares are normalized, so a group "
"observed in only one sample has a finite contribution. The ``reference`` and ``current`` columns "
"always report the observed counts."
msgstr "在归一化占比之前，每个零计数都会被替换为 `smoothing`，因此只在一个样本中出现的组也有有限的贡献值。 ``reference`` 和 ``current`` 列始终报告实际观测到的计数。"

msgid ""
"If both samples are categorical with the same dtype, rows follow the order of the categories with"
" missing values last. Otherwise they follow the order in which the groups first appear, in the "
"reference sample and then in the current sample."
msgstr "如果两个样本都是分类型且 dtype 相同，各行按类别顺序排列，缺失值排在最后。否则按分组首次出现的次序排列，先看基准样本，再看当前样本。"

msgid "[Rb11431c5e9a8-1]_"
msgstr "[Rb11431c5e9a8-1]_"

msgid ""
"Use this when the samples are already aggregated, for example monthly counts per score band from "
"a monitoring report."
msgstr "适用于样本已经汇总的情况，例如监控报表中按分数段统计的月度计数。"

msgid "**reference_counts, current_counts**"
msgstr "**reference_counts, current_counts**"

msgid ""
"One-dimensional, non-negative counts of each group in the reference and the current sample, in "
"the same group order. Two Series must have identical indices. Weighted counts need not be "
"integers."
msgstr "基准样本和当前样本中每组的一维非负计数，两者的分组顺序须一致。两个 Series 的索引必须相同。加权计数不必是整数。"

msgid "The population stability index."
msgstr "群体稳定性指标。"

msgid ""
"If the counts are not one-dimensional, numeric, finite and non-negative, have different lengths "
"or a zero total, or are two Series with different indices, or `smoothing` is not finite and "
"positive."
msgstr "如果计数不是一维、不是数值、不是有限非负数，两组计数长度不同或总和为零，或者是索引不同的两个 Series，或者 `smoothing` 不是有限正数。"

msgid ":obj:`psi_table`"
msgstr ":obj:`psi_table`"

msgid "The index and its contributions from group labels."
msgstr "根据分组标签计算该指标及各组贡献。"

msgid ":obj:`kivi.woe.iv`"
msgstr ":obj:`kivi.woe.iv`"

msgid "The same divergence between events and non-events."
msgstr "事件与非事件之间的同一种散度。"

msgid ""
"With :math:`q_i` and :math:`p_i` the smoothed shares of group :math:`i` in the reference and the "
"current sample,"
msgstr "记 :math:`q_i` 和 :math:`p_i` 为第 :math:`i` 组在基准样本和当前样本中平滑后的占比，则"

msgid "which equals the sum of the ``psi`` column of `psi_table` for the same groups."
msgstr "它等于相同分组下 `psi_table` 中 ``psi`` 列之和。"

msgid ""
"The characteristic stability index (CSI) weights the change of each group's share, from the "
"reference to the current sample, with the scorecard points of the group. Sum the ``csi`` column "
"for the change of the variable's average points."
msgstr "特征稳定性指标（CSI）以每组的评分卡分值为权重，衡量各组占比从基准样本到当前样本的变化。将 ``csi`` 列求和，即得到该变量平均分值的变化。"

msgid ""
"Labels or values binned using the same edges, as for `psi_table`. Missing values and groups "
"observed in only one sample are included."
msgstr "类别标签或按相同边界分箱的数值，与 `psi_table` 相同。保留缺失值以及仅出现在一个样本中的分组。"

msgid "pandas.DataFrame, pandas.Series or mapping"
msgstr "pandas.DataFrame、pandas.Series 或 mapping"

msgid ""
"Points of each group. A DataFrame holds the groups of one variable in a ``bin`` column, or in its"
" index without one, and their points in a ``points`` column, such as ``table.loc[[variable]]`` of"
" a `kivi.scorecard.points_table` result. The variable may be named in the index or in a "
"``variable`` column, as after ``reset_index()``, but only one variable may appear. A Series or "
"mapping gives the points by group. A missing label gives the points of missing values."
msgstr ""
"每个分组的分值。DataFrame 把一个变量的分组放在 ``bin`` 列中（没有该列时放在索引中），把分值放在 ``points`` 列中，例如 "
"`kivi.scorecard.points_table` 结果的 ``table.loc[[variable]]`` 。变量名可以在索引中，也可以在 ``variable`` 列中（如 "
"``reset_index()`` 之后），但只能出现一个变量。Series 或映射按分组给出分值。缺失标签给出缺失值的分值。"

msgid "float, optional"
msgstr "float，可选"

msgid ""
"Points of observed groups that are missing from `points`, such as a new category that "
"`kivi.woe.woe_transform` encoded with ``unseen``. Its applicants receive the "
"`kivi.scorecard.woe_to_points` result for that WOE, not the WOE itself; see the Notes. By default"
" such groups raise an error."
msgstr ""
"`points` 中缺少的已观测分组的分值，例如 `kivi.woe.woe_transform` 用 ``unseen`` 编码的新类别。这些申请人得到的是对该 WOE 调用 "
"`kivi.scorecard.woe_to_points` 的结果，而不是 WOE 本身；参见“说明”。默认情况下，这样的分组会引发错误。"

msgid ""
"Non-negative weight of each observation in the reference and the current sample, matched like the"
" samples. The counts and shares are then sums of weights, and groups whose weights sum to zero in"
" both samples are left out."
msgstr "基准样本和当前样本中每个观测的非负权重，对应方式与样本相同。此时计数和占比都基于权重之和，在两个样本中权重之和都为零的组会被排除。"

msgid ""
"One row per observed group, indexed by ``bin``, with the counts ``reference`` and ``current``, "
"their shares ``reference_share`` and ``current_share``, the group's ``points`` and its "
"contribution ``csi``. Sum the csi column for the index."
msgstr ""
"每个观测到的分组一行，以 ``bin`` 为索引，列出计数 ``reference`` 和 ``current`` 、占比 ``reference_share`` 和 "
"``current_share`` 、该组的 ``points`` 及其贡献 ``csi`` 。将 csi 列求和即得到该指标。"

msgid ""
"If either sample is empty or not one-dimensional, `points` is not a DataFrame, Series or mapping,"
" holds more than one variable, repeats a group or has values that are not finite numbers, "
"`unseen_points` is not a finite number, or an observed group has no points and `unseen_points` is"
" not given. Also if a weight array is invalid, as in `psi_table`."
msgstr ""
"如果任一样本为空或不是一维的， `points` 不是 DataFrame、Series 或映射，包含多个变量、重复某个分组或含有不是有限数的值， `unseen_points` "
"不是有限数，或者某个观测到的分组没有分值且未给出 `unseen_points` 。此外，权重数组无效时也会引发错误，与 `psi_table` 相同。"

msgid "The population stability index of the same groups."
msgstr "相同分组的群体稳定性指标。"

msgid ":obj:`kivi.scorecard.points_table`"
msgstr ":obj:`kivi.scorecard.points_table`"

msgid "The points of every group of a scorecard."
msgstr "评分卡每个分组的分值。"

msgid ""
"For group :math:`i` with points :math:`s_i`, let :math:`q_i` be its share of the reference sample"
" and :math:`p_i` its share of the current sample. Then"
msgstr "对分值为 :math:`s_i` 的第 :math:`i` 组，令 :math:`q_i` 为其在基准样本中的占比， :math:`p_i` 为其在当前样本中的占比，则"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\\mathrm{CSI}_i = (p_i - q_i)\\, s_i, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathrm{CSI} = \\sum_i \\mathrm{CSI}_i\n"
"= \\sum_i p_i s_i - \\sum_i q_i s_i,"
msgstr ""
"\\mathrm{CSI}_i = (p_i - q_i)\\, s_i, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathrm{CSI} = \\sum_i \\mathrm{CSI}_i\n"
"= \\sum_i p_i s_i - \\sum_i q_i s_i,"

msgid ""
"the average points of the variable in the current sample minus those in the reference sample "
"[R05dcc8ea5547-1]_. The shares sum to 1 in both samples, so adding the same number to the points "
"of every group leaves the CSI unchanged: only the differences between the groups count, not the "
"share of the intercept and offset that `kivi.scorecard.points_table` gives each variable. Over "
"all variables of a scorecard, the CSI values add up to the change of the average score."
msgstr ""
"即该变量在当前样本中的平均分值减去在基准样本中的平均分值 [R05dcc8ea5547-1]_ 。两个样本的占比之和都为 1，因此给每组的分值加上同一个数不会改变 "
"CSI：起作用的只是各组之间的差别，而不是 `kivi.scorecard.points_table` 分摊给每个变量的截距和偏移量份额。对评分卡的所有变量，CSI 之和就是平均分数的变化。"

msgid ""
"Unlike in `psi_table`, the shares are not smoothed. A contribution has no logarithm, so an empty "
"group contributes a finite amount without smoothing, and a smoothed share would credit an empty "
"group with applicants it does not have, so the sum would no longer be the change of the average "
"points."
msgstr "与 `psi_table` 不同，这里的占比不做平滑。贡献中没有对数，因此空组不经平滑也只有有限的贡献；而平滑后的占比会让空组拥有它并没有的申请人，求和结果也就不再是平均分值的变化。"

msgid ""
"`unseen_points` is in points, like `points`. For applicants that ``woe_transform(..., "
"unseen=woe)`` encoded, it is ``woe_to_points`` of a one-row frame that holds that WOE; a WOE of 0"
" gives the variable's share of the intercept and offset, the same for every variable. Passing the"
" WOE itself would give a wrong CSI without an error."
msgstr ""
"`unseen_points` 与 `points` 一样以分值为单位。对 ``woe_transform(..., unseen=woe)`` 编码的申请人，它是对包含该 WOE "
"的单行数据调用 ``woe_to_points`` 的结果；WOE 为 0 时得到该变量分摊的截距和偏移量份额，每个变量都相同。如果直接传入 WOE 本身，会在没有任何报错的情况下得到错误的 "
"CSI。"

msgid ""
"Some texts also call the PSI of a single variable its CSI; that is `psi_table` of the variable's "
"groups. Rows are ordered as in `psi_table`, and groups of `points` observed in neither sample are"
" left out, since they contribute nothing."
msgstr ""
"有些文献也把单个变量的 PSI 称为它的 CSI，那就是对该变量的分组调用 `psi_table` 的结果。各行顺序与 `psi_table` 相同； `points` "
"中在两个样本里都没有出现的分组不计入，因为它们没有贡献。"

msgid "[R05dcc8ea5547-1]_"
msgstr "[R05dcc8ea5547-1]_"

msgid "The average points fall from 32.5 to 28.75, by the sum of the ``csi`` column, -3.75."
msgstr "平均分值从 32.5 降到 28.75，降幅即 ``csi`` 列之和 -3.75。"

msgid "Credit strategy"
msgstr "信贷策略"

msgid ""
"Turn scores and PDs into credit decisions. :func:`~kivi.strategy.cutoff_table` shows what each "
"cut-off approves, :func:`~kivi.strategy.confusion_table` counts its right and wrong decisions, "
":func:`~kivi.strategy.swap_set` compares the decisions of two scores, and "
":func:`~kivi.strategy.expected_loss` and :func:`~kivi.strategy.expected_loss_table` give the "
"expected loss of each exposure and of each grade."
msgstr ""
"把评分和 PD 转化为信贷决策。 :func:`~kivi.strategy.cutoff_table` 显示每个截断点通过哪些申请人， "
":func:`~kivi.strategy.confusion_table` 统计其正确和错误的决策， :func:`~kivi.strategy.swap_set` 比较两个评分的决策， "
":func:`~kivi.strategy.expected_loss` 和 :func:`~kivi.strategy.expected_loss_table` "
"给出每笔敞口和每个等级的预期损失。"

msgid "See :doc:`/user_guide/strategy` for examples on the bundled data."
msgstr "基于内置数据的示例见 :doc:`/user_guide/strategy` 。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`cutoff_table <kivi.strategy.cutoff_table>`\\ \\(score\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, cutoffs\\, "
"...\\]\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`cutoff_table <kivi.strategy.cutoff_table>`\\ \\(score\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, cutoffs\\, "
"...\\]\\)"

msgid "Summarize the approved book and the rejected events at each cut-off."
msgstr "汇总每个截断点下通过客群的情况及被拒绝的事件。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`confusion_table <kivi.strategy.confusion_table>`\\ \\(score\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, "
"cutoffs\\, ...\\]\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`confusion_table <kivi.strategy.confusion_table>`\\ \\(score\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, "
"cutoffs\\, ...\\]\\)"

msgid "Count the declined events and non-events at each cut-off, with precision, recall and F1."
msgstr "统计每个截断点下被拒绝的事件和非事件，并给出精确率、召回率和 F1。"

msgid ":py:obj:`swap_set <kivi.strategy.swap_set>`\\ \\(current\\, new\\[\\, target\\, weights\\]\\)"
msgstr ":py:obj:`swap_set <kivi.strategy.swap_set>`\\ \\(current\\, new\\[\\, target\\, weights\\]\\)"

msgid "Compare the decisions of a current and a new score at their cut-offs."
msgstr "在各自的截断点上比较现行评分与新评分的审批决策。"

msgid ":py:obj:`expected_loss <kivi.strategy.expected_loss>`\\ \\(probability\\, lgd\\, ead\\)"
msgstr ":py:obj:`expected_loss <kivi.strategy.expected_loss>`\\ \\(probability\\, lgd\\, ead\\)"

msgid "Compute the expected loss of each exposure from its PD, LGD and EAD."
msgstr "根据 PD、LGD 和 EAD 计算每笔敞口的预期损失。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`expected_loss_table <kivi.strategy.expected_loss_table>`\\ \\(groups\\, probability\\, "
"...\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`expected_loss_table <kivi.strategy.expected_loss_table>`\\ \\(groups\\, probability\\, "
"...\\)"

msgid "Summarize exposure and expected loss by grade or other group."
msgstr "按等级或其他分组汇总敞口和预期损失。"

msgid ""
"A cut-off approves every observation whose score is at or below it, so a higher cut-off approves "
"more applicants and lets more events through. Each row shows the size and the event rate of the "
"approved book and the shares of events and non-events that the cut-off rejects."
msgstr "截断点通过所有评分不高于它的观测，因此截断点越高，通过的申请人越多，放进来的事件也越多。每一行给出通过客群的规模和事件率，以及该截断点拒绝的事件和非事件所占的比例。"

msgid ""
"Finite numeric scores that are higher for a higher risk, such as a PD. Negate scorecard points, "
"which are higher for a lower risk."
msgstr "有限的数值评分，风险越高，评分越高，例如 PD。评分卡分数越高表示风险越低，因此须取负后再传入。"

msgid "**cutoffs**"
msgstr "**cutoffs**"

msgid ""
"Number of quantile cut-offs, or increasing cut-off values. An integer `n` uses the edges of "
"``kivi.binning.bin_edges(score, bins=n)`` above the lowest, so the rows approve about 1/n, 2/n "
"and so on up to all of the sample, and tied scores can leave fewer rows. Pass explicit values as "
"a sequence, also for a single cut-off, such as ``[0.1]``. With `weights`, an integer gives "
"weighted quantiles, as ``bin_edges(score, bins=n, weights=weights)`` does."
msgstr ""
"分位数截断点的数量，或递增的截断点取值。整数 `n` 使用 ``kivi.binning.bin_edges(score, bins=n)`` 中最低边界以上的各个边界，因此各行大约通过样本的 "
"1/n、2/n，依此类推直至全部样本；相同评分可能使行数减少。显式取值须以序列传入，单个截断点也是如此，例如 ``[0.1]`` 。使用 `weights` 时，整数会得到加权分位数，与 "
"``bin_edges(score, bins=n, weights=weights)`` 相同。"

msgid "**loss**"
msgstr "**loss**"

msgid ""
"Non-negative loss of each observation, matched like `target`, such as its expected loss from "
"`expected_loss` or the loss realized on a defaulted account. The table then has a column "
"``approved_loss``."
msgstr "每个观测的非负损失，对应方式与 `target` 相同，例如由 `expected_loss` 得到的预期损失，或违约账户的实际损失。此时表中会增加一列 ``approved_loss`` 。"

msgid ""
"Non-negative weight of each observation, such as the inverse of its sampling rate, matched like "
"`target`. Counts and losses become sums of weights. On the same cut-offs, integer weights give "
"the same table as repeating rows; an integer `cutoffs` can give other cut-offs, because weighted "
"quantiles use the inverted CDF."
msgstr ""
"每个观测的非负权重，例如其抽样比例的倒数，对应方式与 `target` 相同。计数和损失变为权重之和。在相同截断点上，整数权重与重复相应行得到的表相同；而整数 `cutoffs` "
"可能得到不同的截断点，因为加权分位数采用逆累积分布（inverted CDF）。"

msgid ""
"One row per cut-off, from the lowest to the highest, indexed by the cut-off value. The columns "
"are described in the Notes."
msgstr "每个截断点一行，从低到高排列，以截断点取值为索引。各列含义见“说明”。"

msgid ""
"If the inputs are empty or not one-dimensional, their indices or lengths do not match, `target` "
"has a label other than 0 and 1 or lacks one of them, `score` is not real and numeric or has a "
"missing or infinite value, or `cutoffs` is neither a positive integer nor a sequence of "
"increasing numbers. Also if `loss` is not numeric or does not give each observation one finite, "
"non-negative loss, or `weights` is not numeric, does not give each observation one finite, non-"
"negative weight, has an index other than that of `score`, or leaves a class without weight."
msgstr ""
"如果输入为空或不是一维的，索引或长度不一致，`target` 含有 0 和 1 以外的标签或缺少其中之一，`score` 不是实数数值或含有缺失值、无穷值，或 `cutoffs` "
"既不是正整数也不是递增数值的序列。此外，如果 `loss` 不是数值或没有为每个观测给出一个有限非负的损失，或 `weights` 不是数值、没有为每个观测给出一个有限非负的权重、索引与 "
"`score` 不同，或使某一类没有权重。"

msgid ""
"If `cutoffs` is an integer and tied scores leave fewer cut-offs than requested, as in "
"`kivi.binning.bin_edges`."
msgstr "如果 `cutoffs` 是整数，且相同评分使截断点少于请求的数量，与 `kivi.binning.bin_edges` 相同。"

msgid ":obj:`swap_set`"
msgstr ":obj:`swap_set`"

msgid "Compare the decisions of two scores at their cut-offs."
msgstr "在各自的截断点上比较两个评分的审批决策。"

msgid ":obj:`expected_loss`"
msgstr ":obj:`expected_loss`"

msgid "Expected loss of each exposure, to pass as `loss`."
msgstr "每笔敞口的预期损失，可作为 `loss` 传入。"

msgid "Event rates of the bands between cut-offs."
msgstr "相邻截断点之间各评分段的事件率。"

msgid ""
"A score equal to the cut-off is approved, so tied scores always get the same decision. With the "
"cut-offs of an integer `cutoffs`, the approved book of a row consists of the bands of "
"``kivi.metrics.gains_table`` with ``bins=cutoffs`` up to that cut-off."
msgstr ""
"等于截断点的评分予以通过，因此相同评分总是得到相同的决策。对于整数 `cutoffs` 给出的截断点，某一行的通过客群由 ``bins=cutoffs`` 时 "
"``kivi.metrics.gains_table`` 中直至该截断点的各评分段组成。"

msgid "``approved``: observations with a score at or below the cut-off, or the sum of their weights;"
msgstr "``approved``：评分不高于截断点的观测数，或它们的权重之和；"

msgid "``approval_rate``: ``approved`` divided by the whole sample;"
msgstr "``approval_rate``：``approved`` 除以整个样本；"

msgid "``approved_event``: events among the approved observations;"
msgstr "``approved_event``：通过的观测中的事件数；"

msgid ""
"``approved_event_rate``: ``approved_event`` divided by ``approved``, the bad rate of the approved"
" book, NaN when nothing is approved;"
msgstr "``approved_event_rate``：``approved_event`` 除以 ``approved``，即通过客群的坏账率；没有通过任何观测时为 NaN；"

msgid ""
"``rejected_event_share`` and ``rejected_non_event_share``: shares of all events and of all non-"
"events with a score above the cut-off;"
msgstr "``rejected_event_share`` 和 ``rejected_non_event_share``：评分高于截断点的事件和非事件分别占全部事件和全部非事件的比例；"

msgid ""
"``approved_loss``: with `loss`, the sum of the losses of the approved observations, weighted with"
" `weights`."
msgstr "``approved_loss``：传入 `loss` 时，通过的观测的损失之和，按 `weights` 加权。"

msgid ""
"A higher cut-off raises the approval rate and lowers both rejected shares. "
"``rejected_event_share`` is the share of bad outcomes the cut-off avoids, and "
"``rejected_non_event_share`` the share of good business it gives up."
msgstr ""
"截断点越高，通过率越高，两个拒绝比例都越低。``rejected_event_share`` 是该截断点避开的坏结果所占比例，``rejected_non_event_share`` "
"是它放弃的好业务所占比例。"

msgid ""
"A cut-off approves every observation whose score is at or below it and declines the others. "
"Treating a decline as the prediction of an event, each row is the confusion matrix of that "
"decision, with the measures that follow from it."
msgstr "截断点通过评分不高于它的每个观测，拒绝其余观测。把拒绝视为对事件的预测，每一行就是该决策的混淆矩阵，并附有由它得出的各项指标。"

msgid ""
"Number of quantile cut-offs, or increasing cut-off values, as in `cutoff_table`: an integer `n` "
"uses the edges of ``kivi.binning.bin_edges(score, bins=n)`` above the lowest, and tied scores can"
" leave fewer rows. Pass explicit values as a sequence, also for a single cut-off, such as "
"``[0.1]``. With `weights`, an integer gives weighted quantiles."
msgstr ""
"分位数截断点的数量，或递增的截断点取值，与 `cutoff_table` 相同：整数 `n` 使用 ``kivi.binning.bin_edges(score, bins=n)`` "
"中最低边界以上的各个边界，相同评分可能使行数减少。显式取值须以序列传入，单个截断点也是如此，例如 ``[0.1]`` 。使用 `weights` 时，整数会得到加权分位数。"

msgid ""
"Non-negative weight of each observation, such as the inverse of its sampling rate, matched like "
"`target`. The counts become sums of weights. On the same cut-offs, integer weights give the same "
"table as repeating rows; an integer `cutoffs` can give other cut-offs, because weighted quantiles"
" use the inverted CDF."
msgstr ""
"每个观测的非负权重，例如其抽样比例的倒数，对应方式与 `target` 相同。计数变为权重之和。在相同截断点上，整数权重与重复相应行得到的表相同；而整数 `cutoffs` "
"可能得到不同的截断点，因为加权分位数采用逆累积分布（inverted CDF）。"

msgid ""
"One row per cut-off, from the lowest to the highest, indexed by the cut-off value in an index "
"named ``cutoff``, as in `cutoff_table`. The columns are described in the Notes."
msgstr "每个截断点一行，从低到高排列，以截断点取值为索引，索引名为 ``cutoff`` ，与 `cutoff_table` 相同。各列含义见“说明”。"

msgid ""
"If the inputs are empty or not one-dimensional, their indices or lengths do not match, `target` "
"has a label other than 0 and 1 or a missing label, or lacks one of the classes, `score` is not "
"real and numeric or has a missing or infinite value, or `cutoffs` is neither a positive integer "
"nor a sequence of increasing numbers. Also if `weights` is not numeric, does not give each "
"observation one finite, non-negative weight, has an index other than that of `score`, or leaves a"
" class without weight."
msgstr ""
"如果输入为空或不是一维的，索引或长度不一致，`target` 含有 0 和 1 以外的标签或缺失标签，或缺少其中一类，`score` 不是实数数值或含有缺失值、无穷值，或 `cutoffs` "
"既不是正整数也不是递增数的序列。此外，如果 `weights` 不是数值、没有为每个观测给出一个有限非负的权重、索引与 `score` 不同，或使某一类没有权重。"

msgid ":obj:`cutoff_table`"
msgstr ":obj:`cutoff_table`"

msgid "Approval rate and rejected shares at the same cut-offs."
msgstr "相同截断点下的通过率和拒绝比例。"

msgid "The same counts at every threshold, flagging scores at or above it."
msgstr "每个阈值下的同样计数，标记评分不低于阈值的观测。"

msgid ""
"An event is the positive class and a decline, a score above the cut-off, the positive prediction."
" A score equal to the cut-off is approved, so tied scores always get the same decision. The "
"columns are:"
msgstr "事件为正类，拒绝（评分高于截断点）为正预测。评分等于截断点的观测被通过，因此相同评分总得到相同决策。各列为："

msgid ""
"``true_positive`` and ``false_positive``: events and non-events that the cut-off declines, or the"
" sums of their weights;"
msgstr "``true_positive`` 和 ``false_positive`` ：截断点拒绝的事件数和非事件数，或者它们的权重之和；"

msgid "``true_negative`` and ``false_negative``: non-events and events that the cut-off approves;"
msgstr "``true_negative`` 和 ``false_negative`` ：截断点通过的非事件数和事件数；"

msgid ""
"``precision``: ``true_positive`` divided by the declined observations, the event rate among them,"
" which is NaN when the cut-off declines nobody;"
msgstr "``precision`` ： ``true_positive`` 除以被拒绝的观测数，即其中的事件率，截断点不拒绝任何观测时为 NaN；"

msgid ""
"``recall``: ``true_positive`` divided by all events, the share of events that the cut-off "
"declines;"
msgstr "``recall`` ： ``true_positive`` 除以全部事件数，即截断点拒绝的事件所占比例；"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"``f1``: the harmonic mean of ``precision`` and ``recall``, :math:`2 \\mathrm{TP} / (2 "
"\\mathrm{TP} + \\mathrm{FP} + \\mathrm{FN})`, which is 0 when no event is declined, also when "
"nothing is declined;"
msgstr ""
"``f1`` ： ``precision`` 和 ``recall`` 的调和平均，:math:`2 \\mathrm{TP} / (2 \\mathrm{TP} + \\mathrm{FP} "
"+ \\mathrm{FN})` ，没有事件被拒绝时为 0，什么都不拒绝时也是如此；"

msgid "``accuracy``: ``true_positive`` plus ``true_negative``, divided by the whole sample."
msgstr "``accuracy`` ： ``true_positive`` 加 ``true_negative`` ，再除以整个样本。"

msgid ""
"The rows match the other tables of kivi. ``recall`` equals ``rejected_event_share`` of "
"`cutoff_table`, ``false_positive`` divided by all non-events equals its "
"``rejected_non_event_share``, and ``false_negative`` equals its ``approved_event``. The "
"``true_positive``, ``false_positive``, ``recall`` and ``precision`` of a row also equal "
"``cum_event``, ``cum_non_event``, ``true_positive_rate`` and ``precision`` of the row of "
"`kivi.metrics.roc_table` with the lowest threshold above the cut-off, which is infinity when the "
"cut-off is not below any score. The rows are shifted because `roc_table` flags the scores at or "
"above a threshold, while a cut-off declines only those above it."
msgstr ""
"各行与 kivi 的其他表相互对应。 ``recall`` 等于 `cutoff_table` 的 ``rejected_event_share`` ， ``false_positive`` "
"占全部非事件的比例等于它的 ``rejected_non_event_share`` ，而 ``false_negative`` 等于它的 ``approved_event`` 。每行的 "
"``true_positive`` 、 ``false_positive`` 、 ``recall`` 和 ``precision`` 还分别等于 "
"`kivi.metrics.roc_table` 中阈值高于截断点的最低一行的 ``cum_event`` 、 ``cum_non_event`` 、 "
"``true_positive_rate`` 和 ``precision`` ，截断点不低于任何评分时该阈值为无穷大。两者错开一行，是因为 `roc_table` "
"标记评分不低于阈值的观测，而截断点只拒绝高于它的观测。"

msgid ""
"The measures depend on the share of events in the sample. A cut-off that approves everyone has an"
" accuracy of one minus the event rate, and an event rate of a few per cent gives high accuracy "
"and a low ``precision`` at almost every cut-off. Compare cut-offs by the shares of events and "
"non-events they decline, as in `cutoff_table`, or by the costs of the two kinds of error."
msgstr ""
"这些指标取决于样本中事件的占比。通过所有观测的截断点，其准确率等于 1 减去事件率；事件率只有百分之几时，几乎在每个截断点上准确率都很高， ``precision`` "
"都很低。比较截断点时，请看它们拒绝的事件和非事件各占多少，如 `cutoff_table` 所示，或比较两类错误的成本。"

msgid ""
"Each score approves the observations at or below its cut-off. The four rows are the observations "
"both scores approve, the swap-outs that only the current score approves, the swap-ins that only "
"the new score approves, and those both decline."
msgstr "每个评分通过不高于其截断点的观测。四行依次为：两个评分都通过的观测、只有现行评分通过的换出（swap-out）、只有新评分通过的换入（swap-in），以及两个评分都拒绝的观测。"

msgid ""
"Finite numeric scores of the current model, higher for a higher risk, such as a PD. Negate "
"scorecard points."
msgstr "现行模型的有限数值评分，风险越高，评分越高，例如 PD。评分卡分数须取负。"

msgid ""
"Finite numeric scores of the new model, of the same length as `current` and higher for a higher "
"risk. The two scores need not be on the same scale."
msgstr "新模型的有限数值评分，长度与 `current` 相同，风险越高，评分越高。两个评分不必采用同一刻度。"

msgid ""
"Binary labels, with 1 indicating the event, and missing values for unknown outcomes, such as the "
"applicants the current score declined. Without `target`, the table only counts the observations."
msgstr "二元标签，1 表示事件，缺失值表示结果未知，例如被现行评分拒绝的申请人。不传入 `target` 时，表中只统计观测数。"

msgid "**current_cutoff**"
msgstr "**current_cutoff**"

msgid "Cut-off of the current score. Observations with a `current` score at or below it are approved."
msgstr "现行评分的截断点。`current` 评分不高于它的观测予以通过。"

msgid "**new_cutoff**"
msgstr "**new_cutoff**"

msgid "Cut-off of the new score, applied in the same way to `new`."
msgstr "新评分的截断点，以同样方式作用于 `new`。"

msgid ""
"Non-negative weight of each observation, such as the inverse of its sampling rate. Counts become "
"sums of weights, so integer weights give the same table as repeating rows."
msgstr "每个观测的非负权重，例如其抽样比例的倒数。计数变为权重之和，因此整数权重与重复相应行得到的表相同。"

msgid ""
"Four rows indexed by the decisions of the two scores, ``current`` and ``new``, each "
"``\"approve\"`` or ``\"decline\"``. The columns are ``total`` and ``share``, and with `target` "
"also ``known``, ``event`` and ``event_rate``; see the Notes."
msgstr ""
"四行，以两个评分的决策 ``current`` 和 ``new`` 为索引，取值均为 ``\"approve\"`` 或 ``\"decline\"``。列为 ``total`` 和 "
"``share``，传入 `target` 时还有 ``known``、``event`` 和 ``event_rate``；见“说明”。"

msgid ""
"If the inputs are empty or not one-dimensional, their lengths differ, or they are Series with "
"different indices; `current` or `new` is not real and numeric or has a missing or infinite value;"
" `target` has a value other than 0, 1 and missing; a cut-off is not a number or is missing; or "
"`weights` is not numeric, does not give each observation one finite, non-negative weight with a "
"positive total, or has an index other than that of `current`."
msgstr ""
"如果输入为空或不是一维的，长度不同，或为索引不同的 Series；`current` 或 `new` 不是实数数值或含有缺失值、无穷值；`target` 含有 0、1 "
"和缺失值以外的值；截断点不是数值或为缺失值；或 `weights` 不是数值、没有为每个观测给出一个有限非负且总和为正的权重，或索引与 `current` 不同。"

msgid "Approval and event rates over a range of cut-offs."
msgstr "一系列截断点下的通过率和事件率。"

msgid "Infer the outcomes of declined applicants."
msgstr "推断被拒申请人的结果。"

msgid ""
"The rows ``(\"approve\", \"decline\")`` and ``(\"decline\", \"approve\")`` are the swap-outs and "
"the swap-ins. Every row is reported, also when it is empty. The columns are:"
msgstr "``(\"approve\", \"decline\")`` 和 ``(\"decline\", \"approve\")`` 两行分别是换出和换入。每一行都会列出，即使为空。各列为："

msgid "``total``: observations in the row, or the sum of their weights;"
msgstr "``total``：该行的观测数，或它们的权重之和；"

msgid "``share``: ``total`` divided by the whole sample;"
msgstr "``share``：``total`` 除以整个样本；"

msgid "``known``: observations in the row with a known outcome;"
msgstr "``known``：该行中结果已知的观测数；"

msgid "``event``: events in the row;"
msgstr "``event``：该行的事件数；"

msgid "``event_rate``: ``event`` divided by ``known``, NaN without known outcomes."
msgstr "``event_rate``：``event`` 除以 ``known``；没有已知结果时为 NaN。"

msgid ""
"The outcomes of the applicants the current score declined are usually unknown, because they never"
" received a loan. The rows of current declines, including the swap-ins, then have no "
"``event_rate``, and the swap set alone cannot show whether the new score accepts better "
"applicants than it rejects. Reject inference estimates the missing outcomes; pass the inferred "
"labels, with weights for an augmented sample, to complete the table."
msgstr ""
"被现行评分拒绝的申请人从未获得贷款，因此其结果通常未知。这时现行评分拒绝的各行（包括换入）没有 "
"``event_rate``，仅凭交换集无法判断新评分接受的申请人是否优于它拒绝的申请人。拒绝推断可以估计缺失的结果；传入推断得到的标签（对扩充样本还需传入权重），即可补全该表。"

msgid "The current declines usually have no known outcome:"
msgstr "现行评分拒绝的申请人通常没有已知结果："

msgid ""
"The expected loss is the product of the probability of default, the loss given default and the "
"exposure at default."
msgstr "预期损失是违约概率、违约损失率与违约风险敞口的乘积。"

msgid "Probabilities of default, from 0 to 1. Missing values give missing losses."
msgstr "违约概率，取值在 0 到 1 之间。缺失值对应的损失也为缺失。"

msgid ""
"Loss given default as a share of the exposure, from 0 to 1, as one value for all exposures or one"
" per exposure."
msgstr "违约损失率，即损失占敞口的比例，取值在 0 到 1 之间；可以为所有敞口给出一个值，也可以每笔敞口一个值。"

msgid ""
"Exposure at default, such as the outstanding balance, finite and non-negative, as one value or "
"one per exposure."
msgstr "违约风险敞口，例如未偿余额，须为有限非负值；可以给出一个值，也可以每笔敞口一个值。"

msgid ""
"Expected losses, in the units of `ead`, with the broadcast shape of the inputs. If an input is a "
"Series, the result is a Series with its index, named ``expected_loss``; scalar inputs give a "
"float."
msgstr ""
"预期损失，单位与 `ead` 相同，形状为各输入广播后的形状。如果某个输入是 Series，结果为具有其索引、名为 ``expected_loss`` 的 Series；输入均为标量时返回 "
"float。"

msgid ""
"If an input is not real and numeric, the inputs cannot be broadcast together, Series inputs have "
"different indices, `probability` or `lgd` has a value outside [0, 1], or `ead` has a negative or "
"infinite value."
msgstr "如果某个输入不是实数数值，各输入无法一起广播，作为 Series 的输入索引不同，`probability` 或 `lgd` 含有 [0, 1] 以外的值，或 `ead` 含有负值或无穷值。"

msgid ":obj:`expected_loss_table`"
msgstr ":obj:`expected_loss_table`"

msgid "Pass the expected losses as `loss` to sum them by cut-off."
msgstr "将预期损失作为 `loss` 传入，按截断点求和。"

msgid ":obj:`kivi.scorecard.score_to_pd`"
msgstr ":obj:`kivi.scorecard.score_to_pd`"

msgid "The PD implied by a scorecard score."
msgstr "评分卡分数所对应的 PD。"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"For an exposure with probability of default :math:`\\mathrm{PD}`, loss given default "
":math:`\\mathrm{LGD}` and exposure at default :math:`\\mathrm{EAD}`,"
msgstr "对于违约概率为 :math:`\\mathrm{PD}`、违约损失率为 :math:`\\mathrm{LGD}`、违约风险敞口为 :math:`\\mathrm{EAD}` 的敞口，"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "\\mathrm{EL} = \\mathrm{PD} \\times \\mathrm{LGD} \\times \\mathrm{EAD}."
msgstr "\\mathrm{EL} = \\mathrm{PD} \\times \\mathrm{LGD} \\times \\mathrm{EAD}."

msgid ""
"The PD refers to a horizon, usually one year, and the expected loss refers to the same horizon. "
"Missing values are not checked and give a missing loss."
msgstr "PD 对应一个期限，通常为一年，预期损失也对应同一期限。缺失值不做检查，对应的损失为缺失。"

msgid ""
"Each row adds up the exposures and expected losses of a group, such as a grade of a master scale,"
" and gives their ratio, the expected loss rate."
msgstr "每一行汇总一个分组（例如主标尺的一个等级）的敞口和预期损失，并给出两者之比，即预期损失率。"

msgid "Probability of default of each exposure, from 0 to 1, without missing values."
msgstr "每笔敞口的违约概率，取值在 0 到 1 之间，不得含有缺失值。"

msgid "Loss given default, from 0 to 1, as one value for all exposures or one per exposure."
msgstr "违约损失率，取值在 0 到 1 之间；可以为所有敞口给出一个值，也可以每笔敞口一个值。"

msgid ""
"Exposure at default, finite and non-negative, as one value or one per exposure. Series inputs "
"must have identical indices; otherwise the inputs are matched by position."
msgstr "违约风险敞口，须为有限非负值；可以给出一个值，也可以每笔敞口一个值。作为 Series 传入的输入，索引必须完全相同；否则按位置对应。"

msgid ""
"Non-negative weight of each exposure, such as the inverse of its sampling rate, matched like "
"`probability`. Counts, exposures and losses become sums of weights, so integer weights give the "
"same groups and sums as repeating rows, and groups whose weights sum to zero are left out. Groups"
" that are not categorical keep the order in which they first appear, also in rows of zero weight,"
" so their order can differ from that of repeated rows."
msgstr ""
"每笔敞口的非负权重，例如其抽样比例的倒数，对应方式与 `probability` "
"相同。计数、敞口和损失都变为加权和，因此整数权重与重复相应行得到的分组和各项和相同；权重之和为零的分组不列出。非分类型的分组按首次出现的顺序排列，权重为零的行也计入顺序，因此其顺序可能与重复行不同。"

msgid "One row per group with the columns described in the Notes."
msgstr "每个分组一行，各列含义见“说明”。"

msgid ""
"If `groups` or `probability` is empty or not one-dimensional, an input does not have one value "
"per exposure or a Series index other than that of the others, `probability`, `lgd` or `ead` is "
"not real and numeric or has a missing value, `probability` or `lgd` has a value outside [0, 1], "
"or `ead` has a negative or infinite value. Also if `weights` is not numeric, does not give each "
"exposure one finite, non-negative weight with a positive total, or has an index other than that "
"of `groups`."
msgstr ""
"如果 `groups` 或 `probability` 为空或不是一维的，某个输入没有为每笔敞口给出一个值，或其 Series 索引与其他输入不同，`probability`、`lgd` 或 "
"`ead` 不是实数数值或含有缺失值，`probability` 或 `lgd` 含有 [0, 1] 以外的值，或 `ead` 含有负值或无穷值。此外，如果 `weights` "
"不是数值、没有为每笔敞口给出一个有限非负且总和为正的权重，或索引与 `groups` 不同。"

msgid "Expected loss of each exposure."
msgstr "每笔敞口的预期损失。"

msgid "Observed and predicted default rates by grade."
msgstr "按等级比较实际与预测的违约率。"

msgid "For the exposures :math:`i` of a group, with weights :math:`w_i`, the columns are:"
msgstr "对于一个分组中权重为 :math:`w_i` 的敞口 :math:`i`，各列为："

#, python-brace-format
msgid "``exposure``: :math:`\\sum_i w_i \\mathrm{EAD}_i`;"
msgstr "``exposure``： :math:`\\sum_i w_i \\mathrm{EAD}_i`；"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"``exposure_weighted_probability``: :math:`\\sum_i w_i \\mathrm{EAD}_i \\mathrm{PD}_i / \\sum_i "
"w_i \\mathrm{EAD}_i`;"
msgstr ""
"``exposure_weighted_probability``： :math:`\\sum_i w_i \\mathrm{EAD}_i \\mathrm{PD}_i / \\sum_i "
"w_i \\mathrm{EAD}_i`；"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "``expected_loss``: :math:`\\sum_i w_i \\mathrm{PD}_i \\mathrm{LGD}_i \\mathrm{EAD}_i`;"
msgstr "``expected_loss``： :math:`\\sum_i w_i \\mathrm{PD}_i \\mathrm{LGD}_i \\mathrm{EAD}_i`；"

msgid "``expected_loss_rate``: ``expected_loss`` divided by ``exposure``."
msgstr "``expected_loss_rate``：``expected_loss`` 除以 ``exposure``。"

msgid ""
"The two ratios are NaN for a group without exposure. With one LGD for all exposures, "
"``expected_loss_rate`` is the LGD times ``exposure_weighted_probability``. The portfolio's "
"expected loss is the sum of the ``expected_loss`` column, and its expected loss rate is that sum "
"divided by the sum of ``exposure``."
msgstr ""
"没有敞口的分组，两个比率均为 NaN。所有敞口使用同一 LGD 时，``expected_loss_rate`` 等于 LGD 乘以 "
"``exposure_weighted_probability``。组合的预期损失是 ``expected_loss`` 列之和，其预期损失率是该和除以 ``exposure`` 之和。"

msgid "Univariate profile"
msgstr "单变量概况"

msgid ""
"Profile every column of a data frame in one row: how complete it is, how its values are "
"distributed and, with a binary target, how strongly it separates events from non-events. "
":func:`~kivi.univariate.profile_table` is the first look at the candidates of a model."
msgstr ""
"用一行概括数据框的每一列：完整程度、取值分布，以及在给出二元目标变量时区分事件与非事件的能力。 :func:`~kivi.univariate.profile_table` "
"是对模型候选变量的第一次全面审视。"

msgid "See :doc:`/user_guide/univariate` for an example and how to read the profile."
msgstr "示例以及如何解读概况表，见 :doc:`/user_guide/univariate` 。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`profile_table <kivi.univariate.profile_table>`\\ \\(frame\\[\\, target\\, columns\\, "
"...\\]\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`profile_table <kivi.univariate.profile_table>`\\ \\(frame\\[\\, target\\, columns\\, "
"...\\]\\)"

msgid "Summarize each column of a data frame in one row."
msgstr "用一行概括数据框的每一列。"

msgid ""
"Every column gets its kind, its number of missing values and its most frequent value; numeric "
"columns also get their range, quantiles, mean, standard deviation and shape. With a binary "
"target, each column also gets the event rates of its missing and non-missing rows, the "
"information value and the chi-squared test of a quick binning and, for numeric columns, the Gini "
"coefficient and the KS statistic of its values."
msgstr ""
"每一列都会给出其类型、缺失值个数和最常见的取值；数值列还给出取值范围、分位数、均值、标准差和分布形态。有二分类目标时，每一列还会给出缺失行与非缺失行的事件率，以及快速分箱的信息值和卡方检验；数值列还给出其取值的"
" Gini 系数和 KS 统计量。"

msgid ""
"One column per variable. Columns with a numeric dtype other than bool are numeric; all others, "
"such as object, string, category or bool, are categorical, as in `kivi.spec.fit_spec`."
msgstr ""
"每个变量一列。数值 dtype（bool 除外）的列是数值列；其他所有列（例如 object、string、category 或 bool）是类别列，与 `kivi.spec.fit_spec`"
" 相同。"

msgid ""
"Binary labels, with 1 indicating the event, one per row of `frame`. Both classes must be present."
" A Series must have the same index as `frame`; other inputs are matched by position. Without "
"`target` the table describes the columns only."
msgstr "二分类标签，1 表示事件， `frame` 的每一行一个。两类都必须出现。Series 必须与 `frame` 的索引相同；其他输入按位置对应。没有 `target` 时，表格只描述各列。"

msgid "Columns to profile, in the order of the rows. By default every column of `frame`."
msgstr "要分析的列，其顺序即结果中行的顺序。默认为 `frame` 的所有列。"

msgid ""
"Number of quantile bins of the quick binning of numeric columns, from `kivi.binning.bin_edges`, "
"for the ``iv`` column."
msgstr "数值列快速分箱的等频箱数，用于 `kivi.binning.bin_edges` ，结果见 ``iv`` 列。"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Special codes of numeric columns, such as ``{\"pdays\": [-1]}``, as in `kivi.spec.fit_spec`. They"
" count as values, not as missing, but are left out of the numeric summary and of the Gini "
"coefficient, and each code forms its own group in the quick binning."
msgstr ""
"数值列的特殊值编码，例如 ``{\"pdays\": [-1]}`` ，与 `kivi.spec.fit_spec` 相同。它们算作取值而不算缺失，但不参与数值汇总和 Gini "
"系数，并在快速分箱中各自成组。"

msgid ""
"Non-negative frequency weight of each row, matched like `target`, such as the inverse of its "
"sampling rate. Counts become sums of weights and every statistic is weighted, so integer weights "
"give the same result as repeating rows with unit weights. Rows with zero weight count for "
"nothing, so their values are not checked. The chi-squared test treats them as frequency weights: "
"a row of weight :math:`w` counts as :math:`w` observations."
msgstr ""
"每一行的非负频数权重，例如其抽样比例的倒数，对应方式与 `target` "
"相同。计数变为权重之和，每项统计量都加权计算，因此整数权重与重复相应行并使用单位权重的结果相同。权重为零的行不计入，因此也不检查其取值。卡方检验把它们当作频数权重：权重为 :math:`w` "
"的行算作 :math:`w` 个观测。"

msgid ""
"One row per column, indexed by the column names in an index named ``variable``. The columns are "
"described in the Notes."
msgstr "每列一行，以列名为索引，索引名为 ``variable`` 。各列含义见“说明”。"

msgid ""
"If `frame` is not a DataFrame or has no rows or no columns, `columns` repeats a column or names "
"one that `frame` lacks, a column name is not a string, or `bins` is not a positive integer. If "
"`target` does not give each row a label 0 or 1, lacks one of the two classes or is a column being"
" profiled, or if `weights` is invalid or leaves a class without weight. Also if `special` is not "
"a dict by column, names a column that is not profiled or is categorical, or has a code that is "
"not a number, or if a numeric column has infinite values that are not special codes."
msgstr ""
"如果 `frame` 不是 DataFrame、没有行或没有列， `columns` 重复某一列或指定了 `frame` 中没有的列，列名不是字符串，或 `bins` 不是正整数。如果 "
"`target` 的标签不是每行一个 0 或 1、缺少两类中的一类或是被分析的列之一，或者 `weights` 无效或使某一类没有权重。此外，如果 `special` 不是按列的 "
"dict、指定了未分析的列或类别列、含有不是数值的编码，或某个数值列含有不属于特殊值的无穷值。"

msgid ":obj:`kivi.spec.fit_spec`"
msgstr ":obj:`kivi.spec.fit_spec`"

msgid "Bin and encode the columns chosen after profiling."
msgstr "对分析后选出的列进行分箱和编码。"

msgid "The WOE and IV of one grouped column."
msgstr "单个已分组列的 WOE 和 IV。"

msgid ":obj:`kivi.metrics.gini`"
msgstr ":obj:`kivi.metrics.gini`"

msgid "The Gini coefficient of a score."
msgstr "评分的 Gini 系数。"

msgid ":obj:`kivi.metrics.ks`"
msgstr ":obj:`kivi.metrics.ks`"

msgid "The KS statistic of a score."
msgstr "评分的 KS 统计量。"

msgid "The quantile edges of the quick binning."
msgstr "快速分箱的分位数边界。"

msgid "Every column gets"
msgstr "每一列都包含"

msgid "``kind``: ``\"numeric\"`` or ``\"categorical\"``;"
msgstr "``kind`` ： ``\"numeric\"`` 或 ``\"categorical\"`` ；"

msgid ""
"``count`` and ``missing``: the number of rows with and without a value, and ``missing_share``, "
"the share of rows without one;"
msgstr "``count`` 和 ``missing`` ：有取值和无取值的行数； ``missing_share`` ：无取值的行所占的比例；"

msgid "``distinct``: the number of different values;"
msgstr "``distinct`` ：不同取值的个数；"

msgid ""
"``top`` and ``top_share``: the most frequent value and its share of the rows with a value. Of "
"values that are equally frequent, the first in the order of the categories, or else of "
"appearance, is shown;"
msgstr "``top`` 和 ``top_share`` ：最常见的取值及其在有取值的行中所占的比例。若多个取值同样常见，显示类别顺序中的第一个，没有类别顺序时显示最先出现的一个；"

msgid ""
"``special`` and ``special_share``: the number and share of rows with a special code, 0 for "
"categorical columns;"
msgstr "``special`` 和 ``special_share`` ：取特殊值编码的行数及其比例，类别列为 0；"

msgid ""
"``mean``, ``std``, ``min``, ``q01``, ``q50``, ``q99`` and ``max``: the mean, the sample standard "
"deviation, the smallest value, the 1%, 50% and 99% quantiles and the largest value of a numeric "
"column, without missing values and special codes. Categorical columns get NaN."
msgstr ""
"``mean`` 、 ``std`` 、 ``min`` 、 ``q01`` 、 ``q50`` 、 ``q99`` 和 ``max`` "
"：数值列去除缺失值和特殊值编码后的均值、样本标准差、最小值、1%、50% 和 99% 分位数以及最大值。类别列为 NaN。"

msgid ""
"The quantiles interpolate linearly, as ``numpy.quantile`` does; with `weights` they are weighted "
"quantiles by the inverted CDF, as the edges of `kivi.binning.bin_edges`. Weights, even unit "
"weights, therefore change the quantiles and, through the edges, ``iv``, ``chi2_p_value`` and "
"``tied_bins``; with integer weights every other column equals that of the repeated rows without "
"weights. The standard deviation divides by the total weight minus 1, as it divides by the number "
"of rows minus 1 without weights, so it is NaN when the weights of a column's values sum to 1 or "
"less."
msgstr ""
"分位数按线性插值计算，与 ``numpy.quantile`` 相同；使用 `weights` 时，取逆累积分布（inverted CDF）意义下的加权分位数，与 "
"`kivi.binning.bin_edges` 的边界相同。因此权重（即使全为 1）会改变分位数，并通过边界改变 ``iv`` 、 ``chi2_p_value`` 和 "
"``tied_bins`` ；使用整数权重时，其他各列都等于不加权的重复行的结果。标准差除以总权重减 1，正如不加权时除以行数减 1，因此当某列取值的权重之和不超过 1 时，标准差为 NaN。"

msgid "With `target`, every column also gets"
msgstr "有 `target` 时，每一列还包含"

msgid "``event_rate``: the event rate of all rows, the same in every row of the table;"
msgstr "``event_rate`` ：全部行的事件率，在表格的每一行中都相同；"

msgid ""
"``missing_event_rate`` and ``non_missing_event_rate``: the event rates of the rows without and "
"with a value, NaN when there are no such rows;"
msgstr "``missing_event_rate`` 和 ``non_missing_event_rate`` ：无取值和有取值的行的事件率，没有这样的行时为 NaN；"

msgid ""
"``missing_lift`` and ``non_missing_lift``: these rates divided by ``event_rate``, so a lift above"
" 1 marks riskier rows;"
msgstr "``missing_lift`` 和 ``non_missing_lift`` ：上述事件率除以 ``event_rate`` ，提升度大于 1 表示这些行风险更高；"

msgid ""
"``iv``: the information value of the column, summed over the groups of `kivi.woe.woe_table`. "
"Numeric columns are cut into `bins` quantile bins with `kivi.binning.bin_edges` and "
"`kivi.binning.cut`, with a group for each special code; categorical columns keep their labels. "
"Missing values form a group of their own;"
msgstr ""
"``iv`` ：该列的信息值，即 `kivi.woe.woe_table` 各分组之和。数值列用 `kivi.binning.bin_edges` 和 `kivi.binning.cut` "
"切分为 `bins` 个等频箱，每个特殊值编码单独成组；类别列保留其标签。缺失值单独成组；"

msgid ""
"``tied_bins``: True where the quick binning of a numeric column has fewer bins than requested, "
"because tied quantiles were merged or no values are left to bin apart from missing values and "
"special codes. The table records this instead of warning for every column, as "
"`kivi.binning.bin_edges` does; such an IV understates the column until it is binned with custom "
"edges or special codes;"
msgstr ""
"``tied_bins`` ：数值列的快速分箱箱数少于所请求的箱数时为 True，原因是分位数重合而被合并，或者除缺失值和特殊值编码外没有可分箱的取值。表格记录这一情况，而不像 "
"`kivi.binning.bin_edges` 那样对每一列发出警告；在用自定义边界或特殊值编码分箱之前，这样的 IV 会低估该列；"

msgid ""
"``gini``: the Gini coefficient of the values of a numeric column as a score, without missing "
"values and special codes. It is positive when events have higher values, negative when they have "
"lower ones, and NaN for categorical columns or when the values leave out a class."
msgstr "``gini`` ：把数值列的取值作为评分时的 Gini 系数，不含缺失值和特殊值编码。事件的取值较高时为正，较低时为负；对类别列，或这些取值缺少某一类时，为 NaN。"

msgid ""
"After these, or after ``max`` without `target`, every column gets three statistics of the shape "
"of the distribution, computed from the same values as the summary, without missing values and "
"special codes. Categorical columns get NaN."
msgstr "在这些列之后（没有 `target` 时在 ``max`` 之后），每一列还给出描述分布形态的三个统计量，与汇总统计使用相同的取值，不含缺失值和特殊值编码。分类列为 NaN。"

msgid ""
"``skewness``: the bias-corrected sample skewness :math:`G_1`, as ``pandas.Series.skew`` computes "
"it;"
msgstr "``skewness`` ：偏差校正后的样本偏度 :math:`G_1` ，与 ``pandas.Series.skew`` 的计算相同；"

msgid ""
"``kurtosis``: the bias-corrected sample excess kurtosis :math:`G_2`, as ``pandas.Series.kurt`` "
"computes it, 0 for a normal distribution;"
msgstr "``kurtosis`` ：偏差校正后的样本超额峰度 :math:`G_2` ，与 ``pandas.Series.kurt`` 的计算相同，正态分布为 0；"

msgid ""
"``cv``: the coefficient of variation ``std / mean``, with the sign of the mean, NaN when the mean"
" is 0."
msgstr "``cv`` ：变异系数 ``std / mean`` ，符号与均值相同，均值为 0 时为 NaN。"

msgid ""
"With :math:`n` values :math:`x_i`, their mean :math:`\\bar x` and :math:`M_k = \\sum_i (x_i - "
"\\bar x)^k`,"
msgstr "设有 :math:`n` 个取值 :math:`x_i` ，其均值为 :math:`\\bar x` ，并记 :math:`M_k = \\sum_i (x_i - \\bar x)^k` ，则"

msgid ""
"G_1 = \\frac{n \\sqrt{n - 1}}{n - 2} \\frac{M_3}{M_2^{3/2}},\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"G_2 = \\frac{n (n + 1) (n - 1)}{(n - 2)(n - 3)} \\frac{M_4}{M_2^2}\n"
"- \\frac{3 (n - 1)^2}{(n - 2)(n - 3)}."
msgstr ""
"G_1 = \\frac{n \\sqrt{n - 1}}{n - 2} \\frac{M_3}{M_2^{3/2}},\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"G_2 = \\frac{n (n + 1) (n - 1)}{(n - 2)(n - 3)} \\frac{M_4}{M_2^2}\n"
"- \\frac{3 (n - 1)^2}{(n - 2)(n - 3)}."

msgid ""
":math:`G_1` is NaN for 2 values or fewer, :math:`G_2` for 3 or fewer, and both when all values "
"are equal. With `weights`, :math:`n` is the total weight and every sum is weighted, so integer "
"weights equal repeated rows, and the total weight must exceed 2 and 3."
msgstr ""
"取值不超过 2 个时 :math:`G_1` 为 NaN，不超过 3 个时 :math:`G_2` 为 NaN；所有取值都相等时两者均为 NaN。使用 `weights` 时， "
":math:`n` 为总权重，每个求和都加权计算，因此整数权重与重复相应行相同，总权重须分别大于 2 和 3。"

msgid "With `target`, these are followed by"
msgstr "有 `target` 时，其后还有"

msgid ""
"``ks``: the KS statistic of the same values, the largest gap between the cumulative distributions"
" of the values of events and of non-events, from 0 to 1 whichever way the values run, as "
"`kivi.metrics.ks` defines it. NaN where ``gini`` is NaN;"
msgstr ""
"``ks`` ：同一组取值的 KS 统计量，即事件取值的累计分布与非事件取值的累计分布之间的最大差距，无论取值方向如何都在 0 到 1 之间，定义与 `kivi.metrics.ks` 相同。 "
"``gini`` 为 NaN 时它也为 NaN；"

msgid ""
"``chi2_p_value``: the p-value of the chi-squared test of independence between the target and the "
"groups of the quick binning that gives ``iv``, missing values and special codes included. With "
":math:`O` the counts of events and non-events in each of the :math:`k` groups and :math:`E` the "
"counts expected if the event rate were the same in every group, the statistic :math:`\\sum (O - "
"E)^2 / E` is compared with a chi-squared distribution with :math:`k - 1` degrees of freedom. The "
"p-value is 1 when there is a single group."
msgstr ""
"``chi2_p_value`` ：目标与给出 ``iv`` 的快速分箱各组之间卡方独立性检验的 p 值，包含缺失值组和特殊值编码组。记 :math:`O` 为 :math:`k` "
"个组中每组事件和非事件的计数， :math:`E` 为各组事件率相同时的期望计数，则统计量 :math:`\\sum (O - E)^2 / E` 与自由度为 :math:`k - 1` "
"的卡方分布比较。只有一个组时 p 值为 1。"

msgid ""
"The quick binning gives a first ranking, not a final one: an IV from five quantile bins can miss "
"a pattern that other edges would show, and a categorical column with many rare labels gets an "
"inflated IV. The chi-squared test asks only whether the event rate differs between the groups: "
"with thousands of rows a weak relation already gives a p-value close to 0, so rank by ``iv`` and "
"read a large p-value as a column with no evidence of a relation. Weights from sampling rates "
"inflate the number of observations and make the p-value too small."
msgstr ""
"快速分箱只给出初步排序而非最终排序：五个等频箱的 IV 可能遗漏其他边界才能显示的规律，而含有许多稀有标签的类别列，IV "
"会被高估。卡方检验只回答各组的事件率是否不同：样本有数千行时，即使关系很弱，p 值也接近 0，因此请按 ``iv`` 排序，并把较大的 p "
"值理解为没有证据表明该列与目标有关。来自抽样比例的权重会放大观测数，使 p 值偏小。"

msgid "With a target, the event rates and the separation of each column:"
msgstr "有目标变量时，给出各列的事件率和区分能力："

msgid "Vintage and roll-rate analysis"
msgstr "Vintage 与滚动率分析"

msgid ""
"Analyse a loan panel as the loans age. :func:`~kivi.vintage.vintage_table` gives the cumulative "
"bad rate of each cohort by month on book, and :func:`~kivi.vintage.transition_matrix` and "
":func:`~kivi.vintage.roll_rates` show how loans move between delinquency buckets or grades."
msgstr ""
"随着贷款账龄增长分析贷款面板。 :func:`~kivi.vintage.vintage_table` 按账龄给出每个放款批次的累计坏账率， "
":func:`~kivi.vintage.transition_matrix` 和 :func:`~kivi.vintage.roll_rates` 展示贷款在逾期档位或等级之间的迁移。"

msgid "See :doc:`/user_guide/vintage` for examples on a synthetic loan panel."
msgstr "基于合成贷款面板的示例见 :doc:`/user_guide/vintage` 。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`vintage_table <kivi.vintage.vintage_table>`\\ \\(loan\\, cohort\\, month\\_on\\_book\\, "
"...\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`vintage_table <kivi.vintage.vintage_table>`\\ \\(loan\\, cohort\\, month\\_on\\_book\\, "
"...\\)"

msgid "Tabulate the cumulative bad rate of each cohort by month on book."
msgstr "按账龄列出每个批次的累计坏账率。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`transition_matrix <kivi.vintage.transition_matrix>`\\ \\(before\\, after\\, \\*\\[\\, "
"...\\]\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`transition_matrix <kivi.vintage.transition_matrix>`\\ \\(before\\, after\\, \\*\\[\\, "
"...\\]\\)"

msgid "Count the movements of entities between two states."
msgstr "统计对象在两个状态之间的迁移次数。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`roll_rates <kivi.vintage.roll_rates>`\\ \\(before\\, after\\, \\*\\[\\, states\\, "
"weights\\]\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`roll_rates <kivi.vintage.roll_rates>`\\ \\(before\\, after\\, \\*\\[\\, states\\, "
"weights\\]\\)"

msgid "Compute the share of each state's entities that rolled to the next state."
msgstr "计算每个状态中滚动到下一状态的对象所占的比例。"

msgid ""
"A vintage table follows each cohort of loans, usually the loans originated in the same month, as "
"it ages. Its entry for a cohort and a month on book is the share of the cohort's loans that were "
"bad at or before that month on book, so every row is non-decreasing."
msgstr "Vintage 表（账龄表）跟踪每个贷款批次（通常是同一个月发放的贷款）随账龄增长的表现。某个批次在某个账龄上的取值，是该批次贷款中在该账龄或更早时已变坏的比例，因此每一行都不会递减。"

msgid "**loan**"
msgstr "**loan**"

msgid ""
"Identifier of the loan of each row of the panel. A loan has at most one row per month on book, "
"and its rows need not be sorted."
msgstr "面板中每一行所属贷款的标识。每笔贷款在每个账龄最多有一行，各行无需排序。"

msgid "**cohort**"
msgstr "**cohort**"

msgid ""
"Cohort of each row, such as the month of origination. It must be the same on every row of a loan."
" Cohorts are sorted, and categorical cohorts follow the order of their categories."
msgstr "每一行的批次，例如放款月份。同一笔贷款的每一行批次必须相同。批次会被排序；分类型批次按其类别顺序排列。"

msgid "**month_on_book**"
msgstr "**month_on_book**"

msgid "Whole, non-negative number of months since origination of each row."
msgstr "每一行距放款的整月数，不能为负。"

msgid "**bad**"
msgstr "**bad**"

msgid ""
"Whether the loan is bad at that month on book, as booleans or 0 and 1. Pass the bad definition as"
" a condition on the status, such as ``status == \"90+\"``, or ``status >= \"60-89\"`` for an "
"ordered categorical."
msgstr ""
"该贷款在该账龄时是否为坏，取布尔值或 0 和 1。坏的定义以状态上的条件传入，例如 ``status == \"90+\"`` ；对于有序分类变量，也可以写成 ``status >= "
"\"60-89\"`` 。"

msgid ""
"Non-negative weight of each loan, such as the amount lent, repeated on every row of the loan. The"
" table then reports the share of the cohort's weight in loans that were bad, and cohorts whose "
"weights sum to zero are left out."
msgstr "每笔贷款的非负权重，例如放款金额，在该贷款的每一行重复给出。此时表中报告的是批次权重中属于坏贷款的比例，权重之和为零的批次会被排除。"

msgid ""
"Cumulative bad rates with one row per cohort and one column per distinct month on book of the "
"panel. An entry is NaN outside the months on book at which the cohort is observed, from the "
"smallest to the largest month on book of its rows."
msgstr "累计坏账率：每个批次一行，面板中每个不同的账龄一列。在批次被观测的账龄范围（从其各行中最小的账龄到最大的账龄）之外，取值为 NaN。"

msgid ""
"If the inputs are empty, not one-dimensional or of different lengths, or Series with different "
"indices. Also if `loan` or `cohort` has a missing value, a loan has more than one cohort or more "
"than one row for a month on book, `month_on_book` has a value that is not a whole, non-negative "
"number, `bad` has a value other than 0 and 1, or `weights` is not valid or differs between the "
"rows of a loan."
msgstr ""
"如果输入为空、不是一维的或长度不同，或者是索引不同的 Series。此外，如果 `loan` 或 `cohort` 含有缺失值，某笔贷款属于多个批次或在同一账龄有多行， "
"`month_on_book` 含有不是非负整数的值， `bad` 含有 0 和 1 以外的值，或 `weights` 无效或在同一贷款的各行之间不一致，也会抛出此异常。"

msgid ":obj:`transition_matrix`"
msgstr ":obj:`transition_matrix`"

msgid "Movements between states from one month to another."
msgstr "从一个月到另一个月在各状态之间的迁移。"

msgid ":obj:`roll_rates`"
msgstr ":obj:`roll_rates`"

msgid "Share of each delinquency bucket that rolls to the next."
msgstr "每个逾期档位滚动到下一档位的比例。"

msgid ":obj:`kivi.datasets.make_loan_panel`"
msgstr ":obj:`kivi.datasets.make_loan_panel`"

msgid "Synthetic loan panel to try this on."
msgstr "可用于试用此函数的合成贷款面板。"

msgid ""
"Let :math:`L_c` be the loans of cohort :math:`c`, :math:`\\tau_i` the first month on book at "
"which loan :math:`i` is bad (infinite if it never is) and :math:`w_i` its weight, 1 without "
"`weights`. The entry for month on book :math:`k` is"
msgstr ""
"设 :math:`L_c` 为批次 :math:`c` 的贷款， :math:`\\tau_i` 为贷款 :math:`i` 首次为坏的账龄（从未变坏时为无穷大）， :math:`w_i` "
"为其权重（不传 `weights` 时为 1）。账龄 :math:`k` 处的取值为"

msgid ""
"V_{c,k} = \\frac{\\sum_{i \\in L_c} w_i \\, [\\tau_i \\le k]}\n"
"               {\\sum_{i \\in L_c} w_i}."
msgstr ""
"V_{c,k} = \\frac{\\sum_{i \\in L_c} w_i \\, [\\tau_i \\le k]}\n"
"               {\\sum_{i \\in L_c} w_i}."

msgid ""
"The denominator includes every loan of the cohort, also loans that left the panel early, for "
"example because they were repaid; such a loan counts as bad only if it was bad before it left. A "
"loan that is bad once stays counted as bad, even if it later cures."
msgstr "分母包括批次中的每一笔贷款，也包括提前离开面板的贷款（例如已经还清）；这类贷款只有在离开前变坏过才算作坏。贷款一旦变坏，即使之后回到正常，也一直算作坏。"

msgid ""
"A cohort is observed from the smallest to the largest month on book of its rows, and its entries "
"outside that range are NaN, not 0. Later months on book are missing because the cohort is too "
"young to show whether its loans will go bad, and earlier ones because the panel starts after the "
"cohort was originated. Loans that were bad only before the panel starts are not counted, so start"
" the panel at origination where possible. Comparing the cohorts at the same month on book "
"compares them at the same age, which separates a change in the quality of new lending from the "
"seasoning of the portfolio."
msgstr ""
"批次的观测范围从其各行中最小的账龄到最大的账龄，范围之外的取值为 NaN 而不是 "
"0。之后的账龄缺失，是因为该批次的账龄还太短，看不出其贷款是否会变坏；之前的账龄缺失，是因为面板在该批次发放之后才开始。只在面板开始之前变坏过的贷款不会被计入，因此应尽量让面板从放款时开始。在相同账龄上比较各批次，就是在相同的“年龄”上比较它们，从而把新增放款质量的变化与资产组合的账龄成熟效应区分开。"

msgid ""
"Two cases need care. If every loan of a cohort leaves the panel before it ends, for example "
"because all of them were repaid, the cohort's last entry is final, yet its later months on book "
"are NaN; to fill them, keep a row for each month end after a loan left, with a status that is not"
" bad, such as ``\"closed\"``. And a cohort that spans several origination months, such as a "
"quarter, mixes loans of different ages: at its largest months on book, its youngest loans count "
"in the denominator although they have not been observed that long, which biases those entries "
"down. Monthly cohorts avoid this."
msgstr ""
"有两种情况需要注意。如果某个批次的所有贷款都在面板结束前离开（例如全部已经还清），该批次的最后一个取值已是最终结果，但其之后的账龄仍为 "
"NaN；要补齐这些取值，可以在贷款离开后的每个月末保留一行，状态设为不算坏的值，例如 ``\"closed\"`` "
"。另外，跨越多个放款月的批次（例如按季度划分的批次）混合了不同账龄的贷款：在其最大的几个账龄上，最年轻的贷款虽然还没有被观测到这么久，却计入了分母，使这些取值偏低。按月划分批次可以避免这一问题。"

msgid ""
"Loan 1 cured after month on book 2 but stays counted as bad, and the 2024-02 cohort has not "
"reached month on book 3."
msgstr "贷款 1 在账龄 2 之后回到正常，但仍算作坏；2024-02 批次尚未达到账龄 3。"

msgid ""
"Each entity, such as a loan or an obligor, is observed in one state before and one state after, "
"for example its delinquency bucket at two consecutive month ends or its rating grade at two "
"annual reviews. Row :math:`i`, column :math:`j` counts the entities that moved from state "
":math:`i` to state :math:`j`. With `normalize`, each row holds the shares of the states after, "
"the migration matrix of a rating system."
msgstr ""
"每个对象（例如一笔贷款或一位债务人）先后各在一个状态上被观测，例如相邻两个月末的逾期档位，或两次年度复评时的评级。第 :math:`i` 行、第 :math:`j` 列统计从状态 "
":math:`i` 迁移到状态 :math:`j` 的对象数。设置 `normalize` 后，每一行给出之后各状态所占的比例，即评级体系的转移矩阵。"

msgid "**before, after**"
msgstr "**before, after**"

msgid ""
"State of each entity at the first and at the second observation. If both are Series, they must "
"have identical indices; otherwise they are matched by position. Neither may contain missing "
"values: drop the entities that were not observed twice, or give the entities that left a state "
"such as ``\"closed\"``."
msgstr ""
"每个对象在第一次和第二次观测时的状态。如果二者都是 Series，索引必须完全相同；否则按位置对应。二者都不能含有缺失值：请删除没有被观测两次的对象，或给已离开的对象一个单独的状态，例如 "
"``\"closed\"`` 。"

msgid "**states**"
msgstr "**states**"

msgid ""
"All states in order, for delinquency buckets and rating grades from the best to the worst. States"
" without entities still get a row and a column. By default, the categories of categorical inputs,"
" which must then be the same for both, or else the sorted distinct values. Sorting puts labels "
"such as ``\"current\"`` after ``\"90+\"``, so pass `states` or ordered categoricals for "
"delinquency buckets. A state must not be missing."
msgstr ""
"按顺序排列的全部状态；对于逾期档位和评级，从最好到最差排列。没有对象的状态仍会占一行一列。默认取分类型输入的类别（此时两个输入的类别必须相同），否则取排序后的不同取值。排序会把 "
"``\"current\"`` 这样的标签排在 ``\"90+\"`` 之后，因此对于逾期档位，请传入 `states` 或使用有序分类变量。状态不能为缺失值。"

msgid ""
"If True, divide each row by its total, so that it holds the shares of the state's entities that "
"moved to each state. A row without entities is then NaN."
msgstr "如果为 True，每一行除以该行合计，使其给出该状态的对象迁移到各状态的比例。此时没有对象的行为 NaN。"

msgid ""
"Non-negative weight of each entity, such as its balance at the first observation, matched like "
"`after`. The counts are then sums of weights."
msgstr "每个对象的非负权重，例如第一次观测时的余额，对应方式与 `after` 相同。此时计数为权重之和。"

msgid ""
"One row per state before and one column per state after, in the order of `states`. Without "
"`weights` and `normalize`, the entries are integer counts."
msgstr "之前的每个状态一行，之后的每个状态一列，按 `states` 的顺序排列。不传 `weights` 且不设置 `normalize` 时，取值为整数计数。"

msgid ""
"If the inputs are empty, not one-dimensional, of different lengths or Series with different "
"indices, have a missing value or a value that is not one of `states`, or `weights` is not valid. "
"Also if `states` is not one-dimensional or has duplicates or missing values, or is not given "
"while `before` and `after` are categoricals with different categories, or if `normalize` is not a"
" boolean."
msgstr ""
"如果输入为空、不是一维的、长度不同或是索引不同的 Series，含有缺失值或不属于 `states` 的值，或 `weights` 无效。此外，如果 `states` "
"不是一维的、有重复值或缺失值，或者未给出 `states` 而 `before` 和 `after` 是类别不同的分类变量，或者 `normalize` 不是布尔值，也会抛出此异常。"

msgid "Share of each state that moved to the next worse state."
msgstr "每个状态中迁移到下一个更差状态的比例。"

msgid ":obj:`vintage_table`"
msgstr ":obj:`vintage_table`"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "With :math:`n_{ij}` entities moving from state :math:`i` to state :math:`j`, the normalized entry"
msgstr "设有 :math:`n_{ij}` 个对象从状态 :math:`i` 迁移到状态 :math:`j` ，则归一化后的取值"

msgid "p_{ij} = \\frac{n_{ij}}{\\sum_k n_{ik}}"
msgstr "p_{ij} = \\frac{n_{ij}}{\\sum_k n_{ik}}"

msgid ""
"estimates the probability of moving to :math:`j` from :math:`i`. If the movements follow a time-"
"homogeneous Markov chain, the :math:`h`-th power of the normalized matrix gives the probabilities"
" over :math:`h` periods."
msgstr "估计了从 :math:`i` 迁移到 :math:`j` 的概率。如果迁移服从时齐马尔可夫链，归一化矩阵的 :math:`h` 次幂给出 :math:`h` 期内的迁移概率。"

msgid ""
"Roll rates summarize the movements of delinquency between two month ends: the roll rate of "
"``30-59`` days past due is the share of the loans at 30 to 59 days that are at 60 to 89 days a "
"month later. The states must be ordered from the best to the worst, so that the next state is the"
" next worse one."
msgstr ""
"滚动率概括了两个月末之间逾期状态的变化：逾期 ``30-59`` 天的滚动率，是逾期 30 到 59 天的贷款中一个月后逾期 60 到 89 "
"天的比例。状态必须从最好到最差排列，这样下一个状态就是更差的一档。"

msgid ""
"State of each entity at the first and at the second observation, as in `transition_matrix`. "
"Neither may contain missing values."
msgstr "每个对象在第一次和第二次观测时的状态，与 `transition_matrix` 相同。二者都不能含有缺失值。"

msgid ""
"All states from the best to the worst. Required unless `before` and `after` are ordered "
"categoricals with the same categories, whose order is then used. A sorted order would be wrong "
"for most labels, for example ``\"current\"`` would come after ``\"90+\"``."
msgstr ""
"从最好到最差排列的全部状态。除非 `before` 和 `after` 是类别相同的有序分类变量（此时使用其类别顺序），否则必须传入。对大多数标签来说，排序得到的顺序是错误的，例如 "
"``\"current\"`` 会排在 ``\"90+\"`` 之后。"

msgid ""
"Non-negative weight of each entity, such as its balance at the first observation, matched like "
"`after`. The rates are then shares of weight, the balance roll rates."
msgstr "每个对象的非负权重，例如第一次观测时的余额，对应方式与 `after` 相同。此时滚动率是权重的比例，即余额滚动率。"

msgid ""
"Roll rate of every state except the worst, which has no next state, indexed by the state. A state"
" without entities has a NaN rate."
msgstr "除最差状态（没有下一个状态）外每个状态的滚动率，以状态为索引。没有对象的状态，其滚动率为 NaN。"

msgid ""
"In the same cases as `transition_matrix`, and if `states` is not given while `before` and `after`"
" are not ordered categoricals."
msgstr "与 `transition_matrix` 在相同的情况下抛出；此外，如果未给出 `states` 而 `before` 和 `after` 不是有序分类变量，也会抛出。"

msgid "The movements between all pairs of states."
msgstr "所有状态两两之间的迁移。"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"With :math:`n_{ij}` entities moving from state :math:`i` to state :math:`j`, the roll rate of "
"state :math:`i` is"
msgstr "设有 :math:`n_{ij}` 个对象从状态 :math:`i` 迁移到状态 :math:`j` ，则状态 :math:`i` 的滚动率为"

msgid "r_i = \\frac{n_{i,i+1}}{\\sum_k n_{ik}}."
msgstr "r_i = \\frac{n_{i,i+1}}{\\sum_k n_{ik}}."

msgid ""
"Entities that improved, stayed or moved more than one state worse count in the denominator only. "
"A loan can fall at most one delinquency bucket further behind from one month end to the next, so "
"the product of the roll rates estimates the share of current loans that reach the worst bucket "
"after one month per roll, if the movements follow a Markov chain."
msgstr "状态改善、保持不变或恶化超过一档的对象只计入分母。从一个月末到下一个月末，贷款最多再恶化一个逾期档位，因此如果迁移服从马尔可夫链，各滚动率的乘积估计了正常贷款在经过与滚动次数相同的月数后处于最差档位的比例。"

msgid "Weight of evidence and information value"
msgstr "证据权重与信息值"

msgid ""
"Measure how each group of a variable separates a binary target, and encode groups with the "
"result. :func:`~kivi.woe.woe_table` gives the WOE and IV of each group and "
":func:`~kivi.woe.woe_transform` encodes new data with them; :func:`~kivi.woe.woe` and "
":func:`~kivi.woe.iv` compute the same measures from aggregated counts."
msgstr ""
"衡量变量的每个分组区分二元目标变量的能力，并用结果对分组编码。 :func:`~kivi.woe.woe_table` 给出每组的 WOE 和 IV， "
":func:`~kivi.woe.woe_transform` 用它们对新数据编码； :func:`~kivi.woe.woe` 和 :func:`~kivi.woe.iv` "
"根据汇总计数计算同样的指标。"

msgid "See :doc:`/user_guide/woe_iv` for the definitions, examples and how to read the result."
msgstr "定义、示例以及如何解读结果，见 :doc:`/user_guide/woe_iv` 。"

msgid ":py:obj:`woe_table <kivi.woe.woe_table>`\\ \\(groups\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, smoothing\\, ...\\]\\)"
msgstr ":py:obj:`woe_table <kivi.woe.woe_table>`\\ \\(groups\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, smoothing\\, ...\\]\\)"

msgid "Compute weight of evidence and information value for observed groups."
msgstr "按观察到的分组计算证据权重（WOE）和信息值（IV）。"

msgid ":py:obj:`woe_transform <kivi.woe.woe_transform>`\\ \\(groups\\, table\\, \\*\\[\\, unseen\\]\\)"
msgstr ":py:obj:`woe_transform <kivi.woe.woe_transform>`\\ \\(groups\\, table\\, \\*\\[\\, unseen\\]\\)"

msgid "Replace each group with its weight of evidence."
msgstr "将每个分组替换为其证据权重（WOE）。"

msgid ":py:obj:`woe <kivi.woe.woe>`\\ \\(event\\_counts\\, non\\_event\\_counts\\, \\*\\[\\, ...\\]\\)"
msgstr ":py:obj:`woe <kivi.woe.woe>`\\ \\(event\\_counts\\, non\\_event\\_counts\\, \\*\\[\\, ...\\]\\)"

msgid "Compute the weight of evidence of each group from its counts."
msgstr "根据每组的计数计算其证据权重（WOE）。"

msgid ":py:obj:`iv <kivi.woe.iv>`\\ \\(event\\_counts\\, non\\_event\\_counts\\, \\*\\[\\, ...\\]\\)"
msgstr ":py:obj:`iv <kivi.woe.iv>`\\ \\(event\\_counts\\, non\\_event\\_counts\\, \\*\\[\\, ...\\]\\)"

msgid "Compute the information value from counts per group."
msgstr "根据每组的计数计算信息值（IV）。"

msgid ""
"Each group's share of events is compared with its share of non-events. Sum the ``iv`` column for "
"the information value of the variable."
msgstr "比较每组在全部事件中的占比与在全部非事件中的占比。将 ``iv`` 列求和即得到该变量的信息值。"

msgid "Pre-binned values or category labels. Missing values form a group."
msgstr "已分箱的数值或类别标签。缺失值独立成组。"

msgid ""
"Binary labels, with 1 indicating the event. If `groups` and `target` are both pandas Series, they"
" must have identical indices; otherwise they are matched by position."
msgstr "二分类标签，1 表示事件。如果 `groups` 和 `target` 都是 pandas Series，二者的索引必须完全相同；否则按位置对应。"

msgid ""
"Non-negative weight of each observation, for example the inverse of its sampling rate, matched "
"like `target`. The counts are then sums of weights, and groups whose weights sum to zero are left"
" out, so `woe_transform` treats them as unseen. `smoothing` is then in units of weight: scale the"
" weights to sum to the number of observations, or scale `smoothing` with them."
msgstr ""
"每个观测的非负权重，例如其抽样比例的倒数，对应方式与 `target` 相同。此时计数为权重之和，权重之和为零的组会被排除，因此 `woe_transform` 会把它们视为未见过的分组。此时 "
"`smoothing` 以权重为单位：请把权重缩放到总和等于观测数，或按相同比例缩放 `smoothing` 。"

msgid ""
"One row per group with the columns ``non_event``, ``event`` and ``total`` (counts), "
"``non_event_share`` and ``event_share`` (smoothed shares within each class), ``total_share`` "
"(share of all observations), ``event_rate``, ``woe`` and ``iv``. Sum the iv column for the "
"variable's information value."
msgstr ""
"每组一行，包含以下列： ``non_event`` 、 ``event`` 和 ``total`` （计数）， ``non_event_share`` 和 ``event_share`` "
"（各自类别内平滑后的占比）， ``total_share`` （占全部观测的比例）， ``event_rate`` 、 ``woe`` 和 ``iv`` 。将 iv 列求和即得到该变量的信息值。"

msgid ""
"If the inputs are not one-dimensional, their indices or lengths do not match, `target` does not "
"contain both 0 and 1 or has missing or other labels, or `smoothing` is not finite and positive. "
"Also if `weights` is not numeric, does not give each observation one finite, non-negative weight,"
" has an index other than that of `groups`, or leaves a class with a zero total."
msgstr ""
"如果输入不是一维、索引或长度不一致、 `target` 没有同时包含 0 和 1 或含有缺失值及其他标签，或者 `smoothing` 不是有限正数。此外，如果 `weights` "
"不是数值、没有为每个观测给出一个有限非负的权重、索引与 `groups` 不同，或使事件或非事件的权重总和为零。"

msgid ":obj:`woe`, :obj:`iv`"
msgstr ":obj:`woe`, :obj:`iv`"

msgid "The same measures from counts per group."
msgstr "根据每组计数计算同样的指标。"

msgid "Fit edges for numeric variables."
msgstr "为数值变量拟合分箱边界。"

msgid "Compare the distribution of two samples."
msgstr "比较两个样本的分布。"

msgid ""
"For group :math:`i`, let :math:`p_i` and :math:`q_i` be its shares of all events and of all non-"
"events. Then"
msgstr "对第 :math:`i` 组，令 :math:`p_i` 和 :math:`q_i` 分别为其在全部事件和全部非事件中的占比。则"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\\mathrm{WOE}_i = \\ln \\frac{p_i}{q_i}, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathrm{IV}_i = (p_i - q_i)\\,\\mathrm{WOE}_i, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathrm{IV} = \\sum_i \\mathrm{IV}_i."
msgstr ""
"\\mathrm{WOE}_i = \\ln \\frac{p_i}{q_i}, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathrm{IV}_i = (p_i - q_i)\\,\\mathrm{WOE}_i, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathrm{IV} = \\sum_i \\mathrm{IV}_i."

msgid ""
"Each zero count is replaced with `smoothing` before the shares are normalized, so every WOE is "
"finite. The count columns, ``total_share`` and ``event_rate`` always use the observed counts."
msgstr ""
"在归一化占比之前，每个零计数都会被替换为 `smoothing`，因此每个 WOE 都是有限值。计数列、 ``total_share`` 和 ``event_rate`` "
"始终使用实际观测到的计数。"

msgid ""
"Categorical groups, such as the result of `kivi.binning.cut` or ``pandas.cut``, follow the order "
"of their categories with missing values last. Other groups follow the order in which they first "
"appear. Categories that are never observed are omitted."
msgstr "分类型的分组（例如 `kivi.binning.cut` 或 ``pandas.cut`` 的结果）按类别顺序排列，缺失值排在最后。其他分组按首次出现的次序排列。从未出现的类别不会列出。"

msgid "[R86ef760ac44f-1]_"
msgstr "[R86ef760ac44f-1]_"

msgid ""
"The WOE values come from a table fitted on the development sample, so a scorecard model sees the "
"same encoding in development, validation and production."
msgstr "WOE 取自在开发样本上拟合的表，因此评分卡模型在开发、验证和生产环境中看到的是同一套编码。"

msgid ""
"One-dimensional group labels formed in the same way as those passed to `woe_table`, for example "
"with the same edges and ``pandas.cut``."
msgstr "一维分组标签，划分方式须与传给 `woe_table` 的分组相同，例如使用同一组边界和 ``pandas.cut`` 。"

msgid "pandas.DataFrame or pandas.Series"
msgstr "pandas.DataFrame 或 pandas.Series"

msgid ""
"The result of `woe_table`, or a Series of WOE values indexed by group. A missing label in the "
"index gives the WOE of missing values."
msgstr "`woe_table` 的结果，或以分组为索引的 WOE 序列。索引中的缺失标签对应缺失值的 WOE。"

msgid "float or \"raise\", default \"raise\""
msgstr "float 或 \"raise\"，默认 \"raise\""

msgid ""
"Finite WOE for groups that are not in `table`, such as a new category, an interval without "
"development observations, or missing values when `table` has no missing group. By default such "
"groups raise an error."
msgstr "不在 `table` 中的分组所用的有限 WOE，例如新类别、开发样本中没有观测值的区间，或 `table` 没有缺失组时的缺失值。默认情况下，这类分组会引发错误。"

msgid ""
"Float WOE values in the order of `groups`. A Series input gives a Series with the same index and "
"name."
msgstr "按 `groups` 顺序排列的浮点 WOE 值。输入为 Series 时返回 Series，索引和名称保持不变。"

msgid ""
"If `groups` is not one-dimensional, `table` has no ``woe`` column or repeats a group, `unseen` is"
" neither ``\"raise\"`` nor a finite number, or `unseen` is ``\"raise\"`` and some groups are not "
"in `table`."
msgstr ""
"如果 `groups` 不是一维、 `table` 没有 ``woe`` 列或有重复的分组、 `unseen` 既不是 ``\"raise\"`` 也不是有限数值，或者 `unseen` 为 "
"``\"raise\"`` 而部分分组不在 `table` 中。"

msgid ":obj:`woe_table`"
msgstr ":obj:`woe_table`"

msgid "Fit the edges used to form numeric groups."
msgstr "拟合用于划分数值分组的边界。"

msgid ""
"Labels are matched by equality, so an interval from ``pandas.cut`` matches the interval with the "
"same edges in `table`, and a number matches only an equal label, never the interval that contains"
" it. Use the edges fitted on the development sample for every sample that is transformed."
msgstr ""
"标签按相等关系匹配，因此 ``pandas.cut`` 得到的区间会与 `table` "
"中边界相同的区间对应，而数字只与相等的标签对应，绝不会对应包含它的区间。对每个要转换的样本，都请使用在开发样本上拟合的边界。"

msgid ""
"Use this when the counts are already aggregated, for example from a database query or a report, "
"instead of one label per observation."
msgstr "适用于计数已经汇总的情况，例如来自数据库查询或报表，而不是每个观测一个标签。"

msgid "**event_counts, non_event_counts**"
msgstr "**event_counts, non_event_counts**"

msgid ""
"One-dimensional, non-negative counts of events and non-events in each group, in the same group "
"order. Two Series must have identical indices. Weighted counts need not be integers."
msgstr "每组事件和非事件的一维非负计数，两者的分组顺序须一致。两个 Series 的索引必须相同。加权计数不必是整数。"

msgid ""
"The WOE of each group. If a count argument is a Series, the result is a Series with its index, "
"named ``woe``; otherwise it is an array."
msgstr "每组的 WOE。如果某个计数参数是 Series，结果为具有其索引、名为 ``woe`` 的 Series；否则为数组。"

msgid ":obj:`iv`"
msgstr ":obj:`iv`"

msgid "The information value of the same counts."
msgstr "同一组计数的信息值。"

msgid "Counts, shares, WOE and IV from group labels and a target."
msgstr "根据分组标签和目标计算计数、占比、WOE 和 IV。"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"With :math:`p_i` and :math:`q_i` the smoothed shares of group :math:`i` among all events and all "
"non-events, :math:`\\mathrm{WOE}_i = \\ln(p_i / q_i)`, as in the ``woe`` column of `woe_table`."
msgstr ""
"记 :math:`p_i` 和 :math:`q_i` 为第 :math:`i` 组在全部事件和全部非事件中平滑后的占比，则 :math:`\\mathrm{WOE}_i = \\ln(p_i "
"/ q_i)` ，与 `woe_table` 的 ``woe`` 列一致。"

msgid ""
"The information value summarizes how well the groups separate events from non-events, from counts"
" that are already aggregated."
msgstr "信息值概括了各组区分事件与非事件的能力，这里直接根据已汇总的计数计算。"

msgid "The information value of the variable."
msgstr "该变量的信息值。"

msgid ":obj:`woe`"
msgstr ":obj:`woe`"

msgid "The weight of evidence of each group."
msgstr "每组的证据权重。"

msgid "The IV contribution of each group from labels and a target."
msgstr "根据标签和目标计算每组的 IV 贡献。"

msgid ":obj:`kivi.stability.psi`"
msgstr ":obj:`kivi.stability.psi`"

msgid "The same divergence between two samples."
msgstr "两个样本之间的同一种散度。"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "\\mathrm{IV} = \\sum_i (p_i - q_i) \\ln \\frac{p_i}{q_i},"
msgstr "\\mathrm{IV} = \\sum_i (p_i - q_i) \\ln \\frac{p_i}{q_i},"

msgid "which equals the sum of the ``iv`` column of `woe_table` for the same groups."
msgstr "它等于相同分组下 `woe_table` 中 ``iv`` 列之和。"

msgid "Writing documentation"
msgstr "编写文档"

msgid ""
"The English and the simplified Chinese editions are built from the same pages and docstrings. "
"This page describes how they are organized and written. :doc:`index` covers the checks that every"
" pull request runs."
msgstr "英文版和简体中文版由同一套页面和 docstring 构建。本页说明文档的组织方式和写法；每个拉取请求都要运行的检查见 :doc:`index` 。"

msgid "Kinds of pages"
msgstr "页面类型"

msgid ""
"Apart from the home page and the index page of each section, every page is one of five kinds, and"
" its kind decides what it contains."
msgstr "除首页和各部分的目录页外，每个页面都属于下列五种类型之一，类型决定了页面的内容。"

msgid "Kind"
msgstr "类型"

msgid "Pages"
msgstr "页面"

msgid "Contents"
msgstr "内容"

msgid "Tutorial"
msgstr "教程"

msgid ""
"The pages of the getting started section and of the tutorial section, and "
":doc:`/user_guide/risk_workflow`"
msgstr "快速开始部分和教程部分的各个页面，以及 :doc:`/user_guide/risk_workflow`"

msgid ""
"The installation, and worked examples on the bundled data from start to finish. They link to the "
"topic guides for the details instead of repeating them."
msgstr "安装说明，以及用随包数据从头到尾完成的示例。细节链接到对应的主题指南，不在教程里重复。"

msgid "Topic guide"
msgstr "主题指南"

msgid "The other pages of the user guide"
msgstr "用户指南的其余页面"

msgid ""
"One step of a risk model: what it measures, an example and how to read the result. "
":doc:`/user_guide/datasets` describes the example data in the same way."
msgstr "风控模型中的一个步骤：它衡量什么、一个示例，以及如何解读结果。 :doc:`/user_guide/datasets` 以同样的方式介绍示例数据。"

msgid "Reference"
msgstr "参考"

msgid "The pages of the API reference"
msgstr "API 参考的各个页面"

msgid ""
":doc:`/api/conventions`, the rules that every function follows; :doc:`/api/compatibility`, what a"
" release may change; :doc:`/api/glossary`, the terms of the guides; and one page per public "
"module, generated from its docstrings."
msgstr ""
":doc:`/api/conventions` ，即所有函数共同遵守的规则； :doc:`/api/compatibility` ，即一个版本可以改变什么； "
":doc:`/api/glossary` ，即各篇指南所用的术语；以及每个公共模块一页，由模块的 docstring 生成。"

msgid "Release notes"
msgstr "版本说明"

msgid ":doc:`/release/index` and :doc:`/release/migration`"
msgstr ":doc:`/release/index` 和 :doc:`/release/migration`"

msgid ""
"What changed in each version, and how to move code from 0.9 to 1.0 and from the 0.2.x classes to "
"their replacements. The notes of a released version are not edited. The migration guide is "
"revised whenever a release changes what it describes."
msgstr "每个版本的变化，以及如何把代码从 0.9 迁移到 1.0、把使用 0.2.x 类的代码迁移到替代接口。已发布版本的说明不再修改；当某个版本改变了迁移指南所描述的内容时，迁移指南随之修订。"

msgid "Contributor guide"
msgstr "贡献者指南"

msgid "The pages of this section"
msgstr "本节的各个页面"

msgid ""
"How to work on kivi. :doc:`legacy_review` records the review of the 0.2.x code that preceded the "
"rewrite."
msgstr "如何参与 kivi 的开发。 :doc:`legacy_review` 记录重写之前对 0.2.x 代码的评审。"

msgid "Where pages live"
msgstr "页面位置"

msgid ""
"A public module ``kivi.<module>`` has an API page ``docs/api/<module>.rst`` and usually a topic "
"guide ``docs/user_guide/<topic>.rst``. The toctrees of the API reference and of the user guide "
"list their pages in the order of a project and end with a glob, so a new page appears at the end "
"without editing them. The integration moves it to its place, as Entry points below describes."
msgstr ""
"公共模块 ``kivi.<module>`` 有一个 API 页面 ``docs/api/<module>.rst`` ，通常还有一个主题指南 "
"``docs/user_guide/<topic>.rst`` 。API 参考和用户指南的 toctree "
"按项目顺序列出各页，并以通配符结尾，所以新页面无需修改它们就会出现在末尾。集成时再把它移到应有的位置，详见下文“入口页面”。"

msgid ""
"The tutorial section, ``docs/tutorial``, follows one project over several chapters, listed in the"
" order of the project by the toctree of its index page. Each chapter starts with a collapsed "
"``dropdown`` that repeats the code of the earlier chapters that it needs, so that the page runs "
"on its own. Results that only simulated data can give, such as the outcomes of rejected "
"applicants, go in an ``admonition`` titled ``Simulation check`` with the class ``kivi-check``, "
"and the steps of the project never depend on them."
msgstr ""
"教程部分 ``docs/tutorial`` 用多个章节完整跟踪一个项目，各章节由其索引页的 toctree 按项目顺序列出。每章开头有一个折叠的 ``dropdown`` "
"，重复该页需要的前面各章的代码，使每页都能单独运行。只有模拟数据才能给出的结果，例如被拒绝申请人的结果，放在标题为 ``Simulation check`` 、类为 ``kivi-check``"
" 的 ``admonition`` 中，项目的各个步骤从不依赖它们。"

msgid ""
"The conventions, the compatibility promises and the glossary are ``docs/api/conventions.rst``, "
"``docs/api/compatibility.rst`` and ``docs/api/glossary.rst``. They come first in the API "
"reference, and the index of the user guide links to the conventions and the glossary."
msgstr ""
"约定、兼容性承诺和术语表分别是 ``docs/api/conventions.rst`` 、 ``docs/api/compatibility.rst`` 和 "
"``docs/api/glossary.rst`` 。它们排在 API 参考的最前面，用户指南目录页链接到约定和术语表。"

msgid ""
"Page names are part of the URLs, and the language switch links each page to the page of the same "
"name in the other edition. Change the title of a page rather than renaming or removing it."
msgstr "页面名是 URL 的一部分，语言切换也会把每个页面链接到另一种语言中同名的页面。需要调整时改页面标题，不要重命名或删除页面。"

msgid ""
"The API page of a module and its topic guide have the same title. Its cards and its rows in the "
"README use that title or a short form of it, such as WOE and IV."
msgstr "同一个模块的 API 页面和主题指南使用同一个标题。它的卡片和 README 中的行使用这个标题或其简称，例如 WOE 与 IV。"

msgid "Topic guides"
msgstr "主题指南"

msgid ""
"A topic guide follows the order of an analysis, so that readers can stop as soon as they have "
"what they need. Its sections come in the order of the table below, with the titles that the table"
" gives in inline code:"
msgstr "主题指南按分析的顺序组织，读者找到所需内容即可停下。各节按下表的顺序排列，表中以行内代码给出的是各节的固定标题："

msgid "Section"
msgstr "节"

msgid "Opening, without a heading"
msgstr "开篇，不加标题"

msgid ""
"The question that the step answers and where it sits in a risk model, with links to the guides of"
" the steps before and after it in the order of the user guide. The public functions that the page"
" covers, each linked to its API entry. The opening has no examples."
msgstr "这一步回答什么问题，在风控模型中处于什么位置，并按用户指南的顺序链接到前后步骤的指南。本页涉及的公共函数，每个都链接到其 API 条目。开篇不含示例。"

msgid "``Definition``"
msgstr "``Definition`` （定义）"

msgid ""
"The measure and its formula in a math block, before any example. Title it ``Definitions`` when it"
" defines several measures, and leave it out when each tool of the page is defined in its own "
"section."
msgstr "指标及其公式（放在 math 块中），位于所有示例之前。定义多个指标时标题用 ``Definitions`` ；如果页面上的每个工具都在各自的小节中定义，则省略本节。"

msgid "``A worked example``"
msgstr "``A worked example`` （计算示例）"

msgid "A few values that readers can check by hand, right after the definition."
msgstr "读者可以手工验算的几个数值，紧接在定义之后。"

msgid "Body sections"
msgstr "正文各节"

msgid ""
"One section for each task, tool or question of the step, in the order of a project, with an "
"example on the bundled data and how to read its result. Title a body section with a noun phrase, "
"such as ``Gains table``, or a gerund phrase, such as ``Choosing a cut-off``; imperative titles "
"are for the steps of a tutorial. A body section may have subsections."
msgstr ""
"这一步的每个任务、工具或问题各占一节，按项目的顺序排列，并给出基于内置数据的示例以及如何解读其结果。正文小节的标题用名词短语，例如 ``Gains table`` ，或动名词短语，例如 "
"``Choosing a cut-off`` ；祈使句式的标题留给教程的步骤。正文小节可以再分子节。"

msgid "``Reading the result``"
msgstr "``Reading the result`` （解读结果）"

msgid ""
"A table of the columns of the page's main result, the direction of the measure, its usual "
"thresholds and what to check next. It follows the body sections whose examples print that result "
"and comes before the body sections about other tools. On a page whose tools each return their own"
" table, each body section describes its table instead."
msgstr "页面主要结果各列的表格、指标的方向、常用阈值以及下一步要检查什么。它位于打印该结果的正文小节之后、介绍其他工具的正文小节之前。如果页面上的每个工具各自返回一张表，则由各正文小节分别说明自己的表。"

msgid "``Special values``"
msgstr "``Special values`` （特殊值）"

msgid ""
"How codes such as ``-1`` for \"not applicable\" are passed in ``special``, and which group they "
"end up in."
msgstr "如何把表示“不适用”的 ``-1`` 等编码传入 ``special`` ，以及它们最终落入哪个分组。"

msgid "``Missing values``"
msgstr "``Missing values`` （缺失值）"

msgid "How missing values are counted, grouped or rejected."
msgstr "缺失值如何计数、分组或被拒绝。"

msgid "``Sample weights``"
msgstr "``Sample weights`` （样本权重）"

msgid ""
"What ``weights`` changes and what it leaves unchanged, and where weighted results differ from "
"repeated rows."
msgstr "``weights`` 改变什么、不改变什么，以及加权结果在哪些地方与重复行的结果不同。"

msgid "``Limits``"
msgstr "``Limits`` （局限）"

msgid "What the method cannot tell, and what kivi leaves out."
msgstr "方法无法说明什么，以及 kivi 没有实现什么。"

msgid "``Errors and warnings``"
msgstr "``Errors and warnings`` （错误与警告）"

msgid "The errors and warnings that readers are likely to meet, and how to resolve them."
msgstr "读者可能遇到的错误和警告，以及解决方法。"

msgid ""
"Leave out the sections that do not apply, but keep the order and the titles of the others, so "
"that the guides read alike. A variant that one or two sentences explain can stay in the body "
"section that it belongs to, and an error that belongs to one task can be shown where that task "
"is; a section of its own is for a variant or error that needs an example."
msgstr "不适用的小节可以省略，但其余小节要保持顺序和标题不变，让各篇指南读起来一致。一两句话就能说明的变体可以留在它所属的正文小节中，只属于某个任务的错误也可以在该任务处展示；需要示例的变体或错误才单独成节。"

msgid ""
"Section anchors are part of the URLs as well, and the READMEs link to some of them. Keep the "
"title of a section that a README links to, and keep a label when its section moves."
msgstr "小节锚点也是 URL 的一部分，README 会链接其中一些锚点。README 链接到的小节不要改标题；小节移动时要保留它的标签。"

msgid ""
"Examples are doctests, and the ``build`` check runs them. Their output is real: when a change "
"alters a printed table, run the code again and paste the new output instead of editing the "
"numbers."
msgstr "示例都是 doctest，由 ``build`` 检查运行。输出必须真实：改动影响了打印出的表格时，重新运行代码并粘贴新的输出，不要手工修改数字。"

msgid ""
"Examples use the data described in :doc:`/user_guide/datasets`, or a few values that readers can "
"check by hand. Random data comes from a generator with a fixed seed."
msgstr "示例使用 :doc:`/user_guide/datasets` 中介绍的数据，或者少量读者能手工验算的数值。随机数据由固定种子的生成器产生。"

msgid "Import each function from its module, as in ``from kivi.woe import woe_table``."
msgstr "每个函数都从其所在模块导入，例如 ``from kivi.woe import woe_table`` 。"

msgid ""
"Examples must not warn: a warning raised by a doctest, or by a chart or diagram recipe in "
"docs/_plotting.py, docs/_diagrams.py or docs/_tutorial.py, fails the build. When an example is "
"about a warning, catch it with ``warnings.catch_warnings(record=True)`` and print the message."
msgstr ""
"示例不能产生警告：doctest，或 docs/_plotting.py、docs/_diagrams.py 与 docs/_tutorial.py "
"中的图表和示意图函数一旦发出警告，构建就会失败。如果示例要演示某个警告，请用 ``warnings.catch_warnings(record=True)`` 捕获它并打印警告信息。"

msgid ""
"All the examples of a page share one namespace, so a section can use what an earlier section "
"defined. When sections move, check that every name is still defined before it is used."
msgstr "同一页面的所有示例共享一个命名空间，因此后面的小节可以使用前面小节定义的名称。移动小节时，请检查每个名称在使用之前仍有定义。"

msgid ""
"Charts and diagrams are drawn when the documentation is built. A ``plot`` directive calls a "
"``figure_*`` function, which recomputes the example shown just above it, so change the two "
"together:"
msgstr "图表和示意图在构建文档时绘制。 ``plot`` 指令调用一个 ``figure_*`` 函数，该函数重新计算紧挨在它上方的示例，所以两者要一起修改："

msgid ""
"A chart, from ``docs/_plotting.py`` and called as ``kp.figure_*()``, plots a result on the "
"bundled data, such as the WOE of each group or the vintage curves."
msgstr "图表来自 ``docs/_plotting.py`` ，以 ``kp.figure_*()`` 调用，在随包数据上绘制某个结果，例如各组的 WOE 或账龄曲线。"

msgid ""
"A chart of the tutorial, from ``docs/_tutorial.py`` and called as ``kt.figure_*()``, rebuilds the"
" state of the project once and draws it with the functions of ``docs/_plotting.py``."
msgstr "教程的图表来自 ``docs/_tutorial.py`` ，以 ``kt.figure_*()`` 调用，先一次性重建项目的状态，再用 ``docs/_plotting.py`` 中的函数绘制。"

msgid ""
"A diagram, from ``docs/_diagrams.py`` and called as ``kd.figure_*()``, shows how a function "
"computes its result: the input rows, the call and the result table, with the numbers that kivi "
"returns. A topic guide shows its main computation in a diagram right after the worked example, or"
" after the first example of the body section that the computation belongs to."
msgstr ""
"示意图来自 ``docs/_diagrams.py`` ，以 ``kd.figure_*()`` 调用，展示函数如何计算结果：输入的行、调用和结果表，以及 kivi "
"返回的数值。主题指南把主要的计算画成示意图，紧接在计算示例之后，或放在该计算所属正文小节的第一个示例之后。"

msgid ""
"Text inside a chart or a diagram is limited to kivi's column and parameter names, data values and"
" formulas written with them, so that one image serves both editions. The caption explains the "
"image and the alternative text describes it; both are translated. A recipe that computes numbers "
"apart from the function it shows checks them against that function, so that a change of the "
"function fails the build instead of leaving the image out of date."
msgstr ""
"图表和示意图中的文字只使用 kivi "
"的列名、参数名、数据值以及由它们写成的公式，这样一张图可以同时用于两种语言。图注解释图的含义，替代文本描述图的内容，两者都会被翻译。如果绘图函数在所展示的函数之外另行计算数值，就要用该函数核对这些数值，这样函数一旦改变，构建就会失败，而不会留下过时的图。"

msgid "Every diagram gives a color the same meaning:"
msgstr "每张示意图中，同一种颜色含义相同："

msgid "Color"
msgstr "颜色"

msgid "Meaning"
msgstr "含义"

msgid "One tint per category, a blue ramp from light to dark for intervals, gray for missing values"
msgstr "每个类别一种浅色，区间用由浅到深的蓝色，缺失值用灰色"

msgid "Groups and bins, in the input and in the result"
msgstr "输入和结果中的组与分箱"

msgid "Red"
msgstr "红色"

msgid "Events, the rows with target 1"
msgstr "事件，即目标为 1 的行"

msgid "Amber"
msgstr "琥珀色"

msgid "The result that the diagram is about, and the edges and thresholds"
msgstr "示意图所讲的结果，以及边界和阈值"

msgid "Blue and teal"
msgstr "蓝色和青色"

msgid "The reference sample and the current sample"
msgstr "基准样本和当前样本"

msgid ""
"A pull request that adds a module describes the charts and diagrams for its page in its "
"description. They are added when the page is integrated, together with the entry points."
msgstr "新增模块的拉取请求在描述中说明其页面需要的图表和示意图。它们在集成该页面时与入口页面一起加入。"

msgid "Names and links"
msgstr "名称与链接"

msgid "Write argument and column names as inline code, such as ``special`` or ``event_rate``."
msgstr "参数名和列名写成行内代码，例如 ``special`` 或 ``event_rate`` 。"

msgid ""
"In the topic guides and the tutorials, link the first mention of a kivi function, class or module"
" in each section to its API entry. Use the ``:func:``, ``:class:``, ``:exc:``, ``:meth:`` and "
"``:mod:`` roles with the full name and a leading tilde, such as ``:func:`~kivi.woe.woe_table```, "
"so that only the name is shown. Keep the module in the text where it tells two functions apart, "
"as in ``:func:`kivi.binning.cut``` next to ``pandas.cut``. Later mentions in the same section "
"stay inline code."
msgstr ""
"在主题指南和教程中，kivi 的函数、类或模块在每一节第一次出现时链接到其 API 条目。使用 ``:func:`` 、 ``:class:`` 、 ``:exc:`` 、 ``:meth:``"
" 和 ``:mod:`` 角色及完整名称，并在前面加波浪号，例如 ``:func:`~kivi.woe.woe_table``` ，这样只显示名称。需要用模块区分两个函数时保留模块名，例如与 "
"``pandas.cut`` 并列时写 ``:func:`kivi.binning.cut``` 。同一节中后续出现的名称仍写成行内代码。"

msgid ""
"``woe``, ``iv``, ``psi``, ``ks`` and ``gini`` are the names of functions and of columns. Link "
"them only where they mean the function."
msgstr "``woe`` 、 ``iv`` 、 ``psi`` 、 ``ks`` 和 ``gini`` 既是函数名，也是列名。只有表示函数时才加链接。"

msgid "Names inside examples are code and are not linked."
msgstr "示例中的名称是代码，不加链接。"

msgid ""
"Link to another page with the ``:doc:`` role and to a section of another page with the ``:ref:`` "
"role. Give a section a label only when a link points to it."
msgstr "链接到其他页面用 ``:doc:`` 角色，链接到其他页面的某个小节用 ``:ref:`` 角色。只有当某个链接指向一个小节时，才给它加标签。"

msgid ""
":doc:`/api` lists the conventions, the compatibility page, the glossary and then the module pages"
" in the order of the user guide, and ends with a glob for the pages that are not integrated yet. "
"``api/datasets`` comes last through the glob, so that the glob always matches a page."
msgstr ""
":doc:`/api` 先列出约定、兼容性页面和术语表，再按用户指南的顺序列出各模块页面，最后以通配符收录尚未集成的页面。 ``api/datasets`` "
"通过通配符排在最后，从而保证通配符总能匹配到页面。"

msgid ""
"A module page starts with its title, a ``module`` directive, which gives ``:mod:`` links their "
"target, and an introduction: one or two sentences on what the module is for, with links to its "
"main functions, and a sentence that links to its topic guide. The entries follow. For example:"
msgstr ""
"模块页面依次包括：标题、 ``module`` 指令（为 ``:mod:`` "
"链接提供目标）以及简介。简介用一两句话说明模块的用途并链接其主要函数，再用一句话链接到对应的主题指南。之后是各条目。例如："

msgid ""
"The API page of a module documents every name in the module's ``__all__``: first in an "
"``autosummary`` table, then each with its own ``autofunction``, ``autoclass``, ``autoexception`` "
"or ``automethod`` entry, in the same order. ``python docs/build.py`` stops when a name has no "
"such entry."
msgstr ""
"模块的 API 页面要记录模块 ``__all__`` 中的每个名称：先列在 ``autosummary`` 表中，再按同样的顺序各自给出 ``autofunction`` 、 "
"``autoclass`` 、 ``autoexception`` 或 ``automethod`` 条目。某个名称没有这样的条目时， ``python docs/build.py`` 会停止。"

msgid ""
"Docstrings follow the numpydoc conventions and are validated with every check enabled, so a "
"missing section, such as See Also or Examples, fails the build. Their paragraphs are translated "
"like those of the pages."
msgstr "docstring 遵循 numpydoc 约定，并启用全部校验项，因此缺少某个小节（例如 See Also 或 Examples）会导致构建失败。docstring 的段落和页面一样需要翻译。"

msgid ""
":doc:`/api/conventions` holds the rules that every module follows, such as the order of the "
"arguments and the meaning of ``weights``. A guide or a docstring states a rule of its own module "
"and links to the conventions for the shared ones. :doc:`/api/glossary` defines each term once and"
" links to the guide that uses it."
msgstr ""
":doc:`/api/conventions` 收录所有模块共同遵守的规则，例如参数顺序和 ``weights`` 的含义。指南或 docstring "
"只说明本模块自己的规则，共同规则则链接到约定页面。 :doc:`/api/glossary` 对每个术语只定义一次，并链接到使用它的指南。"

msgid "Translations"
msgstr "翻译"

msgid ""
"The Chinese edition is generated from ``docs/locale/zh_CN/LC_MESSAGES/kivi.po``. Every paragraph "
"of the English pages and of the public docstrings is one entry in that file. ``python "
"docs/build.py`` stops when an entry is missing, fuzzy or no longer used."
msgstr ""
"中文版由 ``docs/locale/zh_CN/LC_MESSAGES/kivi.po`` 生成。英文页面和公共 docstring "
"中的每个段落都对应该文件中的一个条目。如果有条目缺失、标记为 fuzzy 或已不再使用，``python docs/build.py`` 会停止构建。"

msgid "After changing English text:"
msgstr "修改英文内容后："

msgid ""
"Run ``python docs/build.py --update-po``. New strings are added with an empty translation, and "
"changed strings keep their old translation marked as fuzzy."
msgstr "运行 ``python docs/build.py --update-po``。新字符串以空译文加入，已修改的字符串保留旧译文并标记为 fuzzy。"

msgid "Translate the empty entries, review the fuzzy ones and delete their ``#, fuzzy`` line."
msgstr "翻译空条目，复核 fuzzy 条目并删除其 ``#, fuzzy`` 行。"

msgid "Run ``python docs/build.py`` again."
msgstr "再次运行 ``python docs/build.py``。"

msgid ""
"In a translation, put a space or Chinese punctuation on both sides of inline markup such as "
"inline code and links, or the markup is not recognized. Translate each term as the catalog "
"already translates it, so that the edition keeps one vocabulary."
msgstr "翻译时，行内代码、链接等行内标记的两侧要留空格或使用中文标点，否则标记无法识别。每个术语沿用翻译目录中已有的译法，让中文版保持统一的用词。"

msgid ""
"A change that only replaces markup, such as inline code by a link, leaves the translations valid."
" Apply it to the source strings and to their translations in ``kivi.po`` before step 1, so that "
"the entries do not turn fuzzy."
msgstr "只替换标记的修改（例如把行内代码换成链接）不会使译文失效。请在第 1 步之前，把同样的修改应用到 ``kivi.po`` 的源字符串及其译文上，这样条目就不会变为 fuzzy。"

msgid "Entry points"
msgstr "入口页面"

msgid ""
"Some pages describe the library as a whole: ``README.md`` and ``README.zh-CN.md``, the home page,"
" the index of the user guide and :doc:`/user_guide/risk_workflow`. A pull request that adds a "
"module leaves them alone. They are updated together after a group of such pull requests has "
"merged, and that update rewrites them for the library as it now is instead of only appending to "
"them:"
msgstr ""
"有些页面描述整个库： ``README.md`` 和 ``README.zh-CN.md`` 、首页、用户指南目录页以及 :doc:`/user_guide/risk_workflow` "
"。新增模块的拉取请求不修改它们。它们在一批这样的拉取请求合并之后统一更新，而且这次更新要按库的现状重写，而不只是追加内容："

msgid "the title, the introduction and the steps on the home page;"
msgstr "首页的标题、简介和步骤；"

msgid "the cards on the home page and on the index of the user guide, and the order of the user guide;"
msgstr "首页和用户指南目录页上的卡片，以及用户指南的页面顺序；"

msgid "the order of the API reference;"
msgstr "API 参考的页面顺序；"

msgid "the links to the previous and the next step in the openings of the guides next to a new one;"
msgstr "新页面前后相邻的指南开篇中指向上一步和下一步的链接；"

msgid "the terms of :doc:`/api/glossary` and the rules of :doc:`/api/conventions` that a new module adds;"
msgstr "新模块需要加入 :doc:`/api/glossary` 的术语和 :doc:`/api/conventions` 的规则；"

msgid "the tables and the roadmap of both READMEs;"
msgstr "两份 README 中的表格和路线图；"

msgid "any sentence in :doc:`/release/migration` about functionality that is not ported yet."
msgstr ":doc:`/release/migration` 中关于尚未迁移功能的所有表述。"

msgid ""
"A pull request that adds a module lists in its description the glossary terms and the conventions"
" that it needs, as it does for its charts."
msgstr "新增模块的拉取请求要在描述中列出它所需的术语和约定，就像列出它的图表一样。"

msgid ""
"``python docs/build.py`` lists every public function that the API tables of the READMEs leave "
"out, and every user guide page without a card on the index of the user guide or a link in the "
"READMEs. ``python docs/build.py --release`` refuses to run until the list is empty."
msgstr ""
"``python docs/build.py`` 会列出 README 的 API 表格中遗漏的每个公共函数，以及每个在用户指南目录页上没有卡片、或在 README "
"中没有链接的用户指南页面。在这个列表清空之前， ``python docs/build.py --release`` 拒绝运行。"

msgid "Publishing the documentation"
msgstr "发布文档"

msgid ""
"The ``Documentation`` workflow on GitHub Actions runs the tests and builds both editions for "
"every pull request. On the master branch it also publishes docs/_build/html to the gh-pages "
"branch, which serves https://gchensy.github.io/kivi/."
msgstr ""
"GitHub Actions 上的 ``Documentation`` 工作流会对每个拉取请求运行测试并构建两种语言的文档。在 master 分支上，它还会把 docs/_build/html "
"发布到 gh-pages 分支，通过 https://gchensy.github.io/kivi/ 访问。"

msgid "Development"
msgstr "开发"

msgid ""
"This section is for contributors. This page sets up a checkout and describes the checks and the "
"rules for pull requests. :doc:`documentation` describes how the documentation is organized, "
"written and translated, and :doc:`releasing` how a version is published."
msgstr "本节面向贡献者。本页介绍如何准备本地仓库，以及检查项和拉取请求的规则。 :doc:`documentation` 介绍文档的组织、写法和翻译， :doc:`releasing` 介绍如何发布版本。"

msgid "Set up"
msgstr "环境准备"

msgid ""
"Clone the repository and install it in editable mode with the test, documentation and lint "
"dependencies, then install the pre-commit hook."
msgstr "克隆仓库，以可编辑模式安装，并同时安装测试、文档和代码检查依赖，然后安装 pre-commit 钩子。"

msgid "Build and verify"
msgstr "构建与验证"

msgid ""
"ruff checks the code against the rules in ``pyproject.toml`` and formats it. The pre-commit hook "
"runs it before every commit, and the ``build`` check runs it on every pull request. A second job "
"runs the tests with the oldest NumPy and pandas versions that kivi supports."
msgstr ""
"ruff 按 ``pyproject.toml`` 中的规则检查代码并统一格式。pre-commit 钩子会在每次提交前运行它， ``build`` 检查也会在每个 pull request "
"上运行它。另一个任务会用 kivi 支持的最低版本 NumPy 和 pandas 运行测试。"

msgid ""
"The doctest builder runs every example in these pages and in the docstrings. The HTML build "
"writes English and simplified Chinese editions under docs/_build/html. API signatures come from "
"the installed package."
msgstr "doctest 构建器会运行本文档页面和 docstring 中的全部示例。HTML 构建会在 docs/_build/html 下生成英文和简体中文两套文档。API 签名从已安装的包提取。"

msgid "Pull requests"
msgstr "拉取请求"

msgid ""
"Branch from the latest master and keep one topic per pull request. The master branch accepts "
"changes only through pull requests, and only after the ``build`` check of the ``Documentation`` "
"workflow has passed on a branch that is up to date with master. Every pull request is therefore "
"tested together with everything merged before it. To update a branch, merge master into it. "
"Merged branches are deleted automatically."
msgstr ""
"从最新的 master 创建分支，每个拉取请求只做一件事。master 分支只接受通过拉取请求合入的改动，而且分支必须已与 master 同步，并通过 ``Documentation`` "
"工作流的 ``build`` 检查。因此，每个拉取请求都会和此前已合并的全部改动一起测试。要更新分支，把 master 合并进来即可。合并后的分支会被自动删除。"

msgid ""
"Pull requests that edit the same files are merged one after the other rather than developed in "
"parallel. Two kinds of file change in almost every pull request and are set up so that they "
"rarely conflict:"
msgstr "修改相同文件的拉取请求应依次完成和合并，不要并行开发。有两类文件几乎每个拉取请求都会改动，它们的组织方式让冲突很少发生："

msgid ""
"Release notes. Describe each user-facing change as a bullet item in a new file "
"``docs/release/unreleased/<topic>.<category>.rst``, where the category is ``new``, ``changed``, "
"``fixed`` or ``removed``. Do not edit :doc:`/release/index` itself: the files appear there under "
"the Unreleased heading."
msgstr ""
"发布说明。在新文件 ``docs/release/unreleased/<topic>.<category>.rst`` 中，把每项面向用户的改动写成一个列表项，其中类别为 ``new`` 、 "
"``changed`` 、 ``fixed`` 或 ``removed`` 。不要直接编辑 :doc:`/release/index` ：这些文件会显示在其中的“未发布”标题下。"

msgid ""
"The translation catalog. When a merge or rebase stops on a conflict in ``kivi.po``, run ``python "
"docs/build.py --merge-po``. It keeps the translations of both sides and adds the strings that are"
" new after the merge. Translate those, then add the catalog to the commit."
msgstr ""
"翻译目录。合并或变基因 ``kivi.po`` 冲突而中止时，运行 ``python docs/build.py --merge-po`` "
"。它会保留双方的翻译，并加入合并后新出现的文本。翻译这些文本后，再把目录加入提交。"

msgid ""
"A pull request that adds a module therefore only adds files: the module, its tests, a user guide "
"page, an API page in ``docs/api/`` and a release note. The API reference and the user guide pick "
"up new pages automatically. The pages that describe the whole library are updated together after "
"a group of such pull requests has merged, as :doc:`documentation` describes."
msgstr ""
"因此，新增模块的拉取请求只需新增文件：模块本身、它的测试、一个用户指南页面、 ``docs/api/`` 中的一个 API 页面，以及一条发布说明。API "
"参考和用户指南会自动收录新页面。描述整个库的页面会在一批这样的拉取请求合并之后统一更新，见 :doc:`documentation` 。"

msgid "Legacy review"
msgstr "旧版评审"

msgid ""
"This review of the 0.2.x code guided the rewrite in 0.3.0. Its findings describe the legacy "
"implementation; :doc:`/release/migration` describes how each part was replaced."
msgstr "这份对 0.2.x 代码的评审指导了 0.3.0 的重写。其中的发现描述的是旧版实现；各部分的替代方式见 :doc:`/release/migration` 。"

msgid "Findings from the legacy implementation"
msgstr "旧版实现中的问题"

msgid ""
"Packaging. The 0.2.8 wheel placed NumPy and pandas behind the all extra. A default installation "
"could import kivi but failed on its dataset and WOE entry points."
msgstr "打包。0.2.8 的 wheel 将 NumPy 和 pandas 列在 all 可选依赖中。默认安装后可以导入 kivi，但加载数据和调用 WOE 都会失败。"

msgid ""
"Dependencies. evaluate/BucketsUtils.py imported PySpark at module load even for pandas PSI. Its "
"standalone CSI function also referenced an undefined self. The new metric functions depend on "
"pandas and NumPy."
msgstr ""
"依赖。evaluate/BucketsUtils.py 在模块加载时导入 PySpark，连 pandas 版 PSI 也依赖 Spark。该文件的独立 CSI 函数引用了未定义的 "
"self。新版指标函数只依赖 pandas 和 NumPy。"

msgid ""
"Numerical results. The old WOE zero-cell logic adjusted one class with an if/elif and used the "
"original totals. The old PSI helper modified the displayed counts. Tests now check raw counts, "
"normalized shares and hand-calculated metrics."
msgstr "数值结果。旧版 WOE 使用 if/elif 处理零频数，一次只调整一类，还沿用调整前的分母。旧版 PSI 会更改展示的计数。新版测试检查原始计数、归一化占比及手算指标。"

msgid ""
"State. Model/Tree.py removed the target column from the caller's frame. Dataset generation also "
"reset NumPy's global random state. Future estimators should preserve inputs and take a local "
"random seed."
msgstr "状态。Model/Tree.py 会从调用方传入的 DataFrame 中移除目标列。模拟数据生成器也会重置 NumPy 的全局随机状态。后续迁移估计器时，应保留输入并使用局部随机种子。"

msgid ""
"Coverage. Legacy scorecard and WOE tests printed tables without asserting the expected numbers. "
"Use frozen datasets to check fitted boundaries, score direction, special values and row counts "
"before porting these workflows."
msgstr "测试。旧版评分卡与 WOE 用例打印结果表，却没有断言具体数值。迁移前应用固定样本核对分箱边界、评分方向、特殊值和总行数。"

msgid ""
"Project scope. The former source tree mixed modeling, databases, distributed execution, notebooks"
" and deployment configuration. Keep infrastructure-specific imports inside optional integrations "
"and keep business SQL and local configuration outside the distribution."
msgstr "项目范围。旧目录混合了建模算法、数据库、分布式计算、笔记本与部署配置。新增集成时应在可选模块内导入相应依赖，将业务 SQL 和本地配置保留在分发包之外。"

msgid "Outcome"
msgstr "落实情况"

msgid ""
"The rewrite began with binning, WOE and PSI and then rebuilt the rest of the scorecard workflow, "
"checking each part against the legacy outputs or reference implementations on fixed samples. "
":doc:`/release/index` lists the parts release by release. Spark, SQL, AHP and the model wrappers "
"were not rebuilt. They are out of scope and remain in the repository history before the rewrite."
msgstr ""
"重写从分箱、WOE 和 PSI 开始，随后重建了评分卡流程的其余部分，每一部分都在固定样本上与旧版输出或参考实现核对过。 :doc:`/release/index` "
"按版本列出了这些部分。Spark、SQL、AHP 和模型封装没有重建：它们不在范围内，保留在重写之前的仓库历史中。"

msgid "Releasing to PyPI"
msgstr "发布到 PyPI"

msgid ""
"The ``Release`` workflow publishes kivi to PyPI when a version tag is pushed. It uses PyPI "
"trusted publishing, so no API token is stored in the repository."
msgstr "推送版本标签时，``Release`` 工作流会把 kivi 发布到 PyPI。它使用 PyPI 可信发布（trusted publishing），因此仓库中不保存任何 API 令牌。"

msgid ""
"Set ``version`` in ``pyproject.toml`` to the new version, for example ``0.3.1``. Run ``python "
"docs/build.py --release 0.3.1``, which moves the release-note files into a section of "
":doc:`/release/index` dated today, and translate the new heading."
msgstr ""
"把 ``pyproject.toml`` 中的 ``version`` 改为新版本号，例如 ``0.3.1`` 。运行 ``python docs/build.py --release "
"0.3.1`` ，它会把发布说明文件移入 :doc:`/release/index` 中以当天日期命名的新章节；然后翻译新章节的标题。"

msgid ""
"The command changes nothing while ``python docs/build.py`` still reports entry points to update, "
"as described in :doc:`documentation`."
msgstr "如果 ``python docs/build.py`` 仍报告有入口页面需要更新，这条命令不会做任何改动，详见 :doc:`documentation` 。"

msgid "Merge the change into the master branch."
msgstr "将改动合并到 master 分支。"

msgid "Tag the merged commit with ``v`` followed by the version and push the tag:"
msgstr "在合并后的提交上打 ``v`` 加版本号的标签，并推送该标签："

msgid ""
"Pushing the tag starts the upload without an approval step, so push it only when the release is "
"ready. The workflow stops before anything is uploaded if the tag does not match the version or "
"points at a commit that is not on master. Otherwise it runs the tests, builds the source "
"distribution and the wheel, checks them with twine and uploads them to PyPI. Only then does it "
"create the GitHub release, with the distributions attached and notes generated from the merged "
"pull requests. A version such as ``0.4.0rc1`` is marked as a pre-release."
msgstr ""
"推送标签后上传会直接开始，没有审批环节，因此只在准备好发布时才推送标签。如果标签与版本号不一致，或者标签指向的提交不在 master "
"上，工作流会在上传任何内容之前停止。否则它会运行测试，构建源码包和 wheel，用 twine 检查后上传到 PyPI。上传成功后，它才会创建 GitHub "
"release，附上安装包，并根据已合并的拉取请求生成说明。``0.4.0rc1`` 这类版本会被标记为预发布。"

msgid "The repository protects this path in three places:"
msgstr "仓库在三处保护这条发布路径："

msgid "Only repository administrators can create, move or delete ``v*`` tags."
msgstr "只有仓库管理员可以创建、移动或删除 ``v*`` 标签。"

msgid "The ``pypi`` environment accepts deployments from ``v*`` tags only."
msgstr "``pypi`` 环境只接受来自 ``v*`` 标签的部署。"

msgid ""
"PyPI trusts only the ``release.yml`` workflow of ``gchensy/kivi`` running in the ``pypi`` "
"environment."
msgstr "PyPI 只信任 ``gchensy/kivi`` 中在 ``pypi`` 环境下运行的 ``release.yml`` 工作流。"

msgid ""
"PyPI never accepts the same version twice. If a run fails before the upload, delete the tag with "
"``git push origin :refs/tags/v0.3.1``, fix the problem and tag again. If the upload succeeded, "
"release the fix under a new version."
msgstr ""
"PyPI 不接受重复上传同一个版本。如果运行在上传之前失败，可以用 ``git push origin :refs/tags/v0.3.1`` "
"删除标签，修复问题后重新打标签。如果已经上传成功，请用新的版本号发布修复。"

msgid "Version numbers"
msgstr "版本号"

msgid "Each release follows the promises of :doc:`/api/compatibility`. From 1.0:"
msgstr "每个版本都遵守 :doc:`/api/compatibility` 中的承诺。从 1.0 起："

msgid "A release that only fixes errors is a patch release, such as 1.3.1."
msgstr "只修复错误的版本是补丁版本，例如 1.3.1。"

msgid ""
"A release that adds to the API, deprecates a part of it or raises a minimum version is a minor "
"release, such as 1.4."
msgstr "扩充 API、弃用其中一部分或提高最低版本的版本是次版本，例如 1.4。"

msgid ""
"A release that removes or changes what earlier releases deprecated is a major release, such as "
"2.0."
msgstr "移除或修改先前版本所弃用内容的版本是主版本，例如 2.0。"

msgid ""
"A fix of a wrong result can go into a patch or a minor release, with a ``fixed`` fragment that "
"says what was wrong."
msgstr "对错误结果的修复可以进入补丁版本或次版本，并附上说明错误所在的 ``fixed`` 片段。"

msgid "Deprecations"
msgstr "弃用"

msgid ""
"A deprecated name, argument or behavior keeps working and warns with ``FutureWarning`` through "
"``_deprecation.warn``, which points the warning at the caller's line however deep the check sits."
" The message names what is deprecated and says what to use instead. "
"``tests/test_deprecations.py`` checks each warning with ``pytest.warns(FutureWarning, "
"match=...)`` and that it points at the test's own line. The code, the documentation and the "
"README examples must not trigger a deprecation themselves, because the tests and the doctests "
"turn warnings into errors."
msgstr ""
"已弃用的名称、参数或行为继续可用，并通过 ``_deprecation.warn`` 发出 ``FutureWarning`` "
"；无论检查位于多深的调用层级，该函数都会把警告指向调用者所在的行。消息指出被弃用的内容，并说明替代用法。 ``tests/test_deprecations.py`` 用 "
"``pytest.warns(FutureWarning, match=...)`` 检查每个警告，并检查它指向测试自身所在的行。代码、文档和 README 示例本身不得触发弃用警告，因为测试和"
" doctest 会把警告变为错误。"

msgid ""
"The ``changed`` fragment of the release names the deprecation and its replacement. The major "
"release that removes it lists the removal in a ``removed`` fragment and deletes its test."
msgstr "该版本的 ``changed`` 片段指出所弃用的内容及其替代用法。移除它的主版本在 ``removed`` 片段中列出这次移除，并删除相应的测试。"

msgid "Minimum versions"
msgstr "最低版本"

msgid ""
"A minimum version of Python, NumPy or pandas rises only in a minor release, and a ``changed`` "
"fragment of the release before announces it. The release that raises it changes ``requires-"
"python`` or ``dependencies`` in ``pyproject.toml``, the ``minimum-versions`` job of "
"``.github/workflows/docs.yml``, which tests the oldest supported versions, and the versions on "
":doc:`/getting_started/install` and :doc:`/api/compatibility` together."
msgstr ""
"Python、NumPy 或 pandas 的最低版本只在次版本中提高，并由前一个版本的 ``changed`` 片段预先公布。提高最低版本的那个版本要同时修改 "
"``pyproject.toml`` 中的 ``requires-python`` 或 ``dependencies`` 、 ``.github/workflows/docs.yml`` "
"中测试最低支持版本的 ``minimum-versions`` 任务，以及 :doc:`/getting_started/install` 和 :doc:`/api/compatibility`"
" 上列出的版本。"

msgid "Getting started"
msgstr "快速开始"

msgid ""
"kivi needs Python 3.10 or newer with NumPy and pandas. Install it, then follow the quickstart to "
"bin a variable, compute its weight of evidence and check its stability between two samples."
msgstr "kivi 需要 Python 3.10 或更高版本，以及 NumPy 和 pandas。安装后，可按快速上手完成一个变量的分箱、计算其证据权重，并检查它在两个样本之间的稳定性。"

msgid "Installation"
msgstr "安装"

msgid "Install from PyPI, GitHub or a local checkout and check the version."
msgstr "从 PyPI、GitHub 或本地仓库安装，并检查版本。"

msgid "Quickstart"
msgstr "快速上手"

msgid "A complete analysis of the bundled bank marketing data, with the output of every step."
msgstr "用随包的银行营销数据完成一次完整分析，并展示每一步的输出。"

msgid ""
"kivi requires Python 3.10 or newer, NumPy 1.24 or newer and pandas 2.0 or newer. pip installs "
"NumPy and pandas automatically. From kivi 1.0, a minimum version rises only in a minor release, "
"announced in the notes of the release before; see :doc:`/api/compatibility`."
msgstr ""
"kivi 需要 Python 3.10 或更高版本、NumPy 1.24 或更高版本，以及 pandas 2.0 或更高版本。pip 会自动安装 NumPy 和 pandas。从 kivi "
"1.0 起，最低版本只会在次版本中提高，并在前一个版本的版本说明中预先公布；参见 :doc:`/api/compatibility` 。"

msgid "PyPI"
msgstr "PyPI"

msgid "Install the latest release:"
msgstr "安装最新发布版本："

msgid "GitHub"
msgstr "GitHub"

msgid "Install the development version directly from the repository:"
msgstr "直接从仓库安装开发版："

msgid "Local checkout"
msgstr "本地仓库"

msgid "Clone the repository and install it from the checkout:"
msgstr "克隆仓库后从本地安装："

msgid "Check the installed version:"
msgstr "检查已安装的版本："

msgid ""
"To work on kivi itself, use an editable install with the test and documentation dependencies. See"
" :doc:`/development/index`."
msgstr "如需参与 kivi 开发，请使用可编辑安装并加装测试和文档依赖，详见 :doc:`/development/index`。"

msgid ""
"The 0.2.x releases have a different API. Read :doc:`/release/migration` before upgrading existing"
" code."
msgstr "0.2.x 版本的 API 与当前版本不同。升级已有代码前，请先阅读 :doc:`/release/migration`。"

msgid ""
"This walkthrough bins a numeric and a categorical variable from the bundled data, measures how "
"well each bin separates the target and checks whether the age distribution shifts between two "
"samples. Every output below is produced by the code above it."
msgstr "本教程对随包数据中的一个数值变量和一个类别变量进行分箱，衡量各箱对目标的区分能力，并检查年龄分布在两个样本之间是否发生偏移。下面的每个输出都由其上方的代码生成。"

msgid "Load the data"
msgstr "加载数据"

msgid ""
"The bundled bank marketing data records whether a customer subscribed to a term deposit. The "
"split below demonstrates two samples; the rows do not represent a chronological validation split."
msgstr "随包的营销数据记录了客户是否认购定期存款。下面按行切出两个样本演示用法，这一切分没有时间验证含义。"

msgid "Fit bins on the reference sample"
msgstr "在基准样本上拟合分箱"

msgid ""
"Fit the edges on the reference sample only, then reuse them for every other sample so that the "
"counts remain comparable."
msgstr "只在基准样本上拟合边界，再将同一组边界用于其他所有样本，使各组计数保持可比。"

msgid ""
"The outer edges are infinite, so an age outside the reference range still falls into the first or"
" last bin."
msgstr "最外侧的边界为无穷，因此超出基准范围的年龄仍会落入第一个或最后一个箱。"

msgid "Weight of evidence"
msgstr "证据权重"

msgid ":func:`~kivi.woe.woe_table` returns one row per bin, in the order of the intervals."
msgstr ":func:`~kivi.woe.woe_table` 每箱返回一行，按区间顺序排列。"

msgid ""
"A positive WOE means that the bin holds a larger share of the subscribers than of the non-"
"subscribers. Age on its own separates the two groups only weakly."
msgstr "WOE 为正表示该箱在认购客户中的占比高于在未认购客户中的占比。仅凭年龄区分这两类客户的能力较弱。"

msgid ""
"Read the per-bin contributions before interpreting a total. A group with few events can have a "
"large WOE despite representing few customers."
msgstr "解读总值前先检查每一箱的贡献。只有少量事件的箱也可能有很大的 WOE，但它代表的客户可能很少。"

msgid "Share of customers, subscription rate and WOE for each age bin"
msgstr "每个年龄箱的客户占比、认购率和 WOE"

msgid ""
"The same table as a chart: the share of customers and the subscription rate per age bin (top) and"
" the WOE (bottom). Younger and older customers subscribe more often."
msgstr "同一张表的图形版本：上图为每个年龄箱的客户占比和认购率，下图为 WOE。年轻和年长的客户认购比例更高。"

msgid "Categorical variables"
msgstr "类别变量"

msgid "Pass category labels directly; they need no edges."
msgstr "类别标签可以直接传入，无需边界。"

msgid "Population stability"
msgstr "群体稳定性"

msgid ":func:`~kivi.stability.psi_table` compares the two samples bin by bin. It does not use the target."
msgstr ":func:`~kivi.stability.psi_table` 逐箱比较两个样本，不使用目标标签。"

msgid "Next steps"
msgstr "后续阅读"

msgid ""
":doc:`/user_guide/binning` explains quantile, uniform and supervised edges, ties, special values "
"and missing values."
msgstr ":doc:`/user_guide/binning` 介绍等频、等距与有监督分箱边界、重复切点、特殊值和缺失值。"

msgid ":doc:`/user_guide/woe_iv` and :doc:`/user_guide/psi` give the formulas and the smoothing rule."
msgstr ":doc:`/user_guide/woe_iv` 和 :doc:`/user_guide/psi` 给出计算公式与平滑规则。"

msgid ":doc:`/api` lists every parameter."
msgstr ":doc:`/api` 列出全部参数。"

msgid "Credit risk modeling with pandas"
msgstr "基于 pandas 的信用风险建模"

msgid ""
"kivi is a pandas toolkit for credit risk and financial modeling. It profiles the candidate "
"variables, bins them and groups their categories, measures how well each bin separates a binary "
"outcome such as default, selects the variables and fits a logistic scorecard, infers the outcomes"
" of rejected applicants, scales the model to points, evaluates it and calibrates it on a master "
"scale, and prices the cut-offs and the expected loss. Once the model is live, it monitors the "
"score period by period, follows how the approved loans perform, and measures their expected "
"credit loss under IFRS 9. Tables come back as pandas DataFrames with one row per bin, grade, cut-"
"off, period or variable."
msgstr ""
"kivi 是面向信用风险与金融建模的 pandas "
"工具包。它分析候选变量、为其分箱并对类别分组，衡量每一箱对违约等二分类结果的区分能力，筛选变量并拟合逻辑回归评分卡，推断被拒申请人的结果，把模型刻度为分值，评估模型并基于主标尺进行校准，衡量各截断点的代价与预期损失。模型上线后，它逐期监控评分，跟踪已批准贷款的表现，并计量其"
" IFRS 9 预期信用损失。表格结果都是 pandas DataFrame，每箱、每个等级、每个截断点、每期或每个变量一行。"

msgid "At a glance"
msgstr "速览"

msgid "WOE chart for age with the share of customers and the event rate per bin"
msgstr "age 的 WOE 图，含每箱的客户占比和事件率"

msgid "The WOE chart for ``age``, drawn from ``evidence``."
msgstr "根据 ``evidence`` 绘制的 ``age`` WOE 图。"

msgid "Built for risk teams"
msgstr "为风控团队打造"

msgid "Missing values, distributions, event rates and a first IV ranking of every candidate in one table."
msgstr "用一张表列出每个候选变量的缺失值、分布、事件率和初步的 IV 排序。"

msgid ""
"Fine and coarse classing, special values, monotonic WOE and grouped categories for logistic "
"regression scorecards."
msgstr "细分箱与粗分箱、特殊值处理、单调 WOE，以及用于逻辑回归评分卡的类别分组。"

msgid "WOE and IV"
msgstr "WOE 与 IV"

msgid ""
"The WOE and IV of every bin, with smoothing that leaves the counts alone, and the WOE encoding of"
" new data."
msgstr "每箱的 WOE 和 IV，平滑时不改动计数，以及新数据的 WOE 编码。"

msgid ""
"Rank candidates by IV, drop correlated variables and select a logistic model whose coefficients "
"all point the right way."
msgstr "按 IV 给候选变量排序，剔除高度相关的变量，并选出系数方向全部正确的逻辑回归模型。"

msgid ""
"Infer the outcomes of declined applicants by fuzzy augmentation, parceling or reweighting, and "
"refit the model on all applicants."
msgstr "用模糊扩充、打包法或重新加权推断被拒申请人的结果，并在全部申请人上重新拟合模型。"

msgid ""
"Turn the model into points with PDO scaling, score new applications and explain each score with "
"reason codes."
msgstr "用 PDO 刻度把模型转换为分值，为新申请打分，并用原因码解释每个分数。"

msgid ""
"AUC, Gini, KS, gains and ROC tables on development and validation samples, with the confidence "
"interval of an AUC and the DeLong test of two scores."
msgstr "在开发样本和验证样本上计算 AUC、Gini、KS、增益表与 ROC 表，并给出 AUC 的置信区间和两个评分的 DeLong 检验。"

msgid ""
"Prior correction, master scales, binomial, Jeffreys and Hosmer-Lemeshow tests per grade, and "
"Platt and isotonic recalibration."
msgstr "先验校正、主标尺，按评级做二项检验、Jeffreys 检验和 Hosmer-Lemeshow 检验，以及 Platt 与保序回归重新校准。"

msgid ""
"Approval and bad rates of every cut-off, swap sets between a current and a new score, and "
"expected loss by grade."
msgstr "每个截断点的通过率与坏账率、现行评分与新评分之间的交换集，以及按等级的预期损失。"

msgid ""
"Save the binning and WOE of every variable as versioned JSON, so production groups new data "
"exactly as development did."
msgstr "把每个变量的分箱和 WOE 保存为带版本号的 JSON，生产环境对新数据的分组与开发时完全一致。"

msgid ""
"Compare live data with the development sample bin by bin, track PSI over time and measure each "
"variable's effect on the score with CSI."
msgstr "逐箱比较线上数据与开发样本，按期跟踪 PSI，并用 CSI 衡量每个变量对分数的影响。"

msgid ""
"One row per period with the population, the known outcomes, AUC, Gini, KS and the PSI of the "
"score, and the PSI of every variable by period."
msgstr "每期一行：样本量、已知结果、AUC、Gini、KS 和评分的 PSI；以及各变量在每期的 PSI。"

msgid ""
"Vintage curves by origination cohort, roll rates and transition matrices between delinquency "
"buckets."
msgstr "按放款批次的 vintage 曲线，以及逾期档位之间的滚动率和转移矩阵。"

msgid ""
"PD term structures from vintage curves and transition matrices, 12-month and lifetime ECL, and "
"the three IFRS 9 stages."
msgstr "由 vintage 曲线和转移矩阵得到 PD 期限结构，计算 12 个月与整个存续期 ECL，并划分 IFRS 9 的三个阶段。"

msgid "How it works"
msgstr "工作流程"

msgid "Profile and bin"
msgstr "概况与分箱"

msgid ""
"``profile_table`` gives a first look at every candidate. ``bin_edges``, or a supervised method "
"such as ``monotonic_edges``, fits edges on the development sample once, and ``chimerge_groups`` "
"groups the categories of a categorical variable. Every later sample is cut with the same edges "
"and groups, and the outer edges are infinite, so later values always fall into a bin."
msgstr ""
"``profile_table`` 让你先概览每个候选变量。 ``bin_edges`` ，或 ``monotonic_edges`` 等有监督方法，在开发样本上拟合一次边界， "
"``chimerge_groups`` 则对类别变量的类别分组。之后的每个样本都用同样的边界和分组，最外侧边界为无穷，因此后续数据总能落入某个箱。"

msgid "Encode and fit"
msgstr "编码与拟合"

msgid ""
"``woe_table`` measures each bin against the target and ``woe_transform`` encodes it. ``stepwise``"
" and ``logistic_regression`` select the variables and fit the model, with ``weights`` for "
"inferred rejects."
msgstr ""
"``woe_table`` 衡量每箱相对目标变量的表现， ``woe_transform`` 据此编码。 ``stepwise`` 和 ``logistic_regression`` "
"筛选变量并拟合模型，可通过 ``weights`` 纳入推断的拒绝样本。"

msgid "Scale and evaluate"
msgstr "刻度与评估"

msgid ""
"``points_table`` turns the model into points, and ``gains_table``, ``roc_auc`` and ``ks`` measure"
" how well the score ranks applicants on a holdout sample. ``roc_auc_interval`` shows how "
"precisely a sample measures the AUC."
msgstr ""
"``points_table`` 把模型转换为分值， ``gains_table`` 、 ``roc_auc`` 和 ``ks`` 在留出样本上衡量分数对申请人的排序能力。 "
"``roc_auc_interval`` 显示一个样本对 AUC 的测量有多精确。"

msgid "Calibrate and decide"
msgstr "校准与决策"

msgid ""
"``master_scale`` and ``assign_grades`` group the PDs into grades, and the binomial and Jeffreys "
"tests check the PD of each grade. ``cutoff_table`` shows what each cut-off approves, and "
"``expected_loss_table`` adds up the expected loss of each grade."
msgstr ""
"``master_scale`` 和 ``assign_grades`` 把 PD 划分为等级，二项检验和 Jeffreys 检验核对每个等级的 PD。 ``cutoff_table`` "
"显示每个截断点通过哪些申请， ``expected_loss_table`` 汇总每个等级的预期损失。"

msgid "Deploy and monitor"
msgstr "部署与监控"

msgid ""
"``BinningSpec`` saves the binning as JSON for production. ``monitoring_table`` and "
"``stability_table`` compare every period with the development sample, and ``csi_table`` measures "
"each variable's effect on the score."
msgstr ""
"``BinningSpec`` 把分箱方案保存为 JSON 供生产环境使用。 ``monitoring_table`` 和 ``stability_table`` 把每一期与开发样本比较， "
"``csi_table`` 衡量各变量对评分的影响。"

msgid "Follow the loans"
msgstr "跟踪贷款"

msgid ""
"``vintage_table`` and ``transition_matrix`` follow the approved loans. ``convert_pd`` and "
"``transition_pd`` turn them into PD term structures, and ``expected_credit_loss`` and "
"``assign_stages`` give the IFRS 9 loss allowance."
msgstr ""
"``vintage_table`` 和 ``transition_matrix`` 跟踪已批准的贷款。 ``convert_pd`` 和 ``transition_pd`` 把它们转换为 PD "
"期限结构， ``expected_credit_loss`` 和 ``assign_stages`` 给出 IFRS 9 损失准备。"

msgid "Documentation"
msgstr "文档"

msgid "Install kivi and walk through a complete analysis of the bundled bank marketing data."
msgstr "安装 kivi，并用随包的银行营销数据完成一次完整分析。"

msgid ""
"A credit scorecard project from the applications to the IFRS 9 loss allowance of the loans, in "
"ten chapters that use nearly every function of kivi."
msgstr "一个信用评分卡项目：从贷款申请一直到贷款的 IFRS 9 损失准备，共十章，用到了 kivi 的几乎所有函数。"

msgid "User guide"
msgstr "用户指南"

msgid ""
"One page per step of a risk model, from the profile of the candidates to the expected credit loss"
" of the approved loans, with definitions, worked examples and how to read each result."
msgstr "风控模型的每个步骤各占一页，从候选变量概况到已批准贷款的预期信用损失，包含定义、完整示例以及各项结果的解读方法。"

msgid ""
"Parameters, return values and examples for every public function, the conventions they share, "
"what a release may change and a glossary of the terms."
msgstr "每个公共函数的参数、返回值和示例，以及它们共同遵循的约定、一个版本可以改变什么和术语表。"

msgid "What changed in each release, and how to migrate code written for 0.9 or 0.2.x."
msgstr "各版本的变化，以及如何迁移为 0.9 或 0.2.x 编写的代码。"

msgid "Unreleased"
msgstr "未发布"

msgid "Changes merged since the last release."
msgstr "上次发布以来合并的改动。"

msgid "New"
msgstr "新增"

msgid ""
"``kivi.strategy.confusion_table`` counts, at each cut-off of a score, the declined events and "
"non-events and the approved ones, with the precision, recall, F1 score and accuracy of the "
"decision. A score above the cut-off is declined, as in ``cutoff_table``, and counts as the "
"prediction of an event. The function takes ``cutoffs`` and ``weights`` as ``cutoff_table`` does, "
"so the rows line up, and its ``recall`` is the ``rejected_event_share`` of that table. "
"``precision`` is NaN for a cut-off that declines nobody."
msgstr ""
"``kivi.strategy.confusion_table`` 统计评分在每个截断点上被拒绝的事件和非事件以及被通过的事件和非事件，并给出该决策的精确率、召回率、F1 "
"分数和准确率。评分高于截断点即被拒绝，与 ``cutoff_table`` 相同，并视为对事件的预测。该函数与 ``cutoff_table`` 一样接受 ``cutoffs`` 和 "
"``weights`` ，因此各行一一对应，其 ``recall`` 就是那张表的 ``rejected_event_share`` 。截断点不拒绝任何观测时 ``precision`` 为 "
"NaN。"

msgid ""
"The new module ``kivi.plotting`` draws the result tables of the other modules with matplotlib, an"
" optional dependency installed with ``pip install \"kivi[plot]\"``. ``woe_chart`` draws the share"
" and the event rate or WOE of each group of a WOE table, ``correlation_chart`` a correlation "
"matrix, ``roc_chart`` the ROC curve with its KS, ``gains_chart`` the cumulative shares of a gains"
" table, ``calibration_chart`` the observed against the predicted event rate of each group, "
"``cutoff_chart`` the event rate of the approved book against the approval rate, ``psi_chart`` the"
" reference and current shares of a PSI table, ``monitoring_chart`` one column of a monitoring or "
"stability table by period, as a line or as bars, and ``vintage_chart`` the curve of each cohort "
"of a vintage table."
msgstr ""
"新增模块 ``kivi.plotting`` ，用 matplotlib 绘制其他模块的结果表；matplotlib 是可选依赖，用 ``pip install \"kivi[plot]\"``"
" 安装。 ``woe_chart`` 绘制 WOE 表中每个分组的占比以及事件率或 WOE， ``correlation_chart`` 绘制相关系数矩阵， ``roc_chart`` 绘制 "
"ROC 曲线及其 KS， ``gains_chart`` 绘制增益表的累计占比， ``calibration_chart`` 绘制每个分组的观测事件率与预测事件率， "
"``cutoff_chart`` 绘制通过客群的事件率随通过率的变化， ``psi_chart`` 绘制 PSI 表的基准占比与当前占比， ``monitoring_chart`` "
"以折线或柱形逐期绘制监控表或稳定性表中的一列， ``vintage_chart`` 绘制 Vintage 表中每个批次的曲线。"

msgid ""
"Each chart draws on the matplotlib Axes passed as ``ax``, or on a new figure, and returns the "
"Axes it drew on. It never shows the figure, never changes ``matplotlib.rcParams`` and never "
"modifies the table, and the text inside it is limited to column names and data values."
msgstr ""
"每个图表函数在 ``ax`` 传入的 matplotlib Axes 上作图，未传入时新建一个图形，并返回所用的 Axes。它不会显示图形，不会修改 "
"``matplotlib.rcParams`` ，也不会修改传入的表；图中的文字只有列名和数据值。"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.univariate.profile_table` appends five columns. Numeric columns get ``skewness`` and"
" ``kurtosis``, the bias-corrected sample skewness and excess kurtosis that ``pandas.Series.skew``"
" and ``pandas.Series.kurt`` compute, and ``cv``, the coefficient of variation, all from the "
"values without missing values and special codes and weighted with ``weights``. With a target, "
"numeric columns get ``ks``, the KS statistic of their values, and every column gets "
"``chi2_p_value``, the p-value of the chi-squared test of independence between the target and the "
"groups of the quick binning that gives ``iv``."
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.univariate.profile_table` 在末尾新增五列。数值列新增 ``skewness`` 和 ``kurtosis`` ，即 "
"``pandas.Series.skew`` 和 ``pandas.Series.kurt`` 计算的偏差校正样本偏度和超额峰度，以及变异系数 ``cv`` "
"；它们都基于不含缺失值和特殊值编码的取值计算，并按 ``weights`` 加权。有目标时，数值列新增其取值的 KS 统计量 ``ks`` ，每一列新增 ``chi2_p_value`` "
"，即目标与给出 ``iv`` 的快速分箱各组之间卡方独立性检验的 p 值。"

msgid "Changed"
msgstr "变更"

msgid ""
"Eleven topic guides gain diagrams that show how a function computes its result, with the numbers "
"of the guide's example: edges and ``pandas.cut``, ``woe_table`` and ``woe_transform``, "
"``psi_table``, the points of a scorecard, the ROC table, isotonic regression, fuzzy augmentation "
"and the bands of parceling and reweighting, the transition matrix, the expected credit loss and "
"the days-past-due backstops of the stages, a binning specification from the fit to JSON, and the "
"monitoring table. The calibration guide gains a small example of isotonic regression to go with "
"its diagram."
msgstr ""
"十一篇主题指南新增示意图，用指南示例中的数值展示函数如何计算结果：边界与 ``pandas.cut`` 、 ``woe_table`` 与 ``woe_transform`` 、 "
"``psi_table`` 、评分卡的分值、ROC 表、保序回归、模糊扩充以及打包法和重新加权的评分段、转移矩阵、预期信用损失和阶段划分的逾期天数兜底标准、分箱方案从拟合到 JSON "
"的过程，以及监控表。校准指南新增一个保序回归的小示例，与其示意图配套。"

msgid ""
"The documentation gains a tutorial section: a credit scorecard project in ten chapters, from the "
"applications of a year to the IFRS 9 loss allowance of the loans. It profiles and bins the "
"candidates, selects the variables, infers the outcomes of the rejects, scales and evaluates the "
"scorecard against the incumbent's PD, calibrates it on a master scale, chooses the cut-off, "
"monitors a year of production with a shift in the applicants, and allocates the loan book to "
"stages. Boxes marked \"Simulation check\" compare each estimate with the outcomes that only the "
"simulated data reveal."
msgstr ""
"文档新增教程部分：一个分十章展开的信用评分卡项目，从一年的贷款申请一直到贷款的 IFRS 9 "
"损失准备。项目依次分析并分箱候选变量、筛选变量、推断拒绝申请人的结果、将模型转换为评分卡并与现行评分卡的 PD "
"对比评估、在主标尺上校准、选择截断点、在申请人结构发生变化的一年中监控投产后的模型，并将贷款组合划分到各个阶段。标为“模拟核对”的方框把每个估计值与只有模拟数据才能揭示的真实结果相比较。"

msgid "1.0.0 (2026-11-22)"
msgstr "1.0.0（2026-11-22）"

msgid ""
"``kivi.woe.woe`` returns a Series named ``woe``, with the index of the counts, when a count "
"argument is a Series, as other functions shape their results like their input. Lists and arrays "
"still give an array. Use ``.to_numpy()`` for the array and ``.iloc`` to select by position."
msgstr ""
"当某个计数参数是 Series 时， ``kivi.woe.woe`` 返回具有计数索引、名为 ``woe`` 的 "
"Series，与其他函数让结果形状与输入一致的做法相同。列表和数组仍返回数组。用 ``.to_numpy()`` 取得数组，用 ``.iloc`` 按位置选取。"

msgid ""
"kivi 1.0 is the first stable release. From now on it follows semantic versioning, as "
":doc:`/api/compatibility` describes, and its package metadata says ``Development Status :: 5 - "
"Production/Stable``."
msgstr ""
"kivi 1.0 是第一个稳定版本。此后 kivi 遵循语义化版本，见 :doc:`/api/compatibility` ，其包元数据标注为 ``Development Status :: 5"
" - Production/Stable`` 。"

msgid "Removed"
msgstr "移除"

msgid ""
"``smoothing=True`` raises a ``ValueError`` in ``kivi.woe.woe_table``, ``kivi.woe.woe``, "
"``kivi.woe.iv``, ``kivi.stability.psi_table``, ``kivi.stability.psi``, "
"``kivi.binning.monotonic_edges``, ``kivi.calibration.fit_grade_pd``, "
"``kivi.monitoring.monitoring_table`` and ``kivi.monitoring.stability_table``, as it already did "
"in ``kivi.spec.fit_spec`` and ``kivi.binning.chimerge_groups``. kivi 0.9 read it as 1 with a "
"``FutureWarning``; pass ``smoothing=1`` for that result."
msgstr ""
"``kivi.woe.woe_table`` 、 ``kivi.woe.woe`` 、 ``kivi.woe.iv`` 、 ``kivi.stability.psi_table`` 、 "
"``kivi.stability.psi`` 、 ``kivi.binning.monotonic_edges`` 、 ``kivi.calibration.fit_grade_pd`` 、 "
"``kivi.monitoring.monitoring_table`` 和 ``kivi.monitoring.stability_table`` 在 ``smoothing=True`` "
"时引发 ``ValueError`` ，与 ``kivi.spec.fit_spec`` 和 ``kivi.binning.chimerge_groups`` 此前的行为一致。kivi 0.9 "
"将其按 1 计算并发出 ``FutureWarning`` ；传入 ``smoothing=1`` 可得到当时的结果。"

msgid ""
"``kivi.woe.woe``, ``kivi.woe.iv`` and ``kivi.stability.psi`` raise a ``ValueError`` when both "
"counts are Series with different indices, which kivi 0.9 matched by position with a "
"``FutureWarning``. Align the counts first, for example with ``Series.align(other, "
"fill_value=0)``, or pass arrays when both list the groups in the same order."
msgstr ""
"当两组计数都是索引不同的 Series 时， ``kivi.woe.woe`` 、 ``kivi.woe.iv`` 和 ``kivi.stability.psi`` 引发 "
"``ValueError`` ；kivi 0.9 会按位置匹配并发出 ``FutureWarning`` 。请先对齐计数，例如使用 ``Series.align(other, "
"fill_value=0)`` ；只有当两者的分组顺序相同时才传入数组。"

msgid ""
"``kivi.datasets.Dataset`` and its method ``bank_data()`` are removed. "
"``kivi.datasets.load_bank()`` returns the same frame."
msgstr "移除 ``kivi.datasets.Dataset`` 及其方法 ``bank_data()`` 。 ``kivi.datasets.load_bank()`` 返回相同的数据框。"

msgid ""
"The ``probabilities`` argument of ``kivi.calibration.isotonic_predict`` is removed; pass "
"``probability``."
msgstr "移除 ``kivi.calibration.isotonic_predict`` 的 ``probabilities`` 参数；请传入 ``probability`` 。"

msgid "0.9.0 (2026-11-22)"
msgstr "0.9.0（2026-11-22）"

msgid ""
"A new page, :doc:`/api/compatibility`, states what kivi promises from 1.0: semantic versioning, "
"with deprecations that warn with a ``FutureWarning`` for the rest of a major version, fixes of "
"wrong results in any release, and Python 3.10, NumPy 1.24 and pandas 2.0 as the oldest supported "
"versions, which rise only in a minor release announced by the release before. It also lists the "
"public names, the index and the columns of every table, the exception and warning types, and what"
" later releases read from a saved ``BinningSpec``."
msgstr ""
"新页面 :doc:`/api/compatibility` 说明 kivi 从 1.0 起的承诺：语义化版本，弃用在主版本的其余版本中发出 ``FutureWarning`` "
"，对错误结果的修复可以出现在任何版本中，最低支持版本为 Python 3.10、NumPy 1.24 和 pandas "
"2.0，并且只在由前一个版本预先公布的次版本中提高。它还列出了公共名称、每个表格的索引和列、异常和警告类型，以及以后的版本能从已保存的 ``BinningSpec`` 读取什么。"

msgid ""
":doc:`/api/conventions` states more of the rules that every function follows: the order of the "
"data of other observations, the names of frames and similar options, the default ``bins``, how "
"Series results are named, the index names of tables, the fixed rows of some tables, missing "
"values in the binning fits, and the functions without ``weights``."
msgstr ""
":doc:`/api/conventions` 说明了更多每个函数都遵循的规则：其他观测数据的顺序、数据框和相近选项的名称、默认的 ``bins`` 、Series "
"结果的命名方式、表格的索引名称、部分表格的固定行、分箱拟合中的缺失值，以及不接受 ``weights`` 的函数。"

msgid ""
"The tests keep specifications saved by kivi 0.6.0 and 0.8.0 and check that they still load and "
"encode a sample as those releases did, and that they match a fresh fit up to rounding."
msgstr "测试保存了由 kivi 0.6.0 和 0.8.0 保存的分箱方案，并检查它们仍能加载、对样本的编码与当时的版本相同，并且在舍入误差范围内与重新拟合的结果一致。"

msgid ""
"kivi ships inline type hints and a ``py.typed`` marker, so type checkers such as mypy check code "
"that calls it. Every function in the package is annotated and checked with mypy."
msgstr "kivi 附带内联类型注解和 ``py.typed`` 标记，因此 mypy 等类型检查器可以检查调用 kivi 的代码。包中的每个函数都有注解，并经过 mypy 检查。"

msgid ""
"``kivi.woe.woe``, ``kivi.woe.iv`` and ``kivi.stability.psi`` warn with a ``FutureWarning`` when "
"both counts are Series with different indices. They still match the counts by position; kivi 1.0 "
"raises a ``ValueError``, as the other functions do for Series that describe the same groups. Pass"
" Series with identical indices, or arrays to keep matching by position."
msgstr ""
"当两组计数都是索引不同的 Series 时， ``kivi.woe.woe`` 、 ``kivi.woe.iv`` 和 ``kivi.stability.psi`` 会发出 "
"``FutureWarning`` 。它们仍按位置匹配计数；kivi 1.0 将引发 ``ValueError`` ，与其他函数对描述同一组分组的 Series 的处理一致。请传入索引相同的 "
"Series，或传入数组以继续按位置匹配。"

msgid ""
"``smoothing=True`` warns with a ``FutureWarning`` in ``kivi.woe.woe_table``, ``kivi.woe.woe``, "
"``kivi.woe.iv``, ``kivi.stability.psi_table``, ``kivi.stability.psi``, "
"``kivi.binning.monotonic_edges``, ``kivi.calibration.fit_grade_pd``, "
"``kivi.monitoring.monitoring_table`` and ``kivi.monitoring.stability_table``. It still counts as "
"1, not as the default 0.5; kivi 1.0 raises a ``ValueError``, as ``kivi.spec.fit_spec`` and "
"``kivi.binning.chimerge_groups`` already do. Pass ``smoothing=1`` for the same result."
msgstr ""
"``kivi.woe.woe_table`` 、 ``kivi.woe.woe`` 、 ``kivi.woe.iv`` 、 ``kivi.stability.psi_table`` 、 "
"``kivi.stability.psi`` 、 ``kivi.binning.monotonic_edges`` 、 ``kivi.calibration.fit_grade_pd`` 、 "
"``kivi.monitoring.monitoring_table`` 和 ``kivi.monitoring.stability_table`` 在 ``smoothing=True`` "
"时会发出 ``FutureWarning`` 。它仍按 1 计算，而不是默认值 0.5；kivi 1.0 将引发 ``ValueError`` ，与 ``kivi.spec.fit_spec``"
" 和 ``kivi.binning.chimerge_groups`` 现在的行为一致。传入 ``smoothing=1`` 可得到相同结果。"

msgid ""
"``kivi.datasets.Dataset.bank_data()`` warns with a ``FutureWarning`` and is removed in kivi 1.0. "
"``kivi.datasets.load_bank()`` returns the same frame."
msgstr ""
"``kivi.datasets.Dataset.bank_data()`` 会发出 ``FutureWarning`` ，并将在 kivi 1.0 中移除。 "
"``kivi.datasets.load_bank()`` 返回相同的数据框。"

msgid ""
"``kivi.calibration.isotonic_predict`` takes the probability of each band as ``probability``, the "
"name the other functions use, and ``kivi.calibration.isotonic_fit`` documents its second result "
"under that name. ``probabilities=`` still works with a ``FutureWarning`` until kivi 1.0."
msgstr ""
"``kivi.calibration.isotonic_predict`` 以 ``probability`` 接收每个分段的概率，与其他函数使用的名称一致； "
"``kivi.calibration.isotonic_fit`` 的文档也以这一名称描述其第二个返回值。 ``probabilities=`` 在 kivi 1.0 之前仍可使用，但会发出 "
"``FutureWarning`` 。"

msgid ""
"``kivi.strategy.expected_loss`` names a Series result ``expected_loss``. It took the name of the "
"first Series among its inputs, such as ``pd`` or ``balance``."
msgstr ""
"``kivi.strategy.expected_loss`` 返回的 Series 名为 ``expected_loss`` 。此前它沿用输入中第一个 Series 的名称，例如 ``pd``"
" 或 ``balance`` 。"

msgid ""
"``kivi.calibration.master_scale`` labels the grades by the index of a Series ``probability`` when"
" ``labels`` is not given, so ``master_scale(fit_grade_pd(event, total))`` keeps the grades of a "
"table. A list or an array still gives grades numbered from 1."
msgstr ""
"未给出 ``labels`` 时， ``kivi.calibration.master_scale`` 以 Series ``probability`` 的索引作为等级标签，因此 "
"``master_scale(fit_grade_pd(event, total))`` 保留表中的等级。列表或数组仍从 1 开始为等级编号。"

msgid ""
"``kivi.lifetime.assign_stages`` also takes ``days_past_due`` and ``defaulted`` by position, as in"
" ``assign_stages(significant_increase, days_past_due, defaulted)``. Calls with keywords work as "
"before."
msgstr ""
"``kivi.lifetime.assign_stages`` 也可以按位置接收 ``days_past_due`` 和 ``defaulted`` ，例如 "
"``assign_stages(significant_increase, days_past_due, defaulted)`` 。使用关键字的调用不受影响。"

msgid ""
"The index of ``kivi.selection.logistic_regression`` and of ``kivi.selection.vif`` is named "
"``variable``, like that of ``kivi.scorecard.points_table``, whatever the name of the columns of "
"``X``. The index of ``kivi.metrics.roc_auc_interval`` is named ``statistic``. ``reset_index()`` "
"therefore gives a column of that name, and ``kivi.scorecard.woe_to_points`` with coefficients "
"taken from ``logistic_regression`` gives columns named ``variable``."
msgstr ""
"``kivi.selection.logistic_regression`` 和 ``kivi.selection.vif`` 的索引名为 ``variable`` ，与 "
"``kivi.scorecard.points_table`` 相同，不论 ``X`` 的列名是什么。 ``kivi.metrics.roc_auc_interval`` 的索引名为 "
"``statistic`` 。因此 ``reset_index()`` 会得到同名的列，而用 ``logistic_regression`` 的系数调用 "
"``kivi.scorecard.woe_to_points`` 时，结果的列名为 ``variable`` 。"

msgid ""
"Error messages show the value at fault in the same form everywhere. NumPy scalars appear as plain"
" numbers, so ``bins=numpy.int64(0)`` gives ``got 0`` instead of ``got np.int64(0)``. Every "
"function that takes a target says ``target must contain only 0 and 1, got 2`` or ``target must "
"contain both 0 and 1, got only 0``; the weights messages show the first invalid weight or the "
"total of each class; and a weights index that differs from the data says ``score and weights must"
" have identical indices``, like the other arguments."
msgstr ""
"错误信息在各处以同样的形式显示出错的值。NumPy 标量显示为普通数字，因此 ``bins=numpy.int64(0)`` 给出 ``got 0`` 而不是 ``got "
"np.int64(0)`` 。每个接受 target 的函数都会给出 ``target must contain only 0 and 1, got 2`` 或 ``target must "
"contain both 0 and 1, got only 0`` ；权重的信息会显示第一个无效的权重或各类别的总权重；权重的索引与数据不同时，信息为 ``score and weights "
"must have identical indices`` ，与其他参数一致。"

msgid ""
"The messages that NumPy and pandas gave for kivi's arguments now name those arguments: "
"``kivi.binning.cut`` says ``edges must be increasing numbers, got [3, 1]`` where pandas spoke of "
"``bins`` and of a ``duplicates`` keyword that ``cut`` does not have, and the binning functions "
"say ``values must be numbers or special values, got 'a'``. ``kivi.binning.bin_edges`` and the "
"supervised binning functions say ``values`` instead of ``reference values``."
msgstr ""
"NumPy 和 pandas 针对 kivi 参数给出的错误信息现在会指明这些参数： ``kivi.binning.cut`` 会说 ``edges must be increasing "
"numbers, got [3, 1]`` ，而 pandas 说的是 ``bins`` ，还提到 ``cut`` 并没有的 ``duplicates`` 参数；各分箱函数会说 ``values"
" must be numbers or special values, got 'a'`` 。 ``kivi.binning.bin_edges`` 和各有监督分箱函数的信息改称 "
"``values`` ，不再称 ``reference values`` 。"

msgid ""
"``kivi.version`` and ``kivi.PackageNotFoundError``, which the package imported from "
"``importlib.metadata`` by accident, no longer exist; use ``kivi.__version__``. The public modules"
" no longer bind the helpers they import, such as ``kivi.binning.as_series`` or "
"``kivi.metrics.normal_quantile``. None of these names was documented."
msgstr ""
"``kivi.version`` 和 ``kivi.PackageNotFoundError`` 是包意外从 ``importlib.metadata`` 导入的名称，现已不再存在；请使用 "
"``kivi.__version__`` 。各公共模块也不再绑定它们导入的辅助函数，例如 ``kivi.binning.as_series`` 或 "
"``kivi.metrics.normal_quantile`` 。这些名称都没有写入文档。"

msgid "Fixed"
msgstr "修复"

msgid ""
"``kivi.woe.woe_transform`` looked a number up in the interval of a ``pandas.cut`` table that "
"contained it, so raw values and special codes that the table did not have, such as ``-1`` grouped"
" by ``kivi.binning.cut`` with ``special=[-1]``, silently got the WOE of an interval. Labels are "
"now matched by equality, as documented, and such groups are unseen: they raise an error unless "
"``unseen`` gives them a WOE."
msgstr ""
"``kivi.woe.woe_transform`` 会在 ``pandas.cut`` 表中查找包含某个数字的区间，因此原始数值以及表中没有的特殊值编码（例如 "
"``kivi.binning.cut`` 在 ``special=[-1]`` 下分出的 ``-1`` ）会悄无声息地得到某个区间的 "
"WOE。现在标签按文档所述的相等关系匹配，这类分组属于未见分组：除非用 ``unseen`` 为其指定 WOE，否则会引发错误。"

msgid ""
"``kivi.binning.cut`` now raises an error for an infinite value that is not a special value. "
"``pandas.cut`` left ``-inf`` in no interval, so that it was counted as a missing value, and put "
"``inf`` in the last interval. Pass infinite codes in ``special`` to give them their own group."
msgstr ""
"``kivi.binning.cut`` 现在对不属于特殊值的无穷值引发错误。 ``pandas.cut`` 会让 ``-inf`` 不落入任何区间、从而被算作缺失值，而把 ``inf`` "
"放进最后一个区间。若要让无穷值编码单独成组，请把它们传入 ``special`` 。"

msgid ""
"``kivi.spec.BinningSpec.woe_transform`` gave ``inf`` the WOE of the last interval, while ``-inf``"
" was unseen. Both are now unseen, like every infinite value that is not a special code of its "
"column, so they raise an error unless the column has an unseen WOE. ``BinningSpec.cut`` leaves "
"both missing."
msgstr ""
"``kivi.spec.BinningSpec.woe_transform`` 会给 ``inf`` 赋予最后一个区间的 WOE，而 ``-inf`` "
"属于未见分组。现在两者都属于未见分组，与所有不属于该列特殊值的无穷值一样：除非该列指定了未见分组的 WOE，否则会引发错误。 ``BinningSpec.cut`` 把两者都留为缺失值。"

msgid ""
"``kivi.stability.csi_table`` raised an error for points of several variables only when the "
"variables were in an index named ``variable``. A ``points_table`` result after ``reset_index()``,"
" with the variables in a ``variable`` column, was read as one variable and mixed their groups. It"
" now raises the same error."
msgstr ""
"``kivi.stability.csi_table`` 只在变量位于名为 ``variable`` 的索引中时，才对包含多个变量的分值引发错误。 ``points_table`` 的结果经过 "
"``reset_index()`` 后，变量位于 ``variable`` 列中，会被当作一个变量读取，从而混淆各变量的分组。现在这种情况会引发同样的错误。"

msgid ""
"``kivi.spec.fit_spec`` binned a column with a complex dtype by its real part, with NumPy's "
"``ComplexWarning``. It now raises an error, and so do ``BinningSpec.cut`` and "
"``BinningSpec.woe_transform`` for a complex column fitted as numeric."
msgstr ""
"``kivi.spec.fit_spec`` 会按实部对复数 dtype 的列分箱，并发出 NumPy 的 ``ComplexWarning`` 。现在它会引发错误；对于按数值列拟合的复数列， "
"``BinningSpec.cut`` 和 ``BinningSpec.woe_transform`` 也会引发错误。"

msgid ""
"``kivi.spec.BinningSpec`` and ``dataclasses.replace`` rejected a numeric table whose intervals "
"ran between the exact edges whenever ``pandas.cut`` rounds them in its labels, such as an edge of"
" 0.6428571428571428 shown as 0.643. Such intervals are now accepted and stored under the labels "
"of ``kivi.binning.cut``, as ``BinningSpec.from_dict`` already did."
msgstr ""
"当 ``pandas.cut`` 在标签中对边界做了舍入时（例如边界 0.6428571428571428 显示为 0.643）， ``kivi.spec.BinningSpec`` 和 "
"``dataclasses.replace`` 会拒绝区间由精确边界构成的数值表。现在这样的区间会被接受，并像 ``BinningSpec.from_dict`` 一直以来那样，以 "
"``kivi.binning.cut`` 的标签保存。"

msgid ""
"``kivi.woe.woe_transform`` accepted ``unseen=numpy.nan``, which gave unseen groups a missing WOE,"
" and infinite values. ``unseen`` must now be ``\"raise\"`` or a finite number, as for "
"``kivi.spec.fit_spec`` and ``kivi.stability.csi_table``."
msgstr ""
"``kivi.woe.woe_transform`` 曾接受 ``unseen=numpy.nan`` （使未见分组的 WOE 为缺失值）以及无穷值。现在 ``unseen`` 必须是 "
"``\"raise\"`` 或有限数值，与 ``kivi.spec.fit_spec`` 和 ``kivi.stability.csi_table`` 一致。"

msgid ""
"``kivi.calibration.prior_correction``, the ``probability`` of ``calibration_table``, "
"``binomial_test``, ``jeffreys_test``, ``hosmer_lemeshow`` and ``herfindahl_index`` read numbers "
"given as strings, so that ``herfindahl_index([\"50\", \"30\"])`` gave 0.53125. They now raise an "
"error that names the argument, such as \"counts must be real and numeric, got dtype object with "
"the value '50'\", as the other functions of the module do."
msgstr ""
"``kivi.calibration.prior_correction`` 、 ``calibration_table`` 的 ``probability`` 、 "
"``binomial_test`` 、 ``jeffreys_test`` 、 ``hosmer_lemeshow`` 和 ``herfindahl_index`` "
"过去会读取以字符串给出的数字，因此 ``herfindahl_index([\"50\", \"30\"])`` 返回 0.53125。现在它们会引发指明参数的错误，例如 \"counts "
"must be real and numeric, got dtype object with the value '50'\"，与该模块的其他函数一致。"

msgid ""
"The counts of ``kivi.calibration`` read True and False as 1 and 0, so that "
"``binomial_test([True], [True], 0.5)`` gave 0.5. The ``event`` and ``total`` of "
"``binomial_test``, ``jeffreys_test``, ``hosmer_lemeshow`` and ``fit_grade_pd`` and the ``counts``"
" of ``herfindahl_index`` now reject booleans, as weights do. Probabilities and scores still count"
" them as 1 and 0."
msgstr ""
"``kivi.calibration`` 的计数参数过去把 True 和 False 读作 1 和 0，因此 ``binomial_test([True], [True], 0.5)`` 返回 "
"0.5。现在 ``binomial_test`` 、 ``jeffreys_test`` 、 ``hosmer_lemeshow`` 和 ``fit_grade_pd`` 的 ``event``"
" 与 ``total`` ，以及 ``herfindahl_index`` 的 ``counts`` 都拒绝布尔值，与权重一致。概率和评分仍把布尔值算作 1 和 0。"

msgid ""
"``kivi.calibration.fit_grade_pd`` raised \"the fitted PDs must rise with the grade\" for grades "
"that were in order when ``smoothing`` was not smaller than the total of a grade without defaults,"
" as with the counts of a ``calibration_table`` whose weights sum to 1. It now says what is wrong,"
" such as \"smoothing must be smaller than the total of each grade without defaults, got 0.5 for "
"grade 1 with a total of 0.4\", and the documentation says that weighted counts must be on the "
"scale of observation counts."
msgstr ""
"当 ``smoothing`` 不小于某个没有违约的等级的总数时（例如权重之和为 1 的 ``calibration_table`` 中的计数）， "
"``kivi.calibration.fit_grade_pd`` 过去会对顺序正确的等级引发 \"the fitted PDs must rise with the "
"grade\"。现在它会指出真正的问题，例如 \"smoothing must be smaller than the total of each grade without defaults,"
" got 0.5 for grade 1 with a total of 0.4\"，文档也说明了加权计数必须与观测数处于同一量级。"

msgid ""
"Invalid arguments that NumPy or pandas used to reject with a ``TypeError`` now raise a "
"``ValueError`` that names the argument, as the conventions promise: a ``smoothing`` that is a "
"string, ``None`` or an array, an ``rng`` that ``numpy.random.default_rng`` does not accept in "
"``kivi.reject_inference.parceling``, ``kivi.datasets.make_applications`` and "
"``kivi.datasets.make_loan_panel``, ``edges`` of ``kivi.binning.cut`` that are not numbers, and a "
"WOE table of ``kivi.woe.woe_transform`` or ``kivi.scorecard.points_table`` that holds a value "
"that is not a number."
msgstr ""
"NumPy 或 pandas 以前用 ``TypeError`` 拒绝的无效参数，现在会按约定引发指明参数的 ``ValueError`` ：字符串、 ``None`` 或数组形式的 "
"``smoothing`` ； ``kivi.reject_inference.parceling`` 、 ``kivi.datasets.make_applications`` 和 "
"``kivi.datasets.make_loan_panel`` 中 ``numpy.random.default_rng`` 不接受的 ``rng`` ； "
"``kivi.binning.cut`` 中不是数字的 ``edges`` ；以及 ``kivi.woe.woe_transform`` 或 "
"``kivi.scorecard.points_table`` 的 WOE 表中不是数字的值。"

msgid ""
"``kivi.lifetime.significant_increase`` let floating-point rounding decide ties: a PD of 0.04 "
"against 0.03 counted as more than one percentage point higher, and 0.45 as more than 1.5 times "
"0.30. A PD within a few units in the last place of a threshold now meets it exactly and is not "
"flagged, as the strict thresholds say. Of the 89 pairs of two-decimal PDs that are 0.01 apart, 71"
" were flagged before and none are now."
msgstr ""
"``kivi.lifetime.significant_increase`` 过去由浮点舍入决定恰好等于阈值的情况：PD 0.04 相对 0.03 被算作升高超过一个百分点，0.45 被算作超过"
" 0.30 的 1.5 倍。现在，与阈值只差末位几个单位的 PD 视为恰好等于阈值，不会被标记，与严格的阈值比较一致。在相差 0.01 的 89 对两位小数 PD 中，过去有 71 "
"对被标记，现在一对也没有。"

msgid ""
"``kivi.lifetime.transition_pd`` accepted a float such as ``horizons=3.0``. A single number of "
"periods must now be an integer, as the ``horizon`` of ``expected_credit_loss`` is; a sequence of "
"horizons may still hold whole numbers as floats."
msgstr ""
"``kivi.lifetime.transition_pd`` 过去接受 ``horizons=3.0`` 这样的浮点数。现在单个期数必须是整数，与 "
"``expected_credit_loss`` 的 ``horizon`` 一致；期限序列仍可以用浮点数表示整数。"

msgid ""
"A list or an object array of numbers with ``pd.NA``, such as ``[0.5, pd.NA]``, raised a "
"``TypeError`` or \"must be real and numeric, got dtype object\" in ``kivi.calibration``, "
"``kivi.scorecard``, ``kivi.strategy`` and ``kivi.lifetime``, and "
"``kivi.calibration.platt_predict([0.5, pd.NA], 1, 0)`` named the valid value 0.5 in its message. "
"These functions now read ``pd.NA`` as a missing value, like None and NaN, and their messages show"
" the first value that is not a number."
msgstr ""
"含有 ``pd.NA`` 的数字列表或 object 数组（例如 ``[0.5, pd.NA]`` ）过去在 ``kivi.calibration`` 、 ``kivi.scorecard`` "
"、 ``kivi.strategy`` 和 ``kivi.lifetime`` 中会引发 ``TypeError`` 或 \"must be real and numeric, got "
"dtype object\"，而 ``kivi.calibration.platt_predict([0.5, pd.NA], 1, 0)`` 的错误信息给出的是有效值 0.5。现在这些函数把 "
"``pd.NA`` 读作缺失值，与 None 和 NaN 相同，错误信息给出第一个不是数字的值。"

msgid ""
"``kivi.scorecard.pd_to_score`` and ``score_to_pd`` read any input as floats: ``score_to_pd`` of a"
" date gave a PD of 0, and ``pd_to_score([\"0.1\", \"0.2\"], ...)`` gave scores. Strings, dates "
"and complex numbers now raise \"must be real and numeric\", as in ``kivi.metrics``, while "
"booleans still count as 1 and 0."
msgstr ""
"``kivi.scorecard.pd_to_score`` 和 ``score_to_pd`` 过去把任何输入都读作浮点数：对日期调用 ``score_to_pd`` 得到 PD 0，而 "
"``pd_to_score([\"0.1\", \"0.2\"], ...)`` 会给出分数。现在字符串、日期和复数会引发 \"must be real and numeric\"，与 "
"``kivi.metrics`` 一致；布尔值仍算作 1 和 0。"

msgid ""
"``kivi.scorecard.reason_codes`` listed a variable twice, such as ``housing, housing, contact``, "
"when a column of ``points`` was repeated. It now raises an error, as ``woe_to_points`` does."
msgstr ""
"当 ``points`` 有重复的列时， ``kivi.scorecard.reason_codes`` 过去会把同一个变量列出两次，例如 ``housing, housing, "
"contact`` 。现在它会引发错误，与 ``woe_to_points`` 一致。"

msgid ""
"``kivi.scorecard.reason_codes`` gave None between two reasons when the points of a group in "
"``table`` were missing, for example after editing the table by hand. Missing or infinite points "
"of a variable of ``points`` now raise an error."
msgstr ""
"当 ``table`` 中某个分组的分值缺失时（例如手工编辑过该表）， ``kivi.scorecard.reason_codes`` 过去会在两个原因之间给出 None。现在， "
"``points`` 中某个变量在 ``table`` 中的分值缺失或为无穷大时会引发错误。"

msgid ""
"``kivi.scorecard.woe_to_points`` aligned a mapping of Series by their index labels, so that one "
"row could combine the WOE values of different applicants. The Series of a mapping must now have "
"identical indices, as the Series that describe the same observations must everywhere in kivi; "
"other values are still matched by position."
msgstr ""
"``kivi.scorecard.woe_to_points`` 过去按索引标签对齐映射中的各个 Series，因此一行可能混合不同申请人的 WOE 值。现在映射中的 Series "
"必须具有相同的索引，与 kivi 中所有描述相同观测的 Series 一致；其他值仍按位置匹配。"

msgid ""
"``kivi.scorecard.score_scaling`` returned NumPy scalars for NumPy arguments, so that a "
"``float32`` ``pdo`` rounded the scores of ``pd_to_score`` and the points of ``points_table`` to "
"single precision. It now returns Python floats."
msgstr ""
"``kivi.scorecard.score_scaling`` 过去对 NumPy 参数返回 NumPy 标量，因此 ``float32`` 的 ``pdo`` 会把 "
"``pd_to_score`` 的分数和 ``points_table`` 的分值舍入到单精度。现在它返回 Python 浮点数。"

msgid ""
"``kivi.scorecard.points_table`` and ``woe_to_points`` said \"tables has no entry for 1 "
"variable(s): 'intercept'\" for the ``coef`` column of ``kivi.selection.logistic_regression``, "
"which includes the intercept. They now say \"coefficients has an 'intercept' entry; drop it and "
"pass it as intercept\"."
msgstr ""
"对于包含截距的 ``kivi.selection.logistic_regression`` 的 ``coef`` 列， ``kivi.scorecard.points_table`` 和 "
"``woe_to_points`` 过去报告 \"tables has no entry for 1 variable(s): 'intercept'\"。现在它们报告 "
"\"coefficients has an 'intercept' entry; drop it and pass it as intercept\"。"

msgid ""
"``kivi.selection.vif`` gave a finite VIF for some exact linear combinations: 1.003 for ``a`` when"
" ``c`` is ``b + 1e-5 * a``, and 5.6e29 for the two columns of a frame with two rows. A column now"
" has an infinite VIF when it is a linear combination of the others up to rounding, as documented;"
" the VIFs of the other columns are unchanged."
msgstr ""
"``kivi.selection.vif`` 过去对某些精确的线性组合给出有限的 VIF：当 ``c`` 为 ``b + 1e-5 * a`` 时， ``a`` 的 VIF 为 "
"1.003；只有两行的数据框中，两列的 VIF 为 5.6e29。现在，某列在舍入误差范围内是其他列的线性组合时，其 VIF 为无穷大，与文档一致；其他列的 VIF 不变。"

msgid ""
"``kivi.vintage.transition_matrix`` read any ``normalize`` that is true in Python as True, so that"
" ``normalize=\"columns\"``, as ``pandas.crosstab`` takes it, gave the shares of each row. It now "
"raises unless ``normalize`` is True or False, as ``kivi.calibration.herfindahl_index`` does."
msgstr ""
"``kivi.vintage.transition_matrix`` 过去把 Python 中为真的任何 ``normalize`` 都当作 True，因此按 "
"``pandas.crosstab`` 的用法传入 ``normalize=\"columns\"`` 时，得到的是每行的占比。现在除非 ``normalize`` 为 True 或 "
"False，否则会引发错误，与 ``kivi.calibration.herfindahl_index`` 一致。"

msgid ""
"``kivi.vintage.transition_matrix`` and ``roll_rates`` gave a missing value in ``states`` a row "
"and a column of its own, although missing values of ``before`` and ``after`` raise. A missing "
"state now raises an error."
msgstr ""
"``kivi.vintage.transition_matrix`` 和 ``roll_rates`` 过去会为 ``states`` 中的缺失值单独生成一行一列，而 ``before`` 和 "
"``after`` 中的缺失值会引发错误。现在缺失的状态会引发错误。"

msgid ""
"``kivi.vintage.vintage_table`` made a column of a negative ``month_on_book``. It now raises an "
"error, because the months on book count from origination."
msgstr "``kivi.vintage.vintage_table`` 过去会为负的 ``month_on_book`` 生成一列。现在会引发错误，因为账龄从放款时开始计算。"

msgid "0.8.0 (2026-11-21)"
msgstr "0.8.0（2026-11-21）"

msgid ""
"``kivi.binning`` groups the categories of categorical variables in the same two steps as numeric "
"binning. ``category_groups`` pools the categories below ``min_share`` or ``min_count`` into one "
"group, and ``chimerge_groups`` sorts the categories by their smoothed WOE and merges neighbours "
"by ChiMerge under ``max_groups``, ``alpha`` and ``min_group_share``. Both return a dict from "
"category to group, take ``special`` and ``weights``, and leave missing values out. "
"``group_categories`` applies the dict to any sample; a category that it does not map raises an "
"error unless ``unseen`` names the group it should join."
msgstr ""
"``kivi.binning`` 以与数值分箱相同的两步对类别变量的类别分组。 ``category_groups`` 把低于 ``min_share`` 或 ``min_count`` "
"的类别归为一组， ``chimerge_groups`` 按平滑后的 WOE 对类别排序，并在 ``max_groups`` 、 ``alpha`` 和 ``min_group_share`` "
"的约束下用 ChiMerge 合并相邻类别。两者都返回从类别到组的 dict，接受 ``special`` 和 ``weights`` ，并排除缺失值。 ``group_categories``"
" 把该 dict 应用到任意样本；分组映射中没有的类别会引发错误，除非 ``unseen`` 指定了它应归入的组。"

msgid ""
"``fit_spec`` groups a categorical column that ``method`` names with ``\"rare\"`` or "
"``\"chimerge\"``; ``special`` and ``options`` then apply to it, and so does ``bins`` with "
"``\"chimerge\"``. ``BinningSpec`` keeps the groupings in a new ``groups`` field and applies them "
"in ``cut`` and ``woe_transform``. Columns without a grouping are fitted as before."
msgstr ""
"``fit_spec`` 对 ``method`` 中以 ``\"rare\"`` 或 ``\"chimerge\"`` 指定的类别列分组，此时 ``special`` 和 "
"``options`` 也适用于该列， ``\"chimerge\"`` 列还适用 ``bins`` 。 ``BinningSpec`` 把分组映射保存在新字段 ``groups`` 中，并在 "
"``cut`` 和 ``woe_transform`` 中应用。没有分组的列与以前的拟合结果相同。"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The unseen policy of a grouped column can name one of its groups as ``{\"group\": label}``: "
"``cut`` then assigns new categories to that group, and ``woe_transform`` gives them its WOE."
msgstr ""
"已分组列的未见分组策略可以用 ``{\"group\": label}`` 指定其中一个组：此时 ``cut`` 把新类别分配到该组， ``woe_transform`` 让它们使用该组的 "
"WOE。"

msgid ""
"A ``BinningSpec`` with a grouped column is saved with ``format_version`` 2, which adds the "
"groupings and the unseen groups; every other specification is still saved as version 1, so "
"earlier versions of kivi read it. ``from_json`` reads both versions."
msgstr ""
"含已分组列的 ``BinningSpec`` 以 ``format_version`` 2 保存，该版本增加了分组映射和未见分组；其他分箱方案仍以版本 1 保存，因此早期版本的 kivi "
"也能读取。 ``from_json`` 能读取这两个版本。"

msgid ""
"The new module ``kivi.lifetime`` covers lifetime PDs and the expected credit loss of IFRS 9. "
"``convert_pd`` converts a PD term structure, such as the cumulative bad rates of a vintage table,"
" between cumulative, marginal and conditional PDs, and keeps the months on book that a cohort has"
" not reached missing. ``transition_pd`` projects the cumulative PD of each state of a transition "
"matrix over any number of periods, with the default state made absorbing."
msgstr ""
"新模块 ``kivi.lifetime`` 提供存续期 PD 和 IFRS 9 的预期信用损失。 ``convert_pd`` 在累计、边际和条件 PD 之间转换 PD 期限结构（例如 "
"vintage 表的累计坏账率），批次尚未达到的账龄保持缺失。 ``transition_pd`` 在违约状态设为吸收态的情况下，推算转移矩阵每个状态在任意期数下的累计 PD。"

msgid ""
"``expected_credit_loss`` adds up the marginal PD, the LGD and the EAD of each period after the "
"reporting date, discounted at the effective interest rate, into the 12-month or the lifetime "
"expected credit loss of each account. The LGD and the EAD can be constants, one value per account"
" or schedules per account and period."
msgstr ""
"``expected_credit_loss`` 把报告日之后每一期的边际 PD、LGD 和 EAD 按实际利率折现求和，得到每个账户的 12 个月或整个存续期预期信用损失。LGD 和 EAD "
"可以是常数、每个账户一个值，或每个账户每期一个值的计划表。"

msgid ""
"``significant_increase`` flags a significant increase in credit risk from a relative and an "
"absolute PD threshold, which have no defaults because they are the entity's policy. "
"``assign_stages`` gives stages 1 to 3 from these flags, the days past due backstops, by default "
"more than 30 days for stage 2 and 90 days or more for stage 3 as presumed by IFRS 9, and "
"defaulted flags, and ``stage_table`` sums the exposure and the loss allowance of each stage, with"
" its coverage ratio."
msgstr ""
"``significant_increase`` 按相对和绝对 PD 阈值标记信用风险显著增加；这两个阈值是主体的政策，因此没有默认值。 ``assign_stages`` "
"根据这些标记、逾期天数兜底标准（默认按 IFRS 9 的假设，第二阶段为逾期超过 30 天，第三阶段为逾期 90 天及以上）以及违约标记确定第一到第三阶段， ``stage_table`` "
"汇总每个阶段的敞口和损失准备，并给出覆盖率。"

msgid ""
"The new module ``kivi.monitoring`` tracks a score over time. ``monitoring_table`` gives one row "
"per period, such as a month, with the number of observations, the known outcomes and events, the "
"AUC, Gini and KS of the known outcomes, and the PSI of the score against a reference period or a "
"reference sample, on bands fitted once on the reference. A missing target marks an outcome that "
"is not known yet; it counts in ``total`` but not in the event columns, and a period without both "
"classes has NaN discrimination instead of an error."
msgstr ""
"新模块 ``kivi.monitoring`` 按期跟踪评分。 ``monitoring_table`` 每期一行（例如每月），给出观测数、已知结果数和事件数、已知结果上的 AUC、Gini 和"
" KS，以及评分相对基准期或基准样本的 PSI，评分段只在基准上拟合一次。缺失的目标值表示结果尚未得知：它计入 ``total`` ，但不计入事件相关的列；两类结果不全的期，其区分能力为 NaN"
" 而不是报错。"

msgid ""
"``stability_table`` gives the PSI of every grouped variable in every period against the same "
"reference, for the variable part of a stability report. Both functions take ``weights``, and "
"integer weights give the same table as repeating rows, for ``monitoring_table`` on the same band "
"edges."
msgstr ""
"``stability_table`` 给出每个已分组变量在每一期相对同一基准的 PSI，用于稳定性报告的变量部分。两个函数都接受 ``weights`` ，整数权重与重复相应行得到的表相同；对"
" ``monitoring_table`` 而言，这要求评分段边界相同。"

msgid ""
"``kivi.metrics.roc_table`` lists the points of the ROC curve, one row per distinct score from the"
" highest to the lowest, with the cumulative event and non-event counts, the true and false "
"positive rates and the precision. The trapezoids under it add up to ``roc_auc``, and the largest "
"gap between the rates is ``ks``."
msgstr ""
"``kivi.metrics.roc_table`` 列出 ROC 曲线上的点，从高到低每个不同的评分一行，包含累计事件数和非事件数、真正例率和假正例率以及精确率。曲线下各梯形的面积之和等于 "
"``roc_auc`` ，两个比率之间的最大差距等于 ``ks`` 。"

msgid ""
"``kivi.metrics.roc_auc_interval`` gives the AUC and the Gini coefficient a standard error and a "
"confidence interval at a ``level``, using DeLong's method with the fast midrank algorithm of Sun "
"and Xu."
msgstr ""
"``kivi.metrics.roc_auc_interval`` 用 DeLong 方法及 Sun 和 Xu 的快速中秩算法，给出 AUC 和 Gini 系数的标准误以及置信水平为 "
"``level`` 的置信区间。"

msgid ""
"``kivi.metrics.delong_test`` tests whether two scores of the same observations have the same AUC,"
" and returns both AUCs, their difference with its standard error and interval, the z statistic "
"and the two-sided p-value."
msgstr "``kivi.metrics.delong_test`` 检验同一批观测的两个评分的 AUC 是否相同，返回两个 AUC、它们的差值及其标准误和区间、z 统计量和双侧 p 值。"

msgid ""
"The standard errors read ``weights`` as frequency weights, so integer weights give the same "
"results as repeating rows. They reproduce the DeLong results that Stata's and SAS's manuals "
"publish for the data of Hanley and McNeil (1982) and of DeLong et al. (1988)."
msgstr ""
"标准误把 ``weights`` 视为频数权重，因此整数权重与重复相应行的结果相同。对于 Hanley 和 McNeil（1982）以及 DeLong 等人（1988）的数据，它们重现了 "
"Stata 和 SAS 手册公布的 DeLong 结果。"

msgid ""
"``BinningSpec.format_version`` is now the version of the JSON format that each specification "
"writes, 1 or 2, instead of a class attribute equal to 1. The new class constant "
"``BinningSpec.FORMAT_VERSION`` is the newest version that kivi reads, now 2."
msgstr ""
"``BinningSpec.format_version`` 现在是每个分箱方案写出的 JSON 格式版本，为 1 或 2，而不再是等于 1 的类属性。新的类常量 "
"``BinningSpec.FORMAT_VERSION`` 是 kivi 能读取的最新版本，目前为 2。"

msgid ""
"The topic guides follow one outline with the same section titles, such as ``Special values``, "
"``Sample weights`` and ``Errors and warnings``, and their openings link to the steps before and "
"after them. The binning guide gathers its special values in one section, and the univariate "
"profile shows special codes after the screening by IV. The first mention of a kivi function in "
"each section links to its API entry."
msgstr ""
"各篇主题指南采用同一结构和相同的小节标题，例如 ``Special values`` （特殊值）、 ``Sample weights`` （样本权重）和 ``Errors and "
"warnings`` （错误与警告），开篇链接到前后两个步骤。分箱指南把特殊值的内容集中到一节，单变量概况在按 IV 筛选之后再介绍特殊值编码。kivi 函数在每一节第一次出现时都链接到其 "
"API 条目。"

msgid ""
"The API reference starts with two new pages: the conventions that every function follows, such as"
" the order of the arguments, keyword-only options, inputs and results, sample weights and error "
"messages, and a glossary of credit risk terms. Its module pages come in the order of the user "
"guide, each with an introduction and a link to its guide, and ``:mod:`` links now reach them."
msgstr ""
"API "
"参考新增两页并排在最前面：一页是所有函数共同遵守的约定，包括参数顺序、仅限关键字的选项、输入与结果、样本权重和错误信息；另一页是信用风险术语表。模块页面按用户指南的顺序排列，每页都有简介和指向对应指南的链接，"
" ``:mod:`` 链接现在也能跳转到这些页面。"

msgid ""
"The migration guide lists the ROC and precision-recall curves, precision, recall, F1 score and "
"confusion matrix of ``BinaryMetrics`` and the correlation heatmaps of ``evaluate/Heatmap.py`` as "
"not ported, with their replacements."
msgstr ""
"迁移指南把 ``BinaryMetrics`` 的 ROC 曲线和精确率-召回率曲线、精确率、召回率、F1 分数和混淆矩阵，以及 ``evaluate/Heatmap.py`` "
"的相关性热力图列为未移植，并给出替代做法。"

msgid ""
"The user guide gains the guides \"Model monitoring\" and \"Lifetime PD and expected credit loss\""
" in their places in a project. The glossary and the conventions page cover the terms and rules of"
" the new functions. The risk modeling workflow reports the DeLong interval of the Gini and points"
" on to monitoring and the expected credit loss. The guides have new charts for category grouping,"
" the ROC curve, the monitoring report, variable stability by period and PD term structures, and "
"the README shows the monitoring and lifetime PD charts."
msgstr ""
"用户指南新增“模型监控”和“存续期 PD 与预期信用损失”两篇指南，并按项目顺序放在相应位置。术语表和约定页涵盖新函数的术语和规则。风控建模流程示例给出 Gini 的 DeLong "
"区间，并引向监控和预期信用损失。各指南新增类别分组、ROC 曲线、监控报告、各期变量稳定性和 PD 期限结构图，README 展示监控图和存续期 PD 图。"

msgid ""
"``kivi.metrics.roc_auc`` and ``kivi.metrics.gini`` could return a value just above 1 when "
"fractional ``weights`` rounded the AUC past it. Both are now at most 1, as documented. Other "
"values are unchanged."
msgstr ""
"使用非整数 ``weights`` 时， ``kivi.metrics.roc_auc`` 和 ``kivi.metrics.gini`` 可能因舍入而返回略大于 1 的值。现在二者都不超过 "
"1，与文档一致；其他取值不变。"

msgid ""
"``kivi.stability.psi_table``, ``kivi.stability.csi_table`` and "
"``kivi.monitoring.stability_table`` counted the groups of the current sample under the wrong "
"labels when both samples were unordered categoricals with the same categories listed in another "
"order, such as ``[\"a\", \"b\"]`` and ``[\"b\", \"a\"]``. The groups are now matched by label."
msgstr ""
"当两个样本都是无序分类且类别相同但排列顺序不同时（例如 ``[\"a\", \"b\"]`` 和 ``[\"b\", \"a\"]`` ）， "
"``kivi.stability.psi_table`` 、 ``kivi.stability.csi_table`` 和 ``kivi.monitoring.stability_table``"
" 会把当前样本的分组计入错误的标签。现在分组按标签匹配。"

msgid ""
"``kivi.stability.psi_table`` and ``kivi.stability.csi_table`` raised pandas' "
"``IntCastingNaNError`` for two samples of ``pandas.cut`` bins on other integer edges when one of "
"them had missing values. Such bins are now joined as intervals of floats, which compare equal to "
"the integer intervals."
msgstr ""
"两个样本是按不同整数边界划分的 ``pandas.cut`` 分箱、且其中一个含有缺失值时， ``kivi.stability.psi_table`` 和 "
"``kivi.stability.csi_table`` 会引发 pandas 的 ``IntCastingNaNError`` 。现在这类分箱以浮点数区间合并，它们与对应的整数区间相等。"

msgid ""
"``kivi.stability.psi_table`` and ``kivi.stability.csi_table`` no longer emit a ``RuntimeWarning``"
" (\"invalid value encountered in cast\") on NumPy older than 2.2 when one sample holds "
"``pandas.cut`` bins with an infinite edge and the other sample has other groups: bins cut on "
"other edges or with unused categories removed, intervals that are not categorical, or other "
"labels. The tables are unchanged."
msgstr ""
"当一个样本是含无穷边界的 ``pandas.cut`` 分箱、而另一个样本是其他分组（按其他边界划分的分箱、移除了未使用类别的分箱、非分类型的区间或其他标签）时， "
"``kivi.stability.psi_table`` 和 ``kivi.stability.csi_table`` 在低于 2.2 版的 NumPy 上不再发出 "
"``RuntimeWarning`` （\"invalid value encountered in cast\"）。表格结果不变。"

msgid ""
"A ``weights`` Series was compared only with the index of the data, so when the score, the values "
"or the groups were an array, it was matched by position to a ``target`` Series with another "
"index. The functions of ``kivi.metrics``, ``kivi.woe.woe_table``, "
"``kivi.calibration.calibration_table``, ``platt_fit`` and ``isotonic_fit``, the supervised "
"functions of ``kivi.binning``, and ``kivi.selection.logistic_regression`` and ``stepwise`` now "
"raise in that case, for example \"target and weights must have identical indices\", as they do "
"for any other two Series that describe the same observations."
msgstr ""
"``weights`` Series 过去只与数据的索引比较，因此当评分、取值或分组是数组时，它会与另一个索引的 ``target`` Series 按位置匹配。 "
"``kivi.metrics`` 的函数、 ``kivi.woe.woe_table`` 、 ``kivi.calibration.calibration_table`` 、 "
"``platt_fit`` 和 ``isotonic_fit`` 、 ``kivi.binning`` 的有监督函数，以及 "
"``kivi.selection.logistic_regression`` 和 ``stepwise`` 现在会在这种情况下引发错误，例如 \"target and weights must "
"have identical indices\"，与描述相同观测的任意其他两个 Series 的处理方式一致。"

msgid "0.7.0 (2026-11-20)"
msgstr "0.7.0（2026-11-20）"

msgid ""
"``kivi.datasets.make_applications`` simulates seeded loan applications with numeric and "
"categorical features, the PD of an incumbent scorecard, policy declines, the approval decision "
"and a true default flag for every applicant, to try reject inference on."
msgstr ""
"``kivi.datasets.make_applications`` 按种子模拟贷款申请数据，每个申请人都有数值型和类别型特征、现行评分卡的 "
"PD、政策拒绝、审批决策和真实的违约标记，可用来试验拒绝推断。"

msgid ""
"``kivi.calibration.master_scale`` builds a master scale from the PD of each grade, such as a "
"geometric grid from ``numpy.geomspace``: one row per grade with its lower bound, PD and upper "
"bound, covering 0 to 1. The bounds are the geometric means of adjacent PDs by default, or their "
"arithmetic means with ``boundary=\"arithmetic\"``, as in the 0.2 versions."
msgstr ""
"``kivi.calibration.master_scale`` 根据每个等级的 PD 构建主标尺，例如由 ``numpy.geomspace`` "
"生成的几何网格：每个等级一行，包含其下界、PD 和上界，覆盖 0 到 1。界限默认取相邻 PD 的几何平均数，设置 ``boundary=\"arithmetic\"`` 时取其算术平均数，与 "
"0.2 版本相同。"

msgid ""
"``fit_grade_pd`` fits the PD of each grade to observed default rates, with the logarithm of the "
"rate a straight line in the grade number, by least squares weighted with the number of "
"observations. A grade without defaults enters the fit with ``smoothing`` defaults, and a grade "
"without observations gets a PD from the line."
msgstr ""
"``fit_grade_pd`` 按观测违约率拟合每个等级的 PD：把违约率的对数拟合为等级编号的直线，使用以观测数为权重的最小二乘法。没有违约的等级以 ``smoothing`` "
"次违约参与拟合，没有观测的等级从这条直线得到 PD。"

msgid ""
"``assign_grades`` gives each predicted PD the grade of a scale as an ordered categorical, which "
"``calibration_table`` counts directly, in the order of the scale. A PD on a bound goes to the "
"lower grade, as with ``pandas.cut``."
msgstr ""
"``assign_grades`` 以有序分类变量的形式为每个预测 PD 指定标尺上的等级， ``calibration_table`` 可以直接按标尺的顺序统计这些等级。恰好落在界限上的 PD"
" 归入较低的等级，与 ``pandas.cut`` 相同。"

msgid ""
"The new module ``kivi.reject_inference`` infers outcomes for rejected applicants, so that a "
"scorecard developed on approved applicants can be refitted on all of them. ``fuzzy_augmentation``"
" splits each reject into a bad and a good row weighted by its PD, ``parceling`` labels the "
"rejects of each score band at the band's bad rate with a seeded generator, or returns the "
"expected weights, and ``reweighting`` weights the approved applicants of each band by the inverse"
" of its approval rate. A ``factor`` above 1 raises the inferred bad rate, and bands without "
"approved applicants raise an error."
msgstr ""
"新模块 ``kivi.reject_inference`` 推断拒绝申请人的结果，使在获批申请人上开发的评分卡能在全部申请人上重新拟合。 ``fuzzy_augmentation`` "
"把每个拒绝申请人拆成按其 PD 加权的一行坏样本和一行好样本； ``parceling`` 用带种子的生成器按各评分段的坏账率标记其中的拒绝申请人，或者返回期望权重； "
"``reweighting`` 以各评分段通过率的倒数为该段获批申请人加权。大于 1 的 ``factor`` 会提高推断的坏账率，没有获批申请人的评分段会引发错误。"

msgid ""
"``logistic_regression`` and ``stepwise`` take ``weights``, frequency weights like those of "
"statsmodels' ``GLM(freq_weights=...)``. Integer weights give the same coefficients, standard "
"errors and selection as repeating rows; weights that do not count observations, such as those of "
"reject inference, make the standard errors and p-values too small."
msgstr ""
"``logistic_regression`` 和 ``stepwise`` 接受 ``weights`` ，即与 statsmodels 的 ``GLM(freq_weights=...)``"
" 相同的频数权重。整数权重与重复行得到相同的系数、标准误和变量选择；不表示观测个数的权重（例如拒绝推断的权重）会使标准误和 p 值偏小。"

msgid ""
"The new module ``kivi.strategy`` supports the credit decisions that follow a scorecard. "
"``cutoff_table`` shows, for each candidate cut-off of a PD or of negated points, the approval "
"rate, the bad rate of the approved book, the shares of bads and goods it rejects and, with "
"``loss``, the expected loss it approves. Scores at or below the cut-off are approved, so tied "
"scores always get the same decision."
msgstr ""
"新模块 ``kivi.strategy`` 支撑评分卡之后的信贷决策。``cutoff_table`` 针对 PD "
"或取负分数的每个候选截断点，给出通过率、通过客群的坏账率、被拒绝的坏客户和好客户所占比例，传入 ``loss`` "
"时还给出通过客群的预期损失。评分不高于截断点即予以通过，因此相同评分总是得到相同的决策。"

msgid ""
"``swap_set`` compares the decisions of a current and a new score at their cut-offs: the "
"applicants both approve, the swap-ins and swap-outs, and those both decline, with event rates "
"where outcomes are known. A missing target marks an unknown outcome, such as that of an applicant"
" the current score declined."
msgstr ""
"``swap_set`` "
"在各自的截断点上比较现行评分与新评分的决策：两者都通过的申请人、换入和换出，以及两者都拒绝的申请人，并在结果已知时给出事件率。缺失的目标值表示结果未知，例如被现行评分拒绝的申请人。"

msgid ""
"``expected_loss`` multiplies PD, LGD and EAD, and ``expected_loss_table`` adds up the exposure "
"and the expected loss of each grade, with the expected loss rate and the exposure-weighted PD."
msgstr "``expected_loss`` 将 PD、LGD 与 EAD 相乘，``expected_loss_table`` 汇总每个等级的敞口和预期损失，并给出预期损失率和按敞口加权的 PD。"

msgid ""
"The new module ``kivi.univariate`` profiles the candidates of a model. ``profile_table`` "
"summarizes every column of a data frame in one row: its kind, missing values, distinct and most "
"frequent values and, for numeric columns, the range, quantiles, mean and standard deviation. With"
" a target it adds the event rates and lifts of missing and non-missing rows, the IV of a quick "
"binning and the Gini coefficient of numeric values. Tied quantiles are recorded in the "
"``tied_bins`` column instead of raising a warning for each column, and ``special`` codes and "
"``weights`` work as in ``fit_spec``."
msgstr ""
"新模块 ``kivi.univariate`` 对模型的候选变量进行概况分析。 ``profile_table`` "
"用一行概括数据框的每一列：类型、缺失值、不同取值个数和最常见的取值；数值列还给出取值范围、分位数、均值和标准差。有目标变量时，还会加入缺失行与非缺失行的事件率和提升度、快速分箱的 IV "
"以及数值取值的 Gini 系数。分位数重合会记录在 ``tied_bins`` 列中，而不会对每一列发出警告； ``special`` 编码和 ``weights`` 的用法与 "
"``fit_spec`` 相同。"

msgid ""
"The risk modeling workflow screens the candidates with ``profile_table``, calibrates the PD on a "
"master scale with ``master_scale`` and ``assign_grades``, and sets a cut-off with "
"``cutoff_table`` and ``expected_loss_table``. The user guide has new charts for cut-off curves, "
"reject inference, grade PDs and missing values, and the README shows the cut-off and reject "
"inference charts."
msgstr ""
"风控建模流程示例改用 ``profile_table`` 筛选候选变量，用 ``master_scale`` 和 ``assign_grades`` 在主标尺上校准 PD，并用 "
"``cutoff_table`` 和 ``expected_loss_table`` 设定截断点。用户指南新增截断点曲线、拒绝推断、等级 PD 和缺失值图，README "
"也展示了截断点图和拒绝推断图。"

msgid ""
"``gains_table`` warned about tied scores by suggesting the ``special`` argument of ``bin_edges``,"
" which ``gains_table`` does not take. It now suggests fewer bins or explicit edges, as "
"``cutoff_table`` does, and the warning points at the line that called it."
msgstr ""
"``gains_table`` 在评分并列时发出的警告曾建议使用 ``bin_edges`` 的 ``special`` 参数，而 ``gains_table`` 并没有这个参数。现在它与 "
"``cutoff_table`` 一样，建议减少箱数或给出明确的边界，并且警告指向调用它的那一行。"

msgid "0.6.0 (2026-11-20)"
msgstr "0.6.0（2026-11-20）"

msgid ""
"``kivi.calibration.platt_fit`` and ``platt_predict`` calibrate a score with a logistic curve, and"
" ``isotonic_fit`` and ``isotonic_predict`` with a step function that rises with the score. The "
"fits return plain numbers, a slope and an intercept or band edges and their probabilities, that "
"apply to the scores of any later sample."
msgstr ""
"``kivi.calibration.platt_fit`` 和 ``platt_predict`` 用逻辑曲线校准评分， ``isotonic_fit`` 和 "
"``isotonic_predict`` 则用随评分上升的阶梯函数进行校准。拟合结果是普通的数值（斜率和截距，或分段边界及其概率），可以应用到之后任何样本的评分上。"

msgid ""
"``kivi.stability.csi_table`` computes the characteristic stability index of a scorecard variable:"
" the change of each group's share from the reference to the current sample, multiplied by the "
"group's points. Its sum is the change of the variable's average points, and over all variables "
"the change of the average score. The shares are not smoothed, and a group without points raises "
"an error unless ``unseen_points`` gives its points."
msgstr ""
"``kivi.stability.csi_table`` "
"计算评分卡变量的特征稳定性指标：每组占比从基准样本到当前样本的变化乘以该组的分值。其总和是该变量平均分值的变化，对所有变量求和则是平均分数的变化。占比不做平滑；没有分值的分组会引发错误，除非用 "
"``unseen_points`` 给出其分值。"

msgid ""
"``kivi.datasets.load_bank`` loads the bank marketing data. ``Dataset.bank_data`` returns the same"
" data and keeps working without a warning."
msgstr "``kivi.datasets.load_bank`` 读取银行营销数据。 ``Dataset.bank_data`` 返回相同的数据，并且可以继续使用，不会发出警告。"

msgid ""
"``kivi.datasets.make_loan_panel`` simulates a seeded monthly panel of instalment loans whose "
"delinquency rolls forward and cures, to try the vintage and roll-rate functions on."
msgstr "``kivi.datasets.make_loan_panel`` 按给定种子模拟分期贷款的月度面板数据，其中逾期会向前滚动，也会回到正常，可用来试用 Vintage 和滚动率相关函数。"

msgid ""
"``reason_codes`` takes ``unseen_points``, the points of applicants in groups that "
"``woe_transform`` encoded with ``unseen``, one value or values by variable. Points that match no "
"group but lie within ``atol`` of ``unseen_points`` cost nothing, so the variable is not one of "
"those applicants' reasons. Every other mismatch still raises an error, which now suggests "
"checking ``atol`` and the model and scaling first."
msgstr ""
"``reason_codes`` 新增 ``unseen_points`` 参数，即 ``woe_transform`` 用 ``unseen`` "
"编码的分组中申请人的分值，可以是一个值，也可以按变量给出。与任何分组都不匹配、但与 ``unseen_points`` 相差不超过 ``atol`` "
"的分值视为没有造成损失，因此该变量不会成为这些申请人的原因。其他任何不匹配仍会引发错误，错误信息现在会先提示检查 ``atol`` 以及模型和刻度。"

msgid ""
"The new module ``kivi.spec`` bins all the columns of a data frame at once. ``fit_spec`` fits each"
" numeric column with ``bin_edges`` or a supervised method chosen by column, or with given edges, "
"and measures the WOE of every group; other columns keep their labels. The binning is never "
"changed automatically."
msgstr ""
"新模块 ``kivi.spec`` 一次对数据框的所有列分箱。 ``fit_spec`` 用 ``bin_edges`` 、按列选定的有监督方法或给定的边界拟合每个数值列，并计算每个分组的 "
"WOE；其他列保留其标签。分箱从不自动更改。"

msgid ""
"The resulting ``BinningSpec`` groups a sample with ``cut``, encodes it with ``woe_transform`` "
"using an unseen-group policy by column, and keeps the ``woe_table`` of every column for review. "
"``to_json`` and ``from_json`` save and load it without changing the groups or the WOE encoding, "
"so production reproduces development exactly."
msgstr ""
"得到的 ``BinningSpec`` 用 ``cut`` 对样本分组，用 ``woe_transform`` 按列的未见分组策略编码，并保留每一列的 ``woe_table`` 供审阅。 "
"``to_json`` 和 ``from_json`` 保存并加载它，分组和 WOE 编码都不会改变，因此生产环境可以完全复现开发时的结果。"

msgid ""
"The new module ``kivi.vintage`` analyses loan portfolios. ``vintage_table`` gives the cumulative "
"bad rate of each origination cohort by month on book, by count or by amount lent, and leaves the "
"months that a cohort has not reached as NaN. ``transition_matrix`` counts the movements of loans "
"between delinquency buckets or of obligors between rating grades, as counts, row shares or sums "
"of balances, and ``roll_rates`` gives the share of each bucket that rolls to the next worse one."
msgstr ""
"新模块 ``kivi.vintage`` 用于分析贷款资产组合。 ``vintage_table`` 按账龄给出每个放款批次的累计坏账率，可以按笔数或按放款金额计算，并把批次尚未达到的账龄留为 "
"NaN。 ``transition_matrix`` 统计贷款在逾期档位之间、或债务人在评级之间的迁移，结果可以是计数、行内比例或余额之和； ``roll_rates`` "
"给出每个档位滚动到下一个更差档位的比例。"

msgid ""
"``roc_auc``, ``gini``, ``ks``, ``gains_table``, ``brier_score`` and ``calibration_table`` take "
"``weights``, like ``woe_table``. Counts become sums of weights, and integer weights give the same"
" result as repeating rows, for ``gains_table`` on fixed edges."
msgstr ""
"``roc_auc`` 、 ``gini`` 、 ``ks`` 、 ``gains_table`` 、 ``brier_score`` 和 ``calibration_table`` 与 "
"``woe_table`` 一样接受 ``weights`` 。计数变为权重之和，整数权重与重复相应行的结果相同（ ``gains_table`` 须使用固定边界）。"

msgid ""
"The risk modeling workflow saves the shortlist's binning with ``fit_spec`` and adds the "
"characteristic stability index of every scorecard variable to its stability report. The user "
"guide has new charts for gains, calibration and vintage curves, and the README shows the gains "
"and vintage charts."
msgstr ""
"风控建模流程示例用 ``fit_spec`` 保存入选变量的分箱，并在稳定性报告中加入每个评分卡变量的特征稳定性指数（CSI）。用户指南新增增益、校准和 vintage 曲线图，README "
"也展示了增益图和 vintage 曲线图。"

msgid "On pandas 2.0, ``calibration_table`` no longer fails when the target has a nullable integer dtype."
msgstr "在 pandas 2.0 上，目标为可空整数类型时， ``calibration_table`` 不再报错。"

msgid ""
"``cut``, ``bin_edges`` and the supervised binning functions match special codes after converting "
"numeric strings, so a column read as text, where ``pdays`` holds ``\"-1\"``, gives the code "
"``-1`` its own group instead of putting it into an interval. Boolean special codes, which ``True "
"== 1`` made match the value 1, raise an error."
msgstr ""
"``cut`` 、 ``bin_edges`` 和有监督分箱函数会在转换数字字符串之后再匹配特殊编码，因此按文本读入的列（例如 ``pdays`` 中的 ``\"-1\"`` ）会让编码 "
"``-1`` 单独成组，而不是落入某个区间。布尔型特殊编码会报错：由于 ``True == 1`` ，它们原先会匹配取值 1。"

msgid ""
"``kivi.evaluate`` is removed; import ``psi_table`` and the other stability functions from "
"``kivi.stability``."
msgstr "移除 ``kivi.evaluate`` ；请从 ``kivi.stability`` 导入 ``psi_table`` 等稳定性函数。"

msgid "``bin_edges`` no longer accepts ``method`` by position; pass ``method=\"uniform\"`` by keyword."
msgstr "``bin_edges`` 不再接受按位置传入的 ``method`` ；请用关键字传入，例如 ``method=\"uniform\"`` 。"

msgid "0.5.0 (2026-11-20)"
msgstr "0.5.0（2026-11-20）"

msgid ""
"The new module ``kivi.calibration`` checks the calibration of PDs. ``prior_correction`` and "
"``corrected_intercept`` correct a model for a development sample with another event rate. "
"``calibration_table`` compares the observed and predicted default rates of master scale grades or"
" other groups, which ``binomial_test``, ``jeffreys_test`` and ``hosmer_lemeshow`` then test. "
"``herfindahl_index`` measures the concentration of the grades."
msgstr ""
"新模块 ``kivi.calibration`` 用于检查 PD 的校准情况。 ``prior_correction`` 和 ``corrected_intercept`` "
"在开发样本的事件率与总体不同时校正模型。 ``calibration_table`` 比较主标尺等级或其他分组的观测违约率与预测违约率，再由 ``binomial_test`` 、 "
"``jeffreys_test`` 和 ``hosmer_lemeshow`` 进行检验。 ``herfindahl_index`` 衡量各等级的集中程度。"

msgid ""
"``kivi.woe.woe``, ``kivi.woe.iv`` and ``kivi.stability.psi`` compute WOE, IV and PSI from counts "
"that are already aggregated, including weighted counts."
msgstr "``kivi.woe.woe`` 、 ``kivi.woe.iv`` 和 ``kivi.stability.psi`` 可直接根据已汇总的计数（包括加权计数）计算 WOE、IV 和 PSI。"

msgid "``kivi.stability`` holds ``psi_table`` and ``psi``."
msgstr "``kivi.stability`` 模块包含 ``psi_table`` 和 ``psi`` 。"

msgid ""
"``kivi.metrics`` evaluates a score against a binary target. ``roc_auc``, ``gini`` and ``ks`` "
"measure how well it ranks events above non-events, ``gains_table`` reports event rates, captured "
"events, KS and lift by score band, and ``brier_score`` compares predicted probabilities with the "
"outcomes. Like ``woe_table``, each takes the score first and the target second, the reverse of "
"scikit-learn. A higher score must mean a higher event probability, so negate scorecard points "
"before passing them in."
msgstr ""
"``kivi.metrics`` 根据二分类目标评估评分。``roc_auc``、``gini`` 和 ``ks`` 衡量评分把事件排在非事件之前的能力，``gains_table`` "
"按评分段报告事件率、捕获的事件、KS 和提升度，``brier_score`` 将预测概率与实际结果进行比较。与 ``woe_table`` 一样，这些函数都是评分在前、目标在后，与 "
"scikit-learn 的顺序相反。评分越高必须表示事件概率越高，因此评分卡分数须取负后再传入。"

msgid ""
"``bin_edges``, ``chimerge_edges``, ``tree_edges``, ``monotonic_edges`` and ``woe_table`` take "
"``weights``, and ``psi_table`` takes ``reference_weights`` and ``current_weights``. Counts become"
" sums of weights, quantile edges become weighted quantiles by the inverted CDF, and observations "
"or groups with zero weight are left out."
msgstr ""
"``bin_edges`` 、 ``chimerge_edges`` 、 ``tree_edges`` 、 ``monotonic_edges`` 和 ``woe_table`` 新增 "
"``weights`` 参数， ``psi_table`` 新增 ``reference_weights`` 和 ``current_weights`` "
"参数。计数变为权重之和，等频边界变为逆累积分布意义下的加权分位数，权重为零的观测或分组会被排除。"

msgid ""
"The new module ``kivi.scorecard`` scales a logistic regression on WOE values into scorecard "
"points. ``score_scaling``, ``pd_to_score`` and ``score_to_pd`` convert between probabilities and "
"scores from the points to double the odds, a base score and base odds. ``points_table`` gives the"
" points of every group, ``woe_to_points`` those of each applicant, and ``reason_codes`` names the"
" variables that cost an applicant the most points."
msgstr ""
"新模块 ``kivi.scorecard`` 把基于 WOE 的逻辑回归转换为评分卡分值。 ``score_scaling`` 、 ``pd_to_score`` 和 "
"``score_to_pd`` 依据 PDO（几率翻倍所需分数）、基准分数和基准几率，在概率与分数之间相互转换。 ``points_table`` 给出每个分组的分值， "
"``woe_to_points`` 给出每个申请人的分值， ``reason_codes`` 列出让申请人失分最多的变量。"

msgid ""
"The new ``kivi.selection`` module selects the variables of a scorecard from WOE-encoded "
"candidates. ``correlation_filter`` drops one variable of each strongly correlated pair, keeping "
"the one with the higher priority, such as its IV. ``vif`` computes variance inflation factors."
msgstr ""
"新增 ``kivi.selection`` 模块，用于从 WOE 编码的候选变量中筛选评分卡变量。 ``correlation_filter`` "
"对每一对强相关的变量剔除其中一个，保留优先级（例如 IV）较高的那个。 ``vif`` 计算方差膨胀因子。"

msgid ""
"``logistic_regression`` fits a logistic regression in NumPy and reports each coefficient with its"
" standard error, Wald z statistic and p-value. It raises ``SeparationError`` when the variables "
"separate the classes, so that the estimates do not exist."
msgstr ""
"``logistic_regression`` 用 NumPy 拟合逻辑回归，并报告每个系数及其标准误、Wald z 统计量和 p 值。当变量把两类完全分开、以致估计值不存在时，它会抛出 "
"``SeparationError`` 。"

msgid ""
"``stepwise`` selects variables by their p-values in forward, backward or both directions. By "
"default, it keeps every coefficient positive, as expected for kivi's WOE."
msgstr "``stepwise`` 按 p 值进行向前、向后或双向的变量筛选。默认情况下，它使每个系数都为正，这正是 kivi 的 WOE 所预期的。"

msgid ""
"``woe_transform`` replaces each group with its WOE from a ``woe_table`` result, the encoding used"
" by a scorecard model. Groups that are not in the table raise an error unless ``unseen`` gives "
"their WOE."
msgstr ""
"``woe_transform`` 用 ``woe_table`` 结果中的 WOE 替换每个分组，这正是评分卡模型使用的编码。不在表中的分组会引发错误，除非用 ``unseen`` 指定其 "
"WOE。"

msgid ""
"The API reference has a page for each module. Links to a function on the former single page now "
"go to the page of its module."
msgstr "API 参考改为每个模块一页。原来指向单页中某个函数的链接，现在改为指向该函数所在模块的页面。"

msgid ""
"``method`` of ``bin_edges`` is keyword-only. Passing it by position raises a ``FutureWarning`` "
"and stops working in 0.6.0."
msgstr "``bin_edges`` 的 ``method`` 参数改为仅限关键字。按位置传入会发出 ``FutureWarning`` ，并将在 0.6.0 中失效。"

msgid ""
"``kivi.evaluate`` is deprecated in favour of ``kivi.stability``. Importing ``psi_table`` from it "
"raises a ``FutureWarning``, and the module is removed in 0.6.0."
msgstr ""
"``kivi.evaluate`` 已弃用，请改用 ``kivi.stability`` 。从中导入 ``psi_table`` 会发出 ``FutureWarning`` ，该模块将在 "
"0.6.0 中移除。"

msgid ""
"The risk modeling workflow runs end to end: variable selection, a fitted logistic model, "
"scorecard points, evaluation, calibration and score stability."
msgstr "风控建模流程现在完整串联：变量筛选、逻辑回归拟合、评分卡分值、模型评估、校准以及分数稳定性。"

msgid ""
"``woe_table`` also reports ``total``, ``total_share`` and ``event_rate`` for each group, the "
"columns of a classing report. They use the observed counts; only ``non_event_share`` and "
"``event_share`` are smoothed."
msgstr ""
"``woe_table`` 为每组新增 ``total`` 、 ``total_share`` 和 ``event_rate`` 三列，即分箱报表中常用的列。它们使用实际观测到的计数；只有 "
"``non_event_share`` 和 ``event_share`` 经过平滑。"

msgid ""
"``woe_table`` and ``psi_table`` no longer cause pandas to issue ``RuntimeWarning: invalid value "
"encountered in cast`` on NumPy older than 2.2 when the groups come from ``pandas.cut`` with "
"infinite edges."
msgstr ""
"分组来自带无穷端点的 ``pandas.cut`` 时， ``woe_table`` 和 ``psi_table`` 在 NumPy 2.2 以下的版本上不再引发 pandas 的 "
"``RuntimeWarning: invalid value encountered in cast`` 。"

msgid ""
"On pandas 2.0, ``cut`` and the supervised binning functions no longer fail when nullable integer "
"or float values are combined with ``special``."
msgstr "在 pandas 2.0 上，可空整数或浮点数与 ``special`` 一起使用时， ``cut`` 和监督分箱函数不再报错。"

msgid "0.4.0 (2026-11-19)"
msgstr "0.4.0（2026-11-19）"

msgid ""
"``bin_edges`` takes a ``special`` argument. Codes such as ``-1`` or ``-999`` are left out when "
"the edges are fitted."
msgstr "``bin_edges`` 新增 ``special`` 参数。 ``-1`` 、 ``-999`` 等编码在拟合边界时会被排除。"

msgid ""
"``kivi.binning.cut`` assigns values to the fitted bins and gives each special value its own "
"group. Without special values it returns the same result as ``pandas.cut``."
msgstr "``kivi.binning.cut`` 把取值分配到拟合好的各箱，并让每个特殊值单独成组。不传特殊值时，结果与 ``pandas.cut`` 相同。"

msgid ""
"``chimerge_edges``, ``tree_edges`` and ``monotonic_edges`` fit edges from a binary target: "
"ChiMerge merging of fine quantile bins, decision-tree splits by entropy or Gini with a minimum "
"bin share, and merging until the WOE is monotonic. They accept the same array-like inputs as "
"``woe_table``, return infinite-ended edges like ``bin_edges`` and need only NumPy and pandas."
msgstr ""
"``chimerge_edges``、``tree_edges`` 和 ``monotonic_edges`` 依据二分类目标拟合边界：分别是对等频细分箱做 ChiMerge "
"合并、按熵或基尼指数做决策树切分（可设定最小箱占比），以及合并到 WOE 单调为止。它们接受与 ``woe_table`` 相同的类数组输入，与 ``bin_edges`` "
"一样返回两端为无穷的边界，只依赖 NumPy 和 pandas。"

msgid "The binning guide compares the three methods on the bank data, with a chart for each."
msgstr "分箱指南在银行数据上对比了这三种方法，并为每种方法配有图表。"

msgid ""
"``chimerge_edges``, ``tree_edges`` and ``monotonic_edges`` take ``special`` like ``bin_edges``. "
"The codes are left out of the fit together with their labels, and ``kivi.binning.cut`` with the "
"same codes gives each one its own group."
msgstr ""
"``chimerge_edges``、``tree_edges`` 和 ``monotonic_edges`` 与 ``bin_edges`` 一样接受 ``special`` "
"参数。这些编码连同其标签不参与拟合；再把相同的编码传给 ``kivi.binning.cut`` ，即可让每个编码单独成组。"

msgid ""
"``bin_edges``, ``woe_table`` and ``psi_table`` accept any one-dimensional array-like input, such "
"as a list or a NumPy array. Group and target series passed to ``woe_table`` must still share an "
"index; arrays and lists are matched by position."
msgstr ""
"``bin_edges`` 、 ``woe_table`` 和 ``psi_table`` 接受任意一维类数组输入，例如列表或 NumPy 数组。传给 ``woe_table`` "
"的分组与标签序列仍须共享同一索引；数组和列表按位置对应。"

msgid ""
"``bin_edges`` issues a ``UserWarning`` when tied edges leave fewer bins than requested. The "
"message names the most frequent value so that it can be passed in ``special``."
msgstr "边界重合导致实际箱数少于期望箱数时， ``bin_edges`` 会发出 ``UserWarning`` 。提示信息会写出出现次数最多的取值，便于将其传给 ``special`` 。"

msgid "Error messages name the argument and report the value received."
msgstr "错误信息会写明参数名以及收到的值。"

msgid ""
"``kivi.__version__`` is ``\"0+unknown\"`` when kivi is imported from a source tree that is not "
"installed, instead of raising an error."
msgstr "从未安装的源码目录导入 kivi 时， ``kivi.__version__`` 为 ``\"0+unknown\"`` ，不再抛出错误。"

msgid "Group counts use ``numpy.bincount``, which is faster on large samples."
msgstr "分组计数改用 ``numpy.bincount`` ，在大样本上更快。"

msgid "The API reference documents errors, warnings, formulas and related functions."
msgstr "API 参考补充了异常、警告、公式和相关函数的说明。"

msgid ""
"``woe_table`` and ``psi_table`` list categorical groups, including the result of ``pandas.cut``, "
"in category order with missing values last. Other labels keep the order in which they first "
"appear. Previously all groups followed first appearance, and ``sort_index`` was needed to put "
"intervals in order."
msgstr ""
"``woe_table`` 和 ``psi_table`` 对分类型分组（包括 ``pandas.cut`` "
"的结果）按类别顺序排列，缺失值排在最后。其他标签仍按首次出现的次序排列。此前所有分组都按首次出现的次序排列，需要用 ``sort_index`` 才能让区间有序。"

msgid "0.3.0 (2026-11-19)"
msgstr "0.3.0（2026-11-19）"

msgid ""
"A rewrite around a small pandas core. Read :doc:`migration` before upgrading code written for "
"0.2.x."
msgstr "围绕精简的 pandas 核心重写。升级为 0.2.x 编写的代码前，请先阅读 :doc:`migration`。"

msgid ""
"``bin_edges`` fits quantile or uniform edges on a reference sample. The outer edges are infinite,"
" so the result can be passed to ``pandas.cut`` for any later sample."
msgstr "``bin_edges`` 在基准样本上拟合等频或等距边界。最外侧边界为无穷，因此结果可以传给 ``pandas.cut``，用于之后的任意样本。"

msgid ""
"``woe_table`` and ``psi_table`` return raw counts, smoothed shares and a contribution for each "
"group, including missing values."
msgstr "``woe_table`` 和 ``psi_table`` 返回每组的原始计数、平滑后的占比和单组贡献，缺失值也单独成组。"

msgid "Documentation in English and Simplified Chinese."
msgstr "提供英文和简体中文文档。"

msgid "NumPy and pandas are required dependencies. The 0.2.8 wheel placed them behind the ``all`` extra."
msgstr "NumPy 和 pandas 成为必需依赖。0.2.8 的 wheel 曾将它们放在 ``all`` 可选依赖中。"

msgid "The ``psi`` column holds the contribution of each bin. It previously repeated the overall total."
msgstr "``psi`` 列给出每箱的贡献，此前该列逐行重复总值。"

msgid ""
"Zero counts are replaced before each distribution is normalized, and reported counts are no "
"longer modified."
msgstr "先替换零计数，再分别对各分布归一化；结果中的计数不再被修改。"

msgid ""
"Spark, SQL, AHP, feature selection, model wrappers, weighted and supervised binning and "
"scorecards. They remain in the repository history."
msgstr "Spark、SQL、AHP、特征选择、模型封装、加权与监督分箱以及评分卡。这些代码仍保留在仓库历史中。"

msgid "Migration guide"
msgstr "迁移指南"

msgid "From 0.9 to 1.0"
msgstr "从 0.9 迁移到 1.0"

msgid ""
"kivi 1.0 removes what 0.9 deprecated. Code that runs on 0.9 without a ``FutureWarning`` runs on "
"1.0 unchanged, except where it imports ``Dataset`` or uses the result of :func:`~kivi.woe.woe` "
"for Series counts. To find the calls to change, run the code or its tests on 0.9 with "
"``FutureWarning`` turned into an error, as ``python -W error::FutureWarning`` or ``pytest -W "
"error::FutureWarning`` do."
msgstr ""
"kivi 1.0 移除了 0.9 中弃用的内容。在 0.9 上运行而不发出 ``FutureWarning`` 的代码可以不加修改地在 1.0 上运行，只有导入 ``Dataset`` 或对 "
"Series 计数使用 :func:`~kivi.woe.woe` 结果的代码除外。要找出需要修改的调用，可以在 0.9 上把 ``FutureWarning`` "
"变为错误来运行代码或其测试，例如 ``python -W error::FutureWarning`` 或 ``pytest -W error::FutureWarning`` 。"

msgid "0.9"
msgstr "0.9"

msgid "1.0"
msgstr "1.0"

msgid ""
"``smoothing=True`` in ``woe_table``, ``woe``, ``iv``, ``psi_table``, ``psi``, "
"``monotonic_edges``, ``fit_grade_pd``, ``monitoring_table`` and ``stability_table`` counts as 1 "
"with a ``FutureWarning``"
msgstr ""
"``woe_table`` 、 ``woe`` 、 ``iv`` 、 ``psi_table`` 、 ``psi`` 、 ``monotonic_edges`` 、 "
"``fit_grade_pd`` 、 ``monitoring_table`` 和 ``stability_table`` 中的 ``smoothing=True`` 按 1 计算，并发出 "
"``FutureWarning``"

msgid ""
"Raises a ``ValueError``, as in every other function. Pass ``smoothing=1`` for the result of 0.9, "
"or leave ``smoothing`` out for the default 0.5"
msgstr "引发 ``ValueError`` ，与其他所有函数一致。传入 ``smoothing=1`` 可得到 0.9 的结果，省略 ``smoothing`` 则使用默认值 0.5"

msgid ""
"``woe``, ``iv`` and ``psi`` match two count Series with different indices by position, with a "
"``FutureWarning``"
msgstr "``woe`` 、 ``iv`` 和 ``psi`` 按位置匹配索引不同的两个计数 Series，并发出 ``FutureWarning``"

msgid ""
"Raise a ``ValueError``. Align the counts first, as in ``reference, current = "
"reference.align(current, fill_value=0)``, or pass arrays when both list the groups in the same "
"order"
msgstr ""
"引发 ``ValueError`` 。请先对齐计数，例如 ``reference, current = reference.align(current, fill_value=0)`` "
"；只有当两者的分组顺序相同时才传入数组"

msgid "``woe`` returns an array"
msgstr "``woe`` 返回数组"

msgid ""
"Returns a Series named ``woe`` with the index of the counts when a count argument is a Series. "
"Use ``.to_numpy()`` for the array and ``.iloc`` to select by position; lists and arrays still "
"give an array"
msgstr "当某个计数参数是 Series 时，返回具有计数索引、名为 ``woe`` 的 Series。用 ``.to_numpy()`` 取得数组，用 ``.iloc`` 按位置选取；列表和数组仍返回数组"

msgid "``Dataset.bank_data()`` warns with a ``FutureWarning``"
msgstr "``Dataset.bank_data()`` 发出 ``FutureWarning``"

msgid "Removed, together with the class ``Dataset``. ``kivi.datasets.load_bank()`` returns the same frame"
msgstr "已移除，类 ``Dataset`` 也一并移除。 ``kivi.datasets.load_bank()`` 返回相同的数据框"

msgid "``isotonic_predict(score, edges, probabilities=...)`` warns with a ``FutureWarning``"
msgstr "``isotonic_predict(score, edges, probabilities=...)`` 发出 ``FutureWarning``"

msgid "Removed. Pass ``probability=``, or the probabilities by position"
msgstr "已移除。请传入 ``probability=`` ，或按位置传入各分段的概率"

msgid ""
"kivi 1.0 still supports Python 3.10, NumPy 1.24 and pandas 2.0. From 1.0 on, kivi follows "
"semantic versioning: a deprecation keeps working with a ``FutureWarning`` until the next major "
"release. :doc:`/api/compatibility` describes what a release may change."
msgstr ""
"kivi 1.0 仍支持 Python 3.10、NumPy 1.24 和 pandas 2.0。从 1.0 起，kivi 遵循语义化版本：弃用的内容在下一个主版本之前仍然可用，并发出 "
"``FutureWarning`` 。 :doc:`/api/compatibility` 说明了各个版本可能改变的内容。"

msgid "From 0.2.x"
msgstr "从 0.2.x 迁移"

msgid ""
"The functions below replace the 0.2.x classes. The example data of ``Dataset.bank_data()``, which"
" 1.0 removed, come from ``kivi.datasets.load_bank()``. The target describes deposit subscription."
msgstr ""
"下表列出取代 0.2.x 各个类的函数。1.0 已移除 ``Dataset.bank_data()`` ，其示例数据由 ``kivi.datasets.load_bank()`` "
"提供。标签表示客户是否认购定期存款。"

msgid "0.2.x"
msgstr "0.2.x"

msgid "Replacement"
msgstr "替代方案"

msgid "``DistanceBins``"
msgstr "``DistanceBins``"

msgid "``bin_edges(values, method=\"uniform\")``, then ``pandas.cut`` and ``woe_table``"
msgstr "``bin_edges(values, method=\"uniform\")``，然后调用 ``pandas.cut`` 和 ``woe_table``"

msgid "``FrequencyBins``"
msgstr "``FrequencyBins``"

msgid "``bin_edges(values, method=\"quantile\")``, then ``pandas.cut`` and ``woe_table``"
msgstr "``bin_edges(values, method=\"quantile\")``，然后调用 ``pandas.cut`` 和 ``woe_table``"

msgid "``abnormal_vals=[...]``"
msgstr "``abnormal_vals=[...]``"

msgid "``special=[...]`` in ``bin_edges`` and ``kivi.binning.cut``"
msgstr "``bin_edges`` 和 ``kivi.binning.cut`` 的 ``special=[...]``"

msgid "``CategoryBins``"
msgstr "``CategoryBins``"

msgid ""
"``woe_table(labels, target)``, after ``category_groups`` or ``chimerge_groups`` and "
"``group_categories`` where the labels should be grouped, from 0.8.0"
msgstr ""
"``woe_table(labels, target)`` ；需要对标签分组时，先用 ``category_groups`` 或 ``chimerge_groups`` 和 "
"``group_categories`` （0.8.0 起提供）"

msgid "``WOEScore``"
msgstr "``WOEScore``"

msgid "``woe_transform(groups, table)`` on groups formed with the development edges, from 0.5.0"
msgstr "对用开发样本边界划分的分组调用 ``woe_transform(groups, table)`` （0.5.0 起提供）"

msgid "``PSI.fit()``"
msgstr "``PSI.fit()``"

msgid "``psi_table(before, after)`` on groups formed with the same edges"
msgstr "对用同一组边界划分的分组调用 ``psi_table(before, after)``"

msgid "``BinaryMetrics``, ``ModelEvaluate``, ``ScoreEvaluate``"
msgstr "``BinaryMetrics``, ``ModelEvaluate``, ``ScoreEvaluate``"

msgid ""
"``kivi.metrics``: ``roc_auc``, ``gini``, ``ks``, ``gains_table`` and ``brier_score``, from 0.5.0,"
" and ``roc_table``, ``roc_auc_interval`` and ``delong_test``, from 0.8.0"
msgstr ""
"``kivi.metrics`` ： ``roc_auc`` 、 ``gini`` 、 ``ks`` 、 ``gains_table`` 和 ``brier_score`` （0.5.0 "
"起提供），以及 ``roc_table`` 、 ``roc_auc_interval`` 和 ``delong_test`` （0.8.0 起提供）"

msgid "``ScoreEvaluate.score_psi``, ``add_psi``"
msgstr "``ScoreEvaluate.score_psi`` 、 ``add_psi``"

msgid "``kivi.monitoring``: ``monitoring_table`` and ``stability_table``, from 0.8.0"
msgstr "``kivi.monitoring`` ： ``monitoring_table`` 和 ``stability_table`` （0.8.0 起提供）"

msgid "``VIF``, ``StepWise``, ``feature.Corr``"
msgstr "``VIF``, ``StepWise``, ``feature.Corr``"

msgid ""
"``kivi.selection``: ``vif``, ``stepwise``, ``correlation_filter`` and ``logistic_regression``, "
"from 0.5.0"
msgstr ""
"``kivi.selection`` ： ``vif`` 、 ``stepwise`` 、 ``correlation_filter`` 和 ``logistic_regression`` "
"（0.5.0 起提供）"

msgid "``PDToScore``, ``BaseScoreAndPDO``"
msgstr "``PDToScore``, ``BaseScoreAndPDO``"

msgid ""
"``kivi.scorecard``: ``pd_to_score``, ``score_to_pd``, ``score_scaling`` and ``points_table``, "
"from 0.5.0"
msgstr ""
"``kivi.scorecard`` ： ``pd_to_score`` 、 ``score_to_pd`` 、 ``score_scaling`` 和 ``points_table`` "
"（0.5.0 起提供）"

msgid "``get_omega``, ``BinomialTest``, ``herfindahl``"
msgstr "``get_omega``, ``BinomialTest``, ``herfindahl``"

msgid ""
"``kivi.calibration``: ``prior_correction``, ``calibration_table``, ``binomial_test`` and "
"``herfindahl_index``, from 0.5.0"
msgstr ""
"``kivi.calibration`` ： ``prior_correction`` 、 ``calibration_table`` 、 ``binomial_test`` 和 "
"``herfindahl_index`` （0.5.0 起提供）"

msgid "``MasterScale``, ``PDToRant``"
msgstr "``MasterScale``, ``PDToRant``"

msgid "``kivi.calibration``: ``master_scale``, ``fit_grade_pd`` and ``assign_grades``, from 0.7.0"
msgstr "``kivi.calibration`` ： ``master_scale`` 、 ``fit_grade_pd`` 和 ``assign_grades`` （0.7.0 起提供）"

msgid "``FeatureEvaluate``"
msgstr "``FeatureEvaluate``"

msgid "``kivi.univariate.profile_table``, from 0.7.0"
msgstr "``kivi.univariate.profile_table`` （0.7.0 起提供）"

msgid "``WOEBatch``, ``ManualBinsTool``"
msgstr "``WOEBatch`` 、 ``ManualBinsTool``"

msgid "``kivi.spec``: ``fit_spec`` and ``BinningSpec``, from 0.6.0"
msgstr "``kivi.spec`` 中的 ``fit_spec`` 和 ``BinningSpec`` ，自 0.6.0 起"

msgid "``CSI``"
msgstr "``CSI``"

msgid "``kivi.stability.csi_table`` on groups formed with the same edges, from 0.6.0"
msgstr "对用同一组边界划分的分组调用 ``kivi.stability.csi_table`` ，自 0.6.0 起"

msgid "``VintagePd``"
msgstr "``VintagePd``"

msgid "``kivi.vintage.vintage_table`` on a loan panel, from 0.6.0"
msgstr "对贷款面板数据调用 ``kivi.vintage.vintage_table`` ，自 0.6.0 起"

msgid "``Dataset.bank_data()``"
msgstr "``Dataset.bank_data()``"

msgid ""
"``kivi.datasets.load_bank()``, from 0.6.0. ``Dataset.bank_data()`` warned with a "
"``FutureWarning`` in 0.9.0 and was removed in 1.0"
msgstr ""
"``kivi.datasets.load_bank()`` ，自 0.6.0 起提供。 ``Dataset.bank_data()`` 在 0.9.0 中发出 ``FutureWarning``"
" ，并已在 1.0 中移除"

msgid "Binning and WOE"
msgstr "分箱与 WOE"

msgid ""
"DistanceBins and FrequencyBins previously calculated group assignments and statistics together. "
"Use bin_edges with uniform or quantile, call pandas.cut, then pass the groups to woe_table. Codes"
" listed in abnormal_vals become the special argument: pass them to bin_edges, and use "
"kivi.binning.cut with the same codes in place of pandas.cut. CategoryBins users can pass the "
"label series directly."
msgstr ""
"旧版 DistanceBins 和 FrequencyBins 在同一步骤中完成分箱和统计。现在先用 bin_edges 选择 uniform 或 quantile，再用 pandas.cut "
"分组，最后将结果传给 woe_table。abnormal_vals 中的编码改由 special 参数指定：传给 bin_edges，并用带相同编码的 kivi.binning.cut 代替 "
"pandas.cut。原 CategoryBins 用户可直接传入类别标签序列。"

msgid ""
"Version 0.5.0 adds woe_transform in place of WOEScore. WOEScore matched raw values against the "
"min_bin and max_bin columns of a WOE table. Form the groups with the development edges instead, "
"then pass them to woe_transform with the woe_table result. A value that matches no group raises "
"an error, as WOEScore did with error=\"error\"; pass unseen to choose its WOE instead."
msgstr ""
"0.5.0 新增 woe_transform，取代 WOEScore。旧版 WOEScore 把原始取值与 WOE 表中的 min_bin 和 max_bin "
"列逐一比对。现在请改用开发样本的边界划分分组，再把分组和 woe_table 的结果一起传给 woe_transform。与 WOEScore 设置 error=\"error\" "
"时一样，匹配不到任何分组的取值会引发错误；也可以传入 unseen 指定其 WOE。"

msgid ""
"Version 0.4.0 adds ``chimerge_edges`` and ``tree_edges`` in place of ``Chi2Bins`` and "
"``TreeBins``. They are new implementations rather than ports, so the edges can differ. "
"``Chi2Bins`` started from 10 quantile bins, tested at a 0.9 confidence level, added 0.5 to every "
"expected count and kept at least three bins; ``chimerge_edges(values, target, alpha=0.1, "
"initial_bins=10)`` comes closest. ``TreeBins`` reported the midpoints that scikit-learn chooses "
"as thresholds, while ``tree_edges`` reports the largest observed value below each cut. Compare "
"the edges on a fixed reference sample before switching."
msgstr ""
"0.4.0 新增 ``chimerge_edges`` 和 ``tree_edges``，用来替代 ``Chi2Bins`` 和 "
"``TreeBins``。它们是重新实现而非移植，因此边界可能不同。``Chi2Bins`` 从 10 个等频箱开始，在 0.9 置信水平下检验，给每个期望计数加 "
"0.5，并至少保留三个箱；最接近的写法是 ``chimerge_edges(values, target, alpha=0.1, initial_bins=10)``。``TreeBins`` "
"报告 scikit-learn 选出的中点阈值，而 ``tree_edges`` 报告每个切分点下方的最大观测值。切换之前，请在固定的基准样本上核对边界。"

msgid ""
"Codes listed in ``abnormal_vals`` of ``Chi2Bins`` and ``TreeBins`` become the ``special`` "
"argument of ``chimerge_edges`` and ``tree_edges``. As before, the codes and their labels are left"
" out of the fit; pass the same codes to ``kivi.binning.cut`` to give each one its own group."
msgstr ""
"``Chi2Bins`` 和 ``TreeBins`` 的 ``abnormal_vals`` 中列出的编码，对应 ``chimerge_edges`` 和 ``tree_edges`` 的 "
"``special`` 参数。与以前一样，这些编码连同其标签不参与拟合；把相同的编码传给 ``kivi.binning.cut`` ，即可让每个编码单独成组。"

msgid ""
"For PSI.fit(), form both sets of groups using the same reference edges, then call psi_table. It "
"returns raw counts and a contribution per bin. Previously the psi column repeated the overall "
"total. The new smoothing rule preserves counts and normalizes each distribution after replacing "
"zeros. Recheck thresholds when migrating saved analyses."
msgstr ""
"迁移 PSI.fit() 时，先用同一组基准边界划分两期样本，再调用 psi_table。新结果包含各组的真实计数和单组贡献；旧结果在 psi "
"列逐行重复总值。新的平滑口径会在补零后归一化。迁移历史分析时应重新核对阈值。"

msgid "Models, scorecards and calibration"
msgstr "模型、评分卡与校准"

msgid ""
"These modules are new implementations, so compare their output with the legacy code on a fixed "
"reference sample before switching."
msgstr "这些模块都是重新实现的，切换之前请先在固定的参考样本上与旧版代码的结果对比。"

msgid ""
"The legacy ``lift`` column was cumulative. In ``gains_table``, ``lift`` is the lift of each band "
"and ``cum_lift`` the cumulative lift. The metrics take a score that rises with risk, such as a "
"PD; pass ``-score`` for scorecard points. ``ModelEvaluate`` rescaled each sample by its own "
"minimum and maximum, so its scores were not comparable across samples; the new functions use the "
"scores as given."
msgstr ""
"旧版的 ``lift`` 列是累计值。在 ``gains_table`` 中， ``lift`` 是每个分数段的提升， ``cum_lift`` 才是累计提升。这些指标要求分数随风险升高，例如 "
"PD；评分卡分值请传入 ``-score`` 。 ``ModelEvaluate`` 会用每个样本自己的最小值和最大值重新缩放分数，导致不同样本间的分数不可比；新函数直接使用传入的分数。"

msgid ""
"``VIF`` called statsmodels without a constant, which measures uncentred R²; ``vif`` includes an "
"intercept in every auxiliary regression, as in the textbook definition, so the values differ. "
"``stepwise`` replaces ``StepWise`` and by default keeps every coefficient positive, as WOE inputs"
" require. ``logistic_regression`` fits the model in NumPy, so statsmodels is no longer needed."
msgstr ""
"``VIF`` 调用 statsmodels 时没有加常数项，衡量的是未中心化的 R²； ``vif`` 按教科书定义在每个辅助回归中都包含截距，因此数值会不同。 ``stepwise`` 取代"
" ``StepWise`` ，默认保证所有系数为正，这正是 WOE 输入的要求。 ``logistic_regression`` 用 NumPy 拟合模型，不再需要 statsmodels。"

msgid ""
"``BaseScoreAndPDO`` took bad:good odds, for example ``odds=1/50``. ``base_odds`` is good:bad, so "
"pass ``base_odds=50``; passing ``1/50`` silently gives an offset of 712.9. The legacy "
"``PDToScore`` divided by ln 2 only in one of its branches; ``pd_to_score`` and ``score_to_pd`` "
"are exact inverses."
msgstr ""
"``BaseScoreAndPDO`` 接收的是坏好比，例如 ``odds=1/50`` 。 ``base_odds`` 是好坏比，因此应传入 ``base_odds=50`` ；若传入 "
"``1/50`` ，会在没有任何提示的情况下得到 712.9 的偏移量。旧版 ``PDToScore`` 只在其中一个分支里除以了 ln 2； ``pd_to_score`` 和 "
"``score_to_pd`` 互为精确的反函数。"

msgid ""
"``get_omega`` becomes ``prior_correction`` for probabilities and ``corrected_intercept`` for the "
"model intercept."
msgstr "``get_omega`` 的功能由 ``prior_correction`` （校正概率）和 ``corrected_intercept`` （校正模型截距）取代。"

msgid "Portfolio analysis and production binning"
msgstr "资产组合分析与生产环境分箱"

msgid ""
"Version 0.6.0 replaces three more legacy classes. They are new implementations as well, so "
"compare their output with the legacy code on a fixed reference sample before switching."
msgstr "0.6.0 版又替代了三个旧版类。它们同样是重新实现的，切换之前请先在固定的参考样本上与旧版代码的结果对比。"

msgid ""
"``WOEBatch`` fitted the WOE of many columns at once, and ``ManualBinsTool`` merged bins by hand "
"afterwards. ``fit_spec`` fits every column with the binning function chosen for it, and its "
"``BinningSpec`` saves the edges and WOE tables as versioned JSON. Nothing is re-binned "
"automatically: to merge bins by hand, pass the merged edges for that column in ``bins``."
msgstr ""
"``WOEBatch`` 一次拟合多列的 WOE， ``ManualBinsTool`` 随后手动合并分箱。 ``fit_spec`` 用为每列选定的分箱函数拟合各列，得到的 "
"``BinningSpec`` 把边界和 WOE 表保存为带版本号的 JSON。它不会自动重新分箱：要手动合并分箱，请在 ``bins`` 中为该列传入合并后的边界。"

msgid ""
"``CSI`` matched the points to the bins by position and lost the missing group. ``csi_table`` "
"matches the points to the groups by label, keeps the missing group, and raises for an observed "
"group without points unless ``unseen_points`` gives them. Its contributions sum to the change of "
"the variable's average points."
msgstr ""
"``CSI`` 按位置把分值对应到各箱，并丢失了缺失值分组。 ``csi_table`` 按标签把分值对应到各组，保留缺失值分组；若某个出现的分组没有分值，除非用 "
"``unseen_points`` 给出，否则会报错。各组贡献之和等于该变量平均分值的变化。"

msgid ""
"``VintagePd`` built the vintage table from repayment schedules and observation dates. "
"``vintage_table`` takes a long panel with one row per loan and month on book and a bad flag that "
"you define, for example ``status == \"90+\"``. Pass ``weights=amount`` for the amount-weighted "
"rates of ``VintagePd``. Months that a cohort has not reached are NaN rather than 0."
msgstr ""
"``VintagePd`` 根据还款计划和观察日期构建 vintage 表。 ``vintage_table`` 接受长格式的面板数据，每笔贷款每个账龄月一行，并由你自行定义坏账标记，例如 "
"``status == \"90+\"`` 。传入 ``weights=amount`` 即可得到 ``VintagePd`` 按金额加权的比率。批次尚未达到的账龄月为 NaN 而不是 0。"

msgid "Master scales, variable profiles and strategy"
msgstr "主标尺、变量概况与策略"

msgid ""
"Version 0.7.0 replaces the legacy master scale and variable profile. Compare their output with "
"the legacy code on a fixed reference sample before switching."
msgstr "0.7.0 版替代了旧版的主标尺和变量概况。切换之前请先在固定的参考样本上与旧版代码的结果对比。"

msgid ""
"``MasterScale.fit_grade_df`` and ``confirm_master_scale`` become ``fit_grade_pd`` and "
"``master_scale``. ``fit_grade_pd`` fits the logarithm of the default rate by least squares "
"weighted with the number of observations of each grade, where the legacy fit gave every grade the"
" same weight; the two agree when the grades are equally large. A grade without defaults enters "
"the fit with half a default instead of a logarithm of zero. The bounds between grades are the "
"geometric means of adjacent PDs; pass ``boundary=\"arithmetic\"`` for the midpoints of the legacy"
" scale."
msgstr ""
"``MasterScale.fit_grade_df`` 和 ``confirm_master_scale`` 改为 ``fit_grade_pd`` 和 ``master_scale`` 。 "
"``fit_grade_pd`` "
"以各等级的观测数为权重，用最小二乘拟合违约率的对数，而旧版的拟合给每个等级相同的权重；各等级规模相同时两者一致。没有违约的等级以半个违约参与拟合，而不是取零的对数。等级之间的边界是相邻 PD "
"的几何平均；传入 ``boundary=\"arithmetic\"`` 可得到旧版标尺的中点。"

msgid ""
"``PDToRant(pd, ranking)`` becomes ``assign_grades(probability, scale)``. The legacy function put "
"a PD that lies exactly on a bound in the grade above it; ``assign_grades`` puts it in the grade "
"below, as the intervals of ``pandas.cut`` are closed on the right. It returns an ordered "
"categorical of the grade labels instead of grade numbers."
msgstr ""
"``PDToRant(pd, ranking)`` 改为 ``assign_grades(probability, scale)`` 。旧版函数把恰好落在边界上的 PD 归入边界之上的等级； "
"``assign_grades`` 则把它归入边界之下的等级，因为 ``pandas.cut`` 的区间是右闭的。它返回由等级标签构成的有序分类，而不是等级编号。"

msgid ""
"``FeatureEvaluate(df, target_name).stats()`` becomes "
"``profile_table(frame.drop(columns=target_name), frame[target_name])``. The columns follow kivi's"
" names, such as ``missing_share``, ``missing_event_rate`` and ``non_missing_lift``, and a target "
"without events raises an error, where the legacy lifts were -9999. The signed Gini coefficient of"
" the values replaces the AUC and KS of a univariate logistic fit. The table adds the IV of a "
"quick binning, special codes, sample weights and the ``tied_bins`` column."
msgstr ""
"``FeatureEvaluate(df, target_name).stats()`` 改为 ``profile_table(frame.drop(columns=target_name), "
"frame[target_name])`` 。各列沿用 kivi 的命名，例如 ``missing_share`` 、 ``missing_event_rate`` 和 "
"``non_missing_lift`` ；目标变量中没有事件时会报错，而旧版的提升度为 -9999。取值本身带符号的 Gini 系数取代了单变量逻辑回归的 AUC 和 "
"KS。该表还新增了快速分箱的 IV、特殊值编码、样本权重以及 ``tied_bins`` 列。"

msgid ""
"Strategy analysis, reject inference and weighted model fits have no 0.2.x counterpart. "
"``kivi.strategy`` replaces approval and bad-rate tables built by hand from score bands, "
"``kivi.reject_inference`` infers the outcomes of declined applicants, and ``logistic_regression``"
" and ``stepwise`` take ``weights`` to refit on them."
msgstr ""
"策略分析、拒绝推断和带权重的模型拟合在 0.2.x 中没有对应功能。 ``kivi.strategy`` 取代按分数段手工制作的通过率与坏账率表， "
"``kivi.reject_inference`` 推断被拒申请人的结果， ``logistic_regression`` 和 ``stepwise`` 则通过 ``weights`` "
"纳入这些申请人重新拟合。"

msgid "Category grouping, validation and monitoring"
msgstr "类别分组、模型验证与监控"

msgid ""
"Version 0.8.0 groups categorical variables, adds the ROC table and the uncertainty of an AUC, and"
" monitors a model period by period. These are new implementations as well."
msgstr "0.8.0 版本对类别变量分组，新增 ROC 表和 AUC 的不确定性，并逐期监控模型。这些同样是新的实现。"

msgid ""
"``CategoryBins`` kept the labels of a categorical variable as they were. ``category_groups`` "
"pools the rare categories and ``chimerge_groups`` merges the categories with similar event rates;"
" both return a dictionary from category to group that is fitted on the reference sample, and "
"``group_categories`` applies it to every sample. A category that the grouping does not know "
"raises an error unless ``unseen`` names its group. ``fit_spec`` groups a column with the methods "
"``\"rare\"`` and ``\"chimerge\"``, and a specification that groups a column is saved as format "
"version 2, which 0.7.0 and earlier refuse to read."
msgstr ""
"``CategoryBins`` 保留类别变量原有的标签。 ``category_groups`` 合并稀有类别， ``chimerge_groups`` "
"合并事件率相近的类别；两者都返回一个在基准样本上拟合、从类别到分组的字典， ``group_categories`` 把它应用于每个样本。分组不认识的类别会引发错误，除非 ``unseen`` "
"指定了它所属的分组。 ``fit_spec`` 用 ``\"rare\"`` 和 ``\"chimerge\"`` 方法对列分组，对列分组的分箱方案保存为第 2 版格式，0.7.0 "
"及更早版本拒绝读取。"

msgid ""
"``BinaryMetrics.roc_curve`` returned the points of scikit-learn's ``roc_curve`` with its default "
"``drop_intermediate=True``. ``roc_table`` has one row for every distinct score, as ``roc_curve`` "
"with ``drop_intermediate=False``, with the cumulative counts, the two rates and the precision. "
"Its ``precision`` and ``true_positive_rate`` columns are the precision and the recall at each "
"threshold, so it also gives the precision-recall curve. ``roc_auc_interval`` adds the DeLong "
"standard error and interval of the AUC and the Gini, and ``delong_test`` compares the AUCs of two"
" scores on the same sample; the legacy code had neither."
msgstr ""
"``BinaryMetrics.roc_curve`` 返回 scikit-learn 的 ``roc_curve`` 在默认 ``drop_intermediate=True`` 下的点。 "
"``roc_table`` 为每个不同的评分各给一行，与 ``drop_intermediate=False`` 时的 ``roc_curve`` 相同，并包含累计计数、两个比率和精确率。它的 "
"``precision`` 和 ``true_positive_rate`` 列就是各阈值下的精确率和召回率，因此它也给出精确率-召回率曲线。 ``roc_auc_interval`` 补充了 "
"AUC 和 Gini 的 DeLong 标准误与区间， ``delong_test`` 比较同一样本上两个评分的 AUC；旧版代码两者都没有。"

msgid ""
"``ScoreEvaluate.score_psi`` and ``add_psi`` compared the band totals of two lift tables. "
"``monitoring_table`` compares every period with one reference sample on score bands fitted once, "
"adds the known outcomes, the AUC, the Gini and the KS of each period, and counts an observation "
"without a known outcome in the population only. ``stability_table`` gives the PSI of every "
"variable in every period."
msgstr ""
"``ScoreEvaluate.score_psi`` 和 ``add_psi`` 比较的是两张提升表的分段合计。 ``monitoring_table`` "
"在只拟合一次的评分段上把每一期与同一个基准样本比较，补充了每期的已知结果、AUC、Gini 和 KS，并且结果未知的观测只计入样本量。 ``stability_table`` "
"给出每个变量在每一期的 PSI。"

msgid ""
"Lifetime PD term structures, the IFRS 9 expected credit loss and the allocation to stages have no"
" 0.2.x counterpart; see ``kivi.lifetime``."
msgstr "存续期 PD 期限结构、IFRS 9 预期信用损失和阶段划分在 0.2.x 中没有对应功能；见 ``kivi.lifetime`` 。"

msgid "Not ported"
msgstr "未迁移的功能"

msgid ""
"Spark, SQL, AHP, model wrappers and application code are out of scope and remain in the "
"historical revisions. These 0.2.x tools have no replacement either:"
msgstr "Spark、SQL、AHP、模型封装和应用代码不在范围之内，仍保留在历史版本中。以下 0.2.x 工具同样没有替代："

msgid ""
"The charts of ``DefaultAnalysis``, ``plot_bin``, ``Calibration.CalibrationCurve`` and the "
"``plot_*`` methods of ``BinaryMetrics``, and the correlation heatmaps ``diagonal_corr`` and "
"``structure_corr`` of ``evaluate/Heatmap.py``. kivi returns tables, which any plotting library "
"can draw; for the heatmaps, draw ``X.corr()`` of the WOE-encoded candidates, which "
"``correlation_filter`` uses as well."
msgstr ""
"``DefaultAnalysis`` 、 ``plot_bin`` 、 ``Calibration.CalibrationCurve`` 的图表和 ``BinaryMetrics`` 的 "
"``plot_*`` 方法，以及 ``evaluate/Heatmap.py`` 中的相关性热力图 ``diagonal_corr`` 和 ``structure_corr`` 。kivi "
"返回表格，任何绘图库都可以绘制；热力图可以绘制 WOE 编码后候选变量的 ``X.corr()`` ， ``correlation_filter`` 用的也是同样的相关系数。"

msgid ""
"The F1 score and the confusion matrix of ``BinaryMetrics``. They judge predicted labels at one "
"threshold, which a scorecard sets with a cut-off: ``cutoff_table`` gives the events that each "
"cut-off approves and the shares of events and non-events that it rejects, and each row of "
"``roc_table`` gives the counts of the flagged events and non-events at its threshold. Use scikit-"
"learn's ``f1_score`` and ``confusion_matrix`` where they are needed."
msgstr ""
"``BinaryMetrics`` 的 F1 分数和混淆矩阵。它们评价的是单个阈值下的预测标签，而评分卡用截断点设定这个阈值： ``cutoff_table`` "
"给出每个截断点通过的事件数以及它拒绝的事件和非事件占比， ``roc_table`` 的每一行给出其阈值下被标记的事件数和非事件数。需要时请使用 scikit-learn 的 "
"``f1_score`` 和 ``confusion_matrix`` 。"

msgid ""
"The sampling helpers ``sampling`` and ``upsampling``, and the ratio and cross features of "
"``FeatureTools``. Use pandas."
msgstr "抽样工具 ``sampling`` 和 ``upsampling`` ，以及 ``FeatureTools`` 的比率特征和交叉特征。请使用 pandas。"

msgid ""
"The grading by the Beta distribution in ``BetaCalibration``, ``BetaDistribution`` and "
"``MasterScale.cal_quantile``, and ``model_score_by_weight``. ``master_scale`` and "
"``woe_to_points`` cover the same steps without them."
msgstr ""
"``BetaCalibration`` 、 ``BetaDistribution`` 和 ``MasterScale.cal_quantile`` 中基于 Beta 分布的分级，以及 "
"``model_score_by_weight`` 。 ``master_scale`` 和 ``woe_to_points`` 不依赖它们即可完成相同的步骤。"

msgid ""
"The repayment-schedule calculations of ``PortfolioAnalysis.Vintage``. Derive the delinquency "
"status with pandas and pass the panel to ``vintage_table``."
msgstr "``PortfolioAnalysis.Vintage`` 中基于还款计划的计算。请用 pandas 推导逾期状态，再把面板数据传给 ``vintage_table`` 。"

msgid ""
"The skewness, kurtosis, coefficient of variation, KS test, univariate logistic fit and chi-"
"squared test of ``FeatureEvaluate``. Compute them with pandas or scipy where they are needed."
msgstr "``FeatureEvaluate`` 中的偏度、峰度、变异系数、KS 检验、单变量逻辑回归和卡方检验。需要时请用 pandas 或 scipy 计算。"

msgid ""
"A scorecard groups every characteristic, so that the effect of each group can be read, explained "
"to the business and monitored. This chapter compares the binning methods on one variable, chooses"
" the binning of every variable, and fits them all at once into a binning specification that later"
" chapters reuse."
msgstr "评分卡会对每个变量分组，以便解读每个组的作用、向业务方解释并持续监控。本章在一个变量上比较各种分箱方法，为每个变量选定分箱方式，再把所有变量一次拟合成一个分箱方案，供后续章节复用。"

msgid "Code from the previous chapters"
msgstr "前面各章的代码"

msgid "Compare the binning methods"
msgstr "比较分箱方法"

msgid ""
"The debt-to-income ratio is a typical continuous characteristic. :func:`~kivi.binning.bin_edges` "
"fits quantile edges from the values alone, while :func:`~kivi.binning.chimerge_edges`, "
":func:`~kivi.binning.tree_edges` and :func:`~kivi.binning.monotonic_edges` also use the target; "
":doc:`/user_guide/binning` describes each one. With at most five bins each, "
":func:`~kivi.woe.woe_table` measures the result:"
msgstr ""
"负债收入比是典型的连续型变量。 :func:`~kivi.binning.bin_edges` 只根据取值拟合等频边界，而 "
":func:`~kivi.binning.chimerge_edges` 、 :func:`~kivi.binning.tree_edges` 和 "
":func:`~kivi.binning.monotonic_edges` 还会用到目标变量； :doc:`/user_guide/binning` 介绍了每一种方法。每种方法最多分五箱，再用 "
":func:`~kivi.woe.woe_table` 衡量结果："

msgid "WOE of the debt-to-income bins for the quantile, ChiMerge, tree and monotonic methods"
msgstr "分位数、ChiMerge、决策树和单调四种方法下负债收入比各分箱的 WOE"

msgid ""
"WOE of the debt-to-income bins for each method. The supervised methods place their edges where "
"the event rate changes, and all four give a WOE that rises with the ratio."
msgstr "各方法下负债收入比各分箱的 WOE。有监督的方法把边界放在事件率变化的地方，四种方法得到的 WOE 都随负债收入比上升。"

msgid ""
"The supervised methods find a little more information than the quantiles, and all four give a WOE"
" that rises with the ratio, as a higher burden of debt should. Only "
":func:`~kivi.binning.monotonic_edges` guarantees that trend, so the project uses it for the four "
"continuous characteristics: ``age``, ``income``, ``debt_to_income`` and ``incumbent_pd``. A trend"
" that the business expects is easier to defend than a slightly higher IV."
msgstr ""
"有监督的方法比等频分箱多找到一点信息，而且四种方法的 WOE 都随负债收入比上升，这正符合债务负担越重风险越高的预期。只有 "
":func:`~kivi.binning.monotonic_edges` 能保证这一趋势，因此项目对四个连续变量 ``age`` 、 ``income`` 、 "
"``debt_to_income`` 和 ``incumbent_pd`` 都采用它。符合业务预期的趋势，比略高一点的 IV 更容易站得住脚。"

msgid "Give inquiries explicit edges"
msgstr "为查询次数指定边界"

msgid ""
"The profile marked ``inquiries`` as tied: almost half of the applicants had no inquiry, so its "
"quantile bins collapse. Its few values get explicit edges instead, with three or more inquiries "
"in one bin:"
msgstr "概况把 ``inquiries`` 标为存在并列值：将近一半的申请人没有查询记录，因此它的等频分箱会塌缩。它只有少数几个取值，因此改用指定的边界，三次及以上的查询归入一箱："

msgid ""
"The event rate rises with every further inquiry, from 8.5% without any to 15.7% with three or "
"more."
msgstr "事件率随查询次数逐级上升，从没有查询时的 8.5% 升到三次及以上时的 15.7%。"

msgid "Group the employment categories"
msgstr "合并就业类别"

msgid ""
"Categorical characteristics keep their labels as groups, unless some labels are too small or too "
"alike to keep apart:"
msgstr "类别型变量保留原有标签作为分组，除非某些标签太小或彼此太相似，不值得分开："

msgid ""
"Temporary and self-employed applicants default at similar rates, both above the permanent "
"employees. :func:`~kivi.binning.chimerge_groups` merges adjacent categories whose event rates do "
"not differ significantly, and returns the grouping as a dict; "
":func:`~kivi.binning.group_categories` applies it to any sample:"
msgstr ""
"临时雇员和自雇人士的违约率相近，都高于长期雇员。 :func:`~kivi.binning.chimerge_groups` 合并事件率差异不显著的相邻类别，并以 dict 返回分组； "
":func:`~kivi.binning.group_categories` 把它应用到任意样本上："

msgid "``housing`` keeps its three labels, whose event rates differ clearly."
msgstr "``housing`` 保留三个标签，它们的事件率差别明显。"

msgid "Fit every variable at once"
msgstr "一次拟合所有变量"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.spec.fit_spec` fits the binning of every column with the methods chosen above and "
"measures the WOE of every group; see :doc:`/user_guide/spec`. The vendor's PD gets up to eight "
"bins, because it carries most of the information:"
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.spec.fit_spec` 按上面选定的方法拟合每一列的分箱，并计算每个组的 WOE；见 :doc:`/user_guide/spec` 。供应商的 PD "
"携带了大部分信息，因此最多分八箱："

msgid ""
"The specification holds the edges, the category groups and the WOE table of each column. The "
"table of the vendor's PD shows the WOE rising over its eight bins:"
msgstr "分箱方案保存了每一列的边界、类别分组和 WOE 表。供应商 PD 的表显示，WOE 在八个分箱中逐级上升："

msgid "Share of applicants, default rate and WOE of the eight bins of incumbent_pd"
msgstr "incumbent_pd 八个分箱的申请人占比、违约率和 WOE"

#, python-format
msgid ""
"The eight bins of the vendor's PD on the development sample. The default rate rises from 2% in "
"the lowest bin to 18% in the highest, which holds the applicants just below the vendor's 15% cut-"
"off."
msgstr "开发样本上供应商 PD 的八个分箱。违约率从最低一箱的 2% 升到最高一箱的 18%，最高一箱是 PD 刚好低于供应商 15% 截断点的申请人。"

msgid ""
"The binning is fitted on the development sample only. Every later sample, from the validation "
"sample to the applications in production, is grouped with the same edges and groups, so that its "
"WOE and its stability are comparable."
msgstr "分箱只在开发样本上拟合。之后的每个样本，从验证样本到投产后的申请，都用相同的边界和分组划分，这样它们的 WOE 和稳定性才可比。"

msgid "Calibration and grades"
msgstr "校准与等级"

msgid ""
"The scorecard will price loans, set limits and feed the loss allowance, so its PDs must match the"
" default rates that follow, not just rank applicants. This chapter groups the PDs into the grades"
" of a master scale, tests each grade on the validation sample and diagnoses what the tests show; "
":doc:`/user_guide/calibration` describes each test."
msgstr ""
"评分卡将用于贷款定价、设定额度并计入损失准备，因此它的 PD 不仅要能排序，还必须与随后出现的违约率相符。本章把 PD 归入主标尺的各个等级，在验证样本上逐级检验，并分析检验结果说明了什么； "
":doc:`/user_guide/calibration` 介绍了每种检验。"

msgid "Build the master scale"
msgstr "构建主标尺"

msgid ""
"A master scale gives PDs from every model of the lender one meaning. "
":func:`~kivi.calibration.master_scale` builds one from the PD of each grade, here five grades in "
"which each PD doubles the one before, with bounds halfway between them on a log scale:"
msgstr ""
"主标尺让贷款机构所有模型给出的 PD 具有统一的含义。 :func:`~kivi.calibration.master_scale` 根据每个等级的 PD 构建主标尺，这里有五个等级，每一级的 "
"PD 是前一级的两倍，等级边界位于相邻 PD 在对数刻度上的中点："

msgid "Test each grade"
msgstr "逐级检验"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.calibration.assign_grades` gives every applicant of the validation sample the grade "
"of their PD, and :func:`~kivi.calibration.calibration_table` compares each grade's default rate "
"with its mean PD. :func:`~kivi.calibration.jeffreys_test` asks whether a grade has more defaults "
"than the PD of the master scale predicts, so a small p-value flags a grade that underestimates "
"the risk. :func:`~kivi.calibration.binomial_test` asks the same question of the grade's mean PD "
"with the exact binomial distribution:"
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.calibration.assign_grades` 按 PD 为验证样本的每个申请人分配等级， "
":func:`~kivi.calibration.calibration_table` 把每个等级的违约率与其平均 PD 相比较。 "
":func:`~kivi.calibration.jeffreys_test` 检验某个等级的违约是否多于主标尺 PD 的预测，因此 p 值很小说明该等级低估了风险。 "
":func:`~kivi.calibration.binomial_test` 用精确二项分布，针对该等级的平均 PD 检验同样的问题："

msgid ""
"No grade underestimates the risk: every p-value is large. Grades A to D match their PDs closely, "
"but grade E has 164 defaults among 699 approved applicants, 23.5%, against a mean PD of 28.3%. "
"Both tests are one-sided and do not flag a PD that is too high. "
":func:`~kivi.calibration.hosmer_lemeshow` tests deviations in both directions, here over the PD "
"deciles of the development sample:"
msgstr ""
"没有哪个等级低估风险：所有 p 值都很大。A 到 D 级与各自的 PD 非常吻合，但 E 级的 699 个获批申请人中有 164 个违约，违约率 23.5%，而平均 PD 为 "
"28.3%。两种检验都是单侧的，不会标出偏高的 PD。 :func:`~kivi.calibration.hosmer_lemeshow` 检验两个方向的偏差，这里按开发样本的 PD "
"十分位分组："

msgid "Diagnose the deviation"
msgstr "分析偏差"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.calibration.platt_fit` regresses the outcomes on the log odds of the PDs. A slope of"
" 1 and an intercept of 0 would mean that the PDs are calibrated on the sample:"
msgstr ":func:`~kivi.calibration.platt_fit` 把结果对 PD 的对数几率做回归。斜率为 1、截距为 0 表示 PD 在该样本上是校准的："

msgid ""
"A slope below 1 means that the PDs spread further than the outcomes. "
":func:`~kivi.calibration.platt_predict` shows what the fit would make of three PDs:"
msgstr "斜率小于 1 说明 PD 的离散程度大于结果。 :func:`~kivi.calibration.platt_predict` 显示这一拟合会把三个 PD 变成多少："

msgid ""
"The fit raises a PD of 2% a little, leaves 10% where it is and lowers 30% to 25%: the highest PDs"
" overstate the risk of the approved applicants most. That is what reject inference does by "
"design. The model now predicts for all eligible applicants, and the approved ones in grade E are "
"better than the declined applicants with the same PD, whom the vendor turned away on bureau data."
" Recalibrating the PDs to the approved applicants, with Platt scaling or isotonic regression, "
"would undo the reject inference, so the project keeps them."
msgstr ""
"拟合把 2% 的 PD 略微调高，10% 基本不变，30% 则降到 25%：PD 越高，对获批申请人风险的高估就越多。这正是拒绝推断有意造成的结果。模型现在预测的是全部合格申请人，而 E "
"级中的获批申请人比 PD 相同的被拒申请人更好，后者是供应商依据征信数据拒绝的。若用 Platt 缩放或保序回归把 PD 重新校准到获批申请人上，就会抵消拒绝推断，因此项目保留现有的 PD。"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.calibration.fit_grade_pd` shows what the approved applicants alone would make of the"
" grades: a log-linear fit of their default rates against the grade number:"
msgstr ":func:`~kivi.calibration.fit_grade_pd` 显示仅凭获批申请人会给各等级什么样的 PD：对其违约率按等级序号做对数线性拟合："

msgid "Simulation check"
msgstr "模拟核对"

msgid ""
"Over all eligible applicants of October to December, approved or not, each grade's default rate "
"is close to its mean PD:"
msgstr "在 10 月至 12 月的全部合格申请人中，无论是否获批，每个等级的违约率都接近其平均 PD："

msgid ""
"Default rate against mean PD of each grade, for the approved applicants of the validation sample "
"and for all eligible applicants of the quarter"
msgstr "各等级违约率与平均 PD 的对比，分别针对验证样本中的获批申请人和该季度的全部合格申请人"

msgid ""
"Default rate against mean PD by grade. The approved applicants of grade E default less often than"
" their PD says; over all eligible applicants, which only simulated data reveal, the grades lie on"
" the diagonal."
msgstr "各等级违约率与平均 PD 的对比。E 级的获批申请人违约少于其 PD 的预测；而在全部合格申请人中（只有模拟数据才能揭示），各等级都落在对角线上。"

msgid "Check the concentration"
msgstr "检查集中度"

msgid ""
"A master scale should spread the applicants over its grades rather than put them all in one. "
":func:`~kivi.calibration.herfindahl_index` measures the concentration of the counts, from 0 for "
"an even spread to 1 for a single grade:"
msgstr ""
"主标尺应当把申请人分散到各个等级，而不是都集中在一个等级。 :func:`~kivi.calibration.herfindahl_index` 衡量计数的集中度，均匀分布时为 "
"0，全部集中在一个等级时为 1："

msgid ""
"The approved applicants spread over the five grades with a normalized index of 0.06, far from "
"concentrated."
msgstr "获批申请人在五个等级中的标准化指数为 0.06，远谈不上集中。"

msgid "Data and samples"
msgstr "数据与样本"

msgid ""
"The project starts from the applications of 2024 and their decisions. This chapter loads them, "
"sets aside the applications that a policy rule declined, splits the approved ones into a "
"development sample and a later validation sample, and takes a first look at every candidate "
"variable."
msgstr "项目从 2024 年的贷款申请及其审批决定开始。本章加载这些申请，剔除被政策规则拒绝的申请，把获批申请分为开发样本和时间更晚的验证样本，并对每个候选变量做初步分析。"

msgid "Load the applications"
msgstr "加载申请数据"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.datasets.make_applications` returns one row per application. The simulated "
"applications have no date, so the example spreads them evenly over the twelve months of 2024 in "
"the order of the rows:"
msgstr ":func:`~kivi.datasets.make_applications` 每笔申请返回一行。模拟的申请没有日期，因此示例按行的顺序把它们平均分配到 2024 年的十二个月中："

msgid ""
"``incumbent_pd`` is the PD of the vendor's scorecard, ``policy_decline`` flags the applications "
"that a policy rule declined, and ``approved`` the applications that the lender approved. "
"``target`` is 1 if the borrower defaulted within the outcome window."
msgstr ""
"``incumbent_pd`` 是供应商评分卡给出的 PD， ``policy_decline`` 标记被政策规则拒绝的申请， ``approved`` "
"标记贷款机构批准的申请。借款人在表现期内违约时 ``target`` 为 1。"

msgid "Split the samples"
msgstr "划分样本"

msgid ""
"A policy decline does not depend on the score, so a scorecard is not developed on those "
"applications: they are declined whatever it says. The other applications are *eligible*. The "
"vendor's scorecard approved the eligible applications with a PD below 15%, the *accepts*, and "
"declined the others, the *rejects*:"
msgstr ""
"政策拒绝与评分无关，因此不在这些申请上开发评分卡：无论评分如何，它们都会被拒绝。其余申请为 *合格申请* 。供应商评分卡批准其中 PD 低于 15% 的合格申请，即 *获批申请人* "
"，拒绝其余的，即 *拒绝申请人* ："

msgid ""
"The model is developed on the accepts of January to September, and the accepts of October to "
"December are kept apart to validate it out of time, as a model in production is applied to "
"applications that come after its development sample. The rejects of the development months enter "
"the project in :doc:`reject_inference`:"
msgstr ""
"模型在 1 月至 9 月的获批申请人上开发，10 月至 12 月的获批申请人则留作跨时间验证，就像投产的模型总是应用于开发样本之后的申请一样。开发月份的拒绝申请人将在 "
":doc:`reject_inference` 中进入项目："

msgid ""
"About one approved borrower in ten defaulted, in both samples. The outcome of the rejects is "
"unknown: they never received a loan."
msgstr "两个样本中都约有十分之一的获批借款人违约。拒绝申请人的结果未知：他们从未拿到贷款。"

msgid ""
"The simulated rejects do have an outcome. They default three times as often as the accepts, "
"partly because the vendor's scorecard saw bureau data that the application form does not hold:"
msgstr "模拟的拒绝申请人确实有结果。他们的违约频率是获批申请人的三倍，部分原因是供应商评分卡看到了申请表中没有的征信数据："

msgid "Profile the candidates"
msgstr "分析候选变量"

msgid ""
"The candidate characteristics are the six fields of the application form and the vendor's PD. "
":func:`~kivi.univariate.profile_table` gives each of them one row on the development sample, with"
" its distribution and the IV of a quick binning; see :doc:`/user_guide/univariate`:"
msgstr ""
"候选变量包括申请表上的六个字段和供应商的 PD。 :func:`~kivi.univariate.profile_table` 在开发样本上为每个变量给出一行，包括其分布和快速分箱的 IV；见 "
":doc:`/user_guide/univariate` ："

msgid ""
"Information value of the seven candidate characteristics on the development sample, sorted, with "
"the 0.02, 0.1 and 0.3 reading bands"
msgstr "开发样本上七个候选变量的信息值排序，含 0.02、0.1 和 0.3 的解读区间"

msgid ""
"IV of each candidate with a quick binning on the development sample. The vendor's PD stands out; "
"the fields of the application form are weak on their own."
msgstr "开发样本上各候选变量快速分箱的 IV。供应商的 PD 遥遥领先；申请表上的字段单独来看都较弱。"

msgid "The profile shapes the next chapters:"
msgstr "这份概况决定了接下来几章的做法："

msgid "No variable has missing values or special codes, so neither needs a group of its own."
msgstr "没有变量存在缺失值或特殊编码，因此都不需要为它们单独设组。"

msgid ""
"``incumbent_pd`` is by far the strongest candidate, followed by ``housing``. The other fields of "
"the application form have an IV between 0.017 and 0.031: weak on their own, but they may add to "
"the vendor's PD."
msgstr ""
"``incumbent_pd`` 是最强的候选变量，其次是 ``housing`` 。申请表上的其他字段 IV 在 0.017 到 0.031 之间：单独来看较弱，但可能为供应商的 PD "
"补充信息。"

msgid ""
"The approved applicants are a selected sample: the vendor's scorecard turned away the riskiest "
"applications, so every variable separates the outcomes less among the accepts than among all "
"applicants."
msgstr "获批申请人是经过筛选的样本：供应商评分卡拒绝了风险最高的申请，因此在获批申请人中，每个变量对结果的区分都弱于在全部申请人中。"

msgid ""
"``inquiries`` is marked in ``tied_bins``: almost half of the applicants had no inquiry, so its "
"quantile bins collapse. :doc:`binning` gives it explicit edges."
msgstr "``inquiries`` 在 ``tied_bins`` 中被标记：将近一半的申请人没有查询记录，因此它的等频分箱会塌缩。 :doc:`binning` 为它指定了边界。"

msgid "Model evaluation"
msgstr "模型评估"

msgid ""
"The model was fitted on the applications of January to September. This chapter measures how well "
"it ranks the approved applicants of October to December, which it has not seen, and whether it "
"ranks them better than the vendor's PD; :doc:`/user_guide/metrics` defines each measure."
msgstr ""
"模型是在 1 月至 9 月的申请上拟合的。本章衡量它对 10 月至 12 月未见过的获批申请人排序得如何，以及是否比供应商的 PD 排序得更好； "
":doc:`/user_guide/metrics` 定义了每个指标。"

msgid "Measure the ranking"
msgstr "衡量排序能力"

msgid ""
"The measures expect a score that rises with the risk, so the PD is passed as it is. "
":func:`~kivi.metrics.roc_auc`, :func:`~kivi.metrics.gini` and :func:`~kivi.metrics.ks` measure "
"how well it separates defaults from non-defaults, and :func:`~kivi.metrics.brier_score` how close"
" the PDs come to the outcomes:"
msgstr ""
"这些指标要求评分随风险升高而增大，因此 PD 直接传入即可。 :func:`~kivi.metrics.roc_auc` 、 :func:`~kivi.metrics.gini` 和 "
":func:`~kivi.metrics.ks` 衡量它区分违约与未违约的能力， :func:`~kivi.metrics.brier_score` 衡量 PD 与结果的接近程度："

#, python-format
msgid ""
"A sample of 6,785 applications with 722 defaults measures the AUC with some uncertainty. "
":func:`~kivi.metrics.roc_auc_interval` gives its DeLong standard error and its 95% confidence "
"interval, and those of the Gini:"
msgstr ""
"6,785 笔申请、722 笔违约的样本对 AUC 的测量存在一定的不确定性。 :func:`~kivi.metrics.roc_auc_interval` 给出 AUC 及 Gini 的 "
"DeLong 标准误和 95% 置信区间："

msgid "Compare with the vendor's PD"
msgstr "与供应商的 PD 比较"

msgid ""
"The validation sample was approved by the vendor's scorecard, so it also has the vendor's PD. "
":func:`~kivi.metrics.delong_test` compares the two AUCs on the same applicants, with the "
"correlation between the two scores taken into account:"
msgstr "验证样本是由供应商评分卡批准的，因此也有供应商的 PD。 :func:`~kivi.metrics.delong_test` 在同一批申请人上比较两个 AUC，并考虑了两个评分之间的相关性："

#, python-format
msgid ""
"The new scorecard raises the AUC by 0.023, and its 95% interval runs from 0.011 to 0.035, so the "
"gain is not chance. :func:`~kivi.metrics.roc_table` gives the points of both ROC curves:"
msgstr ""
"新评分卡把 AUC 提高了 0.023，其 95% 区间为 0.011 到 0.035，因此这一提升并非偶然。 :func:`~kivi.metrics.roc_table` 给出两条 ROC "
"曲线上的点："

msgid "ROC curves of the new scorecard's PD and of the vendor's PD on the validation sample"
msgstr "验证样本上新评分卡 PD 与供应商 PD 的 ROC 曲线"

msgid ""
"ROC curves on the validation sample. The new scorecard's curve lies above the vendor's, most "
"clearly among the riskiest applicants on the left."
msgstr "验证样本上的 ROC 曲线。新评分卡的曲线位于供应商曲线之上，在左侧风险最高的申请人中最为明显。"

msgid ""
"The validation sample holds only approved applicants. Over all eligible applicants of October to "
"December, approved or not, the new scorecard also ranks better than the vendor's PD:"
msgstr "验证样本只包含获批申请人。在 10 月至 12 月的全部合格申请人中，无论是否获批，新评分卡的排序也优于供应商的 PD："

msgid "Break the ranking down by band"
msgstr "按评分段分解排序"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.metrics.gains_table` shows how the defaults spread over score bands. The bands are "
"the PD quintiles of the development sample, so that both samples are cut alike:"
msgstr ":func:`~kivi.metrics.gains_table` 显示违约在各评分段中的分布。评分段取开发样本 PD 的五分位，使两个样本按相同方式切分："

msgid ""
"Default rate and lift of the five PD bands of the validation sample, and the cumulative share of "
"defaults against the share of applicants"
msgstr "验证样本五个 PD 段的违约率和提升度，以及累计违约占比相对于申请人占比的曲线"

#, python-format
msgid ""
"The five PD bands of the validation sample. The riskiest fifth of the applicants holds 40% of the"
" defaults."
msgstr "验证样本的五个 PD 段。风险最高的五分之一申请人集中了 40% 的违约。"

msgid ""
"The riskiest band defaults at 21.7%, twice the average, and the safest at 3%. The bands of the "
"validation sample hold about a fifth of the applicants each, as they did in development, so the "
"model's PDs have not shifted between the two periods."
msgstr "风险最高的评分段违约率为 21.7%，是平均水平的两倍，最安全的为 3%。验证样本各评分段与开发样本一样，各约占五分之一的申请人，说明模型的 PD 在两个时期之间没有偏移。"

msgid ""
"This tutorial follows one credit risk project with kivi from the first look at the data to the "
"loss allowance of the loan book. A lender has decided its personal loan applications with a "
"scorecard bought from a vendor. After a year, it builds a scorecard of its own, sets its cut-off,"
" puts it into production, monitors it and measures the expected credit loss of its loans under "
"IFRS 9. Each chapter is one step of the project, and together they use nearly every function of "
"kivi."
msgstr ""
"本教程用 kivi "
"完整跟踪一个信用风险项目，从初看数据一直到贷款组合的损失准备。一家贷款机构一直用从供应商购买的评分卡审批个人贷款申请。一年后，它构建了自己的评分卡，设定截断点，将其投产并加以监控，再按 IFRS"
" 9 计量贷款的预期信用损失。每一章是项目的一个步骤，合起来用到了 kivi 的几乎所有函数。"

msgid ""
"The chapters build on each other, but each page runs on its own: a collapsed block at its top "
"repeats the code of the earlier chapters that the page needs. The :doc:`/user_guide/index` "
"explains each step in depth; the tutorial shows how the steps fit together and which decisions "
"the project takes on the way."
msgstr ""
"各章前后衔接，但每页都能单独运行：页首一个折叠的代码块重复该页需要的前面各章的代码。 :doc:`/user_guide/index` "
"深入讲解每个步骤；教程则展示各步骤如何衔接，以及项目在途中做出的各项决定。"

msgid "The project"
msgstr "项目背景"

msgid ""
"In 2024 the lender received 40,000 applications. Two policy rules declined some of them whatever "
"their risk: a debt-to-income ratio above 0.6 or an age below 21. The vendor's scorecard decided "
"the others and approved an application when its PD, ``incumbent_pd``, was below 15%. Whether a "
"borrower defaults is known only for the approved applications."
msgstr ""
"2024 年，这家贷款机构收到 40,000 笔申请。两条政策规则不论风险高低都会拒绝部分申请：负债收入比高于 0.6，或年龄低于 21 岁。其余申请由供应商的评分卡决定，当 PD（ "
"``incumbent_pd`` ）低于 15% 时批准。只有获批的申请才知道借款人是否违约。"

msgid ""
"The vendor's scorecard sees credit bureau data that the application form does not hold, but it "
"ignores some of the application data, and the lender cannot explain its decisions to applicants. "
"The project therefore builds a scorecard from the application data that keeps the vendor's PD as "
"one of its characteristics, as lenders do with a credit bureau score. The new scorecard must rank"
" applicants better than the vendor's PD alone, give a PD for every applicant, approved or not, "
"and state the reasons for a decline."
msgstr ""
"供应商的评分卡能看到申请表中没有的征信数据，但忽略了部分申请数据，而且贷款机构无法向申请人解释它的决定。因此，项目用申请数据构建评分卡，并像贷款机构对待征信评分那样，把供应商的 PD "
"保留为其中一个变量。新评分卡必须比单独使用供应商 PD 排序更好，为每个申请人（无论是否获批）给出 PD，并说明拒绝的原因。"

msgid "The data"
msgstr "数据"

msgid ""
"The applications are simulated by :func:`~kivi.datasets.make_applications`, and the loans that "
"the lender booked by :func:`~kivi.datasets.make_loan_panel`; :doc:`/user_guide/datasets` "
"describes both. Because the data are simulated, the outcome of every applicant is known, also of "
"the declined ones. A real project never sees those outcomes. The tutorial uses them only in boxes"
" like the one below, to show how close each estimate comes to the truth:"
msgstr ""
"贷款申请由 :func:`~kivi.datasets.make_applications` 模拟，贷款机构发放的贷款由 "
":func:`~kivi.datasets.make_loan_panel` 模拟； :doc:`/user_guide/datasets` "
"介绍了这两份数据。由于数据是模拟的，每个申请人的结果都是已知的，包括被拒绝的申请人。真实项目永远看不到这些结果。本教程只在下面这样的方框中使用它们，以显示每个估计值与真实情况有多接近："

msgid ""
"A box with this title uses information that a real project does not have. The steps of the "
"project never depend on it."
msgstr "带有这个标题的方框使用了真实项目所没有的信息。项目的各个步骤从不依赖它。"

msgid "The chapters"
msgstr "各章内容"

msgid ""
"Load the applications, split them into development and validation samples, and profile the "
"candidate variables. ``profile_table``"
msgstr "加载申请数据，划分开发样本和验证样本，并分析候选变量。 ``profile_table``"

msgid ""
"Compare the binning methods, group the categories, and fit every variable at once. ``bin_edges`` "
"· ``chimerge_edges`` · ``tree_edges`` · ``monotonic_edges`` · ``chimerge_groups`` · "
"``group_categories`` · ``woe_table`` · ``fit_spec``"
msgstr ""
"比较分箱方法，合并类别，并一次拟合所有变量。 ``bin_edges`` · ``chimerge_edges`` · ``tree_edges`` · ``monotonic_edges`` "
"· ``chimerge_groups`` · ``group_categories`` · ``woe_table`` · ``fit_spec``"

msgid "Variable selection and the model"
msgstr "变量筛选与建模"

msgid ""
"Encode the variables with WOE, check their correlations and fit the logistic regression on the "
"approved applicants. ``woe_transform`` · ``correlation_filter`` · ``vif`` · ``stepwise`` · "
"``logistic_regression``"
msgstr ""
"用 WOE 编码变量，检查相关性，并在获批申请人上拟合逻辑回归。 ``woe_transform`` · ``correlation_filter`` · ``vif`` · "
"``stepwise`` · ``logistic_regression``"

msgid ""
"Infer the outcomes of the declined applicants and refit the model on all applicants. "
"``fuzzy_augmentation`` · ``parceling`` · ``reweighting``"
msgstr "推断被拒申请人的结果，并在全部申请人上重新拟合模型。 ``fuzzy_augmentation`` · ``parceling`` · ``reweighting``"

msgid "The scorecard"
msgstr "评分卡"

msgid ""
"Scale the model to points, score the applicants and give the reasons for a low score. "
"``score_scaling`` · ``points_table`` · ``woe_to_points`` · ``score_to_pd`` · ``reason_codes``"
msgstr ""
"把模型转换为分值，为申请人评分，并给出低分的原因。 ``score_scaling`` · ``points_table`` · ``woe_to_points`` · "
"``score_to_pd`` · ``reason_codes``"

msgid ""
"Measure the ranking on the validation sample and compare it with the vendor's PD. ``roc_auc`` · "
"``gini`` · ``ks`` · ``brier_score`` · ``roc_table`` · ``roc_auc_interval`` · ``delong_test`` · "
"``gains_table``"
msgstr ""
"在验证样本上衡量排序能力，并与供应商的 PD 比较。 ``roc_auc`` · ``gini`` · ``ks`` · ``brier_score`` · ``roc_table`` · "
"``roc_auc_interval`` · ``delong_test`` · ``gains_table``"

msgid ""
"Build a master scale, test the PD of each grade and diagnose the calibration. ``master_scale`` · "
"``assign_grades`` · ``calibration_table`` · ``jeffreys_test`` · ``binomial_test`` · "
"``hosmer_lemeshow`` · ``platt_fit`` · ``fit_grade_pd`` · ``herfindahl_index``"
msgstr ""
"构建主标尺，检验每个等级的 PD，并分析校准情况。 ``master_scale`` · ``assign_grades`` · ``calibration_table`` · "
"``jeffreys_test`` · ``binomial_test`` · ``hosmer_lemeshow`` · ``platt_fit`` · ``fit_grade_pd`` · "
"``herfindahl_index``"

msgid "Cut-off and strategy"
msgstr "截断点与策略"

msgid ""
"Choose the cut-off, compare the new decisions with the old ones and add up the expected loss. "
"``cutoff_table`` · ``swap_set`` · ``expected_loss`` · ``expected_loss_table``"
msgstr ""
"选择截断点，将新的审批决定与原有决定比较，并汇总预期损失。 ``cutoff_table`` · ``swap_set`` · ``expected_loss`` · "
"``expected_loss_table``"

msgid "Production and monitoring"
msgstr "投产与监控"

msgid ""
"Save the binning for production, score a year of new applications and find the cause of a shift. "
"``BinningSpec`` · ``monitoring_table`` · ``stability_table`` · ``psi_table`` · ``csi_table``"
msgstr ""
"保存分箱方案以供投产，为一年的新申请评分，并找出偏移的原因。 ``BinningSpec`` · ``monitoring_table`` · ``stability_table`` · "
"``psi_table`` · ``csi_table``"

msgid "The loan book under IFRS 9"
msgstr "IFRS 9 下的贷款组合"

msgid ""
"Follow the booked loans, project their PDs and allocate them to stages with their loss allowance."
" ``vintage_table`` · ``roll_rates`` · ``transition_matrix`` · ``transition_pd`` · ``convert_pd`` "
"· ``expected_credit_loss`` · ``significant_increase`` · ``assign_stages`` · ``stage_table``"
msgstr ""
"跟踪已发放的贷款，推算它们的 PD，并将其划分到各阶段、计算损失准备。 ``vintage_table`` · ``roll_rates`` · ``transition_matrix`` · "
"``transition_pd`` · ``convert_pd`` · ``expected_credit_loss`` · ``significant_increase`` · "
"``assign_stages`` · ``stage_table``"

msgid ""
"The scorecard is a logistic regression of the default flag on the WOE of each characteristic. "
"This chapter encodes the development sample, checks that the characteristics do not repeat each "
"other, selects them and fits the model on the approved applicants."
msgstr "评分卡是违约标记对各变量 WOE 的逻辑回归。本章对开发样本做 WOE 编码，检查变量之间没有重复信息，筛选变量，并在获批申请人上拟合模型。"

msgid "Encode with WOE"
msgstr "WOE 编码"

msgid ""
":meth:`~kivi.spec.BinningSpec.woe_transform` groups every column of a sample and replaces each "
"group with its WOE:"
msgstr ":meth:`~kivi.spec.BinningSpec.woe_transform` 对样本的每一列分组，并把每个组替换为它的 WOE："

msgid "A higher WOE means a higher risk, so every coefficient of the model should come out positive."
msgstr "WOE 越高风险越高，因此模型的每个系数都应为正。"

msgid "Check the correlations"
msgstr "检查相关性"

msgid ""
"Two strongly correlated characteristics carry the same information and make the coefficients "
"unstable. :func:`~kivi.selection.correlation_filter` drops the weaker variable of every pair "
"correlated above 0.7, and :func:`~kivi.selection.vif` measures how well the other variables "
"together explain each one; see :doc:`/user_guide/selection`:"
msgstr ""
"两个高度相关的变量携带相同的信息，还会让系数不稳定。 :func:`~kivi.selection.correlation_filter` 在每对相关系数超过 0.7 的变量中剔除较弱的一个， "
":func:`~kivi.selection.vif` 衡量其他变量合起来能在多大程度上解释每个变量；见 :doc:`/user_guide/selection` ："

msgid ""
"No pair comes close to the threshold. The vendor's PD has the highest variance inflation factor, "
"because it uses the application data too, but 1.7 is far below the usual limit of 5 to 10."
msgstr "没有哪一对接近阈值。供应商的 PD 方差膨胀因子最高，因为它也用到了申请数据，但 1.7 远低于通常 5 到 10 的上限。"

msgid "Select the variables and fit the model"
msgstr "筛选变量并拟合模型"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.selection.stepwise` adds and removes variables by the p-values of a logistic "
"regression and, with WOE inputs, keeps only variables whose coefficient stays positive. "
":func:`~kivi.selection.logistic_regression` then fits the model:"
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.selection.stepwise` 按逻辑回归的 p 值逐步加入和剔除变量，并且在使用 WOE 输入时只保留系数为正的变量。随后由 "
":func:`~kivi.selection.logistic_regression` 拟合模型："

msgid ""
"Every characteristic is kept, and every coefficient is positive and significant. The vendor's PD "
"and ``housing``, which the vendor's scorecard ignores, have the largest z statistics."
msgstr "所有变量都被保留，每个系数都为正且显著。供应商的 PD 和供应商评分卡忽略的 ``housing`` 的 z 统计量最大。"

msgid ""
"The PD of an applicant is the logistic function of the intercept plus the WOE values times the "
"coefficients. The later chapters compute it with this function:"
msgstr "申请人的 PD 是截距加上 WOE 值乘以系数之和的逻辑函数值。后面各章用下面这个函数计算它："

msgid ""
"On the development sample, the mean PD equals the default rate, as it does for any logistic "
"regression with an intercept. The model is called ``accepts_model`` because it has seen only the "
"approved applicants. :doc:`reject_inference` asks what it predicts for the others."
msgstr ""
"在开发样本上，平均 PD 等于违约率，任何带截距的逻辑回归都是如此。这个模型叫作 ``accepts_model`` ，因为它只见过获批申请人。 :doc:`reject_inference` "
"将考察它对其他申请人的预测。"

msgid ""
"From January 2025 the new scorecard decides the applications. This chapter saves the binning for "
"the scoring system, scores a year of new applications, and follows the model month by month until"
" a shift in the applicants shows up; :doc:`/user_guide/monitoring` and :doc:`/user_guide/psi` "
"describe the measures."
msgstr ""
"从 2025 年 1 月起，由新评分卡审批申请。本章为评分系统保存分箱方案，为一年的新申请评分，并逐月跟踪模型，直到申请人结构出现偏移； "
":doc:`/user_guide/monitoring` 和 :doc:`/user_guide/psi` 介绍了这些指标。"

msgid "Save the binning"
msgstr "保存分箱"

msgid ""
"The scoring system must group and encode each application exactly as the development sample was. "
":meth:`~kivi.spec.BinningSpec.select` keeps the characteristics of the model, and "
":meth:`~kivi.spec.BinningSpec.to_json` writes their edges, groups and WOE tables as versioned "
"JSON; see :doc:`/user_guide/spec`. :meth:`~kivi.spec.BinningSpec.from_json` reads it back into an"
" equal specification:"
msgstr ""
"评分系统必须完全按照开发样本的方式对每笔申请分组和编码。 :meth:`~kivi.spec.BinningSpec.select` 保留模型中的变量， "
":meth:`~kivi.spec.BinningSpec.to_json` 把它们的边界、分组和 WOE 表写成带版本号的 JSON；见 :doc:`/user_guide/spec` 。 "
":meth:`~kivi.spec.BinningSpec.from_json` 把它读回为一个相等的分箱方案："

msgid ""
"The JSON is stored with the coefficients and the scale of :doc:`scorecard`. The examples below "
"score with ``restored``, as the scoring system would:"
msgstr "这份 JSON 与 :doc:`scorecard` 中的系数和刻度一起保存。下面的示例像评分系统一样，用 ``restored`` 来评分："

msgid "Score a year of applications"
msgstr "为一年的申请评分"

#, python-format
msgid ""
"The applications of 2025 come from a new sample of the same generator, 2,000 a month. In October "
"a competitor launches a cheaper loan, and most applicants with a low risk go there instead: from "
"then on, 70% of the applicants with a vendor PD below 7% no longer apply. The policy rules still "
"decline some applications, and the new cut-off decides the others:"
msgstr ""
"2025 年的申请来自同一生成器的新样本，每月 2,000 笔。10 月，一家竞争对手推出了更便宜的贷款，大多数低风险申请人转投对方：从那时起，供应商 PD 低于 7% 的申请人中有 70% "
"不再申请。政策规则仍会拒绝部分申请，其余由新的截断点决定："

msgid ""
"At the end of 2025, the outcomes of the loans granted up to September are known, and the later "
"ones are not. Unknown outcomes are passed as missing values."
msgstr "到 2025 年末，9 月及之前发放的贷款结果已知，之后的还不知道。未知的结果以缺失值传入。"

msgid "Follow the model month by month"
msgstr "逐月跟踪模型"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.monitoring.monitoring_table` gives one row per month: the applications, the known "
"outcomes and their default rate, the AUC, Gini and KS among the known outcomes, and the PSI of "
"the PDs against the eligible applicants of the development months:"
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.monitoring.monitoring_table` 每月给出一行：申请数、已知结果数及其违约率、已知结果上的 AUC、Gini 和 KS，以及 PD "
"相对于开发月份合格申请人的 PSI："

msgid ""
"Monthly applications and known outcomes, the Gini coefficient against its development value, and "
"the PSI of the PDs with the 0.1 and 0.25 thresholds"
msgstr "每月的申请数与已知结果数、Gini 系数及其开发样本值，以及带 0.1 和 0.25 阈值的 PD 的 PSI"

msgid ""
"The monitoring report of 2025. The Gini of the known outcomes scatters around its development "
"value; from October, the PSI of the PDs rises above 0.1."
msgstr "2025 年的监控报告。已知结果的 Gini 在开发样本值附近波动；从 10 月起，PD 的 PSI 升至 0.1 以上。"

msgid ""
"Until September the PSI stays below 0.02, and the Gini of the known outcomes scatters around its "
"value on the development sample:"
msgstr "到 9 月为止，PSI 一直低于 0.02，已知结果的 Gini 在其开发样本值附近波动："

msgid ""
"The approved applicants of 2025 were chosen by the new cut-off rather than the vendor's, so their"
" Gini is not expected to match exactly; a lasting fall would be the warning sign. From October, "
"fewer applications arrive and the PSI rises to between 0.13 and 0.15: above 0.1, the usual "
"threshold for a closer look, though below 0.25."
msgstr ""
"2025 年的获批申请人是由新截断点而不是供应商的截断点挑选的，因此其 Gini 不必与开发样本完全一致；持续下降才是警示信号。从 10 月起，申请量减少，PSI 升到 0.13 到 0.15 "
"之间：高于通常需要进一步检查的 0.1，但低于 0.25。"

msgid "Find the cause"
msgstr "找出原因"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.monitoring.stability_table` gives the PSI of every characteristic in every month, on"
" the groups of the specification:"
msgstr ":func:`~kivi.monitoring.stability_table` 按分箱方案的分组，给出每个变量每个月的 PSI："

msgid "PSI of each characteristic by month in 2025, as a heat map"
msgstr "2025 年各变量逐月 PSI 的热力图"

msgid "PSI of each characteristic by month. Only ``incumbent_pd`` moves, from October."
msgstr "各变量逐月的 PSI。只有 ``incumbent_pd`` 从 10 月起发生了变化。"

msgid ""
"Only the vendor's PD has shifted. :func:`~kivi.stability.psi_table` shows which of its bins "
"changed in December, and :func:`~kivi.stability.csi_table` how much each change moves the average"
" score, with the points of :doc:`scorecard`:"
msgstr ""
"只有供应商的 PD 发生了偏移。 :func:`~kivi.stability.psi_table` 显示 12 月哪些分箱发生了变化， "
":func:`~kivi.stability.csi_table` 则用 :doc:`scorecard` 中的分值显示每处变化使平均评分移动了多少："

msgid ""
"The three lowest bins, the applicants with a vendor PD below 5.4%, lost about two thirds of their"
" share, and through the vendor's PD alone the average score of December is 5.9 points lower. The "
"model is not wrong: it scores the applicants it now sees. The shift is a change of the business, "
"which the lender takes up with pricing and marketing rather than by refitting the scorecard. The "
"outcomes of the last quarter will show whether the PDs still hold."
msgstr ""
"最低的三个分箱，即供应商 PD 低于 5.4% 的申请人，占比减少了约三分之二；仅通过供应商 PD 这一项，12 月的平均评分就降低了 5.9 "
"分。模型并没有错：它为现在看到的申请人评分。这一偏移是业务的变化，贷款机构应当通过定价和营销来应对，而不是重新拟合评分卡。最后一个季度的结果将显示 PD 是否依然成立。"

msgid ""
"The approved applications become loans, and the lender follows them until they are repaid. This "
"chapter tracks how the loans go bad by origination month, how they move between delinquency "
"buckets, and turns those movements into the PD term structures, stages and loss allowance that "
"IFRS 9 requires; :doc:`/user_guide/vintage` and :doc:`/user_guide/lifetime` explain each step."
msgstr ""
"获批的申请变成贷款，贷款机构一直跟踪到它们还清为止。本章按放款月份跟踪贷款如何变坏、如何在逾期档之间移动，并把这些移动转换为 IFRS 9 所要求的 PD 期限结构、阶段和损失准备； "
":doc:`/user_guide/vintage` 和 :doc:`/user_guide/lifetime` 解释了每一步。"

msgid ""
"The loan book is the synthetic panel of :func:`~kivi.datasets.make_loan_panel`: 5,000 instalment "
"loans originated from January 2024 to December 2025, with their status at every month end up to "
"January 2026. It stands in for the loans that the lender booked; it is simulated apart from the "
"applications of the earlier chapters, so this chapter needs none of their code."
msgstr ""
"贷款组合是 :func:`~kivi.datasets.make_loan_panel` 生成的合成面板：2024 年 1 月至 2025 年 12 月发放的 5,000 笔分期贷款，以及它们在"
" 2026 年 1 月之前每个月末的状态。它代表贷款机构发放的贷款；它与前面各章的申请分开模拟，因此本章不需要前面各章的代码。"

msgid "Follow the vintages"
msgstr "跟踪各放款批次"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.vintage.vintage_table` gives, for each origination month and month on book, the "
"share of the loans that have been 90 days past due at least once:"
msgstr ":func:`~kivi.vintage.vintage_table` 对每个放款月份和账龄，给出至少逾期过 90 天一次的贷款占比："

msgid "Cumulative 90+ bad rate by month on book for one cohort in each half year"
msgstr "每半年取一个批次，按账龄展示 90 天以上逾期的累计坏账率"

msgid "Vintage curves of the cohorts in the table: each stops at the cohort's latest month on book."
msgstr "表中各批次的 vintage 曲线：每条曲线止于该批次最新的账龄月。"

msgid ""
"Each row follows one cohort and never decreases, because a loan that went bad stays counted. "
"Months that a cohort has not reached are missing, not zero."
msgstr "每一行跟踪一个批次，且从不下降，因为变坏过的贷款始终计入。批次尚未到达的月份是缺失值，而不是零。"

msgid "Measure the roll rates"
msgstr "计算滚动率"

msgid ""
"A transition matrix counts how loans move between the delinquency buckets from one month end to "
"the next. Pair each row of the panel with the row of the same loan one month later, then pass the"
" two statuses to :func:`~kivi.vintage.transition_matrix` and :func:`~kivi.vintage.roll_rates`:"
msgstr ""
"转移矩阵统计贷款从一个月末到下一个月末在逾期档之间的移动。把面板的每一行与同一笔贷款一个月后的那一行配对，再把两个状态传给 "
":func:`~kivi.vintage.transition_matrix` 和 :func:`~kivi.vintage.roll_rates` ："

#, python-format
msgid ""
"Each month 2.3% of the current loans miss an instalment, and seven in ten loans at 60 to 89 days "
"past due reach 90+ a month later."
msgstr "每月有 2.3% 的正常贷款错过一期还款，而逾期 60 到 89 天的贷款中有七成在一个月后达到 90 天以上。"

msgid "Project the PDs"
msgstr "推算 PD"

msgid ""
"If the movements follow the same monthly matrix every month, its powers give the probability of "
"reaching 90+ within any horizon from each bucket. :func:`~kivi.lifetime.transition_pd` makes 90+ "
"absorbing and returns these cumulative PDs, and :func:`~kivi.lifetime.convert_pd` turns them into"
" the marginal PD of each month:"
msgstr ""
"如果每个月的移动都服从同一个月度矩阵，矩阵的各次幂就给出从每个逾期档出发、在任意期限内到达 90 天以上的概率。 :func:`~kivi.lifetime.transition_pd` 把 "
"90 天以上设为吸收态并返回这些累计 PD， :func:`~kivi.lifetime.convert_pd` 再把它们转换为每个月的边际 PD："

msgid ""
"A current loan needs four months to reach 90+, so its PD is 0 for three months; a loan at 60 to "
"89 days past due reaches 90+ within the year with a probability of 87%."
msgstr "正常贷款需要四个月才能到达 90 天以上，因此前三个月的 PD 为 0；逾期 60 到 89 天的贷款在一年内到达 90 天以上的概率为 87%。"

msgid "Measure the expected credit loss"
msgstr "计量预期信用损失"

msgid ""
"The reporting date is the end of January 2026, the last month of the panel, and the book holds "
"the loans that still have a balance. Each loan gets the marginal PDs of its bucket, one column "
"per month after the reporting date:"
msgstr "报告日是面板的最后一个月，即 2026 年 1 月末；账上贷款是此时仍有余额的贷款。每笔贷款取其所在逾期档的边际 PD，报告日之后每个月一列："

msgid ""
"The exposure of each month is the balance that the loan is expected to owe then, repaid by its "
"remaining instalments of an annuity at 1% a month; :doc:`/user_guide/lifetime` derives it. A loan"
" at 90+ has defaulted at the reporting date, so its loss is not discounted:"
msgstr ""
"每个月的风险敞口是贷款预计届时仍欠的余额，按月利率 1% 的等额本息用剩余期数还款； :doc:`/user_guide/lifetime` 给出了推导。处于 90 "
"天以上的贷款在报告日已经违约，因此其损失不折现："

msgid "Allocate the stages"
msgstr "划分阶段"

msgid ""
"A loan whose credit risk has increased significantly since it was granted is in stage 2 and "
"carries its lifetime ECL; a loan in default is in stage 3. "
":func:`~kivi.lifetime.significant_increase` compares the 12-month PD of each loan's bucket with "
"that of a current loan, as every loan was current when granted, and "
":func:`~kivi.lifetime.assign_stages` adds the backstops of 30 and 90 days past due. The panel "
"records buckets, so the example takes the middle of each bucket as the days past due:"
msgstr ""
"自发放以来信用风险显著增加的贷款处于第二阶段，计提整个存续期的 ECL；已违约的贷款处于第三阶段。 :func:`~kivi.lifetime.significant_increase` "
"把每笔贷款所在逾期档的 12 个月 PD 与正常贷款的相比较（每笔贷款发放时都是正常的）， :func:`~kivi.lifetime.assign_stages` 再加上逾期 30 天和 90"
" 天的兜底标准。面板只记录逾期档，因此示例取每档的中点作为逾期天数："

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.lifetime.stage_table` adds up the exposure and the loss allowance of each stage: the"
" 12-month ECL in stage 1 and the lifetime ECL in stages 2 and 3:"
msgstr ":func:`~kivi.lifetime.stage_table` 汇总每个阶段的敞口和损失准备：第一阶段为 12 个月 ECL，第二、三阶段为存续期 ECL："

#, python-format
msgid ""
"Stage 1 holds nine tenths of the exposure at a coverage below 1%, while stage 3 holds the "
"defaulted loans at the LGD of 45%. The loss allowance of the whole book is 4% of its exposure."
msgstr "第一阶段占九成敞口，覆盖率不到 1%；第三阶段是已违约的贷款，覆盖率等于 45% 的 LGD。整个贷款组合的损失准备为其敞口的 4%。"

msgid "Close the loop"
msgstr "形成闭环"

msgid ""
"The project has gone from the applications to the loss allowance of the loans they became. In "
"production the steps repeat: the monitoring of :doc:`monitoring` watches the applicants and the "
"scorecard, the vintages and roll rates of this chapter watch the loans, and when either drifts, "
"the project returns to the data of :doc:`data` with the new outcomes."
msgstr ""
"项目从贷款申请一直走到这些申请所形成贷款的损失准备。投产后，这些步骤循环往复： :doc:`monitoring` 中的监控关注申请人和评分卡，本章的 vintage "
"和滚动率关注贷款；一旦任何一方发生漂移，项目就带着新的结果回到 :doc:`data` 的数据。"

msgid ""
"The model of :doc:`model` learned from the approved applicants only, but it will decide on every "
"applicant, including the kind that the vendor's scorecard used to decline. This chapter infers "
"the outcomes of the rejects and refits the model on all eligible applicants; "
":doc:`/user_guide/reject_inference` compares the methods in depth."
msgstr ""
":doc:`model` 中的模型只从获批申请人身上学习，但它将对每个申请人做决定，包括供应商评分卡过去会拒绝的那类申请人。本章推断拒绝申请人的结果，并在全部合格申请人上重新拟合模型； "
":doc:`/user_guide/reject_inference` 深入比较了各种方法。"

msgid "Score the rejects"
msgstr "为拒绝申请人评分"

msgid ""
"The accepts-only model gives the rejects of the development months a mean PD of about 20%, twice "
"the default rate of the accepts:"
msgstr "仅基于获批申请人的模型给开发月份的拒绝申请人的平均 PD 约为 20%，是获批申请人违约率的两倍："

msgid ""
"The accepts cannot show whether that is right. The vendor's scorecard declined these applicants "
"partly on bureau data that the model does not see, so they are probably riskier than accepts with"
" the same characteristics."
msgstr "获批申请人无法说明这是否正确。供应商评分卡拒绝这些申请人，部分依据的是模型看不到的征信数据，因此他们很可能比特征相同的获批申请人风险更高。"

msgid "The rejects default at 29.5%, so the accepts-only model underestimates their risk by a third:"
msgstr "拒绝申请人的违约率为 29.5%，因此仅基于获批申请人的模型把他们的风险低估了三分之一："

msgid "Infer their outcomes"
msgstr "推断他们的结果"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.reject_inference.fuzzy_augmentation` splits each reject into a bad row, weighted "
"with its PD times ``factor``, and a good row with the rest of its weight of 1. A factor above 1 "
"assumes that the rejects are riskier than their PD says. :func:`~kivi.reject_inference.parceling`"
" labels the rejects of each score band at the band's bad rate times ``factor``, and "
":func:`~kivi.reject_inference.reweighting` adds no rows and instead gives the accepts of each "
"band the weight (accepts + rejects) / accepts. The inferred rows join the development sample with"
" weight 1 for the accepts:"
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.reject_inference.fuzzy_augmentation` 把每个拒绝申请人拆成一行坏样本和一行好样本，坏样本的权重为其 PD 乘以 ``factor``"
" ，好样本取权重 1 的其余部分。 ``factor`` 大于 1 意味着假定拒绝申请人比其 PD 显示的风险更高。 "
":func:`~kivi.reject_inference.parceling` 按每个评分段的坏账率乘以 ``factor`` 把该段的拒绝申请人标为坏， "
":func:`~kivi.reject_inference.reweighting` 则不增加行，而是给每个评分段的获批申请人权重（获批 + 拒绝）/ 获批。推断出的行与权重为 1 "
"的获批申请人一起加入开发样本："

msgid "Each method gives the rejects an inferred bad rate and, after the refit, a mean PD:"
msgstr "每种方法都给出拒绝申请人的推断坏账率，以及重新拟合后的平均 PD："

msgid ""
"With a factor of 1, fuzzy augmentation infers exactly what the accepts-only model predicts and "
"leaves the model where it was. Reweighting cannot make the rejects riskier than the accepts of "
"their band. A factor of 1.5, for fuzzy augmentation or parceling, raises the inferred bad rate to"
" about 30%."
msgstr ""
"``factor`` 为 1 时，模糊扩充推断的正好是仅基于获批申请人的模型的预测，模型保持不变。重新加权无法让拒绝申请人比所在评分段的获批申请人风险更高。 ``factor`` 为 1.5 "
"时，模糊扩充和打包法都把推断的坏账率提高到约 30%。"

msgid ""
"The factor is an assumption that the approved applicants cannot confirm. The project assumes that"
" the rejects default half as often again as their PD says, a factor of 1.5, and keeps fuzzy "
"augmentation, which uses each reject's own PD rather than the band it falls into."
msgstr ""
"``factor`` 是获批申请人无法验证的假设。项目假定拒绝申请人的违约率是其 PD 的 1.5 倍，即 ``factor`` 为 1.5，并选用模糊扩充，因为它使用每个拒绝申请人自己的 "
"PD，而不是其所在评分段。"

msgid ""
"A factor of 1.5 brings the inferred bad rate within half a percentage point of the rejects' true "
"29.5%. On real data the factor is a judgment, and a sensitivity analysis as in "
":doc:`/user_guide/reject_inference` shows how much the results depend on it."
msgstr ""
"``factor`` 为 1.5 时，推断的坏账率与拒绝申请人真实的 29.5% 相差不到半个百分点。在真实数据上， ``factor`` 只能凭判断确定，像 "
":doc:`/user_guide/reject_inference` 中那样做敏感性分析，可以看出结果在多大程度上依赖于它。"

msgid "Refit the model"
msgstr "重新拟合模型"

msgid "The final model is fitted on the accepts and the inferred rejects together:"
msgstr "最终模型在获批申请人和推断出的拒绝申请人上共同拟合："

msgid ""
"Every coefficient grows: across all eligible applicants, the characteristics separate good from "
"bad more strongly than among the accepts alone. The intercept rises, because the sample now "
"includes the riskier rejects. The standard errors, however, are too small: the inferred rows "
"count as observations although they add no information. That is why the variables were selected "
"on the accepts in :doc:`model`, not on the augmented sample."
msgstr ""
"每个系数都变大了：在全部合格申请人中，各变量对好坏的区分比只在获批申请人中更强。截距上升，因为样本现在包含了风险更高的拒绝申请人。不过标准误偏小：推断出的行被当作观测值，尽管它们并没有增加信息。这就是为什么"
" :doc:`model` 在获批申请人上而不是在扩充后的样本上筛选变量。"

msgid ""
"A scorecard gives every group of every characteristic a number of points, so that an applicant's "
"score is a sum that anyone can retrace. This chapter scales the model of :doc:`reject_inference` "
"to points, scores the validation sample and gives the reasons for a low score."
msgstr "评分卡给每个变量的每个组一个分值，使申请人的评分成为任何人都能复核的加总。本章把 :doc:`reject_inference` 中的模型转换为分值，为验证样本评分，并给出低分的原因。"

msgid "Choose the scale"
msgstr "选择刻度"

msgid ""
"The score is linear in the log of the good:bad odds. The lender keeps the scale of its other "
"scorecards: 600 points stand for odds of 50 to 1, and every 20 points double the odds. "
":func:`~kivi.scorecard.score_scaling` gives the factor and the offset of that scale; see "
":doc:`/user_guide/scorecard`:"
msgstr ""
"评分与好坏比的对数成线性关系。贷款机构沿用其他评分卡的刻度：600 分对应 50 比 1 的好坏比，每增加 20 分好坏比翻一倍。 "
":func:`~kivi.scorecard.score_scaling` 给出该刻度的因子和偏移量；见 :doc:`/user_guide/scorecard` ："

msgid "Build the points table"
msgstr "构建分值表"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.scorecard.points_table` turns the WOE tables and the coefficients into points. A "
"higher WOE means more risk and therefore fewer points:"
msgstr ":func:`~kivi.scorecard.points_table` 把 WOE 表和系数转换为分值。WOE 越高风险越大，分值也就越低："

msgid ""
"Within a characteristic, the points of two groups differ by the factor times the coefficient "
"times the difference of their WOE. The vendor's PD spans 66 points from its best bin to its "
"worst, ``housing`` 25 points and ``employment`` 8."
msgstr ""
"在同一变量内，两个组的分值之差等于因子乘以系数再乘以它们的 WOE 之差。供应商的 PD 从最好的分箱到最差的分箱相差 66 分， ``housing`` 相差 25 分， "
"``employment`` 相差 8 分。"

msgid "Score the applicants"
msgstr "为申请人评分"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.scorecard.woe_to_points` gives every applicant the points of their groups, and the "
"points add up to the score:"
msgstr ":func:`~kivi.scorecard.woe_to_points` 给每个申请人所在各组的分值，各分值相加即为评分："

msgid ""
"The score is the scaled log odds of the model, so :func:`~kivi.scorecard.score_to_pd` turns it "
"back into the model's PD:"
msgstr "评分是模型对数几率经刻度转换的结果，因此 :func:`~kivi.scorecard.score_to_pd` 能把它还原为模型的 PD："

msgid "Explain a low score"
msgstr "解释低分"

msgid ""
"A declined applicant is told which characteristics lowered the score most. "
":func:`~kivi.scorecard.reason_codes` compares the points of each characteristic with those of its"
" best group and lists the largest shortfalls. For the three lowest scores of the validation "
"sample:"
msgstr ""
"被拒绝的申请人会被告知哪些变量让评分降低最多。 :func:`~kivi.scorecard.reason_codes` "
"把每个变量的分值与该变量最佳分组的分值相比较，列出差距最大的变量。以验证样本中评分最低的三人为例："

msgid ""
"All three have a vendor PD in its worst bin and rent their home, so ``incumbent_pd`` and "
"``housing`` come first; the third reason differs. The reasons follow from the points table alone,"
" so they are the same in every system that applies the scorecard."
msgstr ""
"三人的供应商 PD 都在最差的分箱，而且都是租房，因此 ``incumbent_pd`` 和 ``housing`` "
"排在前面；第三个原因各不相同。原因只取决于分值表，因此在任何应用该评分卡的系统中都相同。"

msgid ""
"The scorecard ranks the applicants, and the cut-off decides whom to approve. This chapter "
"estimates what each cut-off would approve over all eligible applicants, compares the new "
"decisions with the vendor's, and adds up the expected loss of the approved book; "
":doc:`/user_guide/strategy` describes each table."
msgstr ""
"评分卡为申请人排序，截断点决定批准谁。本章估计每个截断点在全部合格申请人中会批准哪些人，将新的审批决定与供应商的相比较，并汇总获批贷款的预期损失； "
":doc:`/user_guide/strategy` 介绍了每张表。"

msgid "Estimate each cut-off"
msgstr "估计每个截断点的效果"

msgid ""
"The cut-off applies to every eligible applicant, but the outcome is known only for those that the"
" vendor approved. The declined ones get inferred outcomes, as in :doc:`reject_inference`: "
":func:`~kivi.reject_inference.fuzzy_augmentation` with a factor of 1, because the model's PDs "
"already include the uplift of the rejects. Together with the approved applicants and their known "
"outcomes, they stand for all eligible applicants of October to December:"
msgstr ""
"截断点适用于每个合格申请人，但只有供应商批准的申请人结果已知。与 :doc:`reject_inference` 一样，被拒绝的申请人使用推断的结果：用 ``factor`` 为 1 的 "
":func:`~kivi.reject_inference.fuzzy_augmentation` ，因为模型的 PD 已经包含了对拒绝申请人的上调。它们与获批申请人及其已知结果一起，代表 10"
" 月至 12 月的全部合格申请人："

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.strategy.cutoff_table` gives, for each PD cut-off, the share of applicants that it "
"approves and the default rate of the approved book. The upper bounds of the grades approve the "
"grades up to each one:"
msgstr ":func:`~kivi.strategy.cutoff_table` 对每个 PD 截断点给出它批准的申请人占比和获批贷款的违约率。以各等级的上界作为截断点，就是批准截至该等级的所有等级："

#, python-format
msgid ""
"The vendor's scorecard approved 73.4% of the eligible applicants of the quarter, at a default "
"rate of 10.6%. Approving the grades A to D, a PD of at most 22.6%, approves 76.1% at an estimated"
" default rate of 10.4%: more loans at a slightly lower risk. The project takes that cut-off."
msgstr ""
"供应商评分卡批准了该季度 73.4% 的合格申请人，违约率为 10.6%。批准 A 到 D 级，即 PD 不超过 22.6%，可批准 76.1%，估计违约率为 "
"10.4%：贷款更多，风险还略低。项目采用这个截断点。"

msgid ""
"With the true outcomes of all eligible applicants, the same cut-offs give the same approval rates"
" and almost the same default rates:"
msgstr "用全部合格申请人的真实结果，同样的截断点给出相同的通过率和几乎相同的违约率："

msgid "Compare the decisions"
msgstr "比较审批决定"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.strategy.swap_set` puts the new decisions next to the vendor's. The vendor approved "
"a PD below 15%, while a cut-off approves PDs at or below it, so the vendor's cut-off is passed as"
" 0.1499, just below 15% at the four decimals of ``incumbent_pd``. The outcome is known only where"
" the vendor approved:"
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.strategy.swap_set` 把新的审批决定与供应商的并列。供应商批准 PD 低于 15% 的申请，而截断点批准不高于它的 PD，因此供应商的截断点按 "
"0.1499 传入，在 ``incumbent_pd`` 的四位小数下恰好低于 15%。只有供应商批准的申请结果已知："

msgid ""
"The new scorecard turns away 699 applicants whom the vendor approved, and who defaulted at 23.5%."
" It approves 951 applicants whom the vendor declined, the *swap-ins*, whose outcome no one knows."
" Their PDs say how risky they are expected to be:"
msgstr "新评分卡拒绝了 699 个供应商批准过的申请人，他们的违约率为 23.5%。它批准了 951 个供应商拒绝过的申请人，即 *换入* 申请人，他们的结果无人知道。他们的 PD 显示了预期的风险："

#, python-format
msgid ""
"The swap-ins default at 18.4%, close to their mean PD and below the 23.5% of the swap-outs, so "
"the exchange lowers the risk of the book:"
msgstr "换入申请人的违约率为 18.4%，接近其平均 PD，低于换出申请人的 23.5%，因此这一交换降低了贷款组合的风险："

msgid "Add up the expected loss"
msgstr "汇总预期损失"

msgid ""
"The expected loss of a loan is its PD times its loss given default times its exposure at default."
" The simulated applications have no loan amount, so the example lends each approved applicant six"
" months of income and takes one LGD of 45%. :func:`~kivi.strategy.expected_loss` gives the loss "
"of each loan, and :func:`~kivi.strategy.expected_loss_table` adds it up by grade:"
msgstr ""
"一笔贷款的预期损失等于其 PD 乘以违约损失率再乘以违约风险敞口。模拟的申请没有贷款金额，因此示例给每个获批申请人发放相当于六个月收入的贷款，并统一取 45% 的 LGD。 "
":func:`~kivi.strategy.expected_loss` 给出每笔贷款的损失， :func:`~kivi.strategy.expected_loss_table` 按等级汇总："

msgid ""
"Grade D holds over a third of the exposure but almost two thirds of the expected loss. Which "
"grades to approve, and at which price, is a business decision; the tables show its cost."
msgstr "D 级占三分之一以上的敞口，却占了将近三分之二的预期损失。批准哪些等级、以什么价格批准是业务决策；这些表格显示了它的代价。"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.binning.bin_edges` fits numeric bin edges on a reference sample and returns them as "
"an array for ``pandas.cut``. The reference can be a list, a NumPy array or a pandas Series. Keep "
"the array: the same edges must be applied to every sample that is compared with the reference."
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.binning.bin_edges` 在基准样本上拟合数值分箱边界，并以数组形式返回，供 ``pandas.cut`` 使用。基准样本可以是列表、NumPy 数组或 "
"pandas Series。请保存这个数组：与基准样本比较的每个样本都必须使用同一组边界。"

msgid ""
"In credit scoring, binning is the classing step of scorecard development: a continuous variable "
"becomes a handful of groups whose WOE can be read, explained to the business and monitored over "
"time. This page compares the ways to choose the edges."
msgstr "在信用评分中，分箱是评分卡开发的变量分组环节：连续变量被划分为少数几组，每组的 WOE 都可以解读、向业务解释并持续监控。本页比较选择边界的几种方式。"

msgid ""
"Binning follows the :doc:`univariate profile <univariate>`, which ranks the candidates by a quick"
" binning, and comes before the :doc:`weight of evidence <woe_iv>`, which measures and encodes the"
" groups. ``bin_edges`` chooses the edges from the values alone; "
":func:`~kivi.binning.chimerge_edges`, :func:`~kivi.binning.tree_edges` and "
":func:`~kivi.binning.monotonic_edges` also use the target, and :func:`~kivi.binning.cut` groups a"
" sample, with a group of its own for each special code."
msgstr ""
"分箱位于 :doc:`单变量概况 <univariate>` 之后（概况用快速分箱对候选变量排序），位于 :doc:`证据权重 <woe_iv>` 之前（证据权重衡量并编码各分组）。 "
"``bin_edges`` 只根据取值选择边界； :func:`~kivi.binning.chimerge_edges` 、 :func:`~kivi.binning.tree_edges` "
"和 :func:`~kivi.binning.monotonic_edges` 还会用到目标变量， :func:`~kivi.binning.cut` 则对样本分组，并让每个特殊值编码单独成组。"

msgid ""
"Categorical variables are grouped in the same two steps: :func:`~kivi.binning.category_groups` "
"pools rare categories, :func:`~kivi.binning.chimerge_groups` merges categories with similar event"
" rates, and :func:`~kivi.binning.group_categories` applies the grouping to a sample."
msgstr ""
"类别变量也按同样的两步分组： :func:`~kivi.binning.category_groups` 归并稀有类别， "
":func:`~kivi.binning.chimerge_groups` 合并事件率相近的类别， :func:`~kivi.binning.group_categories` "
"把分组映射应用到样本上。"

msgid "Quantile and uniform edges"
msgstr "等频与等距边界"

msgid ""
"Use quantile bins to divide the reference observations by rank, or uniform bins to divide their "
"numeric range into equal widths."
msgstr "等频分箱按基准样本中的秩划分观测，等距分箱按取值范围等宽划分。"

msgid ""
"Quantile bins hold roughly equal numbers of observations, which suits skewed variables. Uniform "
"bins keep equal widths, so a long tail can leave some bins nearly empty."
msgstr "等频分箱中各箱的观测数大致相同，适合偏态变量。等距分箱保持宽度一致，长尾可能让部分箱几乎为空。"

msgid ""
"Account balances are typical of financial data: most customers hold small amounts and a few hold "
"very large ones. On the bank data, quantile bins split the reference sample evenly, while uniform"
" bins put almost everyone into the first bin."
msgstr "账户余额是典型的金融数据：大多数客户余额不高，少数客户余额极大。在银行数据上，等频分箱把基准样本均匀切开，而等距分箱几乎把所有人都放进第一个箱。"

msgid ""
"Histogram of account balance with quantile and uniform edges, and the number of customers in each"
" bin for both methods"
msgstr "账户余额的直方图及等频、等距边界，以及两种方法下每箱的客户数"

msgid ""
"Left: the balance distribution, cut at its 99th percentile, with the quantile edges (solid) and "
"the first uniform edge (dashed). Right: customers per bin. Uniform bins leave the upper bins "
"almost empty, so their WOE would rest on a handful of customers."
msgstr "左图：余额分布（截断于第 99 百分位），实线为等频边界，虚线为第一个等距边界。右图：每箱的客户数。等距分箱让高位的箱几乎为空，这些箱的 WOE 只能依赖极少数客户。"

msgid "Custom edges"
msgstr "自定义边界"

msgid ""
"The edges do not have to come from :func:`~kivi.binning.bin_edges`. Any increasing array works "
"with ``pandas.cut`` and the metric functions, so policy bands and expert edges fit the same "
"workflow. Keep infinite outer edges so that every future value is covered."
msgstr ""
"边界不一定来自 :func:`~kivi.binning.bin_edges`。任何递增数组都可以传给 ``pandas.cut`` "
"和指标函数，因此政策分段和专家边界也能用于同一流程。请保留两端的无穷边界，确保之后的任何取值都有归属。"

#, python-format
msgid ""
"Risk data often encode a state as a number, for example -1 for \"never contacted\" or 999 for "
"\"no record\". In the bank data, 82% of the reference customers have ``pdays == -1``, so quantile"
" binning collapses the variable into a single bin and its information value is lost. An edge at "
"-1 gives the code a bin of its own."
msgstr ""
"风控数据常用数字编码某种状态，例如用 -1 表示“从未联系”，用 999 表示“无记录”。在银行数据中，82% 的基准样本客户 ``pdays == "
"-1``，因此等频分箱会把该变量压缩成一个箱，信息值随之丢失。在 -1 处设置边界，可以让这个编码单独成箱。"

msgid "WOE by age band and by days since the previous contact"
msgstr "按年龄分段和距上次联系天数计算的 WOE"

msgid ""
"Left: age bands show a U shape, with the youngest and oldest customers more likely to subscribe. "
"Right: customers contacted in a previous campaign within 200 days stand out once the -1 code has "
"its own bin."
msgstr "左图：年龄分段呈 U 形，最年轻和最年长的客户更可能认购。右图：-1 编码单独成箱后，200 天内在上一轮营销中被联系过的客户明显突出。"

msgid ""
"The edge at -1 works because no real value of ``pdays`` lies below the code. To fit the other "
"edges from the data instead, or for a code inside the range of real values, pass the code in "
"``special``; see :ref:`special-values`."
msgstr ""
"在 -1 处设边界之所以可行，是因为 ``pdays`` 的真实取值都不小于这个编码。如果想让其余边界由数据拟合，或者编码落在真实取值的范围之内，请把编码传给 ``special`` ，见 "
":ref:`special-values` 。"

msgid "Merging fine bins"
msgstr "合并细分箱"

msgid ""
"Scorecard development usually starts from many fine bins and merges neighbours, a step known as "
"coarse classing, until each bin is large enough to be stable and the WOE follows a trend that can"
" be explained. Select a subset of the fitted edges to merge bins; keeping the first and last edge"
" keeps the infinite ends."
msgstr ""
"评分卡开发通常先做较多的细分箱，再合并相邻的箱（即粗分箱），直到每箱样本足够稳定，WOE "
"也呈现可以解释的趋势。从已拟合的边界中选取一部分即可合并分箱；保留第一个和最后一个边界，就保留了两端的无穷边界。"

msgid "WOE of ten fine balance bins next to WOE of three merged bins"
msgstr "余额 10 个细分箱与合并后 3 个箱的 WOE 对比"

msgid ""
"Ten fine bins (left) zigzag; three merged bins (right) rise steadily with balance and give up "
"little information value."
msgstr "10 个细分箱（左）呈锯齿状；合并后的 3 个箱（右）随余额稳步上升，信息值损失很小。"

msgid ""
"Choosing the merges by hand works for a few variables. The supervised methods in the next section"
" search for them automatically, and two of them start from fine quantile bins in the same way."
msgstr "变量不多时，可以手工选择合并方式。下一节的有监督方法会自动搜索合并方案，其中两种同样从等频细分箱出发。"

msgid "Supervised binning"
msgstr "有监督分箱"

msgid ""
"Quantile and uniform edges ignore the target. The supervised methods use it to place edges "
"between customers with different event rates, which is what the WOE of each bin measures. They "
"take the values and a 0/1 target, as Series on the same index or as arrays and lists matched by "
"position, omit missing values and any codes passed in ``special`` while fitting, and return edges"
" in the same form as :func:`~kivi.binning.bin_edges`: increasing, with infinite outer edges, "
"ready for ``pandas.cut``, :func:`~kivi.woe.woe_table` and :func:`~kivi.stability.psi_table`. Each"
" returns at most ``max_bins`` bins, 5 by default."
msgstr ""
"等频与等距边界不考虑目标变量。有监督方法则利用目标变量，把边界放在事件率不同的客户之间，而这正是每箱 WOE 所度量的差异。它们接收数值和 0/1 目标变量：二者是 Series "
"时须索引相同，是数组或列表时按位置对应；拟合时忽略缺失值以及传给 ``special`` 的编码，返回的边界与 :func:`~kivi.binning.bin_edges` "
"形式相同：严格递增、两端为无穷，可直接用于 ``pandas.cut``、:func:`~kivi.woe.woe_table` 和 "
":func:`~kivi.stability.psi_table`。每种方法最多返回 ``max_bins`` 个箱，默认为 5。"

msgid "How it fits the edges"
msgstr "拟合边界的方式"

msgid "Main options"
msgstr "主要参数"

msgid ":func:`~kivi.binning.chimerge_edges`"
msgstr ":func:`~kivi.binning.chimerge_edges`"

msgid "Merges adjacent fine bins whose event rates do not differ significantly."
msgstr "合并事件率没有显著差异的相邻细分箱。"

msgid "``max_bins``, ``alpha``"
msgstr "``max_bins``、``alpha``"

msgid ":func:`~kivi.binning.tree_edges`"
msgstr ":func:`~kivi.binning.tree_edges`"

msgid "Splits the values where a decision tree gains the most purity."
msgstr "在决策树纯度提升最大的位置切分数值。"

msgid "``max_bins``, ``min_bin_share``, ``criterion``"
msgstr "``max_bins``、``min_bin_share``、``criterion``"

msgid ":func:`~kivi.binning.monotonic_edges`"
msgstr ":func:`~kivi.binning.monotonic_edges`"

msgid "Merges adjacent fine bins until the WOE rises or falls steadily."
msgstr "合并相邻细分箱，直到 WOE 稳定上升或下降。"

msgid "``max_bins``, ``direction``"
msgstr "``max_bins``、``direction``"

msgid ""
"As with ``bin_edges``, fit the edges on the reference sample only and apply the saved array to "
"every other sample."
msgstr "与 ``bin_edges`` 一样，只在基准样本上拟合边界，再把保存的数组用于其他所有样本。"

msgid "ChiMerge"
msgstr "ChiMerge（卡方分箱）"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.binning.chimerge_edges` starts from fine quantile bins, 20 by default, and "
"repeatedly merges the adjacent pair whose event rates are most alike, the pair with the smallest "
"chi-square statistic. Merging continues while more than ``max_bins`` bins remain or while some "
"adjacent pair does not differ significantly at level ``alpha``."
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.binning.chimerge_edges` 从等频细分箱（默认 20 个）开始，反复合并事件率最接近、即卡方统计量最小的一对相邻箱。只要箱数仍多于 "
"``max_bins``，或仍有相邻两箱在显著性水平 ``alpha`` 下差异不显著，就继续合并。"

msgid ""
"Five bins were allowed, but with five and with four bins some adjacent pair still had a chi-"
"square below 3.84, the critical value at ``alpha=0.05``, so merging went on to three bins. Pass "
"``alpha=None`` to merge down to ``max_bins`` only, or a larger ``alpha`` to keep more bins."
msgstr ""
"虽然允许 5 个箱，但在 5 箱和 4 箱时，仍有相邻两箱的卡方值低于 ``alpha=0.05`` 对应的临界值 3.84，因此继续合并到 3 个箱。传入 ``alpha=None`` "
"只合并到 ``max_bins`` 个箱；传入更大的 ``alpha`` 可保留更多箱。"

msgid ""
"Smallest chi-square between adjacent balance bins as ChiMerge merges them, and the WOE of the "
"three final bins"
msgstr "ChiMerge 合并余额分箱过程中相邻箱的最小卡方值，以及最终 3 个箱的 WOE"

msgid ""
"Left: the smallest chi-square between adjacent bins as the fine bins are merged, read from left "
"to right. Merging stops at the first count no larger than max_bins at which every pair lies above"
" the alpha line. Right: the WOE of the final bins rises with balance."
msgstr "左图：细分箱逐步合并时相邻箱之间的最小卡方值，从左向右阅读。当箱数不超过 max_bins 且所有相邻箱都位于 alpha 线上方时，合并停止。右图：最终各箱的 WOE 随余额上升。"

msgid "Decision tree"
msgstr "决策树"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.binning.tree_edges` grows a decision tree on the one variable. Each split cuts a bin"
" at the value that most reduces the impurity of the target, measured by entropy (the default) or "
"by the Gini index with ``criterion=\"gini\"``. The bin whose best split gains the most is split "
"next, until there are ``max_bins`` bins or no allowed split reduces the impurity. "
"``min_bin_share`` keeps every bin above a share of the observations, 5% by default, so that its "
"WOE rests on enough customers. The interior edges are observed values."
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.binning.tree_edges` 在单个变量上生长一棵决策树。每次切分都选在使目标变量不纯度下降最多的取值处，不纯度默认用熵度量，传入 "
"``criterion=\"gini\"`` 则用基尼指数。最优切分收益最大的箱先被切分，直到箱数达到 ``max_bins``，或没有允许的切分能降低不纯度。``min_bin_share``"
" 要求每箱的观测占比不低于给定值（默认 5%），使每箱的 WOE 建立在足够多的客户之上。内部边界都是观测值。"

msgid ""
"The tree separates the classes best, but it does not look for a trend: customers above 6,046 "
"subscribe less often than those just below them. A scorecard needs a WOE pattern that can be "
"explained, so check the trend of tree bins before using them, and merge bins where it breaks."
msgstr ""
"决策树对两类客户的区分最好，但它并不追求趋势：余额高于 6,046 的客户，认购比例反而低于余额略低于该值的客户。评分卡需要可以解释的 WOE "
"形态，因此使用决策树分箱前应检查趋势，并在趋势被打破处合并分箱。"

msgid "Entropy reduction of every possible first cut of balance, and the WOE of the five tree bins"
msgstr "余额每个可能的第一次切分带来的熵下降，以及决策树 5 个箱的 WOE"

msgid ""
"Left: the entropy reduction of every possible first cut. Cuts in the shaded areas would leave "
"less than min_bin_share of the customers in a bin. The dashed lines are the tree's cuts, numbered"
" in the order they were made. Right: the WOE of the five bins rises, then falls in the top bin."
msgstr ""
"左图：每个可能的第一次切分带来的熵下降。阴影区域内的切分会让某个箱的客户占比低于 min_bin_share。虚线是决策树的切分点，编号为切分的先后顺序。右图：5 个箱的 WOE "
"先上升，在最高的箱中回落。"

msgid "Monotonic binning"
msgstr "单调分箱"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.binning.monotonic_edges` also starts from fine quantile bins. Whenever two adjacent "
"bins break the trend, it merges them and recomputes the WOE (pool adjacent violators), so the WOE"
" of the final bins is strictly increasing or strictly decreasing. If more than ``max_bins`` bins "
"remain, it then merges the most similar adjacent pairs by chi-square. ``direction=\"auto\"`` "
"tries both trends and keeps the one with the larger information value; pass ``\"increasing\"`` or"
" ``\"decreasing\"`` to impose the trend that the business expects."
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.binning.monotonic_edges` 同样从等频细分箱开始。每当相邻两箱违背趋势，就将它们合并并重新计算 WOE（合并相邻违序者，pool adjacent"
" violators），因此最终各箱的 WOE 严格递增或严格递减。若箱数仍多于 ``max_bins``，再按卡方统计量合并最相近的相邻箱。``direction=\"auto\"`` "
"会尝试两种趋势，保留信息值较大的一种；传入 ``\"increasing\"`` 或 ``\"decreasing\"`` 可以指定业务预期的趋势。"

msgid ""
"The trend is checked with the same smoothing as :func:`~kivi.woe.woe_table`, so the WOE that "
"``woe_table`` reports for these bins is monotonic as well, even when a bin has no events."
msgstr "趋势检查使用与 :func:`~kivi.woe.woe_table` 相同的平滑规则，因此即使某个箱没有事件，``woe_table`` 对这些箱给出的 WOE 也是单调的。"

msgid "WOE of the fine balance bins with the pooled monotonic WOE, and the WOE of the five final bins"
msgstr "余额细分箱的 WOE 与合并后的单调 WOE，以及最终 5 个箱的 WOE"

msgid ""
"Left: the WOE of the fine quantile bins zigzags; pooling adjacent violators turns it into a "
"rising step (max_bins=None). Right: merged further to max_bins=5, the WOE still rises with "
"balance."
msgstr "左图：等频细分箱的 WOE 呈锯齿状；合并相邻违序箱后变为上升的阶梯（max_bins=None）。右图：进一步合并到 max_bins=5 后，WOE 仍随余额上升。"

msgid "Comparing the methods"
msgstr "方法对比"

msgid ""
"Supervised edges are chosen to separate the sample they are fitted on, so the information value "
"on that sample is optimistic. Compare the methods on a later sample as well, keeping the edges "
"fixed."
msgstr "有监督边界是为区分拟合样本而选出的，因此在该样本上算出的信息值偏乐观。保持边界不变，在之后的样本上也对比一次各方法。"

msgid ""
"On the reference sample all three supervised methods beat five quantile bins. On the later sample"
" they fall behind: much of the extra separation they found in balance was noise, which is common "
"for a weak variable and a few hundred events. Validate supervised edges on a later or held-out "
"sample before adopting them, and keep the variable under PSI monitoring once it is in use."
msgstr ""
"在基准样本上，三种有监督方法都优于 5 "
"个等频箱；在之后的样本上却落在后面：它们在余额上多找到的区分度，很大一部分是噪声。对于较弱的变量和仅有几百个事件的样本，这种情况很常见。采用有监督边界之前，应先在之后的样本或留出样本上验证；变量投入使用后，还要持续做"
" PSI 监控。"

msgid "Applying the edges"
msgstr "应用边界"

msgid ""
"Infinite endpoints cover finite future observations outside the training range. Use the saved "
"edges with pandas.cut on every sample."
msgstr "两端延伸至无穷，因此可覆盖后续超出训练范围的有限值。保存边界，再对每期数据调用 pandas.cut。"

msgid ""
"Six reference values with the fitted edge at 35, and the sample values 5, 35, 99 and a missing "
"value with the groups that pandas.cut gives them"
msgstr "六个基准值及拟合出的边界 35，以及样本值 5、35、99 和一个缺失值，和 pandas.cut 给它们分的组"

msgid ""
"``bin_edges`` fits the edge at 35 on the reference values (dots), and ``pandas.cut`` applies it "
"to the sample (diamonds). 5 and 99 lie outside the reference range but fall into the infinite end"
" bins, 35 lies on the edge and goes to the lower bin, and the missing value stays missing."
msgstr ""
"``bin_edges`` 在基准值（圆点）上拟合出边界 35， ``pandas.cut`` 把它应用到样本（菱形）上。5 和 99 超出了基准值的范围，但落入两端的无穷分箱；35 "
"正好在边界上，归入较低的分箱；缺失值仍然是缺失值。"

msgid ""
"Intervals are closed on the right, so a value equal to an edge belongs to the lower bin. Pass "
"``labels=False`` to ``pandas.cut`` for integer bin numbers instead of intervals."
msgstr "区间为左开右闭，因此等于某个边界的值归入较低的箱。若要得到整数箱号而不是区间，可向 ``pandas.cut`` 传入 ``labels=False``。"

msgid ""
"Pass categorical labels directly to the metric functions. A missing label is a separate group. "
"Only observed groups appear. Categorical groups, including the result of ``pandas.cut``, follow "
"the order of their categories with missing values last; other labels follow the order in which "
"they first appear. For WOE, group and target series must have identical indices; arrays and lists"
" are matched by position. :doc:`/api/conventions` describes these rules for every function."
msgstr ""
"类别变量可直接传给指标函数。缺失标签独立成组。输出仅列出实际观测到的组。分类型分组（包括 ``pandas.cut`` 的结果）按类别顺序排列，缺失值排在最后；其他标签按首次出现的次序排列。计算"
" WOE 时，分组与标签序列的索引必须完全一致；数组和列表按位置对应。 :doc:`/api/conventions` 说明了所有函数共同遵守的这些规则。"

msgid "Grouping categories"
msgstr "类别分组"

msgid ""
"A categorical variable needs no edges: each label is already a group. It may still need coarse "
"classing. The WOE of a label held by a few dozen customers rests on a handful of events, and a "
"scorecard with a group for each of many labels is hard to explain and to monitor. On the bank "
"data, the WOE of four of the twelve jobs changes sign on the later sample:"
msgstr ""
"类别变量不需要边界：每个标签本身就是一组。但它可能仍需要粗分箱。只有几十位客户的标签，其 WOE 只建立在寥寥几个事件之上；而为众多标签各设一组的评分卡难以解释，也难以监控。在银行数据中，12 "
"种职业里有 4 种的 WOE 在之后的样本上改变了符号："

msgid ""
"Grouping categories follows the same two steps as binning. :func:`~kivi.binning.category_groups` "
"and :func:`~kivi.binning.chimerge_groups` fit a grouping on the reference sample and return it as"
" a dict from category to group, which can be reviewed, edited and saved like an array of edges. "
":func:`~kivi.binning.group_categories` applies it to every sample, as :func:`~kivi.binning.cut` "
"applies edges."
msgstr ""
"类别分组与分箱一样分两步。 :func:`~kivi.binning.category_groups` 和 :func:`~kivi.binning.chimerge_groups` "
"在基准样本上拟合分组映射，并以从类别到组的 dict 返回，可以像边界数组一样审阅、修改和保存。 :func:`~kivi.binning.group_categories` "
"把它应用到每个样本上，就像 :func:`~kivi.binning.cut` 应用边界一样。"

msgid "Pooling rare categories"
msgstr "归并稀有类别"

#, python-format
msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.binning.category_groups` pools the categories that hold less than ``min_share`` of "
"the reference, 5% by default, or fewer than ``min_count`` customers, into one group labelled "
"``rare_label``, ``\"other\"`` by default. Every other category keeps a group of its own. Four "
"jobs hold less than 3% of the reference customers:"
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.binning.category_groups` 把占基准样本比例低于 ``min_share`` （默认 5%）或客户数少于 ``min_count`` "
"的类别归为一组，标签为 ``rare_label`` （默认 ``\"other\"`` ）。其他类别各自单独成组。有 4 种职业的客户占基准样本不到 3%："

msgid ""
"Pooling needs no target, so it also suits variables that are only monitored. It ignores the event"
" rates, however: here students, who subscribe more than twice as often as the average customer, "
"share a group with the unemployed, who subscribe less often."
msgstr "归并不需要目标变量，因此也适用于只做监控的变量。不过它忽略了事件率：这里学生的认购率是平均客户的两倍多，却与认购率较低的失业者同在一组。"

msgid "Merging categories by event rate"
msgstr "按事件率合并类别"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.binning.chimerge_groups` sorts the categories by their WOE, smoothed as in "
":func:`~kivi.woe.woe_table`, and merges neighbours in that order, so that every group joins "
"categories with similar event rates. First, a group that holds less than ``min_group_share`` of "
"the reference, 5% by default, is merged with the neighbour it is more similar to. Then, as in "
":ref:`ChiMerge <supervised-binning>`, the neighbours with the smallest chi-square statistic are "
"merged while more than ``max_groups`` groups remain or while some pair does not differ "
"significantly at level ``alpha``. Ties, between equal WOE or equal statistics, go to the category"
" that appears first. A merged group is labelled with its categories in increasing order of their "
"WOE, or, when it has more than five, with the first four and the number of the others, such as "
"``'a, b, c, d, ... (+3)'``:"
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.binning.chimerge_groups` 按 WOE（与 :func:`~kivi.woe.woe_table` "
"一样做平滑）对类别排序，再合并该顺序下相邻的类别，使每组都由事件率相近的类别组成。首先，占基准样本比例低于 ``min_group_share`` （默认 "
"5%）的组与更相似的那个相邻组合并。然后像 :ref:`ChiMerge <supervised-binning>` 一样，只要组数仍多于 ``max_groups`` "
"，或仍有一对相邻组在显著性水平 ``alpha`` 下差异不显著，就合并卡方统计量最小的相邻组。WOE 或统计量相同时，取先出现的类别。合并后的组以其各类别命名，按类别的 WOE "
"从小到大排列；超过五个类别时只列出前四个和其余类别的个数，例如 ``'a, b, c, d, ... (+3)'`` ："

msgid ""
"The groups come in increasing order of WOE, so their WOE rises from the first to the last by "
"construction. On the later sample the three groups keep that order, although the WOE of their "
"categories does not:"
msgstr "各组按 WOE 从小到大排列，因此其 WOE 从第一组到最后一组必然递增。在之后的样本上，这三组保持了这一顺序，尽管其中各类别的 WOE 并没有保持："

msgid ""
"WOE of the twelve jobs on the reference and the later sample, sorted by reference WOE, with the "
"three merged groups shaded and the WOE of each group drawn as steps"
msgstr "十二种职业在基准样本和后续样本上的 WOE，按基准样本的 WOE 排序，三个合并后的分组以阴影标出，各分组的 WOE 画成阶梯线"

msgid ""
"WOE of each job on the reference sample (circles) and on the later sample (diamonds), sorted by "
"reference WOE. The shaded bands are the three groups of ``chimerge_groups`` and the steps the WOE"
" of each group: the jobs move between the samples, but the groups keep their order."
msgstr ""
"各职业在基准样本（圆点）和后续样本（菱形）上的 WOE，按基准样本的 WOE 排序。阴影带是 ``chimerge_groups`` 的三个分组，阶梯线是各分组的 "
"WOE：职业在两个样本之间有所移动，但分组保持原有顺序。"

msgid ""
"Grouping lowers the information value on both samples. The IV of many small groups is biased "
"upward, because each group adds a positive term even where its WOE is noise, so a lower IV with "
"stable groups is often the better variable:"
msgstr "分组会降低两个样本上的信息值。许多小组的 IV 有向上的偏差，因为即使某组的 WOE 只是噪声，它也会贡献一个正项；因此 IV 较低但分组稳定的变量往往更好："

#, python-format
msgid ""
"``min_group_share`` can also merge a small category that does differ. In the bank data, the 83 "
"customers whose previous campaign succeeded, 2.8% of the reference, subscribe at a rate of 63%, "
"yet with the default they share a group with the outcome ``other``. Pass ``min_group_share=0`` to"
" rely on the chi-square test alone:"
msgstr ""
"``min_group_share`` 也可能合并一个确实不同的小类别。在银行数据中，上一轮营销成功的 83 位客户占基准样本的 2.8%，认购率为 63%，但在默认设置下他们与结果为 "
"``other`` 的客户同在一组。传入 ``min_group_share=0`` 则只依据卡方检验："

msgid "Applying the groups"
msgstr "应用分组"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.binning.group_categories` replaces each value with its group and keeps missing "
"values missing. The result is categorical, with the groups in the order of the dict, so "
":func:`~kivi.woe.woe_table`, :func:`~kivi.woe.woe_transform` and "
":func:`~kivi.stability.psi_table` take it as they take the result of :func:`~kivi.binning.cut`. A"
" category that the grouping does not know, such as a job that appears only in production, raises "
"an error instead of becoming a missing value. Pass ``unseen`` to give such categories one of the "
"groups, for example the group of rare categories:"
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.binning.group_categories` 把每个取值替换为其所属的组，缺失值保持缺失。结果为分类型，各组按 dict 中的顺序排列，因此 "
":func:`~kivi.woe.woe_table` 、 :func:`~kivi.woe.woe_transform` 和 :func:`~kivi.stability.psi_table`"
" 可以像使用 :func:`~kivi.binning.cut` 的结果一样使用它。分组映射中没有的类别（例如只在生产环境中出现的职业）会引发错误，而不会变成缺失值。传入 ``unseen`` "
"可为这类类别指定一个组，例如稀有类别组："

msgid ""
"The grouping is a plain dict, so a reviewer can move a category to another group or write a "
"grouping by hand. Keep the categories of a group under one label: the label is what "
":func:`~kivi.woe.woe_table` reports and what :func:`~kivi.binning.group_categories` returns. "
":doc:`spec` groups the categorical columns of a whole data frame and saves the groupings with the"
" edges."
msgstr ""
"分组映射就是普通的 dict，审阅者可以把某个类别移到另一组，也可以手工编写分组映射。同一组的类别要使用同一个标签： :func:`~kivi.woe.woe_table` 报告的、 "
":func:`~kivi.binning.group_categories` 返回的都是这个标签。 :doc:`spec` 对整个数据框的类别列分组，并把分组映射与边界一起保存。"

msgid "Special values"
msgstr "特殊值"

msgid ""
"Many credit variables use codes such as ``-1`` or ``-999`` for \"not applicable\" or \"no "
"record\". Such a code is not a measurement, so it should neither shape the edges nor share an "
"interval with real values. Pass the codes in ``special`` to :func:`~kivi.binning.bin_edges` to "
"leave them out of the fit, and pass the same codes to :func:`kivi.binning.cut` to give each one "
"its own group."
msgstr ""
"许多信贷变量用 ``-1`` 或 ``-999`` 这样的编码表示“不适用”或“无记录”。这类编码不是测量值，既不应影响边界，也不应与真实取值共用一个区间。把这些编码传给 "
":func:`~kivi.binning.bin_edges` 的 ``special`` 参数，拟合时会排除它们；再把同样的编码传给 :func:`kivi.binning.cut` "
"，每个编码就会单独成组。"

#, python-format
msgid ""
"In the bundled data, ``pdays`` is ``-1`` for the 82% of customers who were not contacted in an "
"earlier campaign. Without ``special``, every quantile is tied at ``-1``: ``bin_edges`` returns a "
"single bin and warns that ``-1`` makes up 82% of the fitted values. With ``special=[-1]`` the "
"remaining values are divided into five bins:"
msgstr ""
"在随包数据中，82% 的客户此前未被联系过，他们的 ``pdays`` 为 ``-1`` 。不传 ``special`` 时，所有分位点都重合在 ``-1`` ： ``bin_edges`` "
"只返回一个箱，并警告 ``-1`` 占拟合取值的 82%。传入 ``special=[-1]`` 后，其余取值被分成五个箱："

msgid ""
"The single bin had an IV of zero; separating the code shows that ``pdays`` is informative. The "
"categories of the result are the special values in the order given, followed by the intervals, "
"and :func:`~kivi.woe.woe_table` and :func:`~kivi.stability.psi_table` list the rows in that "
"order. Special values are matched by equality, so ``-1`` and ``-1.0`` are the same code. Without "
"``special``, ``cut`` returns the same result as ``pandas.cut``."
msgstr ""
"原来那唯一一个箱的 IV 为零；把编码单独分出来之后，可以看出 ``pdays`` 是有信息量的。结果的类别依次为按给定顺序排列的特殊值和各区间， "
":func:`~kivi.woe.woe_table` 和 :func:`~kivi.stability.psi_table` 也按这个顺序列出各行。特殊值按相等关系匹配，因此 ``-1`` 和"
" ``-1.0`` 视为同一个编码。不传 ``special`` 时， ``cut`` 的结果与 ``pandas.cut`` 相同。"

msgid "Special values in supervised binning"
msgstr "有监督分箱中的特殊值"

msgid ""
"A code such as ``pdays == -1`` is fitted as an ordinary value unless it is passed in ``special``."
" Monotonic binning then puts the 2,475 reference customers coded -1, who were never contacted "
"before, into one bin with the 78 customers contacted within 96 days, the group most likely to "
"subscribe:"
msgstr ""
"像 ``pdays == -1`` 这样的编码，如果不传给 ``special`` ，就会被当作普通取值参与拟合。此时单调分箱会把基准样本中编码为 -1、此前从未被联系过的 2,475 "
"位客户，与 96 天内被联系过的 78 位客户放进同一个箱，而后者正是最可能认购的群体："

msgid ""
"With ``special=[-1]`` the code and its labels are left out of the fit, and "
":func:`~kivi.binning.cut` with the same code gives it a group of its own ahead of the intervals:"
msgstr "传入 ``special=[-1]`` 后，该编码连同其标签不参与拟合；再把同一编码传给 :func:`~kivi.binning.cut` ，它就会单独成组，排在各区间之前："

msgid ""
"Fitted on the contacted customers alone, the WOE falls steadily: the more recent the previous "
"contact, the more likely a customer is to subscribe. ``max_bins`` and the trend apply to the "
"intervals only, so each special group comes on top of them with a WOE of its own. "
":func:`~kivi.binning.chimerge_edges` and :func:`~kivi.binning.tree_edges` take ``special`` in the"
" same way, and ``min_bin_share`` counts only the values that are fitted."
msgstr ""
"只用被联系过的客户拟合后，WOE 稳定下降：上一次联系越近，客户越可能认购。``max_bins`` 和单调趋势只约束各区间，每个特殊值组在此之外单独成组，并有自己的 "
"WOE。:func:`~kivi.binning.chimerge_edges` 和 :func:`~kivi.binning.tree_edges` 以同样的方式接受 ``special`` "
"，``min_bin_share`` 也只统计参与拟合的取值。"

msgid "Special values in category groups"
msgstr "类别分组中的特殊值"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.binning.category_groups` and :func:`~kivi.binning.chimerge_groups` take ``special`` "
"as well, for a label such as ``\"unknown\"`` that should never share a group. The codes are "
"matched by equality, left out of the fit with their labels, and placed first in the grouping, "
"each mapped to itself, so that :func:`~kivi.binning.group_categories` needs no ``special`` "
"argument. A code that the reference lacks is still in the grouping, and its group has no row in "
":func:`~kivi.woe.woe_table`. ``max_groups``, ``min_share`` and ``min_group_share`` count only the"
" other categories:"
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.binning.category_groups` 和 :func:`~kivi.binning.chimerge_groups` 也接受 ``special`` ，用于"
" ``\"unknown\"`` 这类不应与其他类别同组的标签。这些编码按相等关系匹配，连同其标签一起排除在拟合之外，并各自映射到自身、排在分组映射的最前面，因此 "
":func:`~kivi.binning.group_categories` 不需要 ``special`` 参数。基准样本中没有的编码仍在分组映射中，其组在 "
":func:`~kivi.woe.woe_table` 中没有对应的行。 ``max_groups`` 、 ``min_share`` 和 ``min_group_share`` "
"只计入其他类别："

msgid ""
"The 25 customers with an unknown job now have a group of their own. A group this small has an "
"unstable WOE, so give a special code its own group only when the business needs it."
msgstr "职业未知的 25 位客户现在单独成组。这么小的组 WOE 并不稳定，因此只在业务需要时才让特殊值单独成组。"

msgid "Missing values"
msgstr "缺失值"

msgid ""
"Missing reference values are ignored when the edges are fitted, and ``pandas.cut`` leaves them "
"missing. The metric functions then count them as a separate group."
msgstr "拟合边界时会忽略基准样本中的缺失值，``pandas.cut`` 也会保留缺失值。指标函数随后将它们计为单独的一组。"

msgid ""
"Missing categories are left out of a grouping in the same way, with their labels, and "
":func:`~kivi.binning.group_categories` keeps them missing, so they form a group of their own in "
":func:`~kivi.woe.woe_table` rather than joining a group of categories."
msgstr ""
"缺失的类别同样连同其标签一起排除在分组映射的拟合之外， :func:`~kivi.binning.group_categories` 让它们保持缺失，因此它们在 "
":func:`~kivi.woe.woe_table` 中单独成组，而不会并入某个类别组。"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.binning.bin_edges` and the supervised methods take ``weights``, for example the "
"inverse sampling rates of a stratified development sample, so that quantile edges and bin counts "
"describe the population rather than the sample. Weighted quantiles use the inverted CDF, so every"
" interior edge is an observed value, while unweighted quantile edges interpolate between "
"observations:"
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.binning.bin_edges` 和监督分箱方法都接受 ``weights`` "
"，例如分层抽样开发样本中各观测抽样比例的倒数，使等频边界和每箱计数反映总体而不是样本。加权分位数采用逆累积分布（inverted "
"CDF），因此每个内部边界都是实际观测到的取值；不加权时，等频边界则在观测值之间线性插值："

msgid ""
"Observations with zero weight are left out; the supervised methods leave out their labels too. "
":doc:`woe_iv` shows the same weights in :func:`~kivi.woe.woe_table`."
msgstr "权重为零的观测会被排除，监督分箱方法同时排除其标签。 :doc:`woe_iv` 展示了在 :func:`~kivi.woe.woe_table` 中使用同样的权重。"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.binning.category_groups` and :func:`~kivi.binning.chimerge_groups` take ``weights`` "
"as well. Shares, counts and the chi-square statistic then use sums of weights, so integer weights"
" give the same grouping as repeated rows. A category whose rows all have zero weight is left out "
"of the grouping, and :func:`~kivi.binning.group_categories` treats it as unseen."
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.binning.category_groups` 和 :func:`~kivi.binning.chimerge_groups` 也接受 ``weights`` "
"。此时占比、计数和卡方统计量都使用权重之和，因此整数权重与重复行得到的分组映射相同。所有行权重都为零的类别不进入分组映射， "
":func:`~kivi.binning.group_categories` 把它视为未见类别。"

msgid "Limits"
msgstr "局限"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.binning.chimerge_groups` merges one pair of groups at a time, so its time grows with"
" the square of the number of categories: a few seconds for 20,000 categories. For a variable with"
" that many labels, such as a postcode, pool the rarest ones with "
":func:`~kivi.binning.category_groups` first, group the pooled labels with ``chimerge_groups``, "
"and combine the two dicts as ``{category: groups[pooled[category]] for category in pooled}``."
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.binning.chimerge_groups` 每次合并一对组，因此所需时间随类别数的平方增长：2 万个类别需要几秒钟。对于标签这么多的变量（例如邮政编码），请先用 "
":func:`~kivi.binning.category_groups` 归并最稀有的类别，再用 ``chimerge_groups`` 对归并后的标签分组，最后用 ``{category: "
"groups[pooled[category]] for category in pooled}`` 组合两个 dict。"

msgid ""
"A grouping is fitted on the categories of the reference sample only. It cannot tell where a new "
"category belongs; :func:`~kivi.binning.group_categories` raises an error for it or sends it to "
"the group named in ``unseen``, and the right group is a business decision."
msgstr ""
"分组映射只根据基准样本中的类别拟合，无法判断新类别应归入哪一组； :func:`~kivi.binning.group_categories` 会为新类别引发错误，或把它归入 "
"``unseen`` 指定的组，而哪一组合适是业务决策。"

msgid "Ties and constant values"
msgstr "重复切点与常量"

msgid "Tied cut points are collapsed. A constant reference produces one bin."
msgstr "重复的切点会被合并。常量基准样本只产生一个箱。"

msgid ""
"The number of bins can therefore be smaller than requested, and :func:`~kivi.binning.bin_edges` "
"then issues a ``UserWarning``. A single value that covers much of the reference, such as a code "
"for \"not applicable\", often causes this. Pass that value in ``special``, as described in :ref"
":`special-values`."
msgstr ""
"因此实际箱数可能少于请求的箱数，此时 :func:`~kivi.binning.bin_edges` 会发出 ``UserWarning`` "
"。某个取值（例如表示“不适用”的编码）在基准样本中占比很大时，常会出现这种情况。请按 :ref:`special-values` 中的方法把该取值传给 ``special`` 。"

msgid "Invalid input"
msgstr "无效输入"

msgid ":func:`~kivi.binning.bin_edges` raises ``ValueError`` when:"
msgstr "以下情况下，:func:`~kivi.binning.bin_edges` 会抛出 ``ValueError``："

msgid "``bins`` is not a positive integer;"
msgstr "``bins`` 不是正整数；"

msgid "``method`` is neither ``\"quantile\"`` nor ``\"uniform\"``;"
msgstr "``method`` 既不是 ``\"quantile\"`` 也不是 ``\"uniform\"``；"

msgid "the reference values are not one-dimensional or not numeric;"
msgstr "基准样本的取值不是一维或不是数值；"

msgid "``special`` is not one-dimensional or contains a missing value;"
msgstr "``special`` 不是一维或含有缺失值；"

msgid ""
"the reference has no observations apart from missing and special values, or contains an infinite "
"value that is not special."
msgstr "除缺失值和特殊值外，基准样本没有观测值，或含有不属于特殊值的无穷值。"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.binning.cut` raises ``ValueError`` for an infinite value that is not a special "
"value, because ``pandas.cut`` would count ``-inf`` as missing and put ``inf`` in the last "
"interval. Pass infinite codes in ``special`` to give each one its own group."
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.binning.cut` 对不属于特殊值的无穷值抛出 ``ValueError`` ，因为 ``pandas.cut`` 会把 ``-inf`` 算作缺失值，而把 "
"``inf`` 放进最后一个区间。把无穷值编码传入 ``special`` ，即可让每个编码单独成组。"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.binning.chimerge_edges`, :func:`~kivi.binning.tree_edges` and "
":func:`~kivi.binning.monotonic_edges` raise ``ValueError`` for the same problems with the values,"
" for an option outside its range, and when:"
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.binning.chimerge_edges`、:func:`~kivi.binning.tree_edges` 和 "
":func:`~kivi.binning.monotonic_edges` 在数值出现上述同样的问题、参数超出取值范围，以及以下情况下会抛出 ``ValueError``："

msgid "``values`` and ``target`` are Series without identical indices, or have different lengths;"
msgstr "``values`` 与 ``target`` 是索引不完全相同的 Series，或者长度不同；"

msgid "``target`` contains a label other than 0 and 1, or a missing label;"
msgstr "``target`` 含有 0 和 1 以外的标签，或含有缺失标签；"

msgid "the observed values, apart from special values, do not cover both classes."
msgstr "除特殊值外，非缺失数值对应的标签没有同时包含两个类别。"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.binning.category_groups` and :func:`~kivi.binning.chimerge_groups` raise "
"``ValueError`` for the same problems with the values and the target and for an option outside its"
" range. :func:`~kivi.binning.category_groups` also raises it when ``rare_label`` is the label of "
"a category that is not rare, and :func:`~kivi.binning.chimerge_groups` when the label of a merged"
" group would be the label of another group, which can only happen when labels contain ``\", \"``."
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.binning.category_groups` 和 :func:`~kivi.binning.chimerge_groups` "
"在取值和目标变量有同样的问题、或某个选项超出范围时引发 ``ValueError`` 。当 ``rare_label`` 是某个非稀有类别的标签时， "
":func:`~kivi.binning.category_groups` 也会引发该错误；当合并后某组的标签会与另一组的标签相同时， "
":func:`~kivi.binning.chimerge_groups` 也会引发该错误，这只在标签含有 ``\", \"`` 时才会发生。"

msgid "Unseen categories"
msgstr "未见类别"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.binning.group_categories` raises ``ValueError`` for a category that its grouping "
"does not map, and names a few of them. Map each new category in the grouping, or pass ``unseen`` "
"with the group that new categories should join, as in :ref:`category-groups`. The string "
"``\"raise\"`` always raises, so it cannot be the label of that group."
msgstr ""
"遇到分组映射中没有的类别时， :func:`~kivi.binning.group_categories` 引发 ``ValueError`` "
"，并列出其中几个类别。请在分组映射中为每个新类别指定组，或像 :ref:`category-groups` 中那样传入 ``unseen`` ，指定新类别应归入的组。字符串 "
"``\"raise\"`` 总是表示引发错误，因此不能作为该组的标签。"

msgid ""
"A PD model is calibrated when its probabilities match the default rates that are later observed. "
"Calibration is a separate question from ranking: a model can order applicants well and still "
"predict default rates that are too low for the whole portfolio. :mod:`kivi.calibration` corrects "
"probabilities for the sampling of the development data, builds a master scale, summarizes its "
"grades and tests them, and maps a score to probabilities with Platt scaling or isotonic "
"regression."
msgstr ""
"如果 PD 模型给出的概率与之后观测到的违约率相符，就称模型是校准的。校准与排序是两个不同的问题：一个模型可以把申请人排得很好，却仍然对整个资产组合预测了过低的违约率。 "
":mod:`kivi.calibration` 针对开发数据的抽样方式校正概率，构建主标尺，汇总其各个等级并进行检验，还能用 Platt 缩放或保序回归把评分映射为概率。"

msgid ""
"Calibration follows :doc:`metrics`, which measures the ranking, and comes before the :doc:`credit"
" strategy <strategy>`, which sets cut-offs on the calibrated PDs. "
":func:`~kivi.calibration.prior_correction` and :func:`~kivi.calibration.corrected_intercept` "
"correct for the sampling; :func:`~kivi.calibration.master_scale`, "
":func:`~kivi.calibration.fit_grade_pd` and :func:`~kivi.calibration.assign_grades` build and "
"apply a master scale; :func:`~kivi.calibration.calibration_table`, "
":func:`~kivi.calibration.binomial_test`, :func:`~kivi.calibration.jeffreys_test`, "
":func:`~kivi.calibration.hosmer_lemeshow` and :func:`~kivi.calibration.herfindahl_index` count "
"and test the grades; and :func:`~kivi.calibration.platt_fit`, "
":func:`~kivi.calibration.platt_predict`, :func:`~kivi.calibration.isotonic_fit` and "
":func:`~kivi.calibration.isotonic_predict` recalibrate a score."
msgstr ""
"校准位于 :doc:`metrics` 之后（后者衡量排序能力），位于 :doc:`信贷策略 <strategy>` 之前（后者在校准后的 PD 上设定截断点）。 "
":func:`~kivi.calibration.prior_correction` 和 :func:`~kivi.calibration.corrected_intercept` "
"校正抽样的影响； :func:`~kivi.calibration.master_scale` 、 :func:`~kivi.calibration.fit_grade_pd` 和 "
":func:`~kivi.calibration.assign_grades` 构建并应用主标尺； :func:`~kivi.calibration.calibration_table` 、 "
":func:`~kivi.calibration.binomial_test` 、 :func:`~kivi.calibration.jeffreys_test` 、 "
":func:`~kivi.calibration.hosmer_lemeshow` 和 :func:`~kivi.calibration.herfindahl_index` 统计并检验各等级； "
":func:`~kivi.calibration.platt_fit` 、 :func:`~kivi.calibration.platt_predict` 、 "
":func:`~kivi.calibration.isotonic_fit` 和 :func:`~kivi.calibration.isotonic_predict` 则重新校准评分。"

msgid "Correcting for oversampling"
msgstr "过采样校正"

msgid ""
"Bad outcomes are often oversampled for development, for example to a sample with as many bads as "
"goods. The model then predicts probabilities for that sample, not for the portfolio. With the "
"development sample's event rate :math:`\\bar y` and the portfolio's event rate :math:`\\tau`, the"
" prior correction of King and Zeng multiplies the odds of every probability by"
msgstr ""
"开发模型时，常常对坏样本做过采样，例如使好坏样本数量相等。这样模型预测的是该样本上的概率，而不是资产组合上的概率。设开发样本的事件率为 :math:`\\bar y` ，资产组合的事件率为 "
":math:`\\tau` ，King 和 Zeng 的先验校正把每个概率的几率乘以"

#, python-format
msgid ""
"A model developed on a sample with 50% bads, for a portfolio with a 2% default rate, turns a "
"probability of 0.5 into 0.02:"
msgstr "如果模型在坏样本占 50% 的样本上开发，而资产组合的违约率为 2%，那么概率 0.5 会变为 0.02："

msgid ""
"The correction keeps the order of the probabilities. For a logistic regression it only shifts the"
" intercept by :math:`\\ln \\omega`, so the coefficients and the points per WOE in "
":doc:`scorecard` stay the same:"
msgstr "校正不改变概率的排序。对逻辑回归而言，它只是把截距平移 :math:`\\ln \\omega` ，因此系数以及 :doc:`scorecard` 中每单位 WOE 对应的分值都保持不变："

msgid "Grades of a master scale"
msgstr "主标尺的等级"

msgid ""
"A master scale divides the PD range into a fixed set of grades, so that ratings from different "
"models share one meaning. Each grade has a PD, and the bounds between the grades decide which "
"grade a predicted PD falls into. The examples below use the PDs of the scorecard from "
":doc:`scorecard` on the development and monitoring samples:"
msgstr ""
"主标尺把 PD 的取值范围划分为一组固定的等级，使不同模型给出的评级具有统一的含义。每个等级有一个 PD，等级之间的界限决定预测 PD 落入哪个等级。下面的示例使用 "
":doc:`scorecard` 中的评分卡在开发样本和监控样本上给出的 PD："

msgid "Building a scale"
msgstr "构建标尺"

msgid ""
"The PDs of a master scale usually grow by a constant factor from grade to grade. "
":func:`~kivi.calibration.master_scale` takes the PD of each grade and adds the bounds of the "
"grades. Here the PDs are a geometric grid of six grades from 2% to 64%, each with twice the PD of"
" the grade before:"
msgstr ""
"主标尺的 PD 通常逐级按固定倍数增长。 :func:`~kivi.calibration.master_scale` 接收每个等级的 PD，并加上各等级的界限。这里的 PD 是从 2% 到 "
"64% 共六个等级的几何网格，每个等级的 PD 是前一个等级的两倍："

#, python-format
msgid ""
"Each bound is the geometric mean of the PDs on either side of it, their midpoint on a logarithmic"
" scale, so a PD goes to the grade whose PD is nearer by ratio. ``boundary=\"arithmetic\"`` takes "
"the arithmetic mean instead, as the 0.2 versions of kivi did. The arithmetic mean lies above the "
"geometric one, so each grade reaches further up than down. Grade A then holds the PDs up to 3% "
"instead of 2.83%. A Series of PDs gives its index as the grade labels:"
msgstr ""
"每个界限是其两侧 PD 的几何平均数，即对数尺度上的中点，因此 PD 归入按比值更接近的那个等级。 ``boundary=\"arithmetic\"`` 改用算术平均数，与 kivi 0.2 "
"版本相同。算术平均数高于几何平均数，因此每个等级向上延伸得比向下更远。这时等级 A 包含直到 3%（而不是 2.83%）的 PD。以 Series 给出的 PD 以其索引作为等级标签："

msgid ""
"With arithmetic bounds, most PDs of a grade lie above its PD, so the observed default rate of a "
"calibrated model tends to exceed the PD of the grade."
msgstr "使用算术界限时，一个等级中的大多数 PD 高于该等级的 PD，因此校准良好的模型的观测违约率往往高于等级的 PD。"

msgid "Assigning the grades"
msgstr "划分等级"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.calibration.assign_grades` gives each PD the grade whose bounds hold it. A PD on a "
"bound goes to the lower grade, as the intervals of ``pandas.cut`` are closed on the right, and a "
"PD of 0 goes to the first grade. The grades are an ordered categorical of the labels, so "
":func:`~kivi.calibration.calibration_table` lists them in the order of the scale when it compares"
" the observed default rate of each grade with its mean predicted PD. Joining the scale adds the "
"PD of each grade:"
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.calibration.assign_grades` 为每个 PD 指定界限包含它的那个等级。恰好落在界限上的 PD 归入较低的等级，因为 ``pandas.cut``"
" 的区间是左开右闭的；PD 为 0 时归入第一个等级。等级是标签的有序分类变量，因此 :func:`~kivi.calibration.calibration_table` "
"比较每个等级的观测违约率与平均预测 PD 时，按标尺的顺序列出各等级。连接（join）标尺即可加入每个等级的 PD："

msgid ""
"The model gives no customer a PD below 2.83%, so grade A is empty and ``calibration_table`` "
"leaves it out."
msgstr "模型没有给任何客户低于 2.83% 的 PD，因此等级 A 为空， ``calibration_table`` 将其略去。"

msgid "Fitting the PDs of the grades"
msgstr "拟合各等级的 PD"

msgid ""
"The PDs of the grades can also come from the default rates observed in them. "
":func:`~kivi.calibration.fit_grade_pd` fits the logarithm of the default rate as a straight line "
"in the grade number, by least squares weighted with the number of observations of each grade, so "
"the fitted PDs again grow by a constant factor. A grade without defaults enters the fit with half"
" a default, and a grade without observations is left out of the fit but still gets a PD. Count "
"the development sample by the grades of the scale:"
msgstr ""
"各等级的 PD 也可以来自其中观测到的违约率。 :func:`~kivi.calibration.fit_grade_pd` "
"把违约率的对数拟合为等级编号的直线，使用以各等级观测数为权重的最小二乘法，因此拟合的 PD 同样逐级按固定倍数增长。没有违约的等级以半次违约参与拟合，没有观测的等级不参与拟合，但仍会得到 "
"PD。按标尺的等级统计开发样本："

msgid ""
"The grades are numbered by their position in the input, so reindex the counts to every grade of "
"the scale before the fit. The empty grade A then keeps its place with a count of 0:"
msgstr "等级按其在输入中的位置编号，因此拟合之前要把计数重新索引到标尺的所有等级。这样空的等级 A 会以计数 0 保留其位置："

msgid ""
"The fitted PDs grow by a factor of 1.81 from grade to grade and follow the default rates of "
"grades B to E closely. Grade F, with a default rate of 64%, lies far above the line: it holds "
"only 81 customers and so weighs little in the fit. The tests below show whether that matters."
msgstr ""
"拟合的 PD 逐级增长为 1.81 倍，与等级 B 到 E 的违约率吻合得很好。等级 F 的违约率为 64%，远高于这条直线：它只有 81 "
"个客户，因此在拟合中权重很小。下面的检验会说明这是否要紧。"

msgid ""
"Observed default rate of each grade of the development sample, the PDs fitted by fit_grade_pd and"
" the geometric grid of the scale, on a logarithmic axis"
msgstr "开发样本各等级的实际违约率、fit_grade_pd 拟合的 PD 以及标尺的几何网格，纵轴为对数刻度"

msgid ""
"Observed default rates of the development sample by grade, the PDs fitted by ``fit_grade_pd`` and"
" the geometric grid of the scale, on a logarithmic axis. Larger points hold more customers; grade"
" F lies above the fitted line."
msgstr "开发样本各等级的实际违约率、 ``fit_grade_pd`` 拟合的 PD 以及标尺的几何网格，纵轴为对数刻度。点越大，客户越多；等级 F 位于拟合线之上。"

msgid "Grades given by their bounds"
msgstr "按界限给出的等级"

msgid ""
"A scale can also be given by its bounds alone, for example by an existing rating system. Cut the "
"PDs at the bounds with ``pandas.cut``, whose intervals are closed on the right like those of "
":func:`~kivi.calibration.assign_grades`; ``include_lowest=True`` keeps a PD of exactly 0 in the "
"first grade. The rest of this page uses these grades:"
msgstr ""
"标尺也可以只由其界限给出，例如来自现有的评级体系。用 ``pandas.cut`` 在这些界限处切分 PD，其区间与 "
":func:`~kivi.calibration.assign_grades` 一样是左开右闭的； ``include_lowest=True`` 让恰好为 0 的 PD "
"留在第一个等级。本页其余部分使用这些等级："

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.calibration.calibration_table` accepts any grouping, such as score bands or deciles "
"of the PD. It counts the groups like :func:`~kivi.woe.woe_table`: categorical groups keep the "
"order of their categories, and grades without observations are left out."
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.calibration.calibration_table` 接受任意分组，例如分数段或 PD 的十分位组。它的计数方式与 "
":func:`~kivi.woe.woe_table` 相同：分类型分组保持类别顺序，没有观测值的等级会被略去。"

msgid "Testing each grade"
msgstr "逐个等级检验"

msgid ""
"Each grade is tested on its own against the hypothesis that its PD is not too low. Both tests are"
" one-sided: a small p-value means that the grade has more defaults than its PD predicts."
msgstr "每个等级单独检验，原假设是其 PD 没有偏低。两种检验都是单侧的：p 值较小，说明该等级的违约数多于其 PD 的预测。"

msgid ""
"The **binomial test** treats the :math:`N` obligors of a grade as independent, each defaulting "
"with probability :math:`p`. Its p-value is the probability of at least the observed :math:`d` "
"defaults, :math:`P(D \\ge d)`."
msgstr ""
"**二项检验** 把一个等级中的 :math:`N` 个债务人视为相互独立，每人以概率 :math:`p` 违约。其 p 值是至少出现观测到的 :math:`d` 次违约的概率，即 "
":math:`P(D \\ge d)` 。"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The **Jeffreys test** starts from the Jeffreys prior :math:`\\mathrm{Beta}(1/2, 1/2)` for the "
"default rate. Its p-value is the posterior probability that the default rate is at most "
":math:`p`, the distribution function of :math:`\\mathrm{Beta}(d + 1/2, N - d + 1/2)` at "
":math:`p`. The European Central Bank asks for this test in the validation of PD models."
msgstr ""
"**Jeffreys 检验** 以 Jeffreys 先验 :math:`\\mathrm{Beta}(1/2, 1/2)` 作为违约率的先验分布。其 p 值是违约率不超过 :math:`p` "
"的后验概率，即 :math:`\\mathrm{Beta}(d + 1/2, N - d + 1/2)` 在 :math:`p` 处的分布函数值。欧洲央行在 PD 模型验证中要求使用这一检验。"

#, python-format
msgid ""
"No grade is rejected at the usual 5% level. To see the tests at work, scale the PDs down as if "
"the portfolio defaulted at 6% rather than at the 11.6% of the development sample. The monitoring "
"sample still defaults at the development rate, so the PDs are now too low:"
msgstr "在常用的 5% 水平下，没有等级被拒绝。为了观察检验的效果，把 PD 按资产组合违约率为 6%（而非开发样本的 11.6%）的情形调低。监控样本的违约率仍与开发样本相当，因此这些 PD 现在偏低："

msgid ""
"Observed default rate against mean predicted PD for each grade, for the original and the scaled-"
"down PDs"
msgstr "原始 PD 与下调后 PD 的各评级实际违约率对平均预测 PD"

msgid ""
"The grades of the original PDs lie close to the diagonal, while those of the scaled-down PDs lie "
"above it: more defaults than predicted. Larger points hold more customers."
msgstr "原始 PD 的各评级贴近对角线，而下调后 PD 的各评级位于对角线上方：违约多于预测。点越大，客户越多。"

msgid ""
"For the same counts, the Jeffreys p-value is always a little lower than the binomial one, so the "
"Jeffreys test rejects slightly more readily. Both tests assume independent defaults; defaults "
"that move together in a downturn make them reject more often than their nominal level."
msgstr "对相同的计数，Jeffreys 检验的 p 值总是略低于二项检验，因此 Jeffreys 检验稍微更容易拒绝。两种检验都假定违约相互独立；经济下行期违约同涨同落，会使它们的拒绝频率高于名义水平。"

msgid ""
"On a master scale, test each grade against its own PD as well, the PD that every customer of the "
"grade is assigned. On the monitoring sample, the fitted scale from above passes for grades B to "
"E, but grade F has more defaults than its PD of 47% predicts:"
msgstr ""
"对于主标尺，还要用每个等级自身的 PD（即该等级的每个客户被赋予的 PD）对其进行检验。在监控样本上，上面拟合的标尺在等级 B 到 E 上通过了检验，但等级 F 的违约数多于其 47% 的 PD"
" 所预测的数量："

msgid ""
"The straight line understates the riskiest grade. Give grade F the PD of its own default rate "
"instead, or merge it into grade E, and test the scale again."
msgstr "这条直线低估了风险最高的等级。可以改用等级 F 自身的违约率作为其 PD，或把它并入等级 E，然后重新检验标尺。"

msgid "Testing all grades at once"
msgstr "一次检验所有等级"

msgid ""
"The Hosmer-Lemeshow test adds up the squared differences between observed and predicted defaults "
"over all :math:`g` groups:"
msgstr "Hosmer-Lemeshow 检验把全部 :math:`g` 个分组中观测违约数与预测违约数之差的平方累加起来："

#, python-brace-format
msgid "H = \\sum_{k=1}^{g} \\frac{(d_k - n_k \\bar p_k)^2}{n_k \\bar p_k (1 - \\bar p_k)}."
msgstr "H = \\sum_{k=1}^{g} \\frac{(d_k - n_k \\bar p_k)^2}{n_k \\bar p_k (1 - \\bar p_k)}."

msgid ""
"On the sample the model was fitted on, form about ten groups of similar size from the sorted PDs "
"and compare :math:`H` with a chi-square distribution with :math:`g - 2` degrees of freedom, the "
"default:"
msgstr "在拟合模型所用的样本上，把排序后的 PD 分成约十个大小相近的组，并将 :math:`H` 与自由度为 :math:`g - 2` 的卡方分布比较，这也是默认设置："

msgid ""
"PDs that were not fitted on the tested sample, such as the grades of the monitoring sample, lose "
"no degrees of freedom, so pass ``ddof=0``:"
msgstr "如果 PD 不是在被检验的样本上拟合的（例如监控样本的各等级），自由度不会减少，因此传入 ``ddof=0`` ："

msgid "Concentration of the grades"
msgstr "等级的集中度"

msgid ""
"A master scale differentiates risk poorly when most obligors fall into a few grades. The "
"Herfindahl-Hirschman index sums the squared shares of the grades: it is :math:`1/k` when all "
":math:`k` grades are equally full and 1 when one grade holds everybody. With ``normalize=True`` "
"it runs from 0 to 1 instead:"
msgstr ""
"如果大多数债务人都落在少数几个等级，主标尺对风险的区分能力就较差。赫芬达尔-赫希曼指数是各等级占比的平方和： :math:`k` 个等级人数相同时为 :math:`1/k` "
"，所有人都在同一等级时为 1。设置 ``normalize=True`` 后，取值范围改为 0 到 1："

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.calibration.calibration_table` leaves out empty grades. To count them, pass the "
"counts of every grade of the scale, for example ``grades.value_counts(sort=False)``."
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.calibration.calibration_table` 会略去空等级。如需把空等级计算在内，请传入标尺上每个等级的计数，例如 "
"``grades.value_counts(sort=False)`` 。"

msgid "Calibrating a score"
msgstr "校准评分"

msgid ""
"A score that ranks applicants well need not be a probability, and the PDs of a model may need "
"recalibrating on recent data. :mod:`kivi.calibration` fits two common mappings from a score to "
"probabilities. Like :func:`~kivi.binning.bin_edges` and :func:`~kivi.binning.cut`, each comes as "
"a pair: the fit returns plain numbers, fitted once on a calibration sample, and the predict "
"function applies them to the scores of any later sample."
msgstr ""
"能把申请人排好序的评分不一定是概率，模型的 PD 也可能需要在近期数据上重新校准。 :mod:`kivi.calibration` 拟合两种常用的从评分到概率的映射。与 "
":func:`~kivi.binning.bin_edges` 和 :func:`~kivi.binning.cut` "
"一样，每种映射都成对出现：拟合函数在校准样本上拟合一次并返回普通的数值，预测函数再把它们应用到之后任何样本的评分上。"

msgid "Platt scaling"
msgstr "Platt 缩放"

msgid "Platt scaling fits a logistic regression of the target on the score :math:`s`:"
msgstr "Platt 缩放以评分 :math:`s` 为自变量，对目标拟合逻辑回归："

#, python-brace-format
msgid "p(s) = \\frac{1}{1 + \\exp(-(a s + b))}."
msgstr "p(s) = \\frac{1}{1 + \\exp(-(a s + b))}."

#, python-format
msgid ""
"For a score that is already the log odds of a model, this is the logistic recalibration of Cox: a"
" slope of 1 and an intercept of 0 mean that the model is calibrated on the sample. Take the PDs "
"that were scaled down to a 6% default rate above. On the development sample, the fit keeps the "
"slope at 1 and raises the intercept by about 0.72, the log of the odds ratio that the correction "
"applied:"
msgstr ""
"如果评分本身就是某个模型的对数几率，这就是 Cox 的逻辑再校准：斜率为 1、截距为 0 说明模型在该样本上是校准的。以上文按 6% 违约率调低的 PD 为例。在开发样本上，拟合得到的斜率仍为 "
"1，截距则提高约 0.72，正是该校正所用优势比的对数："

msgid ""
"Apply the slope and intercept to the low PDs of the monitoring sample. The recalibrated grades "
"have the counts and rates of the grades of the original PDs again:"
msgstr "把斜率和截距应用到监控样本中偏低的 PD 上。再校准后的各等级，其计数和事件率又与原始 PD 的等级相同："

msgid ""
"The score need not be log odds. Platt scaling fits any score, and a score that falls as the risk "
"rises, such as scorecard points, gets a negative slope. When the score separates the classes, the"
" slope that maximizes the likelihood is infinite, and :func:`~kivi.calibration.platt_fit` raises "
":class:`kivi.selection.SeparationError`."
msgstr ""
"评分不必是对数几率。Platt 缩放适用于任何评分；风险越高评分越低的评分（例如评分卡分值）会得到负的斜率。当评分把两类完全分开时，使似然最大的斜率为无穷大， "
":func:`~kivi.calibration.platt_fit` 会引发 :class:`kivi.selection.SeparationError` 。"

msgid "Isotonic regression"
msgstr "保序回归"

msgid ""
"Isotonic regression assumes only that the event rate rises with the score. The pool-adjacent-"
"violators algorithm merges adjacent score bands until their event rates increase, and each band "
"gets its event rate. :func:`~kivi.calibration.isotonic_fit` returns the band edges, from ``-inf``"
" to ``inf`` like those of :func:`~kivi.binning.bin_edges`, and the probability of each band:"
msgstr ""
"保序回归只假定事件率随评分上升。相邻违序合并算法不断合并相邻的评分段，直到各段的事件率递增，每段取其事件率。 :func:`~kivi.calibration.isotonic_fit` "
"返回分段边界（与 :func:`~kivi.binning.bin_edges` 一样从 ``-inf`` 到 ``inf`` ）以及每个分段的概率："

msgid ""
"The algorithm goes through the scores from the lowest to the highest. Each score starts a band of"
" its own, and while a band has a higher event rate than the band after it, the two are pooled. "
"Here the outcome 0 at score 3 follows an event at score 2, so scores 2 and 3 are pooled at 0.5, "
"and the 0 at score 4 pools them again at 1/3. Each edge is the highest score of its band:"
msgstr ""
"算法从最低评分到最高评分依次处理。每个评分先自成一段；只要某段的事件率高于其后一段，就把两段合并。这里评分 3 的结果 0 跟在评分 2 的事件之后，所以评分 2 和 3 合并为 0.5；评分 "
"4 的 0 又使它们再次合并为 1/3。每个边界都是其分段中的最高评分："

msgid ""
"Ten scores and outcomes, the bands after each pooling, and the fitted probabilities with the "
"edges 1, 4, 6 and 9"
msgstr "十个评分及其结果、每次合并后的分段，以及拟合出的概率和边界 1、4、6、9"

msgid ""
"Pool-adjacent-violators on the ten scores. Each row shows the bands once the scores up to the one"
" on its left are processed; the outlined band has just been pooled, and the gray outcomes are not"
" processed yet. The last row holds the fitted probabilities."
msgstr "对十个评分执行相邻违序合并。每一行显示处理完左侧所标评分及之前所有评分后的分段；带边框的分段刚刚合并，灰色的结果尚未处理。最后一行是拟合出的概率。"

msgid "On the development PDs, the fit gives 16 bands:"
msgstr "在开发样本的 PD 上，拟合得到 16 个分段："

msgid ""
"The bands are closed on the right, as in ``pandas.cut``, so they can also serve as grades. "
":func:`~kivi.calibration.isotonic_predict` gives each monitoring PD the probability of its band, "
"and scores outside the development range get the probability of the lowest or the highest band. A"
" score that falls between the observed scores of two bands gets the upper band; with "
"``increasing=False``, as for scorecard points, that is the band with the lower risk:"
msgstr ""
"与 ``pandas.cut`` 一样，各分段为右闭区间，因此也可以用作等级。 :func:`~kivi.calibration.isotonic_predict` 给监控样本的每个 PD "
"赋予其所在分段的概率，超出开发样本范围的评分取最低或最高分段的概率。落在两个分段的观测评分之间的评分取上方的分段；若 ``increasing=False`` "
"（例如评分卡分值），这就是风险较低的分段："

msgid ""
"The step function follows the development sample closely, so some bands are small: the smallest "
"holds four customers of the monitoring sample. Fit isotonic regression on a large sample, and "
"check its bands on another sample as above. A band without events has a probability of 0, so "
"floor the probabilities where a PD of zero is not allowed."
msgstr ""
"阶梯函数紧贴开发样本，因此有些分段很小：最小的分段只有监控样本中的四位客户。请在大样本上拟合保序回归，并像上面那样在另一个样本上检查其分段。没有事件的分段概率为 0，因此在不允许 PD "
"为零的场合，请为概率设定下限。"

msgid ""
"A development sample that keeps every bad but only some of the goods can be weighted back to the "
"portfolio, with each observation weighted by the inverse of its sampling rate. "
":func:`~kivi.calibration.calibration_table`, :func:`~kivi.calibration.platt_fit` and "
":func:`~kivi.calibration.isotonic_fit` take such weights in ``weights``: counts become sums of "
"weights, and integer weights give the same result as repeating rows. The binomial, Jeffreys and "
"Hosmer-Lemeshow tests need whole numbers of observations and events, so run them on an unweighted"
" table."
msgstr ""
"保留全部坏样本、只保留部分好样本的开发样本，可以用每个观测抽样比例的倒数作为权重，加权还原到资产组合。 :func:`~kivi.calibration.calibration_table` 、"
" :func:`~kivi.calibration.platt_fit` 和 :func:`~kivi.calibration.isotonic_fit` 通过 ``weights`` "
"接受这样的权重：计数变为权重之和，整数权重与重复相应行的结果相同。二项检验、Jeffreys 检验和 Hosmer-Lemeshow "
"检验需要整数的观测数和事件数，因此请在不加权的表上进行这些检验。"

msgid ""
":mod:`kivi.datasets` provides three kinds of example data: real bank marketing data with one row "
"per customer and a binary target, a synthetic panel of loans with one row per loan and month, and"
" synthetic loan applications with one row per applicant and an approval decision. "
":func:`~kivi.datasets.load_bank`, :func:`~kivi.datasets.make_loan_panel` and "
":func:`~kivi.datasets.make_applications` return them."
msgstr ""
":mod:`kivi.datasets` "
"提供三类示例数据：真实的银行营销数据，每位客户一行，带二分类目标；合成的贷款面板数据，每笔贷款每个月一行；以及合成的贷款申请数据，每个申请人一行，带审批决策。 "
":func:`~kivi.datasets.load_bank` 、 :func:`~kivi.datasets.make_loan_panel` 和 "
":func:`~kivi.datasets.make_applications` 分别返回这三类数据。"

msgid "Bank marketing data"
msgstr "银行营销数据"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.datasets.load_bank` loads 4,521 customers from the Bank Marketing data set. It has "
"sixteen features and an integer ``target``: 1 means that the customer subscribed to a term "
"deposit."
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.datasets.load_bank` 读取 Bank Marketing 数据集中的 4,521 位客户。数据包含 16 个特征和整数标签 ``target`` ：1"
" 表示客户认购了定期存款。"

msgid ""
"The examples in this documentation split the rows by position only to demonstrate two samples; "
"the split is not chronological."
msgstr "本文档中的示例按行的位置切分出两个样本，仅用于演示；这一切分不代表时间顺序。"

msgid "Synthetic loan panel"
msgstr "合成贷款面板"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.datasets.make_loan_panel` simulates the monthly history of a portfolio of instalment"
" loans, for the vintage and roll-rate analysis in :doc:`vintage`. The data is generated, not "
"taken from a real portfolio, and the same ``rng`` seed always gives the same panel:"
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.datasets.make_loan_panel` 模拟一个分期贷款资产组合的月度历史，供 :doc:`vintage` 中的 Vintage "
"分析和滚动率分析使用。数据是生成的，并非取自真实的资产组合；同一个 ``rng`` 种子总是给出同样的面板："

msgid ""
"The loans are spread at random over ``n_months`` origination months from January 2024, and each "
"loan has one row for every month end it is on book, up to the month after the last origination "
"month. The columns are:"
msgstr "贷款随机分布在从 2024 年 1 月开始的 ``n_months`` 个放款月中；每笔贷款在账上的每个月末都有一行，直到最后一个放款月的下一个月。各列如下："

msgid "Column"
msgstr "列"

msgid "``loan_id``"
msgstr "``loan_id``"

msgid "Identifier of the loan, increasing with the origination month."
msgstr "贷款标识，随放款月份递增。"

msgid "Origination month, a monthly ``pandas.Period``."
msgstr "放款月份，为月度 ``pandas.Period`` 。"

msgid "``month``"
msgstr "``month``"

msgid "Month of the observation, ``cohort + month_on_book``."
msgstr "观测所在月份，即 ``cohort + month_on_book`` 。"

msgid "``month_on_book``"
msgstr "``month_on_book``"

msgid "Months since origination, from 1."
msgstr "放款后经过的月数（账龄），从 1 开始。"

msgid "``term``"
msgstr "``term``"

msgid "Number of monthly instalments: 12, 24 or 36."
msgstr "月供期数：12、24 或 36。"

msgid "``amount``"
msgstr "``amount``"

msgid "Amount lent."
msgstr "放款金额。"

msgid "``balance``"
msgstr "``balance``"

msgid "Outstanding principal at the end of the month."
msgstr "月末的剩余本金。"

msgid "``status``"
msgstr "``status``"

msgid ""
"Days past due at the end of the month, an ordered categorical: ``current``, ``1-29``, ``30-59``, "
"``60-89`` and ``90+``."
msgstr "月末的逾期天数，为有序分类变量： ``current`` 、 ``1-29`` 、 ``30-59`` 、 ``60-89`` 和 ``90+`` 。"

msgid "How the panel is simulated"
msgstr "面板的模拟方式"

#, python-format
msgid ""
"Each loan is repaid in equal monthly instalments at 1% interest a month. Its status counts the "
"months since its oldest unpaid instalment fell due: one is ``1-29``, two ``30-59``, three "
"``60-89`` and four or more ``90+``. Within the term this is the number of instalments past due. "
"Every month:"
msgstr ""
"每笔贷款按月等额本息还款，月利率为 1%。其状态记录自最早一期未还期款到期以来的月数：一个月为 ``1-29`` ，两个月为 ``30-59`` ，三个月为 ``60-89`` ，四个月及以上为"
" ``90+`` 。在期限内，这就是逾期未还的期数。每个月："

msgid ""
"a current loan misses its instalment with a probability that peaks at its sixth month on book and"
" then declines, scaled by a risk factor of the loan and one of its cohort;"
msgstr "正常贷款漏缴当期期款的概率在账龄第六个月达到峰值，之后下降，并乘以该贷款和所在批次各自的风险系数；"

msgid ""
"a delinquent loan pays all its arrears and becomes current, pays one instalment and keeps its "
"status, or pays nothing and rolls to the next bucket, also after its term, and the later the "
"bucket, the less likely it cures and the more likely it rolls;"
msgstr "逾期贷款要么还清全部欠款、回到正常，要么只还一期、保持原状态，要么完全不还、滚动到下一个档位（期限结束后也是如此）；档位越靠后，回到正常的可能越小，滚动的可能越大；"

msgid "a ``90+`` loan pays nothing more, so its status and balance stay the same."
msgstr "``90+`` 的贷款不再还款，因此其状态和余额保持不变。"

msgid ""
"A loan leaves the panel in the month it pays its last instalment, which can come after its term "
"if it was behind. Loans are not charged off or prepaid."
msgstr "贷款在还清最后一期的当月离开面板；如果曾经逾期，这可能发生在期限之后。贷款不会被核销，也不会提前还款。"

msgid "Synthetic loan applications"
msgstr "合成贷款申请"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.datasets.make_applications` simulates loan applications that an incumbent scorecard "
"and two policy rules decided, for the reject inference in :doc:`reject_inference`. Every "
"applicant has a true default flag, also the rejected ones, so that the inferred outcomes can be "
"compared with the real ones. The same ``rng`` seed always gives the same applications:"
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.datasets.make_applications` 模拟由现行评分卡和两条政策规则决定审批的贷款申请，供 :doc:`reject_inference` "
"中的拒绝推断使用。每个申请人（包括被拒绝的申请人）都有真实的违约标记，以便把推断的结果与真实结果比较。同一个 ``rng`` 种子总是给出同样的申请数据："

msgid "``age``"
msgstr "``age``"

msgid "Age in years, from 18 to 75."
msgstr "年龄（岁），从 18 到 75。"

msgid "``income``"
msgstr "``income``"

msgid "Monthly income, rounded to tens."
msgstr "月收入，取整到十位。"

msgid "``debt_to_income``"
msgstr "``debt_to_income``"

msgid "Monthly debt payments over income, rounded to hundredths."
msgstr "每月还债额与收入之比，保留两位小数。"

msgid "``inquiries``"
msgstr "``inquiries``"

msgid "Number of credit inquiries in the last six months."
msgstr "近六个月的征信查询次数。"

msgid "``housing``"
msgstr "``housing``"

msgid "A categorical: ``own``, ``mortgage`` or ``rent``."
msgstr "分类变量： ``own`` 、 ``mortgage`` 或 ``rent`` 。"

msgid "``employment``"
msgstr "``employment``"

msgid "A categorical: ``permanent``, ``temporary`` or ``self_employed``."
msgstr "分类变量： ``permanent`` 、 ``temporary`` 或 ``self_employed`` 。"

msgid "``incumbent_pd``"
msgstr "``incumbent_pd``"

msgid "PD of the scorecard that decided the application, rounded to four decimals."
msgstr "决定该申请的评分卡给出的 PD，保留四位小数。"

msgid "``policy_decline``"
msgstr "``policy_decline``"

msgid ""
"True if a policy rule declined the application, whatever its PD: a debt-to-income ratio above 0.6"
" or an age below 21."
msgstr "若某条政策规则拒绝了该申请（无论其 PD 如何）则为 True，规则为负债收入比高于 0.6 或年龄低于 21 岁。"

msgid "``approved``"
msgstr "``approved``"

msgid "True if ``incumbent_pd`` is below 0.15 and no policy rule declined the application."
msgstr "若 ``incumbent_pd`` 低于 0.15 且没有政策规则拒绝该申请，则为 True。"

msgid "``target``"
msgstr "``target``"

msgid "1 if the applicant defaults, else 0."
msgstr "申请人违约为 1，否则为 0。"

msgid "How the applications are simulated"
msgstr "申请数据的模拟方式"

msgid ""
"The incumbent scorecard weighs the features differently and ignores ``housing``. Like an "
"underwriter with a credit bureau report, it also sees part of the hidden risk factor. Rejected "
"applicants are therefore riskier than approved applicants with the same features, so a model "
"fitted on the approved applicants alone underestimates how often the rejected ones default, as "
":doc:`reject_inference` shows. Overall, the rejected applicants default three times as often:"
msgstr ""
"现行评分卡对各特征的权重不同，并且不使用 ``housing`` "
"。它还像手握征信报告的审批人员一样，能看到隐藏风险因子的一部分。因此，在特征相同时，拒绝申请人比获批申请人风险更高，只用获批申请人拟合的模型会低估拒绝申请人的违约频率，见 "
":doc:`reject_inference` 。总体而言，拒绝申请人的违约频率是获批申请人的三倍："

msgid ""
"In practice, the outcome is known only for approved applicants. ``target`` is given for the "
"rejected applicants only to evaluate reject inference; fitting a model on it would make reject "
"inference pointless."
msgstr "实际中只有获批申请人的结果是已知的。给出拒绝申请人的 ``target`` 只是为了评估拒绝推断；用它拟合模型会使拒绝推断失去意义。"

msgid "Dataset and attribution"
msgstr "示例数据和署名"

msgid ""
"Bank Marketing by S. Moro, P. Rita and P. Cortez (2014) is distributed under CC BY 4.0. The "
"bundled CSV was converted from the legacy workbook. The loader encodes subscription as 1 and non-"
"subscription as 0. See the `dataset record <https://doi.org/10.24432/C5K306>`_ and `license "
"<https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/>`_. The loan panel and the applications are "
"synthetic and have no source to attribute."
msgstr ""
"Bank Marketing 由 S. Moro、P. Rita 和 P. Cortez 于 2014 年发布，按 CC BY 4.0 授权。随包 CSV "
"由旧版工作簿转换而来。加载时将认购存款编码为 1，未认购编码为 0。详见 `数据集说明 <https://doi.org/10.24432/C5K306>`_ 和 `许可证 "
"<https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/>`_。贷款面板和申请数据是合成数据，没有需要注明的来源。"

msgid ""
"The user guide follows the steps of a credit risk model in the order of a project: profile and "
"bin the candidate variables, encode them with WOE, select the variables and fit the model, infer "
"the outcomes of rejected applicants, scale the model to a scorecard, evaluate and calibrate it, "
"set the cut-offs, save the binning for production, monitor the model period by period, follow the"
" loans that it approves, and measure their expected credit loss under IFRS 9. "
":doc:`risk_workflow` runs the steps from the profile to the stability report on the bundled data,"
" leaving out reject inference."
msgstr ""
"用户指南按项目的顺序介绍信用风险模型的各个步骤：分析候选变量并分箱，用 WOE "
"编码，筛选变量并拟合模型，推断被拒申请人的结果，把模型刻度为评分卡，评估并校准模型，设定截断点，保存分箱供生产环境使用，逐期监控模型，跟踪模型批准的贷款，并计量其 IFRS 9 预期信用损失。 "
":doc:`risk_workflow` 在随包数据上完成了从变量概况到稳定性报告的各个步骤，其中不包括拒绝推断。"

msgid ""
"kivi keeps fitting and applying apart. Bin edges, category groupings, WOE tables, master scales "
"and cut-offs are fitted on the development sample and then applied unchanged to every later "
"sample, so that counts and rates stay comparable. The tables take the groups as they are, so "
"category labels can be passed directly."
msgstr "kivi 把拟合与应用分开。分箱边界、类别分组、WOE 表、主标尺和截断点都在开发样本上拟合，然后原样用于之后的每个样本，使计数和比率保持可比。各表格按原样接收分组，因此可以直接传入类别标签。"

msgid ""
"Every function follows the rules of :doc:`/api/conventions`, such as the order of its arguments "
"and the meaning of ``weights``, and the :doc:`/api/glossary` defines the terms that these guides "
"use."
msgstr "每个函数都遵守 :doc:`/api/conventions` 中的规则，例如参数顺序和 ``weights`` 的含义； :doc:`/api/glossary` 给出这些指南所用术语的定义。"

msgid "Risk modeling workflow"
msgstr "风控建模流程"

msgid ""
"An end-to-end example: profile and screen the variables, bin and encode the shortlist, fit and "
"scale a scorecard, evaluate and calibrate it, set a cut-off and report stability."
msgstr "端到端示例：分析并筛选变量，对入选变量分箱并编码，拟合评分卡并刻度为分值，评估和校准模型，设定截断点，并输出稳定性报告。"

msgid "One row per candidate: missing values, distribution, event rates and the IV of a quick binning."
msgstr "每个候选变量一行：缺失值、分布、事件率以及快速分箱的 IV。"

msgid ""
"Quantile, uniform and custom edges, special values, merging fine bins, supervised binning, "
"grouping the categories of categorical variables, and missing values."
msgstr "等频、等距与自定义边界，特殊值，合并细分箱，有监督分箱，类别变量的类别分组，以及缺失值。"

msgid ""
"Definitions, the smoothing rule for empty cells, how to read the result and how to encode new "
"data."
msgstr "定义、空单元格的平滑规则、结果的解读方法以及如何对新数据编码。"

msgid ""
"Correlation filtering, variance inflation factors, logistic regression and stepwise selection "
"with positive coefficients."
msgstr "相关性过滤、方差膨胀因子、逻辑回归，以及保证系数为正的逐步回归。"

msgid ""
"Fuzzy augmentation, parceling and reweighting, to refit a model developed on approved applicants "
"on all applicants."
msgstr "模糊扩充、打包法和重新加权，把基于获批申请人开发的模型在全部申请人上重新拟合。"

msgid "PDO scaling, points per group, scores for new data and reason codes."
msgstr "PDO 刻度、每组分值、为新数据打分以及原因码。"

msgid ""
"AUC, Gini, KS, gains and ROC tables, with the score oriented so that higher means riskier, and "
"the confidence interval and DeLong test of an AUC."
msgstr "AUC、Gini、KS、增益表和 ROC 表，分数方向约定为越高风险越大，并给出 AUC 的置信区间和 DeLong 检验。"

msgid ""
"Prior correction, master scales built from PDs or fitted to default rates, tests of each grade's "
"PD, and Platt and isotonic recalibration."
msgstr "先验校正、由 PD 构建或按违约率拟合的主标尺、对每个评级 PD 的统计检验，以及 Platt 与保序回归重新校准。"

msgid "Approval and bad rates of each cut-off, swap sets between two scores, and expected loss by grade."
msgstr "每个截断点的通过率与坏账率、两个评分之间的交换集，以及按等级的预期损失。"

msgid ""
"Bin a whole data frame at once, including category groupings, and save the edges and WOE tables "
"as versioned JSON for production scoring."
msgstr "一次对整个数据框分箱（包括类别分组），并把边界和 WOE 表保存为带版本号的 JSON，供生产环境打分。"

msgid ""
"Compare the distribution of two samples, including categories seen in only one of them, and "
"measure each variable's effect on the score with CSI."
msgstr "比较两个样本的分布，包括只在其中一个样本出现的类别，并用 CSI 衡量每个变量对分数的影响。"

msgid ""
"A per-period report of the population, the known outcomes, AUC, Gini, KS and PSI of a score, and "
"the PSI of every variable by period."
msgstr "按期的报告：评分的样本量、已知结果、AUC、Gini、KS 和 PSI，以及每个变量在每期的 PSI。"

msgid ""
"Cumulative bad rates by cohort and month on book, roll rates and transition matrices between "
"delinquency buckets."
msgstr "按批次和账龄统计的累计坏账率，以及逾期档位之间的滚动率和转移矩阵。"

msgid ""
"PD term structures from vintage curves and transition matrices, 12-month and lifetime expected "
"credit loss, and IFRS 9 stages."
msgstr "由 vintage 曲线和转移矩阵得到 PD 期限结构，计算 12 个月与整个存续期预期信用损失，并划分 IFRS 9 阶段。"

msgid ""
"The bundled bank marketing data, a synthetic loan panel for portfolio analysis and synthetic "
"applications for reject inference."
msgstr "随包的银行营销数据、用于资产组合分析的合成贷款面板数据，以及用于拒绝推断的合成申请数据。"

msgid ""
"IFRS 9 requires a lender to hold a loss allowance for the credit losses that it expects on its "
"loans. While the credit risk of a loan has not increased significantly since it was granted, the "
"allowance covers the losses from defaults in the next 12 months; once it has, and once the loan "
"is in default, it covers the losses over the remaining life of the loan. Both need the "
"probability of a default in each period after the reporting date, a PD term structure, rather "
"than the single 12-month PD of a scorecard."
msgstr ""
"IFRS 9 要求贷款人为其预期的贷款信用损失计提损失准备。只要贷款的信用风险自发放以来没有显著增加，损失准备覆盖未来 12 "
"个月内违约造成的损失；一旦信用风险显著增加，以及贷款已经违约，损失准备覆盖贷款剩余存续期内的损失。两者都需要报告日之后每一期的违约概率，即 PD 期限结构，而不只是评分卡给出的一个 12 个月 "
"PD。"

msgid ""
"The term structures come from the vintage curves and the transition matrices of :doc:`vintage`, "
"and the loss allowance is the last step of this user guide. :func:`~kivi.lifetime.convert_pd` "
"converts a term structure between cumulative, marginal and conditional PDs, "
":func:`~kivi.lifetime.transition_pd` projects one from a transition matrix, "
":func:`~kivi.lifetime.expected_credit_loss` gives the 12-month and the lifetime expected credit "
"loss of each account, :func:`~kivi.lifetime.significant_increase` and "
":func:`~kivi.lifetime.assign_stages` allocate the accounts to the three stages, and "
":func:`~kivi.lifetime.stage_table` sums the loss allowance of each stage."
msgstr ""
"期限结构来自 :doc:`vintage` 中的 vintage 曲线和转移矩阵，损失准备是本用户指南的最后一步。 :func:`~kivi.lifetime.convert_pd` "
"在累计、边际和条件 PD 之间转换期限结构， :func:`~kivi.lifetime.transition_pd` 由转移矩阵推算期限结构， "
":func:`~kivi.lifetime.expected_credit_loss` 给出每个账户的 12 个月和整个存续期预期信用损失， "
":func:`~kivi.lifetime.significant_increase` 和 :func:`~kivi.lifetime.assign_stages` 把账户划分到三个阶段， "
":func:`~kivi.lifetime.stage_table` 汇总每个阶段的损失准备。"

msgid "Definitions"
msgstr "定义"

msgid ""
"A PD term structure describes the risk of each period after a starting point, such as the "
"origination of a loan or the reporting date. For period :math:`k`, the *cumulative PD* "
":math:`C_k` is the probability of a default in periods 1 to :math:`k`, the *marginal PD* "
":math:`m_k` the probability of a default in period :math:`k`, and the *conditional PD* "
":math:`h_k`, also called the hazard rate, the probability of a default in period :math:`k` given "
"that there was none before. With :math:`C_0 = 0`, each of them gives the others:"
msgstr ""
"PD 期限结构描述从某个起点（例如贷款发放日或报告日）开始每一期的风险。对第 :math:`k` 期， *累计 PD* :math:`C_k` 是在第 1 期到第 :math:`k` "
"期之间违约的概率， *边际 PD* :math:`m_k` 是在第 :math:`k` 期违约的概率， *条件 PD* :math:`h_k` （又称风险率，hazard "
"rate）是此前未违约的前提下在第 :math:`k` 期违约的概率。令 :math:`C_0 = 0` ，三者可以相互推出："

msgid ""
"m_k = C_k - C_{k-1}, \\qquad\n"
"h_k = \\frac{m_k}{1 - C_{k-1}}, \\qquad\n"
"C_k = \\sum_{j \\le k} m_j = 1 - \\prod_{j \\le k} (1 - h_j)."
msgstr ""
"m_k = C_k - C_{k-1}, \\qquad\n"
"h_k = \\frac{m_k}{1 - C_{k-1}}, \\qquad\n"
"C_k = \\sum_{j \\le k} m_j = 1 - \\prod_{j \\le k} (1 - h_j)."

msgid ""
"The expected credit loss (ECL) of an account adds up, over the periods :math:`t = 1, \\ldots, H` "
"after the reporting date, the marginal PD of each period times the loss given default (LGD) and "
"the exposure at default (EAD) in that period, discounted to the reporting date at the effective "
"interest rate :math:`r` per period:"
msgstr ""
"账户的预期信用损失（ECL）对报告日之后的各期 :math:`t = 1, \\ldots, H` 求和：每一期的边际 PD "
"乘以该期的违约损失率（LGD）和违约风险敞口（EAD），再按每期实际利率 :math:`r` 折现到报告日："

#, python-brace-format
msgid "\\mathrm{ECL} = \\sum_{t=1}^{H} m_t \\, \\mathrm{LGD}_t \\, \\mathrm{EAD}_t \\, (1 + r)^{-t}."
msgstr "\\mathrm{ECL} = \\sum_{t=1}^{H} m_t \\, \\mathrm{LGD}_t \\, \\mathrm{EAD}_t \\, (1 + r)^{-t}."

msgid ""
"The 12-month ECL adds up the periods of the next 12 months, and the lifetime ECL every period up "
"to maturity. :func:`~kivi.lifetime.expected_credit_loss` uses these conventions:"
msgstr ""
"12 个月 ECL 对未来 12 个月内的各期求和，整个存续期 ECL 对直到到期的每一期求和。 :func:`~kivi.lifetime.expected_credit_loss` "
"采用以下约定："

msgid ""
"Period 1 starts at the reporting date and ends one period later, so with monthly periods the "
"12-month ECL has ``horizon=12``."
msgstr "第 1 期从报告日开始，一期后结束，因此按月分期时，12 个月 ECL 对应 ``horizon=12`` 。"

msgid ""
"The marginal PDs are seen from the reporting date. They are not conditional on survival, and they"
" add up to the cumulative PD."
msgstr "边际 PD 是在报告日看来的概率。它们不以存续为条件，之和等于累计 PD。"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"A default in period :math:`t` occurs at its end, so its loss is discounted over :math:`t` "
"periods. The rate is the effective interest rate per period, such as :math:`(1 + "
"r_\\text{annual})^{1/12} - 1` for monthly periods."
msgstr ""
"第 :math:`t` 期的违约发生在该期期末，因此其损失折现 :math:`t` 期。利率是每期的实际利率，例如按月分期时为 :math:`(1 + "
"r_\\text{annual})^{1/12} - 1` 。"

msgid "IFRS 9 allocates each exposure to one of three stages, which decide its horizon:"
msgstr "IFRS 9 把每笔敞口划入三个阶段之一，阶段决定其求和期限："

msgid "Exposures"
msgstr "敞口"

msgid "1"
msgstr "1"

msgid "Credit risk not increased significantly since initial recognition"
msgstr "自初始确认以来信用风险未显著增加"

msgid "12-month ECL"
msgstr "12 个月 ECL"

msgid "2"
msgstr "2"

msgid "Credit risk increased significantly since initial recognition"
msgstr "自初始确认以来信用风险已显著增加"

msgid "Lifetime ECL"
msgstr "整个存续期 ECL"

msgid "3"
msgstr "3"

msgid ""
"IFRS 9 defines credit-impaired exposures by events that hurt their expected cash flows, such as a"
" default or the significant financial difficulty of the borrower. In practice, lenders usually "
"align them with their definition of default."
msgstr "IFRS 9 按对预计现金流量产生不利影响的事件来界定已发生信用减值的敞口，例如违约或借款人发生重大财务困难。实务中，贷款人通常使其与自身的违约定义保持一致。"

msgid "A worked example"
msgstr "计算示例"

msgid ""
"A loan defaults in its first year with probability 0.02, by the end of its second year with "
"probability 0.05 and by the end of its third year with probability 0.08:"
msgstr "一笔贷款在第一年内违约的概率为 0.02，到第二年末为 0.05，到第三年末为 0.08："

#, python-format
msgid ""
"The marginal PD of the second year is 0.05 − 0.02 = 0.03. Of the 98% of loans without a default "
"in the first year, 0.03 / 0.98 = 3.06% default in the second, the conditional PD."
msgstr "第二年的边际 PD 为 0.05 − 0.02 = 0.03。在第一年未违约的 98% 贷款中，有 0.03 / 0.98 = 3.06% 在第二年违约，这就是条件 PD。"

msgid ""
"With an LGD of 50%, an exposure that amortizes from 1,000 to 700 and 400, and an effective "
"interest rate of 5% a year, the expected credit losses of the loan are:"
msgstr "设 LGD 为 50%，敞口从 1,000 摊还到 700 和 400，实际利率为每年 5%，这笔贷款的预期信用损失为："

msgid ""
"The first year contributes 0.02 × 0.5 × 1,000 / 1.05 = 9.52, which is the 12-month ECL. The "
"second contributes 0.03 × 0.5 × 700 / 1.05² = 9.52 and the third 0.03 × 0.5 × 400 / 1.05³ = 5.18,"
" so the lifetime ECL is 24.23. Each row of the PDs is one account, so a portfolio is computed in "
"one call."
msgstr ""
"第一年贡献 0.02 × 0.5 × 1,000 / 1.05 = 9.52，即 12 个月 ECL。第二年贡献 0.03 × 0.5 × 700 / 1.05² = 9.52，第三年贡献 "
"0.03 × 0.5 × 400 / 1.05³ = 5.18，因此整个存续期 ECL 为 24.23。PD 的每一行是一个账户，因此一次调用就能算出整个资产组合。"

msgid ""
"The three years of the worked example with their cumulative, marginal and conditional PDs, LGD, "
"EAD, discount factors and discounted losses"
msgstr "计算示例的三年，以及各年的累计、边际和条件 PD、LGD、EAD、折现因子和折现后的损失"

msgid ""
"The worked example year by year. ``convert_pd`` gives the marginal and conditional PDs, and "
"``expected_credit_loss`` adds up the discounted losses: the first year with ``horizon=1``, all "
"three by default."
msgstr ""
"逐年展开的计算示例。 ``convert_pd`` 给出边际和条件 PD， ``expected_credit_loss`` 把折现后的损失加总： ``horizon=1`` "
"时只加第一年，默认加总全部三年。"

msgid "Term structures from vintage curves"
msgstr "由 vintage 曲线得到期限结构"

msgid ""
"A vintage table holds the cumulative bad rate of each cohort by month on book: a cumulative PD "
"term structure from origination. The examples use the synthetic loan panel of "
":func:`~kivi.datasets.make_loan_panel`, which :doc:`datasets` describes, and the 90+ bad "
"definition of :doc:`vintage`. The conditional PDs of each cohort follow from "
":func:`~kivi.vintage.vintage_table` and :func:`~kivi.lifetime.convert_pd`:"
msgstr ""
"Vintage 表给出每个批次按账龄的累计坏账率，也就是从放款起的累计 PD 期限结构。示例使用 :func:`~kivi.datasets.make_loan_panel` "
"生成的合成贷款面板（见 :doc:`datasets` ），以及 :doc:`vintage` 中 90+ 的坏定义。每个批次的条件 PD 可由 "
":func:`~kivi.vintage.vintage_table` 和 :func:`~kivi.lifetime.convert_pd` 得到："

msgid ""
"Each entry is the share of a cohort's loans that went bad at that month on book among the loans "
"that had not gone bad before. The months on book that a cohort has not reached stay missing. A "
"cohort has about 200 loans, so a single bad loan moves its rate by half a percentage point, and "
"many entries are 0."
msgstr "每个值是批次中此前尚未变坏的贷款在该账龄变坏的比例。批次尚未达到的账龄保持缺失。每个批次约有 200 笔贷款，一笔坏贷款就会使比率变动半个百分点，因此很多值为 0。"

msgid ""
"Conditional PDs at the same month on book are comparable across cohorts, which makes them the "
"quantity to pool. The mean of each column averages the cohorts that reached that month on book "
"and skips the others, because ``mean`` ignores missing values. The early months rest on many "
"cohorts and the late ones on few:"
msgstr "同一账龄的条件 PD 在不同批次之间可比，因此适合合并。每一列的均值对达到该账龄的批次取平均并跳过其他批次，因为 ``mean`` 会忽略缺失值。较早的账龄基于很多批次，较晚的账龄只基于少数批次："

msgid ""
"Cumulative 90+ bad rate of every cohort by month on book as thin lines, and the cumulative PD of "
"the pooled conditional PDs as a bold line"
msgstr "各批次按账龄的累计 90+ 坏账率（细线），以及由合并后的条件 PD 得到的累计 PD（粗线）"

msgid ""
"Cumulative 90+ bad rate of each cohort by month on book (thin) and the curve of the pooled "
"conditional PDs (bold). The young cohorts stop after a few months on book, while the pooled curve"
" runs to the last month on book of the panel."
msgstr "各批次按账龄的累计 90+ 坏账率（细线），以及合并后的条件 PD 所得的曲线（粗线）。较新的批次只观测到前几个月的账龄，合并曲线则一直延伸到面板中的最后一个账龄。"

msgid ""
"The pooled curve reaches the oldest month on book of the panel for every cohort. From month on "
"book 12 on, it lies below the curve of the oldest cohort, 2024-01, which was riskier than the "
"average one, and beyond month on book 18 it rests on seven cohorts or fewer."
msgstr "合并后的曲线让每个批次都延伸到面板中最大的账龄。从账龄 12 起，它低于最早的批次 2024-01 的曲线，因为该批次的风险高于平均水平；账龄 18 之后，它只基于七个或更少的批次。"

msgid "From the reporting date"
msgstr "从报告日开始"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.lifetime.expected_credit_loss` takes PDs seen from the reporting date, for a loan "
"that has not defaulted by then. For a loan of a given age, convert the conditional PDs of the "
"months on book after that age to marginal PDs. A loan at month on book 6 has these marginal PDs "
"for the next 12 months:"
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.lifetime.expected_credit_loss` 需要在报告日看来的 PD，适用于截至报告日未违约的贷款。对于某一账龄的贷款，请把该账龄之后各账龄的条件 "
"PD 转换为边际 PD。账龄为 6 的贷款，未来 12 个月的边际 PD 为："

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Their sum, 6.23%, is the probability that a loan without a default by month on book 6 defaults by"
" month on book 18, :math:`(C_{18} - C_6) / (1 - C_6)` on the pooled curve. A vintage table counts"
" every loan of a cohort, also the loans repaid early, which can no longer go bad. These PDs "
"therefore already allow for early repayment, and they go with the balance of a loan that is still"
" on book, such as its contractual schedule."
msgstr ""
"其和 6.23% 是截至账龄 6 未违约的贷款在账龄 18 之前违约的概率，即合并曲线上的 :math:`(C_{18} - C_6) / (1 - C_6)` 。Vintage "
"表计入批次中的每一笔贷款，也包括提前还清、不会再变坏的贷款。因此这些 PD 已经考虑了提前还款，应与仍在账上的贷款的余额（例如合同还款计划）搭配使用。"

msgid "Term structures from transition matrices"
msgstr "由转移矩阵得到期限结构"

msgid ""
"A transition matrix gives the probabilities of moving from each delinquency bucket or rating "
"grade to each other one in a period, as in :doc:`vintage`. If the movements follow a time-"
"homogeneous Markov chain, the powers of the matrix give a term structure for each starting state."
" :func:`~kivi.lifetime.transition_pd` makes the default state absorbing, so that loans that cure "
"from default still count as defaulted, and returns the cumulative PD of each state at each "
"horizon:"
msgstr ""
"转移矩阵给出一期内从每个逾期档位或评级迁移到其他各档位或评级的概率，见 :doc:`vintage` 。如果迁移服从时齐马尔可夫链，矩阵的各次幂就给出每个起始状态的期限结构。 "
":func:`~kivi.lifetime.transition_pd` 把违约状态设为吸收态，使从违约回到正常的贷款仍算作违约，并返回每个状态在每个期限的累计 PD："

msgid ""
"The default state is the last one, here ``90+``, unless ``default_state`` names another. A loan "
"falls at most one bucket further behind per month, so a current loan needs four months to reach "
"90+ and its PD is 0 for three months. The PD of every state rises with the horizon, and the worse"
" the bucket, the higher it starts: six in ten loans at 30 to 59 days past due reach 90+ within a "
"year."
msgstr ""
"违约状态默认是最后一个状态，这里是 ``90+`` ，也可以用 ``default_state`` 指定。贷款每个月最多再落后一个档位，因此正常贷款需要四个月才能达到 90+，前三个月的 PD "
"为 0。每个状态的 PD 都随期限上升，档位越差，起点越高：逾期 30 到 59 天的贷款中，有六成在一年内达到 90+。"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Because :math:`P^{a+b} = P^a P^b`, the PD at :math:`a + b` months is the PD at :math:`b` months "
"of the states reached after :math:`a` months. A monthly matrix therefore gives the PD over any "
"number of months, but only as far as the movements are a Markov chain with the same probabilities"
" in every month. The current state against the pooled vintage curve shows how far that holds:"
msgstr ""
"由于 :math:`P^{a+b} = P^a P^b` ， :math:`a + b` 个月的 PD 等于 :math:`a` 个月后所到达各状态的 :math:`b` 个月 "
"PD。因此月度矩阵可以给出任意月数的 PD，但前提是迁移构成每个月概率都相同的马尔可夫链。把正常状态与合并后的 vintage 曲线对比，可以看出这一前提在多大程度上成立："

msgid ""
"Cumulative PD by horizon for the states current, 1-29, 30-59, 60-89 and 90+, with the pooled "
"vintage curve as a dashed line next to the current state"
msgstr "状态 current、1-29、30-59、60-89 和 90+ 按期限的累计 PD，合并后的 vintage 曲线以虚线画在 current 状态旁边"

msgid ""
"Cumulative PD of each state by horizon from the monthly transition matrix. The dashed line is the"
" pooled vintage curve, which follows the curve of the current state in the first year and levels "
"off in the second."
msgstr "由月度转移矩阵得到的各状态按期限的累计 PD。虚线是合并后的 vintage 曲线，它在第一年与 current 状态的曲线吻合，第二年则趋于平稳。"

msgid ""
"The two agree in the first year and part in the second. The matrix mixes loans of every age, "
"while the chance of missing an instalment depends on the month on book, and the vintage curve "
"beyond month on book 18 rests on a few cohorts."
msgstr "二者在第一年一致，到第二年出现分歧。矩阵混合了各种账龄的贷款，而漏缴期款的概率取决于账龄；同时，账龄 18 之后的 vintage 曲线只基于少数批次。"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.lifetime.convert_pd` gives the marginal PDs of each state, which add up to the PD at"
" the last horizon:"
msgstr ":func:`~kivi.lifetime.convert_pd` 给出每个状态的边际 PD，其和等于最后一个期限的 PD："

msgid "Expected credit loss"
msgstr "预期信用损失"

msgid ""
"The reporting date here is the end of January 2026, the last month of the panel, and the book "
"holds the loans that still have a balance:"
msgstr "这里的报告日是面板的最后一个月，即 2026 年 1 月末；账上贷款是此时仍有余额的贷款："

msgid ""
"Each loan gets the marginal PDs of its delinquency bucket, with one row per loan and one column "
"per month after the reporting date:"
msgstr "每笔贷款取其所在逾期档位的边际 PD，每笔贷款一行，报告日之后每个月一列："

msgid ""
"The exposure at default of each month is the balance that the loan is expected to have "
"outstanding in that month: the balance at the reporting date, repaid by the remaining instalments"
" of an annuity at the loans' interest rate of 1% a month. ``paid`` counts the instalments paid "
"before each month. Loans past their term, which keep rolling in this data, owe their balance at "
"once. After the last instalment the exposure is 0, so the months after a loan's term add nothing:"
msgstr ""
"每个月的违约风险敞口是贷款在该月预计的未偿余额：以报告日的余额为起点，按月利率 1% 的等额本息方式由剩余期款偿还。 ``paid`` "
"是每个月之前已还的期数。在这份数据中，超过期限的贷款会继续滚动，其余额视为立即到期。最后一期还清后敞口为 0，因此贷款期限之后的各月不再增加损失："

msgid ""
"The losses are discounted at the loans' effective interest rate of 1% a month. A loan already at "
"90+ has defaulted at the reporting date, so its loss is measured at that date without "
"discounting, and its rate is 0. With an LGD of 45%, :func:`~kivi.lifetime.expected_credit_loss` "
"gives the 12-month and the lifetime ECL of each loan:"
msgstr ""
"损失按贷款的实际利率（每月 1%）折现。已经处于 90+ 的贷款在报告日已经违约，因此其损失在报告日计量、不做折现，利率为 0。设 LGD 为 45%， "
":func:`~kivi.lifetime.expected_credit_loss` 给出每笔贷款的 12 个月 ECL 和整个存续期 ECL："

msgid ""
"These are the first loans of each bucket with more than two years to run. The lifetime ECL of the"
" current loan is half as large again as its 12-month ECL: its PD is 0 for three months and its "
"risk builds up over the following ones. The delinquent loans default mostly within the year, so "
"their two ECLs are close. For a loan already at 90+, the PD is 1 in the first month and the rate "
"is 0, so the ECL is the LGD times the balance: 0.45 × 10,371.94 = 4,667.37."
msgstr ""
"这些是每个档位中剩余期限超过两年的第一笔贷款。正常贷款的整个存续期 ECL 比 12 个月 ECL 高出一半：它的 PD 在前三个月为 "
"0，风险在随后几个月逐渐积累。逾期贷款大多在一年内违约，因此两种 ECL 很接近。对于已经处于 90+ 的贷款，第一个月的 PD 为 1、利率为 0，因此 ECL 等于 LGD "
"乘以余额：0.45 × 10,371.94 = 4,667.37。"

msgid "Stage allocation"
msgstr "阶段划分"

msgid ""
"A significant increase in credit risk is judged against the risk expected at initial recognition."
" :func:`~kivi.lifetime.significant_increase` compares the PD at the reporting date with the PD "
"expected at origination, as a ratio, a difference or both. With ``relative=2.0`` and "
"``absolute=0.01``, a PD must have more than doubled and risen by more than one percentage point:"
msgstr ""
"信用风险是否显著增加，要与初始确认时预期的风险相比较。 :func:`~kivi.lifetime.significant_increase` 比较报告日的 PD 与发放时预期的 "
"PD，可以看比率、差值或两者兼看。在 ``relative=2.0`` 和 ``absolute=0.01`` 下，PD 必须增加到两倍以上，并且上升超过一个百分点："

msgid ""
"The first PD quadrupled but rose by only 0.3 percentage points, the second barely rose, and the "
"last rose by 4 points without doubling. IFRS 9 does not set these thresholds. They are the "
"lender's policy, like the definition of default, so both arguments are required, and either can "
"be None to leave its test out. For a rule under which either test suffices, combine two calls, "
"each with one threshold, with ``|``; qualitative criteria, such as a watch list, combine with the"
" flags in the same way."
msgstr ""
"第一个 PD 增加到四倍，但只上升了 0.3 个百分点；第二个几乎没有上升；最后一个上升了 4 个百分点，但没有翻倍。IFRS 9 "
"没有规定这些阈值。它们与违约定义一样，是贷款人的政策，因此两个参数都必须传入，任一参数都可以为 None 以略去相应的测试。若规则只要求通过任一项测试，请分别用一个阈值调用两次，再用 ``|``"
" 合并；定性标准（例如关注名单）也以同样的方式与这些标记合并。"

msgid ""
"Compare PDs of the same horizon. In the panel, a loan's delinquency bucket is the only risk "
"driver, and every loan was current at origination, so the 12-month PD of each bucket against that"
" of a current loan gives the test:"
msgstr "请比较相同期限的 PD。在这份面板中，贷款的逾期档位是唯一的风险因素，而且每笔贷款发放时都是正常的，因此用每个档位的 12 个月 PD 与正常贷款的 12 个月 PD 比较，就构成了这项测试："

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.lifetime.assign_stages` adds the backstops: an exposure more than 30 days past due "
"is at least in stage 2, and one 90 days past due or more, or flagged as defaulted, is in stage 3."
" The defaults follow the rebuttable presumptions of IFRS 9: credit risk has increased "
"significantly when contractual payments are more than 30 days past due (paragraph 5.5.11), and "
"default occurs no later than when a financial asset is 90 days past due (paragraph B5.5.37). Pass"
" ``stage_2_days`` and ``stage_3_days`` for other thresholds. The panel records buckets rather "
"than days, so the example takes the middle of each bucket, and it flags the 90+ loans as "
"defaulted:"
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.lifetime.assign_stages` 加上兜底标准：逾期超过 30 天的敞口至少处于第二阶段，逾期 90 天及以上或被标记为违约的敞口处于第三阶段。默认值依据"
" IFRS 9 的可推翻假设：合同付款逾期超过 30 天时，信用风险已显著增加（第 5.5.11 段）；违约的发生不晚于金融资产逾期 90 天之时（第 B5.5.37 段）。如需其他阈值，请传入"
" ``stage_2_days`` 和 ``stage_3_days`` 。面板记录的是逾期档位而不是天数，因此示例取每个档位的中点，并把 90+ 的贷款标记为违约："

msgid ""
"The PD test flags every delinquent bucket, so here the stages follow the buckets. A behavioural "
"score or a rating would also separate the current loans from each other."
msgstr "PD 测试标记了所有逾期档位，因此这里的阶段与档位一致。行为评分或评级还能把正常贷款彼此区分开。"

msgid ""
"The wording of the two presumptions sets the boundaries. Like the PD thresholds, the 30 days must"
" be exceeded, so an exposure exactly 30 days past due stays in stage 1, while an exposure exactly"
" 90 days past due is already in stage 3:"
msgstr "两项假设的表述决定了边界。与 PD 阈值一样，30 天必须被超过，因此恰好逾期 30 天的敞口仍处于第一阶段；而恰好逾期 90 天的敞口已处于第三阶段："

msgid "A days-past-due axis with the thresholds 30 and 90, and the stages of 0, 30, 31, 89 and 90 days"
msgstr "带有阈值 30 和 90 的逾期天数轴，以及逾期 0、30、31、89 和 90 天对应的阶段"

msgid ""
"The days-past-due backstops of ``assign_stages``. More than 30 days past due is at least stage 2,"
" and 90 days or more is stage 3."
msgstr "``assign_stages`` 的逾期天数兜底标准：逾期超过 30 天至少处于第二阶段，逾期 90 天及以上处于第三阶段。"

msgid "Loss allowance by stage"
msgstr "按阶段汇总损失准备"

msgid ""
"The loss allowance of a loan in stage 1 is its 12-month ECL, and that of a loan in stage 2 or 3 "
"its lifetime ECL. :func:`~kivi.lifetime.stage_table` sums the exposures and the allowances of "
"each stage:"
msgstr ""
"第一阶段贷款的损失准备是其 12 个月 ECL，第二、三阶段贷款的损失准备是其整个存续期 ECL。 :func:`~kivi.lifetime.stage_table` "
"汇总每个阶段的敞口和损失准备："

msgid "Reading the result"
msgstr "解读结果"

msgid "``total``"
msgstr "``total``"

msgid "Number of exposures in the stage, or their total weight with ``weights``."
msgstr "该阶段的敞口数，使用 ``weights`` 时为其权重之和。"

msgid "``exposure``"
msgstr "``exposure``"

msgid "Sum of the exposures, such as the gross carrying amounts."
msgstr "敞口之和，例如账面余额之和。"

msgid "``exposure_share``"
msgstr "``exposure_share``"

msgid "The stage's share of the exposure of all stages."
msgstr "该阶段占全部阶段敞口的比例。"

msgid "``expected_credit_loss``"
msgstr "``expected_credit_loss``"

msgid "Sum of the loss allowances."
msgstr "损失准备之和。"

msgid "``coverage``"
msgstr "``coverage``"

msgid ""
"``expected_credit_loss`` divided by ``exposure``, the coverage ratio. NaN for a stage without "
"exposure."
msgstr "``expected_credit_loss`` 除以 ``exposure`` ，即覆盖率。没有敞口的阶段为 NaN。"

#, python-format
msgid ""
"The coverage ratio rises from stage to stage, here from 1% in stage 1 to 18% in stage 2 and 45% "
"in stage 3. In stage 3 the default has happened and the loss is not discounted, so the coverage "
"is the LGD. In stage 1 it is below the LGD times the 12-month PD of a current loan, 0.45 × 0.0393"
" = 1.8%, because the balances amortize and many loans have less than a year to run. The coverage "
"of the portfolio, 4.0% here, is the sum of the loss allowances divided by the sum of the "
"exposures. The share of the exposure in stage 2 shows how much of the book carries lifetime "
"losses; recompute the table with other thresholds to see how much the allowance depends on them."
msgstr ""
"覆盖率逐阶段上升，这里从第一阶段的 1% 升到第二阶段的 18% 和第三阶段的 45%。第三阶段已经违约，损失不做折现，因此覆盖率就是 LGD。第一阶段的覆盖率低于 LGD 乘以正常贷款的 12"
" 个月 PD，即 0.45 × 0.0393 = 1.8%，因为余额逐步摊还，而且很多贷款的剩余期限不足一年。资产组合的覆盖率（这里为 "
"4.0%）是损失准备之和除以敞口之和。第二阶段的敞口占比表明有多少资产需要计提整个存续期损失；用其他阈值重新计算这张表，可以看出损失准备在多大程度上取决于这些阈值。"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.lifetime.convert_pd` treats a missing value as a period that is not observed, and "
"never fills it. The marginal and conditional PDs of a period need the cumulative PDs at its end "
"and at the end of the period before, and a cumulative PD needs every period before it. A curve "
"that starts with missing values, as in a panel that starts after origination, gives marginal and "
"conditional PDs from its second observed period on, but no cumulative PDs. Fill the periods that "
"are not observed first, for example by pooling the cohorts as above or by extending the curve "
"beyond its last month, before passing the PDs on."
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.lifetime.convert_pd` 把缺失值视为没有观测到的期，从不填补。某一期的边际和条件 PD 需要该期期末和上一期期末的累计 PD，累计 PD "
"则需要此前的每一期。开头有缺失值的曲线（例如面板晚于放款开始）从第二个观测期起有边际和条件 PD，但没有累计 "
"PD。请先填补没有观测到的期，例如像上文那样合并各批次，或把曲线延伸到最后一个月之后，再把 PD 传给后续函数。"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.lifetime.expected_credit_loss` converts each account on its own, so as "
":doc:`/api/conventions` describes, an account with a missing PD, LGD or EAD in a period that is "
"added up, or with a missing rate, gets a missing ECL; the periods after ``horizon`` are not used."
" :func:`~kivi.lifetime.transition_pd` needs a complete row for every state other than the default"
" state. The staging functions reject missing values, because a flag or a stage cannot be missing:"
" decide how to stage an exposure without a PD or without its days past due before passing it in."
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.lifetime.expected_credit_loss` 对每个账户单独计算，因此按 :doc:`/api/conventions` 的说明，若求和的某一期 "
"PD、LGD 或 EAD 缺失，或者利率缺失，该账户的 ECL 为缺失； ``horizon`` 之后的各期不会被使用。 :func:`~kivi.lifetime.transition_pd`"
" 需要除违约状态外每个状态的完整一行。阶段划分函数不接受缺失值，因为标记和阶段不能缺失：请先决定没有 PD 或没有逾期天数的敞口如何划分阶段，再传入。"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.lifetime.stage_table` takes ``weights``, such as the inverse of a sampling rate. The"
" counts, exposures and losses become sums of weights, so integer weights give the same table as "
"repeated rows. The other functions work on single accounts or states and take no weights; to "
"weight the loans of a vintage table by amount, pass ``weights`` to "
":func:`~kivi.vintage.vintage_table`."
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.lifetime.stage_table` 接受 ``weights`` "
"，例如抽样比例的倒数。计数、敞口和损失都变为加权和，因此整数权重与重复相应行得到的表相同。其他函数针对单个账户或状态计算，不接受权重；若要按金额对 vintage 表中的贷款加权，请把 "
"``weights`` 传给 :func:`~kivi.vintage.vintage_table` 。"

msgid ""
"A transition matrix gives a term structure only as far as the movements are a time-homogeneous "
"Markov chain: the same probabilities in every period, whatever the age of a loan or the time it "
"has spent in its state."
msgstr "只有当迁移是时齐马尔可夫链时，转移矩阵才能给出期限结构：每一期的概率都相同，与贷款的账龄或在当前状态停留的时间无关。"

msgid ""
"IFRS 9 asks for an unbiased, probability-weighted amount that reflects forecasts of economic "
"conditions. These functions compute the ECL of one set of PDs, LGDs and EADs: compute it for each"
" economic scenario and weight the results with the probabilities of the scenarios."
msgstr "IFRS 9 要求无偏、按概率加权并反映经济状况预测的金额。这些函数计算的是一组 PD、LGD 和 EAD 下的 ECL：请对每个经济情景分别计算，再按各情景的概率加权。"

msgid ""
"Early repayment enters only through the EAD schedule and through the vintage curves, which count "
"repaid loans as not bad."
msgstr "提前还款只通过 EAD 计划表以及 vintage 曲线（把已还清的贷款计为非坏）体现。"

msgid ""
"For revolving facilities, such as credit cards, IFRS 9 measures the expected credit losses over "
"the period in which the lender is exposed to credit risk, which can be longer than the "
"contractual period (paragraphs B5.5.39 and B5.5.40). Choose the periods and the EAD schedule, "
"including drawings of undrawn limits, for that period."
msgstr ""
"对于循环额度（例如信用卡），IFRS 9 按贷款人面临信用风险的期间计量预期信用损失，该期间可能长于合同期间（第 B5.5.39 段和第 B5.5.40 段）。请据此选择期数和 EAD "
"计划表，并考虑未使用额度的提用。"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.lifetime.significant_increase` does not apply the exemption for exposures with low "
"credit risk at the reporting date (paragraph 5.5.10); combine its flags with a low-risk criterion"
" of your own."
msgstr ":func:`~kivi.lifetime.significant_increase` 不适用报告日信用风险较低的敞口的豁免（第 5.5.10 段）；请把其标记与自己的低信用风险标准合并。"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.lifetime.assign_stages` looks at one reporting date. Probation periods, during which"
" an exposure that no longer meets a criterion stays in its stage, need the history of each "
"exposure and are not applied, and neither are the rules for assets that are credit-impaired when "
"they are purchased or originated."
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.lifetime.assign_stages` "
"只看一个报告日。观察期（敞口不再满足某项标准后仍留在原阶段的期间）需要每笔敞口的历史，此处不予处理；购入或源生时已发生信用减值的资产所适用的规则也不予处理。"

msgid ""
"Published transition matrices are rounded, so their rows rarely add up to 1. "
":func:`~kivi.lifetime.transition_pd` allows a rounding error of 1e-9 only, and asks to divide "
"each row by its sum:"
msgstr "公开发布的转移矩阵经过舍入，每行之和很少恰好为 1。 :func:`~kivi.lifetime.transition_pd` 只允许 1e-9 的舍入误差，并提示把每行除以该行之和："

msgid ""
"``relative`` is a ratio, not an increase: for a PD that rose by more than 50%, pass 1.5 rather "
"than 0.5."
msgstr "``relative`` 是比率而不是增幅：PD 上升超过 50% 时，应传入 1.5 而不是 0.5。"

msgid ""
"A horizon longer than the term structure raises an error, because leaving out the missing periods"
" would understate the loss:"
msgstr "求和期限长于期限结构时会报错，因为略去缺失的期会低估损失："

msgid ""
":mod:`kivi.metrics` measures how well a score separates events from non-events. "
":func:`~kivi.metrics.roc_auc`, :func:`~kivi.metrics.gini` and :func:`~kivi.metrics.ks` summarize "
"the ranking in one number, and :func:`~kivi.metrics.roc_table` lists the points of the ROC curve "
"behind them. :func:`~kivi.metrics.roc_auc_interval` gives the AUC a standard error and a "
"confidence interval, and :func:`~kivi.metrics.delong_test` tests whether two scores of the same "
"customers rank equally well. :func:`~kivi.metrics.gains_table` breaks the ranking down by score "
"band, and :func:`~kivi.metrics.brier_score` checks predicted probabilities against the outcomes."
msgstr ""
":mod:`kivi.metrics` 衡量评分区分事件与非事件的能力。 :func:`~kivi.metrics.roc_auc` 、 :func:`~kivi.metrics.gini` 和"
" :func:`~kivi.metrics.ks` 用一个数概括排序效果， :func:`~kivi.metrics.roc_table` 列出这些指标背后的 ROC 曲线上的点。 "
":func:`~kivi.metrics.roc_auc_interval` 给出 AUC 的标准误和置信区间， :func:`~kivi.metrics.delong_test` "
"检验同一批客户的两个评分排序效果是否一样好。 :func:`~kivi.metrics.gains_table` 按评分段展开排序效果， "
":func:`~kivi.metrics.brier_score` 将预测概率与实际结果对照。"

msgid ""
"Performance is measured once the model is scaled to a :doc:`scorecard`, and before its "
"probabilities are checked in :doc:`calibration`."
msgstr "模型刻度为 :doc:`scorecard` 之后衡量其表现，然后再在 :doc:`calibration` 中检查其概率。"

msgid ""
"For :math:`n_1` events and :math:`n_0` non-events, let :math:`R_1` be the sum of the ranks of the"
" events among all scores, where tied scores share their average rank. The area under the ROC "
"curve and the Gini coefficient are"
msgstr "设有 :math:`n_1` 个事件和 :math:`n_0` 个非事件，:math:`R_1` 为事件在全部评分中的秩之和，相同评分取平均秩。ROC 曲线下面积和 Gini 系数为"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\\mathrm{AUC} = \\frac{R_1 - n_1 (n_1 + 1) / 2}{n_1 n_0}, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathrm{Gini} = 2\\,\\mathrm{AUC} - 1."
msgstr ""
"\\mathrm{AUC} = \\frac{R_1 - n_1 (n_1 + 1) / 2}{n_1 n_0}, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathrm{Gini} = 2\\,\\mathrm{AUC} - 1."

msgid ""
"The AUC is the probability that a randomly chosen event scores higher than a randomly chosen non-"
"event, with ties counted as one half. A score unrelated to the target gives an AUC of about 0.5 "
"and a Gini of about 0."
msgstr "AUC 是随机抽取的一个事件比随机抽取的一个非事件评分更高的概率，评分相同时计为二分之一。与目标无关的评分，AUC 约为 0.5，Gini 约为 0。"

msgid ""
"Let :math:`F_1` and :math:`F_0` be the empirical distribution functions of the scores of events "
"and of non-events. The Kolmogorov-Smirnov statistic is their largest gap:"
msgstr "设 :math:`F_1` 和 :math:`F_0` 分别为事件评分和非事件评分的经验分布函数。Kolmogorov-Smirnov 统计量是二者的最大差距："

#, python-brace-format
msgid "\\mathrm{KS} = \\max_t \\, \\lvert F_1(t) - F_0(t) \\rvert."
msgstr "\\mathrm{KS} = \\max_t \\, \\lvert F_1(t) - F_0(t) \\rvert."

msgid ""
"The gap is taken in absolute value, as in the two-sample test. KS therefore says nothing about "
"the direction of the score, and its largest gap can come from a range of scores where the ranking"
" is reversed. Read it together with the Gini."
msgstr "差距取绝对值，与双样本检验相同。因此 KS 不反映评分的方向，其最大差距也可能来自排序方向相反的评分区间。应与 Gini 一起解读。"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Flagging every customer who scores at or above a threshold :math:`t` catches a share "
":math:`\\mathrm{TPR}(t)` of the events, the true positive rate, and a share "
":math:`\\mathrm{FPR}(t)` of the non-events, the false positive rate. The ROC curve joins the "
"points :math:`(\\mathrm{FPR}(t), \\mathrm{TPR}(t))` from the highest threshold to the lowest. The"
" AUC is the area under it, and the KS is the largest gap :math:`\\lvert \\mathrm{TPR}(t) - "
"\\mathrm{FPR}(t) \\rvert` between the two rates. Tied scores move the curve diagonally, so the "
"area counts a tied pair as one half, as the AUC does."
msgstr ""
"把评分不低于阈值 :math:`t` 的客户全部标记出来，可以捕获比例为 :math:`\\mathrm{TPR}(t)` 的事件，即真正例率；同时也标记了比例为 "
":math:`\\mathrm{FPR}(t)` 的非事件，即假正例率。ROC 曲线从最高阈值到最低阈值依次连接各点 :math:`(\\mathrm{FPR}(t), "
"\\mathrm{TPR}(t))` 。AUC 是曲线下的面积，KS 是两个比率之间的最大差距 :math:`\\lvert \\mathrm{TPR}(t) - "
"\\mathrm{FPR}(t) \\rvert` 。评分相同的观测使曲线沿对角方向移动，因此面积与 AUC 一样，把评分相同的一对计为二分之一。"

msgid ""
"Three of these six customers are events. Of the nine pairs of an event and a non-event, six are "
"ordered correctly, two are not, and one is tied at 0.4, so the AUC is :math:`(6 + 0.5) / 9`:"
msgstr "下面六位客户中有三位是事件。在九对“事件—非事件”组合中，六对排序正确，两对错误，一对在 0.4 处并列，因此 AUC 为 :math:`(6 + 0.5) / 9`："

msgid ""
"At a cut-off of 0.4, two thirds of the non-events but only one third of the events score at or "
"below it. No cut-off separates the two classes further, so the KS is one third:"
msgstr "以 0.4 为切分点，三分之二的非事件评分不高于它，而事件只有三分之一。没有哪个切分点能把两类分得更开，因此 KS 为三分之一："

msgid ""
"The ROC table has one row for each of the five distinct scores, after a first row at infinity "
"that flags nobody. At 0.4 it flags the tied event and non-event together, so the curve moves "
"diagonally from (1/3, 2/3) to (2/3, 1):"
msgstr ""
"ROC 表在第一行（阈值为无穷大，不标记任何人）之后，为五个不同的评分各列一行。在 0.4 处，评分相同的事件和非事件被同时标记，因此曲线从 (1/3, 2/3) 沿对角方向移到 (2/3, "
"1)："

msgid ""
"The trapezoids under the curve have the areas 1/9 from 0.9 to 0.8, 5/18 from 0.7 to 0.4 and 1/3 "
"from 0.4 to 0.1, which add up to the AUC of 13/18. The largest gap between the two rates is the "
"KS of 1/3."
msgstr ""
"曲线下各梯形的面积为：从 0.9 到 0.8 为 1/9，从 0.7 到 0.4 为 5/18，从 0.4 到 0.1 为 1/3，合计等于 AUC 13/18。两个比率之间的最大差距就是 "
"KS，即 1/3。"

msgid ""
"The six scores and targets, their ROC table, and the ROC curve with the areas under it and the "
"largest gap between the two rates"
msgstr "六个评分和目标、它们的 ROC 表，以及 ROC 曲线、曲线下的面积和两个比率之间的最大差距"

msgid ""
"The ROC table of the example and its curve. The three areas under the curve add up to the AUC. "
"The outlined rows and the amber segments mark the largest gap between the two rates, the KS."
msgstr "示例的 ROC 表及其曲线。曲线下三块面积之和等于 AUC。带边框的行和琥珀色线段标出两个比率之间的最大差距，即 KS。"

msgid "Score direction"
msgstr "评分方向"

msgid ""
"Every function expects a score that is higher for a higher event probability, such as a predicted"
" probability of default (PD). Scorecard points run the other way, because more points mean a "
"lower risk, so negate them before passing them in: ``roc_auc(-points, target)``."
msgstr "所有函数都要求事件概率越高、评分越高，例如预测的违约概率（PD）。评分卡分数的方向相反，分数越高表示风险越低，因此须先取负再传入：``roc_auc(-points, target)``。"

msgid ""
"Every function takes the score first and the target second, as ``woe_table(groups, target)`` "
"takes the groups first. scikit-learn's metrics take the target first, so check the order when "
"porting code from them."
msgstr ""
"所有函数都是评分在前、目标在后，就像 ``woe_table(groups, target)`` 把分组放在前面。scikit-learn "
"的指标函数把目标放在前面，从那里移植代码时请检查参数顺序。"

msgid ""
"As in :func:`~kivi.woe.woe_table`, the target is 1 for an event and 0 for a non-event. Two Series"
" must share the same index; arrays and lists are matched by position, as :doc:`/api/conventions` "
"describes for every function. Scores must be finite, so decide how missing values are scored "
"before evaluating the model."
msgstr ""
"与 :func:`~kivi.woe.woe_table` 相同，目标为 1 表示事件，为 0 表示非事件。两个 Series 的索引必须相同；数组和列表按位置对应， "
":doc:`/api/conventions` 说明了所有函数共同遵守的这一规则。评分必须是有限值，因此评估模型之前要先确定缺失值如何评分。"

msgid "Evaluating a WOE score"
msgstr "评估 WOE 评分"

msgid ""
"The bank data give a more realistic example. The score below adds up the WOE values of four "
"variables, fitted on the development sample. A higher WOE means a higher event rate, so the sum "
"already runs in the direction the metrics expect. A scorecard would weight the variables with a "
"logistic regression; the metrics treat any score in the same way."
msgstr ""
"银行数据提供了一个更贴近实际的例子。下面的评分把四个变量的 WOE 值相加，这些 WOE 在开发样本上拟合。WOE "
"越高表示事件率越高，因此这个和的方向已经符合指标的要求。评分卡会用逻辑回归为各变量加权；对任何评分，这些指标的处理方式都一样。"

msgid ""
"Measure the score on both samples. The validation rows played no part in fitting the WOE values, "
"so they show how the score holds up on new customers:"
msgstr "在两个样本上分别衡量评分。验证样本没有参与 WOE 的拟合，因此能反映评分在新客户上的表现："

msgid ""
"A clear drop from development to validation would point to overfitting. Here the validation "
"values are even slightly higher, which is within the sampling noise of 173 validation events."
msgstr "如果指标从开发样本到验证样本明显下降，可能意味着过拟合。这里验证样本的数值甚至略高，仍在 173 个验证事件的抽样误差范围之内。"

msgid ""
"Points that fall as the risk rises rank the customers in the opposite order. Passed as they are, "
"they give an AUC below 0.5 and a negative Gini; negated, they give the values above. KS is the "
"same in both directions, so it cannot reveal a reversed score:"
msgstr "风险越高分数越低的评分卡分数，会把客户按相反的顺序排列。直接传入时，AUC 低于 0.5，Gini 为负；取负后则得到上面的数值。KS 在两个方向上相同，因此无法发现评分方向反了："

msgid ""
"No threshold makes a Gini or a KS good in general: the values that can be reached depend on the "
"portfolio, the target definition and the data available. Compare a new score with the one it "
"replaces on the same validation sample."
msgstr "Gini 或 KS 没有通用的合格线：能达到的水平取决于资产组合、目标定义和可用的数据。应在同一个验证样本上，把新评分与它要替换的评分进行比较。"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.metrics.roc_table` lists the points of the ROC curve, one row per distinct score "
"from the highest to the lowest, after a first row at infinity. Each row counts the events and "
"non-events that score at or above its threshold, in ``cum_event`` and ``cum_non_event``, and "
"divides them by all events and all non-events to give ``true_positive_rate`` and "
"``false_positive_rate``. ``precision`` is the event rate among the customers it flags. On the "
"validation sample the WOE score takes 79 distinct values:"
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.metrics.roc_table` 列出 ROC "
"曲线上的点：在第一行（阈值为无穷大）之后，从高到低每个不同的评分一行。每一行统计评分不低于其阈值的事件数和非事件数，记在 ``cum_event`` 和 ``cum_non_event`` "
"中，再分别除以全部事件数和全部非事件数，得到 ``true_positive_rate`` 和 ``false_positive_rate`` 。 ``precision`` "
"是被该行标记的客户中的事件率。在验证样本上，WOE 评分共有 79 个不同的取值："

msgid ""
"The trapezoids under the curve add up to the AUC, and the largest gap between the two rates is "
"the KS:"
msgstr "曲线下各梯形的面积之和等于 AUC，两个比率之间的最大差距等于 KS："

msgid ""
"The threshold with the largest gap flags 104 of the 173 events, a true positive rate of 60%, but "
"only 378 of the 1,348 non-events. About one in five of the customers it flags is an event, twice "
"the event rate of the sample:"
msgstr "差距最大的阈值标记了 173 个事件中的 104 个，真正例率为 60%，而 1,348 个非事件中只标记了 378 个。被它标记的客户中约五分之一是事件，是样本事件率的两倍："

msgid ""
"ROC curve of the validation score, true positive rate against false positive rate, with the "
"diagonal and the KS marked as a vertical segment"
msgstr "验证评分的 ROC 曲线：真正例率对假正例率，带有对角线，KS 以一条竖线段标出"

msgid ""
"ROC curve of the WOE score on the validation sample. The vertical segment at the threshold with "
"the largest gap between the two rates is the KS; the dashed diagonal is a random ordering."
msgstr "验证样本上 WOE 评分的 ROC 曲线。两个比率差距最大的阈值处的竖线段就是 KS；虚线对角线表示随机排序。"

msgid ""
"The rates are the ``cum_event_share`` and ``cum_non_event_share`` of a gains table with one band "
"per distinct score, and scikit-learn's ``roc_curve(target, score, drop_intermediate=False)`` "
"gives the same points."
msgstr ""
"这两个比率就是每个不同评分各成一段时增益表中的 ``cum_event_share`` 和 ``cum_non_event_share`` ，scikit-learn 的 "
"``roc_curve(target, score, drop_intermediate=False)`` 也给出相同的点。"

msgid "Confidence interval of the AUC"
msgstr "AUC 的置信区间"

msgid ""
"Another sample of customers would give another AUC. :func:`~kivi.metrics.roc_auc_interval` "
"estimates the standard error of the AUC by the method of DeLong, DeLong and Clarke-Pearson "
"(1988), which makes no assumption about the distribution of the scores. Each event gets a "
"placement value, the share of non-events that score below it, and each non-event the share of "
"events that score above it, with ties counted as one half. Both sets of placement values average "
"to the AUC :math:`\\hat\\theta`. With :math:`n_1` events and :math:`n_0` non-events, as in the "
"definitions above, the variance of the AUC is estimated by"
msgstr ""
"换一批客户，AUC 也会不同。 :func:`~kivi.metrics.roc_auc_interval` 用 DeLong、DeLong 和 Clarke-"
"Pearson（1988）的方法估计 AUC "
"的标准误，该方法不对评分的分布作任何假设。每个事件有一个位置值，即评分低于它的非事件所占的比例；每个非事件的位置值则是评分高于它的事件所占的比例；评分相同时计为二分之一。两组位置值的均值都等于 "
"AUC :math:`\\hat\\theta` 。与上面的定义一样，设有 :math:`n_1` 个事件和 :math:`n_0` 个非事件，AUC 的方差估计为"

msgid "\\mathrm{SE}^2 = \\frac{S_{10}}{n_1} + \\frac{S_{01}}{n_0},"
msgstr "\\mathrm{SE}^2 = \\frac{S_{10}}{n_1} + \\frac{S_{01}}{n_0},"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"where :math:`S_{10}` and :math:`S_{01}` are the sample variances of the placement values of the "
"events and of the non-events. The interval at the confidence ``level`` is :math:`\\hat\\theta "
"\\pm z \\, \\mathrm{SE}`, with the normal quantile :math:`z`, which is 1.96 for the default level"
" of 0.95, and it is cut off at 0 and 1. The Gini coefficient gets the same interval, rescaled to "
":math:`2\\,\\mathrm{AUC} - 1`."
msgstr ""
"其中 :math:`S_{10}` 和 :math:`S_{01}` 分别是事件和非事件位置值的样本方差。置信水平为 ``level`` 的区间为 :math:`\\hat\\theta "
"\\pm z \\, \\mathrm{SE}` ，其中 :math:`z` 是正态分位数，默认水平 0.95 下为 1.96；区间截断到 0 与 1 之间。Gini 系数的区间相同，只是换算为"
" :math:`2\\,\\mathrm{AUC} - 1` 。"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"For the six customers of the worked example, the placement values of the events are 1/2, 2/3 and "
"1 and those of the non-events 1, 5/6 and 1/3. Their sample variances are 7/108 and 13/108, so "
":math:`\\mathrm{SE}^2 = 5/81` and the standard error is 0.248:"
msgstr ""
"对于计算示例中的六个客户，事件的位置值为 1/2、2/3 和 1，非事件的位置值为 1、5/6 和 1/3。它们的样本方差分别为 7/108 和 13/108，因此 "
":math:`\\mathrm{SE}^2 = 5/81` ，标准误为 0.248："

msgid "On the validation sample, the AUC of 0.716 is known to about 0.04 either way:"
msgstr "在验证样本上，AUC 为 0.716，上下误差约为 0.04："

msgid ""
"The development and validation samples hold different customers, so their AUCs can be treated as "
"independent, with a difference whose standard error is :math:`\\sqrt{\\mathrm{SE}_1^2 + "
"\\mathrm{SE}_2^2}`. This is only a rough check, because the WOE values were fitted on the "
"development sample, whose AUC is therefore optimistic. The difference between the two samples is "
"well within the noise:"
msgstr ""
"开发样本和验证样本包含不同的客户，因此可以把两者的 AUC 视为相互独立，其差值的标准误为 :math:`\\sqrt{\\mathrm{SE}_1^2 + \\mathrm{SE}_2^2}`"
" 。这只是粗略的检查，因为 WOE 值是在开发样本上拟合的，开发样本的 AUC 因而偏乐观。两个样本之间的差异完全在噪声范围之内："

msgid "Comparing two scores"
msgstr "比较两个评分"

msgid ""
"A new score, such as a challenger to the model in use, is best compared with the current one on "
"the same customers. Both AUCs then come from the same pairs of events and non-events, so they are"
" correlated, and their difference is known more precisely than that of two independent samples. "
":func:`~kivi.metrics.delong_test` estimates its standard error from the differences between the "
"placement values of the two scores, and tests whether the two AUCs are equal."
msgstr ""
"新评分（例如现行模型的挑战者）最好与现行评分在同一批客户上比较。此时两个 AUC 来自同样的事件与非事件对，因而是相关的，其差值比两个独立样本的差值估计得更精确。 "
":func:`~kivi.metrics.delong_test` 根据两个评分位置值之差估计差值的标准误，并检验两个 AUC 是否相等。"

msgid ""
"The WOE score adds up the WOE values of its variables, so a new variable joins it by adding its "
"WOE. The two new scores below add ``month`` or ``loan`` to the four variables of the current "
"score:"
msgstr "WOE 评分是各变量 WOE 值之和，因此加入新变量只需加上它的 WOE。下面两个新评分分别在现行评分的四个变量之外加入 ``month`` 或 ``loan`` ："

msgid ""
"ROC curves of the current WOE score and of the scores with month or loan added, on the validation"
" sample, with each AUC in the legend"
msgstr "验证样本上现行 WOE 评分以及加入 month 或 loan 后的评分的 ROC 曲线，图例中标出各自的 AUC"

msgid ""
"ROC curves of the current score and of the scores with ``month`` or ``loan`` added, on the "
"validation sample. ``month`` lifts the curve at false positive rates between about 5% and 45%; "
"the curve with ``loan`` stays close to the current one."
msgstr ""
"验证样本上现行评分以及加入 ``month`` 或 ``loan`` 后的评分的 ROC 曲线。 ``month`` 在假正例率约 5% 到 45% 之间抬高了曲线；加入 ``loan`` "
"的曲线则与现行评分的曲线很接近。"

msgid ""
"``difference`` is ``new_auc`` minus ``current_auc``, ``lower`` and ``upper`` bound it at the "
"confidence ``level``, and ``p_value`` is the two-sided p-value of ``z``. Adding ``month`` raises "
"the AUC by 0.025, and the interval of the gain excludes 0. The gain of 0.010 from ``loan`` could "
"be chance (p = 0.13), although its standard error of 0.006 is a third of that of either AUC on "
"its own. For a one-sided test that the new score ranks better, halve ``p_value`` when ``z`` is "
"positive."
msgstr ""
"``difference`` 是 ``new_auc`` 减去 ``current_auc`` ， ``lower`` 和 ``upper`` 是它在置信水平 ``level`` "
"下的区间上下限， ``p_value`` 是 ``z`` 的双侧 p 值。加入 ``month`` 使 AUC 提高 0.025，提升的区间不包含 0。加入 ``loan`` 带来的 0.010"
" 的提升可能出于偶然（p = 0.13），尽管其标准误 0.006 只有单个 AUC 标准误的三分之一。如需单侧检验新评分的排序是否更好，在 ``z`` 为正时把 ``p_value`` 减半。"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.metrics.gains_table` sorts the sample into score bands, from the highest scores to "
"the lowest. Each row shows the event rate of its band and the share of all events found by "
"reviewing that band and every band above it. The default ``bins=10`` cuts the sample at the edges"
" of ``bin_edges(score, bins=10)``, and tied scores always share a band."
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.metrics.gains_table` 把样本按评分分段，从最高评分到最低评分排列。每行给出该段的事件率，以及审查该段及其以上各段时找到的事件占全部事件的比例。默认的"
" ``bins=10`` 在 ``bin_edges(score, bins=10)`` 的边界处切分样本，相同评分总在同一段。"

msgid ""
"In monitoring, fix the bands on the development sample so that every later sample is cut at the "
"same scores. Fit the edges with :func:`~kivi.binning.bin_edges` and round them to readable cut-"
"offs:"
msgstr "在监控中，评分段应在开发样本上固定，使之后的每个样本都在相同的评分处切分。用 :func:`~kivi.binning.bin_edges` 拟合边界，再取整为易读的切分点："

msgid ""
"Event rate and lift of each score band, and the cumulative share of events against the cumulative"
" share of customers"
msgstr "各分数段的事件率与提升度，以及累计事件占比对累计客户占比的曲线"

msgid ""
"Left: the event rate falls from the top score band to the bottom one; the dashed line is the "
"event rate of the whole sample. Right: the gains curve rises well above the diagonal of a random "
"ordering."
msgstr "左：事件率从最高分数段到最低分数段逐级下降；虚线是整个样本的事件率。右：增益曲线明显高于随机排序的对角线。"

#, python-format
msgid ""
"The top band holds 17% of the validation customers (264 of 1,521) but 42% of the events, so its "
"event rate is 2.4 times that of the whole sample. The table checks the gap between the two "
"classes only at the four interior cut-offs, so its largest ``ks`` stays below the KS over all "
"scores:"
msgstr ""
"最高的评分段只占验证样本客户的 17%（1,521 人中的 264 人），却包含 42% 的事件，因此其事件率是整个样本的 2.4 倍。该表只在四个内部切分点上检查两类之间的差距，因此其 "
"``ks`` 的最大值低于在全部评分上计算的 KS："

msgid ""
"Every band is reported, including a band that no customer falls into, so two samples cut on the "
"same edges give tables with the same rows. Their ``total`` columns then give the PSI of the score"
" bands, here far below 0.1, the usual upper bound of a small shift (see :doc:`psi`):"
msgstr ""
"结果列出每个评分段，包括没有客户落入的评分段，因此用相同边界切分的两个样本得到的表行相同。由二者的 ``total`` 列即可得到评分段的 PSI，这里远低于 "
"0.1，即通常视为小幅变化的上限（见 :doc:`psi`）："

msgid "``non_event``, ``event``, ``total``"
msgstr "``non_event``, ``event``, ``total``"

msgid "Non-events, events and all observations in the band, as in :func:`~kivi.woe.woe_table`."
msgstr "该段的非事件数、事件数和总观测数，与 :func:`~kivi.woe.woe_table` 相同。"

msgid "``event_rate``"
msgstr "``event_rate``"

msgid "``event`` divided by ``total``; NaN for an empty band."
msgstr "``event`` 除以 ``total``；空评分段为 NaN。"

msgid "``lift``"
msgstr "``lift``"

msgid "The event rate of the band divided by the event rate of the whole sample."
msgstr "该段的事件率除以整个样本的事件率。"

msgid "``cum_non_event_share``, ``cum_event_share``"
msgstr "``cum_non_event_share``, ``cum_event_share``"

msgid "Shares of all non-events and of all events in this band and the bands above it."
msgstr "该段及其以上各段分别占全部非事件和全部事件的比例。"

msgid "``cum_total_share``"
msgstr "``cum_total_share``"

msgid ""
"Share of all observations in this band and the bands above it. Plotting ``cum_event_share`` "
"against ``cum_total_share`` gives the gains chart."
msgstr "该段及其以上各段占全部观测的比例。以 ``cum_total_share`` 为横轴、``cum_event_share`` 为纵轴作图，即为增益图。"

msgid "``ks``"
msgstr "``ks``"

msgid ""
"The absolute gap between ``cum_event_share`` and ``cum_non_event_share`` at the lower edge of the"
" band. Like :func:`~kivi.metrics.ks`, it can come from a band where the score runs the wrong way,"
" with ``cum_non_event_share`` above ``cum_event_share``."
msgstr ""
"在该段下边界处，``cum_event_share`` 与 ``cum_non_event_share`` 之差的绝对值。与 :func:`~kivi.metrics.ks` "
"一样，它可能来自评分方向相反的评分段，即 ``cum_non_event_share`` 高于 ``cum_event_share``。"

msgid "``cum_lift``"
msgstr "``cum_lift``"

msgid ""
"``cum_event_share`` divided by ``cum_total_share``: the lift of reviewing this band and every "
"band above it."
msgstr "``cum_event_share`` 除以 ``cum_total_share``，即审查该段及其以上各段时的提升度。"

msgid "Brier score"
msgstr "Brier 分数"

msgid ""
"The ranking measures ignore the probability scale: any increasing transformation of the score "
"gives the same AUC, Gini and KS. When a model predicts probabilities, for example a PD used for "
"pricing or provisions, also compare them with the observed outcomes. "
":func:`~kivi.metrics.brier_score` is the mean squared difference between the probability "
":math:`p_i` and the outcome :math:`y_i`, so a lower value is better:"
msgstr ""
"排序度量与概率的尺度无关：对评分做任何递增变换，AUC、Gini 和 KS 都不变。如果模型预测的是概率，例如用于定价或拨备的 "
"PD，还要把概率与观测结果对照。:func:`~kivi.metrics.brier_score` 是概率 :math:`p_i` 与结果 :math:`y_i` "
"之差的平方的均值，因此越低越好："

#, python-brace-format
msgid "\\mathrm{BS} = \\frac{1}{n} \\sum_{i=1}^{n} (p_i - y_i)^2."
msgstr "\\mathrm{BS} = \\frac{1}{n} \\sum_{i=1}^{n} (p_i - y_i)^2."

msgid ""
"The example below predicts the probability of each validation customer by the development event "
"rate of the customer's ``poutcome`` group, and compares it with predicting the development event "
"rate for everyone:"
msgstr "下面的例子用客户所在 ``poutcome`` 组在开发样本中的事件率预测每位验证客户的概率，并与对所有人都预测开发样本事件率的做法进行比较："

#, python-format
msgid ""
"The group rates lower the Brier score by about 10% compared with the constant forecast. Unlike "
"the ranking measures, the Brier score needs no events in the sample, so it can also be computed "
"for a period without any."
msgstr "与常数预测相比，分组事件率使 Brier 分数降低了约 10%。与排序度量不同，Brier 分数不要求样本中有事件，因此在没有事件的时期也能计算。"

msgid ""
"Validation samples often keep every event but only some of the non-events. Every function of "
":mod:`kivi.metrics` takes ``weights``, one non-negative weight per observation matched like the "
"target, and then counts sums of weights instead of observations. Integer weights give the same "
"result as repeating rows, for :func:`~kivi.metrics.gains_table` on fixed edges: with an integer "
"``bins``, the weighted quantiles of :func:`~kivi.binning.bin_edges` use the inverted CDF and can "
"give other edges than the repeated rows. To weight a sample back to the population, give each "
"observation the inverse of its sampling rate. Below, every event of the validation sample is kept"
" but only every second non-event:"
msgstr ""
"验证样本常常保留全部事件、只保留部分非事件。 :mod:`kivi.metrics` 的每个函数都接受 ``weights`` "
"，即每个观测一个非负权重，对应方式与目标相同；此时统计的是权重之和而不是观测个数。整数权重与重复相应行的结果相同，对 :func:`~kivi.metrics.gains_table` "
"而言须使用固定边界：若 ``bins`` 为整数， :func:`~kivi.binning.bin_edges` "
"的加权分位数采用逆累积分布，得到的边界可能与重复行不同。要把样本加权还原到总体，给每个观测赋予其抽样比例的倒数。下面保留验证样本中的全部事件，但非事件每两个只保留一个："

msgid ""
"Without weights the sample has twice as many events per non-event as the population, and every "
"band's event rate is inflated. The weights restore rates close to those of all customers. The "
"ranking measures do not change, because a weight that is the same for every observation of a "
"class cancels out of the AUC, the Gini and the KS:"
msgstr ""
"不加权时，样本中每个非事件对应的事件数是总体的两倍，每个评分段的事件率都被抬高。加权后，事件率恢复到与全部客户接近的水平。排序指标不变，因为对同一类的每个观测都相同的权重会在 AUC、Gini "
"和 KS 中相互抵消："

msgid ""
"Weights that differ within a class, such as the inverse sampling rates of a stratified sample, do"
" change them."
msgstr "同一类内部各不相同的权重（例如分层样本的抽样比例倒数）则会改变这些指标。"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.metrics.roc_auc_interval` and :func:`~kivi.metrics.delong_test` read ``weights`` as "
"frequency weights: an observation of weight :math:`w` counts as :math:`w` observations. Integer "
"weights therefore give the same standard error as repeating rows, which suits data aggregated "
"into counts. The weights above stand for the non-events left out of the sample, so they give a "
"standard error as small as that of all customers, although the sample holds only half of the non-"
"events:"
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.metrics.roc_auc_interval` 和 :func:`~kivi.metrics.delong_test` 把 ``weights`` "
"视为频数权重：权重为 :math:`w` 的观测计为 :math:`w` "
"个观测。因此整数权重与重复相应行得到相同的标准误，适合已汇总为计数的数据。上面的权重代表样本之外的非事件，所以给出的标准误与全部客户的一样小，尽管样本只包含一半的非事件："

msgid ""
"A weight that is the same for every observation of a class leaves the AUC unchanged, so compute "
"its interval without such weights."
msgstr "同一类所有观测的权重都相同时，AUC 不受影响，因此计算其区间时不要使用这样的权重。"

msgid ""
"The intervals and the test rest on a normal approximation, which is poor for an AUC close to 0 or"
" 1 and for a class with few observations. The standard error is 0 whenever the placement values "
"are constant within each class, as they are for a score that separates the classes perfectly, one"
" that reverses them and a constant score, so the interval collapses to the estimate. Without "
"weights, both functions need at least two events and two non-events, and with weights a total "
"weight above 1 in each class."
msgstr ""
"区间和检验依赖正态近似，当 AUC 接近 0 或 1，或某一类的观测很少时，近似效果较差。只要每一类内部的位置值都相同，标准误就为 "
"0，例如把两类完全分开的评分、把两类完全颠倒的评分以及常数评分，此时区间缩为估计值本身。不使用权重时，两个函数都至少需要两个事件和两个非事件；使用权重时，每一类的权重之和都必须大于 1。"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.metrics.delong_test` needs both scores on the same observations. For the AUCs of "
"different samples, combine the standard errors of the two intervals, as in the comparison of the "
"development and validation samples above."
msgstr ":func:`~kivi.metrics.delong_test` 要求两个评分来自同一批观测。比较不同样本的 AUC 时，应合并两个区间的标准误，如上文对开发样本和验证样本的比较。"

msgid ""
"The standard errors measure the noise of sampling customers from one population. A shift of the "
"population over time is a separate question, which :doc:`psi` answers."
msgstr "标准误衡量的是从同一总体中抽取客户带来的噪声。总体随时间发生的偏移是另一个问题，由 :doc:`psi` 回答。"

msgid ""
"kivi gives no p-value for the KS statistic and no confidence bands for the ROC curve or the gains"
" table."
msgstr "kivi 不提供 KS 统计量的 p 值，也不提供 ROC 曲线或增益表的置信带。"

msgid ""
"A model in use is checked every month or quarter: does it still see the population that it was "
"developed on, and does it still rank the outcomes as it did? "
":func:`~kivi.monitoring.monitoring_table` answers both questions for a score in one table, with "
"one row per period: the number of observations, the events among the known outcomes, the AUC, "
"Gini and KS, and the PSI of the score against a reference sample. "
":func:`~kivi.monitoring.stability_table` gives the PSI of every variable of the model in every "
"period, to find the variables behind a shift."
msgstr ""
"使用中的模型每月或每季度都要检查：它面对的人群是否仍是开发时的人群？它对结果的排序是否仍和以前一样好？ :func:`~kivi.monitoring.monitoring_table` "
"用一张表回答评分的这两个问题，每期一行：观测数、已知结果中的事件数、AUC、Gini 和 KS，以及评分相对基准样本的 PSI。 "
":func:`~kivi.monitoring.stability_table` 给出模型每个变量在每一期的 PSI，用于找出造成偏移的变量。"

msgid ""
"Monitoring repeats the measures of :doc:`metrics` and of the :doc:`population stability index "
"<psi>` period by period, once the model is in production with its :doc:`binning specification "
"<spec>`. :doc:`vintage` then follows the loans that the model approves."
msgstr ""
"模型连同其 :doc:`分箱方案 <spec>` 投入生产后，监控按期重复 :doc:`metrics` 和 :doc:`群体稳定性指标 <psi>` 中的度量。随后 "
":doc:`vintage` 跟踪模型所通过的贷款。"

msgid ""
"Each row of the table describes the observations of one period, such as the applications of a "
"month. The outcome of an observation is known once its outcome window has ended, such as twelve "
"months after the loan was granted, and only if a loan was granted at all. The event rate of "
"period :math:`t` is that of its known outcomes,"
msgstr "表中每一行描述一期的观测，例如一个月的申请。观测的结果在其表现期结束后才能得知，例如放款后十二个月，而且只有获得贷款时才有结果。第 :math:`t` 期的事件率是其已知结果中的事件率，"

msgid "\\text{event rate}_t = \\frac{\\text{events}_t}{\\text{known outcomes}_t},"
msgstr "\\text{事件率}_t = \\frac{\\text{事件数}_t}{\\text{已知结果数}_t},"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"and the AUC, Gini and KS are those of :doc:`metrics`, computed on the known outcomes of the "
"period alone. The stability of the score is the PSI over score bands whose edges are fitted once "
"on the reference scores, so that every period is compared on the same bands. With :math:`q_i` the"
" share of the reference scores in band :math:`i` and :math:`p_{t,i}` that of the scores of period"
" :math:`t`, both smoothed as in :doc:`psi`,"
msgstr ""
"AUC、Gini 和 KS 与 :doc:`metrics` 中的相同，只在该期的已知结果上计算。评分的稳定性是评分段上的 "
"PSI，评分段边界只在基准评分上拟合一次，因此每一期都在同一组评分段上比较。记 :math:`q_i` 为基准评分落在评分段 :math:`i` 的占比， :math:`p_{t,i}` 为第 "
":math:`t` 期评分的相应占比，二者都按 :doc:`psi` 中的方法平滑，则"

msgid "\\mathrm{PSI}_t = \\sum_i (p_{t,i} - q_i) \\ln \\frac{p_{t,i}}{q_i}."
msgstr "\\mathrm{PSI}_t = \\sum_i (p_{t,i} - q_i) \\ln \\frac{p_{t,i}}{q_i}."

msgid ""
"The reference is either one of the periods, often the first after development, passed as "
"``reference_period``, or a separate sample, usually the development sample itself, passed as "
"``reference_score``. The PSI does not use the outcomes, so it is available as soon as the scores "
"of a period are. As in :doc:`metrics`, the score rises with the risk: pass a PD as it is and "
"negate scorecard points."
msgstr ""
"基准可以是其中一期，通常是开发之后的第一期，以 ``reference_period`` 传入；也可以是单独的样本，通常就是开发样本本身，以 ``reference_score`` 传入。PSI"
" 不使用结果，因此一期的评分一出来就可以计算。与 :doc:`metrics` 中一样，评分随风险升高：PD 直接传入，评分卡分数取负后传入。"

msgid ""
"Three months of four scores each, where two outcomes of March are not known yet. With ``bins=2``,"
" the median of the January scores, 0.25, splits the scores into two bands:"
msgstr "三个月、每月四个评分，其中 3 月有两个结果尚未得知。 ``bins=2`` 时，1 月评分的中位数 0.25 把评分分成两个评分段："

msgid ""
"January has two scores in each band, February one and three, and March none and four. The PSI of "
"February is :math:`(0.25 - 0.5) \\ln 0.5 + (0.75 - 0.5) \\ln 1.5 = 0.2747`. The empty band of "
"March is smoothed to 0.5, which gives the shares 0.5/4.5 and 4/4.5 and a PSI of 0.8087. In "
"February, the events 0.3 and 0.7 score higher than the non-events 0.2 and 0.6 in three of the "
"four pairs, so the AUC is 0.75. The two known outcomes of March, a non-event at 0.5 and an event "
"at 0.8, are ranked correctly."
msgstr ""
"1 月每个评分段各有两个评分，2 月分别为一个和三个，3 月分别为零个和四个。2 月的 PSI 为 :math:`(0.25 - 0.5) \\ln 0.5 + (0.75 - 0.5) "
"\\ln 1.5 = 0.2747` 。3 月的空评分段平滑为 0.5，得到占比 0.5/4.5 和 4/4.5，PSI 为 0.8087。2 月的事件 0.3 和 0.7 "
"在四对中有三对高于非事件 0.2 和 0.6，因此 AUC 为 0.75。3 月的两个已知结果，0.5 处的非事件和 0.8 处的事件，排序正确。"

msgid ""
"Twelve scores and targets in three months, split into two bands by the median of the January "
"scores, and the monitoring table with one row per month"
msgstr "三个月中的十二个评分和目标，按一月评分的中位数分为两个评分段，以及每月一行的监控表"

msgid ""
"The worked example. The median of the January scores splits every month into the same two bands, "
"and each month becomes one row of the table."
msgstr "计算示例。一月评分的中位数把每个月都分成同样的两个评分段，每个月成为表中的一行。"

msgid "A monitoring report"
msgstr "监控报告"

msgid ""
"The examples on this page use the synthetic applications of "
":func:`~kivi.datasets.make_applications`, scored by an incumbent scorecard whose PD is "
"``incumbent_pd``; see :doc:`datasets`. One sample of 10,000 applications is the development "
"sample, and a second one stands for the 24,000 applications of 2025, 2,000 a month. From October,"
" a marketing campaign aimed at permanent employees ends, and half of them no longer apply, which "
"changes the mix of applicants; the example leaves out half of the permanent employees of the last"
" quarter:"
msgstr ""
"本页示例使用 :func:`~kivi.datasets.make_applications` 生成的合成申请数据，由一张现行评分卡打分，其 PD 为 ``incumbent_pd`` ；见 "
":doc:`datasets` 。一份 10,000 笔申请的样本作为开发样本，另一份代表 2025 年的 24,000 笔申请，每月 2,000 笔。从 10 "
"月起，一项面向长期雇员的营销活动结束，其中一半不再申请，申请人的构成随之改变；示例去掉了最后一个季度一半的长期雇员："

msgid ""
"The outcome of an application is known only if it was approved, and only once its outcome window "
"has ended. At the end of the year, the applications up to September have outcomes and those of "
"the last quarter do not. Unknown outcomes are passed as missing values:"
msgstr "申请只有获批后才有结果，而且要等表现期结束。到年底时，9 月及之前的申请已有结果，最后一个季度的申请还没有。未知的结果以缺失值传入："

msgid ""
"The ten score bands are the deciles of the development scores, as :func:`~kivi.binning.bin_edges`"
" fits them, so the PSI of each month compares its scores with the development scores on the same "
"bands."
msgstr "十个评分段是开发样本评分的十分位组，由 :func:`~kivi.binning.bin_edges` 拟合，因此每个月的 PSI 都在同一组评分段上把该月评分与开发样本评分作比较。"

#, python-format
msgid ""
"The volume falls in the last quarter, when fewer permanent employees apply. The event rate stays "
"close to the 9.7% of the approved applications of the development sample, and the Gini "
"coefficient scatters around their value of 0.31:"
msgstr "最后一个季度申请的长期雇员减少，申请量随之下降。事件率始终接近开发样本中获批申请的 9.7%，Gini 系数在获批申请的 0.31 上下波动："

msgid ""
"Three panels by month: applications and known outcomes, the Gini coefficient with the development"
" value as a dashed line, and the PSI with the 0.1 and 0.25 thresholds"
msgstr "按月份的三个面板：申请数与已知结果数，Gini 系数及以虚线表示的开发样本值，以及带 0.1 和 0.25 阈值的 PSI"

msgid ""
"The monitoring report by month. Top: the applications and those with a known outcome; the last "
"quarter has none yet. Middle: the Gini coefficient of each month against the 0.309 of the "
"approved development applications. Bottom: the PSI against the development scores, far below the "
"0.1 and 0.25 thresholds also in the last quarter."
msgstr ""
"按月份的监控报告。上：申请数以及结果已知的申请数；最后一个季度还没有已知结果。中：每月的 Gini 系数，对照开发样本中已批准申请的 0.309。下：相对于开发样本评分的 "
"PSI，最后一个季度也远低于 0.1 和 0.25 两个阈值。"

msgid ""
"With about 130 events a month, the Gini coefficient of a single month moves by several points "
"from sampling noise alone, so read a trend over several months rather than one low value. The "
"last quarter has no known outcomes, and its discrimination is NaN."
msgstr "每月约 130 个事件，单月的 Gini 系数仅因抽样噪声就会波动几个百分点，因此应看几个月的趋势，而不是某一个偏低的值。最后一个季度没有已知结果，其区分能力为 NaN。"

msgid ""
"The PSI stays at about 0.01 or below up to September and rises to about 0.02 to 0.03 in the last "
"quarter: still a small shift by the usual thresholds. The mix of applicants has changed, but "
"employment is only one input of the score, so the score moves less than the population. The "
"variable report below shows which variables moved."
msgstr ""
"9 月之前 PSI 一直在 0.01 左右或更低，最后一个季度升到约 0.02 到 "
"0.03：按常用阈值仍属于小幅偏移。申请人的构成变了，但就业状况只是评分的输入之一，因此评分的变动小于人群的变动。下面的变量报告显示哪些变量发生了变化。"

msgid ""
"The reference can also be a period, such as the first month of the year. Its PSI is then 0, and "
"the other months are compared with it:"
msgstr "基准也可以是某一期，例如一年中的第一个月。此时该期的 PSI 为 0，其他月份都与它比较："

msgid "Observations in the period, including those whose outcome is not known yet."
msgstr "该期的观测数，包括结果尚未得知的观测。"

msgid "``known``, ``event``"
msgstr "``known`` 、 ``event``"

msgid "Observations with a known outcome, and the events among them."
msgstr "结果已知的观测数，以及其中的事件数。"

msgid "``event`` divided by ``known``, NaN without known outcomes."
msgstr "``event`` 除以 ``known`` ，没有已知结果时为 NaN。"

msgid "``auc``, ``gini``, ``ks``"
msgstr "``auc`` 、 ``gini`` 、 ``ks``"

msgid ""
"The discrimination of the score on the known outcomes of the period, NaN unless both classes are "
"present."
msgstr "评分在该期已知结果上的区分能力，两类结果不全时为 NaN。"

msgid "``psi``"
msgstr "``psi``"

msgid ""
"The PSI of the scores of the period against the reference scores, on bands fitted on the "
"reference."
msgstr "该期评分相对基准评分的 PSI，基于在基准上拟合的评分段。"

msgid ""
"Read each column against the development sample rather than against a fixed number. The "
"discrimination is measured on the approved applications only, whose scores the cut-off has "
"truncated, so it is lower than on all applicants: compare it with the development value of the "
"approved applications, as above. A falling Gini over several months means that the score ranks "
"the new outcomes less well than it did."
msgstr ""
"每一列都应与开发样本对照解读，而不是与某个固定数值比较。区分能力只在获批的申请上衡量，它们的评分已被截断点截断，因此低于在全部申请人上的值：应与开发样本中获批申请的数值比较，如上所示。Gini "
"连续几个月下降，说明评分对新结果的排序不如以前。"

msgid ""
"The PSI of the score follows the conventions of :doc:`psi`: below 0.1 a small shift, from 0.1 to "
"0.25 a moderate one and above 0.25 a large one. A shift of the score asks which variables moved "
"and whether the event rate moves with them. In a small period the PSI and the discrimination "
"mostly reflect sampling noise, so read them together with ``total`` and ``known``, and set a "
"minimum size before a value raises an alert."
msgstr ""
"评分的 PSI 沿用 :doc:`psi` 中的惯例：低于 0.1 为小幅偏移，0.1 到 0.25 为中等偏移，高于 0.25 "
"为大幅偏移。评分发生偏移时，要看是哪些变量变了，以及事件率是否随之变化。小样本期的 PSI 和区分能力主要反映抽样噪声，因此应结合 ``total`` 和 ``known`` "
"一起解读，并在用某个数值触发预警之前先设定最小样本量。"

msgid ""
"The two functions of this page keep every category of a categorical period as a row, also one "
"without observations, whose counts are 0 and whose other columns are NaN, so that the monthly "
"reports of different samples line up even when a month has no applications. "
":func:`~kivi.vintage.vintage_table` and :func:`~kivi.calibration.calibration_table` leave such "
"categories out, so join their tables to these by period label rather than by position. Periods "
"that are not categorical are the distinct values that occur, sorted."
msgstr ""
"本页的两个函数把分类型期的每个类别都保留为一行，包括没有观测的类别，其计数为 0，其他列为 NaN，因此即使某个月没有申请，不同样本的月度报告也能对齐。 "
":func:`~kivi.vintage.vintage_table` 和 :func:`~kivi.calibration.calibration_table` "
"会略去这样的类别，因此把它们的表与这里的表合并时，应按期的标签而不是按位置对齐。非分类型的期就是实际出现的不同取值，按升序排列。"

msgid "Variable stability"
msgstr "变量稳定性"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.monitoring.stability_table` takes the grouped variables of every period and gives "
"the PSI of each against the groups of the reference sample. Group both samples with the binning "
"specification fitted on the development sample, as in :doc:`spec`. ``inquiries`` gets explicit "
"edges because 0 is the most common value:"
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.monitoring.stability_table` 接收每一期已分组的变量，给出每个变量相对基准样本分组的 PSI。两个样本都用在开发样本上拟合的分箱方案分组，见 "
":doc:`spec` 。 ``inquiries`` 最常见的取值是 0，因此给定显式边界："

msgid ""
"Heatmap of the PSI of six variables in twelve months, coloured by the 0.1 and 0.25 thresholds, "
"with employment above 0.1 from October to December"
msgstr "六个变量在十二个月中的 PSI 热力图，按 0.1 和 0.25 阈值着色，employment 从 10 月到 12 月高于 0.1"

msgid ""
"PSI of each variable of the model in each month, coloured by the 0.1 and 0.25 thresholds. Only "
"``employment`` crosses 0.1, from October, when half of the permanent employees no longer apply."
msgstr "模型各变量在每个月的 PSI，按 0.1 和 0.25 阈值着色。只有 ``employment`` 从 10 月起超过 0.1，因为此时一半的长期雇员不再申请。"

msgid ""
"Every variable stays below 0.01 up to September. From October, ``employment`` rises above 0.1, a "
"moderate shift, while the other variables do not move: the report points at the change of mix "
"before any outcomes of the new applicants are known. Each entry is the PSI of "
":func:`~kivi.stability.psi_table` for the month alone, which shows the groups that moved:"
msgstr ""
"9 月之前每个变量都低于 0.01。从 10 月起， ``employment`` 升到 0.1 "
"以上，属于中等偏移，其他变量则没有变化：在新申请人的任何结果出来之前，报告就已经指向了构成的变化。每个值都是仅对该月计算的 :func:`~kivi.stability.psi_table` 的"
" PSI，后者显示哪些组发生了变化："

msgid ""
"The share of permanent employees has fallen from 65% to 49%. Whether the new mix defaults as the "
"score expects shows only when its outcomes are known; follow the event rate of the last quarter "
"closely as they arrive."
msgstr "长期雇员的占比从 65% 降到 49%。新的构成下违约是否符合评分的预期，要等结果已知后才能看出；结果陆续出来时，应密切跟踪最后一个季度的事件率。"

msgid ""
"A missing target is an outcome that is not known yet. Most functions raise an error for a missing"
" label, as :doc:`/api/conventions` describes; :func:`~kivi.monitoring.monitoring_table` reads it "
"as an unknown outcome, as :func:`~kivi.strategy.swap_set` does. It counts in ``total`` but not in"
" ``known``, ``event``, ``event_rate`` or the discrimination, so pass the outcomes that are not "
"yet observed as missing values rather than as 0. A period without both classes among its known "
"outcomes, such as the last quarter above, gets NaN discrimination instead of an error."
msgstr ""
"缺失的目标值表示结果尚未得知。大多数函数遇到缺失标签会报错，见 :doc:`/api/conventions` ； "
":func:`~kivi.monitoring.monitoring_table` 则与 :func:`~kivi.strategy.swap_set` 一样，把它视为未知结果。它计入 "
"``total`` ，但不计入 ``known`` 、 ``event`` 、 ``event_rate`` 和区分能力，因此尚未观测到的结果应以缺失值而不是 0 "
"传入。已知结果中两类结果不全的期（例如上面的最后一个季度）的区分能力为 NaN，而不是报错。"

msgid ""
"A missing score or a missing period raises an error: a missing score has no band and no rank, and"
" an observation without a period has no row."
msgstr "缺失的评分或缺失的期会报错：缺失的评分没有评分段也没有排序，没有期的观测也没有所属的行。"

msgid ""
"In :func:`~kivi.monitoring.stability_table`, a missing value is a group of its own, as in "
":func:`~kivi.stability.psi_table`, and groups observed in only one of the two samples are "
"included."
msgstr ""
"在 :func:`~kivi.monitoring.stability_table` 中，缺失值单独成组，与 :func:`~kivi.stability.psi_table` "
"相同；只在两个样本之一中出现的组也会包含在内。"

msgid ""
"Both functions take ``weights``, one non-negative weight per observation, and "
"``reference_weights`` for a reference sample passed as ``reference_score`` or "
"``reference_groups``; a reference period takes its weights from ``weights``. Counts become sums "
"of weights, as :doc:`/api/conventions` describes for every function, and the discrimination and "
"the PSI are weighted. On the same band edges, integer weights give the same table as repeating "
"rows. An integer ``bins`` fits the edges by weighted quantiles, as "
":func:`~kivi.binning.bin_edges` does, so its edges can differ from those of the repeated rows."
msgstr ""
"两个函数都接受 ``weights`` （每个观测一个非负权重），以及以 ``reference_score`` 或 ``reference_groups`` 传入的基准样本的 "
"``reference_weights`` ；基准期的权重取自 ``weights`` 。计数变为权重之和，这与 :doc:`/api/conventions` 对所有函数的约定相同，区分能力和"
" PSI 也按权重计算。在相同的评分段边界上，整数权重与重复相应行得到的表相同。整数 ``bins`` 按加权分位数拟合边界，与 :func:`~kivi.binning.bin_edges` "
"相同，因此其边界可能与重复相应行时的边界不同。"

msgid ""
"Monitoring samples often keep every event but only some of the non-events. Below, every "
"application with an event or an unknown outcome is kept, but only a quarter of the known non-"
"events, which get a weight of 4:"
msgstr "监控样本常常保留全部事件，但只保留部分非事件。下面保留每一笔有事件或结果未知的申请，但已知的非事件只保留四分之一，并给它们权重 4："

msgid ""
"The sample overstates the event rate threefold, and the weights restore it to that of all "
"applications, up to sampling noise."
msgstr "抽样后样本的事件率约为全部申请的三倍，加上权重后则恢复到全部申请的水平，差异只在抽样噪声之内。"

msgid ""
"The PSI shows that the scores have moved, not whether the score still ranks or predicts the "
"outcomes. The outcomes arrive only after the outcome window, so the discrimination of the latest "
"periods is missing or rests on few outcomes."
msgstr "PSI 显示评分发生了变动，但不能说明评分是否仍能排序或预测结果。结果要在表现期结束后才会出现，因此最近几期的区分能力要么缺失，要么只基于很少的结果。"

msgid ""
"The table has no confidence intervals or tests. Judge a change of the Gini coefficient or the PSI"
" against the size of the period, or compare periods of similar size."
msgstr "表中没有置信区间或检验。判断 Gini 系数或 PSI 的变化时要考虑该期的样本量，或者比较样本量相近的期。"

msgid ""
"The table does not check calibration. Pass the period as the groups of "
":func:`~kivi.calibration.calibration_table`, with the rows whose outcomes are known, to compare "
"the predicted and observed default rates of each period."
msgstr "表中不检查校准。把期作为 :func:`~kivi.calibration.calibration_table` 的分组，并只传入结果已知的行，即可比较每一期的预测违约率和观测违约率。"

msgid ""
"The change of the average score that each variable causes is its CSI, from "
":func:`~kivi.stability.csi_table`, computed for one period at a time."
msgstr "每个变量对平均评分的影响是其 CSI，由 :func:`~kivi.stability.csi_table` 逐期计算。"

msgid ""
"An integer ``bins`` fits quantile edges on the reference scores. When many reference scores are "
"tied, as for a score rounded to one decimal, the edges coincide and fewer bands remain. A "
"``UserWarning`` says so, and every period is compared on the bands that remain:"
msgstr ""
"整数 ``bins`` 在基准评分上拟合分位数边界。许多基准评分并列时（例如评分只保留一位小数），边界会重合，剩下的评分段就会变少。此时会发出 ``UserWarning`` "
"，每一期都在剩下的评分段上比较："

msgid ""
"Pass fewer bins or explicit edges, such as those of the development report, to remove the "
"warning. Explicit edges must cover every score, so use infinite outer edges; a score outside them"
" raises an error."
msgstr "传入更少的箱数或显式边界（例如开发报告中的边界）即可消除警告。显式边界必须覆盖所有评分，因此两端应使用无穷边界；落在边界之外的评分会报错。"

msgid ""
"The reference is ``reference_period`` or ``reference_score``, or ``reference_groups`` for "
":func:`~kivi.monitoring.stability_table`; passing neither or both raises an error. A "
"``reference_period`` that is not one of the periods raises an error that lists the first periods:"
msgstr ""
"基准以 ``reference_period`` 或 ``reference_score`` 给出， :func:`~kivi.monitoring.stability_table` 则用 "
"``reference_groups`` ；两者都不给或同时给出都会报错。不是其中一期的 ``reference_period`` 会报错，并列出前几期："

msgid ""
"A list of labels is not a period label, and a boolean mask of the reference rows is not a sample "
"of scores, so both raise an error too. Pass the scores of the reference rows, such as "
"``score[mask]``, as ``reference_score``."
msgstr "标签列表不是期的标签，基准行的布尔掩码也不是评分样本，因此二者同样会报错。应把基准行的评分（例如 ``score[mask]`` ）作为 ``reference_score`` 传入。"

msgid ""
"A risk report shows its tables as charts: the event rate of each bin, the ROC curve of a score, "
"the shares that moved since development. :mod:`kivi.plotting` draws the result tables of the "
"other modules with matplotlib, one function per table: :func:`~kivi.plotting.woe_chart` for a WOE"
" table, :func:`~kivi.plotting.correlation_chart` for a correlation matrix, "
":func:`~kivi.plotting.roc_chart` and :func:`~kivi.plotting.gains_chart` for the ROC and gains "
"tables, :func:`~kivi.plotting.calibration_chart` for a calibration table, "
":func:`~kivi.plotting.cutoff_chart` for a cut-off table, :func:`~kivi.plotting.psi_chart` for a "
"PSI table, :func:`~kivi.plotting.monitoring_chart` for a monitoring report and "
":func:`~kivi.plotting.vintage_chart` for a vintage table."
msgstr ""
"风险报告用图表展示各种表：每个分箱的事件率、评分的 ROC 曲线、自开发以来发生变化的占比。 :mod:`kivi.plotting` 用 matplotlib "
"绘制其他模块的结果表，每种表对应一个函数：WOE 表用 :func:`~kivi.plotting.woe_chart` ，相关系数矩阵用 "
":func:`~kivi.plotting.correlation_chart` ，ROC 表和增益表用 :func:`~kivi.plotting.roc_chart` 和 "
":func:`~kivi.plotting.gains_chart` ，校准表用 :func:`~kivi.plotting.calibration_chart` ，截断点表用 "
":func:`~kivi.plotting.cutoff_chart` ，PSI 表用 :func:`~kivi.plotting.psi_chart` ，监控报告用 "
":func:`~kivi.plotting.monitoring_chart` ，Vintage 表用 :func:`~kivi.plotting.vintage_chart` 。"

msgid ""
"The charts draw the tables of the earlier guides, from :doc:`woe_iv` to :doc:`vintage`, so this "
"page comes last in the user guide, after :doc:`lifetime`."
msgstr "这些图表绘制的是前面各篇指南中的表，从 :doc:`woe_iv` 到 :doc:`vintage` ，因此本页放在用户指南的最后，位于 :doc:`lifetime` 之后。"

msgid "matplotlib is an optional dependency of kivi. Install it with the ``plot`` extra:"
msgstr "matplotlib 是 kivi 的可选依赖。通过 ``plot`` 可选依赖组安装："

msgid "The other modules do not need it, and :mod:`kivi.plotting` imports it only when a chart is drawn."
msgstr "其他模块不需要它， :mod:`kivi.plotting` 也只在绘制图表时才导入它。"

msgid ""
"A chart draws the values of its table and nothing else. Ten observations, nine in three groups "
"and one missing, give this WOE table:"
msgstr "图表只绘制其表中的数值，别无其他。十个观测值，其中九个分属三个分组，一个缺失，得到如下 WOE 表："

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.plotting.woe_chart` is the one chart with two y-axes, and so the one that returns "
"two Axes: one for the bars, with the left y-axis, and one for the line, which shares the x-axis "
"of the bars and has a y-axis of its own on the right. The bars are the ``total_share`` column, "
"the line is the ``event_rate`` column, the tick labels are the groups of the index, and the "
"legend gives the sum of the ``iv`` column:"
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.plotting.woe_chart` 是唯一带有两个 y 轴的图表，因此也是唯一返回两个 Axes 的图表：一个用于柱形，对应左侧 y 轴；一个用于折线，与柱形共用 "
"x 轴，并在右侧有自己的 y 轴。柱形是 ``total_share`` 列，折线是 ``event_rate`` 列，刻度标签是索引中的分组，图例给出 ``iv`` 列之和："

msgid "Bars of the share of groups a, b, c and NaN with a line of their event rates"
msgstr "分组 a、b、c 和 NaN 的占比柱形及其事件率折线"

#, python-format
msgid ""
"The bars read 20%, 40%, 30% and 10% on the left axis, and the line 50%, 25%, 67% and 0% on the "
"right axis."
msgstr "柱形在左轴上分别为 20%、40%、30% 和 10%，折线在右轴上分别为 50%、25%、67% 和 0%。"

msgid "Figures and axes"
msgstr "图形与坐标轴"

msgid ""
"Every function takes an optional ``ax``. Without it, the function creates a figure of its own, "
"sized for the chart and with matplotlib's constrained layout. With it, the function draws on that"
" Axes, so that several charts can share one figure:"
msgstr ""
"每个函数都接受可选参数 ``ax`` 。不传入时，函数自行新建一个图形，尺寸适合该图表，并使用 matplotlib 的 constrained 布局；传入时，函数在该 Axes "
"上作图，这样多个图表可以共用一个图形："

msgid ""
"Each function returns the Axes it drew on, ``ax`` when it is given, so that titles, limits and "
"labels can be changed afterwards with matplotlib, as in ``right.set_title(\"woe\")``. "
":func:`~kivi.plotting.woe_chart` returns the Axes of the bars and that of the line, which is why "
"the figure above has four Axes."
msgstr ""
"每个函数都返回所绘制的 Axes（给出 ``ax`` 时即为 ``ax`` ），以便之后用 matplotlib 修改标题、坐标范围和标签，例如 "
"``right.set_title(\"woe\")`` 。 :func:`~kivi.plotting.woe_chart` 返回柱形的 Axes 和折线的 Axes，所以上面的图形有四个 "
"Axes。"

msgid ""
"The functions never call ``matplotlib.pyplot.show``, never change ``matplotlib.rcParams`` and "
"never modify the table. Save a figure with ``figure.savefig(\"woe.png\")``, or show it with "
"``plt.show()`` outside a notebook. The curves that can be compared on one ``ax``, those of "
":func:`~kivi.plotting.roc_chart`, :func:`~kivi.plotting.gains_chart`, "
":func:`~kivi.plotting.calibration_chart`, :func:`~kivi.plotting.cutoff_chart` and "
":func:`~kivi.plotting.monitoring_chart`, take the next color of the Axes' color cycle. The other "
"charts use fixed colors. Fonts, grids and spines follow the active matplotlib style, so a style "
"set with ``plt.style.context`` applies to the charts drawn inside it."
msgstr ""
"这些函数从不调用 ``matplotlib.pyplot.show`` ，从不修改 ``matplotlib.rcParams`` ，也从不修改传入的表。用 "
"``figure.savefig(\"woe.png\")`` 保存图形，在 notebook 之外用 ``plt.show()`` 显示图形。可以在同一个 ``ax`` 上比较的曲线，即 "
":func:`~kivi.plotting.roc_chart` 、 :func:`~kivi.plotting.gains_chart` 、 "
":func:`~kivi.plotting.calibration_chart` 、 :func:`~kivi.plotting.cutoff_chart` 和 "
":func:`~kivi.plotting.monitoring_chart` 的曲线，使用 Axes 颜色循环中的下一种颜色；其他图表使用固定的颜色。字体、网格线和坐标轴边框遵循当前的 "
"matplotlib 样式，因此用 ``plt.style.context`` 设置的样式会作用于其中绘制的图表。"

msgid ""
"Text inside a chart is limited to column names, such as ``total_share`` and ``event_rate``, and "
"data values, such as the group labels and the IV. Each axis is labeled with the columns it shows,"
" or with the name of the index for the groups and periods. The same chart therefore suits a "
"report in any language; add titles in the language of the report."
msgstr ""
"图表中的文字只有列名（例如 ``total_share`` 和 ``event_rate`` ）和数据值（例如分组标签和 "
"IV）。每个坐标轴以其所示的列为标签，分组和各期所在的坐标轴则以索引的名称为标签。因此同一张图表适用于任何语言的报告；标题请用报告的语言另行添加。"

msgid ""
"Legends are placed so that they cover no data: :func:`~kivi.plotting.woe_chart` and "
":func:`~kivi.plotting.psi_chart` leave room for theirs at the top of the Axes, and "
":func:`~kivi.plotting.vintage_chart` and :func:`~kivi.plotting.monitoring_chart` put theirs to "
"the right of the Axes."
msgstr ""
"图例的位置不会遮挡数据： :func:`~kivi.plotting.woe_chart` 和 :func:`~kivi.plotting.psi_chart` 在 Axes "
"顶部为图例留出空间， :func:`~kivi.plotting.vintage_chart` 和 :func:`~kivi.plotting.monitoring_chart` 则把图例放在 "
"Axes 的右侧。"

msgid "WOE and event rate"
msgstr "WOE 与事件率"

msgid ""
"The examples from here on use the bundled bank data, split as in :doc:`risk_workflow` into a "
"development sample of 3,000 rows and a validation sample of 1,521 rows. A "
":class:`~kivi.spec.BinningSpec` bins five columns on the development sample:"
msgstr ""
"从这里开始，示例使用内置的银行数据，并像 :doc:`risk_workflow` 中那样分为 3,000 行的开发样本和 1,521 行的验证样本。一个 "
":class:`~kivi.spec.BinningSpec` 在开发样本上对五列分箱："

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.plotting.woe_chart` draws one of its tables in the order of the table. The bins of a"
" numeric column are already in order; sort the groups of a categorical column, for example by "
"WOE, and draw the WOE as the line with ``line=\"woe\"``:"
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.plotting.woe_chart` 按表中的顺序绘制其中一张表。数值列的分箱本身已经有序；类别列的分组可以先排序（例如按 WOE），再用 "
"``line=\"woe\"`` 把 WOE 画成折线："

msgid "Share and event rate of the age bins, and share and WOE of the poutcome groups"
msgstr "age 各分箱的占比与事件率，以及 poutcome 各分组的占比与 WOE"

msgid ""
"Left: the event rate of age is lowest in the middle bins. Right: four fifths of the customers "
"have an unknown previous outcome, and the few with a previous success have by far the highest "
"WOE."
msgstr "左：age 的事件率在中间几个分箱最低。右：五分之四的客户上次营销结果未知，而少数上次营销成功的客户 WOE 远高于其他分组。"

msgid ""
"Read the bars and the line together: a bin with a high event rate matters more when it holds many"
" customers. The bars use the left axis and the line the right axis, which starts at 0 for "
"``event_rate`` and includes 0 for ``woe``."
msgstr "柱形和折线要结合起来看：事件率高的分箱，客户越多就越重要。柱形使用左轴，折线使用右轴；右轴对 ``event_rate`` 从 0 开始，对 ``woe`` 则包含 0。"

msgid "Correlation"
msgstr "相关性"

msgid ""
"Before :doc:`selection`, :func:`~kivi.plotting.correlation_chart` shows which WOE-encoded "
"candidates carry the same information. It takes a correlation matrix, such as the result of "
"``DataFrame.corr``, rather than the data, so that any method of correlation can be drawn:"
msgstr ""
"在 :doc:`selection` 之前， :func:`~kivi.plotting.correlation_chart` 展示哪些 WOE "
"编码后的候选变量携带相同的信息。它接受的是相关系数矩阵（例如 ``DataFrame.corr`` 的结果）而不是原始数据，因此可以绘制任何一种相关系数："

msgid "Heatmap of the correlations between the WOE values of five columns"
msgstr "五列 WOE 值之间相关系数的热力图"

msgid "The largest correlation between two different columns is 0.21, between housing and contact."
msgstr "不同两列之间最大的相关系数是 housing 与 contact 之间的 0.21。"

msgid ""
"Each cell shows its value, blue for a positive correlation and amber for a negative one, darker "
"towards 1 and -1. The colors always span -1 to 1, so charts of different samples compare "
"directly, and a value outside that range, as in a covariance matrix, raises an error. For "
"Spearman's rank correlation, pass ``woe.corr(method=\"spearman\")``."
msgstr ""
"每个单元格标出其数值，正相关为蓝色，负相关为琥珀色，越接近 1 和 -1 颜色越深。颜色总是覆盖 -1 到 "
"1，因此不同样本的图表可以直接比较；超出这一范围的值（例如协方差矩阵中的值）会引发错误。要使用 Spearman 秩相关系数，请传入 "
"``woe.corr(method=\"spearman\")`` 。"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.plotting.roc_chart` draws a :func:`~kivi.metrics.roc_table`. The score below adds up"
" the WOE values of the five columns, so that it is higher for a higher risk, as :doc:`metrics` "
"requires. A second call with the same ``ax`` adds the curve of ``poutcome`` alone, and ``label`` "
"names both curves in the legend:"
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.plotting.roc_chart` 绘制 :func:`~kivi.metrics.roc_table` 的结果。下面的评分把五列的 WOE "
"值相加，因此风险越高评分越高，符合 :doc:`metrics` 的要求。用同一个 ``ax`` 再调用一次，加上只用 ``poutcome`` 的曲线， ``label`` "
"在图例中为两条曲线命名："

msgid "ROC curves of the WOE score and of poutcome alone, with the KS of the score marked"
msgstr "WOE 评分与单独 poutcome 的 ROC 曲线，并标出评分的 KS"

msgid ""
"The score lies above the curve of poutcome alone at most false positive rates. The dotted segment"
" marks its KS of 0.299."
msgstr "在大多数假正率下，评分的曲线都高于单独 poutcome 的曲线。点线段标出评分的 KS，为 0.299。"

msgid ""
"The dotted segment marks the KS statistic, the largest gap between ``true_positive_rate`` and "
"``false_positive_rate``, which equals :func:`~kivi.metrics.ks` of the score. Each curve takes the"
" next color of the Axes, and its KS segment shares its color; pass ``ks=False`` for the curves "
"whose KS is not needed."
msgstr ""
"点线段标出 KS 统计量，即 ``true_positive_rate`` 与 ``false_positive_rate`` 之间的最大差距，它等于该评分的 "
":func:`~kivi.metrics.ks` 。每条曲线使用 Axes 的下一种颜色，其 KS 线段与曲线同色；不需要 KS 的曲线请传入 ``ks=False`` 。"

msgid "Gains and KS"
msgstr "增益与 KS"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.plotting.gains_chart` draws a :func:`~kivi.metrics.gains_table`: the shares of all "
"events and of all non-events in the bands reviewed so far, from the highest band down, against "
"the share of the sample reviewed:"
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.plotting.gains_chart` 绘制 :func:`~kivi.metrics.gains_table` "
"的结果：从最高的评分段向下，到目前为止已审视的评分段中的事件和非事件分别占全部事件和全部非事件的比例，横轴是已审视的样本占比："

msgid "Cumulative event and non-event shares of ten score bands, with the largest gap marked"
msgstr "十个评分段的累计事件占比与非事件占比，并标出最大差距"

#, python-format
msgid ""
"The riskiest 30% of the validation sample holds 54% of its events and 27% of its non-events, the "
"largest gap of the ten bands."
msgstr "验证样本中风险最高的 30% 包含了 54% 的事件和 27% 的非事件，这是十个评分段中最大的差距。"

msgid ""
"The solid ``cum_event_share`` curve lies above the diagonal and the dashed "
"``cum_non_event_share`` curve below it when the score ranks well. The dotted segment marks the "
"band with the largest ``ks``. The KS of the bands is at most that of "
":func:`~kivi.plotting.roc_chart`, which compares every score rather than the band edges. As in "
":func:`~kivi.plotting.roc_chart`, ``ks=False`` leaves the segment out, and ``label`` names the "
"score in the legend, so that the gains of several scores can be drawn on one ``ax``."
msgstr ""
"评分排序良好时，实线 ``cum_event_share`` 曲线位于对角线上方，虚线 ``cum_non_event_share`` 曲线位于下方。点线段标出 ``ks`` "
"最大的评分段。各评分段的 KS 至多等于 :func:`~kivi.plotting.roc_chart` 中的 KS，后者比较的是每个评分而不只是评分段的边界。与 "
":func:`~kivi.plotting.roc_chart` 一样， ``ks=False`` 不画这条线段， ``label`` 在图例中为评分命名，因此可以在同一个 ``ax`` "
"上绘制多个评分的增益曲线。"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.plotting.calibration_chart` draws a :func:`~kivi.calibration.calibration_table`. "
"Below, :func:`~kivi.calibration.platt_fit` turns the score into PDs on the development sample, "
"and the validation PDs are grouped into the grades of a :func:`~kivi.calibration.master_scale`, "
"as in :doc:`calibration`:"
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.plotting.calibration_chart` 绘制 :func:`~kivi.calibration.calibration_table` "
"的结果。下面先在开发样本上用 :func:`~kivi.calibration.platt_fit` 把评分转换为 PD，再像 :doc:`calibration` 中那样，把验证样本的 PD "
"分入 :func:`~kivi.calibration.master_scale` 的各个等级："

msgid "Event rate against mean predicted probability of grades A to E, next to the diagonal"
msgstr "等级 A 到 E 的事件率与平均预测概率，以及对角线"

msgid "The five grades lie close to the diagonal; grade D has fewer events than predicted."
msgstr "五个等级都贴近对角线；等级 D 的事件少于预测。"

msgid ""
"Points above the diagonal have more events than predicted, and points below it fewer. Both axes "
"run from 0 to just above the largest rate, so that the diagonal stays at 45 degrees. The chart "
"shows how far each grade lies from its prediction, not whether the difference is significant; "
":func:`~kivi.calibration.binomial_test` answers that."
msgstr ""
"位于对角线上方的点事件多于预测，位于下方的点事件少于预测。两个坐标轴都从 0 延伸到略高于最大比率，使对角线保持 45 度。图表展示每个等级偏离预测的程度，但不说明差异是否显著；这个问题由 "
":func:`~kivi.calibration.binomial_test` 回答。"

msgid "Cut-offs"
msgstr "截断点"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.plotting.cutoff_chart` draws a :func:`~kivi.strategy.cutoff_table`: the bad rate of "
"the approved book against the share of applicants approved, one point per cut-off of the PD:"
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.plotting.cutoff_chart` 绘制 :func:`~kivi.strategy.cutoff_table` "
"的结果：通过客群的坏账率随通过申请人占比的变化，PD 的每个截断点对应一个点："

msgid "Event rate of the approved book against the approval rate for twenty PD cut-offs"
msgstr "二十个 PD 截断点下通过客群的事件率与通过率"

#, python-format
msgid ""
"Approving more applicants raises the event rate of the approved book, from about 1% for the "
"safest 5% of applicants to 11% when all of them are approved."
msgstr "通过的申请人越多，通过客群的事件率越高：只通过最安全的 5% 申请人时约为 1%，全部通过时为 11%。"

msgid ""
"The slope of the curve is the price in risk of a higher approval rate. Draw the tables of a "
"current and a new score on the same ``ax``, each with a ``label``, to compare them at the same "
"approval rate, as :doc:`strategy` does."
msgstr "曲线的斜率就是提高通过率所付出的风险代价。把现行评分和新评分的表画在同一个 ``ax`` 上并各自给出 ``label`` ，就能像 :doc:`strategy` 那样在相同通过率下比较二者。"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.plotting.psi_chart` draws a :func:`~kivi.stability.psi_table` as pairs of bars, the "
"reference share and the current share of each group. Single customers, as in :doc:`psi`, are much"
" younger than the development sample:"
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.plotting.psi_chart` 把 :func:`~kivi.stability.psi_table` 的结果画成成对的柱形，即每个分组的基准占比和当前占比。与"
" :doc:`psi` 中一样，单身客户比开发样本年轻得多："

msgid "Reference and current shares of five age bins for single customers"
msgstr "单身客户在五个 age 分箱中的基准占比与当前占比"

msgid ""
"Half of the single customers fall into the youngest bin, against less than a quarter of the "
"development sample."
msgstr "一半的单身客户落在最年轻的分箱中，而开发样本中这一比例不到四分之一。"

msgid ""
"The groups whose bars differ most contribute most of the PSI, which the legend gives for the "
"whole table."
msgstr "两根柱形相差最大的分组对 PSI 的贡献最大；图例给出整张表的 PSI。"

msgid "Monitoring"
msgstr "监控"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.plotting.monitoring_chart` draws one column of a "
":func:`~kivi.monitoring.monitoring_table` period by period. The applications below are simulated "
"as in :doc:`monitoring`; the outcomes of the last three months are not known yet:"
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.plotting.monitoring_chart` 逐期绘制 :func:`~kivi.monitoring.monitoring_table` "
"中的一列。下面的申请数据像 :doc:`monitoring` 中那样模拟生成；最后三个月的结果尚未可知："

msgid ""
"Call the function once for each column, on the panels of one figure. ``kind`` draws a column as a"
" line, the default, or as bars, and ``levels`` marks the values that a column is compared with, "
"such as the PSI thresholds 0.1 and 0.25. ``label_outer`` then hides the x-axis labels of the "
"upper panel, which shares the x-axis of the lower one:"
msgstr ""
"对每一列各调用一次此函数，画在同一图形的不同子图上。 ``kind`` 把一列绘制为折线（默认）或柱形， ``levels`` 标出与该列比较的数值，例如 PSI 阈值 0.1 和 "
"0.25。随后用 ``label_outer`` 隐藏上方子图的 x 轴标签，因为它与下方子图共用 x 轴："

msgid "Gini and PSI of the incumbent PD for each month of 2025, with the PSI thresholds 0.1 and 0.25"
msgstr "现行 PD 在 2025 年每个月的 Gini 和 PSI，以及 PSI 阈值 0.1 和 0.25"

msgid ""
"The Gini stops in September, the last month with known outcomes. The PSI stays far below 0.1 in "
"every month."
msgstr "Gini 止于 9 月，这是最后一个结果已知的月份。每个月的 PSI 都远低于 0.1。"

msgid ""
"A line suits rates and measures of discrimination, and several columns on one ``ax``; bars suit "
"counts such as ``total`` and a single ``psi``. ``kind`` decides, not the name of the column, so "
"any table with one row per period can be drawn either way."
msgstr ""
"折线适合比率和区分能力指标，也适合在同一个 ``ax`` 上绘制多列；柱形适合 ``total`` 等计数和单独的 ``psi`` 。决定画法的是 ``kind`` "
"而不是列名，因此任何每期一行的表都可以用两种方式绘制。"

msgid ""
"A :func:`~kivi.monitoring.stability_table` holds the PSI of each variable by period. Draw its "
"columns on one ``ax``, each with a ``label``. The y-axis is labeled ``psi``, because the columns "
"of a stability table are named ``variable``:"
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.monitoring.stability_table` 给出每个变量逐期的 PSI。把它的各列画在同一个 ``ax`` 上，每列带一个 ``label`` "
"。由于稳定性表的列名为 ``variable`` ，y 轴的标签为 ``psi`` ："

msgid "PSI of age, income and debt_to_income for each month of 2025"
msgstr "age、income 和 debt_to_income 在 2025 年每个月的 PSI"

msgid "The PSI of the three variables stays below 0.01 in every month."
msgstr "三个变量的 PSI 在每个月都低于 0.01。"

msgid "Vintage curves"
msgstr "vintage 曲线"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.plotting.vintage_chart` draws a :func:`~kivi.vintage.vintage_table` with one curve "
"per cohort, later cohorts in darker blue. The legend, to the right of the Axes, names eight of "
"the twenty-four cohorts, evenly spread from the first to the last, since the shades of the others"
" lie between theirs:"
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.plotting.vintage_chart` 为 :func:`~kivi.vintage.vintage_table` "
"的每个批次绘制一条曲线，越晚的批次蓝色越深。位于 Axes 右侧的图例从二十四个批次中列出八个，从第一个到最后一个均匀分布，其余批次的颜色深浅介于它们之间："

msgid "Cumulative 90+ rate of twenty-four cohorts by month on book"
msgstr "二十四个批次按账龄的累计 90+ 比率"

msgid ""
"No cohort has a loan 90 days past due before its fourth month on book, and the curves of the "
"later cohorts end where their observation ends."
msgstr "在第四个账龄月之前，没有任何批次出现逾期 90 天的贷款；较晚批次的曲线在其观测结束处终止。"

msgid ""
"A cohort whose curve rises above those of the cohorts before it is worth a closer look. The "
"function takes any table of the same shape, such as the cumulative PDs of "
":func:`~kivi.lifetime.convert_pd`."
msgstr "如果某个批次的曲线升到之前各批次的曲线之上，就值得仔细查看。此函数接受任何形状相同的表，例如 :func:`~kivi.lifetime.convert_pd` 给出的累计 PD。"

msgid ""
"A special value keeps the group that :func:`~kivi.binning.cut` gave it, and the chart labels it "
"with its code. For ``pdays``, where -1 means that the customer was not contacted before:"
msgstr "特殊值保留 :func:`~kivi.binning.cut` 赋予它的分组，图表用其编码作为标签。以 ``pdays`` 为例，-1 表示此前没有联系过该客户："

#, python-format
msgid ""
"The bar of ``-1`` holds 82.5% of the sample. Charts do not reorder groups, so the special group "
"stays where the table has it, ahead of the intervals."
msgstr "``-1`` 的柱形占样本的 82.5%。图表不会重排分组，因此特殊值分组保持在表中的位置，即各区间之前。"

msgid ""
"The group of missing values is labeled ``NaN``, as in the worked example. A missing value in a "
"column, such as the ``gini`` of a month without known outcomes or a month on book that a cohort "
"has not reached, leaves a gap in a line and no bar. A cut-off that approves nothing has a missing"
" ``approved_event_rate`` and no point on the curve of :func:`~kivi.plotting.cutoff_chart`."
msgstr ""
"与计算示例中一样，缺失值分组标为 ``NaN`` 。列中的缺失值（例如没有已知结果的月份的 ``gini`` "
"，或某个批次尚未到达的账龄月）会在折线上留下缺口，也不画柱形。不通过任何申请人的截断点，其 ``approved_event_rate`` 缺失，在 "
":func:`~kivi.plotting.cutoff_chart` 的曲线上没有对应的点。"

msgid ""
"The charts draw a table as it is. They have no ``weights`` argument: draw a table computed with "
"weights to show weighted shares and rates."
msgstr "图表按原样绘制表。它们没有 ``weights`` 参数：要展示加权的占比和比率，请绘制用权重计算的表。"

msgid ""
"The functions choose the size of a new figure, the colors and the labels, and pass no other "
"matplotlib properties through; change them on the returned Axes."
msgstr "新图形的尺寸、颜色和标签由函数决定，函数也不转发其他 matplotlib 属性；请在返回的 Axes 上修改它们。"

msgid "A chart has no title, so that it fits a report in any language. Add one with ``ax.set_title``."
msgstr "图表不带标题，以便适用于任何语言的报告。可以用 ``ax.set_title`` 添加标题。"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.plotting.monitoring_chart` draws one column per call, and "
":func:`~kivi.plotting.correlation_chart` one matrix without a color bar; add one with "
"``figure.colorbar(ax.images[0], ax=ax)``."
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.plotting.monitoring_chart` 每次调用只绘制一列， :func:`~kivi.plotting.correlation_chart` "
"绘制的矩阵不带颜色条；可以用 ``figure.colorbar(ax.images[0], ax=ax)`` 添加颜色条。"

msgid "The charts are static matplotlib figures, not interactive ones."
msgstr "这些图表是静态的 matplotlib 图形，不支持交互。"

msgid ""
"Without matplotlib, every chart raises an ``ImportError`` that asks for ``pip install "
"\"kivi[plot]\"``."
msgstr "未安装 matplotlib 时，每个图表函数都会抛出 ``ImportError`` ，提示运行 ``pip install \"kivi[plot]\"`` 。"

msgid ""
"A table that lacks a column a chart needs raises a ``ValueError`` that names the columns of the "
"table it expects and those that are missing, as when a PSI table is passed to "
":func:`~kivi.plotting.woe_chart`:"
msgstr ""
"如果表缺少图表所需的列，会抛出 ``ValueError`` ，其中列出所期望的表应有的列以及缺少的列，例如把 PSI 表传给 :func:`~kivi.plotting.woe_chart` "
"时："

msgid ""
"An ``ax`` that is not a matplotlib Axes, an empty table, a column that is not numeric and a "
"correlation matrix with a value outside [-1, 1] raise a ``ValueError`` as well. A chart that "
"raises does not leave an empty figure behind."
msgstr ""
"不是 matplotlib Axes 的 ``ax`` 、空表、非数值的列以及含有超出 [-1, 1] 的值的相关系数矩阵同样会抛出 ``ValueError`` "
"。抛出错误的图表函数不会留下空白图形。"

msgid ""
"matplotlib warns when more than 20 figures are open. When a report draws a chart for each of many"
" variables, save each figure and close it with ``plt.close(ax.figure)``."
msgstr "打开的图形超过 20 个时，matplotlib 会发出警告。如果报告要为许多变量各画一张图，请保存每个图形后用 ``plt.close(ax.figure)`` 关闭它。"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.stability.psi_table` compares the distribution of a variable in two samples, "
"typically the development sample and a later monitoring sample. Group both samples with the same "
"edges or labels before calling it. :func:`~kivi.stability.csi_table` measures how much such a "
"change moves a scorecard's score; see :ref:`characteristic-stability`."
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.stability.psi_table` 比较一个变量在两个样本中的分布，通常是开发样本和之后的监测样本。调用前，请用同一组边界或标签对两个样本分组。 "
":func:`~kivi.stability.csi_table` 衡量这种变化使评分卡分数移动了多少，参见 :ref:`characteristic-stability` 。"

msgid ""
"Stability is monitored once a model is in use, on samples grouped as its :doc:`binning "
"specification <spec>` groups them. :doc:`monitoring` then repeats the PSI and the measures of "
":doc:`metrics` period by period."
msgstr ""
"模型投入使用后开始监控稳定性，所用样本按模型的 :doc:`分箱方案 <spec>` 分组。随后 :doc:`monitoring` 逐期重复 PSI 和 :doc:`metrics` "
"中的各项指标。"

msgid "Definition"
msgstr "定义"

msgid ""
"Each contribution is zero or positive. PSI describes distribution change; it does not use the "
"outcome label."
msgstr "每一项贡献都大于或等于零。PSI 描述的是分布变化，不使用目标标签。"

msgid ""
"Missing values form their own group, and categories appearing in only one sample are retained. "
"Their empty cells are smoothed exactly as in :doc:`woe_iv`, so every contribution stays finite."
msgstr "缺失值单独成组，只在一个样本中出现的类别也会保留。它们的空单元格按 :doc:`woe_iv` 中的方式平滑，因此每一项贡献都是有限值。"

msgid "The reference and current samples, and the psi_table result with counts, shares and PSI per group"
msgstr "基准样本和当前样本，以及 psi_table 的结果：各组的计数、占比和 PSI"

msgid ""
"How ``psi_table`` computes the example. Missing values form a group of their own. A group that is"
" empty in one sample (outlined) counts as 0.5 before the shares are taken, so that its "
"contribution stays finite."
msgstr "``psi_table`` 如何计算该示例。缺失值单独成组。在某个样本中为空的组（带边框）在计算占比之前按 0.5 计，从而使其贡献保持有限。"

msgid ""
"When only the counts per group are available, for example from a monitoring report, "
":func:`~kivi.stability.psi` gives the total from the counts of each sample in the same group "
"order:"
msgstr "如果只有每组的计数（例如来自监控报表），可以用 :func:`~kivi.stability.psi` 按相同的分组顺序传入两个样本的计数，得到总的 PSI："

msgid "Stable and shifted samples"
msgstr "稳定与偏移的样本"

msgid ""
"Two samples from the same population give a PSI close to zero. When the population changes, the "
"bins that moved stand out. Below, the current sample is replaced by single customers only, who "
"are much younger than the reference."
msgstr "来自同一客群的两个样本，PSI 接近于零。客群发生变化时，发生移动的箱会凸显出来。下面把当前样本换成只包含单身客户的样本，他们比基准样本年轻得多。"

msgid "Reference and current age distributions for a random split and for single customers"
msgstr "随机切分样本与单身客户样本的基准、当前年龄分布"

msgid ""
"Left: the remaining customers look like the reference sample. Right: single customers crowd into "
"the youngest bin, and the youngest and oldest bins contribute most of the PSI."
msgstr "左图：其余客户与基准样本基本一致。右图：单身客户集中在最年轻的箱，最年轻和最年长的两个箱贡献了大部分 PSI。"

msgid "``reference``, ``current``"
msgstr "``reference``, ``current``"

msgid "Observed counts in each group."
msgstr "每组的实际观测数。"

msgid "``reference_share``, ``current_share``"
msgstr "``reference_share``, ``current_share``"

msgid ":math:`q_i` and :math:`p_i` after smoothing; each column sums to 1."
msgstr "平滑后的 :math:`q_i` 和 :math:`p_i`；每列之和为 1。"

msgid "The group's contribution. Sum the column to obtain total drift."
msgstr "该组的贡献。对该列求和得到整体漂移。"

msgid ""
"A common convention reads a PSI below 0.1 as a small shift, 0.1 to 0.25 as a moderate shift and "
"above 0.25 as a large shift. The thresholds depend on the number of bins and on the smoothing "
"rule, so recheck them when moving analyses from 0.2.x."
msgstr "一种常见的经验口径是：PSI 低于 0.1 视为变化较小，0.1 到 0.25 为中等变化，高于 0.25 为显著变化。这些阈值取决于箱数和平滑规则，从 0.2.x 迁移分析时请重新核对。"

msgid "Monitoring over time"
msgstr "按期监控"

msgid ""
"In production, PSI is computed for every period against the development sample and compared with "
"the conventions above. The bank data record the month of the last contact but not the year, so "
"the months below mix several years; read them as an example of a monitoring report."
msgstr "在生产环境中，每一期都要相对开发样本计算 PSI，并按上面的经验口径判断。银行数据只记录了最后一次联系的月份而没有年份，因此下面的月份混合了多个年份，请把它看作一份监控报告的示例。"

msgid ""
"PSI of age for each contact month, with the 0.1 and 0.25 thresholds and the sample size of each "
"month"
msgstr "每个联系月份 age 的 PSI，含 0.1 与 0.25 阈值及各月样本量"

msgid ""
"PSI of age for each contact month against the reference sample, with the number of customers "
"under each month."
msgstr "每个联系月份的 age 相对基准样本的 PSI，各月下方标注了客户数。"

msgid ""
"The months that cross the thresholds are also the smallest. With 20 customers, the December value"
" mostly reflects sampling noise. Set a minimum sample size before a high PSI raises an alert."
msgstr "越过阈值的月份恰好也是样本最少的月份。12 月只有 20 位客户，其 PSI 主要反映抽样噪声。在用高 PSI 触发预警之前，应先设定最小样本量。"

msgid ""
"For a model in production, :func:`~kivi.monitoring.stability_table` computes this table for every"
" variable at once, and :func:`~kivi.monitoring.monitoring_table` the PSI of the score together "
"with the outcomes and the discrimination of each period; see :doc:`monitoring`."
msgstr ""
"对于生产环境中的模型， :func:`~kivi.monitoring.stability_table` 一次为每个变量计算这张表， "
":func:`~kivi.monitoring.monitoring_table` 则给出评分的 PSI 以及每期的结果和区分能力；见 :doc:`monitoring` 。"

msgid "Characteristic stability index"
msgstr "特征稳定性指标"

msgid ""
"PSI shows that a distribution has moved, but not what the move does to the score. The "
"characteristic stability index (CSI) weights the change of each group's share with the scorecard "
"points :math:`s_i` of the group:"
msgstr "PSI 能说明分布发生了移动，却不能说明这种移动对分数有什么影响。特征稳定性指标（CSI）以每组的评分卡分值 :math:`s_i` 为权重，衡量各组占比的变化："

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\\mathrm{CSI}_i = (p_i - q_i)\\, s_i, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathrm{CSI} = \\sum_i \\mathrm{CSI}_i = \\sum_i p_i s_i - \\sum_i q_i s_i."
msgstr ""
"\\mathrm{CSI}_i = (p_i - q_i)\\, s_i, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathrm{CSI} = \\sum_i \\mathrm{CSI}_i = \\sum_i p_i s_i - \\sum_i q_i s_i."

msgid ""
"The CSI is the change of the variable's average points from the reference to the current sample: "
"a negative CSI means that the variable now gives fewer points on average. Over all the variables "
"of a scorecard, the CSI values add up to the change of the average score. Since the shares of "
"each sample sum to 1, adding the same number to the points of every group leaves the CSI "
"unchanged, so only the differences between the groups matter."
msgstr ""
"CSI 是该变量平均分值从基准样本到当前样本的变化：CSI 为负，说明该变量现在平均给出的分值更少。对评分卡的所有变量，CSI 之和就是平均分数的变化。由于每个样本的占比之和都为 "
"1，给每组的分值加上同一个数不会改变 CSI，因此起作用的只是各组之间的差别。"

msgid ""
"Some texts call the PSI of a single variable its CSI. kivi follows the score-weighted definition "
"of the characteristic analysis report; for the PSI of a variable, use "
":func:`~kivi.stability.psi_table` on its groups as above."
msgstr ""
"有些文献把单个变量的 PSI 称为它的 CSI。kivi 采用特征分析报告中按分值加权的定义；要计算某个变量的 PSI，请像上文那样对其分组调用 "
":func:`~kivi.stability.psi_table` 。"

msgid ""
"The example uses the scorecard of :doc:`scorecard`. Fit the WOE of four variables on the "
"development sample and turn the model into points:"
msgstr "示例使用 :doc:`scorecard` 中的评分卡。在开发样本上拟合四个变量的 WOE，并把模型转换为分值："

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.stability.csi_table` takes the groups of both samples and the points of the "
"variable's groups, here the rows of the points table for age:"
msgstr ":func:`~kivi.stability.csi_table` 接受两个样本的分组以及该变量各分组的分值，这里取分值表中 age 的各行："

msgid ""
"The shares are not smoothed, unlike those of ``psi_table``. A contribution has no logarithm, so "
"an empty group contributes a finite amount as it is, and a smoothed share would credit an empty "
"group with customers it does not have: the sum would no longer be the change of the average "
"points."
msgstr "与 ``psi_table`` 不同，这里的占比不做平滑。贡献中没有对数，因此空组无需平滑也只有有限的贡献；而平滑后的占比会让空组拥有它并没有的客户，求和结果也就不再是平均分值的变化。"

msgid ""
"A characteristic analysis report lists both indices for every variable of the scorecard. The CSI "
"column adds up to the change of the average score, here less than a fifth of a point:"
msgstr "特征分析报告列出评分卡每个变量的这两个指标。CSI 列之和就是平均分数的变化，这里不到五分之一分："

msgid ""
"The two indices answer different questions. Single customers, from the shifted sample above, have"
" a very different age distribution, but the age bands they crowd into have about the same points "
"as the others, so age lowers their average score by less than half a point:"
msgstr "这两个指标回答的是不同的问题。上文偏移样本中的单身客户，年龄分布差别很大，但这些客户集中的年龄段与其他年龄段的分值相差无几，因此年龄只让其平均分数降低不到半分："

msgid ""
"A group without points, such as a category that the development sample did not have, raises an "
"error unless ``unseen_points`` gives the points that its customers receive. These are points, not"
" a WOE: if :func:`~kivi.woe.woe_transform` encoded the category with ``unseen=0.0``, pass the "
"points of a WOE of 0, :func:`~kivi.scorecard.woe_to_points` of a one-row frame of zeros, which "
"are the same for every variable."
msgstr ""
"没有分值的分组（例如开发样本中没有的类别）会引发错误，除非用 ``unseen_points`` 给出其客户得到的分值。这里要传入的是分值而不是 WOE：如果 "
":func:`~kivi.woe.woe_transform` 用 ``unseen=0.0`` 编码了该类别，就传入 WOE 为 0 时的分值，即对一行全零调用 "
":func:`~kivi.scorecard.woe_to_points` 的结果，每个变量都相同。"

msgid ""
"For weighted samples, pass ``reference_weights`` and ``current_weights`` to "
":func:`~kivi.stability.psi_table`; the counts are then sums of weights. "
":func:`~kivi.stability.csi_table` takes the same two arguments, and its shares are then shares of"
" the total weight of each sample."
msgstr ""
"对于加权样本，请把 ``reference_weights`` 和 ``current_weights`` 传给 :func:`~kivi.stability.psi_table` "
"；此时计数为权重之和。 :func:`~kivi.stability.csi_table` 接受同样的两个参数，此时占比是各样本总权重中的占比。"

msgid ""
"A scorecard is developed on past applicants with a known outcome, and the outcome is known only "
"for the applicants that the previous policy approved. The model learns from them and is then "
"applied to every applicant, including the kind that used to be declined. Reject inference "
"supplies outcomes for the rejected applicants so that the model can be refitted on all of them. "
":mod:`kivi.reject_inference` returns those outcomes as rows with weights, or returns weights for "
"the approved applicants. The ``weights`` arguments of "
":func:`~kivi.selection.logistic_regression`, :func:`~kivi.woe.woe_table` and "
":func:`~kivi.spec.fit_spec` take either."
msgstr ""
"评分卡在结果已知的历史申请人上开发，而只有以往政策批准的申请人才有已知结果。模型从他们身上学习，随后却应用于每一个申请人，包括过去会被拒绝的那类申请人。拒绝推断为拒绝申请人补上结果，使模型可以在全部申请人上重新拟合。"
" :mod:`kivi.reject_inference` 以带权重的行返回这些结果，或者返回获批申请人的权重。 "
":func:`~kivi.selection.logistic_regression` 、 :func:`~kivi.woe.woe_table` 和 "
":func:`~kivi.spec.fit_spec` 的 ``weights`` 参数都可以接受这两种结果。"

msgid ""
"Reject inference follows :doc:`variable selection <selection>`, whose model it refits on all "
"applicants, and comes before the :doc:`scorecard`, which scales the refitted model. "
":func:`~kivi.reject_inference.fuzzy_augmentation` and :func:`~kivi.reject_inference.parceling` "
"return inferred rows, and :func:`~kivi.reject_inference.reweighting` returns weights for the "
"approved applicants."
msgstr ""
"拒绝推断位于 :doc:`变量筛选 <selection>` 之后，在全部申请人上重新拟合其模型；之后是 :doc:`scorecard` ，对重新拟合的模型进行刻度。 "
":func:`~kivi.reject_inference.fuzzy_augmentation` 和 :func:`~kivi.reject_inference.parceling` "
"返回推断行， :func:`~kivi.reject_inference.reweighting` 返回获批申请人的权重。"

msgid ""
"Every method rests on an assumption about the rejected applicants that the approved ones cannot "
"confirm. The examples therefore use synthetic applications whose outcomes are known for everyone,"
" so that each method can be checked against the model the full outcomes would give. Real data "
"never allow that check."
msgstr "每种方法都依赖一个关于拒绝申请人的假设，而获批申请人无法证实它。因此示例使用每个人结果都已知的合成申请数据，以便把每种方法与完整结果所能得到的模型相对照。真实数据永远无法做这样的检验。"

msgid "Applications and approvals"
msgstr "申请与审批"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.datasets.make_applications` simulates loan applications decided by an incumbent "
"scorecard and two policy rules; :doc:`datasets` describes them. Policy declines would be declined"
" whatever their score, so they are usually left out of the development population, as here. The "
"approved applicants are the *accepts* and the others the *rejects*:"
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.datasets.make_applications` 模拟由现行评分卡和两条政策规则决定审批的贷款申请， :doc:`datasets` "
"介绍了这些数据。政策拒绝的申请无论评分如何都会被拒绝，因此通常不纳入开发总体，这里也是如此。获批的申请人称为 *通过样本* ，其余称为 *拒绝样本* ："

msgid ""
"In practice, ``target`` would be missing for the rejects. Here it shows what reject inference "
"tries to recover: the rejects default three times as often as the accepts."
msgstr "实际中拒绝样本的 ``target`` 是缺失的。这里它展示了拒绝推断试图还原的东西：拒绝样本的违约频率是通过样本的三倍。"

msgid "The accepts-only model"
msgstr "仅用通过样本的模型"

msgid ""
"All the models below use the same groups and the same WOE encoding, fitted on the accepts, so "
"that their coefficients can be compared. Quantile edges need no outcome, so they are fitted on "
"every applicant of the population. The number of inquiries takes few values and gets explicit "
"edges:"
msgstr "下面所有模型都使用相同的分组和在通过样本上拟合的同一套 WOE 编码，以便比较它们的系数。分位数边界不需要结果，因此在总体的全部申请人上拟合。征信查询次数取值很少，因此给定显式边界："

msgid ""
"The PD of the model is the logistic function of the intercept plus the WOE values times the "
"coefficients:"
msgstr "模型的 PD 是截距加上 WOE 值乘以系数之和的逻辑函数值："

#, python-format
msgid ""
"The model predicts a bad rate of 19.1% for the rejects, who actually default at 30.1%. The "
"incumbent scorecard used information that is not among the features, like an underwriter who "
"reads a credit bureau report, so the rejects are riskier than accepts with the same features. A "
"model fitted on the accepts alone cannot see that."
msgstr ""
"模型预测拒绝样本的坏账率为 19.1%，而他们实际的违约率为 "
"30.1%。现行评分卡像阅读征信报告的审批人员一样，用到了特征之外的信息，因此在特征相同时，拒绝样本比通过样本风险更高。只用通过样本拟合的模型看不到这一点。"

msgid "Fuzzy augmentation"
msgstr "模糊扩充"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.reject_inference.fuzzy_augmentation` splits each reject into a bad row, weighted "
"with its PD, and a good row with the rest of its weight of 1. The rows repeat the index of the "
"rejects, so ``rejects.loc[inferred.index]`` gives their features:"
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.reject_inference.fuzzy_augmentation` 把每个拒绝申请人拆成以其 PD 为权重的一行坏样本和以总权重 1 "
"的其余部分为权重的一行好样本。这些行重复拒绝样本的索引，因此 ``rejects.loc[inferred.index]`` 给出它们的特征："

msgid "Three rejects with their PDs, each split into a row with target 1 and a row with target 0"
msgstr "三个拒绝申请人及其 PD，每人拆成一行目标为 1 和一行目标为 0"

msgid ""
"``fuzzy_augmentation`` splits each reject into two rows with its index: target 1 with its PD as "
"the weight, and target 0 with the rest of the weight of 1."
msgstr "``fuzzy_augmentation`` 把每个拒绝申请人拆成两行，索引不变：目标为 1 的行以其 PD 为权重，目标为 0 的行取权重 1 的其余部分。"

msgid ""
"To refit, concatenate the accepts at weight 1 with the inferred rows and pass the weights. Only "
"the features of the rejects enter the fit, never their ``target`` column:"
msgstr "重新拟合时，把权重为 1 的通过样本与推断出的行拼接起来，并传入权重。进入拟合的只有拒绝样本的特征，绝不包括其 ``target`` 列："

msgid ""
"The refitted coefficients are those of the accepts-only model. At those coefficients, the bad row"
" of each reject weighs exactly its fitted PD, so the inferred rows leave the fit where it was. "
"Only the standard errors shrink, although the inferred rows add no information: they count as "
"observations, so the standard errors of any fit with inferred rows are too small. Choose the "
"variables on the accepts, not by the p-values of an augmented fit. With a factor of 1, fuzzy "
"augmentation changes the model only if the encoding is refitted on the augmented sample or the "
"variables change."
msgstr ""
"重新拟合的系数就是仅用通过样本的模型的系数。在这组系数下，每个拒绝申请人坏样本行的权重恰好等于其拟合 "
"PD，因此推断出的行不会改变拟合结果。只有标准误变小，尽管推断出的行并没有增加任何信息：它们被计为观测，因此任何包含推断行的拟合，其标准误都偏小。应在通过样本上选择变量，而不是依据扩充后拟合的 "
"p 值。倍数为 1 时，只有在扩充后的样本上重新拟合编码或变量发生变化时，模糊扩充才会改变模型。"

msgid "Sensitivity to the factor"
msgstr "对倍数的敏感性"

msgid ""
"``factor`` multiplies the PDs of the rejects, so a factor above 1 assumes that they are riskier "
"than accepts with the same PD. The accepts cannot tell how much riskier, so compare several "
"factors. ``summary`` gathers three results: the inferred bad rate of the rejects, their mean PD "
"under the refitted model, and the Gini on a second sample from the same generator, where every "
"applicant's outcome is known. The *known* model, fitted on all applicants with their true "
"outcomes, is the benchmark that real data never provide; its inferred rate is the rejects' true "
"bad rate:"
msgstr ""
"``factor`` 乘以拒绝样本的 PD，因此大于 1 的倍数假定拒绝样本比 PD 相同的通过样本风险更高。通过样本无法告诉我们高出多少，所以要比较几个倍数。 ``summary`` "
"汇总三项结果：拒绝样本推断的坏账率、它们在重新拟合的模型下的平均 PD，以及在同一生成器产生的第二个样本上的 Gini，该样本中每个申请人的结果都已知。 *known* "
"模型用全部申请人及其真实结果拟合，是真实数据永远无法提供的基准；它的推断坏账率就是拒绝样本的真实坏账率："

#, python-format
msgid ""
"A factor of 1.5 brings the inferred bad rate of the rejects to 28.6%, near their true 30.1%, and "
"their mean PD under the refitted model to 25.1%, close to the known model's 25.2%. Even the known"
" model predicts less than 30.1% for the rejects: it is fitted on all applicants and lacks the "
"information that set the rejects apart. The Gini hardly moves. On these data, reject inference "
"corrects how risky the model takes the rejects to be, not how it ranks applicants."
msgstr ""
"倍数为 1.5 时，拒绝样本推断的坏账率为 28.6%，接近其真实的 30.1%；它们在重新拟合的模型下的平均 PD 为 25.1%，接近 known 模型的 25.2%。即使 known "
"模型对拒绝样本的预测也低于 30.1%：它在全部申请人上拟合，缺少使拒绝样本与众不同的那部分信息。Gini "
"几乎不变。在这些数据上，拒绝推断纠正的是模型认为拒绝样本有多大风险，而不是模型如何对申请人排序。"

msgid ""
"Inferred bad rate and mean refitted PD of the rejects for factors from 1 to 2.5, with the true "
"bad rate of the rejects and the known model's mean PD as dashed lines"
msgstr "倍数从 1 到 2.5 时拒绝样本推断的坏账率和重新拟合后的平均 PD，虚线为拒绝样本的真实坏账率和 known 模型的平均 PD"

msgid ""
"The inferred bad rate and the mean refitted PD of the rejects rise with ``factor``. The dashed "
"lines are the true bad rate of the rejects and the mean PD that the known model gives them; a "
"factor of 1.5 meets the second."
msgstr "拒绝样本推断的坏账率和重新拟合后的平均 PD 都随 ``factor`` 上升。虚线分别是拒绝样本的真实坏账率，以及 known 模型给出的平均 PD；倍数为 1.5 时与后者相交。"

msgid ""
"Here the known outcomes say which factor fits. With real data, the factor is an assumption, best "
"supported from outside the development sample: the bureau outcomes of rejects who borrowed "
"elsewhere, a small sample of rejects approved on purpose, or business judgement. Report the "
"results for a range of factors, as above."
msgstr "这里已知的结果告诉我们哪个倍数合适。对于真实数据，倍数是一个假设，最好从开发样本之外寻找依据：在别处借款的拒绝申请人的征信结果、有意批准的一小部分拒绝申请人，或者业务判断。像上面那样报告一系列倍数下的结果。"

msgid "Parceling"
msgstr "打包法"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.reject_inference.parceling` divides the scores of accepts and rejects into bands, by"
" default ten quantile bands of both samples together. In each band, the rejects are labelled bad "
"at the accepts' bad rate times ``factor``. The labels are drawn with a local generator, so a seed"
" in ``rng`` makes them reproducible:"
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.reject_inference.parceling` "
"把通过样本和拒绝样本的评分划分为评分段，默认是两个样本合并后的十个分位数评分段。在每个评分段内，按通过样本的坏账率乘以 ``factor`` 把拒绝样本标记为坏。标签用局部生成器抽取，因此在 "
"``rng`` 中给定种子即可复现："

msgid ""
"The rejects are labelled bad at 26.3%, less than the 28.6% that fuzzy augmentation infers with "
"the same factor. Parceling knows only the band of a reject, not its features or its own PD. The "
"riskiest band is open above and holds almost a third of the rejects, and they all get the bad "
"rate of the band's accepts, which is below the mean PD that the model gives them."
msgstr ""
"拒绝样本中有 26.3% 被标记为坏，低于同一倍数下模糊扩充推断的 28.6%。打包法只知道拒绝申请人所在的评分段，不知道其特征和自身的 "
"PD。风险最高的评分段上端开放，容纳了近三分之一的拒绝样本，它们都得到该评分段通过样本的坏账率，而这一坏账率低于模型给它们的平均 PD。"

msgid ""
"The draw adds noise to the refit. Over ten seeds, the Gini on the second sample varies by several"
" thousandths:"
msgstr "随机抽取给重新拟合带来噪声。在十个种子下，第二个样本上的 Gini 相差千分之几："

msgid ""
"``expected=True`` instead returns the band's rate as the weight of a bad row and its complement "
"as the weight of a good row, like :func:`~kivi.reject_inference.fuzzy_augmentation`. That removes"
" the noise of the draw, so the comparison below uses it:"
msgstr ""
"``expected=True`` 则像 :func:`~kivi.reject_inference.fuzzy_augmentation` "
"那样，以评分段的坏账率作为坏样本行的权重、以其补数作为好样本行的权重。这样消除了抽样噪声，因此下面的比较使用这种方式："

msgid "Reweighting"
msgstr "重新加权"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.reject_inference.reweighting` adds no rows. In each score band, it gives every "
"accept the weight (accepts + rejects) / accepts, so that the weighted accepts stand for all "
"applicants of their band:"
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.reject_inference.reweighting` 不增加任何行。在每个评分段内，它给每个通过样本权重（通过样本 + 拒绝样本）/ "
"通过样本，使加权后的通过样本代表该评分段的全部申请人："

msgid ""
"The ten score bands with their accepts, rejects and event rates, the bad weights of parceling and"
" the weights of reweighting"
msgstr "十个评分段及其获批和拒绝申请人数、事件率，打包法的坏样本权重和重新加权的权重"

msgid ""
"The ten bands of the scores of both samples. Parceling labels the rejects of a band bad at the "
"event rate of its accepts times ``factor``, and reweighting gives the accepts of a band the "
"weight (accepts + rejects) / accepts. The rejects crowd into the riskiest bands, where accepts "
"are fewest."
msgstr ""
"两个样本的评分合起来划分的十个评分段。打包法按评分段内获批申请人的事件率乘以 ``factor`` 把该段的拒绝申请人标为坏；重新加权给评分段内的获批申请人权重（获批 + 拒绝）/ "
"获批。拒绝申请人集中在风险最高的评分段，而那里的获批申请人最少。"

msgid ""
"Reweighting assumes that rejects default like accepts with the same score, which is exactly what "
"fails here. The weights add up to all 9,237 applicants of the population, although only the 6,770"
" accepts have an observed outcome, so the standard errors of the fit are too small. Each band "
"must also hold accepts. On the incumbent PD, which decided the approval with a hard cut-off, the "
"bands above the cut-off hold only rejects:"
msgstr ""
"重新加权假定拒绝样本与评分相同的通过样本违约情况相同，而这里恰恰不成立。权重之和等于总体的全部 9,237 个申请人，而只有 6,770 "
"个通过样本有观测到的结果，因此拟合的标准误偏小。每个评分段还必须有通过样本。现行评分卡的 PD 以硬截断决定审批，按它划分时，截断点以上的评分段只有拒绝样本："

msgid "Hard cut-off"
msgstr "硬截断"

#, python-format
msgid ""
"The simplest method needs no function. Score the rejects with the accepts-only model, label those"
" above a PD cut-off bad and the others good, and refit. Here the cut-off labels the riskiest 30% "
"of the rejects bad, close to their true bad rate; like the factor, that share is chosen with the "
"known outcomes:"
msgstr ""
"最简单的方法不需要专门的函数：用仅用通过样本的模型给拒绝样本打分，把 PD 高于截断点的标记为坏、其余标记为好，然后重新拟合。这里的截断点把风险最高的 30% "
"拒绝样本标记为坏，接近它们的真实坏账率；与倍数一样，这个比例是借助已知结果选定的："

msgid "Comparison"
msgstr "比较"

msgid ""
"With the accepts' WOE, the known model weighs every variable more than the accepts-only model: "
"across all applicants, the features separate good from bad more strongly than among the accepts. "
"The methods compare as follows:"
msgstr "在通过样本的 WOE 编码下，known 模型给每个变量的权重都高于仅用通过样本的模型：在全部申请人中，特征区分好坏的能力比在通过样本中更强。各方法的比较如下："

msgid ""
"**Ranking.** The Gini on the second sample stays between 0.418 and 0.422 for every method in the "
"table, and the known model reaches only 0.425; the random labels of parceling reach that only by "
"chance. The extra risk of the rejects comes from information that no feature holds, so no method "
"can recover it."
msgstr ""
"**排序。** 表中每种方法在第二个样本上的 Gini 都在 0.418 到 0.422 之间，known 模型也只有 "
"0.425；打包法的随机标签只是偶然达到这一水平。拒绝样本额外的风险来自任何特征都不包含的信息，因此没有方法能把它找回来。"

msgid ""
"**Fuzzy augmentation and parceling.** With a factor above 1, both raise the predicted bad rate of"
" the rejects towards their true rate and move most coefficients towards those of the known model."
" With a factor of 1.5, fuzzy augmentation brings the intercept and four of the six variables "
"within 0.07 of the known model, but overshoots ``income`` and ``employment``. Parceling lowers "
"the coefficient of ``housing``, which the known model raises. Both methods help only as far as "
"the factor is right."
msgstr ""
"**模糊扩充和打包法。** 倍数大于 1 时，两者都会把拒绝样本的预测坏账率推向其真实值，并使大多数系数向 known 模型的系数靠拢。倍数为 1.5 时，模糊扩充使截距和六个变量中的四个与 "
"known 模型的差距在 0.07 以内，但 ``income`` 和 ``employment`` 的系数超过了 known 模型。打包法降低了 ``housing`` 的系数，而 known"
" 模型提高了它。两种方法的作用都以倍数正确为限。"

msgid ""
"**Reweighting.** It does not help here: weights cannot make the rejects riskier than the accepts "
"of their band."
msgstr "**重新加权。** 它在这里没有帮助：权重无法使拒绝样本比同一评分段的通过样本风险更高。"

msgid ""
"**Hard cut-off.** It treats the rejects above the cut-off as certainly bad and the others as "
"certainly good, so the inferred outcomes follow the model's own score without error. The refit "
"multiplies the coefficient of every variable by 1.9 to 2.4 and ranks slightly worse."
msgstr "**硬截断。** 它把截断点以上的拒绝样本视为必然为坏、其余视为必然为好，因此推断的结果与模型自身的评分完全一致。重新拟合使每个变量的系数变为原来的 1.9 到 2.4 倍，排序能力也略差。"

msgid "Refitting the WOE"
msgstr "重新拟合 WOE"

msgid ""
"The comparisons keep the accepts' WOE encoding. In practice, the groups are often refitted on the"
" augmented sample with the inferred weights, so that the rejects also inform the WOE of the "
"groups they fill. :func:`~kivi.spec.fit_spec` takes the weights:"
msgstr ""
"上面的比较保留了通过样本的 WOE 编码。实际中常常用推断出的权重在扩充后的样本上重新拟合分组，使拒绝样本也影响它们所在分组的 WOE。 :func:`~kivi.spec.fit_spec` "
"接受这些权重："

msgid ""
"Refitting the WOE raises the Gini from 0.422 to 0.425, against 0.430 for the known outcomes with "
"their own WOE. It recovers part of a gap that is small to begin with, and it does about as well "
"with a factor of 1: the gain comes from refitting the WOE of the groups that the rejects fill, "
"not from the factor."
msgstr ""
"重新拟合 WOE 使 Gini 从 0.422 升到 0.425，而用已知结果及其自身 WOE 编码的模型为 0.430。它弥补了一部分差距，而这个差距本来就很小；倍数为 1 "
"时效果也差不多：提升来自重新拟合拒绝样本所在分组的 WOE，而不是来自倍数。"

msgid ""
"The methods infer outcomes from the accepts, so they cannot reveal what the accepts do not show. "
"A factor above 1 encodes how much riskier the rejects are, and the data cannot estimate it."
msgstr "这些方法都从通过样本推断结果，因此无法揭示通过样本没有体现的东西。大于 1 的倍数表达的是拒绝样本风险高出多少，而数据无法估计它。"

msgid ""
"The weights of every method make the standard errors of "
":func:`~kivi.selection.logistic_regression` too small and the p-values of "
":func:`~kivi.selection.stepwise` too low, because inferred rows and extra weight count as "
"observations. Select the variables on the accepts and read the p-values of a refit as optimistic."
msgstr ""
"每种方法的权重都会使 :func:`~kivi.selection.logistic_regression` 的标准误偏小、 :func:`~kivi.selection.stepwise` 的"
" p 值偏低，因为推断出的行和额外的权重被计为观测。应在通过样本上选择变量，并把重新拟合的 p 值视为偏乐观的结果。"

msgid ""
"kivi does not implement the Heckman two-stage model or other bivariate probit models of sample "
"selection, nor iterative reclassification."
msgstr "kivi 没有实现 Heckman 两阶段模型或其他样本选择的双变量 probit 模型，也没有实现迭代重分类。"

msgid ""
"This example follows the steps of a scorecard project with kivi: profile and screen the candidate"
" variables, bin the shortlist, encode it with WOE and save the binning for production, select the"
" variables and fit the model, scale it to a scorecard, evaluate it, calibrate it on a master "
"scale, set a cut-off with its expected loss, and prepare the stability report used in monitoring."
" The bundled data record a marketing response rather than a default, but the steps are the same "
"for a credit default flag: use the bad flag as ``target``."
msgstr ""
"本示例用 kivi 走一遍评分卡项目的各个步骤：分析并筛选候选变量，对入选变量分箱，用 WOE "
"编码并保存分箱供生产环境使用，筛选变量并拟合模型，刻度为评分卡，评估模型，基于主标尺校准模型，设定截断点并计算预期损失，并准备监控所需的稳定性报告。随包数据记录的是营销响应而非违约，但对信用违约标记来说步骤完全相同：把坏样本标记作为"
" ``target`` 即可。"

msgid "Screen variables by IV"
msgstr "按 IV 筛选变量"

msgid ""
"Start with a profile of every candidate. :func:`~kivi.univariate.profile_table` gives each one "
"row with its missing values, its most frequent value and, with the target, the IV of a quick, "
"uniform binning: five quantile bins for numeric variables and the raw labels for categorical "
"ones; see :doc:`univariate`. The IV of each variable gives a first ranking, and ``tied_bins`` "
"marks the numeric variables whose tied values leave fewer bins than requested:"
msgstr ""
"先为每个候选变量做概况分析。 :func:`~kivi.univariate.profile_table` "
"为每个变量给出一行，包括缺失值、最常见的取值，以及在给定目标变量时按统一方式快速分箱得到的 IV：数值变量分为五个等频箱，类别变量直接使用原始标签；见 :doc:`univariate` "
"。各变量的 IV 给出初步排序， ``tied_bins`` 标出取值并列导致箱数少于要求的数值变量："

msgid ""
"Information value of every variable in the bank data, sorted, with the 0.02, 0.1 and 0.3 reading "
"bands"
msgstr "银行数据中各变量的信息值排序，含 0.02、0.1 和 0.3 的解读区间"

msgid ""
"IV of every candidate variable with quick binning. The dashed lines mark the 0.02, 0.1 and 0.3 "
"bands; ``duration`` is cut off at the right edge of the chart."
msgstr "快速分箱下各候选变量的 IV。虚线标出 0.02、0.1 和 0.3 三个区间；``duration`` 的柱子在图的右边缘被截断。"

msgid "Read the ranking critically before building the shortlist:"
msgstr "在确定入选名单之前，请审慎地解读这个排序："

msgid ""
"``duration`` is the length of the last call. It is only known after the call, when the outcome is"
" largely decided, so its IV of 1.59 is a leak rather than a signal. The dataset's documentation "
"recommends leaving it out of a realistic model. In credit risk, look for the same pattern in "
"fields filled in after the decision, such as collection status."
msgstr ""
"``duration`` 是最后一次通话的时长。它只有在通话结束后才知道，而那时结果基本已经确定，因此它 1.59 的 IV "
"是信息泄漏而非有效信号。数据集的说明建议在构建实际可用的模型时排除它。在信用风险中，也要警惕在决策之后才填写的字段，例如催收状态。"

msgid ""
"``month`` describes when the campaign ran rather than who the customer is, so it is left out as "
"well."
msgstr "``month`` 描述的是营销活动开展的时间，而不是客户本身，因此同样排除。"

msgid ""
"``pdays`` and ``previous`` show an IV of zero only because their tied values collapse into one "
"quantile bin. Custom edges or the ``special`` argument recover ``pdays``; see :ref:`custom-edges`"
" and :ref:`special-values`."
msgstr ""
"``pdays`` 和 ``previous`` 的 IV 为零，只是因为大量重复值使它们被压缩进一个等频箱。自定义边界或 ``special`` 参数都可以挽回 ``pdays`` ，见 "
":ref:`custom-edges` 和 :ref:`special-values` 。"

msgid "Bin the shortlist"
msgstr "对入选变量分箱"

msgid ""
"Each variable on the shortlist gets edges that can be explained: merged balance bins with a "
"monotonic WOE, a bin of its own for the ``pdays == -1`` code, policy age bands, and the raw "
"labels of the categorical variables. The twelve labels of ``job`` could also be grouped first, as"
" in :ref:`category-groups`; this example keeps them as they are. Keep the binning in one place so"
" that development and monitoring data are grouped identically."
msgstr ""
"每个入选变量都使用可以解释的边界：余额采用合并后 WOE 单调的分箱，``pdays == -1`` 编码单独成箱，年龄采用政策分段，类别变量使用原始标签。 ``job`` "
"的十二个标签也可以先按 :ref:`category-groups` 分组，本例保留原样。把分箱逻辑集中在一处，确保开发数据和监控数据的分组完全一致。"

msgid ""
"``tables`` holds one :func:`~kivi.woe.woe_table` result per variable. Review each one as a WOE "
"chart (see :doc:`woe_iv`) before moving on. ``pdays`` and ``poutcome`` both describe the previous"
" campaign, so check how strongly they are correlated before keeping both."
msgstr ""
"``tables`` 为每个变量保存一个 :func:`~kivi.woe.woe_table` 结果。继续之前，请逐一以 WOE 图的形式复核（见 "
":doc:`woe_iv`）。``pdays`` 和 ``poutcome`` 都描述上一轮营销，同时保留之前请先检查二者的相关性。"

msgid ""
"A logistic regression on WOE values is the classic scorecard model. Replace each group with the "
"WOE from the development tables using :func:`~kivi.woe.woe_transform`:"
msgstr "基于 WOE 值的逻辑回归是经典的评分卡模型。用 :func:`~kivi.woe.woe_transform` 把每个分组替换为开发样本表中对应的 WOE："

msgid ""
"``woe_transform`` raises an error for a group that never appeared in development, such as a new "
"category. Agree on a policy before scoring new data, for example ``unseen=0.0`` for a neutral "
"WOE."
msgstr "对开发样本中从未出现的分组（例如新类别）， ``woe_transform`` 会引发错误。对新数据评分之前，请先约定处理方式，例如用 ``unseen=0.0`` 取中性的 WOE。"

msgid ""
"Production systems must group and encode new applications exactly as the development sample was. "
":func:`~kivi.spec.fit_spec` fits the edges and the WOE table of every column at once, and the "
"resulting :class:`~kivi.spec.BinningSpec` saves them as versioned JSON; see :doc:`spec`. Passing "
"the edges of the shortlist as ``bins`` reproduces the encoding above:"
msgstr ""
"生产系统对新申请的分组和编码必须与开发样本完全一致。 :func:`~kivi.spec.fit_spec` 一次拟合每列的边界和 WOE 表，得到的 "
":class:`~kivi.spec.BinningSpec` 把它们保存为带版本号的 JSON；参见 :doc:`spec` 。把入选变量的边界作为 ``bins`` "
"传入，即可复现上面的编码："

msgid ""
"Store the JSON with the model. A scoring service that loads it with ``BinningSpec.from_json`` "
"encodes new data with ``restored.woe_transform(frame)``, without the code of the development "
"project."
msgstr ""
"把 JSON 与模型一起保存。打分服务用 ``BinningSpec.from_json`` 加载后，用 ``restored.woe_transform(frame)`` "
"对新数据编码，无需开发项目的代码。"

msgid "Select variables and fit the model"
msgstr "筛选变量并拟合模型"

msgid ""
"Strongly correlated variables carry the same information and make the coefficients unstable. "
":func:`~kivi.selection.correlation_filter` keeps the variable with the higher IV from each pair "
"correlated above 0.7, and :func:`~kivi.selection.stepwise` then selects variables by the p-values"
" of a logistic regression. With WOE inputs every coefficient should be positive, and ``stepwise``"
" rejects a variable that would make one negative; see :doc:`selection`."
msgstr ""
"高度相关的变量携带相同的信息，还会让系数不稳定。 :func:`~kivi.selection.correlation_filter` 在每对相关系数超过 0.7 的变量中保留 IV "
"较高的一个，随后 :func:`~kivi.selection.stepwise` 按逻辑回归的 p 值筛选变量。以 WOE 作为输入时，所有系数都应为正， ``stepwise`` "
"会拒绝会使某个系数变为负的变量；详见 :doc:`selection` 。"

msgid ""
"No pair is correlated strongly enough to drop a variable, and ``stepwise`` leaves out ``age``. "
"The model is fitted on the development sample only."
msgstr "没有哪对变量的相关性高到需要剔除， ``stepwise`` 去掉了 ``age`` 。模型只用开发样本拟合。"

msgid ""
"The bank data record the outcome of every customer. A credit development sample usually holds "
"only the applications that the previous policy approved, and a model fitted on them alone "
"underestimates the risk of the applicants it used to decline. :doc:`reject_inference` infers "
"their outcomes and refits the model with ``weights``."
msgstr ""
"银行数据记录了每位客户的结果。信贷开发样本通常只包含原有策略批准的申请，仅用这些申请拟合的模型会低估原先被拒申请人的风险。 :doc:`reject_inference` "
"推断这些申请人的结果，并通过 ``weights`` 重新拟合模型。"

msgid "Scale to a scorecard"
msgstr "刻度为评分卡"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.scorecard.points_table` turns the WOE tables and the coefficients into points for "
"every group. Here 20 points double the odds of a good outcome, and a score of 600 stands for "
"good:bad odds of 50; see :doc:`scorecard`. A higher WOE means more risk and therefore fewer "
"points:"
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.scorecard.points_table` 把 WOE 表和系数转换为每组的分值。这里每增加 20 分，好坏比翻一倍；600 分对应 50 的好坏比；详见 "
":doc:`scorecard` 。WOE 越高风险越大，分值也就越低："

msgid ""
"Score the monitoring sample with the development tables: each customer's score is the sum of "
"their points."
msgstr "用开发样本的表给监控样本打分：每个客户的分数是其各项分值之和。"

msgid "Evaluate the model"
msgstr "评估模型"

msgid ""
"A higher score means lower risk, while the measures in :doc:`metrics` expect a score that rises "
"with the event probability. Pass the probability that each score stands for. The gains table uses"
" bands fitted on the development scores, so that both samples are cut alike:"
msgstr "分数越高风险越低，而 :doc:`metrics` 中的指标要求分数随事件概率升高。因此请传入每个分数对应的概率。增益表使用在开发样本分数上拟合的分段，使两个样本按同样的方式切分："

#, python-format
msgid ""
"The riskiest band, about a fifth of the monitoring sample, holds 48% of its events at about twice"
" the average event rate."
msgstr "风险最高的分段约占监控样本的五分之一，却包含了 48% 的事件，事件率约为平均水平的两倍。"

#, python-format
msgid ""
"A monitoring sample of this size measures the Gini with some uncertainty. "
":func:`~kivi.metrics.roc_auc_interval` gives the DeLong standard error and the 95% interval of "
"the AUC and of the Gini:"
msgstr ""
"这种规模的监控样本对 Gini 的测量存在一定的不确定性。 :func:`~kivi.metrics.roc_auc_interval` 给出 AUC 和 Gini 的 DeLong 标准误及 "
"95% 区间："

msgid ""
"With 173 events among 1,521 customers, the interval of the Gini runs from 0.286 to 0.464. It "
"contains the development Gini of 0.432, which is itself optimistic because the binning, the "
"variables and the coefficients were all fitted on the development sample, so the lower Gini of "
"the monitoring sample is within the sampling noise. :doc:`metrics` also compares two scores on "
"the same sample with the DeLong test."
msgstr ""
"在 1,521 名客户中有 173 个事件，Gini 的区间从 0.286 到 0.464。它包含开发样本的 Gini "
"0.432，而后者本身偏乐观，因为分箱、变量和系数都是在开发样本上拟合的，所以监控样本的 Gini 较低仍在抽样误差范围内。 :doc:`metrics` 还用 DeLong "
"检验比较同一样本上的两个评分。"

msgid "Check calibration"
msgstr "检查校准"

msgid ""
"Rating grades give PDs from different models one meaning. :func:`~kivi.calibration.master_scale` "
"builds a scale from the PD of each grade, here five grades in which each PD doubles the one "
"before, and :func:`~kivi.calibration.assign_grades` gives every customer of the monitoring sample"
" the grade of their PD; see :doc:`calibration`. Each grade is then compared with its PD. The "
"Jeffreys test asks whether a grade has more events than its PD predicts, so a small p-value flags"
" a grade that underestimates risk:"
msgstr ""
"评级让不同模型的 PD 具有统一的含义。 :func:`~kivi.calibration.master_scale` 由每个等级的 PD 构建标尺，这里共五个等级，每个等级的 PD "
"是前一个的两倍； :func:`~kivi.calibration.assign_grades` 为监控样本中的每位客户分配其 PD 所属的等级；见 :doc:`calibration` "
"。然后把每个等级与其 PD 比较。Jeffreys 检验考察一个等级的事件数是否多于其 PD 的预测，因此较小的 p 值提示该等级低估了风险："

#, python-format
msgid ""
"No grade is rejected at the 5% level, but grades A and B come close: their event rates of 4.3% "
"and 6.4% exceed their PDs of 2.5% and 5%, and the monitoring of the next periods should watch "
"them. Grade D has fewer events than its PD, which this one-sided test does not flag."
msgstr ""
"在 5% 的水平下没有等级被拒绝，但等级 A 和 B 已接近拒绝：它们 4.3% 和 6.4% 的事件率高于各自 2.5% 和 5% 的 PD，后续各期的监控应重点关注。等级 D 的事件少于其 "
"PD 的预测，这种单侧检验不会标出这种情况。"

msgid "Set a cut-off"
msgstr "设定截断点"

msgid ""
"The scorecard ranks the applicants, and a cut-off decides whom to approve. "
":func:`~kivi.strategy.cutoff_table` shows, for each candidate PD cut-off, the share of applicants"
" it approves, the bad rate of the approved book and the share of the events it turns away; see "
":doc:`strategy`. The upper bounds of the grades as cut-offs approve the grades up to each one:"
msgstr ""
"评分卡为申请人排序，截断点决定批准谁。 :func:`~kivi.strategy.cutoff_table` 对每个候选的 PD "
"截断点给出它批准的申请人占比、通过客群的坏账率以及它拒绝的事件占比；见 :doc:`strategy` 。以各等级的上界作为截断点，就是批准截至该等级的所有等级："

#, python-format
msgid ""
"Approving the grades up to C, a PD of at most 14.1%, approves 75.4% of the applicants at a bad "
"rate of 7.8% and turns away 48.6% of the events. Approving grade D as well approves 94.2% at a "
"bad rate of 9.4%. Which row to choose is a business decision; the table shows its price."
msgstr ""
"批准等级 A 到 C，即 PD 不超过 14.1%，会以 7.8% 的坏账率批准 75.4% 的申请人，并拒绝 48.6% 的事件。若再批准等级 D，则以 9.4% 的坏账率批准 94.2% "
"的申请人。选择哪一行是业务决策；这张表给出了每种选择的代价。"

msgid ""
"The expected loss of an exposure is its PD times its loss given default times its exposure at "
"default. :func:`~kivi.strategy.expected_loss_table` adds it up for each grade. The bank data have"
" no loan amounts, so the example takes the balance, floored at zero, as the exposure and one LGD "
"of 45%:"
msgstr ""
"一笔敞口的预期损失等于其 PD 乘以违约损失率，再乘以违约风险敞口。 :func:`~kivi.strategy.expected_loss_table` "
"按等级汇总预期损失。银行数据没有贷款金额，因此示例把余额（负值记为零）作为敞口，并对所有客户使用 45% 的违约损失率："

#, python-format
msgid ""
"Grade E holds 6.8% of the exposure but 20.7% of the expected loss of 154,978, and grades D and E "
"together hold 41% of the exposure and 64% of the expected loss."
msgstr "等级 E 只占敞口的 6.8%，却占 154,978 预期损失的 20.7%；等级 D 和 E 合计占敞口的 41%、预期损失的 64%。"

msgid "Report stability"
msgstr "稳定性报告"

msgid ""
"Compare each variable of the monitoring sample with its development distribution. The status "
"column applies the PSI conventions from :doc:`psi`."
msgstr "把监控样本中的每个变量与其开发样本分布比较。status 列采用 :doc:`psi` 中的 PSI 经验口径。"

msgid ""
"Every variable is stable here, as expected when the monitoring rows come from the same "
"population. The ``csi`` column weights each group's change of share with its points, so it is the"
" change of the variable's average points; ``age`` is not in the scorecard and has none. Over the "
"variables of the scorecard, the CSI adds up to the change of the average score:"
msgstr ""
"这里所有变量都是稳定的，监控数据与开发数据来自同一客群时理应如此。 ``csi`` 列用各组的分值对其占比变化加权，因此等于该变量平均分值的变化； ``age`` 不在评分卡中，所以没有 "
"CSI。对评分卡的所有变量求和，CSI 等于平均分的变化："

msgid "The score itself is monitored the same way, with bands fitted on the development scores:"
msgstr "分数本身也按同样的方式监控，使用在开发样本分数上拟合的分段："

msgid ""
":doc:`psi` shows what a shift looks like. In production, "
":func:`~kivi.monitoring.monitoring_table` repeats this PSI for every period together with the "
"known outcomes and the Gini, and :func:`~kivi.monitoring.stability_table` the PSI of every "
"variable; see :doc:`monitoring`. Once the approved loans are booked, :doc:`vintage` follows their"
" delinquency, and :doc:`lifetime` turns it into PD term structures and the IFRS 9 loss allowance."
msgstr ""
":doc:`psi` 展示了分布偏移的样子。在生产环境中， :func:`~kivi.monitoring.monitoring_table` 对每一期重复计算这一 PSI，并给出已知结果和 "
"Gini， :func:`~kivi.monitoring.stability_table` 给出每个变量的 PSI；见 :doc:`monitoring` 。已批准的贷款入账后， "
":doc:`vintage` 跟踪其逾期情况， :doc:`lifetime` 再把它转换为 PD 期限结构和 IFRS 9 损失准备。"

msgid ""
"A scorecard turns a logistic regression on WOE values into points. Every applicant receives the "
"points of their group in each variable, and the points add up to a score that stands for the odds"
" of a good outcome. kivi takes the coefficients and the intercept as plain numbers, so the model "
"can come from any library."
msgstr "评分卡把基于 WOE 的逻辑回归转换为分值。每个申请人在每个变量上获得其所属分组的分值，这些分值相加得到一个代表好结果几率的分数。kivi 把系数和截距当作普通数值接收，因此模型可以来自任何库。"

msgid ""
"The scorecard follows :doc:`variable selection <selection>` and :doc:`reject_inference`, which "
"give the coefficients, and comes before :doc:`metrics`, which evaluates the score. "
":func:`~kivi.scorecard.score_scaling`, :func:`~kivi.scorecard.pd_to_score` and "
":func:`~kivi.scorecard.score_to_pd` set the scale, :func:`~kivi.scorecard.points_table` and "
":func:`~kivi.scorecard.woe_to_points` give the points, and :func:`~kivi.scorecard.reason_codes` "
"explains a score."
msgstr ""
"评分卡位于 :doc:`变量筛选 <selection>` 和 :doc:`reject_inference` 之后（它们给出系数），位于 :doc:`metrics` 之前（后者评估评分）。 "
":func:`~kivi.scorecard.score_scaling` 、 :func:`~kivi.scorecard.pd_to_score` 和 "
":func:`~kivi.scorecard.score_to_pd` 设定刻度， :func:`~kivi.scorecard.points_table` 和 "
":func:`~kivi.scorecard.woe_to_points` 给出分值， :func:`~kivi.scorecard.reason_codes` 解释评分。"

msgid "Scaling"
msgstr "刻度"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"A score is linear in the log of the good:bad odds :math:`o = (1 - \\mathrm{PD}) / \\mathrm{PD}`. "
"Three numbers set the scale: the base score, the odds at the base score and the points to double "
"the odds (PDO):"
msgstr ""
"分数与好坏比 :math:`o = (1 - \\mathrm{PD}) / \\mathrm{PD}` "
"的对数呈线性关系。刻度由三个数决定：基准分数、基准分数对应的几率，以及几率翻倍所需增加的分数（PDO）："

msgid ""
"Every function of :mod:`kivi.scorecard` takes the three numbers as keyword arguments, so keep "
"them together in one dictionary:"
msgstr ":mod:`kivi.scorecard` 的每个函数都以关键字参数接收这三个数，因此可以把它们放在同一个字典里："

msgid ""
"On this scale, odds of 50:1, a PD of 1/51, score 600, and odds of 100:1 score 20 points more. "
":func:`~kivi.scorecard.score_to_pd` converts in the other direction:"
msgstr "在这一刻度下，几率 50:1（即 PD 为 1/51）对应 600 分，几率 100:1 则多 20 分。 :func:`~kivi.scorecard.score_to_pd` 进行反向转换："

msgid ""
"kivi's WOE is :math:`\\ln(p_i / q_i)`, the event share over the non-event share, with the bad "
"outcome as the event (see :doc:`woe_iv`). A higher WOE therefore means more risk, a logistic "
"regression of the bad flag on WOE values has positive coefficients, and a higher WOE gives fewer "
"points. Some textbooks define WOE the other way round; their coefficients and WOE values both "
"change sign, and the points stay the same."
msgstr ""
"kivi 的 WOE 为 :math:`\\ln(p_i / q_i)` ，即事件占比与非事件占比之比的对数，并以坏结果作为事件（参见 :doc:`woe_iv` ）。因此 WOE "
"越高表示风险越高，以坏标记为因变量、以 WOE 为自变量的逻辑回归系数为正，WOE 越高得到的分值越低。有些教材的 WOE 定义方向相反；此时系数和 WOE 值都会变号，而分值保持不变。"

msgid "Points for each group"
msgstr "每个分组的分值"

msgid ""
"The example below builds a small scorecard on the bundled bank data. The data record a marketing "
"response rather than a default, so read target 1 as the bad outcome, as in :doc:`risk_workflow`. "
"Group the development sample and fit the WOE of each variable:"
msgstr ""
"下面的示例在随包附带的银行数据上构建一张小型评分卡。这份数据记录的是营销响应而非违约，因此与 :doc:`risk_workflow` 一样，把 target 为 1 "
"视为坏结果。先对开发样本分组，并拟合每个变量的 WOE："

msgid ""
"A logistic regression of ``target`` on the four WOE columns of the development sample gives the "
"coefficients and the intercept below, rounded to three decimals. "
":func:`~kivi.scorecard.points_table` turns them into points:"
msgstr ""
"在开发样本上以 ``target`` 为因变量、以四个 WOE 列为自变量做逻辑回归，得到下面的系数和截距（保留三位小数）。 "
":func:`~kivi.scorecard.points_table` 把它们转换为分值："

msgid "Group :math:`i` of variable :math:`j`, one of :math:`m` variables, receives"
msgstr "共有 :math:`m` 个变量时，变量 :math:`j` 的第 :math:`i` 组得到"

msgid ""
"\\mathrm{points}_{ij} = \\frac{\\mathrm{offset} - \\mathrm{factor} \\cdot \\beta_0}{m}\n"
"- \\mathrm{factor} \\cdot \\beta_j \\, \\mathrm{WOE}_{ij}."
msgstr ""
"\\mathrm{points}_{ij} = \\frac{\\mathrm{offset} - \\mathrm{factor} \\cdot \\beta_0}{m}\n"
"- \\mathrm{factor} \\cdot \\beta_j \\, \\mathrm{WOE}_{ij}."

msgid ""
"The intercept :math:`\\beta_0` and the offset are spread evenly across the variables, so each of "
"the four variables above carries a quarter of :math:`487.12 + 28.85 \\times 2.028 = 545.64` "
"points. Within a variable, the points of two groups differ only by their WOE term. A group with a"
" WOE of zero, which has the event rate of the whole sample, receives exactly the variable's "
"share."
msgstr ""
"截距 :math:`\\beta_0` 和偏移量平均分摊到各个变量，因此上面四个变量各自承担 :math:`487.12 + 28.85 \\times 2.028 = 545.64` "
"分的四分之一。在同一变量内，两个分组的分值只在 WOE 项上有差别。WOE 为零的分组，其事件率与整个样本相同，恰好得到该变量分摊的份额。"

msgid ""
"A negative coefficient reverses a variable's direction, so that riskier groups receive more "
"points. It usually points to correlated variables; review the signs before scaling a model."
msgstr "负的系数会使变量的方向反转，让风险更高的分组得到更多分值。这通常说明变量之间存在相关性；在对模型做刻度转换之前，请检查系数的符号。"

msgid "Scoring applicants"
msgstr "为申请人评分"

msgid ""
"Encode new applicants with the development WOE tables, as described in :doc:`woe_iv`, and give "
"them the points of each variable with :func:`~kivi.scorecard.woe_to_points`. The row sums are the"
" scores:"
msgstr ""
"按 :doc:`woe_iv` 中的方法，用开发样本的 WOE 表对新申请人编码，再用 :func:`~kivi.scorecard.woe_to_points` "
"给出每个变量的分值。每行之和即为分数："

msgid ""
"The applicant with index 3001: values, groups, WOE, coefficients and points of four variables, "
"and the score"
msgstr "索引为 3001 的申请人：四个变量的取值、分组、WOE、系数和分值，以及总评分"

msgid ""
"Scoring the applicant with index 3001: each value is grouped, encoded with the WOE of its group "
"and turned into points, and the points add up to the score."
msgstr "为索引为 3001 的申请人评分：每个取值先分组，再编码为所在组的 WOE 并换算成分值，各分值相加即为评分。"

msgid ""
"The score is the scaled log odds of the model, so it equals :func:`~kivi.scorecard.pd_to_score` "
"of the model's probability:"
msgstr "分数就是模型对数几率经刻度转换后的结果，因此等于 :func:`~kivi.scorecard.pd_to_score` 对模型概率给出的分数："

msgid ""
"Deployed scorecards usually round the points to whole numbers. Round the points table and the "
"applicant points in the same way, with ``table.round()`` and ``points.round()``: "
"``woe_to_points`` computes each point exactly as :func:`~kivi.scorecard.points_table` does, so "
"the rounded values match. The rounded total can differ from the exact score by up to half a point"
" per variable."
msgstr ""
"上线的评分卡通常把分值取整。请用 ``table.round()`` 和 ``points.round()`` 以同样的方式对分值表和申请人分值取整： ``woe_to_points`` "
"的每个分值与 :func:`~kivi.scorecard.points_table` 的计算方式完全一致，因此取整后的结果也相同。取整后的总分与精确分数之差，每个变量最多半分。"

msgid ""
"A declined applicant is told which variables lowered the score most. "
":func:`~kivi.scorecard.reason_codes` matches the points of each variable to a group of the points"
" table, compares them with those of the variable's best group and lists the variables from the "
"largest shortfall:"
msgstr ""
"被拒绝的申请人会被告知哪些变量让分数降低最多。 :func:`~kivi.scorecard.reason_codes` "
"把每个变量的分值匹配到分值表中的某个分组，与该变量最佳分组的分值比较，并按差距从大到小列出变量："

msgid ""
"Applicant 3000 was contacted by telephone, 21.3 points below the best contact group, and has no "
"housing loan, 13.2 points below the best housing group. Applicant 3001 is in the best group of "
"every variable, so no variable lowered the score."
msgstr ""
"申请人 3000 通过固定电话联系，比 contact 的最佳分组少 21.3 分；没有住房贷款，比 housing 的最佳分组少 13.2 分。申请人 3001 "
"在每个变量上都处于最佳分组，因此没有变量拉低其分数。"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The scaling does not change the order of the reasons, because every shortfall is "
":math:`\\mathrm{factor} \\cdot \\beta_j` times a difference in WOE. Points that match no group of"
" the table within ``atol``, for example points computed with another intercept, raise an error "
"instead of giving reasons against the wrong groups."
msgstr ""
"刻度不会改变原因的顺序，因为每个差距都等于 :math:`\\mathrm{factor} \\cdot \\beta_j` 乘以 WOE 之差。在 ``atol`` "
"范围内无法匹配分值表中任何分组的分值（例如用其他截距算出的分值）会引发错误，而不会对照错误的分组给出原因。"

msgid ""
"Applicants in a group without development observations, such as a new category, have no group of "
"their own in the table. Their WOE comes from ``unseen`` in :func:`~kivi.woe.woe_transform`, a "
"value chosen for the group rather than evidence about the applicant, so by default their points "
"raise an error too. Pass their points as ``unseen_points`` to count them as costing nothing: the "
"variable is then not a reason for those applicants. ``unseen_points`` holds points, not a WOE. "
"Run :func:`~kivi.scorecard.woe_to_points` on a one-row frame that holds the WOE given to "
"``unseen``; a WOE of 0 gives the base points, the same for every variable. Below, the first "
"applicant has a housing status that the development sample did not have:"
msgstr ""
"开发样本中没有观测的分组（例如新类别）里的申请人，在分值表中没有自己的分组。其 WOE 来自 :func:`~kivi.woe.woe_transform` 中的 ``unseen`` "
"，这是为该分组选定的取值，而不是关于申请人的证据，因此默认情况下这些分值同样会引发错误。把它们的分值作为 ``unseen_points`` "
"传入，即可视为没有造成损失：此时该变量不会成为这些申请人的原因。 ``unseen_points`` 是分值而不是 WOE：对包含 ``unseen`` 所给 WOE 的单行数据调用 "
":func:`~kivi.scorecard.woe_to_points` 即可得到；WOE 为 0 时得到基础分值，每个变量都相同。下例中，第一个申请人的住房状况在开发样本中从未出现："

msgid ""
"The first applicant's housing points are those of a WOE of 0, so only the telephone contact is a "
"reason. The second applicant has no housing loan, the less favourable housing group, and is in "
"the best contact group, ``unknown``. Only points near ``unseen_points`` are exempt: points from "
"another model, or WOE values rounded more coarsely than ``atol`` allows, still raise an error."
msgstr ""
"第一个申请人的 housing 分值就是 WOE 为 0 时的分值，因此只有电话联系方式（telephone）是原因。第二个申请人没有住房贷款，属于较不利的住房分组，并且处于最佳的联系方式分组 "
"``unknown`` 。只有接近 ``unseen_points`` 的分值才会豁免：来自其他模型的分值，或舍入比 ``atol`` 允许的更粗的 WOE，仍会引发错误。"

msgid ""
"A model developed on a sample that over- or undersamples bad outcomes has an intercept for that "
"sample. Correct it with :func:`kivi.calibration.corrected_intercept` before building the points "
"table; see :doc:`calibration`."
msgstr ""
"如果开发样本对坏结果做了过采样或欠采样，模型的截距只适用于该样本。在构建分值表之前，请用 :func:`kivi.calibration.corrected_intercept` 校正截距；参见"
" :doc:`calibration` 。"

msgid ""
"A scorecard is a logistic regression on a short list of WOE-encoded variables. "
":mod:`kivi.selection` covers the usual steps from the candidates to that list: drop one variable "
"of each strongly correlated pair, check the rest for collinearity, select variables by their "
"p-values and read the fitted model. Every function takes a DataFrame with one WOE-encoded column "
"per variable, such as the output of :func:`~kivi.woe.woe_transform`, and the functions that fit a"
" model also take the 0/1 target."
msgstr ""
"评分卡是基于少量 WOE 编码变量的逻辑回归。 :mod:`kivi.selection` 涵盖了从候选变量到入选名单的常用步骤：对每一对强相关的变量剔除其中一个，检查其余变量的共线性，按 p "
"值筛选变量，并解读拟合的模型。每个函数都接收一个每个变量一列 WOE 编码值的 DataFrame，例如 :func:`~kivi.woe.woe_transform` "
"的输出；拟合模型的函数还需要 0/1 目标变量。"

msgid ""
"Selection follows :doc:`woe_iv`, which encodes the candidates, and comes before "
":doc:`reject_inference` and the :doc:`scorecard`, which refit and scale the chosen model. "
":func:`~kivi.selection.correlation_filter` drops correlated variables, "
":func:`~kivi.selection.vif` measures collinearity, :func:`~kivi.selection.logistic_regression` "
"fits the model and :func:`~kivi.selection.stepwise` selects its variables."
msgstr ""
"变量筛选位于 :doc:`woe_iv` 之后（后者对候选变量编码），位于 :doc:`reject_inference` 和 :doc:`scorecard` "
"之前（它们重新拟合所选模型并进行刻度）。 :func:`~kivi.selection.correlation_filter` 剔除相关变量， "
":func:`~kivi.selection.vif` 衡量共线性， :func:`~kivi.selection.logistic_regression` 拟合模型， "
":func:`~kivi.selection.stepwise` 筛选模型变量。"

msgid "Preparing the candidates"
msgstr "准备候选变量"

msgid ""
"Group every candidate as in :doc:`risk_workflow`: quantile bins for most numeric variables, "
"explicit edges where tied values would collapse the quantiles, and the raw labels of categorical "
"variables. Then fit one WOE table per variable on the development sample, rank the variables by "
"IV and encode those with an IV of at least 0.02."
msgstr ""
"按 :doc:`risk_workflow` "
"中的方式对每个候选变量分组：多数数值变量使用分位数分箱，重复值会使分位数重合的变量使用显式边界，类别变量直接使用原始标签。然后在开发样本上为每个变量拟合一张 WOE 表，按 IV 排序，并对 "
"IV 不低于 0.02 的变量做 WOE 编码。"

msgid "Correlated variables"
msgstr "相关变量"

msgid ""
"Variables that describe the same behavior carry the same information twice. ``poutcome``, "
"``pdays`` and ``previous`` all describe the previous campaign:"
msgstr "描述同一行为的变量会重复携带相同的信息。 ``poutcome`` 、 ``pdays`` 和 ``previous`` 都描述上一次营销活动："

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.selection.correlation_filter` visits the variables from the highest ``priority`` to "
"the lowest and keeps a variable unless its absolute correlation with a variable already kept "
"exceeds ``threshold`` (0.7 by default). Pass the IV as the priority, so that of two correlated "
"variables the more predictive one stays:"
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.selection.correlation_filter` 按 ``priority`` 从高到低依次考察各变量，若某变量与已保留变量的相关系数绝对值超过 "
"``threshold`` （默认 0.7）则将其剔除，否则保留。把 IV 作为优先级传入，两个相关变量中预测力更强的一个就会被保留："

msgid ""
"``previous`` is dropped for ``pdays``, which has a higher IV. ``poutcome`` and ``pdays`` stay "
"together because their correlation of 0.68 is below the threshold. Thresholds between 0.6 and 0.8"
" are common; a lower one gives a shorter list."
msgstr ""
"``previous`` 因与 IV 更高的 ``pdays`` 相关而被剔除。 ``poutcome`` 与 ``pdays`` 的相关系数为 "
"0.68，低于阈值，因此二者都被保留。常用的阈值在 0.6 到 0.8 之间；阈值越低，入选名单越短。"

msgid "Variance inflation factor"
msgstr "方差膨胀因子"

msgid ""
"A correlation compares two variables, but a variable can also be explained by several others "
"together. The variance inflation factor (VIF) regresses each variable on all the others: it is 1 "
"for a variable that the others do not explain and grows without bound as they explain it "
"completely. The square root of the VIF is the factor by which collinearity inflates the standard "
"error of the variable's coefficient."
msgstr ""
"相关系数只比较两个变量，但一个变量也可能由其他几个变量共同解释。方差膨胀因子（VIF）将每个变量对其他所有变量做回归：其他变量完全无法解释的变量 VIF 为 1；其他变量越接近完全解释它，VIF"
" 越大，且没有上限。VIF 的平方根是共线性使该变量系数的标准误放大的倍数。"

msgid ""
"A common rule of thumb flags a VIF above 5, or above 10, as harmful collinearity. Every value "
"here is well below that, and dropping ``previous`` lowers the VIF of the other two variables of "
"the previous campaign."
msgstr "常见的经验法则把 VIF 高于 5（或高于 10）视为有害的共线性。这里所有的值都远低于这一水平；剔除 ``previous`` 后，另外两个描述上一次营销活动的变量的 VIF 也随之降低。"

msgid "Logistic regression on WOE"
msgstr "基于 WOE 的逻辑回归"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.selection.logistic_regression` fits the model with an intercept and reports each "
"coefficient with its standard error, its Wald z statistic and the two-sided p-value of that "
"statistic. A model with a single WOE-encoded variable shows why WOE suits a logistic regression:"
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.selection.logistic_regression` 拟合带截距项的模型，并报告每个系数及其标准误、Wald z 统计量和该统计量的双侧 p 值。只含一个 "
"WOE 编码变量的模型说明了 WOE 为什么适合逻辑回归："

msgid ""
"kivi defines the WOE of a group as :math:`\\ln(p_i / q_i)`, the log of its share of events over "
"its share of non-events. That equals the log odds of the group minus the log odds of the whole "
"sample, so an intercept equal to the sample log odds and a coefficient of 1 reproduce the log "
"odds of every group exactly. The coefficient is exactly 1 whenever no cell needed smoothing."
msgstr ""
"kivi 将分组的 WOE 定义为 :math:`\\ln(p_i / q_i)` "
"，即其事件占比与非事件占比之比的对数。它等于该组的对数优势减去整个样本的对数优势，因此截距取样本的对数优势、系数取 1，就能精确重现每个组的对数优势。只要没有单元格需要平滑，系数就恰好为 1。"

msgid ""
"With several variables, each coefficient weighs a variable against the others. A higher WOE "
"always means a higher event rate, so every coefficient should be positive. A negative one means "
"that the other variables reverse the variable's effect, usually because of collinearity. In the "
"model with every candidate, ``previous`` gets a negative coefficient:"
msgstr ""
"有多个变量时，每个系数衡量的是一个变量相对于其他变量的权重。WOE "
"越高总是意味着事件率越高，所以每个系数都应为正。负系数表示其他变量反转了该变量的作用，通常源于共线性。在包含全部候选变量的模型中， ``previous`` 的系数为负："

msgid ""
"A scorecard built on that model would give fewer points to customers with more previous contacts,"
" although they subscribe more often."
msgstr "基于这个模型的评分卡会给此前联系次数更多的客户更低的分数，尽管他们的认购率更高。"

msgid "Stepwise selection"
msgstr "逐步回归"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.selection.stepwise` selects the variables of the model by their p-values. With the "
"default ``direction=\"both\"``, it starts from the intercept alone and repeatedly adds the "
"variable with the smallest p-value below ``p_enter`` (0.05), then removes any selected variable "
"whose p-value has risen above ``p_remove`` (0.10). ``direction=\"forward\"`` only adds variables "
"and ``direction=\"backward\"`` starts from every variable and only removes them."
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.selection.stepwise` 按 p 值筛选模型的变量。默认的 ``direction=\"both\"`` 从只含截距的模型开始，反复加入 p 值最小且低于"
" ``p_enter`` （0.05）的变量，然后移除 p 值已升至 ``p_remove`` （0.10）以上的已选变量。 ``direction=\"forward\"`` 只加入变量； "
"``direction=\"backward\"`` 则从全部变量开始，只移除变量。"

msgid "``education`` and ``campaign`` were left out because their p-values stay above 0.05."
msgstr "``education`` 和 ``campaign`` 的 p 值始终高于 0.05，因此未入选。"

msgid ""
"By default, ``positive=True`` keeps every coefficient positive: a variable enters only if all "
"coefficients of the extended model are positive, and a variable whose coefficient is not positive"
" is removed first. Here ``previous`` fails on its p-value anyway. With lenient levels it would "
"pass the p-value test, and only the sign rule keeps it out:"
msgstr ""
"默认的 ``positive=True`` 使每个系数都为正：只有扩展后模型的所有系数都为正时变量才会入选，系数不为正的变量会被优先移除。这里 ``previous`` 本来就因 p "
"值而未能入选。若放宽显著性水平，它能通过 p 值检验，只有符号规则会把它排除在外："

msgid ""
"Stepwise selection tests many models on the same data, so the p-values of the selected model are "
"optimistic. Treat the result as a proposal: review each variable with the business, and check the"
" model on a validation sample before using it."
msgstr "逐步回归在同一份数据上检验了许多模型，因此所选模型的 p 值偏乐观。请把结果当作建议：与业务方逐一审核变量，并在使用前用验证样本检验模型。"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.selection.logistic_regression` and :func:`~kivi.selection.stepwise` take "
"``weights``: frequency weights that count each row as that many identical observations. Integer "
"weights therefore give the same coefficients, standard errors and selection as repeating the "
"rows:"
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.selection.logistic_regression` 和 :func:`~kivi.selection.stepwise` 接受 ``weights`` "
"：把每一行计为相应个数相同观测的频数权重。因此整数权重与重复这些行得到相同的系数、标准误和变量选择："

msgid ""
"The standard errors treat the total weight as the number of independent observations, so they "
"depend on the scale of the weights: doubling every weight divides them by :math:`\\sqrt 2` and "
"lowers every p-value, as doubling the sample would."
msgstr "标准误把总权重当作独立观测的个数，因此取决于权重的尺度：把每个权重加倍会使标准误除以 :math:`\\sqrt 2` ，并降低每个 p 值，就像样本加倍一样。"

msgid ""
"Weights that do not count observations do not give the standard errors of the data. Those of "
"reject inference in :doc:`reject_inference` make them too small. A rejected applicant becomes a "
"bad and a good row whose outcomes are inferred, not observed, and reweighting lets each approved "
"applicant count as several, but all of these rows count as observations. Read the p-values of "
"such a fit as optimistic, and select the variables on the approved applicants."
msgstr ""
"不表示观测个数的权重给不出与数据相符的标准误。 :doc:`reject_inference` "
"中拒绝推断的权重会使标准误偏小：拒绝申请人变成一行坏样本和一行好样本，其结果是推断出来的而不是观测到的；重新加权则让每个获批申请人计为多个申请人，但这些行都被计为观测。应把这类拟合的 p "
"值视为偏乐观的结果，并在获批申请人上选择变量。"

msgid ""
"A scorecard must group and encode every variable in the same way in development, validation and "
"production. :func:`~kivi.spec.fit_spec` bins all the columns of a development sample in one call "
"and measures the WOE of every group. The resulting :class:`~kivi.spec.BinningSpec` groups and "
"encodes any other sample with the same edges and WOE values. It can be saved as JSON and loaded "
"again in production without changing the groups or the encoding."
msgstr ""
"评分卡在开发、验证和生产中必须以同样的方式对每个变量分组和编码。 :func:`~kivi.spec.fit_spec` 一次调用即可对开发样本的所有列分箱，并计算每个分组的 WOE。得到的 "
":class:`~kivi.spec.BinningSpec` 用同样的边界和 WOE 值对任意其他样本分组和编码。它可以保存为 JSON，并在生产环境中重新加载，且不会改变分组和编码。"

msgid ""
"Each column is fitted with the functions of :doc:`binning` and :doc:`woe_iv`, so a column of the "
"specification has exactly the edges and table that those steps give it alone. A specification "
"takes a model to production once the :doc:`credit strategy <strategy>` is set, and the samples "
"that it groups are monitored with the :doc:`population stability index <psi>`."
msgstr ""
"每一列都用 :doc:`binning` 和 :doc:`woe_iv` 中的函数拟合，因此分箱方案中某一列的边界和 WOE 表，与单独对该列执行这些步骤的结果完全相同。确定 "
":doc:`信贷策略 <strategy>` 之后，分箱方案把模型带入生产，它分组的样本再用 :doc:`群体稳定性指标 <psi>` 监控。"

msgid "Screening the candidates"
msgstr "筛选候选变量"

msgid ""
"With the defaults, every numeric column gets five quantile bins and every other column keeps its "
"labels. The information value of each column gives a first ranking. A warning names each column "
"whose tied quantiles leave fewer bins than requested:"
msgstr "使用默认设置时，每个数值列分为五个等频箱，其他列保留其标签。各列的信息值给出初步排序。如果重合的分位数使某一列的箱数少于期望值，警告会指明该列："

msgid ""
"``quick.tables`` maps each column to its :func:`~kivi.woe.woe_table` result. The columns of "
"``frame`` are fitted unless ``columns`` names some of them. Leave the target out: "
":func:`~kivi.spec.fit_spec` raises an error if a column has the name of the ``target`` series."
msgstr ""
"``quick.tables`` 把每一列映射到其 :func:`~kivi.woe.woe_table` 结果。除非 ``columns`` 指定了部分列，否则会拟合 ``frame`` "
"的所有列。请排除目标变量：如果某一列与 ``target`` Series 同名， :func:`~kivi.spec.fit_spec` 会引发错误。"

msgid ""
"Which columns are binned depends on their dtype. Numeric columns, apart from booleans, are "
"binned; columns of any other dtype, such as strings, categories or booleans, keep their labels as"
" groups. To keep integer codes as labels, convert the column to the ``category`` dtype before "
"fitting. A column of dtype ``object`` that holds only numbers raises a warning, because each "
"distinct number would become a group; convert it with ``pandas.to_numeric`` to bin it."
msgstr ""
"哪些列会被分箱取决于其 dtype。数值列（布尔列除外）会被分箱；其他 dtype 的列（例如字符串、类别或布尔列）以其标签作为分组。若要把整数编码当作标签，请在拟合前把该列转换为 "
"``category`` dtype。只含数值的 ``object`` dtype 列会引发警告，因为每个不同的数值都会各成一组；若要对其分箱，请用 ``pandas.to_numeric`` "
"转换。"

msgid "Choosing the binning of each column"
msgstr "为每一列选择分箱方式"

msgid ""
"``method``, ``bins``, ``special`` and ``options`` can each be a dict by column. Here ``balance`` "
"is merged until its WOE is monotonic, ``pdays`` is split by a decision tree with the ``-1`` code "
"(\"not contacted before\") in its own group, and ``age`` gets policy bands. A list of edges in "
"``bins`` is used as given; it must run from ``-inf`` to ``inf``, so that every future value falls"
" into a bin:"
msgstr ""
"``method`` 、 ``bins`` 、 ``special`` 和 ``options`` 都可以是按列的 dict。这里 ``balance`` 合并到 WOE 单调为止， "
"``pdays`` 用决策树切分，并让 ``-1`` 编码（“之前未联系过”）单独成组， ``age`` 使用政策分段。 ``bins`` 中的边界列表按原样使用；它必须从 ``-inf`` "
"延伸到 ``inf`` ，以确保之后的任何取值都能落入某个箱："

msgid ""
"Special codes must be numbers, and infinite values must be special codes, as in "
":func:`~kivi.binning.bin_edges`. The methods are ``\"quantile\"`` and ``\"uniform\"`` for "
"``bin_edges`` and ``\"chimerge\"``, ``\"tree\"`` and ``\"monotonic\"`` for the supervised "
"functions. ``bins`` is passed as ``bins`` to ``bin_edges`` and as ``max_bins`` to the others, and"
" ``options`` holds their remaining arguments, such as ``alpha`` or ``min_bin_share``. "
"``\"monotonic\"`` uses the ``smoothing`` of the specification, so its trend holds in the tables. "
"``weights`` passes sample weights to every binning function and to :func:`~kivi.woe.woe_table`."
msgstr ""
"特殊值编码必须是数值，无穷值必须作为特殊值传入，与 :func:`~kivi.binning.bin_edges` 相同。方法 ``\"quantile\"`` 和 "
"``\"uniform\"`` 对应 ``bin_edges`` ， ``\"chimerge\"`` 、 ``\"tree\"`` 和 ``\"monotonic\"`` 对应有监督分箱函数。"
" ``bins`` 作为 ``bins`` 传给 ``bin_edges`` ，作为 ``max_bins`` 传给其他函数； ``options`` 存放它们的其余参数，例如 "
"``alpha`` 或 ``min_bin_share`` 。 ``\"monotonic\"`` 使用分箱方案的 ``smoothing`` ，因此其单调趋势在 WOE 表中同样成立。 "
"``weights`` 把样本权重传给每个分箱函数和 :func:`~kivi.woe.woe_table` 。"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.spec.fit_spec` never re-bins a column on its own. The legacy ``WOEBatch`` lowered "
"the number of bins until the WOE was monotonic; here the method and its options decide, and a "
"column that should be monotonic is fitted with ``\"monotonic\"``."
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.spec.fit_spec` 从不自行重新分箱。旧版的 ``WOEBatch`` 会不断减少箱数，直到 WOE 单调；这里由方法及其选项决定，需要单调的列请用 "
"``\"monotonic\"`` 拟合。"

msgid "Grouping categorical columns"
msgstr "对类别列分组"

msgid ""
"A categorical column keeps its labels unless ``method`` names it with ``\"rare\"``, which pools "
"rare categories with :func:`~kivi.binning.category_groups`, or ``\"chimerge\"``, which merges "
"categories with similar event rates with :func:`~kivi.binning.chimerge_groups`; see :ref"
":`category-groups`. ``bins`` is then the ``max_groups`` of ``\"chimerge\"``, ``special`` holds "
"labels such as ``\"unknown\"``, and ``options`` the other arguments of the grouping function, "
"such as ``min_share`` or ``min_group_share``. A string ``method`` applies to the numeric columns "
"only, so a categorical column is grouped only when a dict names it:"
msgstr ""
"类别列保留其标签，除非 ``method`` 用 ``\"rare\"`` （用 :func:`~kivi.binning.category_groups` 归并稀有类别）或 "
"``\"chimerge\"`` （用 :func:`~kivi.binning.chimerge_groups` 合并事件率相近的类别）指定该列；见 :ref:`category-"
"groups` 。此时 ``bins`` 是 ``\"chimerge\"`` 的 ``max_groups`` ， ``special`` 存放 ``\"unknown\"`` 这类标签， "
"``options`` 存放分组函数的其他参数，例如 ``min_share`` 或 ``min_group_share`` 。字符串形式的 ``method`` 只作用于数值列，因此只有 "
"dict 指定的类别列才会分组："

msgid ""
"``grouped.groups`` maps each grouped column to its dict from category to group, the result of the"
" grouping function, and :meth:`~kivi.spec.BinningSpec.cut` and "
":meth:`~kivi.spec.BinningSpec.woe_transform` apply it. A category that the grouping does not map "
"keeps its own label in ``cut``, so that :func:`~kivi.stability.psi_table` shows it as a new "
"group, and gets the column's ``unseen`` policy in ``woe_transform``, which raises an error by "
"default:"
msgstr ""
"``grouped.groups`` 把每个已分组的列映射到其从类别到组的 dict，即分组函数的结果， :meth:`~kivi.spec.BinningSpec.cut` 和 "
":meth:`~kivi.spec.BinningSpec.woe_transform` 会应用它。分组映射中没有的类别在 ``cut`` 中保留自身标签，这样 "
":func:`~kivi.stability.psi_table` 会把它显示为一个新组；在 ``woe_transform`` 中则按该列的 ``unseen`` 策略处理，默认会引发错误："

msgid ""
"To change a grouping, edit the dict, measure the WOE of the new groups and replace both with "
"``dataclasses.replace``, which checks that every group of the table is a group of the grouping. "
"Here the customers with an unknown education join those with a primary education:"
msgstr ""
"若要修改分组映射，先编辑 dict，再计算新分组的 WOE，然后用 ``dataclasses.replace`` 同时替换两者；它会检查 WOE "
"表中的每个分组都是分组映射中的组。这里把教育程度未知的客户并入初等教育程度的客户："

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"To give new categories the WOE of one of the groups, for example the group of rare categories, "
"name it in ``unseen`` as ``{\"group\": label}``. :meth:`~kivi.spec.BinningSpec.cut` then assigns "
"them to that group, and :meth:`~kivi.spec.BinningSpec.woe_transform` gives them its WOE, which "
"follows the group when the column is fitted again. Missing values get it as well when the "
"development sample had none:"
msgstr ""
"若要让新类别使用某个组（例如稀有类别组）的 WOE，请在 ``unseen`` 中用 ``{\"group\": label}`` 指定该组。此时 "
":meth:`~kivi.spec.BinningSpec.cut` 把新类别分配到该组， :meth:`~kivi.spec.BinningSpec.woe_transform` "
"让它们使用该组的 WOE；重新拟合该列后，它们使用的仍是该组新的 WOE。开发样本没有缺失值时，缺失值也使用该组的 WOE："

msgid "Grouping and encoding a sample"
msgstr "对样本分组和编码"

msgid ""
":meth:`~kivi.spec.BinningSpec.cut` groups every column of a sample, and "
":meth:`~kivi.spec.BinningSpec.woe_transform` replaces each group with its WOE. Both return the "
"columns of the specification in its order, with the index of the sample:"
msgstr ""
":meth:`~kivi.spec.BinningSpec.cut` 对样本的每一列分组， :meth:`~kivi.spec.BinningSpec.woe_transform` "
"把每个分组替换为其 WOE。二者都按分箱方案的顺序返回其中的列，索引与样本相同："

msgid ""
"A column fitted as numeric must have a numeric dtype in every sample. Read as strings, the code "
"``\"-1\"`` would miss its special group, so ``cut`` and ``woe_transform`` raise an error instead;"
" convert such a column with ``pandas.to_numeric``:"
msgstr ""
"按数值列拟合的列在每个样本中都必须是数值 dtype。如果按字符串读入，编码 ``\"-1\"`` 就无法匹配其特殊值分组，因此 ``cut`` 和 ``woe_transform`` "
"会引发错误；请用 ``pandas.to_numeric`` 转换这样的列："

msgid ""
"A value whose group is not in its column's table, such as a new category, raises an error by "
"default, so it never turns into a silent NaN:"
msgstr "分组不在该列 WOE 表中的取值（例如新类别）默认会引发错误，因此不会悄无声息地变成 NaN："

msgid ""
"The ``unseen`` argument of :func:`~kivi.spec.fit_spec` sets a WOE for such values, for all "
"columns or by column. The same holds for a special code or an interval that has no development "
"observations, and for missing values when the development sample had none. A specification is "
"immutable, so change the policy of a fitted one with ``dataclasses.replace``:"
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.spec.fit_spec` 的 ``unseen`` 参数为这类取值指定 "
"WOE，可以对所有列统一指定，也可以按列指定。开发样本中没有观测值的特殊值或区间，以及开发样本没有缺失值时的缺失值，也同样处理。分箱方案不可变，因此请用 "
"``dataclasses.replace`` 修改已拟合方案的策略："

msgid "Keeping the model variables"
msgstr "保留模型变量"

msgid ""
"After variable selection, keep only the variables of the model before saving the specification "
"for production:"
msgstr "完成变量筛选后，在为生产环境保存分箱方案之前，只保留模型中的变量："

msgid ""
"``production.tables`` can be passed to :func:`~kivi.scorecard.points_table` as it is; see "
":doc:`scorecard`."
msgstr "``production.tables`` 可以直接传给 :func:`~kivi.scorecard.points_table` ；参见 :doc:`scorecard` 。"

msgid "Saving and loading a specification"
msgstr "保存和加载分箱方案"

msgid ""
":meth:`~kivi.spec.BinningSpec.to_json` writes the specification as JSON text, and "
":meth:`~kivi.spec.BinningSpec.from_json` reads it back into an equal specification that groups "
"and encodes every sample identically. Two specifications are equal when their JSON text is the "
"same, which includes the version of kivi that fitted them:"
msgstr ""
":meth:`~kivi.spec.BinningSpec.to_json` 把分箱方案写成 JSON 文本， :meth:`~kivi.spec.BinningSpec.from_json` "
"将其读回为相等的分箱方案，对每个样本的分组和编码完全相同。两个分箱方案的 JSON 文本相同时二者相等，文本中包含拟合它们的 kivi 版本："

msgid ""
"A specification saved by an earlier release of kivi loads and encodes as it did, but it differs "
"from the same fit made today, because equality includes ``kivi_version``. To compare the content "
"only, give the saved specification the version of the new one with ``dataclasses.replace``. Here "
"``saved`` stands for a file written by kivi 0.7.0:"
msgstr ""
"由 kivi 较早版本保存的分箱方案仍按原样加载和编码，但它与今天做出的同一拟合结果不相等，因为相等比较包含 ``kivi_version`` 。若只比较内容，可用 "
"``dataclasses.replace`` 把新方案的版本赋给已保存的方案。这里的 ``saved`` 代表由 kivi 0.7.0 写出的文件："

msgid ""
"Equality compares every digit, and NumPy picks its vectorized routines by the processor, so the "
"same fit repeated on another computer can differ in the last digit of a WOE and then compare "
"unequal."
msgstr "相等比较的是每一位数字，而 NumPy 根据处理器选择向量化例程，因此在另一台计算机上重复同一拟合时，WOE 的最后一位数字可能不同，比较结果便为不相等。"

msgid ":doc:`/api/compatibility` lists what later releases promise for saved files."
msgstr ":doc:`/api/compatibility` 列出了以后的版本对已保存文件的承诺。"

msgid ""
"The same specification always gives the same text, so it can be kept under version control and "
"compared. Labels are written as they are, including non-ASCII ones, so save the text as UTF-8:"
msgstr "同一个分箱方案总是得到相同的文本，因此可以纳入版本控制并相互比较。标签按原样写出（包括非 ASCII 标签），因此请以 UTF-8 保存文本："

msgid ""
":meth:`~kivi.spec.BinningSpec.to_dict` gives the same content as a dict. Each column is one entry"
" of ``variables``:"
msgstr ":meth:`~kivi.spec.BinningSpec.to_dict` 以 dict 给出相同的内容。每一列是 ``variables`` 中的一项："

msgid ""
"The pdays column from the development sample to the fitted specification, its JSON text, and a "
"monitoring sample encoded with the loaded specification"
msgstr "pdays 列从开发样本到拟合出的分箱方案、方案的 JSON 文本，以及用加载后的方案编码的监控样本"

msgid ""
"A specification from the fit to production, followed for ``pdays``. ``fit_spec`` fits the edges "
"and the WOE table on the development sample, ``to_json`` writes them with the exact edges, and "
"the specification loaded with ``from_json`` groups and encodes a monitoring sample in the same "
"way."
msgstr ""
"以 ``pdays`` 为例，跟踪分箱方案从拟合到投产的过程。 ``fit_spec`` 在开发样本上拟合边界和 WOE 表， ``to_json`` 按精确的边界写出它们，用 "
"``from_json`` 加载的方案以完全相同的方式对监控样本分组和编码。"

msgid "The format"
msgstr "格式"

msgid "Key"
msgstr "键"

msgid "Content"
msgstr "内容"

msgid "``format``"
msgstr "``format``"

msgid "Always ``\"kivi.BinningSpec\"``."
msgstr "始终为 ``\"kivi.BinningSpec\"`` 。"

msgid "``format_version``"
msgstr "``format_version``"

msgid ""
"Version of the format: 2 when a column is grouped, otherwise 1, which earlier versions of kivi "
"read as well. ``BinningSpec.FORMAT_VERSION`` is the newest version. A file with a newer version "
"raises an error that asks for a newer kivi, instead of being read in part."
msgstr ""
"格式的版本：有已分组的列时为 2，否则为 1，早期版本的 kivi 也能读取版本 1。 ``BinningSpec.FORMAT_VERSION`` "
"是最新的版本。版本更新的文件会引发错误，提示升级 kivi，而不会只读取其中一部分。"

msgid "``kivi_version``"
msgstr "``kivi_version``"

msgid "Version of kivi that fitted the specification."
msgstr "拟合该分箱方案的 kivi 版本。"

msgid "``smoothing``"
msgstr "``smoothing``"

msgid ""
"Smoothing of the WOE tables. It records the fit: changing it, for example with "
"``dataclasses.replace``, recomputes nothing."
msgstr "WOE 表的平滑参数。它只记录拟合时的设置：修改它（例如用 ``dataclasses.replace`` ）不会重新计算任何内容。"

msgid "``variables``"
msgstr "``variables``"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"One entry per column, in order, with ``name``, ``kind`` (``\"numeric\"`` or ``\"categorical\"``),"
" ``unseen`` (``\"raise\"``, a number or, for a grouped column, ``{\"group\": label}``) and "
"``table``, plus ``edges`` and ``special`` for numeric columns and ``groups`` for grouped "
"categorical columns."
msgstr ""
"每列一项，按顺序排列，包含 ``name`` 、 ``kind`` （ ``\"numeric\"`` 或 ``\"categorical\"`` ）、 ``unseen`` （ "
"``\"raise\"`` 、数值，或对已分组的列为 ``{\"group\": label}`` ）和 ``table`` ，数值列另有 ``edges`` 和 ``special`` "
"，已分组的类别列另有 ``groups`` 。"

msgid "``groups``"
msgstr "``groups``"

msgid "One entry per group, in order, with its label ``group`` and the list of its ``categories``."
msgstr "每组一项，按顺序排列，包含其标签 ``group`` 和类别列表 ``categories`` 。"

msgid "``table``"
msgstr "``table``"

msgid ""
"One entry per group with its label ``bin`` and the columns of :func:`~kivi.woe.woe_table`. An "
"interval of a numeric column is written with the two exact edges that bound it. Encoding reads "
"only ``bin`` and ``woe``; the other columns describe the fit and are loaded as written, with the "
"same keys in every entry."
msgstr ""
"每个分组一项，包含其标签 ``bin`` 和 :func:`~kivi.woe.woe_table` 的各列。数值列的区间用界定它的两个精确边界写出。编码只读取 ``bin`` 和 "
"``woe`` ；其他列描述拟合结果，按写入时的内容加载，每一项的键都必须相同。"

msgid ""
"JSON has no infinite numbers and does not keep the types of labels apart in every language, so "
"labels and edges are written as follows:"
msgstr "JSON 没有无穷数值，在某些语言中也无法区分标签的类型，因此标签和边界按以下方式写出："

msgid "Value"
msgstr "取值"

msgid "JSON"
msgstr "JSON"

msgid "Strings, integers and booleans"
msgstr "字符串、整数和布尔值"

msgid "As they are: ``\"yes\"``, ``1``, ``true``."
msgstr "按原样写出： ``\"yes\"`` 、 ``1`` 、 ``true`` 。"

msgid "Floats"
msgstr "浮点数"

msgid "With a decimal point or an exponent, such as ``1.0``, so that they stay apart from integers."
msgstr "带小数点或指数，例如 ``1.0`` ，以便与整数区分。"

msgid "Infinite numbers"
msgstr "无穷数值"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "``{\"float\": \"inf\"}`` and ``{\"float\": \"-inf\"}``."
msgstr "``{\"float\": \"inf\"}`` 和 ``{\"float\": \"-inf\"}`` 。"

msgid "Intervals"
msgstr "区间"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "``{\"interval\": [left, right], \"closed\": \"right\"}``."
msgstr "``{\"interval\": [left, right], \"closed\": \"right\"}`` 。"

msgid "The missing group"
msgstr "缺失组"

msgid "``null``."
msgstr "``null`` 。"

msgid ""
"Labels of categorical columns must be strings, integers, floats, booleans or intervals; "
":func:`~kivi.spec.fit_spec` rejects other labels, such as dates. "
":meth:`~kivi.spec.BinningSpec.from_json` checks every value and rejects ``NaN`` or ``Infinity`` "
"in the text, so a damaged file fails with a message instead of encoding wrong values."
msgstr ""
"类别列的标签必须是字符串、整数、浮点数、布尔值或区间； :func:`~kivi.spec.fit_spec` 会拒绝其他标签，例如日期。 "
":meth:`~kivi.spec.BinningSpec.from_json` 会检查每个值，并拒绝文本中的 ``NaN`` 或 ``Infinity`` "
"，因此损坏的文件会报错，而不会编码出错误的值。"

msgid ""
"The interval labels of a table are those of ``pandas.cut``, which rounds their bounds for "
"display. The file writes each interval of a numeric column with its two exact edges instead, and "
"``from_json`` turns them back into the labels of ``pandas.cut``:"
msgstr ""
"表中的区间标签来自 ``pandas.cut`` ，其边界为便于显示而经过舍入。文件改用两个精确边界写出数值列的每个区间， ``from_json`` 再把它们还原为 "
"``pandas.cut`` 的标签："

msgid ""
"Software outside kivi that reads the file should bin with ``edges``, match ``special`` codes "
"before intervals as :func:`kivi.binning.cut` does, and find the row of each interval by its two "
"edges. An interval without development observations has no row. Intervals are closed on the "
"right. An infinite value that is not a special code falls into no group, and "
":meth:`~kivi.spec.BinningSpec.woe_transform` treats it as unseen. For a grouped column, look up "
"the category of each value in ``groups`` and then the row of its group; a category that "
"``groups`` does not list is unseen."
msgstr ""
"在 kivi 之外读取该文件的软件应使用 ``edges`` 分箱，像 :func:`kivi.binning.cut` 一样先匹配 ``special`` "
"编码再匹配区间，并按两个边界找到每个区间对应的行。开发样本中没有观测值的区间没有对应的行。区间为左开右闭。不属于特殊值编码的无穷值不落入任何组， "
":meth:`~kivi.spec.BinningSpec.woe_transform` 把它视为未见分组。对于已分组的列，先在 ``groups`` "
"中查到每个取值的类别所属的组，再找到该组对应的行； ``groups`` 中没有列出的类别视为未见类别。"

msgid ""
"A scorecard ranks applicants; a credit strategy decides whom to approve. :mod:`kivi.strategy` "
"supports the decisions that follow: :func:`~kivi.strategy.cutoff_table` shows what each candidate"
" cut-off approves and how many bad outcomes it lets through, "
":func:`~kivi.strategy.confusion_table` counts the right and the wrong decisions of each cut-off, "
":func:`~kivi.strategy.swap_set` compares the decisions of a current and a new score, and "
":func:`~kivi.strategy.expected_loss` and :func:`~kivi.strategy.expected_loss_table` turn PDs, "
"LGDs and exposures into the expected loss of each applicant and of each grade."
msgstr ""
"评分卡对申请人排序，信贷策略决定通过哪些申请人。:mod:`kivi.strategy` 支撑随后的决策：:func:`~kivi.strategy.cutoff_table` "
"显示每个候选截断点通过哪些申请人、放进多少坏结果，:func:`~kivi.strategy.confusion_table` "
"统计每个截断点正确和错误的决策，:func:`~kivi.strategy.swap_set` "
"比较现行评分与新评分的决策，:func:`~kivi.strategy.expected_loss` 和 :func:`~kivi.strategy.expected_loss_table` 将"
" PD、LGD 和敞口转换为每个申请人和每个等级的预期损失。"

msgid ""
"The strategy follows :doc:`calibration`, which gives PDs and grades, and comes before the "
":doc:`binning specifications <spec>` that take the model to production."
msgstr "信贷策略位于 :doc:`calibration` 之后（后者给出 PD 和等级），位于把模型带入生产的 :doc:`分箱方案 <spec>` 之前。"

msgid "Score direction and the approval rule"
msgstr "评分方向与通过规则"

msgid ""
"As in :doc:`metrics`, every score is higher for a higher risk, such as a PD. An applicant is "
"approved when the score is at or below the cut-off, so a higher cut-off approves more applicants."
" A score equal to the cut-off is approved, and tied scores therefore always get the same "
"decision."
msgstr ""
"与 :doc:`metrics` 相同，所有评分都是风险越高、评分越高，例如 "
"PD。评分不高于截断点的申请人予以通过，因此截断点越高，通过的申请人越多。等于截断点的评分予以通过，所以相同评分总是得到相同的决策。"

msgid ""
"Scorecard points run the other way: a policy that approves 600 points or more approves the "
"applicants whose negated points are at most -600. Pass ``-points`` and the negated cut-offs, for "
"example ``cutoff_table(-points, target, cutoffs=[-620, -600, -580])``."
msgstr ""
"评分卡分数方向相反：通过 600 分及以上的策略，等于通过取负分数不超过 -600 的申请人。请传入 ``-points`` 和取负后的截断点，例如 "
"``cutoff_table(-points, target, cutoffs=[-620, -600, -580])`` 。"

msgid "PDs of two scorecards"
msgstr "两张评分卡的 PD"

msgid ""
"The examples on this page use the bundled bank data. The data record a marketing response rather "
"than a default, so read target 1 as a default, as in :doc:`scorecard`. The first 3,000 rows are "
"the development sample and the remaining 1,521 rows stand for the applicants of a later period. "
"Two logistic regressions on WOE values give the PDs of a current scorecard with four variables "
"and of a new one that adds ``loan`` and ``marital``:"
msgstr ""
"本页示例使用内置的银行数据。该数据记录的是营销响应而非违约，因此与 :doc:`scorecard` 一样，将目标值 1 视为违约。前 3,000 行为开发样本，其余 1,521 "
"行代表后一时期的申请人。基于 WOE 值的两个逻辑回归分别给出现行评分卡（四个变量）和新评分卡（增加 ``loan`` 和 ``marital`` ）的 PD："

msgid "The new scorecard ranks the applicants a little better:"
msgstr "新评分卡对申请人的排序略好一些："

msgid "Choosing a cut-off"
msgstr "选择截断点"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.strategy.cutoff_table` takes the candidate cut-offs and reports, for each, the "
"approved book and what the cut-off rejects. A PD of 1 approves everyone and gives the reference "
"row:"
msgstr ":func:`~kivi.strategy.cutoff_table` 接收候选截断点，并对每个截断点报告通过客群以及被拒绝的部分。PD 为 1 的截断点通过所有人，给出参照行："

#, python-format
msgid ""
"Each row is a possible policy. A cut-off of 0.10 approves 784 of the 1,521 applicants, 51.5%, and"
" their bad rate of 6.25% is about half the 11.4% of all applicants. It avoids 71.7% of the bad "
"outcomes, but also turns away 45.5% of the good applicants. Raising the cut-off to 0.15 approves "
"87.4% at a bad rate of 8.3%: the lender gains volume and accepts more risk. Which row to choose "
"is a business decision; the table shows its price."
msgstr ""
"每一行都是一种可能的策略。截断点 0.10 通过 1,521 名申请人中的 784 名，即 51.5%，其坏账率为 6.25%，约为全部申请人 11.4% 的一半。它避开了 71.7% "
"的坏结果，但也拒绝了 45.5% 的好申请人。将截断点提高到 0.15，通过率为 87.4%，坏账率为 "
"8.3%：放款机构获得了更多业务量，也承担了更多风险。选择哪一行是业务决策，表中给出了每种选择的代价。"

msgid "Applicants with a score at or below the cut-off."
msgstr "评分不高于截断点的申请人数。"

msgid "``approval_rate``"
msgstr "``approval_rate``"

msgid "Share of all applicants that the cut-off approves."
msgstr "截断点通过的申请人占全部申请人的比例。"

msgid "``approved_event``, ``approved_event_rate``"
msgstr "``approved_event``, ``approved_event_rate``"

msgid "Events among the approved applicants and their rate, the bad rate of the approved book."
msgstr "通过的申请人中的事件数及其比率，即通过客群的坏账率。"

msgid "``rejected_event_share``"
msgstr "``rejected_event_share``"

msgid "Share of all events with a score above the cut-off: the bad outcomes the cut-off avoids."
msgstr "评分高于截断点的事件占全部事件的比例，即该截断点避开的坏结果。"

msgid "``rejected_non_event_share``"
msgstr "``rejected_non_event_share``"

msgid "Share of all non-events with a score above the cut-off: the good business the cut-off gives up."
msgstr "评分高于截断点的非事件占全部非事件的比例，即该截断点放弃的好业务。"

msgid "``approved_loss``"
msgstr "``approved_loss``"

msgid "With ``loss``, the sum of the losses of the approved applicants; see below."
msgstr "传入 ``loss`` 时，通过的申请人的损失之和；见下文。"

msgid ""
"The bad rate of the approved book averages over everyone approved. The cut-off itself is better "
"judged by the marginal bad rate, the bad rate of the applicants that a higher cut-off adds:"
msgstr "通过客群的坏账率是对所有通过者的平均。评判截断点本身，更适合看边际坏账率，即提高截断点后新增申请人的坏账率："

msgid ""
"Suppose a good loan earns a margin :math:`m` and a bad loan loses :math:`L`. A group of "
"applicants with bad rate :math:`b` earns :math:`(1 - b)\\,m - b L`, which is positive while "
":math:`b < m / (m + L)`. With a margin of 1 and a loss of 10 the break-even bad rate is "
":math:`1/11 \\approx 9.1\\%`. The applicants between 0.05 and 0.08 default at 5.6% and pay for "
"themselves, while those between 0.08 and 0.10 default at 10.4% and do not, so 0.08 is the most "
"profitable of these cut-offs. For a well-calibrated PD the break-even rate is itself the PD cut-"
"off; the marginal rates check it against the observed outcomes."
msgstr ""
"假设一笔好贷款赚取利润 :math:`m`，一笔坏贷款损失 :math:`L`。坏账率为 :math:`b` 的一组申请人带来 :math:`(1 - b)\\,m - b L` 的收益，当 "
":math:`b < m / (m + L)` 时为正。利润为 1、损失为 10 时，盈亏平衡坏账率为 :math:`1/11 \\approx 9.1\\%`。PD 在 0.05 到 0.08"
" 之间的申请人违约率为 5.6%，能够覆盖自身的损失；而 0.08 到 0.10 之间的申请人违约率为 10.4%，无法覆盖，因此在这些截断点中 0.08 的利润最高。对于校准良好的 "
"PD，盈亏平衡坏账率本身就是 PD 截断点；边际坏账率则用实际结果对其加以检验。"

msgid ""
"An integer ``cutoffs`` places the cut-offs at the quantile edges of "
":func:`~kivi.binning.bin_edges`, so that the rows approve about a fifth, two fifths and so on of "
"the applicants. Tied scores move the steps, because all applicants with the same score get the "
"same decision:"
msgstr ""
"整数 ``cutoffs`` 将截断点放在 :func:`~kivi.binning.bin_edges` "
"的分位数边界上，使各行大约通过五分之一、五分之二……的申请人。相同评分会使各级的位置偏移，因为评分相同的申请人总是得到相同的决策："

msgid "Confusion matrix"
msgstr "混淆矩阵"

msgid ""
"A cut-off is also a classifier: it predicts an event for every applicant it declines. "
":func:`~kivi.strategy.confusion_table` counts, at each cut-off, how those predictions match the "
"outcomes, with an event as the positive class and a decline as the positive prediction:"
msgstr ""
"截断点也是一个分类器：它对每个被拒绝的申请人预测为事件。 :func:`~kivi.strategy.confusion_table` "
"在每个截断点上统计这些预测与结果的吻合情况，以事件为正类，拒绝为正预测："

msgid "``true_positive``"
msgstr "``true_positive``"

msgid "Events with a score above the cut-off: the bad outcomes it avoids."
msgstr "评分高于截断点的事件，即该截断点避开的坏结果。"

msgid "``false_positive``"
msgstr "``false_positive``"

msgid "Non-events with a score above the cut-off: the good business it gives up."
msgstr "评分高于截断点的非事件，即该截断点放弃的好业务。"

msgid "``true_negative``"
msgstr "``true_negative``"

msgid "Non-events at or below the cut-off: the good business it keeps."
msgstr "评分不高于截断点的非事件，即该截断点保留的好业务。"

msgid "``false_negative``"
msgstr "``false_negative``"

msgid "Events at or below the cut-off: the bad outcomes it lets through."
msgstr "评分不高于截断点的事件，即该截断点放进的坏结果。"

msgid "``precision``"
msgstr "``precision``"

msgid ""
"``true_positive`` divided by the declined applicants, the event rate among them. It is NaN when "
"the cut-off declines nobody."
msgstr "``true_positive`` 除以被拒绝的申请人数，即其中的事件率。截断点不拒绝任何申请人时为 NaN。"

msgid "``recall``"
msgstr "``recall``"

msgid "Share of all events that the cut-off declines."
msgstr "截断点拒绝的事件占全部事件的比例。"

msgid "``f1``"
msgstr "``f1``"

msgid "The harmonic mean of ``precision`` and ``recall``; 0 when no event is declined."
msgstr " ``precision`` 和 ``recall`` 的调和平均；没有事件被拒绝时为 0。"

msgid "``accuracy``"
msgstr "``accuracy``"

msgid "Share of applicants whose decision matches the outcome: declined events and approved non-events."
msgstr "决策与结果相符的申请人所占比例：被拒绝的事件和被通过的非事件。"

#, python-format
msgid ""
"A cut-off of 0.10 declines 737 applicants, 124 of them events. It declines 71.7% of the events, "
"and 16.8% of the declined applicants are events, 1.5 times the 11.4% of all applicants. The rows "
"are those of :func:`~kivi.strategy.cutoff_table`: ``recall`` is its ``rejected_event_share``, "
"``false_negative`` its ``approved_event``, and ``false_positive`` divided by all non-events its "
"``rejected_non_event_share``. The table adds the counts that these shares are made of, and the "
"measures of a classifier:"
msgstr ""
"0.10 的截断点拒绝 737 名申请人，其中 124 名是事件。它拒绝了 71.7% 的事件，而被拒绝的申请人中 16.8% 是事件，是全部申请人 11.4% 的 1.5 倍。各行与 "
":func:`~kivi.strategy.cutoff_table` 的行对应： ``recall`` 就是它的 ``rejected_event_share`` ， "
"``false_negative`` 就是它的 ``approved_event`` ， ``false_positive`` 占全部非事件的比例就是它的 "
"``rejected_non_event_share`` 。这张表补上了这些比例所依据的计数，以及分类器的各项指标："

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.metrics.roc_table` has the same counts at every distinct score, but its rows flag "
"the scores at or above a threshold, while a cut-off declines only those above it. A row of "
"``confusion_table`` equals the ``roc_table`` row with the lowest threshold above the cut-off:"
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.metrics.roc_table` 给出每个不同评分处的同样计数，但它的各行标记评分不低于阈值的观测，而截断点只拒绝高于它的观测。 "
"``confusion_table`` 的一行等于 ``roc_table`` 中阈值高于截断点的最低一行："

#, python-format
msgid ""
"These measures depend on the share of events. Approving everyone, the last row, is right about "
"88.6% of the applicants, one minus the event rate, so among these cut-offs the accuracy is "
"highest for the one that declines nobody. Precision stays low for the same reason. The F1 score "
"is highest at 0.20, which declines 111 applicants, 7.3%, but it counts a declined good applicant "
"and an approved bad one as equally costly. With the margin of 1 and the loss of 10 above, the "
"second error costs ten times the first, and the cut-off of 0.08 that pays most there has an F1 of"
" 0.26. Use these measures to compare scores or to report a classification at a chosen cut-off, "
"and choose the cut-off from the marginal bad rate and the costs, as above."
msgstr ""
"这些指标取决于事件占比。通过所有申请人（最后一行）的决策对 88.6% 的申请人是正确的，即 1 "
"减去事件率，因此在这些截断点中，不拒绝任何人的截断点准确率最高。精确率也因同样的原因保持在低位。F1 分数在 0.20 处最高，该截断点拒绝 111 名申请人，占 "
"7.3%，但它把拒绝一个好申请人与通过一个坏申请人视为同等代价。按上文利润 1、损失 10 计算，后一种错误的代价是前一种的十倍，而在那里获利最多的 0.08 截断点，F1 只有 "
"0.26。这些指标适合用来比较评分，或报告所选截断点下的分类结果；截断点本身应像上文那样，根据边际坏账率和成本来选。"

msgid ""
"Unlike :func:`~kivi.strategy.swap_set`, ``confusion_table`` takes no missing outcomes: remove the"
" applicants whose outcome is unknown, or fill it in with reject inference, before counting."
msgstr "与 :func:`~kivi.strategy.swap_set` 不同， ``confusion_table`` 不接受缺失的结果：计数前请先去掉结果未知的申请人，或用拒绝推断补上这些结果。"

msgid "Swap sets"
msgstr "交换集"

msgid ""
"A new score changes the decisions of some applicants. At the cut-offs of both scores, "
":func:`~kivi.strategy.swap_set` sorts the applicants into four groups: those both scores approve,"
" the swap-outs that only the current score approves, the swap-ins that only the new score "
"approves, and those both decline. To compare the scores at the same approval rate, give the new "
"score the cut-off that approves as many applicants as the current cut-off of 0.10:"
msgstr ""
"新评分会改变部分申请人的决策。在两个评分各自的截断点上，:func:`~kivi.strategy.swap_set` 将申请人分为四组：两个评分都通过的、只有现行评分通过的换出（swap-"
"out）、只有新评分通过的换入（swap-in），以及两个评分都拒绝的。为了在相同通过率下比较两个评分，给新评分设定一个截断点，使其通过的申请人数与现行截断点 0.10 相同："

msgid ""
"The new score swaps out 105 applicants with a bad rate of 15.2% and swaps in 118 with a bad rate "
"of 6.8%. Because of tied scores, its cut-off approves 797 applicants, 13 more than the current "
"one, and the bad rate of the approved book falls from 6.25% to 5.1%:"
msgstr ""
"新评分换出 105 名坏账率为 15.2% 的申请人，换入 118 名坏账率为 6.8% 的申请人。由于存在相同评分，其截断点通过 797 名申请人，比现行截断点多 13 名，通过客群的坏账率从"
" 6.25% 降至 5.1%："

msgid ""
"Bad rate of the approved book against the approval rate for the current and the new score, with "
"the cut-offs of the swap set marked"
msgstr "现行评分与新评分在各通过率下的通过客群坏账率，并标出交换集所用的截断点"

msgid ""
"The bad rate of the approved book at each approval rate. Up to an approval rate of about 65%, the"
" new score approves a book with a lower bad rate; above it, the two curves run close together, "
"with the new score mostly a little higher. The points mark the cut-offs of the swap set."
msgstr "各通过率下通过客群的坏账率。通过率约在 65% 以下时，新评分批准的客群坏账率更低；超过这一水平后，两条曲线相距很近，新评分大多略高。图中的点标出交换集所用的截断点。"

msgid ""
"A new score is worth adopting when its swap-ins are better than its swap-outs; the applicants "
"both scores approve or decline do not change. The row shares give the approval rate of each "
"score, for example ``swaps[\"share\"].xs(\"approve\", level=\"new\").sum()`` for the new one."
msgstr ""
"当换入优于换出时，新评分才值得采用；两个评分都通过或都拒绝的申请人不受影响。各行的比例给出每个评分的通过率，例如新评分的通过率为 "
"``swaps[\"share\"].xs(\"approve\", level=\"new\").sum()`` 。"

msgid ""
"In practice the outcomes of the swap-ins are unknown: the current score declined them, so they "
"never received a loan. Pass a target with missing values for unknown outcomes. They count in "
"``total`` and ``share`` but not in ``known``, ``event`` and ``event_rate``:"
msgstr ""
"实际上，换入申请人的结果是未知的：现行评分拒绝了他们，所以他们从未获得贷款。对结果未知的申请人，在目标值中传入缺失值。他们计入 ``total`` 和 ``share``，但不计入 "
"``known``、``event`` 和 ``event_rate``："

msgid ""
"The swap-outs are known, but the bad rate of the swap-ins is missing, and with it half of the "
"comparison. Reject inference, described in :doc:`reject_inference`, estimates the outcomes of "
"declined applicants from their scores and the outcomes of similar approved ones. Pass the "
"inferred labels, or the augmented sample with its weights, to fill in the table, and treat the "
"result as an estimate: it depends on the assumptions of the inference."
msgstr ""
"换出申请人的结果已知，但换入申请人的坏账率缺失，比较也就缺了一半。 :doc:`reject_inference` "
"中介绍的拒绝推断，根据被拒申请人的评分和相似的已通过申请人的结果，估计被拒申请人的结果。传入推断得到的标签，或带权重的扩充样本，即可补全该表；但应把结果视为估计值，它取决于推断所依据的假设。"

msgid "Expected loss"
msgstr "预期损失"

msgid ""
"The expected loss of an exposure is the product of its probability of default, its loss given "
"default and its exposure at default:"
msgstr "一笔敞口的预期损失是其违约概率、违约损失率与违约风险敞口的乘积："

#, python-format
msgid ""
"The bank data have no loan amounts, so the examples take the average balance as the exposure, "
"with negative balances set to zero, and one LGD of 45% for all applicants. "
":func:`~kivi.strategy.expected_loss` accepts one value or one per applicant for the LGD and the "
"EAD, and keeps the index of a Series:"
msgstr ""
"银行数据中没有贷款金额，因此示例以平均余额作为敞口，负余额记为零，所有申请人的 LGD 均取 45%。:func:`~kivi.strategy.expected_loss` 的 LGD 和 "
"EAD 可以是一个值，也可以每个申请人一个值，并保留 Series 的索引："

msgid ""
"Pass the expected losses as ``loss`` to :func:`~kivi.strategy.cutoff_table` to add the expected "
"loss of the approved book:"
msgstr "将预期损失作为 ``loss`` 传给 :func:`~kivi.strategy.cutoff_table`，即可加入通过客群的预期损失："

msgid ""
"Approving everyone carries an expected loss of 125,487, or 82.50 per applicant. A cut-off of 0.10"
" approves half of the applicants and only a fifth of that expected loss, 35.26 per approved "
"applicant. ``approved_loss`` adds up whatever is passed as ``loss``: pass realized losses to see "
"the losses each cut-off lets through, whose difference from the last row is the loss it avoids, "
"or pass the exposures to see the volume it approves."
msgstr ""
"通过所有人时，预期损失为 125,487，即每名申请人 82.50。截断点 0.10 通过一半申请人，预期损失却只有其五分之一，即每名通过的申请人 35.26。``approved_loss``"
" 对作为 ``loss`` 传入的任何金额求和：传入实际损失，可看到每个截断点放进来的损失，它与最后一行之差就是该截断点避开的损失；传入敞口，可看到它通过的业务量。"

msgid "Expected loss by grade"
msgstr "按等级的预期损失"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.strategy.expected_loss_table` adds up the exposures and expected losses of each "
"grade or other group. Cut the PDs of the new score at the edges of a master scale, as in "
":doc:`calibration`:"
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.strategy.expected_loss_table` 汇总每个等级或其他分组的敞口和预期损失。与 :doc:`calibration` "
"一样，按主标尺的边界切分新评分的 PD："

#, python-format
msgid ""
"The expected loss rate, expected loss divided by exposure, rises from 1.7% in grade A to 29% in "
"grade F. With one LGD for everyone it is the LGD times the exposure-weighted PD; with an LGD per "
"applicant it also reflects the collateral of each grade. The rows follow the grades of the scale,"
" as in :func:`~kivi.calibration.calibration_table`, and grades without applicants are left out."
msgstr ""
"预期损失率即预期损失除以敞口，从 A 级的 1.7% 上升到 F 级的 29%。所有人使用同一 LGD 时，它等于 LGD 乘以按敞口加权的 PD；每个申请人有各自的 LGD "
"时，它还反映了各等级的担保情况。与 :func:`~kivi.calibration.calibration_table` 一样，各行按标尺的等级排列，没有申请人的等级不列出。"

msgid ""
"The portfolio totals are the sums of the columns, and its expected loss rate is the ratio of two "
"sums:"
msgstr "组合的合计是各列之和，其预期损失率是两个和之比："

msgid ""
"Comparing each grade's share of the exposure with its share of the expected loss shows where the "
"losses concentrate:"
msgstr "比较每个等级在敞口中的占比与在预期损失中的占比，可以看出损失集中在哪里："

#, python-format
msgid ""
"Grades E and F hold under a tenth of the exposure but almost 30% of the expected loss. A policy "
"that declines grade F, a PD above 0.4, gives up 2.7% of the exposure and avoids 14.4% of the "
"expected loss; the price of those loans would otherwise have to cover a loss rate of 29%."
msgstr ""
"E 级和 F 级的敞口不到十分之一，却占预期损失的近 30%。拒绝 F 级（PD 高于 0.4）的策略放弃 2.7% 的敞口，避开 14.4% 的预期损失；否则这些贷款的定价就必须覆盖 29% "
"的损失率。"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.strategy.cutoff_table`, :func:`~kivi.strategy.confusion_table`, "
":func:`~kivi.strategy.swap_set` and :func:`~kivi.strategy.expected_loss_table` take ``weights``, "
"one non-negative weight per applicant, as the functions of :mod:`kivi.metrics` do. Counts, "
"exposures and losses become sums of weights, and integer weights give the same counts and sums as"
" repeating rows. For ``cutoff_table`` and ``confusion_table`` this holds on explicit cut-offs: an"
" integer ``cutoffs`` uses the weighted quantiles of :func:`~kivi.binning.bin_edges`, which can "
"differ from the quantiles of repeated rows. Use the weights of an outcome-based sample, which "
"keeps all bad outcomes but only some of the good ones, to report approval and bad rates for the "
"whole population."
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.strategy.cutoff_table`、:func:`~kivi.strategy.confusion_table`、:func:`~kivi.strategy.swap_set`"
" 和 :func:`~kivi.strategy.expected_loss_table` 与 :mod:`kivi.metrics` 中的函数一样接受 "
"``weights``，即每个申请人一个非负权重。计数、敞口和损失都变为加权和，整数权重与重复相应行得到的计数和各项和相同。对 ``cutoff_table`` 和 "
"``confusion_table`` 而言，这只在显式截断点上成立：整数 ``cutoffs`` 使用 :func:`~kivi.binning.bin_edges` "
"的加权分位数，可能与重复行的分位数不同。对于保留全部坏结果、只保留部分好结果的按结果抽样样本，使用其权重即可报告整个总体的通过率和坏账率。"

msgid ""
"Before any variable is binned with care, look at all of them at once: how complete each one is, "
"how its values are distributed, and how strongly it separates events from non-events on its own. "
":func:`kivi.univariate.profile_table` summarizes every column of a data frame in one row, so the "
"whole list of candidates fits in one table."
msgstr ""
"在仔细地为任何变量分箱之前，先把所有变量放在一起看：每个变量的完整程度如何，取值如何分布，单独区分事件与非事件的能力有多强。 "
":func:`kivi.univariate.profile_table` 用一行概括数据框的每一列，因此全部候选变量可以放在一张表中。"

msgid ""
"The profile is the first step of a model. The candidates that pass its screening are binned with "
"care next, as :doc:`binning` describes, and :doc:`risk_workflow` follows them through the "
"remaining steps."
msgstr "概况是建模的第一步。通过筛选的候选变量接下来按 :doc:`binning` 中的方法仔细分箱， :doc:`risk_workflow` 则沿后续各步继续处理它们。"

msgid "Profiling the candidates"
msgstr "分析候选变量"

msgid ""
"The bundled bank data code missing values of its categorical variables with the label "
"``unknown``. Turn them into missing values first, so that the profile counts them:"
msgstr "自带的银行数据用标签 ``unknown`` 表示类别变量的缺失值。先把它们转换为缺失值，让概况表统计它们："

msgid "Every column gets one row, indexed by its name:"
msgstr "每一列占一行，以列名为索引："

msgid ""
"``kind`` is ``numeric`` for numeric dtypes other than bool and ``categorical`` for all others, as"
" in :func:`~kivi.spec.fit_spec`."
msgstr ""
"``kind`` 对 bool 以外的数值 dtype 为 ``numeric`` ，对其他所有 dtype 为 ``categorical`` ，与 "
":func:`~kivi.spec.fit_spec` 相同。"

#, python-format
msgid ""
"``count`` and ``missing`` count the rows with and without a value, and ``missing_share`` is the "
"share of rows without one. ``poutcome`` is missing for 82.5% of the customers, those who were not"
" in the previous campaign."
msgstr ""
"``count`` 和 ``missing`` 统计有取值和无取值的行数， ``missing_share`` 是无取值的行所占的比例。 ``poutcome`` 对 82.5% "
"的客户缺失，即未参加上一次营销活动的客户。"

msgid "``distinct`` is the number of different values."
msgstr "``distinct`` 是不同取值的个数。"

#, python-format
msgid ""
"``top`` is the most frequent value and ``top_share`` its share of the rows with a value. A share "
"close to 1 marks an almost constant variable: 98.4% of the customers have no ``default``."
msgstr "``top`` 是最常见的取值， ``top_share`` 是它在有取值的行中所占的比例。比例接近 1 表示该变量几乎是常数：98.4% 的客户的 ``default`` 为 no。"

msgid "Distribution of numeric variables"
msgstr "数值变量的分布"

msgid ""
"Numeric columns also get the mean, the sample standard deviation, the smallest value, the 1%, 50%"
" and 99% quantiles and the largest value. Categorical columns get NaN:"
msgstr "数值列还给出均值、样本标准差、最小值、1%、50% 和 99% 分位数以及最大值。类别列为 NaN："

msgid ""
"The 1% and 99% quantiles show the range of the bulk of the values. The largest ``balance`` is "
"three times its 99% quantile, so a few customers have far larger balances than the rest. The "
"median of ``pdays`` is -1, the code for a customer who was never contacted before."
msgstr ""
"1% 和 99% 分位数显示了大部分取值的范围。 ``balance`` 的最大值是其 99% 分位数的三倍，说明少数客户的余额远高于其他人。 ``pdays`` 的中位数为 "
"-1，这是此前从未联系过的客户的编码。"

msgid ""
"Three more columns describe the shape of a numeric distribution. ``skewness`` and ``kurtosis`` "
"are the bias-corrected sample skewness and excess kurtosis, as ``pandas.Series.skew`` and "
"``pandas.Series.kurt`` compute them, and ``cv``, the coefficient of variation, is the standard "
"deviation divided by the mean:"
msgstr ""
"另有三列描述数值分布的形态。 ``skewness`` 和 ``kurtosis`` 是偏差校正后的样本偏度和超额峰度，与 ``pandas.Series.skew`` 和 "
"``pandas.Series.kurt`` 的计算相同； ``cv`` 是变异系数，即标准差除以均值："

msgid ""
"A normal distribution has a skewness and an excess kurtosis of 0. ``balance``, ``campaign`` and "
"``previous`` have a skewness near 5 and a kurtosis above 35: a long right tail of a few very "
"large values, which quantile bins absorb but which dominate the mean and any linear fit of the "
"raw values. ``day`` is spread almost evenly over the month, with a kurtosis of -1. The "
"coefficient of variation compares spreads on different scales: the standard deviation of "
"``previous`` is three times its mean, that of ``age`` a quarter of it. It has the sign of the "
"mean and is NaN when the mean is 0. The skewness needs at least 3 values and the kurtosis at "
"least 4; both are NaN when all values are equal."
msgstr ""
"正态分布的偏度和超额峰度都为 0。 ``balance`` 、 ``campaign`` 和 ``previous`` 的偏度接近 5，峰度超过 "
"35：少数极大的取值形成长长的右尾，等频分箱能吸收它们，但它们会主导均值以及对原始取值的任何线性拟合。 ``day`` 在一个月内分布得几乎均匀，峰度为 "
"-1。变异系数可以比较不同尺度上的离散程度： ``previous`` 的标准差是其均值的三倍， ``age`` 的标准差只有均值的四分之一。它的符号与均值相同，均值为 0 时为 "
"NaN。偏度至少需要 3 个取值，峰度至少需要 4 个；所有取值都相等时两者均为 NaN。"

msgid "Screening by IV"
msgstr "按 IV 筛选变量"

msgid ""
"The ``iv`` column is the information value of a quick binning: ``bins`` quantile bins from "
":func:`~kivi.binning.bin_edges` for numeric columns, with a group for each special code, and the "
"labels for categorical ones. Missing values form a group of their own. The ``gini`` column is the"
" Gini coefficient of the values of a numeric column used as a score: positive when events have "
"higher values, negative when they have lower ones."
msgstr ""
"``iv`` 列是快速分箱的信息值：数值列使用 :func:`~kivi.binning.bin_edges` 的 ``bins`` "
"个等频箱，每个特殊值编码单独成组；类别列使用其标签。缺失值单独成组。 ``gini`` 列是把数值列的取值作为评分时的 Gini 系数：事件的取值较高时为正，较低时为负。"

msgid ""
"These are the IVs of the screening step of :doc:`risk_workflow`, which bins every candidate in "
"the same way. ``bin_edges`` warns about tied quantiles; :func:`~kivi.univariate.profile_table` "
"records them in ``tied_bins`` instead, so profiling many columns raises no warnings. Most values "
"of ``pdays`` and ``previous`` are -1 and 0, so their tied quantiles merge into a single bin, and "
"their IV of 0 understates them until they are binned with care: ``pdays`` with its special code, "
"as below, and ``previous`` with custom edges."
msgstr ""
"这些正是 :doc:`risk_workflow` 筛选步骤中的 IV，该步骤以同样的方式为每个候选变量分箱。 ``bin_edges`` 会对重合的分位数发出警告； "
":func:`~kivi.univariate.profile_table` 则将其记录在 ``tied_bins`` 中，因此分析很多列时不会产生警告。 ``pdays`` 和 "
"``previous`` 的大多数取值分别是 -1 和 0，因此它们重合的分位数合并为一个箱，在仔细分箱之前，IV 为 0 会低估它们的作用： ``pdays`` 要像下文那样使用特殊值编码， "
"``previous`` 要使用自定义边界。"

msgid ""
"Two more columns measure the separation in other ways. ``ks`` is the KS statistic of the values "
"of a numeric column used as a score, the largest gap between the cumulative distributions of "
"events and non-events, as :func:`~kivi.metrics.ks` computes it; unlike ``gini``, it has no sign "
"and lies between 0 and 1 whichever way the values run. ``chi2_p_value`` is the p-value of the "
"chi-squared test of independence between the target and the groups of the quick binning, the same"
" groups as ``iv``, with one degree of freedom fewer than there are groups:"
msgstr ""
"另外两列从其他角度衡量区分能力。 ``ks`` 是把数值列的取值当作评分时的 KS 统计量，即事件与非事件累计分布之间的最大差距，与 :func:`~kivi.metrics.ks` "
"的计算相同；与 ``gini`` 不同，它没有符号，无论取值方向如何都在 0 到 1 之间。 ``chi2_p_value`` 是目标与快速分箱各组（与 ``iv`` "
"的分组相同）之间卡方独立性检验的 p 值，自由度比组数少 1："

msgid ""
"On 3000 rows every column with an IV above 0.03 has a p-value below 0.05: with this many rows "
"even a weak relation is significant, so the p-value does not rank the columns. A large p-value is"
" more telling: the quick binnings of ``age``, ``day`` and ``default`` show no evidence that the "
"response rate depends on them. ``pdays`` and ``previous`` have a single group, so their p-value "
"is 1, while their ``ks`` of 0.192 shows that their values do separate the classes: the test, like"
" the IV, sees only the groups."
msgstr ""
"在 3000 行数据上，IV 高于 0.03 的每一列的 p 值都低于 0.05：行数这么多时，即使很弱的关系也是显著的，因此 p 值不能用来给各列排序。较大的 p 值更能说明问题： "
"``age`` 、 ``day`` 和 ``default`` 的快速分箱没有显示响应率依赖于它们的证据。 ``pdays`` 和 ``previous`` 只有一个组，因此 p 值为 "
"1，而它们 0.192 的 ``ks`` 表明其取值确实能区分两类：卡方检验与 IV 一样，只看得到分组。"

msgid ""
"The quick binning gives a first ranking, not a final one. Five quantile bins can miss a pattern "
"that other edges would show, and a categorical variable with many rare labels gets an inflated IV"
" until its categories are grouped as in :ref:`category-groups`. Read the ranking critically, as "
"the workflow does, and bin the shortlist with care in :doc:`binning`."
msgstr ""
"快速分箱只给出初步排序而非最终排序。五个等频箱可能遗漏其他边界才能显示的规律，而含有许多稀有标签的类别变量，在按 :ref:`category-groups` 对类别分组之前，IV "
"会被高估。像工作流程中那样审慎地解读这一排序，并在 :doc:`binning` 中仔细地为入选变量分箱。"

msgid ""
"A special code such as ``pdays == -1`` is a value, not a number on the scale of the others. Pass "
"it in ``special``, by column as in :func:`~kivi.spec.fit_spec`. The code still counts as a value "
"in ``count``, ``distinct`` and ``top``, but ``special`` and ``special_share`` count it "
"separately, and the numeric summary and its shape, the Gini coefficient, the KS statistic and the"
" quick binning leave it out:"
msgstr ""
"``pdays == -1`` 这样的特殊值编码是一个取值，而不是与其他取值处于同一尺度上的数。把它按列传入 ``special`` ，与 :func:`~kivi.spec.fit_spec`"
" 相同。该编码在 ``count`` 、 ``distinct`` 和 ``top`` 中仍算作取值，但 ``special`` 和 ``special_share`` "
"会单独统计它，数值汇总及其形态、Gini 系数、KS 统计量和快速分箱则不包含它："

msgid "Among the customers contacted before, half were contacted more than 188 days earlier."
msgstr "在此前联系过的客户中，一半客户的上次联系是在 188 天以前。"

msgid ""
"Left out of the quick binning, the code gets a group of its own, and the other values fill the "
"five quantile bins. The IV of ``pdays`` rises from 0 to 0.355, the third highest of all the "
"candidates:"
msgstr "从快速分箱中排除后，该编码单独成组，其余取值填满五个等频箱。 ``pdays`` 的 IV 从 0 升至 0.355，在全部候选变量中排第三："

msgid ""
"Its ``chi2_p_value`` falls from 1 to about 1e-35, as the groups now differ in their response "
"rates. The Gini coefficient of ``pdays`` was 0.175 when the code -1 counted as the lowest value; "
"among the customers contacted before, a more recent contact goes with more responses, so the sign"
" turns. ``ks`` has no sign, and it rises from 0.192 to 0.330."
msgstr ""
"它的 ``chi2_p_value`` 从 1 降到约 1e-35，因为各组的响应率现在有了差别。把编码 -1 当作最小值时， ``pdays`` 的 Gini 系数为 "
"0.175；在此前联系过的客户中，上次联系越近，响应越多，因此符号反转。 ``ks`` 没有符号，它从 0.192 升到 0.330。"

msgid ""
"With a target, every column also gets the event rate of all rows, ``event_rate``, and the event "
"rates of the rows without and with a value, ``missing_event_rate`` and "
"``non_missing_event_rate``. The lifts divide them by ``event_rate``, so a lift above 1 marks rows"
" riskier than average:"
msgstr ""
"有目标变量时，每一列还给出全部行的事件率 ``event_rate`` ，以及无取值和有取值的行的事件率 ``missing_event_rate`` 和 "
"``non_missing_event_rate`` 。提升度是它们除以 ``event_rate`` 的结果，提升度大于 1 表示这些行的风险高于平均水平："

#, python-format
msgid ""
"Customers whose contact type is missing responded at 5.0%, less than half the rate of 11.6% of "
"all customers. A missing value that carries information like this is worth its own group in the "
"binning, which :func:`~kivi.woe.woe_table` gives it."
msgstr "联系方式缺失的客户响应率为 5.0%，不到全部客户 11.6% 的一半。像这样携带信息的缺失值值得在分箱中单独成组， :func:`~kivi.woe.woe_table` 正是这样处理的。"

msgid "Share of missing values and their lift for job, education, contact and poutcome"
msgstr "job、education、contact 和 poutcome 的缺失值占比及其提升度"

msgid ""
"Share of missing values and their lift for the four columns with missing values. The missing "
"values of ``job`` respond more often than average, those of the other columns less often."
msgstr "四个有缺失值的列的缺失值占比及其提升度。 ``job`` 缺失的客户响应率高于平均水平，其他列缺失的客户则低于平均水平。"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.univariate.profile_table` takes ``weights``, for example the inverse of the sampling"
" rate of each row. Counts become sums of weights and every statistic is weighted, so integer "
"weights give the same table as repeating rows with unit weights. The quantiles are then weighted "
"quantiles by the inverted CDF, as the edges of :func:`~kivi.binning.bin_edges`, while the "
"unweighted quantiles interpolate. Weights therefore change the quantiles and, through the edges "
"of the quick binning, ``iv``, ``chi2_p_value`` and ``tied_bins``, even when they are all 1; every"
" other column equals that of the repeated rows without weights. ``skewness`` and ``kurtosis`` "
"take the total weight as the number of values, so they need weights that add up to more than 2 "
"and 3. Without ``target``, the table has only the columns that describe the variables."
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.univariate.profile_table` 接受 ``weights`` "
"，例如每一行抽样比例的倒数。计数变为权重之和，每项统计量都加权计算，因此整数权重与重复相应行并使用单位权重得到的表格相同。此时分位数是逆累积分布意义下的加权分位数，与 "
":func:`~kivi.binning.bin_edges` 的边界相同，而不加权的分位数会进行插值。因此，即使权重全为 1，也会改变分位数，并通过快速分箱的边界改变 ``iv`` 、 "
"``chi2_p_value`` 和 ``tied_bins`` ；其他各列都等于不加权的重复行的结果。 ``skewness`` 和 ``kurtosis`` "
"把总权重当作取值个数，因此权重之和须分别大于 2 和 3。没有 ``target`` 时，表格只包含描述变量的列。"

msgid ""
"The chi-squared test reads the weights as frequency weights: a row of weight 3 counts as three "
"observations. Weights that are the inverse of a sampling rate add up to the population rather "
"than to the sample, so they make the p-value too small; read it as a screening aid, not as a test"
" of the sample."
msgstr "卡方检验把权重当作频数权重：权重为 3 的行算作三个观测。抽样比例的倒数作为权重时，其总和对应的是总体而不是样本，因此会使 p 值偏小；请把它当作筛选的辅助指标，而不是对样本的检验。"

msgid ""
"Once a scorecard is in use, the loans it approves are monitored as they age. :mod:`kivi.vintage` "
"covers the two standard views of a loan portfolio: vintage curves, which follow the bad rate of "
"each origination cohort by month on book, and roll rates and transition matrices, which show how "
"loans move between delinquency buckets from one month end to the next."
msgstr ""
"评分卡投入使用后，需要跟踪其批准的贷款随账龄增长的表现。 :mod:`kivi.vintage` 提供贷款资产组合的两种标准视角：vintage "
"曲线按账龄跟踪每个放款批次的坏账率；滚动率和转移矩阵展示贷款从一个月末到下一个月末在逾期档位之间的迁移。"

msgid ""
"Vintage analysis complements :doc:`monitoring` and the :doc:`population stability index <psi>`, "
"which monitor the applicants, by following the loans themselves. Its curves and matrices then "
"give the PD term structures of :doc:`lifetime`, the last step of the user guide. "
":func:`~kivi.vintage.vintage_table` gives the vintage curves, and "
":func:`~kivi.vintage.transition_matrix` and :func:`~kivi.vintage.roll_rates` the movements "
"between buckets."
msgstr ""
"Vintage 分析直接跟踪贷款本身，与监控申请人的 :doc:`monitoring` 和 :doc:`群体稳定性指标 <psi>` 相互补充。它的曲线和矩阵进而给出 "
":doc:`lifetime` 中的 PD 期限结构，这是用户指南的最后一步。 :func:`~kivi.vintage.vintage_table` 给出 vintage 曲线， "
":func:`~kivi.vintage.transition_matrix` 和 :func:`~kivi.vintage.roll_rates` 给出贷款在逾期档位之间的迁移。"

msgid "The loan panel"
msgstr "贷款面板"

msgid ""
"Vintage curves and roll rates both work on a loan panel in long format, with one row per loan and"
" month on book. The examples use the synthetic panel of :func:`~kivi.datasets.make_loan_panel`: "
"5,000 instalment loans originated from January 2024 to December 2025 and observed at every month "
"end up to January 2026."
msgstr ""
"vintage 曲线和滚动率都基于长格式的贷款面板数据，每笔贷款的每个账龄一行。示例使用 :func:`~kivi.datasets.make_loan_panel` 生成的合成面板：5,000"
" 笔分期贷款，在 2024 年 1 月至 2025 年 12 月间发放，并在每个月末观测，直到 2026 年 1 月。"

msgid ""
"The status is an ordered categorical of days past due, so a comparison such as "
"``panel[\"status\"] >= \"60-89\"`` follows the order of the buckets. :doc:`datasets` describes "
"how the panel is simulated."
msgstr ""
"状态是按逾期天数排列的有序分类变量，因此像 ``panel[\"status\"] >= \"60-89\"`` 这样的比较会遵循档位的顺序。 :doc:`datasets` "
"介绍了面板的模拟方式。"

msgid ""
"A loan is *ever bad* by month on book :math:`k` if it was bad at any month on book up to "
":math:`k`. A vintage table holds, for each cohort and month on book, the share of the cohort's "
"loans that are ever bad by then. :func:`~kivi.vintage.vintage_table` takes the loan, the cohort, "
"the month on book and whether the loan is bad on each row, so the bad definition is a condition "
"on the status. Here a loan is bad once it is 90 days past due:"
msgstr ""
"如果贷款在账龄 :math:`k` 及之前的任一账龄为坏，就称它到账龄 :math:`k` 为止 *曾经为坏* （ever bad）。Vintage "
"表对每个批次和账龄，给出该批次贷款中到该账龄为止曾经为坏的比例。 :func:`~kivi.vintage.vintage_table` "
"接受每一行的贷款、批次、账龄以及该贷款是否为坏，因此坏的定义就是状态上的一个条件。这里贷款一旦逾期 90 天即为坏："

msgid "Cumulative 90+ bad rate by month on book for one cohort in each quarter"
msgstr "每个季度取一个批次，按账龄展示 90 天以上逾期的累计坏账率"

msgid "Vintage curves of the cohorts in the table: each curve stops at the cohort's latest month on book."
msgstr "表中各批次的 vintage 曲线：每条曲线止于该批次最新的账龄月。"

msgid ""
"Each row follows one cohort and never decreases from left to right, because a loan that was bad "
"stays counted as bad even if it cures later. The entries a cohort has not reached are NaN, not 0:"
" the 2025-04 cohort is observed up to month on book 9, so its bad rate at month 12 is not known "
"yet. Reading down a column compares the cohorts at the same age, which separates the quality of "
"new lending from the seasoning of the portfolio. The latest value of each cohort mixes the two, "
"because older cohorts have had more time to go bad."
msgstr ""
"每一行跟踪一个批次，从左到右不会递减，因为变坏过的贷款即使之后回到正常，也一直算作坏。批次尚未达到的取值为 NaN，而不是 0：2025-04 批次只观测到账龄 9，因此其账龄 12 "
"的坏账率还不得而知。沿一列向下读，是在相同账龄上比较各批次，从而把新增放款的质量与资产组合的账龄成熟效应区分开。每个批次的最新取值则混合了二者，因为较早的批次有更长的时间变坏。"

msgid ""
"Every cohort here has about 200 loans, so one bad loan moves its rate by half a percentage point."
" Compare small differences only after averaging several cohorts."
msgstr "这里每个批次约有 200 笔贷款，因此一笔坏贷款就会让坏账率变动半个百分点。比较细小的差异前，应先对多个批次取平均。"

msgid "Bad definitions and amounts"
msgstr "坏的定义与金额"

msgid ""
"An earlier bad definition gives an earlier signal. On the ordered status, ``>= \"60-89\"`` counts"
" the loans that reached 60 days past due or worse:"
msgstr "更早的坏定义能更早给出信号。在有序状态上， ``>= \"60-89\"`` 统计逾期达到 60 天或更严重的贷款："

msgid ""
"To weight each loan by the amount lent, pass ``weights``. The table then reports the share of the"
" cohort's amount lent that went to loans that turned bad:"
msgstr "要按放款金额给每笔贷款加权，请传入 ``weights`` 。此时表中报告的是批次放款金额中属于变坏贷款的比例："

msgid ""
"The weight must be the same on every row of a loan, so pass the amount lent rather than the "
"outstanding balance."
msgstr "同一笔贷款每一行的权重必须相同，因此应传入放款金额，而不是剩余余额。"

msgid "Roll rates"
msgstr "滚动率"

msgid ""
"A roll rate is the share of the loans in a delinquency bucket at one month end that are in the "
"next worse bucket at the next month end. To pair each row with the row of the same loan one month"
" on book later, merge the panel with itself shifted by one month. The last row of a loan has no "
"partner, because the loan was repaid or the panel ends, and drops out. Unlike shifting the rows "
"within each loan, the merge pairs the right months however the rows are sorted and wherever a "
"month is missing:"
msgstr "滚动率是某个月末处于某一逾期档位的贷款中，下一个月末处于下一个更差档位的比例。要把每一行与同一笔贷款账龄大一个月的那一行配对，可以把面板与平移一个月后的自身合并。贷款的最后一行没有配对行（因为贷款已还清或面板已结束），会被去掉。与在每笔贷款内部平移各行不同，无论各行如何排序、中间是否缺少某个月，合并都能配对正确的月份："

#, python-format
msgid ""
"Both columns are ordered categoricals, so :func:`~kivi.vintage.roll_rates` takes the order of the"
" states, from the best to the worst, from their categories. For plain labels, pass ``states``: "
"sorted, ``\"current\"`` would come after ``\"90+\"``. Each month about 2.3% of the current loans "
"miss an instalment, and the share that rolls on rises with the days past due: seven in ten of the"
" loans at 60 to 89 days are 90 days past due a month later."
msgstr ""
"两列都是有序分类变量，因此 :func:`~kivi.vintage.roll_rates` 从其类别中获得状态从最好到最差的顺序。对于普通标签，请传入 ``states`` ：如果按排序， "
"``\"current\"`` 会排在 ``\"90+\"`` 之后。每个月约有 2.3% 的正常贷款漏缴期款，且继续滚动的比例随逾期天数增加：逾期 60 到 89 "
"天的贷款中，有七成在一个月后逾期达到 90 天。"

msgid ""
"A loan falls at most one bucket further behind per month, so the only way from current to 90+ in "
"four months is to roll every month. If the movements follow a Markov chain, the product of the "
"roll rates is the share of current loans that are 90+ four months later:"
msgstr "贷款每个月最多再恶化一个档位，因此四个月内从正常到 90+ 的唯一途径是每个月都滚动。如果迁移服从马尔可夫链，各滚动率的乘积就是正常贷款在四个月后处于 90+ 的比例："

msgid "Balance roll rates weight each loan by its balance at the first month end, as loss forecasts do:"
msgstr "余额滚动率按第一个月末的余额给每笔贷款加权，这也是损失预测的做法："

msgid "Transition matrices"
msgstr "转移矩阵"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.vintage.transition_matrix` shows all the movements, not only the roll to the next "
"bucket. Row ``i``, column ``j`` counts the loans that moved from state ``i`` to state ``j``:"
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.vintage.transition_matrix` 展示全部迁移，而不只是滚动到下一档位的部分。第 ``i`` 行、第 ``j`` 列统计从状态 ``i`` "
"迁移到状态 ``j`` 的贷款数："

msgid "With ``normalize=True``, each row holds the shares of its loans and sums to 1:"
msgstr "设置 ``normalize=True`` 后，每一行给出该行贷款的比例，合计为 1："

msgid ""
"The monthly transition matrix between the delinquency buckets, with the roll rates outlined just "
"right of the diagonal"
msgstr "逾期分档之间的月度转移矩阵，对角线右侧紧邻的滚动率带有边框"

msgid ""
"The monthly transition matrix with ``normalize=True``. The shares just right of the diagonal, "
"outlined, are the roll rates that ``roll_rates`` returns."
msgstr "``normalize=True`` 时的月度转移矩阵。紧挨对角线右侧、带边框的比例，就是 ``roll_rates`` 返回的滚动率。"

msgid ""
"The diagonal holds the loans that stayed in their bucket, the ``current`` column the cures and "
"the entries just right of the diagonal the roll rates. A loan that reaches 90+ stays there in "
"this data, so the last row is all 90+."
msgstr "对角线是保持在原档位的贷款， ``current`` 列是回到正常的贷款，紧挨对角线右侧的取值就是滚动率。在这份数据中，到达 90+ 的贷款会一直停留在 90+，因此最后一行全部是 90+。"

msgid "Migration between two dates"
msgstr "两个日期之间的迁移"

msgid ""
"The same function compares any two observations of the same entities, such as the rating grades "
"of obligors at two annual reviews or the delinquency buckets of a portfolio at two month ends. "
"Here are the loans on book at the end of both June and December 2025:"
msgstr "同一个函数可以比较同一批对象的任意两次观测，例如债务人在两次年度复评时的评级，或资产组合在两个月末的逾期档位。下面是 2025 年 6 月末和 12 月末都在账上的贷款："

msgid ""
"Only the loans on book at both month ends are compared. The 226 loans repaid in between, almost "
"all of them current in June, drop out, so the ``current`` row describes the loans that stayed on "
"book. Missing values raise an error instead of being counted, so first decide what to do with the"
" entities observed only once: drop them, as here, or give them a state of their own, such as "
"``\"closed\"``, to keep them in the shares."
msgstr ""
"这里只比较两个月末都在账上的贷款。期间还清的 226 笔贷款（6 月时几乎都是正常状态）被去掉了，因此 ``current`` "
"行描述的是仍在账上的贷款。缺失值会引发错误，而不会被计入，因此请先决定如何处理只被观测到一次的对象：像这里一样删除，或者给它们一个单独的状态，例如 ``\"closed\"`` "
"，使它们保留在比例中。"

msgid ""
"If the monthly movements followed a time-homogeneous Markov chain, the sixth power of the monthly"
" matrix would give the six-month matrix. Comparing the shares that end in 90+ shows how far that "
"holds:"
msgstr "如果月度迁移服从时齐马尔可夫链，月度矩阵的六次幂就会给出六个月的矩阵。比较最终处于 90+ 的比例，可以看出这一假设在多大程度上成立："

msgid ""
"The projection is of the right size but not exact: loans differ in risk, and the chance of "
"missing an instalment depends on the month on book, so the movements are not a time-homogeneous "
"Markov chain. Few loans are 30 to 89 days past due in June, so those rows are also uncertain."
msgstr "推算值的量级正确，但并不精确：贷款的风险各不相同，且漏缴期款的概率取决于账龄，因此迁移并不是时齐马尔可夫链。6 月逾期 30 到 89 天的贷款很少，因此这些行本身也不确定。"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.woe.woe_table` measures how each group separates a binary target. An event is target"
" 1 and a non-event is target 0. Both target classes must be present. Group and target series must"
" share the same index; arrays and lists are matched by position, as :doc:`/api/conventions` "
"describes for every function."
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.woe.woe_table` 衡量每组对二分类目标的区分能力。标签 1 表示事件，0 "
"表示非事件。数据须同时包含两类标签。分组与标签序列的索引必须相同；数组和列表按位置对应， :doc:`/api/conventions` 说明了所有函数共同遵守的这一规则。"

msgid ""
"WOE and IV follow :doc:`binning`, which forms the groups, and come before :doc:`variable "
"selection <selection>`, which fits a logistic regression on the WOE-encoded variables. "
":func:`~kivi.woe.woe_transform` encodes new data with the fitted WOE, and :func:`~kivi.woe.woe` "
"and :func:`~kivi.woe.iv` compute the measures from counts that are already aggregated."
msgstr ""
"WOE 和 IV 位于 :doc:`binning` 之后（后者形成分组），位于 :doc:`变量筛选 <selection>` 之前（后者在 WOE 编码的变量上拟合逻辑回归）。 "
":func:`~kivi.woe.woe_transform` 用拟合的 WOE 对新数据编码， :func:`~kivi.woe.woe` 和 :func:`~kivi.woe.iv` "
"根据已经汇总的计数计算这些指标。"

msgid ""
"For group :math:`i`, let :math:`E_i` and :math:`N_i` be its numbers of events and non-events. Its"
" shares of all events and of all non-events are"
msgstr "对第 :math:`i` 组，令 :math:`E_i` 和 :math:`N_i` 分别为其事件数和非事件数。它在全部事件和全部非事件中的占比为"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "p_i = \\frac{E_i}{\\sum_j E_j}, \\qquad q_i = \\frac{N_i}{\\sum_j N_j}."
msgstr "p_i = \\frac{E_i}{\\sum_j E_j}, \\qquad q_i = \\frac{N_i}{\\sum_j N_j}."

msgid "The weight of evidence and the information value contribution of the group are"
msgstr "该组的证据权重和信息值贡献为"

msgid ""
"A positive WOE means that the group is relatively more common among events. Each IV contribution "
"is zero or positive, because :math:`p_i - q_i` and :math:`\\ln(p_i / q_i)` always share a sign."
msgstr "WOE 为正表示该组在事件中相对更常见。每组的 IV 贡献都大于或等于零，因为 :math:`p_i - q_i` 与 :math:`\\ln(p_i / q_i)` 的符号始终相同。"

msgid ""
"Two thirds of group ``a`` are events and two thirds of group ``b`` are non-events, so the two "
"groups have opposite WOE values of :math:`\\pm\\ln 2`."
msgstr "组 ``a`` 中三分之二是事件，组 ``b`` 中三分之二是非事件，因此两组的 WOE 互为相反数，等于 :math:`\\pm\\ln 2`。"

msgid ""
"The first columns describe each group on its own: its counts, its share of all observations and "
"its event rate."
msgstr "前几列描述每组本身：计数、占全部观测的比例和事件率。"

msgid "The remaining columns compare the two classes:"
msgstr "其余各列比较两个类别："

msgid ""
"The six rows of groups a and b with their targets, and the woe_table result with counts, shares, "
"WOE and IV"
msgstr "组 a 和 b 的六行及其目标，以及 woe_table 的结果：计数、占比、WOE 和 IV"

msgid ""
"How ``woe_table`` computes the example: it counts the non-events and events of each group, "
"divides each count by its column total, takes the log of the ratio of the two shares as the WOE, "
"and multiplies the WOE by the difference of the shares for the IV."
msgstr "``woe_table`` 如何计算该示例：统计每组的非事件数和事件数，用每个计数除以所在列的合计，取两个占比之比的对数作为 WOE，再用 WOE 乘以两个占比之差得到 IV。"

msgid ""
"When the counts are already aggregated, for example from a database query, :func:`~kivi.woe.woe` "
"and :func:`~kivi.woe.iv` take the event and non-event counts of each group and give the same "
"values:"
msgstr "如果计数已经汇总（例如来自数据库查询），可以把每组的事件数和非事件数传给 :func:`~kivi.woe.woe` 和 :func:`~kivi.woe.iv` ，得到相同的结果："

msgid "Smoothing empty cells"
msgstr "空单元格的平滑"

msgid ""
"A group without events or without non-events would have an infinite WOE. Before the shares are "
"computed, each zero count is replaced by the ``smoothing`` value :math:`s`:"
msgstr "没有事件或没有非事件的组，其 WOE 会是无穷。计算占比前，每个零计数都会被替换为 ``smoothing`` 参数值 :math:`s`："

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\\tilde E_i = \\begin{cases} E_i & E_i > 0 \\\\ s & E_i = 0 \\end{cases}, \\qquad\n"
"p_i = \\frac{\\tilde E_i}{\\sum_j \\tilde E_j},"
msgstr ""
"\\tilde E_i = \\begin{cases} E_i & E_i > 0 \\\\ s & E_i = 0 \\end{cases}, \\qquad\n"
"p_i = \\frac{\\tilde E_i}{\\sum_j \\tilde E_j},"

msgid ""
"and likewise for non-events. Smoothing replaces zero cells with 0.5 by default. Each column is "
"then normalized separately. Counts in the result always report observations."
msgstr "非事件同理。平滑默认用 0.5 替换零频数，再按列分别归一化。结果表中的计数始终是实际观测数。"

msgid ""
"Changing smoothing can materially change the result for sparse bins. Merge small bins, or compare"
" several smoothing values, before relying on their WOE."
msgstr "修改平滑参数可能显著改变稀疏分箱的结果。在依赖这些箱的 WOE 之前，请合并小箱，或比较多个平滑取值的结果。"

msgid "``non_event_share``, ``event_share``"
msgstr "``non_event_share``, ``event_share``"

msgid "``total_share``"
msgstr "``total_share``"

msgid "The group's share of all observations, without smoothing."
msgstr "该组占全部观测的比例，不做平滑。"

msgid ""
"Events divided by the total of the group, without smoothing. For a default target this is the bad"
" rate."
msgstr "该组事件数除以该组总数，不做平滑。当目标为违约时，即为坏账率。"

msgid "``woe``"
msgstr "``woe``"

msgid ":math:`\\ln(p_i / q_i)`."
msgstr ":math:`\\ln(p_i / q_i)`."

msgid "``iv``"
msgstr "``iv``"

msgid "The group's IV contribution. Sum the column for the variable's IV."
msgstr "该组的 IV 贡献。对该列求和得到变量的 IV。"

msgid ""
"A widely used rule of thumb reads an IV below 0.02 as not predictive, 0.02 to 0.1 as weak, 0.1 to"
" 0.3 as medium and above 0.3 as strong. Treat these bands as a starting point, not as a test; a "
"very high IV often points to a leak of the target into the variable."
msgstr ""
"一种广泛使用的经验口径是：IV 低于 0.02 视为无预测力，0.02 到 0.1 为弱，0.1 到 0.3 为中等，高于 0.3 为强。这些区间只是参考起点，而非检验标准；IV "
"过高往往意味着目标信息泄漏到了该变量中。"

msgid "Charting WOE"
msgstr "绘制 WOE 图"

msgid ""
"A WOE chart is the usual way to review a variable with the business: the share of customers and "
"the event rate of each group on top, the WOE below. Categorical variables read best when sorted "
"by WOE."
msgstr "WOE 图是与业务方一起评审变量的常用方式：上图为每组的客户占比和事件率，下图为 WOE。类别变量按 WOE 排序后最易阅读。"

msgid "Share of customers, subscription rate and WOE for each job"
msgstr "每种职业的客户占比、认购率和 WOE"

#, python-format
msgid ""
"WOE by job. Students and retired customers subscribe far more often than blue-collar workers, but"
" students are only 2% of the sample, so their WOE rests on few customers."
msgstr "按职业的 WOE。学生和退休客户的认购率远高于蓝领工人，但学生只占样本的 2%，其 WOE 依赖的客户很少。"

msgid "Plotting code"
msgstr "绘图代码"

msgid ""
"The documentation draws its WOE charts with this matplotlib function. It takes a "
":func:`~kivi.woe.woe_table` result."
msgstr "本文档用下面这个 matplotlib 函数绘制 WOE 图，它接收 :func:`~kivi.woe.woe_table` 的结果。"

msgid "To compare many variables at once, rank them by IV; see :doc:`risk_workflow`."
msgstr "要同时比较多个变量，可以按 IV 排序，见 :doc:`risk_workflow`。"

msgid "Encoding new data"
msgstr "对新数据编码"

msgid ""
"A scorecard model takes WOE values as inputs. :func:`~kivi.woe.woe_transform` replaces each group"
" with its WOE from a development table, so the validation sample and later production data are "
"encoded with exactly the same values. Group every sample with the edges fitted on the development"
" sample:"
msgstr ""
"评分卡模型以 WOE 值作为输入。 :func:`~kivi.woe.woe_transform` 用开发样本表中的 WOE "
"替换每个分组，因此验证样本和之后的生产数据都会使用完全相同的编码。请用在开发样本上拟合的边界为每个样本分组："

msgid ""
"Four new rows grouped by age, each linked to its row in the development WOE table and to the WOE "
"it receives"
msgstr "按年龄分组的四个新行，每行都连到开发样本 WOE 表中的对应行以及它得到的 WOE"

msgid ""
"``woe_transform`` looks up the group of each row in the development table and returns its WOE, "
"with the index of the rows."
msgstr "``woe_transform`` 在开发样本的表中查找每一行所在的组，返回其 WOE，并保留各行的索引。"

msgid ""
"The result keeps the index of the groups. A missing value takes the WOE of the missing group when"
" the development sample had missing values."
msgstr "结果保留分组的索引。如果开发样本中有缺失值，缺失值会取缺失组的 WOE。"

msgid ""
"A group that is not in the table, such as a category that appears only in later data, raises an "
"error by default, so a mapping problem cannot go unnoticed:"
msgstr "不在表中的分组（例如只在后来的数据中出现的类别）默认会引发错误，因此映射问题不会被忽略："

msgid ""
"Pass ``unseen`` to give such groups a WOE instead. A WOE of 0 is the neutral choice: it stands "
"for the event rate of the whole development sample."
msgstr "也可以传入 ``unseen`` 为这类分组指定 WOE。WOE 为 0 是中性的选择：它代表整个开发样本的事件率。"

msgid ""
"Development samples are often stratified: every bad account is kept, but only a fraction of the "
"good ones. Pass the inverse of each observation's sampling rate as ``weights`` so that the counts"
" describe the population. Below, the sample keeps every subscriber and every fourth other "
"customer, so each non-subscriber stands for four customers."
msgstr ""
"开发样本常常是分层抽样得到的：保留全部坏账户，但只保留一部分好账户。把每个观测抽样比例的倒数作为 ``weights`` "
"传入，计数就能反映总体。下面的样本保留了全部认购客户和每四个其他客户中的一个，因此每个未认购客户代表四个客户。"

msgid ""
"The unweighted sample overstates the event rate, and the weights bring it back to the population "
"level. The WOE does not change, because it compares shares within each class and the weights of a"
" class scale all of its counts alike. That holds while no group is empty in either class: "
"``smoothing`` replaces an empty cell in units of weight, so with weights that do not sum to the "
"number of observations, scale ``smoothing`` along with them. In a weighted result the counts are "
"sums of weights, and groups whose weights sum to zero are left out; "
":func:`~kivi.woe.woe_transform` treats them as unseen."
msgstr ""
"不加权的样本高估了事件率，加权后事件率回到总体水平。WOE "
"不变，因为它比较的是事件与非事件各自内部的占比，而同一目标类别的权重会使其所有计数按相同比例缩放。前提是没有任何组在某一目标类别中为空： ``smoothing`` "
"以权重为单位替换空单元格，因此当权重总和不等于观测数时，请按相同比例缩放 ``smoothing`` 。加权结果中的计数为权重之和，权重之和为零的组会被排除， "
":func:`~kivi.woe.woe_transform` 会把它们视为未见过的分组。"

